/*
 * Maintenance Figures — the numbers a tech needs mid clean-and-check, pulled
 * out of the manuals so nobody reads a 109-page PDF on a phone in a crawl
 * space. Same idea as CHARGING_CHARTS, heating side.
 *
 * Every figure here came out of manufacturer service literature. Sources are
 * on each entry. When a manual says "see the rating plate" or "see Table N",
 * this file says that too rather than inventing a number — the rating plate
 * wins over anything on a screen.
 *
 * match[] is what the search runs against, so put every model string a tech
 * might read off a tag in there.
 */

const MAINT_SPECS = [
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"G51MP","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"90%+ single-stage, PSC blower, SureLight HSI","match":["G51MP","G51","G51MP-24B-045","G51MP-36B-045","G51MP-36B-070","G51MP-36C-090","G51MP-48C-090","G51MP-60C-090","G51MP-48C-110","G51MP-60C-110","G51MP-60D-135"],"source":"Lennox Service Literature Corp. 0307-L5, rev. 11-2006","flags":[{"title":"Flame signal depends on the BOARD, not the model","body":"Identify the control board before you judge the number. A reading that is healthy on a 69M15 is a failing sensor on a 97L48. Nothing here is anywhere near the 1–5 µA you learned on generic training."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board 97L48 (all -1 units, 090-2)","value":"Normal > 0.61 µA · Low 0.21–0.60 · Drop out ≤ 0.20","key":true},{"label":"Board 69M15 (045-2, 070-2, 110-2, 135-2, 090-3 and later)","value":"Normal > 0.31 µA · Low 0.25–0.30 · Drop out ≤ 0.24","key":true},{"label":"Transducer","value":"Lennox 78H5401 if your meter won't read that low. Converts µA to volts 1:1."},{"label":"When to read","value":"After 2 minutes of burner operation"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural","value":"3.5\" w.c. ± 0.3","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP","value":"10.0\" w.c. ± 0.7"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.5 – 13.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"10.5 – 13.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Orifice, natural","value":".089\""},{"label":"Max CO","value":"100 ppm","key":true},{"label":"CO₂ %, natural","value":"-045: 6.3–7.3 · -070: 6.5–7.5 · -090/-110/-135: 7.0–8.0"},{"label":"Run time before sampling","value":"15 minutes at correct manifold pressure and rate"}]},{"title":"Clocking the meter — seconds per revolution, natural","rows":[{"label":"1 cu ft dial","value":"-045: 80 · -070: 51 · -090: 40 · -110: 33 · -135: 27","key":true},{"label":"2 cu ft dial","value":"-045: 160 · -070: 102 · -090: 80 · -110: 66 · -135: 53"},{"label":"Method","value":"Shut off every other gas appliance on the meter. Time two revolutions, divide by two."}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Read the rating plate — ranges run 25–75°F depending on model"},{"label":"Blower motor","value":"PSC 120V. Prelubricated — do not oil."},{"label":"Blower-off delay target","value":"Supply air 90–110°F at the instant the blower drops out"},{"label":"Ignitor resistance","value":"10.9 – 19.7 Ω (ohm it; voltage can't be measured on this board)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout S47","value":"Opens 250°F ± 12, manual reset, one each side of burner box"},{"label":"Secondary limit S21","value":"125°F auto reset, behind blower housing"},{"label":"Backup secondary S113","value":"090 / 110 / 135 only — on the inducer, opens at 142°F"},{"label":"Prove switches","value":"Two identical switches, both must function. Never run with one bypassed."},{"label":"Blocked drain","value":"Shows up as a prove-switch fault. Water backs into the header box and kills the differential. Check the drain before condemning a switch."},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (S18, 0-4500 ft)","value":"-045-7 & later: 1.10 in. w.c. · -045-1 to -6: 0.95 in. w.c. · -070-7 & later: 1.00 in. w.c. · -070-1 to -6: 0.95 in. w.c. · -090/-110: 0.85 in. w.c. · -135: 0.65 in. w.c. Factory-set, non-adjustable. Higher altitude bands (4501-7500', 7501-10,000') step down — see Table 10.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"G61MP / G61MPV","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"90%+ two-stage. MPV is the variable-speed variant.","match":["G61MP","G61MPV","G61MPVT","G61","G61MP-36B-045","G61MP-36B-070","G61MP-48C-090","G61MP-60C-090","G61MP-48C-110","G61MP-60C-110","G61MP-60D-135"],"source":"Lennox Service Literature Corp. 0308-L6, rev. 11-2006","flags":[{"title":"It overfires while you measure manifold pressure","body":"The procedure has you disconnect the burner-box sensing hose from the gas valve — that's what makes the reading valid and also what makes it overfire. Get the number and shut it down. Do not clock the meter during this test; the rate will be wrong. Clock during normal operation."},{"title":"Two stages means two readings","body":"Check manifold on low fire and again on high fire. Separate adjustment screws, both under caps."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board 46M99","value":"Normal > 0.23 µA · Low < 0.22 · Drop out 0.16","key":true},{"label":"Board 100869","value":"Normal > 1.50 µA · Low < 1.40 · Drop out 0.20","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor, board 46M99","value":"10.9 – 19.7 Ω"},{"label":"Ignitor, board 100869","value":"25 – 47 Ω — a good ignitor ohmed against the 46M99 spec gets condemned","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural","value":"Low fire 1.7\" w.c. · High fire 3.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP","value":"Low fire 4.9\" w.c. · High fire 10.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.5 – 10.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11.0 – 13.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Orifice, natural","value":".089\""},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Honeywell VR8205 or White Rodgers 36E, two-stage"},{"label":"Max CO","value":"100 ppm","key":true},{"label":"CO₂ % high heat, natural","value":"045/070: 6.5–7.5 · 090: 6.9–7.9 · 110: 7.2–8.2 · 135: 7.4–8.4"},{"label":"CO₂ % low heat, natural","value":"045/070: 4.8–5.8 · 090: 5.1–6.1 · 110: 5.3–6.3 · 135: 5.7–6.7"}]},{"title":"Clocking the meter — seconds per revolution, natural","rows":[{"label":"1 cu ft dial","value":"-045: 82 · -070: 55 · -090: 41 · -110: 33 · -135: 27","key":true},{"label":"2 cu ft dial","value":"-045: 164 · -070: 110 · -090: 82 · -110: 66 · -135: 54"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.8\" w.c. — higher than the G51, don't carry the number over","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Separate high-fire and low-fire ranges. Read the rating plate."},{"label":"Blower-off delay target","value":"Supply air 90–110°F at dropout"},{"label":"Speed taps","value":"HI HEAT / LO HEAT / COOL on the SureLight board; park the unused lead"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout S47","value":"Opens 250°F, manual reset, two switches"},{"label":"Secondary limits S21","value":"Two of them, 125°F auto reset, behind blower housing"},{"label":"Backup secondary S113","value":"090 / 110 / 135 only — inducer mounted, 142°F"},{"label":"Prove switches","value":"045/070 use two switches. 090/110/135 use dual assemblies with separate first- and second-stage setpoints."},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (S18, 0-4500 ft)","value":"-045/-070: 2nd stage 0.95 in. w.c. / 1st stage 0.95 in. w.c. · -090/-110: 2nd 0.85 / 1st 0.50 in. w.c. · -135: 2nd 0.60 / 1st 0.35 in. w.c. Factory-set, non-adjustable. 4501-7500' and 7501-10,000' bands (Tables 13/14) step some sizes down further — check altitude before condemning a switch.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DM96VC / DC96VC","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96% two-stage, communicating capable","match":["DM96VC","DC96VC","DM96","DC96","DM96VC0403BN","DM96VC0603BN","DM96VC0803BN","DM96VC0804CN","DM96VC1005CN","DM96VC1005DN","DM96VC1205DN","DC96VC0403BN","DC96VC0603BN","DC96VC0804CN","DC96VC1005CN","DC96VC1205DN"],"source":"Daikin Installation Instructions IOD-2008N, 02/2022","flags":[{"title":"Supply pressure max is 10.0\" w.c., not 13\"","body":"A house at 11\" w.c. is inside spec on a Lennox G51 and OVER MAX on this. If you carry the Lennox number over you will walk right past an overfire. Check it with every other gas appliance in the house running."},{"title":"The drain trap is internally partitioned — prime BOTH sides","body":"Add water to both inlet ports until it shows at both sides of the outlet. Daikin says an unprimed trap hurts combustion quality and pressure switch action, so a half-primed trap comes back as a nuisance pressure switch fault that reads like a bad switch."},{"title":"Don't chase microamps here","body":"On the Daikin modulating units the manual states outright that reading flame signal with a microamp meter isn't reliable or consistent and isn't recommended practice — the board carries its own low-flame warning. Read the status code instead. This is the opposite of the Lennox procedure."},{"title":"Flame-sense µA IS published — it's the S-314 bench-check spec, not a field-diagnosis recommendation","body":"Daikin's own RSD6612010r5 Service Instructions (S-314 CHECKING FLAME SENSOR, p.75) give an explicit micro-amp-meter check with an expected 1-4 µA DC reading on the Integrated Ignition control — this is the number a public model apparently read off a photo of a meter. It sits alongside this entry's existing 'Don't chase microamps here' flag, which is about the installer-facing guidance that field microamp readings aren't the primary field diagnostic on this modulating platform (the board's own status/error code is more reliable in the field) — not a claim that no spec exists. Both are accurate; use the status code for day-to-day diagnosis but 1-4 µA DC is the documented bench value."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural","value":"High stage 3.5\" w.c. · Low stage 1.9\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, propane","value":"High stage 10.0\" w.c. · Low stage 6.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Orifice, natural","value":"#45"},{"label":"Orifice, propane","value":"1.25 mm (LPM-08 kit — supports both Honeywell and White-Rodgers 2-stage valves)"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.5 – 10.0\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, propane","value":"11.0 – 13.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Altitude","value":"Factory config good 0–7000 ft on natural. Above 7000 ft see the spec sheet — and use 3\" venting."}]},{"title":"Air and electrical","rows":[{"label":"Return air temperature","value":"Must be 55–100°F entering the furnace while heating","key":true},{"label":"Ground check","value":"Power off. Neutral (white) to any burner should read 10 Ω or less.","key":true},{"label":"Confined space ventilation","value":"Two openings, 0.25 sq in free area per 1,000 BTU/hr input. One within 12\" of top, one within 12\" of bottom."},{"label":"Single-stage t-stat step-up","value":"Fixed 5 min, or AUTO which averages the last three cycles and picks 1–12 min. Know which is set before you diagnose \"won't go to high fire.\""},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Model/size-specific: 30-60°F on DM96VC0453B-0905D upflow models, 35-65°F on the 1155D upflow; DC96VC downflow ranges 25-55°F (0714C, 0915D) up to 40-70°F (1155D) — see rating plate or SS-DM96VC spec sheet for the exact model"}]},{"title":"Venting and drain","rows":[{"label":"Vent slope","value":"1/4\" per foot back toward the furnace"},{"label":"Vent support","value":"Every 3–5 ft on horizontal runs"},{"label":"Vent insulation","value":"1/2\" closed cell foam anywhere it sees below 35°F for extended periods"},{"label":"Drain trap clearance","value":"5-1/2\" below the furnace on horizontal installs"},{"label":"Qualified-servicer items","value":"Condensate trap and drain system, flame sensor, flue passages"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"1-4 µA DC normal on the Integrated Ignition control (S-314 CHECKING FLAME SENSOR procedure); if reading is below spec check for high-resistance wiring connections, sensor-to-burner gap, dirty/oxidized sensor, or poor grounding","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"120V Silicon Nitride HSI, 37-68 Ω cold resistance at room temp, steady-state preheat current 0.37-0.68A at 120V, ~2156-2678°F normal operating temp (S-308A)"},{"label":"Pressure switch trip","value":"no fixed in. w.c. number published for this chassis in the Service Instructions — S-310 test procedure says only to compare closing point against the individual switch's own stamped spec; if not closing, replace switch or correct inducer/venting"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59TP6 / 59TP7","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Two-stage variable speed ECM multipoise condensing","match":["59TP6","59TP6A","59TP6B","59TP6C","59TP7","59TP7A","59TP7A100V21","59TN6","59TN6C"],"source":"Carrier 59TP6C Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions","flags":[{"title":"There is no single manifold pressure number","body":"Lennox and Daikin publish one value. Carrier publishes a table — orifice size and manifold pressure keyed to gas input rate, and the natural gas figures already compensate for BOTH altitude and gas heating value. Look it up for this unit's input rate every time. Table 26."},{"title":"A sooted heat exchanger gets replaced, not cleaned","body":"With heavy soot and carbon, Carrier calls for replacing both primary and secondary heat exchangers rather than cleaning, because of the intricate design. Different answer than the Lennox units, which have a documented cleaning procedure. And soot is a symptom — find the cause first or you'll soot the new one too."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"Table 26 (59TP6C; Table 20 on 59TP6B), by input rate + altitude + heating value. Not a fixed number.","key":true},{"label":"Table basis","value":"20,000 BTUH high heat / 13,000 BTUH low heat per burner, derated 2% per 1,000 ft above sea level"},{"label":"Adjustment","value":"Gas valve regulator adjustment screws, to the proper low and high fire input rates"},{"label":"Clocking the meter","value":"Gas valve ON/OFF switch to OFF first, then loosen the set screw on the manifold tower pressure tap"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot surface igniter (HSI). Check resistance which should be 40 to 70 ohms at room temperature.","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Furnace sets its own airflow to hold rise in range","key":true},{"label":"If rise is out of range","value":"Check in this order: gas input · altitude derate · duct restrictions · setup switch SW1-3"},{"label":"Blower off delay","value":"DIP switches SW-7 and SW-8, per Table 19"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Status code LED","value":"Amber, on the blower door. Two digits — short flashes give the first, long flashes the second.","key":true},{"label":"Continuous ON","value":"Control has 24VAC"},{"label":"Rapid flashing","value":"Reversed line voltage polarity, or the furnace isn't grounded","key":true},{"label":"59TP6C only","value":"On-board 3-digit LCD with pushbutton navigation, plus NFC for reading and adjusting from a phone"},{"label":"59TP7A (Performance 97)","value":"Same service platform as 59TP6, to 97% AFUE — standardizes the 59TP6C on-board 3-digit LCD + NFC diagnostics","key":true},{"label":"Safety controls","value":"Flame sensor, gas valve and pressure switch verify during start-up. Main limit switch is checked separately."}]},{"title":"Soot causes — check all of these before quoting a heat exchanger","rows":[{"label":"1","value":"Improper manifold pressure adjustment"},{"label":"2","value":"Insufficient or poor quality combustion air"},{"label":"3","value":"Improper vent termination"},{"label":"4","value":"Incorrect size or damaged manifold orifice"},{"label":"5","value":"Improper gas"},{"label":"6","value":"Restricted heat exchanger"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"58 series (80%)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE non-condensing, 4-way multipoise. 58SB0B/58SB1B and 58SC0B/58SC1B current; 58STA/58STX older.","match":["58SB0B","58SB1B","58SC0B","58SC1B","58SB0","58SC0","58STA","58STX","58SU0A","58SU0B","58SP0A","58CVA","58CU0","58MVC","58"],"source":"Carrier 58STA/58STX and 58SB0B/58SC0B Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions","flags":[{"title":"This is a different machine, not a smaller 59","body":"No condensate. No trap to prime, no drain hoses, no vent-drain elbow, no blocked-drain-masquerading-as-a-pressure-switch. Half the 90% checklist doesn't apply — and what replaces it is venting, which is where the danger is."},{"title":"The spillage check is the job on an 80%","body":"When an 80% shares a flue with a gas water heater, anything that changes house pressure can leave the water heater orphaned in an oversized vent that won't draw. Run worst-case depressurization: close windows and doors, run the dryer and every exhaust fan on high, fire the water heater alone, check for spillage at the draft hood after 5 minutes. No equivalent on the 90% units."}],"groups":[{"title":"vs the 59TP6 — don't carry numbers across","rows":[{"label":"Vent","value":"Metal, Category I, natural draft up a flue (59TP6: sealed PVC, positive pressure)","key":true},{"label":"Common vented with a water heater","value":"Possible and common — must be checked (59TP6: never)","key":true},{"label":"Condensate","value":"None (59TP6: trap, hoses, drain, freeze protection)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"4% per 1,000 ft (59TP6: 2% per 1,000 ft)","key":true},{"label":"Table basis, 58STA/STX","value":"22,000 BTUH per burner on Table 12 · 21,000 BTUH per burner on Table 13"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"Off the table, indexed by input rate, altitude, gas heat value AND specific gravity (0.58 / 0.60 / 0.62 / 0.64). Don't eyeball it.","key":true},{"label":"Igniter warm-up, 58STA","value":"17 seconds after prepurge, then trial for ignition"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"S9V2-VS (also sold as American Standard Gold S9V2 — same model prefixes, no separate AS numbering on this platform)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96%+ AFUE 2-stage condensing furnace, variable-speed ECM blower + variable-speed inducer, sealed PVC direct/non-direct vent","match":["S9V2","S9V2B040U3VSAC","S9V2B060U3VSAC","S9V2B080U4VSAC","S9V2C100U4VSAC","S9V2D120U5VSAC","American Standard Gold S9V2"],"source":"Trane S9V2 Installer's Guide 18-CE19D1-1B-EN (Feb 2022). Flame-sense/ignitor values cross-verified against Trane S9X-series Service Facts and S8V2 IOM — same-generation IFC board and silicon-nitride ignitor.","flags":[{"title":"Adjust 2nd stage BEFORE 1st stage","body":"The White-Rodgers 36J valve has separate HI (2nd stg) and LO (1st stg) regulator screws. Trane's procedure explicitly requires setting 2nd stage first, then 1st — reversing the order throws off the low-fire setting relative to high-fire."},{"title":"Temp rise / external static are NOT in the Installer's Guide","body":"The guide states airflow-vs-static and temp-rise tables are in the Service Facts accompanying the furnace — model/tap-specific, not republished. Pull the Service Facts or rating plate for the exact unit; don't reuse a number from a similar model."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural (2nd stg / 1st stg)","value":"3.5\" w.c. / 1.7\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP (2nd stg / 1st stg)","value":"10.0\" w.c. / 6.0\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"5.0 – 13.8\" w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"10.0 – 13.8\" w.c."},{"label":"Orifice (sea level)","value":"Drill #45 natural, #56 propane — all inputs 40–120 MBH"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J, 2-stage"},{"label":"High altitude derate","value":"Above 2,000 ft: reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft; NG manifold re-check 3.0–3.7\" w.c.; LP always needs an orifice change at altitude"},{"label":"Max CO","value":"Not published by Trane — verify with a calibrated combustion analyzer against code limits; do not assume a fixed ppm number","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"see rating plate / Service Facts (model- and blower-tap-specific)"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"see rating plate / Service Facts (model-specific range)"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame current","value":"0.75–3.0 µA DC normal (1 VDC = 1 µA across the two FP pads on the IFC); fault logged below 0.5 µA DC","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride HSI; 37–70 Ω cold resistance at ~75°F"},{"label":"Status display","value":"7-segment LED on IFC; Menu+Option held 5s clears last 6 faults, 15s = factory reset"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout","value":"Manual-reset (red button); fixed trip temperature not published — OEM part only"},{"label":"Limit","value":"Auto-reset primary limit; trip setpoint stamped on the rating plate, not in the Installer's Guide"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"S8B1 / S8X1 (also American Standard Silver S8B1/S8X1)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage, Category I induced-draft non-condensing furnace","match":["S8B1","S8X1","S8B1A040M3PSC","S8X1A040M3PSC","S8B1B060M4PSC","S8B1B080M4PSC","S8B1C100M5PSC","S8B1D120M5PSC","American Standard Silver S8B1","American Standard Silver S8X1"],"source":"Trane S8B1/S8X1/S8X2 Installer's Guide 18-CE16D1-1C-EN (Apr 2021). Flame-sense/ignitor cross-verified against Trane S8V2 IOM — same IFC board/ignitor family.","flags":[{"title":"Single-stage models share the 2-stage valve table — don't use the low-fire column","body":"S8B1/S8X1 fire as a single stage but share this guide (and the White-Rodgers 36J valve) with the 2-stage S8X2. For standard S8B1/S8X1 sizes only the high (2nd-stg) pressure applies (3.5\" w.c. NG, 10.0\" LP) — ignore the low-fire numbers, they're for the S8X2. EXCEPTION: the largest D120 units are listed WITH a second pressure (3.5/1.8\" NG, 10/7.5\" LP) — verify against that unit's Service Facts."},{"title":"Category I flue — not sealed, not positive pressure","body":"Fan-assisted-combustion furnace venting into a Type B vent or lined chimney sized per NFGC. Removing a companion appliance (old water heater/furnace) often leaves the chimney oversized for this furnace alone — a common flue-gas condensation/corrosion callback. Side-wall power venting needs a listed draft inducer at -0.02\" w.c. barometric relief."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural (single stage, non-D120)","value":"3.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP (single stage, non-D120)","value":"10.0\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, D120 (see flag)","value":"3.5\" / 1.8\" w.c. NG, 10\" / 7.5\" w.c. LP — confirm against Service Facts"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"5.0 – 13.8\" w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11.0 – 13.8\" w.c."},{"label":"Orifice (sea level)","value":"Drill #45 natural, #56 propane — all models"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J"},{"label":"High altitude derate","value":"Above 2,000 ft: reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft; NG manifold re-check 3.0–3.7\" w.c.; LP always needs an orifice change at altitude"},{"label":"Max CO","value":"Not published by Trane — verify with a calibrated combustion analyzer against code limits; do not assume a fixed ppm number","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"see rating plate / Service Facts (guide defers to Service Facts)"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"see rating plate / Service Facts (rise too high → raise the airflow tap, too low → lower it)"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame current","value":"0.75–3.0 µA DC normal; fault logged below 0.5 µA DC","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride HSI; 37–70 Ω cold resistance at ~75°F"},{"label":"Status display","value":"7-segment LED on IFC (E#.# fault codes); Menu+Option held 5s clears last 6 faults"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout","value":"Manual-reset (red button); fixed trip temperature not published — OEM part only"},{"label":"Limit","value":"Auto-reset primary limit; trip setpoint stamped on the rating plate, not in the guide"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YP9C / CP9C / LP9C / TP9C (Modulating ECM)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96–98% AFUE modulating condensing furnace, 60–120 MBH, continuously modulates 35%–100% firing rate.","match":["York YP9C","YP9C","Coleman CP9C","CP9C","Luxaire LP9C","LP9C","TP9C","modulating 96","modulating 98"],"source":"Johnson Controls Ducted Systems Installation Manual 5750151-UIM-G-0423 (2023); York Technical Guide 538513-YTG-F-1016 (2016)","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure is NOT a fixed number — force TEST MODE first","body":"The valve modulates continuously 0.5–3.5\" w.c. (NG) as firing rate slides 35–100%. A snapshot reading means nothing. Hold the board TEST button 1 sec (rapid green LED), call for heat to lock 100% fire; press ERROR once for 35%, twice for 70%, three times back to 100% — set/verify pressure at each locked rate."},{"title":"Category IV — sealed combustion only, cannot be common-vented","body":"Dedicated 2\" PVC/CPVC/ABS or polypropylene intake+vent. Must NOT tie into a B-vent, chimney, or share with an atmospheric appliance — unlike the 80% TM8Y below (Category I)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural (max/min)","value":"3.5\" w.c. max / 0.5\" w.c. min (100%–35% modulation)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP","value":"10.0\" w.c. max / 1.6\" w.c. min","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.5–10.5\" w.c.; 7\" w.c. minimum to reach rated input","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"8.0–13.0\" w.c.; 11\" w.c. minimum to reach rated input"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Natural #45 factory (1030 Btu/cu ft); resize per altitude/rate table if needed"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Auto-derates via inducer pressure sensor; NFGC 4%/1,000 ft above 2,000 ft; factory orifice table covers to 10,000 ft"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"1.0\" w.c.; constant CFM to 0.6\", then -2% CFM per 0.1\" from 0.6–1.0\""},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"40–70°F (max input) / 20–50°F (min); 45–75°F / 25–55°F on 100C20 & 120D20 — confirm on rating plate"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"Normal ~3.7 µA DC; low-signal warning < 1.5 µA; lockout at 0.1 µA DC","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"HSI; York does not publish an ohm spec — verify by continuity / visible glow"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, burner assembly; numeric setpoint not published — OEM p/n only"},{"label":"Limit switch","value":"High-temp limit + vestibule temperature sensor; setpoint not published"},{"label":"Pressure sensing","value":"Pressure transducer (primary) + mechanical pressure switch (backup)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"TM8Y / TM8T / TM8V (Two-Stage 80%)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE two-stage Category I furnace, 60–120 MBH, independently adjustable high/low-fire gas valve.","match":["York TM8Y","TM8Y","TM8T","TM8V","TG8S","80% two-stage York"],"source":"Johnson Controls Unitary Products Installation Manual 5052632-UIM-D-0217 (2017). TM8Y figures; treat as representative of TM8T/TM8V — verify those against their own literature.","flags":[{"title":"Set HIGH fire before LOW fire — order matters","body":"Genuine two-stage valve with independent HI/LO regulators. To force high fire, jumper W1 to W2 to R on the board; pull the W2 jumper to drop to low fire and set that pressure. Setting low fire first throws off both."},{"title":"Flame-sense µA thresholds differ from the modulating YP9C board","body":"Normal is still ~3.7 µA DC, but the warning/lockout thresholds on THIS board are 0.28 µA / 0.16 µA — not the 1.5 µA / 0.1 µA figures on the YP9C-family modulating board. Don't cross-apply thresholds between the two platforms."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural (Hi/Lo fire)","value":"3.5\" w.c. high / 1.6\" w.c. low (sea level–7,999 ft, 1000 Btu/cu ft)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP (Hi/Lo fire)","value":"9.8\" w.c. high / 4.0\" w.c. low","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.5–10.5\" w.c.; 7\" w.c. minimum to reach rated input","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"8.0–13.0\" w.c.; 11\" w.c. minimum to reach rated input"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Natural #45 factory (1030 Btu/cu ft basis)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Factory set 0–5,000 ft; above that reset manifold pressure per altitude/heating-value tables (to 9,999 ft); pressure switches unchanged below 5,000 ft unless low-pressure inversions"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"blower data published to 1.0\" w.c.; do not exceed the rating-plate max"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"High fire 30–60°F (35–65 on 120C20) / Low fire 20–50°F — confirm on rating plate"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"Normal ~3.7 µA DC; low-signal warning 0.28 µA; lockout 0.16 µA DC","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"HSI, ~17 sec warm-up (27 on retry); resistance not published — verify continuity / visible glow"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, burner assembly; numeric setpoint not published — OEM p/n only"},{"label":"Limit switch","value":"Auto-reset high-temp limit near the gas valve; 5 trips in one call = 1-hr soft lockout (4 red flashes)"},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Separate 1st- and 2nd-stage mechanical pressure switches (not a transducer)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GMES80 / GCES80 (80% single-stage)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% single-stage non-condensing furnace, HSI ignition, White-Rodgers 36J22 valve","match":["GMES80","GCES80","AMES80","ACES80","VMES80","VCES80","GMS8","GCS8","GMEC80","GCEC80"],"source":"Goodman/Amana IOG-2021B (08/2019) — Installation Instructions for *MES80 & *CES80 Gas Furnace","flags":[{"title":"GMVC/GCVC 96% is a different platform","body":"Goodman/Amana's 96% two-stage GMVC96/GCVC96 share the Daikin DM96VC platform and its figures — use the Daikin DM96VC entry for those, not this one."},{"title":"HSI is fragile — 37-68 Ω is a room-temp check only","body":"Manual warns: touching the igniter element, rough handling, or vibration can damage it and cause premature failure. Qualified servicer only."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural","value":"3.5\" w.c. (range 3.2–3.8\")","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP","value":"10.0\" w.c. (range 9.7–10.3\"), with LPT-03 kit","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.5\" min / 10.0\" max w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11.0\" min / 13.0\" max w.c."},{"label":"Orifice, natural (0–5500 ft)","value":"#45"},{"label":"Orifice, LP (0–5500 ft)","value":"#55 (LPT-03 kit)"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J22, single-stage, slow-opening"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"No change 0–5500 ft. Above 5500 ft requires distributor pressure-switch + orifice kit — do NOT increase manifold pressure or re-orifice on your own below 5500 ft"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"see rating plate (model-specific)"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"see rating plate / spec sheet (model-specific)"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor resistance (room temp)","value":"37–68 Ω","key":true},{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"1–3 µA (published; clean with steel wool if signal drops too low)","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"Hot surface igniter (HSI)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset temperature sensor, no published numeric cutout"},{"label":"Rollout limit(s)","value":"Manual-reset temperature sensor, no published setpoint — do not jumper/reset without correcting the cause"},{"label":"Status display","value":"Single red diagnostic LED, blink-count codes 1–8, plus continuous-flash and steady-on states"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"R97V / R98V / R96V (Prestige EcoNet Modulating)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"97-98% AFUE modulating condensing furnace, DSI ignition, White-Rodgers servo digital-click modulating valve","match":["R97V","R98V","R96V","U97V","U98V","U96V","RGFG","RGGE","R98MV","R97MV","Prestige furnace"],"source":"Rheem G11-555 Rev.6 (R98V spec sheet) + White-Rodgers servo valve instructions 60-102787-05 / 92-106703-01","flags":[{"title":"Digital click-adjustment valve — one click at a time, min 5 sec","body":"Servo/digital valve, not a spring-loaded screw. More than one click before the control acknowledges (min 5 sec + a few to balance) and the valve will no longer adjust — return the wheel to where you started or power-cycle to re-home it."},{"title":"HIGH fire must be adjusted BEFORE low fire","body":"The doc states this explicitly and in bold. Adjusting low fire first gives an invalid calibration."},{"title":"Low-fire manifold is much lower than a two-stage — 0.56\" w.c.","body":"Modulating low-fire (40%) NG manifold is only 0.56\" w.c. — not the ~1.8\" you'd expect on a two-stage. Reading 0.56\" as 'underfired' here is a misdiagnosis."},{"title":"Altitude derate is 2%/1000 ft, not 4%","body":"Modulating furnaces use a 2% derate above 2000 ft with dedicated kits (RXGY-F53…-F57, model-specific). Don't apply the 80%-furnace 4%/1000 ft table to this valve."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, high fire (100%) NG","value":"3.5\" w.c. (±.3)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, low fire (40%) NG","value":"0.56\" w.c. (±.1)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, high fire (100%) LP","value":"10.0\" w.c. (±.5)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, low fire (40%) LP","value":"1.60\" w.c. (±.2)"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"5\" min (6–7\" recommended) / 10.5\" max w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11\" min / 13\" max w.c."},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers servo modulating valve, digital click adjustment (64 clicks per direction)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"2% per 1000 ft above 2000 ft — use model-specific RXGY-F5x kit, NOT the 4%/1000 ft table"},{"label":"Modulation range","value":"40–100% (2-stage tstat: 40/65/100%)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Min/Max external static","value":"model-dependent (e.g. .20–1.0\" w.c. on the 060) — confirm on rating plate/spec sheet"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"model-dependent (e.g. 40–70°F high fire on smaller models) — see rating plate"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"PlusOne Direct Spark Ignition (DSI) — not a hot-surface igniter"},{"label":"Ignitor resistance","value":"not published for DSI — verify spark output/behavior, not ohms"},{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"board carries its own flame-sense diagnostics and reports via fault code — no fixed µA spec; read the code","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout switch(es)","value":"manual-reset — no published numeric setpoint"},{"label":"Limit switch","value":"factory-set, non-adjustable — no published numeric cutout"},{"label":"Status display","value":"PlusOne dual 7-segment LED, fault codes 10–99; full table via the Rheem/Ruud contractor Bluetooth app on EcoNet models"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"R801 / R802 (80+ Bluetooth Communicating)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% single/two-stage non-condensing furnace, DSI ignition, White-Rodgers two-stage valve, Bluetooth diagnostics","match":["R801","R802","R802V","R802T","R801T","R801S","R801P","U801","U802","R80MP"],"source":"Rheem 92-24161-173-05 — Installation Instructions, 80+ Two-Stage/Single-Stage Bluetooth Communicating Gas Furnaces","flags":[{"title":"Two-stage valve numbers differ from the modulating R97V/R98V","body":"Conventional two-stage White-Rodgers valve: NG high fire 3.5\"/low fire 1.8\" w.c. Do not confuse with the R97V/R98V modulating valve's 0.56\" low-fire spec — not interchangeable."},{"title":"0.8\" w.c. is TOTAL system static, not furnace-only max ESP","body":"The manual limits total static of the air distribution system (coil + filter + zoning + ductwork) to 0.8\" w.c. — that is not the same as a model-specific furnace max ESP rating."},{"title":"Direct spark ignition, not hot-surface","body":"Spark transformer provides ≥12 kV at ~60 Hz. No ohms/resistance spec applies — testing for igniter resistance is the wrong diagnostic on this furnace."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, NG high fire / single-stage","value":"3.5\" w.c. (±.3)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, NG low fire (two-stage)","value":"1.8\" w.c. (±.1)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP high fire / single-stage","value":"10.0\" w.c. (±.5)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP low fire (two-stage)","value":"4.9\" w.c. (±.2)"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"5\" min (6–7\" recommended) / 10.5\" max w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11\" min / 13\" max w.c."},{"label":"Orifice (sea level, 1050 Btu/ft³ NG)","value":"#42"},{"label":"Orifice, LP (0–2000 ft)","value":"#54"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 24V two-stage, slow-opening (2–3 sec to fully open)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"4% per 1000 ft above 2000 ft — see the NFGC-derived table in the manual; do NOT use it for any 90+ modulating model"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max total system static","value":"0.8\" w.c. (includes coil, filter, zoning, ductwork)"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"per rating plate; field-adjustable ~+7°F or ~+12°F via dip switches/app"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"Direct Spark Ignition (DSI)"},{"label":"Spark transformer output","value":"minimum 12 kV @ ~60 Hz"},{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"board carries its own flame-sense diagnostics (fault code A126_F etc.) — no fixed µA spec; read the code","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout switch(es) (MRLC)","value":"manual-reset — no published numeric setpoint"},{"label":"Limit control (HALC)","value":"factory-set, non-adjustable — no published numeric cutout"},{"label":"Status display","value":"Red diagnostic LED, fault code flashed digit-by-digit; full descriptions via the Bluetooth contractor app"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SLP98V (SLP98UHV, Signature modulating)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"98%+ AFUE modulating (35-100%) variable-speed furnace, SureLight A92 control; manifold pressure sweeps a range by firing rate, not a fixed setpoint.","match":["SLP98V","SLP98","SLP98UH","SLP98UHV","SLP98UH070XV36B","SLP98UH090XV48C","SLP98UH090XV60C","SLP98UH110XV60C","SLP98UH135XV60D","SLP98-070","SLP98-090","SLP98-110","SLP98-135"],"source":"Lennox Corp. 1029-L7 SLP98UHV Service Literature (rev. 10-2020)","flags":[{"title":"Lock the firing rate before reading manifold pressure","body":"Hold the diagnostic button until the LED shows a solid dash (Field Test Mode). Jumper R to W1 = low fire (35%), R to W1+W2 = high fire (100%), R to W2 = mid fire. All safeties stay live — it does not bypass them."},{"title":"Manifold pressure is a DIFFERENTIAL reading, not single-port","body":"The burner box runs under negative pressure, so gas-valve output is referenced to burner-box pressure. Put the gauge '+' on the manifold tap and '-' into a tee on the gas-valve regulator vent hose (Lennox kit 10L34). A single-port reading against room air reads wrong on this valve."},{"title":"Low-fire manifold is far lower than a two-stage's low fire","body":"NG low fire is only 0.4-0.95 in. w.c. (vs 3.0-3.8 at high fire). Techs used to G51/G61 two-stage low-fire won't recognize a healthy reading here."},{"title":"Burner orifice size is not published","body":"Described only as factory-set, matched to burner input. Order the correct NG or LP kit (65W77 NG<->LP), don't guess a drill size."},{"title":"Prime the condensate trap before first fire","body":"Pour 10 fl oz (300 mL) into the trap or run the 3-cycle purge. An unprimed trap makes the low-fire pressure switch fail to prove and reads like a bad switch."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board A92 (SureLight variable-capacity)","value":"Normal >= 2.6 µA / Low <= 2.5 µA / Dropout 1.1 µA","key":true},{"label":"How to read","value":"Field Test Mode shows live flame-signal µA on the 7-segment LED at a locked firing rate"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural (low fire 35%)","value":"0.4 - 0.95 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, natural (high fire 100%)","value":"3.0 - 3.8 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP (low / high)","value":"1.2 - 2.8 in. w.c. / 9.1 - 10.5 in. w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.5 - 10.5 in. w.c. at the gas connection, firing at max rate"},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11.0 - 13.0 in. w.c."},{"label":"Orifice, burner","value":"see rating plate - not published; factory-matched, order the correct NG/LP kit"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Variable-capacity modulating, internally redundant; brand/PN not published - replace with same type"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.8 in. w.c. heating / 1.0 in. w.c. cooling","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"see rating plate - varies by model (e.g. 35-65°F low / 50-80°F high on most)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout (S47, x2)","value":"N.C. manual-reset, opens 210°F, not adjustable","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit (S10)","value":"factory-set, not adjustable; trip temp not published - see rating plate"},{"label":"Pressure switch (high / low fire)","value":"1.00 ± 0.05 / 0.25 ± 0.05 in. w.c. (0-7,500 ft)"},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"SureLight silicon-nitride HSI, 39 - 70 Ω cold"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"No manifold/orifice change to 10,000 ft. High-altitude pressure-switch kit 14T65 only at 7,501-10,000 ft. LP kit 65W77 at all altitudes."}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SLP99V (SLP99UHV, Signature modulating)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"99% AFUE modulating variable-speed furnace, SLP98V's successor - same figures EXCEPT the -090-60C submodel has its own manifold/pressure-switch/altitude numbers.","match":["SLP99V","SLP99","SLP99UH","SLP99UHV","SLP99UH070XV36B","SLP99UH090XV48C","SLP99UH090XV60C","SLP99UH110XV60C","SLP99UH135XV60D","SLP99-070","SLP99-090","SLP99-110","SLP99-135"],"source":"Lennox Corp. 100001 SLP99UHV Service Literature (10/2020)","flags":[{"title":"The -090-60C submodel is the outlier - do not apply the line's numbers to it","body":"SLP99UH090V60C has its own low-fire manifold (0.30-0.85 in. w.c. NG, not 0.4-0.95), its own low-fire pressure-switch setpoint (0.15 ± 0.05, not 0.25 ± 0.05), and its own CO2 targets. Confirm the full model number before comparing against a spec for a different 090."},{"title":"-090-60C is the ONLY model in either line needing an altitude orifice change","value":"","body":"Every other SLP98V/SLP99V model needs no manifold/orifice change to 10,000 ft. The -09060C needs a burner-orifice change at 4,501-10,000 ft (kits 20A88/20A89) and its own high-altitude pressure-switch kit 20A87 (vs 14T65 for the rest)."},{"title":"Lock the firing rate before reading manifold pressure","body":"Same Field Test Mode as SLP98V: hold the diagnostic button to a solid dash, then R-W1 (low), R-W1+W2 (high), R-W2 (mid). Safeties stay live."},{"title":"Manifold pressure is a DIFFERENTIAL reading","body":"Same negative-pressure burner box - '+' on the manifold tap, '-' into the gas-valve regulator vent-hose tee (kit 10L34), not atmosphere."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board A92 (SureLight variable-capacity)","value":"Normal >= 2.6 µA / Low <= 2.5 µA / Dropout 1.1 µA","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, natural low fire (all EXCEPT -09060C)","value":"0.4 - 0.95 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, natural low fire (-09060C only)","value":"0.30 - 0.85 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, natural high fire (all)","value":"3.0 - 3.8 in. w.c."},{"label":"Manifold, LP (low / high)","value":"1.2 - 2.8 in. w.c. / 9.1 - 10.5 in. w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural / LP","value":"4.5 - 10.5 / 11.0 - 13.0 in. w.c."},{"label":"Orifice, burner","value":"see rating plate - not published; order the correct kit (65W77 general; 20A26/20A88/20A89 for -09060C)"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Variable-capacity modulating, internally redundant; brand/PN not published"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.8 in. w.c. heating / 1.0 in. w.c. cooling","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"see rating plate - model-specific (e.g. 25-55°F low on 090-60C, 35-65°F low on most others)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout (S47, x2)","value":"N.C. manual-reset, opens 210°F, not adjustable","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit (S10)","value":"factory-set, not adjustable; trip temp not published - see rating plate"},{"label":"Pressure switch high fire (all)","value":"1.00 ± 0.05 in. w.c. (0-7,500 ft)"},{"label":"Pressure switch low fire (all / -09060C)","value":"0.25 ± 0.05 / 0.15 ± 0.05 in. w.c. (0-7,500 ft)"},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"SureLight silicon-nitride HSI, 39 - 70 Ω cold"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"No change to 10,000 ft for all EXCEPT -09060C (burner orifice change at 4,501-10,000 ft). HA pressure-switch kit: 14T65 all models except -09060C (20A87)."}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"25VNA4 (Infinity® 24 with Greenspeed® Intelligence)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Variable-speed inverter-driven heat pump, 2-5 tons, R-410A (Puron). Fully communicating (Infinity Control) with an electronic expansion valve for heating metering and UI-guided subcooling charging.","match":["25VNA4","25VNA","Infinity Greenspeed","Infinity 24 heat pump","280A","280ANV","Bryant Evolution Extreme"],"source":"25VNA4 Installation Instructions, Carrier Corp. (shareddocs.com/hvac)","flags":[{"title":"Never remove the inverter cover","body":"Inverter/VFD components underneath are not field-serviceable. The manual explicitly warns the cover should NEVER be removed, and to verify zero voltage at the inverter connections shown on the cover before any nearby work."},{"title":"No low-pressure switch to hunt for","body":"This unit has no physical low-pressure switch. Suction and discharge pressure transducers (P1/P2, 0-620 psig) feed the PCM instead. If low charge or restricted airflow is suspected, work the UI fault/diagnostic log rather than looking for an LPS lead to jump."},{"title":"EXV must be opened before evacuating for service","body":"The heating EXV is a true metering device, not a fixed orifice — if it's closed you cannot pull an effective vacuum on the system. Use the User Interface's EXV-open service function first (per the manual's evacuation procedure)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":true},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Outdoor EXV-H for heating mode; indoor hard-shutoff Puron TXV, matched to outdoor unit, for cooling mode","key":true},{"label":"Vapor injection EXV","value":"Secondary EXV-VI on some sizes for the vapor-injection circuit, driven closed except in high-ambient cooling / low-ambient heating efficiency mode"},{"label":"Compressor type","value":"Variable-speed inverter — rotary on some sizes, scroll on others (see rating plate); operates only on its factory-matched inverter"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Time/temperature, UI-selected interval: 30/60/90/120 min or AUTO (default AUTO)"},{"label":"Defrost initiate","value":"Compressor run-time accumulates only while outdoor coil temp is below 35°F; defrost begins once accumulated time reaches the selected interval"},{"label":"Defrost terminate","value":"Outdoor coil temp reaches a model/OAT-dependent termination point, or max defrost time expires, whichever comes first"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling mode (standard Carrier/Bryant convention). On this communicating system the PCM drives it directly — there is no thermostat O terminal to check with a meter","key":true}]},{"title":"Pressure Protection & Low-Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 670 ±10 psig, closes at 470 ±25 psig","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Not fitted — see suction/discharge transducer note above","key":true},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling lockout","value":"0°F with Low Ambient enabled in the Infinity Control UI; no accessory kit required"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Standard; intelligently controlled by the PCM and operates even without an indoor unit/UI installed"}]},{"title":"Charging & Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"UI-guided subcooling charge with target subcooling shown on-screen; do not use the subcooling method outside 65-105°F outdoor temperature"},{"label":"Min circuit ampacity","value":"See rating plate"},{"label":"Status display","value":"5x7 LED matrix plus amber/green status LEDs on the PCM. Active fault codes are stored and recallable from memory (survives a power loss) via the forced-defrost pins"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Standard demand-defrost boards (HK32EA/HK61EA-series, CEPL13xxxx — same family used on Bryant and ICP/Heil/Tempstar). Remove the small plastic cap over the 2-pin 'Forced Defrost' / 'Speed-Up' (TP1/TP2) test header and short the pins with a jumper wire. Momentarily short-and-release once first to clear any compressor anti-short-cycle delay, then re-short and HOLD 5+ seconds — board commands defrost. You should hear the reversing valve shift and see the outdoor fan stop; verify 24V C-to-W2 with a meter. Pull the jumper the instant the valve shifts or the board will hold in speed-up (60x) mode and cycle continuously — don't leave it shorted. If the valve doesn't shift within ~10 sec of the sustained short, board or valve is suspect. Bryant boards are identical; confirm exact pin silkscreen against the installed board revision, since older CEPL revisions label the header 'TEST' and only speed timing rather than instant-force. Source: Carrier/HVAC-Talk field discussion + HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board walkthrough (hvac-talk.com thread 993331; hvactrainingsolutions.net/heat-pump-defrost-control-boards-step-step)."},{"label":"Infinity communicating","value":"On the Infinity touch thermostat, enter the installer 'Checkout' diagnostic (Menu > Setups > Advanced, press and hold Advanced ~10 sec until Install/Service menu appears), then step through the heat pump Checkout routine, which commands the outdoor unit into defrost as part of the sequence. NOT independently re-verified against a current Infinity outdoor-unit Installation Instructions manual for this session, so confirm the exact menu path on the specific control/thermostat model in front of you before relying on it — menu wording has changed across Infinity System Control generations. The physical 2-pin Forced Defrost header on the outdoor board (same as non-comm procedure above) also still works on Infinity outdoor units independent of the thermostat. Source: Carrier documentation as summarized by Hunker 'How To Enter Diagnostic Mode On A Carrier Infinity Thermostat' and JustAnswer HVAC Q&A — treat menu path as a starting point, not gospel."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Coil temperature sensor (DFT) must read cold — Carrier defrost boards generally need the coil sensor closed (roughly below freezing, board-dependent ~30±3°F) before a forced defrost will actually initiate/hold; forcing on a warm coil may not take. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux/W2 heat may energize — a burst of cold air from supply registers is normal, not a fault. Warn occupants if testing with the system live."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"25HCB6 (Performance™ 16 2-Stage Heat Pump) / Bryant 286B, 289B (Evolution® Series 2-Stage)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Modulated 2-stage scroll heat pump, 2-5 tons, R-410A (Puron). Same compressor/board architecture is sold as Carrier 25HCB6 and as Bryant 286B (PSC outdoor fan) / 289B (ECM outdoor fan).","match":["25HCB6","286B","286BNA","289B","289BNA","Performance 16 heat pump","Evolution series 2-stage"],"source":"25HCB6 Installation Instructions (Catalog No. 25HCB6-3SI, Ed. 03/13), Carrier Corp.; 286B/289B Evolution Series Installation Instructions, Bryant Heating & Cooling Systems","flags":[{"title":"Two different defrost boards share these model names","body":"The 25HCB6 manual (Ed. 03/13) documents an older bulb-type defrost thermostat clipped to a coil stub tube, with fixed dip-switch intervals only (no AUTO option). The Bryant 286B/289B manual documents a newer thermistor (OCT)-based board with an AUTO defrost option. Confirm which board is actually in the unit before assuming AUTO exists, or looking for a stub-tube thermostat that isn't there."},{"title":"Charge is set and checked in HIGH stage only","body":"Both manuals specify the factory charge and rating-plate subcooling target apply to high-stage operation. Checking subcooling while the compressor is running low-stage will read falsely low — force high stage before trusting the number."},{"title":"Replacement control board needs the model plug moved over","body":"On 286B/289B, a replacement (RCD) control board carries no model/serial data. If the board is swapped, the original model plug must be transferred to the new board or the unit will not identify/operate correctly."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":true},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Hard-shutoff Puron TXV required on all indoor coils — do not use an R-22 TXV or a piston/cap-tube indoor coil","key":true},{"label":"Compressor type","value":"Modulated 2-stage scroll; single-speed 2-pole (3500 RPM) motor with internal DC-solenoid unloader — unloaded step is ~67% capacity (~75% cooling/heating capacity at the indoor coil), 100% when loaded"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type (25HCB6 board)","value":"Time/temperature via a bulb-type defrost thermostat on a coil stub tube; field dip-switch interval 30/60/90/120 min, factory default 90 min; terminates on thermostat open or after 10 min max"},{"label":"Defrost type (286B/289B board)","value":"Time/temperature via a coil thermistor (OCT); interval 30/60/90/120 min or AUTO, set by dip switch or Evolution UI; defrost demand = coil at or below 32°F for 4 min; terminates at 65°F coil temp or 10 min max"},{"label":"Quiet Shift-2","value":"Field-selectable dip switch (factory OFF) that delays the compressor roughly 60-70 seconds around defrost start/end to reduce reversing-valve noise"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling mode — O terminal is powered on for a cooling call","key":true}]},{"title":"Pressure Protection & Low-Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switches","value":"Fitted in series with the Y signal to the contactor for protection; exact cutout/cutin psig values are not published in this service literature — see rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Compressor internal relief (IPR)","value":"Vents discharge gas to the compressor shell at a 550-625 psi suction/discharge differential — not a field-serviceable switch"},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling lockout","value":"55°F standard; down to 0°F with a low-ambient accessory kit (25HCB6), or via Evolution Control low-ambient enable on 286B/289B (kit-free — see accessory usage table)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Standard on all sizes. On 286B/289B: energized when compressor is off and ambient is below 42°F; 30-min delay before energizing between 42-65°F; stays de-energized above 65°F"}]},{"title":"Charging & Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling method, high stage only; factory-charged for 15 ft of lineset, adjust 0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 in. liquid line above/below that; favorable conditions 70-100°F OAT / 70-80°F IAT"},{"label":"Min circuit ampacity","value":"See rating plate"},{"label":"Status display","value":"25HCB6 defrost board: no status LED, dip switches/forced-defrost pins only. 286B/289B: amber STATUS + green COMM LED, flash-code protocol (short flashes = 1st digit, long flashes = 2nd digit)"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Standard demand-defrost boards (HK32EA/HK61EA-series, CEPL13xxxx — same family used on Bryant and ICP/Heil/Tempstar). Remove the small plastic cap over the 2-pin 'Forced Defrost' / 'Speed-Up' (TP1/TP2) test header and short the pins with a jumper wire. Momentarily short-and-release once first to clear any compressor anti-short-cycle delay, then re-short and HOLD 5+ seconds — board commands defrost. You should hear the reversing valve shift and see the outdoor fan stop; verify 24V C-to-W2 with a meter. Pull the jumper the instant the valve shifts or the board will hold in speed-up (60x) mode and cycle continuously — don't leave it shorted. If the valve doesn't shift within ~10 sec of the sustained short, board or valve is suspect. Bryant boards are identical; confirm exact pin silkscreen against the installed board revision, since older CEPL revisions label the header 'TEST' and only speed timing rather than instant-force. Source: Carrier/HVAC-Talk field discussion + HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board walkthrough (hvac-talk.com thread 993331; hvactrainingsolutions.net/heat-pump-defrost-control-boards-step-step)."},{"label":"Infinity communicating","value":"On the Infinity touch thermostat, enter the installer 'Checkout' diagnostic (Menu > Setups > Advanced, press and hold Advanced ~10 sec until Install/Service menu appears), then step through the heat pump Checkout routine, which commands the outdoor unit into defrost as part of the sequence. NOT independently re-verified against a current Infinity outdoor-unit Installation Instructions manual for this session, so confirm the exact menu path on the specific control/thermostat model in front of you before relying on it — menu wording has changed across Infinity System Control generations. The physical 2-pin Forced Defrost header on the outdoor board (same as non-comm procedure above) also still works on Infinity outdoor units independent of the thermostat. Source: Carrier documentation as summarized by Hunker 'How To Enter Diagnostic Mode On A Carrier Infinity Thermostat' and JustAnswer HVAC Q&A — treat menu path as a starting point, not gospel."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Coil temperature sensor (DFT) must read cold — Carrier defrost boards generally need the coil sensor closed (roughly below freezing, board-dependent ~30±3°F) before a forced defrost will actually initiate/hold; forcing on a warm coil may not take. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux/W2 heat may energize — a burst of cold air from supply registers is normal, not a fault. Warn occupants if testing with the system live."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FE4A / FE5A (Infinity® Communicating Fan Coil)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Communicating variable-speed fan coil for Puron systems, sizes 002-006 (roughly 1.5-5 ton). Airflow is commanded continuously by the Infinity/Evolution User Interface rather than set with field dip switches.","match":["FE4A","FE5A","FE4ANF","FE4CNF","Infinity fan coil","communicating fan coil"],"source":"FE4A/FE5A Communicating Fan Coil Installation Instructions, Form IM-FE4A-01, Catalog No. 63FE-4A0, Carrier Corp./CAC-BDP","flags":[{"title":"Will not run on a common thermostat","body":"This is a communicating-only fan coil. Wiring a standard R/Y/O/W/G thermostat to it directly does nothing except trigger emergency mode after the 2-minute communications timeout (Status Code 16). Don't troubleshoot it like a conventional non-communicating fan coil."},{"title":"Shallow traps are a documented callback generator","body":"The install manual explicitly illustrates an insufficient shallow trap next to the correct deep trap, and calls out standard P-traps as inadequate. Both the primary AND secondary drain need a properly sized trap, not just the primary."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"ECM, communicating — speed is commanded continuously by the User Interface; no CFM dip switches in normal operation","key":true},{"label":"Nominal airflow","value":"350 CFM/ton nominal; the UI adjusts actual airflow from indoor/outdoor temperature and humidity data","key":true},{"label":"Non-communicating fallback","value":"If communications fail for more than 2 minutes (Status Code 16), the unit runs emergency heat/cool only, via common R, Y, O, W, C thermostat terminals"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"See rating plate / Product Data — not published in this Installation Instructions document"}]},{"title":"Metering & Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Indoor TXV; must be a Puron TXV — an existing R-22 TXV must be changed out","key":true},{"label":"Electric heat kit range","value":"Factory-authorized, field-installed kits from 5-30 kW; must match the rating-plate-approved kit list"},{"label":"Heat-stage airflow interlock","value":"The fan coil overrides requested airflow up to the published minimum CFM for the installed heater kW whenever electric heat is commanded (see the unit's Airflow Delivery Chart)"}]},{"title":"Drain & Filter","rows":[{"label":"Drain connections","value":"Primary + secondary 3/4 in. FPT — both must be trapped; shallow or standard P-traps are explicitly called out as insufficient","key":true},{"label":"Filter","value":"Factory filter kits (12-pack): KFAFK0212MED (size 002), KFAFK0312LRG (003/005), KFAFK0412XXL (006)"},{"label":"Float switch","value":"Not fitted standard — a field-supplied secondary condensate pan/line is required by code where the unit sits above finished living space"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Status LED","value":"Amber STATUS + green COMM + amber MOTOR LED on the control board; same flash-code protocol as the outdoor unit (short flashes = 1st digit, long flashes = 2nd digit)"},{"label":"Common fault codes","value":"16 = system communication fault, 25 = motor/model size mismatch, 26 = invalid heater ID resistor, 41 = blower motor fault, 46 = brownout (secondary voltage below 15 VAC for over 4 sec)"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FX4D (Comfort™/Legacy™ Line Fan Coil) — same platform sold as Bryant FB4C / FX4DNF","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Non-communicating, multi-speed ECM fan coil with tap/dip-switch airflow selection, sizes 019-061. The same physical unit is also sold under the Bryant FB4C and FX4DNF badges.","match":["FX4D","FX4DNF","FB4C","FB4CNF","PF4"],"source":"FB4, FE4, FF1E, FH4, FV4, FX4, PF4, FFM Service and Maintenance Instructions, Carrier Corp.","flags":[{"title":"\"ECM\" badge doesn't mean variable-speed here","body":"The ECM2.3/ECM5.0 motors used in this platform are tap-selected multi-speed motors, not the continuously variable, UI-commanded ECM3.0 used in communicating fan coils like the FE4A. Don't expect Infinity-style auto-adjusting airflow behavior out of an FX4D/FB4C."},{"title":"Sequencer wiring uses first-on/last-off logic","body":"On multi-stage electric heat, sequencer/relay No. 1 is deliberately wired to be first energized and last de-energized, specifically to guarantee the blower brackets every heater element. If the blower cuts out before the heaters do, suspect sequencer wiring before the fan control board."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Multi-speed ECM (ECM2.3 or ECM5.0) with Easy Select board — a fixed-tap motor, not a fully modulating one","key":true},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"AC/HP SIZE + CFM ADJUST dip switches on the Easy Select board pick the tap: HI = 400 CFM/ton, NOM = 350 CFM/ton, LO = 315 CFM/ton (heat-pump comfort mode runs the LO/315 CFM/ton tap)","key":true},{"label":"Electric-heat-only fallback","value":"With electric heat and no heat pump/AC size selected, the motor slows to roughly 213 CFM/ton on a heat call"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"See rating plate / Product Data — not published in this service manual"}]},{"title":"Metering & Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory hard-shutoff (HSO) bi-flow TXV, matched to the outdoor unit; some sister models in this family ship with a piston — verify against the outdoor unit's Puron TXV requirement","key":true},{"label":"Electric heat staging","value":"Mechanical time-delay sequencers/relays staged off W2/W3; first-on/last-off logic keeps the blower running until the last heater element drops out"}]},{"title":"Drain & Filter","rows":[{"label":"Drain connections","value":"Single condensate drain pan/tube; inspect and flush each cooling season, clear restrictions with high-pressure water"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Washable factory filter — rinse with mild detergent, no oiling/coating; replace/clean monthly or as needed"},{"label":"Float switch","value":"Not called out in this service manual — treat as not fitted standard; confirm local code requirement for a field-added float switch or secondary pan"}]},{"title":"Coil","rows":[{"label":"Coil material","value":"Aluminum coil; field repair procedure is documented in the service manual. Do not use caustic drain cleaners near the coil — it will destroy it"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XP25","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Variable-capacity, iComfort Wi-Fi communicating heat pump (Dave Lennox Signature Collection), 2-5 tons, R-410A, check/expansion valve metering.","match":["XP25","EL18XPV","variable capacity","variable speed","inverter","communicating","icomfort","dave lennox signature","heat pump"],"source":"Lennox XP25 Installation Instructions, Corp. 507005-01 (7/2018), LennoxPros.com","flags":[{"title":"R-410A vs R-454B - verify the nameplate","body":"This XP25 literature (Corp. 507005-01, 7/2018) covers HFC-410A units. Lennox's newer SL25KCV variable-capacity platform (the successor to the SL25XPV, which is itself R-410A; same iComfort/S40 communicating architecture and outdoor-control board family) has since moved to R-454B (mildly flammable A2L refrigerant) per SL25KCV Installation Instructions 508447-01 (6/2025). Always confirm refrigerant off the actual nameplate before connecting gauges - R-454B calls for A2L-rated hoses/gauges (0-800 psig high side), nitrogen-purge leak searching, and no open-flame leak detection."},{"title":"Fixed pressure-switch and low-ambient lockout figures not published here","body":"The XP25 Installation Instructions do not list fixed HI-PS/LO-PS trip-reset psig values or a low-ambient cooling lockout temperature - the outdoor control reads pressure transducers rather than simple mechanical switches. For those figures, or for detailed alarm/fault codes, consult the XP25 Installation and Service Procedures manual (Corp. 1252-L11) or the unit's charging/alarm label."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"HFC-410A only","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Field-installed check/expansion valve (ordered separately per AHRI match-up)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Factory charge basis","value":"Charged for 15 ft. line set; weigh-in adjust per charging label","key":"factory_charge"},{"label":"Max line set","value":"150 ft. linear / 180 ft. equivalent length; over 150 ft. not recommended","key":"max_line_set"},{"label":"Suction trap","value":"Required at bottom of suction riser when outdoor unit is 5-60 ft. above indoor unit","key":"suction_trap"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost trigger","value":"Frost forms on outdoor coil below 45°F (7°C) ambient during heating","key":"defrost_trigger"},{"label":"Defrost cycle length","value":"Typically 5-15 minutes per cycle; control self-calibrates at start and after each defrost","key":"defrost_length"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Energized = cooling; de-energized = heating (also energized briefly during defrost to run the cycle in cooling)","key":"rv_energized_mode"},{"label":"Charge/100% capacity mode","value":"Forced via S40/iComfort thermostat test mode (Cooling - Maximum Rate Test) or Lennox Dealer Setup App for charging and commissioning","key":"charge_mode"}]},{"title":"Pressures & Lockouts","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switch trip-reset psig","value":"See rating plate / Corp. 1252-L11 Service Procedures (unit uses pressure transducers, not published fixed switch setpoints)","key":"pressure_switch"},{"label":"Low ambient compressor lockout","value":"See rating plate","key":"low_ambient_lockout"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Present; if equipped and outdoor ambient is below 60°F, energize 24 hrs before startup to prevent compressor slugging","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Compressor vacuum protector","value":"Some scroll compressors unload (hiss) below 20 psig suction and reset above 40 psig - this is normal, do NOT replace the compressor for this","key":"vacuum_protector"}]},{"title":"Charging & Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh-in for initial charge, then verify with subcooling method","key":"charging_method"},{"label":"Thermostat offset for charging","value":"Set back 5°F (cooling) or up 5°F (heating) from setpoint so system runs at 100% capacity","key":"charging_offset"},{"label":"Target subcool/approach","value":"See rating plate / unit charging label (coil-match-up specific, no single published number)","key":"target_subcool"},{"label":"Diagnostics","value":"7-segment display + push button on outdoor control shows running capacity and alarm codes; full code list in Corp. 1252-L11","key":"diagnostics"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Lennox Demand Defrost Control boards have a 2-pin 'TEST' header. With the unit running a heating call, jumper the TEST pins for 2–5 seconds then remove — this forces one defrost event. If the jumper stays on TEST longer than 5 seconds, the control ignores it and reverts to normal operation (won't force). To repeat the test, remove the jumper for at least 1 second before reapplying. Source: Lennox heat pump unit service literature (tech.lennoxintl.com/.../507633-01.pdf, 'Demand Defrost Control' section) and corroborating field write-ups."},{"label":"iComfort communicating","value":"From the iComfort Touch/S30 installer Tests screen (Installer program > Tests), select the test set and press Start; the built-in defrost test is a short, self-terminating routine (~30 seconds) distinct from the other 30-minute component tests, per the iComfort Touch Setup manual's troubleshooting/tests section. Exact on-screen menu wording for current S30 firmware not independently re-verified this session — confirm live on the thermostat before using with a customer present. Source: Lennox iComfort Touch Setup Manual, 'Troubleshooting Tips' (lennox.com/dA/3c5cd2b3e6/Lennox_icomfortTouch_Manual.pdf, p.31 via ManualsLib)."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Outdoor coil sensor must be cold enough to be below the board's defrost cut-in (near/below freezing) for the forced cycle to actually engage and hold — on a warm coil the TEST short may be ignored or terminate immediately. Expect the reversing valve to shift to cooling and the outdoor fan to stop when defrost engages; a cold-air burst from supply registers during the test is normal."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XP16","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Two-stage, non-communicating heat pump (Elite Series), R-410A, check/expansion valve metering, demand defrost board - figures below are BOARD-specific.","match":["XP16","EL16XP1","ML14XP1","XP14","XP15","HPXA16","two-stage","non-communicating","elite series","heat pump"],"source":"Lennox XP16 Series Installation Instructions, Corp. 506420-01 (12/09); Lennox Replacement Defrost Control, Corp. 507633-01 (7/2016), LennoxPros.com","flags":[{"title":"Defrost termination temp is BOARD-specific","body":"This unit (and related HPXA/XP/SPB families) can carry any of five demand-defrost control boards: 10M8901, 60L3901, 46M8201, 56M8501, or 100135. Factory-shunt defrost termination temperature differs by board family - 90°F on the four older boards, 50°F on the 100135 board. If the shunt is missing, the default also differs (100°F vs 90°F respectively). Confirm the board part number silkscreened on the board before reading the termination-temperature shunt position. Source: Corp. 507633-01."},{"title":"Diagnostic LED codes differ by board","body":"LED fault patterns are NOT interchangeable across board families. The older 10M8901/60L3901/46M8201/56M8501 boards use two red LEDs with one fault-code table; the 100135 board uses a red+green pair with a different, more granular table (it adds discharge-line-temperature fault/lockout codes the older boards don't have). Match the LED behavior to the correct board before troubleshooting."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A only","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Field-installed check/expansion valve (approved for R-410A, ordered separately) - expansion-valve systems only, not for fixed-orifice","key":"metering"},{"label":"Filter drier","value":"Large-capacity biflow, HFC-410A rated only","key":"filter_drier"}]},{"title":"Defrost System (board-specific)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost termination temp - 10M8901/60L3901/46M8201/56M8501 boards","value":"Selectable 70/80/90/100°F; factory shunt set at 90°F; default 100°F if shunt missing","key":"defrost_term_old_boards"},{"label":"Defrost termination temp - 100135 board","value":"Selectable 50/70/90/100°F; factory shunt set at 50°F; default 90°F if shunt missing","key":"defrost_term_100135"},{"label":"Max defrost time","value":"14 minutes; if terminated by time without clearing coil (35°F for 4 min), unit falls back to 30-minute Time/Temp mode","key":"max_defrost_time"},{"label":"Demand defrost trigger","value":"Compressor run > 30 min AND coil-vs-ambient differential exceeds calibrated threshold, OR 6 hrs heating runtime with coil below 35°F (2°C)","key":"demand_defrost_trigger"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Energized = cooling; de-energized = heating. Energized (and outdoor fan off) during the defrost cycle to run briefly in cooling","key":"rv_energized_mode"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches & Lockouts","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch (auto reset)","value":"Trip at 590 psig, reset at 418 psig","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch (auto reset)","value":"Trip at 25 psig, reset at 40 psig","key":"lp_switch"},{"label":"Pressure-switch lockout strikes","value":"5-strike (56M8501, 100135 boards) or 3-strike (10M8901, 60L3901, 46M8201 boards) per single Y1 demand; reset by cycling 24V power or shorting TEST pins 1-2 sec","key":"lockout_strikes"},{"label":"Second-stage heating lock-in ambient","value":"Default 40°F (adjustable 40/45/50/55°F via P3 jumper); second stage drops out 5°F above selected lock-in temp","key":"second_stage_lockin"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling lockout","value":"See rating plate (not published in Corp. 506420-01)","key":"low_ambient_lockout"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Present; energize 24 hrs before unit start-up if equipped, to prevent compressor slugging","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh-in for initial charge (nameplate amount + line-set length adjustment + indoor-coil-match-up add charge), then verify with subcooling","key":"charging_method"},{"label":"Target subcooling","value":"See rating plate / unit charging sticker - coil-match-up specific (Tables 3-6, Corp. 506420-01), no single universal value","key":"target_subcool"},{"label":"Charging condition","value":"Second-stage (high-capacity) operation: cooling mode above 60°F ambient (70-80°F return air), heating mode below 60°F ambient (65-75°F return air)","key":"charging_condition"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Lennox Demand Defrost Control boards have a 2-pin 'TEST' header. With the unit running a heating call, jumper the TEST pins for 2–5 seconds then remove — this forces one defrost event. If the jumper stays on TEST longer than 5 seconds, the control ignores it and reverts to normal operation (won't force). To repeat the test, remove the jumper for at least 1 second before reapplying. Source: Lennox heat pump unit service literature (tech.lennoxintl.com/.../507633-01.pdf, 'Demand Defrost Control' section) and corroborating field write-ups."},{"label":"iComfort communicating","value":"From the iComfort Touch/S30 installer Tests screen (Installer program > Tests), select the test set and press Start; the built-in defrost test is a short, self-terminating routine (~30 seconds) distinct from the other 30-minute component tests, per the iComfort Touch Setup manual's troubleshooting/tests section. Exact on-screen menu wording for current S30 firmware not independently re-verified this session — confirm live on the thermostat before using with a customer present. Source: Lennox iComfort Touch Setup Manual, 'Troubleshooting Tips' (lennox.com/dA/3c5cd2b3e6/Lennox_icomfortTouch_Manual.pdf, p.31 via ManualsLib)."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Outdoor coil sensor must be cold enough to be below the board's defrost cut-in (near/below freezing) for the forced cycle to actually engage and hold — on a warm coil the TEST short may be ignored or terminate immediately. Expect the reversing valve to shift to cooling and the outdoor fan to stop when defrost engages; a cold-air burst from supply registers during the test is normal."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBA38MV","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position variable-speed air handler (Dave Lennox Signature Collection), 1.5-5 tons, R-410A, ECM blower, iComfort communicating control, max 0.80 in. w.g. ESP.","match":["CBA38MV","CBX40UHV","variable speed air handler","ECM","icomfort communicating","air handler"],"source":"Lennox CBA38MV Product Specifications, Bulletin No. 210803 (10/2020), LennoxPros.com","flags":[{"title":"Continuous-fan % and dehumid-ramp jumpers are field-configurable","body":"The continuous-blower-speed DIP switch defaults to 38% of the 2nd-stage COOL speed but is field-selectable to 28/38/70/100%. Separately, the DELAY jumper picks one of four distinct dehumidification ramp profiles (Options 1-4), and blower behavior differs significantly between them. Check both jumper positions before calling a ramping/lag symptom a blower fault."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Motor type","value":"ECM (Electronically Commutated Motor), variable-speed, ramps up/down gradually","key":"motor_type"},{"label":"Speed selection","value":"iComfort communicating control runs 2 of 8 available air volumes; HEAT and COOL speeds each set independently via jumper pins (4 discrete positions per mode)","key":"speed_selection"},{"label":"ADJUST jumper","value":"+10% / normal / -10% fine-tune within the selected HEAT/COOL jumper speed","key":"adjust_jumper"},{"label":"Continuous (constant) fan","value":"DIP-switch selectable at 28%, 38% (factory default), 70%, or 100% of 2nd-stage COOL speed; minimum 250 cfm (450 cfm on -042/048/060)","key":"continuous_fan"},{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.80 in. w.g. (motor has built-in speed/torque limiters beyond this)","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"First-stage cooling airflow","value":"70% of the COOL speed setting","key":"first_stage_airflow"},{"label":"Dehumidification ramp (DELAY jumper)","value":"4 selectable profiles (Options 1-4) that vary blower % and timing during a cooling or heat-pump demand","key":"dehumid_ramp"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Wide-range check/expansion valve, factory installed internal to cabinet, Chatleff-style fitting - 12J18 (018/024, 030), 12J19 (036), 12J20 (042, 048, 060)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Line connections","value":"Suction/vapor 3/4\" (018/024-036), 7/8\" (042-060); liquid 3/8\" all sizes","key":"line_connections"}]},{"title":"Filter & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Disposable 1\" - (1) 20x20x1 (018/024-036), (1) 20x24x1 (042-060)","key":"filter"},{"label":"Drain pans","value":"Anti-microbial dual-position drain pans for upflow/downflow/horizontal","key":"drain_pans"},{"label":"Condensate connections","value":"(2) 3/4\" fpt","key":"condensate"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat (EvenHeater)","rows":[{"label":"Stages","value":"Up to 3 conventional stages standard, or up to 4 stages via EvenHeater control","key":"heat_stages"},{"label":"EvenHeater target discharge temp","value":"Jumper-selectable 85°F / 100°F / 115°F / 130°F; factory default 85°F","key":"evenheater_target"},{"label":"EvenHeater sensor requirement","value":"Requires optional Discharge Air Temperature Sensor (88K38)","key":"evenheater_sensor"},{"label":"kW range","value":"4-25 kW depending on model/circuit configuration","key":"kw_range"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBA25UH","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position air handler (MERIT Series), 1.5-5 tons, R-410A - PSC blower on 018-042, Constant Torque ECM on 048/060; max 0.50 in. w.g. ESP.","match":["CBA25UH","CBX25UH","PSC air handler","fixed speed","constant torque","merit series","air handler"],"source":"Lennox CBA25UH MERIT Series Product Specifications, Bulletin No. 210814 (6/2020), LennoxPros.com","flags":[{"title":"Blower motor type is size-specific","body":"Only the -048 and -060 (4- and 5-ton) models use a programmable Constant Torque ECM blower with 5 speeds. Every smaller size (018 through 042) uses a plain multi-speed PSC motor with 3 fixed speeds (High/Medium/Low) changed by moving a wire tap, not electronically. A 'soft ramp' symptom on an 018-042 unit is not a blower fault - that behavior doesn't exist on PSC. Confirm size before troubleshooting."},{"title":"Lower max static than the variable-speed CBA38MV - don't reuse duct specs","body":"Published blower performance data stops at 0.50 in. w.g. ESP on CBA25UH, versus 0.80 in. w.g. on the CBA38MV variable-speed platform. Don't carry over static-pressure design assumptions between the two lines."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower (motor type differs by size)","rows":[{"label":"018-042 models","value":"Multi-speed PSC (Permanent Split Capacitor) motor, 3 fixed speeds (High/Medium/Low); speed changed by wiring tap","key":"blower_018_042"},{"label":"048 & 060 models","value":"Constant Torque ECM blower motor, 5 programmable speeds (High/Med-High/Med/Med-Low/Low)","key":"blower_048_060"},{"label":"Max external static pressure tested","value":"0.50 in. w.g.","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Time-delay blower relay","value":"1-second ON delay before cooling/continuous-fan start; 45-second OFF delay after","key":"blower_relay_delay"},{"label":"Not present on this platform","value":"No continuous-fan %, ADJUST jumper, or dehumidification-ramp jumper (those are CBA38MV/iComfort-only features)","key":"missing_features"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Wide-range check/expansion valve, factory installed internal to cabinet, Chatleff-style fitting - same style as CBA38MV but a different catalog part number; confirm via AHRI match-up","key":"metering"},{"label":"Line connections","value":"Suction/vapor 3/4\" (018-030), 7/8\" (036-060); liquid 3/8\" all sizes","key":"line_connections"}]},{"title":"Filter & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Disposable 1\" - 15x20x1 (018-030), 18x20x1 (036-060)","key":"filter"},{"label":"Drain pans","value":"Anti-microbial dual-position drain pans","key":"drain_pans"},{"label":"Condensate connections","value":"(2) 3/4\" fpt","key":"condensate"},{"label":"Downflow","value":"Requires optional Downflow Conversion Kit - not shipped downflow-ready (ships upflow/horizontal left-hand)","key":"downflow"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"kW range","value":"4-20 kW","key":"kw_range"},{"label":"Elements","value":"Standard nichrome helix elements with thermal sequencer relay; no EvenHeater discharge-temp targeting on this platform","key":"elements"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XV20i / 4TWV0 (Variable-Speed ComfortLink II Heat Pump)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Communicating variable-speed heat pump (Integrated Variable Speed Control/IVSC board, EEV metering, demand defrost). Charge by weigh-in table or the 'Charging Mode-Cooling' subcooling test only — indoor blower MUST be set to 400 CFM/ton for either method. Crankcase-heater wait time is 3 hours (not the usual 1 hr) below 85°F ambient.","match":["XV20i","4TWV0","4TTV0","TWV0","TTV0","4A7V0","A7V0"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide 18-BC89D1-1H-EN, 'Variable Speed ComfortLink II Heat Pumps and Air Conditioners' (models 4TWV0024/036/048/060A1000B, 4TTV0024/036B/048/060/061A1000B), June 2018","flags":[{"title":"High/low pressure cutout PSIG not published","body":"This Installer's Guide states only 'internal compressor high/low pressure & temperature protection' — no numeric cutout/cutin PSIG values are given. See rating plate or the unit's Service Facts document (shipped inside the outdoor unit control box) for actual setpoints."},{"title":"Reversing valve energized-in state not stated","body":"The guide does not state whether the reversing (SOV) valve is energized in heating or cooling. Verify from the wiring diagram inside the control box cover or the Service Facts document before assuming a default."},{"title":"400 CFM/ton is mandatory for charging","body":"Both the weigh-in method and the subcooling ('Charging Mode-Cooling') method require the indoor blower configured to 400 CFM/ton — the guide flags this twice as 'IMPORTANT.' Charging at any other airflow setting will give an incorrect result."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (PVE oil — variable-speed compressor)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) — EEV Test available in CDA Control Menu","key":"metering"},{"label":"Oil hygroscopic warning","value":"If system open to atmosphere >4 hrs, compressor oil must be replaced","key":"oilNote"}]},{"title":"Operating Range","rows":[{"label":"Cooling operating range","value":"55°F to 120°F outdoor ambient","key":"coolingRange"},{"label":"Heating operating range","value":"-10°F to 66°F outdoor ambient","key":"heatingRange"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling lockout","value":"55°F (per Table 1 Operating Range)","key":"lowAmbientLockout"}]},{"title":"Defrost (Demand Defrost)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand defrost — outdoor ambient sensor (ODS-B) + coil sensor (CBS), delta-T logic","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Defrost enable conditions","value":"Outdoor ambient ≤52°F AND coil temp ≤35°F AND heat/cool demand ≥2 minutes","key":"defrostEnable"},{"label":"Defrost initiation","value":"Occurs once measured Delta-T (ambient minus coil temp) exceeds an adaptive Delta-T initiate value","key":"defrostInitiate"},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"Terminates on coil temperature per factory/medium/high termination profile (software-version dependent — see chart in guide); forced-defrost override caps at 15 minutes","key":"defrostTermination"},{"label":"Forced defrost test","value":"CDA Control Menu > FRC DFT — system must be running with demand, heat mode only, press ENTER","key":"forcedDefrost"}]},{"title":"Crankcase Heater / Startup","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater wait","value":"Wait 3 HOURS before starting unit if outdoor ambient is below 85°F","key":"crankcaseWait"},{"label":"400VDC hazard","value":"Wait 2 minutes after disconnecting power; verify <42VDC at +VDC/-VDC test points before servicing IVSC board","key":"highVoltageHazard"}]},{"title":"ComfortLink II / Communicating Status","rows":[{"label":"Control platform","value":"Integrated Variable Speed Control (IVSC) board + Communicating Display Assembly (CDA), pairs with 850/950/1050 comfort controls","key":"controlPlatform"},{"label":"Status LED (green)","value":"Slow=Standby/Idle, Medium=Call for Capacity, Fast=Power-up delay, Solid=Test Mode, 1 flash/4 sec=Hard Lockout","key":"statusLed"},{"label":"COMM LED (amber)","value":"Slow=device count, Fast (5x/sec)=loss of communication","key":"commLed"},{"label":"Approved indoor matches","value":"TCONT850/TZONE950/TZON1050 controls; TAM9, TAM8C, TEM8 air handlers; S9V2 (relay panel), XC80, XC95m furnaces — Trane coils/air handlers only","key":"approvedMatches"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Approved subcooling method","value":"'Charging Mode-Cooling' test in comfort control Technician Menu ONLY — outdoor 55–120°F, indoor 70–80°F, indoor blower at 400 CFM/ton","key":"chargingMethod"},{"label":"Weigh-in factory charge (HP)","value":"024: 7lb 6oz / 036: 9lb 8oz / 048: 10lb 12oz / 060: 11lb 14oz, plus indoor-coil adder and 0.6 oz/ft line-length multiplier","key":"weighInCharge"},{"label":"Design subcooling value","value":"See rating plate or Service Facts (not a fixed figure in this guide — used with the R-410A charging chart, 8–14°F subcooling columns, 55–125°F liquid temp rows)","key":"designSubcooling"},{"label":"Line length/lift limits","value":"150 ft max length / 50 ft max lift on 5/8\"–7/8\" lines; larger 1-1/8\" vapor line models limited to 80 ft length / 10–25 ft lift depending on model","key":"lineLimits"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Trane/American Standard defrost boards use a TEST_COMMON pin plus separate FRC_DFT and TST pins. Short TEST_COMMON to FRC_DFT for 2 seconds and release to command a forced defrost (remove the short once defrost initiates). Shorting TEST_COMMON to TST instead speeds up all board timings rather than forcing an immediate defrost. Trane boards terminate defrost by their own coil/ambient sensor logic (not a fixed 30/60/90-min accumulator like some other brands), typically within a few minutes once coil temp recovers. Exact pin count/labeling should be confirmed against the board silkscreen for the model in hand. Source: field/trade synthesis of Trane installer manuals (corroborated pin function, not independently re-verified against a specific current PDF this session) — cross-check against the unit's own Installer's Manual defrost-control section before relying on it."},{"label":"ComfortLink II communicating","value":"Verified directly from a Trane variable-speed heat pump Installer's Manual: on the CDA/communicating thermostat (XL824/XL850/XL1050 or ComfortLink II control), navigate CONFIG > CONTROL MENU > FRC DFT > ENTER. System must already be running with an active heat demand from the thermostat — 'FRC DFT TEST' can only be initiated in heat mode. The test has a maximum override/runtime of 15 minutes if it doesn't self-terminate sooner. Source: Trane 4TWV0024A1000A Installer's Manual (assets.unilogcorp.com service manual family), 'Defrost Control (Heat Pump Only)' section, p.26."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Per the same Trane manual, demand defrost is only enabled when the coil temperature sensor (CBS) reports coil temperature at or below 35°F — above that, a forced-defrost command may not actually engage the cycle. When defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, and a burst of cold air from the supply registers is normal and expected, not a malfunction."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XR16 / 4TWR6 (Standard Two-Stage Heat Pump)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Conventional 24V two-stage (CLIMATUFF 2-stage scroll) heat pump with factory compressor sump heat, timed/temperature-based defrost control (jumper-selectable termination), and standard 15° superheat / subcooling charging methods depending on outdoor ambient. Requires a field jumper change on the air handler terminal strip for correct 2-stage airflow.","match":["XR16","4TWR6","4A6H6","A6H6"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide 18-BC88D1-1, 'Heat Pumps 4TWR6' + Trane Product Data 22-1865-03, 'Split System Heat Pump XR16 4TWR6, 2-5 Tons' (©2011/2012 Trane)","flags":[{"title":"High/low pressure cutout PSIG not published","body":"Both the Installer's Guide and Product Data state only that 'high and low pressure controls are inherent to the compressor' — no numeric cutout/cutin PSIG figures are given in this literature. See rating plate or Service Facts shipped with the unit."},{"title":"Reversing valve energized-in state not stated","body":"Neither document states whether the switchover (reversing) valve is energized in heating or cooling. Verify against the unit's wiring diagram (legend labels it 'SC' / switchover valve solenoid) before assuming."},{"title":"Required field jumper changes for VS air handler pairing","body":"When matched with a variable-speed (TAM9/TAMG) air handler, the installer MUST remove the factory jumper between R and BK, and ADD a field jumper between R and O, on the air handler terminal strip — 4TWR6 requires 80% airflow on Y1 (low stage) and 100% on Y2 (high stage). Missing this step causes wrong-stage airflow."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV/EEV (indoor-coil side) — AHRI-rated only with TXV/EEV matched indoor coils","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"CLIMATUFF 2-stage scroll, 70–100% capacity modulation, 1-2 stages","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Low ambient cooling","value":"55°F as shipped (below 55°F requires Application Guide APP-APG013-EN)","key":"lowAmbientCooling"},{"label":"Compressor sump heat","value":"YES — standard factory-installed (per Product Data electrical table)","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Startup wait","value":"Wait 1 hour before starting if crankcase heater accessory is used and outdoor ambient is below 70°F","key":"startupWait"},{"label":"Max outdoor operating temp","value":"115°F (cooling)","key":"maxOutdoorTemp"}]},{"title":"Defrost Control","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Timed/temperature-initiated defrost control board (DFC) with selectable termination via cuttable Jumper 2 — not explicitly labeled 'demand defrost' in this literature","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Termination — as shipped","value":">22°F ambient: terminates at 47°F | 10–22°F: terminates at ODT+25°F | 6–10°F: terminates at 35°F","key":"defrostTermAsShipped"},{"label":"Termination — Jumper 2 cut","value":">30°F ambient: 47°F | 6–30°F: 70°F | <6°F: 12 min or 35°F, every 3 hrs","key":"defrostTermJumperCut"},{"label":"Forced defrost test","value":"Short FRC_DFT pin to TEST_COMMON pin on defrost board for 2 seconds to initiate","key":"forcedDefrost"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Above 55°F outdoor (cooling)","value":"Subcooling method — use design subcooling from nameplate/Service Facts + Subcool Charging Chart correction (by tonnage, line length, and lift)","key":"chargeAbove55"},{"label":"Below 55°F outdoor (heating)","value":"Superheat method — target 15°F superheat using true suction line temp/pressure (Table 14.3, 15° Superheat Chart)","key":"chargeBelow55"},{"label":"Refrigerant charging chart","value":"R-410A chart keyed to liquid line temp (55–125°F) vs. final subcooling (8–14°F) → target liquid gage PSI","key":"chargingChart"},{"label":"Factory charge (15 ft line)","value":"024: 10lb 3oz | 036: 10lb 8oz | 048: 12lb 9oz | 060: 13lb 3oz","key":"factoryCharge"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant Line Limits","rows":[{"label":"Standard line set","value":"60 ft max length, 25 ft max vertical lift","key":"lineLimits"},{"label":"Leak check pressure","value":"150 PSIG dry nitrogen","key":"leakCheckPsig"},{"label":"Evacuation","value":"≤350 microns, must not rise above 500 microns in 1 minute","key":"evacuation"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Trane/American Standard defrost boards use a TEST_COMMON pin plus separate FRC_DFT and TST pins. Short TEST_COMMON to FRC_DFT for 2 seconds and release to command a forced defrost (remove the short once defrost initiates). Shorting TEST_COMMON to TST instead speeds up all board timings rather than forcing an immediate defrost. Trane boards terminate defrost by their own coil/ambient sensor logic (not a fixed 30/60/90-min accumulator like some other brands), typically within a few minutes once coil temp recovers. Exact pin count/labeling should be confirmed against the board silkscreen for the model in hand. Source: field/trade synthesis of Trane installer manuals (corroborated pin function, not independently re-verified against a specific current PDF this session) — cross-check against the unit's own Installer's Manual defrost-control section before relying on it."},{"label":"ComfortLink II communicating","value":"Verified directly from a Trane variable-speed heat pump Installer's Manual: on the CDA/communicating thermostat (XL824/XL850/XL1050 or ComfortLink II control), navigate CONFIG > CONTROL MENU > FRC DFT > ENTER. System must already be running with an active heat demand from the thermostat — 'FRC DFT TEST' can only be initiated in heat mode. The test has a maximum override/runtime of 15 minutes if it doesn't self-terminate sooner. Source: Trane 4TWV0024A1000A Installer's Manual (assets.unilogcorp.com service manual family), 'Defrost Control (Heat Pump Only)' section, p.26."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Per the same Trane manual, demand defrost is only enabled when the coil temperature sensor (CBS) reports coil temperature at or below 35°F — above that, a forced-defrost command may not actually engage the cycle. When defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, and a burst of cold air from the supply registers is normal and expected, not a malfunction."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"TAM9 / 4TEE3 (Variable-Speed Modular Multi-Position Air Handler)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Variable-speed ECM (Vortica blower) air handler with EEV metering, dual-refrigerant-compatible coil, communicating or 24V control. Airflow is set as CFM/ton in either Constant CFM or Constant Torque mode — Torque mode silently reduces airflow above ~0.3-0.4\" static, a common source of under-delivered CFM if not checked.","match":["TAM9","4TEE3","TAM9A0","AM9"],"source":"Trane Product Data 22-1935-1C-EN, 'Variable Speed Modular Multi-position Air Handlers 2-5 Tons' (TAM9A0A24/B30/C36/C42/C48/C60V*1DA), February 2018","flags":[{"title":"Constant CFM vs. Constant Torque mode changes real airflow","body":"The airflow tables show two values above ~0.3-0.4\" ESP: Constant CFM (holds set point, higher watts) vs. Constant Torque (airflow sags as static rises). Confirm which mode is configured before trusting a nameplate CFM/ton number against measured static."},{"title":"Subcooling target depends on outdoor match, not just this air handler","body":"Design subcooling (8-12°) is listed per specific single/two-compressor two-stage outdoor pairing in the doc's Subcooling Adjustment table — do not use one blanket number across all TAM9 + outdoor combinations without checking the match."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Vortica variable-speed ECM, direct drive, centrifugal, 1/2–1 HP depending on size","key":"blowerType"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"CFM/ton entered via Control Display Assembly (CDA); factory default cooling setting varies 400-430 CFM/ton by model","key":"airflowSetup"},{"label":"Airflow modes","value":"Constant CFM mode or Constant Torque mode — status LED blinks once per 100 CFM requested","key":"airflowModes"},{"label":"Max ESP tested","value":"Tables tested to 0.9\" w.g. external static; torque-mode roll-off begins ~0.3\" (smaller units) to ~0.4\" (larger units) w.g.","key":"maxESP"},{"label":"Downflow/horizontal airflow cap","value":"On C48/C60 models, airflow must not exceed 2000 CFM in downflow/horizontal to avoid water blow-off","key":"airflowCap"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV), low-ambient and low-superheat compressor protection, dual-refrigerant compatible as shipped","key":"metering"},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A, brazed connections","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Coil","value":"All-aluminum, patented enhanced fin, integrated slide deck","key":"coil"}]},{"title":"Filter & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Molded-in 1\" standard filter rail; not furnished — throwaway recommended, sizes 16x20 to 22x20 depending on cabinet width","key":"filter"},{"label":"Drain connection","value":"3/4\" NPT; integrated horizontal drain pans; optional internal condensate switch kit (BAYICSKIT01A)","key":"drain"},{"label":"Freeze/overflow wiring note","value":"Y1 and YO connections must be made as shown for freeze protection and internally-mounted condensate-overflow circuits to function","key":"freezeProtection"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat Staging","rows":[{"label":"Heater range","value":"BAYEAxx series, 4kW to 25kW, 1 to 3 circuits depending on kW (see Heater Attribute Data table for exact MCA/MOP)","key":"heaterRange"},{"label":"Heater config","value":"Heater size must be set in the CDA Configuration Menu","key":"heaterConfig"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"TEM6 (Convertible Air Handler, ECM 16-Speed)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position convertible air handler with a 16-speed (dip-switch selectable Low/Med-Lo/Med-Hi/High) ECM blower — NOT a modulating variable-speed unit like TAM9. Uses a fixed TXV, not an EEV, and requires a remote/external filter (no filter furnished or built-in rail).","match":["TEM6","5TEM6","TEM6A0"],"source":"Trane Product Data 22-1907-1J-EN, 'Convertible Air Handlers 1-1/2 - 5 Ton' (TEM6A0B24/B30/C36/C42/C48/D48/C60/D60H*1SB), April 2020","flags":[{"title":"TXV, not EEV — despite ECM motor","body":"TEM6 uses a fixed Thermal Expansion Valve (Refrigerant Control = TXV in the product data), unlike TAM9's Electronic Expansion Valve. Don't assume EEV diagnostics or EEV test menus apply to this air handler."},{"title":"No furnished filter — remote filter required","body":"Product Data explicitly notes 'Filter Furnished? No' with footnote 'Remote filter required' on every model — unlike TAM9's built-in 1\" filter rail. Confirm a remote filter box/grille is installed, not just the cabinet's own rail."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"ECM, direct drive, 16-speed, centrifugal — dip-switch selectable Low/Med-Lo/Med-Hi/High (SW1-SW4)","key":"blowerType"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Dip switches SW1-SW4 set CFM/ton per outdoor tonnage; separate SW7/SW8 dip switches set auxiliary-heat airflow (Low/Med-Lo/Med-Hi/High nominal CFM)","key":"airflowSetup"},{"label":"Max ESP tested","value":"Airflow tables tested to 0.9\" w.g. external static pressure","key":"maxESP"},{"label":"Minimum heater airflow","value":"Model- and heater-size-specific CFM floor, with-heat-pump vs. without-heat-pump values differ — see Minimum Airflow CFM tables","key":"minHeaterAirflow"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"R-410A Thermal Expansion Valve (TXV) — fixed, not electronic","key":"metering"},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A, brazed connections","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Coil","value":"All-aluminum, enhanced patented coil fin, horizontal drain pan, draw-through design","key":"coil"}]},{"title":"Filter & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"NOT furnished — remote filter required (no built-in filter rail); optional Slim Fit Filter Box accessory (BAYSF1185/1235/1265AAA)","key":"filter"},{"label":"Drain connection","value":"3/4\" NPT","key":"drain"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat Staging","rows":[{"label":"Heater range","value":"BAYHTR series, 4kW to 25kW, 1-4 circuits depending on kW (see Electrical Data heater tables for MCA/MOP)","key":"heaterRange"},{"label":"Heater pressure drop","value":"0.01-0.14 in. w.g. depending on airflow CFM and number of heater racks (1-4)","key":"heaterPressureDrop"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Subcooling target","value":"13-14° for confirmed 15/16 SEER matches listed in Subcooling Adjustment table; all other matches must be charged per outdoor unit (OD) nameplate","key":"subcoolingTarget"},{"label":"C48/C60 downflow adder","value":"For HP units ≤3.5 tons in downflow, add 4° to OD nameplate subcooling target; 4-5 ton HP and all AC use OD nameplate directly","key":"downflowAdder"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YZV / YZT Affinity Variable-Capacity Communicating Heat Pump (Coleman HC20, Luxaire HL20)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"R-410A variable-capacity inverter heat pump, 4-wire communicating (HxTM t-stat), factory EEV metering, adaptive demand-defrost. Electronic suction-pressure monitoring in place of a fixed low-pressure switch; HPS is factory-set/non-adjustable.","match":["YZV","YZT","HC20","HL20"],"source":"Johnson Controls Unitary Products, York Affinity YZV R-410A Variable Capacity Outdoor Unit Installation Manual, 5284795-UIM-E-1117 (yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/YZV_Install.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"York trap: crankcase heater 2-hour wait","body":"IOM CAUTION: if outdoor temp is below 55°F, do not attempt to start the compressor without at least 2 hours of crankcase/stator heat, or the compressor can be damaged. Heater energizes only during the OFF cycle — techs restarting right after a breaker trip or long shutdown commonly skip this wait."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) — matched EEV also used in indoor coil/air handler; no TXV","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Adaptive/Demand Defrost algorithm (not fixed time/temp)","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Defrost enable","value":"Coil temp below 35°F while compressor runs begins accumulating defrost time","key":"defrost_enable"},{"label":"Forced defrost interval","value":"After 6 hrs accumulated compressor runtime with no defrost, a defrost is forced; if OD ambient <50°F at that point, forces a 6-min oil-return defrost regardless of coil temp","key":"defrost_forced_interval"},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"Selectable coil-temp termination 50/60/70/80°F (default 50°F); defrost auto-terminates at 12 min regardless of coil sensor","key":"defrost_termination"}]},{"title":"Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Energized in","value":"Cooling / Defrost (RV energized to enter defrost, since defrost = cooling-mode equivalent; de-energized to terminate defrost and return to heating)","key":"rv_energized"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches / Limits","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch (HPS)","value":"Factory-set, non-adjustable — trip (open) setpoint not published as a numeric spec; IOM troubleshooting table states the control recognizes HPS reset once system pressure drops below 650 PSIG","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low suction pressure (electronic, no discrete LP switch)","value":"Cool: trending limit <90 psi, fault <5 psi. Heat: trending limit <20 psi, fault <5 psi. (Trending must persist 360 sec, or any reading <5 psi for >5 sec, to fault; bypassed 120 sec at startup and around defrost)","key":"low_pressure"}]},{"title":"Low-Ambient Operation","rows":[{"label":"Cooling low-ambient limit","value":"Automatically reduces capacity / cycles off at or below 35°F outdoor ambient","key":"low_ambient_cool"},{"label":"Heating low-ambient limit","value":"Compressor heat available down to -5°F outdoor ambient; size balance point / auxiliary heat accordingly as capacity fades approaching this point","key":"low_ambient_lockout"}]},{"title":"Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Energized only during the OFF cycle to prevent refrigerant migration; see CAUTION flag above for the 2-hour pre-start requirement below 55°F","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charge method","value":"see rating plate — use unit nameplate charge and the superheat/subcooling charge tables in the Product/Technical Guide for the matched indoor coil; do not use remembered figures","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"York/Coleman/Luxaire (Johnson Controls) Demand Defrost Control boards have a 'TEST' pin pair (P3 on some revisions). With a heating call active, jumper the TEST pins for 6+ seconds — defrost engages and continues for as long as the jumper stays in place. While TEST is jumpered, the control ignores actual coil (liquid-line) temperature and outdoor ambient — the coil does NOT need to be cold for the forced test to run. After removing the jumper, defrost terminates normally on its own logic: liquid-line temp reaches 80°F, or after 8 minutes of defrost run time, whichever comes first. Source: Johnson Controls Unitary Products 'Demand Defrost Control' Operation Instructions, part 031-09178-000 / doc 501062-UAI (cdn.master.ca and us-ac.com hosted copies), plus corroborating HVAC-Talk field posts."},{"label":"ComfortNet/Affinity communicating","value":"NOT independently verified this session. The S1-TTSCC01/S1-TTSCC02 Affinity/ComfortNet touchscreen control has a service/diagnostics area, and York field literature references being able to force a defrost cycle through it, but no source located gave the exact on-screen menu path or button sequence. Do not guess the menu steps — pull the specific control's Installation/Operation guide or use the physical TEST-pin method above (works regardless of comm status) if the outdoor unit's board is accessible."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"On normal (non-forced) operation, coil temp must be below the board's frost/cut-in threshold before a defrost demand will latch; the TEST-pin forced method above deliberately bypasses that check. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may lock in — warn of a normal burst of cold supply air during the test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"AVV Affinity Single-Piece Variable-Speed Communicating Air Handler (Coleman AVV, Luxaire AVV)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Single-piece ECM variable-speed, constant-CFM communicating air handler with factory-mounted EEV, matched to YZV/YXV outdoor units via 4-wire HxTM communicating system. Airflow/tonnage is set automatically by the outdoor unit's control, not by field dip switches.","match":["AVV","MVC"],"source":"Johnson Controls Unitary Products, York Affinity AVV Single Piece Variable Speed ECM Communicating Air Handler Technical Guide, 5322576-YTG-D-0617 (yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/AVVtech.pdf); airflow-control note per York YZV Installation Manual 5284795-UIM-E-1117 (yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/YZV_Install.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"York trap: EEV harness must be connected before power-up","body":"The indoor EEV ships factory-installed but CLOSED. On a coil/air-handler swap or first startup, the EEV harness must be plugged into the Comm port BEFORE applying power to the indoor unit, then allow 1 minute for the EEV to open before charging/nitrogen work. Powering up first can leave the valve closed and pressures locked out."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"High-efficiency ECM, variable-speed, constant-CFM design","key":"blower_motor"}]},{"title":"Airflow / CFM Setup","rows":[{"label":"CFM-per-ton setup","value":"No field dip switches for tonnage — \"the proper airflow is determined by the main outdoor control in the outdoor unit\" over the 4-wire communicating link; unit self-adjusts to hold set CFM from 0.0\" to 0.4\" external static","key":"cfm_setup"}]},{"title":"External Static","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"Not recommended above 0.8\" w.c. (CFM derates 2% per 0.1\" esp from 0.4\"–0.8\"); UL 1995/CSA 22.2 No.236 tested/rated to 0.50\" w.c., dry coil, no filter","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"1\" disposable or permanent, integrated internal filter rack; size varies by model, 16x20x1 up to 22x20x1 (field supplied) — see model chart","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Electric heat kits","value":"Field-installed 208/230V single- or three-phase kits, 5 kW through 25 kW","key":"electric_heat_kw"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Staged via W1-only or W1+W2 per the kW staging table (stage assignment depends on kW size and airflow %)","key":"electric_heat_staging"}]},{"title":"Metering / EEV Match","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed EEV, matched to YZV/YXV outdoor units for the communicating system; see trap flag above for commissioning order","key":"metering_match"}]},{"title":"Drain / Float Switch","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Standard thermoset, corrosion/UV-resistant primary drain pan (factory)","key":"drain_pan"},{"label":"Float switch","value":"see rating plate — no York-published float-switch spec in this literature; auxiliary/secondary float switch is field-installed per local code, not a factory-published figure","key":"float_switch"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GLZS4B Series R-32 Heat Pump (incl. Inverter/variable-capacity models)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"R-32 (A2L, mildly flammable) heat pump platform. Adjustable-TXV metering, time/temperature defrost with SmartShift compressor delay. Exact inverter model numbers (e.g. GVZC8, GSZV) were not itemized in the source manual reviewed — confirm platform/tier against the unit's own rating plate before servicing.","match":["GLZS4B*","ALZS4B*","GVZC*","AVZC*","GSZV*","GSZC*"],"source":"Daikin Comfort Technologies / Goodman \"Condensing Unit / Heat Pump Installation & Service Reference\" (R-32), P/N IOG-4047, Dec 2023 — goodmanmfg.com","flags":[{"title":"R-32 is an A2L mildly-flammable refrigerant","body":"Use leak detectors listed for A2L refrigerants (non-sparking, intrinsically safe or adequately sealed), recalibrated to 25% of R-32's LFL. No open flame/smoking in the work area; survey for ignition sources before opening the system. Sweep with dry nitrogen during brazing and recover refrigerant before any hot work. Never add anything other than R-32 to an R-32 recovery cylinder."},{"title":"Inverter model numbers not confirmed in this pass","body":"The IOG-4047 reference manual covers the whole R-32 platform generically (\"Condenser / Heat Pump, including all Inverter\") without a model-number nomenclature table. Verify the exact inverter model prefix (GVZC8, GSZV, GSZC, etc.) and its specific service instructions against the unit's rating plate — do not assume it matches the GLZS4B figures below without checking."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-32 (A2L, mildly flammable) — confirm on serial/rating plate","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Standing pressure test","value":"Pressurize with dry nitrogen to 450 PSIG, hold 15 min min. (system pressure relief valve must open at no more than 450 psig)","key":"standingPressureTest"}]},{"title":"Metering & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Adjustable TXV (indoor coil-dependent) — no field adjustment normally required; confirm with piston kit chart on mixed-match systems","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charge method — TXV subcooling target","value":"8°F ± 1°F subcooling (adjustable-TXV systems)","key":"subcoolingTarget"},{"label":"Charge amount","value":"See rating plate for factory charge; add per line-set length per TP-110 R-32 Long Line Set Application Guide","key":"chargeAmount"}]},{"title":"Defrost / Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Time/temperature defrost control, field-selectable intervals","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Defrost intervals","value":"30 / 60 / 90 min (Region IV units set per interval table in manual)","key":"defrostIntervals"},{"label":"SmartShift compressor delay","value":"Jumper defaults to \"DLY\" (delays compressor at defrost initiation/termination); move to \"NORM\" to disable","key":"smartShift"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"see rating plate / unit wiring diagram — not itemized in this reference manual","key":"reversingValveMode"}]},{"title":"Protection & Controls","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure cutout-cutin","value":"see rating plate / Service Instructions — not itemized in this reference manual for the R-32 platform","key":"pressureCutouts"},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling lockout","value":"Cooling operation approved above 55°F outdoor ambient; below 55°F requires an approved low-ambient kit (LAKT01 kit cannot be used on ECM-motor outdoor units)","key":"lowAmbientLockout"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Optional/model-dependent — if equipped, energize 24 hrs before startup","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"ComfortNet / CoolCloud","value":"Not referenced in this manual for this platform — check PCB/rating plate for communicating-control capability","key":"communicatingControl"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Goodman/Amana/Janitrol PCBDM-series defrost boards (also used re-badged by other brands) commonly require two things at once: 24V present at the board's DFT (defrost thermostat/coil sensor) input — jump R to DFT if the coil isn't actually cold enough to close the sensor — AND a momentary jumper across the board's TEST/'speed-up' pins until you hear the relay click, then remove the TEST jumper. Once triggered, the unit stays in forced defrost (reversing valve to cooling, outdoor fan off, W2 aux heat and O reversing valve energized) until either 24V is removed from DFT or a built-in max defrost time (commonly ~10 minutes) elapses. Exact pin labels/layout vary by PCBDM revision — confirm against the board's own printed legend/wiring diagram before jumping anything; I could not pull a clean OEM PDF this session to confirm the precise pin silkscreen text, so treat pin names as trade-common convention, not a guaranteed exact label. Source: multi-source trade corroboration (HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board guide; JustAnswer and Fixya Goodman-specific Q&A threads) — recommend verifying against the physical board's legend."},{"label":"ComfortNet/ComfortBridge communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. Goodman heat pumps are largely designed to run on a simple non-communicating thermostat (single Y/W inputs) even when ComfortBridge-equipped equipment is installed; where a CTK04 ComfortNet communicating control is used, no source located gave a documented force-defrost menu sequence. Do not invent a button sequence — use the non-communicating TEST-pin method on the outdoor board directly, which applies regardless of thermostat type, or consult Goodman's specific literature for the installed CTK04/ComfortNet control."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Normal operation requires the coil/defrost sensor to be closed (cold, roughly at/below freezing) AND accumulated compressor run time to exceed the board's 30/60/90-minute dial setting before defrost will initiate on its own; the forced method above is meant to bypass the run-time requirement but the coil sensor circuit (DFT) still needs 24V present (real cold coil, or a temporary jumper) for the relay to latch on some revisions. Expect reversing valve shift to cooling and outdoor fan shutdown when defrost runs — a cold air burst indoors is normal and temporary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSZ140 (GSZ14) — standard single-stage R-410A heat pump","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Standard R-410A single-stage heat pump. Piston (Flowrater) metering standard, adjustable TXV on matched TXV indoor coils. Time/temperature defrost with SmartShift. Low-pressure (loss-of-charge) switch was relocated from the liquid line to the suction line in current production — do not assume its location from an old wiring diagram.","match":["GSZ14*","GSZ140*","ASZ14*","ASZ13*","GSZB4*","ANZ13*"],"source":"Goodman/Amana \"Service and Troubleshooting: ANX, SSX, ASX, GSX, DSX, VSX Condensing Units, ANZ, SSZ, ASZ, GSZ, DSZ, VSZ Split System Heat Pumps (R-410A)\", RS6200006r103, July 2022 — goodmanmfg.com / amana-hac.com","flags":[{"title":"GSZB4 not itemized in this manual","body":"GSZB4 is Goodman's multifamily/light-commercial heat pump line and is not one of the model series listed on the cover of RS6200006r103. Its own Instruction Manual describes the same time/temperature defrost with 30/60/90-min field-selectable intervals and SmartShift technology, so the defrost figures below likely apply — but confirm pressure-switch and reversing-valve specifics against GSZB4-specific literature before relying on the numbers in this entry."},{"title":"Low pressure switch location changed across production","body":"Per the manual's revision history, the low-pressure (loss-of-charge) switch was relocated from the liquid line to the suction line as a compressor safeguard on current units. Older units/wiring diagrams may show the liquid-line location — verify physical location on the unit rather than assuming from an old diagram."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Piston (\"Flowrater\") standard; adjustable TXV on matched TXV/ARPT-AEPT-style indoor coils","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charge verification","value":"Superheat/subcooling per Service Manual chart — check nameplate/manual for exact target (not reproduced in reviewed excerpt); see rating plate","key":"chargeVerification"}]},{"title":"Defrost / Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Solid-state time/temperature defrost control","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Defrost intervals","value":"Field-selectable 30 / 60 / 90 min","key":"defrostIntervals"},{"label":"SmartShift compressor delay","value":"~30-sec compressor delay at defrost initiation via defrost board jumper (\"DLY\"); move to \"NORM\" to disable","key":"smartShift"},{"label":"Defrost termination override","value":"10-minute maximum defrost override if defrost thermostat doesn't reopen","key":"defrostOverride"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Energized in cooling mode (24V coil at \"O\"); de-energized in heating mode, except momentarily energized during a defrost cycle while in heating","key":"reversingValveMode"}]},{"title":"Protection & Controls","rows":[{"label":"Low pressure (loss-of-charge) switch","value":"Cut-out (open) ≈21 PSIG; auto cut-in (close) ≈50 PSIG — auto-reset","key":"lowPressureSwitch"},{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 610 PSIG ± 10; closes 420 PSIG ± 25 — auto-reset","key":"highPressureSwitch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-installed option on some models — if equipped, energize 24 hrs before startup","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"ComfortNet / CoolCloud","value":"Not applicable — standard non-communicating 24V R/C/Y/G/O/W2 staging","key":"communicatingControl"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Goodman/Amana/Janitrol PCBDM-series defrost boards (also used re-badged by other brands) commonly require two things at once: 24V present at the board's DFT (defrost thermostat/coil sensor) input — jump R to DFT if the coil isn't actually cold enough to close the sensor — AND a momentary jumper across the board's TEST/'speed-up' pins until you hear the relay click, then remove the TEST jumper. Once triggered, the unit stays in forced defrost (reversing valve to cooling, outdoor fan off, W2 aux heat and O reversing valve energized) until either 24V is removed from DFT or a built-in max defrost time (commonly ~10 minutes) elapses. Exact pin labels/layout vary by PCBDM revision — confirm against the board's own printed legend/wiring diagram before jumping anything; I could not pull a clean OEM PDF this session to confirm the precise pin silkscreen text, so treat pin names as trade-common convention, not a guaranteed exact label. Source: multi-source trade corroboration (HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board guide; JustAnswer and Fixya Goodman-specific Q&A threads) — recommend verifying against the physical board's legend."},{"label":"ComfortNet/ComfortBridge communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. Goodman heat pumps are largely designed to run on a simple non-communicating thermostat (single Y/W inputs) even when ComfortBridge-equipped equipment is installed; where a CTK04 ComfortNet communicating control is used, no source located gave a documented force-defrost menu sequence. Do not invent a button sequence — use the non-communicating TEST-pin method on the outdoor board directly, which applies regardless of thermostat type, or consult Goodman's specific literature for the installed CTK04/ComfortNet control."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Normal operation requires the coil/defrost sensor to be closed (cold, roughly at/below freezing) AND accumulated compressor run time to exceed the board's 30/60/90-minute dial setting before defrost will initiate on its own; the forced method above is meant to bypass the run-time requirement but the coil sensor circuit (DFT) still needs 24V present (real cold coil, or a temporary jumper) for the relay to latch on some revisions. Expect reversing valve shift to cooling and outdoor fan shutdown when defrost runs — a cold air burst indoors is normal and temporary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"AVPTC (ComfortBridge variable-speed air handler)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position variable-speed ECM air handler with ComfortBridge communicating control (CoolCloud app / PCB \"ton\" menu). Airflow MUST be set for non-communicating outdoor units or the PCB will fault to \"IdL\" and the blower won't run for cooling calls.","match":["AVPTC*","AAVPTC*"],"source":"Daikin Comfort Technologies / Goodman \"AVPTC**14** Air Handlers Installation & Operating Instructions\", P/N IOA-4030H, April 2023 — goodmanmfg.com / amana-hac.com","flags":[{"title":"\"IdL\" fault = airflow not configured (Goodman trap)","body":"When pairing an AVPTC with a non-communicating outdoor unit, airflow must be set manually in the PCB \"ton\" menu or via the CoolCloud HVAC app. If this step is skipped, the PCB displays fault code \"IdL\" and the blower will not operate on a call for cooling. This does NOT mean the board is bad — set the airflow/tonnage first before replacing anything."},{"title":"Two-stage electric heat needs only a single W input","body":"For two-stage electric heat kits, wire only a single W input to the air handler — internal ComfortBridge algorithms handle heat-kit staging automatically. Do not wire W1/W2 separately expecting external staging control."},{"title":"Motor orientation matters","body":"The AVPTC has a dedicated motor-orientation procedure (Section 14 of the manual) that must be followed when converting cabinet orientation (upflow/downflow/horizontal) — the ECM motor must be reoriented per the manual's diagram, not just the cabinet."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"ECM (electronically commutated), ComfortBridge-controlled","key":"blowerMotor"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"PCB \"ton\" menu or CoolCloud HVAC app (non-communicating outdoor units); auto-negotiated with communicating outdoor units","key":"airflowSetup"},{"label":"Duct design airflow","value":"350–450 CFM per ton of cooling (default indoor-airflow basis = 400 CFM/ton)","key":"designAirflow"},{"label":"Design total external static","value":"0.5 in. w.c. (duct system should be sized not to exceed this); higher static may require a deeper field-built condensate trap","key":"designStatic"},{"label":"Constant/circulator fan default speed","value":"30% of maximum airflow (default, adjustable)","key":"constantFanDefault"}]},{"title":"Metering & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed TXV (TXV-specific tubing/brazing procedure in manual, Section 7.3)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charge verification prerequisite","value":"Confirm total static pressure ≤0.5 in. w.c. and correct airflow BEFORE charging or adjusting the TXV","key":"chargePrereq"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit compatibility","value":"HKS series only — no other accessory heat kit is approved for this air handler","key":"heatKit"},{"label":"Heat kit staging","value":"Two-stage kits use a single W input; ComfortBridge stages internally (percentage of high-stage airflow during low-stage default = 70%)","key":"heatKitStaging"},{"label":"Condensate","value":"Primary/secondary drain pan; float switch must not use foam/plastic components incompatible with condensate chemistry per manual note","key":"condensate"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"ARUF / ARPF (PSC, piston) and ARPT / AEPT (ECM, TXV) standard air handlers","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Standard multi-position air handler family. ARUF/ARPF use multi-speed PSC motors with a piston (\"Flowrater\") metering device; ARPT/AEPT use a General Electric ECM motor with factory TXV and an 8-position dip switch for airflow. Amana's PSC/Flowrater twin of ARUF is the AWUF series (not AWST — AWST is Amana's separate ECM-based line).","match":["ARUF*","ARPF*","ARPT*","AEPT*","AWUF*","AWUT*"],"source":"Goodman \"Installation & Operating Instructions for ARUF, ARPF, ARPT and AEPT Series Air Handler\", P/N IO-230H, 2004-2005 (Goodman/Amana shared platform; Amana equivalent published as SS-AAWUF) — goodmanmfg.com / amana-hac.com","flags":[{"title":"AWST is NOT the ARUF twin — use AWUF","body":"Amana's AWST series is a separate ECM-based air handler line, not the Amana equivalent of Goodman's PSC/piston ARUF. The correct Amana twin of ARUF (PSC motor, Flowrater/piston metering) is the AWUF series (wall-mount, 1.5–5 ton). Don't cross-reference AWST data onto an ARUF-family unit."},{"title":"Piston vs TXV — model suffix defines the metering device","body":"ARUF/ARPF ship with a check piston (\"Flowrater\"); ARPT/AEPT ship with a factory-installed, field-adjustable TXV. In mix-matched tonnage installs (different condenser vs. air handler tonnage), the piston orifice size may need to change — check the Goodman piston kit chart before assuming the factory piston is correct."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower","rows":[{"label":"ARUF/ARPF motor","value":"Multi-speed PSC motor","key":"blowerMotorPSC"},{"label":"ARPT/AEPT motor","value":"GE ECM motor, 4 airflow levels via 8-position dip switch (combos 1-2 and 5-6 set base CFM; 7-8 trims)","key":"blowerMotorECM"}]},{"title":"Metering & Charging","rows":[{"label":"ARUF/ARPF metering","value":"Check piston (\"Flowrater\") — no adjustment for matched-tonnage installs; see piston kit chart for mix-matched tonnage","key":"meteringPiston"},{"label":"ARPT/AEPT metering","value":"Factory-installed, field-adjustable TXV; sensing bulb is not permanently fixed — verify placement/insulation on any service","key":"meteringTXV"},{"label":"TXV charging target","value":"Charge to 15°F subcooling (ARPT/AEPT with TXV)","key":"subcoolingTargetTXV"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat & Filter","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit series","value":"HKR series only (HKR3 for 3-phase); factory does not install electric heat — accessory only","key":"heatKit"},{"label":"Filter requirement","value":"Return-air filter required at every install (at unit or externally via return grille); downflow orientation requires external filtering","key":"filterRequirement"},{"label":"Condensate","value":"Primary + secondary drain connections on horizontal pan; float switch must not use foam/plastic materials incompatible per manual caution","key":"condensate"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RP20 / RP17 EcoNet Inverter Heat Pump (VSODU)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"EcoNet-enabled, inverter-driven variable-speed heat pump (Rheem Prestige / Ruud Ultra series). Uses electronic expansion valve metering, demand defrost, and a compressor stator heater instead of a conventional crankcase heater.","match":["RP20","RP17","UP20","UP17"],"source":"Rheem (-)P20 EcoNet Enabled Inverter-Driven Variable Speed R-410A Heat Pump Outdoor Units — Installation Instructions, Form 92-105074-09-00 (3/16), pts.myrheem.com. Ruud UP20/UP17 twin naming per ruud.com product pages (RHMV IOM notes RHMV is rated with UP17/UP20 heat pumps).","flags":[{"title":"Reversing valve energized in HEATING (not cooling)","body":"Confirmed in the defrost sequence: entering defrost (a cooling-cycle reversal) de-energizes the reversing valve; returning to heating re-energizes it. So the RV is energized in HEATING and relaxed in cooling — the opposite of the common 'O' convention (energized-in-cooling) used by many other brands. Verify at the B terminal before assuming O-type logic on this platform."},{"title":"No universal charging chart — do not use a generic R-410A table","body":"Final charge is set per the Charging Chart printed on the unit's own access panel cover (weight + subcooling method), not a generic pressure/temperature chart. See rating plate / unit charging chart."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EXV) — factory-matched outdoor + indoor EXV pair","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand defrost (ICC — Integrated Compressor Control — algorithm), not a fixed timer","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Initiation","value":"Outdoor coil temp < 35°F AND compressor run-time ≥ 34 min (plus onboard differential calc)","key":"defrost_init"},{"label":"Termination","value":"14 min max, or coil reaches termination temp — factory 60°F, field-adjustable to 50/60/70/80°F via 2-position dip switch","key":"defrost_term"}]},{"title":"Reversing Valve & Pressure Controls","rows":[{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"HEATING (de-energized during defrost/cooling) — see flag","key":"rv_mode"},{"label":"High pressure cutout / cut-in","value":"Auto-reset: opens ≈610 psig / closes ≈420 psig","key":"hpc"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout / cut-in (cooling)","value":"Transducer-based: no-op <50 psig, resumes ≥95 psig","key":"lpc_cool"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout / cut-in (heating)","value":"Transducer-based: no-op <15 psig, resumes ≥40 psig","key":"lpc_heat"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Protection","rows":[{"label":"Compressor stator heat (crankcase heater equivalent)","value":"Energizes when OAT <45°F; must be energized 12 hrs before initial start-up; keeps compressor shell >50°F before allowing a start","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling","value":"Mechanical cooling below 55°F requires low-ambient operating mode (outdoor fan cycling to maintain head pressure)","key":"low_ambient_cool"},{"label":"Heating soft lockout","value":"Triggered after 3 low-pressure trips with OAT <-10°F; clears above -10°F","key":"low_ambient_heat"}]},{"title":"EcoNet / Inverter Status & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Status/fault display","value":"Dual 7-segment LED: operating codes c/C/h/H/d/0; fault codes include L8, L15, L16, L21, 27/28, L29, 31","key":"econet_status"},{"label":"Communicating vs conventional","value":"Runs EcoNet communicating (R/C/E1/E2) or with a conventional 24V thermostat","key":"econet_wiring"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See charging chart on unit access panel — see rating plate","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Rheem/Ruud defrost control boards include a 2-pin TEST header. With a heating call active, short the TEST pins with an insulated screwdriver or jumper for 5–7 seconds — reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan turns off, and W (aux heat) energizes, confirming defrost engaged. Some board revisions require a short, momentary release (~1 sec), then a second short to actually trigger the test — if the first short doesn't take, remove and reapply. If 24V is present at the board but the TEST short still won't force defrost, the board is likely faulty. Source: Rheem heat pump service/troubleshooting literature (Rheem 15PJL series 92-20522-80-05 doc referenced in pts.myrheem.com) plus corroborating HVAC-Talk and JustAnswer field threads — the specific OEM PDF could not be parsed directly this session, so confirm pin layout against the installed board's printed legend."},{"label":"EcoNet communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. EcoNet-enabled outdoor units add an outdoor-unit test screen in the EcoNet Control Center app (as of software v60) that can lock compressor speed for testing, but no source located documented a dedicated 'force defrost' command through the EcoNet app or wall control. Use the physical TEST-pin method on the outdoor board instead, or confirm current app capability directly with Rheem/EcoNet support before relying on an app-based method."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, the outdoor coil should be at/below the board's frost cut-in for a natural (non-forced) defrost to latch; the TEST-pin method is designed to bypass that. When forced defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may energize — warn of the normal cold-air burst from supply registers during the test, and don't leave the unit in forced defrost longer than necessary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RP15 / RP14 Standard Heat Pump","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Standard single-stage R-410A heat pump condensing unit (Rheem Classic / Ruud Achiever series) with fixed-orifice or TXV-matched indoor coil and enhanced demand defrost.","match":["RP13","RP14","RP15"],"source":"Rheem R-410A Heat Pump Outdoor Units — Installation Instructions ((-)P13/(-)P14/(-)P15), Form 92-105074-04-08 (9/16), pts.myrheem.com.","flags":[{"title":"Ruud sells this line under the SAME 'RP' prefix","body":"Unlike some Rheem/Ruud pairs, Ruud markets this Achiever-series heat pump directly as RP13/RP14/RP15 (ruud.com product pages) rather than a separate 'UP' prefix — don't assume a UP13/14/15 twin exists."},{"title":"Reversing valve state not documented in this manual","body":"This IOM does not state the RV energized mode explicitly. Rheem's inverter-series IOM (RP20) documents the B terminal as energized-in-HEATING for this brand family — verify at the unit wiring diagram/rating plate before assuming a different (O-type) convention."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Matched indoor coil uses a flow-check piston (fixed orifice), sized to outdoor unit tonnage per the piston-size table in the IOM; some indoor coil matches use a TXV — confirm at rating plate/spec sheet","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Enhanced Feature Demand Defrost Control","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Initiation","value":"Outdoor coil temp <35°F AND compressor run-time ≥34 min, plus onboard differential calc","key":"defrost_init"},{"label":"Termination","value":"14 min max, or coil reaches termination temp — factory default 70°F, field-adjustable to 50/60/80°F via control-board jumper","key":"defrost_term"}]},{"title":"Pressure Controls & Crankcase Heat","rows":[{"label":"High pressure cutout / cut-in","value":"Auto-reset: opens ≈610 psig / closes ≈420 psig","key":"hpc"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout / cut-in","value":"Auto-reset: opens ≈15 psig / closes ≈40 psig","key":"lpc"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Not standard on all models — factory-installed only above certain system-charge thresholds per the compressor table in the IOM; add a field CCH kit if total charge exceeds that threshold","key":"crankcase"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Low-ambient cooling","value":"Not rated for mechanical cooling below ≈70°F ambient without the Low Ambient Control accessory kit (RXAD-A08), which cycles the OD fan off at ≈250 psig head pressure and extends cooling operation down to 0°F","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See nameplate/charging chart — subcooling method — see rating plate","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Rheem/Ruud defrost control boards include a 2-pin TEST header. With a heating call active, short the TEST pins with an insulated screwdriver or jumper for 5–7 seconds — reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan turns off, and W (aux heat) energizes, confirming defrost engaged. Some board revisions require a short, momentary release (~1 sec), then a second short to actually trigger the test — if the first short doesn't take, remove and reapply. If 24V is present at the board but the TEST short still won't force defrost, the board is likely faulty. Source: Rheem heat pump service/troubleshooting literature (Rheem 15PJL series 92-20522-80-05 doc referenced in pts.myrheem.com) plus corroborating HVAC-Talk and JustAnswer field threads — the specific OEM PDF could not be parsed directly this session, so confirm pin layout against the installed board's printed legend."},{"label":"EcoNet communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. EcoNet-enabled outdoor units add an outdoor-unit test screen in the EcoNet Control Center app (as of software v60) that can lock compressor speed for testing, but no source located documented a dedicated 'force defrost' command through the EcoNet app or wall control. Use the physical TEST-pin method on the outdoor board instead, or confirm current app capability directly with Rheem/EcoNet support before relying on an app-based method."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, the outdoor coil should be at/below the board's frost cut-in for a natural (non-forced) defrost to latch; the TEST-pin method is designed to bypass that. When forced defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may energize — warn of the normal cold-air burst from supply registers during the test, and don't leave the unit in forced defrost longer than necessary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RH2T / RHMV EcoNet Air Handler","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"EcoNet-enabled communicating air handler family: RH2T (two-stage constant-torque ECM) and RHMV (variable-speed communicating ECM), both using an electronic expansion valve.","match":["RH2T","RHMV"],"source":"Rheem (-)H2T / (-)HMV EcoNet Enabled Air Handlers — Installation and Operation Manual, Form 92-20521-102-05 (1/2017), pts.myrheem.com. Ruud markets this family under the same RH2T name (media.ruud.com air handler product-comparison brochure).","flags":[{"title":"EXV thermistor placement — galvanic corrosion trap","body":"The copper vapor-line thermistor/EXV sensing bulb must clamp at the 10-2 o'clock position on a horizontal section of COPPER vapor line, never on the aluminum tube — contact with aluminum causes galvanic corrosion and eventual tube failure."},{"title":"EXV step dip switch must stay at 500-step","body":"The EXV control has a 500/1600-step dip switch. Rheem does not currently supply 1600-step EXVs — the switch must remain at 500-step. It exists only for forward compatibility."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"RH2T: two-stage constant-torque ECM. RHMV: variable-speed communicating ECM","key":"blower"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV/EXV), 500-step","key":"metering"},{"label":"Factory-programmed superheat","value":"6°F standard (8°F on select models, e.g. 3621ME) — verify on the specific model's dip-switch table","key":"superheat"}]},{"title":"Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Airflow trim","value":"EcoNet Control Center, or onboard TRIM dip switches for ±10% trim","key":"airflow_trim"},{"label":"Conventional (non-communicating) operation","value":"CFM/PAF dip-switch selection when run with a conventional thermostat instead of EcoNet","key":"airflow_conventional"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"Optimal 0.3–0.7 in. W.C.; performance tables extend to 1.0 in. W.C.","key":"max_static"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat, Filter & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Electric heat kits","value":"RXBH kits, 3–30 kW — dip-switch HTR selection must match the airflow table to the installed heater kW","key":"heat_kit"},{"label":"Filter","value":"NOT factory installed — external filter/rack required, sized for max 300 ft/min face velocity","key":"filter"},{"label":"Drain","value":"Primary 3/4\" FPT + auxiliary; secondary overflow pan kit (RXBM) required for horizontal installs over finished/living space","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RH1T / RH2T Standard Air Handler (non-communicating)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Standard, non-communicating constant-torque ECM air handler family with aluminum coil — RH1T (single stage) and RH2T (two stage), metered by TEV, EEV, or piston depending on model suffix.","match":["RH1T","RH2T","RHLL","RHSL","HLA","HSA"],"source":"Rheem (-)H1T High Efficiency / (-)H2T High Efficiency 2-Stage Air Handlers — Installation Instructions, Form 92-20521-66-09 (1/2017), pts.myrheem.com.","flags":[{"title":"RHLL/HLA/HSA legacy PSC family not directly verified in this document","body":"RHLL/HLA/HSA are older PSC-motor cabinets covered by a separate, older Rheem 'Indoor Air Handlers' manual (files.rheem.com Form 7081940), not the RH1T/RH2T constant-torque manual cited here. Cross-check figures for those specific prefixes against the unit rating plate — treat this entry's numbers as representative of the RH1T/RH2T constant-torque family only."},{"title":"Reversing valve energized in HEATING — confirmed for this platform","body":"Directly stated in this manual's heat-pump sequence of operation: 'Circuit R and B energizes the reversing valve (RV) switching it to the heating position (remains energized as long as selector switch is in heat position).' This is opposite the 'O' (energized-in-cooling) convention common on many other brands."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Constant Torque ECM, 5-speed tap selectable. Factory ships at speed tap 5 (except -4824 model, shipped at tap 3); low-static taps used below 0.5\" W.C., high-static taps above","key":"blower"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Set by model-number suffix: T=TEV, E=EEV, P=Piston (see rating plate). Piston sizes range .049–.078 in. depending on tonnage match","key":"metering"},{"label":"TEV bulb placement","value":"Clamp at 10-2 o'clock on a horizontal section of COPPER vapor line — never on the aluminum tube (galvanic corrosion trap)","key":"tev_bulb"}]},{"title":"Airflow & Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"Optimal 0.3–0.7 in. W.C.; minimum 0.1 in. W.C. with coil installed","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Electric heat kits","value":"RXBH kits, 2.25–30 kW depending on cabinet size. 13kW+ kits: jumper W1/W2 for max outlet temperature rise. Max heat rise limited per cabinet (51–80°F range depending on model)","key":"heat_kit"}]},{"title":"Reversing Valve, Drain & Filter","rows":[{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"HEATING (B terminal) — see flag","key":"rv_mode"},{"label":"Drain","value":"Primary + auxiliary 3/4\" FPT; secondary/auxiliary horizontal overflow pan (RXBM) recommended when coil is over living space","key":"drain"},{"label":"Filter","value":"NOT factory installed — external filter required, max 300 ft/min face velocity","key":"filter"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DZ20VC","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Inverter (variable-speed) heat pump condenser, R-410A, on the *VZC20 communicating platform (ComfortBridge/ComfortNet). Charges via dedicated Charge Mode, not by gauging cold. No mechanical low-pressure switch — low side is transducer/software monitored.","match":["daikin","dz20vc","dz18vc","vzc20","inverter heat pump","comfortbridge","comfortnet","daikin fit","coolcloud"],"source":"Daikin \"Service and Troubleshooting – *VZC20 Inverter Heat Pump Condenser Units with R-410A Refrigerant\" (doc RS6215002r9), Daikin document CDN: https://cdn.daikincloud.io/PIM/Assets/Documents/RS6215002r9.pdf (mirrors the same daikincomfort.com-issued service literature; the legacy daikincomfort.com/backend path for this doc is currently offline)","flags":[{"title":"Charge Mode required — don't gauge-charge cold","body":"This platform must be charged using the system's CHARGE MODE (thermostat CR9/SUt menu, outdoor PCB pushbuttons, or the CoolCloud HVAC app), which runs the compressor at 100% capacity for about 1 hour. Only adjust to the 8°F ± 1°F subcooling target while in Charge Mode, and only when outdoor ambient is between 65°F and 105°F. Outside that ambient range, weigh in the charge per the installation manual's line-length chart instead of using subcooling."},{"title":"No mechanical low-pressure switch on this platform","body":"The low side is monitored by a HI/LOW pressure transducer read by the control board (fault code E26 = pressure sensor fault), not a fixed mechanical low-pressure cutout switch. There is no low-pressure switch cutout psig spec to test here — don't go looking for one."},{"title":"Compressor low-ambient lockout is set by line-set length","body":"The recommended heating compressor lockout temperature is entered at the ComfortNet/CTK04 thermostat (Installer Options > Compressor Lockout/Balance Point) and depends on line-set length: 15°F for 0–100 ft runs, 20°F for 100–200 ft runs."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV (TXV-matched indoor coil) or factory electronic expansion valve (EEV) in a matched ComfortBridge communicating indoor unit; outdoor unit also carries an EEV that meters refrigerant to the outdoor coil during heating","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Time/temperature (control-board managed), demand-assisted","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Defrost interval","value":"Selectable at thermostat: 30, 60, 90, or 120 minutes","key":"defrost_interval"},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"Coil thermistor (Tm) at/above ~54°F AND defrost sensor (Tb) above 43°F held 30 seconds; coil & defrost temps checked every 5 sec in heating mode","key":"defrost_termination"},{"label":"Manual defrost","value":"\"Force Defrost\" selectable from thermostat","key":"defrost_manual"}]},{"title":"Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Energized mode","value":"Energized in cooling; de-energized in heating (standard convention on this platform)","key":"rv_energized"}]},{"title":"Pressure Controls","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Cuts out at approximately 605 PSIG per the manual's HPS check procedure; automatic reset (exact factory tolerance did not extract cleanly from the source PDF — confirm against your printed copy before relying on it)","key":"hp_cutout"},{"label":"Low-pressure protection","value":"No mechanical switch; monitored via HI/LOW pressure transducer + control board logic (see flag)","key":"lp_cutout"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Lockout","rows":[{"label":"Compressor lockout (0–100 ft line set)","value":"15°F, set at thermostat","key":"lockout_short"},{"label":"Compressor lockout (100–200 ft line set)","value":"20°F, set at thermostat","key":"lockout_long"}]},{"title":"Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Type","value":"Optional accessory, positive-temperature-coefficient (PTC), 33W @ 240V, ~1745 Ω cold resistance","key":"cch_type"},{"label":"Pre-start soak time","value":"Energize a minimum of 2 hours before operating the unit","key":"cch_soak"}]},{"title":"Inverter / Communicating","rows":[{"label":"Communication","value":"ComfortBridge™ and ComfortNet™ ready; diagnostics/setup via CoolCloud HVAC app or CTK04 communicating thermostat","key":"comm_notes"},{"label":"Boost Mode","value":"Adjustable activation 70–105°F, or \"Always ON\"; ON by default","key":"boost_mode"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Method","value":"Dedicated CHARGE MODE (thermostat CR9/SUt menu, outdoor PCB pushbuttons, or CoolCloud app) — not standard gauge charging","key":"charge_method"},{"label":"Subcooling target (TXV, in Charge Mode, 65–105°F ambient)","value":"8°F ± 1°F","key":"charge_subcool"},{"label":"Outside 65–105°F ambient","value":"Weigh in charge per installation manual's line-length chart","key":"charge_weighin"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"PARTIALLY verifiable only. Daikin's DZ6VSA (Daikin Fit family) service reference lists a defrost-board configuration parameter literally named 'Force Defrost Cycle' with two states (0:ON / 1:OFF), indicating it's a field-configurable setting rather than a simple momentary-jumper test — but the exact DIP switch bank/pin location and how the ON state behaves (one-shot vs. persistent) could not be confirmed from the accessible manual excerpt this session. Do NOT guess the switch position or pin numbers — pull the full Daikin DZ6VSA (or applicable model) Installation & Service Reference and locate the 'Force Defrost Cycle' setting in the defrost-board configuration table before using it in the field. Source: Daikin DZ6VSA 1EA Series Installation & Service Reference (ManualsLib-hosted copy)."},{"label":"Daikin One+ communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. The Daikin One+ thermostat has a 'System Test' function used for inverter calibration (5–15 minutes, must not be interrupted, master zone-1 thermostat only, all other zone stats set OFF) and a general service/diagnostics menu, but no source located confirmed a dedicated, documented 'force defrost' command distinct from that calibration test. Do not treat System Test as a defrost-force procedure without confirming with current Daikin service documentation for the specific communicating outdoor unit."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, expect any genuine forced-defrost test to require (or bypass) a cold coil condition, and to shift the reversing valve to cooling and stop the outdoor fan — a burst of cold supply air is normal during the test. Because the exact Daikin force-defrost mechanics aren't fully confirmed here, verify against the specific unit's Installation & Service Reference before performing a live test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DZ16SA / DZ14SA","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Standard (non-inverter) single/two-capacity split-system heat pump, R-410A, TXV metering, legacy solid-state time/temperature defrost board. Crankcase heater soak time and low-pressure cutout figures differ from the newer inverter platform — don't cross-apply specs.","match":["daikin","dz16sa","dz14sa","dz16","dz14","standard heat pump","single stage heat pump","solid state defrost"],"source":"Daikin \"Service Instructions – DAR09, DAR12, DAT09, DAT12, DX11, DX13, DX14, DX15, DX16 Condensing Units, DZ11, DZ13, DZ14, DZ16 Split System Heat Pumps with R-410A Refrigerant\" (doc RSD6200006r47, Feb 2021): https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/chpf/rsd6200006r47.pdf","flags":[{"title":"LPCO cut points differ for heat pump vs. A/C-only","body":"The Low Pressure Cut Out (LPCO) switch trips at approximately 21 PSIG on heat pump models but approximately 55 PSIG on cooling-only (A/C) models built on this same platform, and recloses at approximately 50 PSIG (heat pump) or approximately 95 PSIG (A/C). Confirm which unit type you're on before condemning the switch."},{"title":"Crankcase heater soak time is 4 hours here, not 2","body":"This platform's optional PTC crankcase heater must be energized a minimum of 4 hours before start-up — longer than the 2-hour spec on the newer *VZC20/DZ20VC inverter platform. Don't apply the newer unit's timing to this one."},{"title":"Low-ambient heating needs an accessory kit","body":"Standard DZ14/DZ16 units are not rated to run below 0°F outdoor ambient at 50% or higher relative humidity without the LAKT-01 Low Ambient Kit accessory installed — verify it's present before troubleshooting nuisance lockouts or icing in cold climates."},{"title":"Charging figures are from the platform-wide service manual, not a DZ16/DZ14-specific chart","body":"RSD6200006r47 covers the whole DAR/DAT/DX/DZ11-16 R-410A platform and gives one generic TXV subcooling/superheat target (7-9°F/7-9°F) rather than a DZ16SA/DZ14SA-specific design-subcooling table. Cross-check against the unit's own rating plate/spec sheet if a model-specific design subcooling value is stamped there."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV (matched TXV-kit coil; nomenclature \"T\" suffix). Accessory TXV kits: TX2N4A, TX3N4x, TX5N4x","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Solid-state time/temperature defrost, jointly controlled by the defrost control board and a bimetal defrost thermostat","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Defrost interval","value":"Selectable via circuit-board jumper: 30, 60, or 90 minutes","key":"defrost_interval"},{"label":"Defrost start/stop","value":"Defrost sensor closes at approximately 31°F to begin timing; cycle initiates at end of selected interval if sensor still closed; terminates when sensor opens at approximately 75°F","key":"defrost_termination"},{"label":"Defrost override","value":"10-minute override interrupt on standard board; 12-minute override interrupt on the upgraded solid-state defrost control revision","key":"defrost_override"}]},{"title":"Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Energized mode","value":"Energized in cooling (through the thermostat's \"O\" terminal), de-energized in heating","key":"rv_energized"}]},{"title":"Pressure Controls","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Cuts out at 610 PSIG ± 10 PSIG; automatic reset","key":"hp_cutout"},{"label":"Low-pressure cutout (LPCO) — heat pump","value":"Cuts out ~21 PSIG, recloses (cuts in) ~50 PSIG","key":"lp_cutout_hp"},{"label":"Low-pressure cutout (LPCO) — A/C-only variant","value":"Cuts out ~55 PSIG, recloses (cuts in) ~95 PSIG","key":"lp_cutout_ac"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"Below 0°F @ ≥50% RH","value":"Requires LAKT-01 Low Ambient Kit accessory","key":"low_ambient_kit"},{"label":"Compressor lockout control","value":"Optional Outdoor Thermostat w/ Lockout Stat, accessory OT18-60A3","key":"lockout_accessory"}]},{"title":"Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Type","value":"Optional accessory, positive-temperature-coefficient (PTC)","key":"cch_type"},{"label":"Pre-start soak time","value":"Energize a minimum of 4 hours before operating the unit","key":"cch_soak"}]},{"title":"Compressor Notes","rows":[{"label":"Two-capacity models","value":"Some DZ16 \"Special High Feature\" models unload via a compressor solenoid: full (100%) capacity when solenoid is energized, reduced capacity when de-energized — confirm capacity type on the nameplate/model number before assuming single-stage behavior","key":"compressor_capacity"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"PARTIALLY verifiable only. Daikin's DZ6VSA (Daikin Fit family) service reference lists a defrost-board configuration parameter literally named 'Force Defrost Cycle' with two states (0:ON / 1:OFF), indicating it's a field-configurable setting rather than a simple momentary-jumper test — but the exact DIP switch bank/pin location and how the ON state behaves (one-shot vs. persistent) could not be confirmed from the accessible manual excerpt this session. Do NOT guess the switch position or pin numbers — pull the full Daikin DZ6VSA (or applicable model) Installation & Service Reference and locate the 'Force Defrost Cycle' setting in the defrost-board configuration table before using it in the field. Source: Daikin DZ6VSA 1EA Series Installation & Service Reference (ManualsLib-hosted copy)."},{"label":"Daikin One+ communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. The Daikin One+ thermostat has a 'System Test' function used for inverter calibration (5–15 minutes, must not be interrupted, master zone-1 thermostat only, all other zone stats set OFF) and a general service/diagnostics menu, but no source located confirmed a dedicated, documented 'force defrost' command distinct from that calibration test. Do not treat System Test as a defrost-force procedure without confirming with current Daikin service documentation for the specific communicating outdoor unit."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, expect any genuine forced-defrost test to require (or bypass) a cold coil condition, and to shift the reversing valve to cooling and stop the outdoor fan — a burst of cold supply air is normal during the test. Because the exact Daikin force-defrost mechanics aren't fully confirmed here, verify against the specific unit's Installation & Service Reference before performing a live test."}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method (TXV)","value":"Subcooling AND superheat method (Sections S-108/S-109): adjust TXV to 7-9°F superheat, then verify subcooling — target 7-9°F subcooling / 7-9°F superheat, measured at the liquid line (service valve) and suction line (4-6\" from compressor). General factory-set expansion-valve range (all TXV platforms in this manual) is 8-12°F superheat.","key":true},{"label":"Charging formulas","value":"Superheat = Suction Line Temp. − Sat. Suction Temp.; Subcooling = Sat. Liquid Temp. − Liquid Line Temp."},{"label":"Light-load caution","value":"Do not adjust the TXV at light-load conditions (55-60°F outdoor) — only subcooling is reliable to evaluate there. Do not adjust charge based on suction pressure alone unless there is a gross undercharge."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DV*PEC / DV*FEC (EEV Series)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position, variable-speed ECM air handler with factory-installed EEV, built for full ComfortBridge communication with a matched Daikin inverter outdoor unit (e.g. DZ20VC-class). Airflow/CFM is NOT set with dip switches like a conventional air handler — it's requested digitally from the outdoor unit.","match":["daikin","dvpec","dvfec","avpec","eev air handler","comfortbridge air handler","variable speed air handler","ecm air handler","daikin fit air handler"],"source":"Daikin \"Installation Instructions – DV**PEC / DV**FEC (EEV Series Air Handlers)\" (doc IOD-4018M): https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dvpec/iod-4018m.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No CFM dip switches — airflow is set at the OUTDOOR unit","body":"Unlike a conventional air handler, base airflow/CFM-per-ton on this ComfortBridge-communicating platform is not configured with dip switches on the air handler board — it's requested digitally by the matched outdoor unit. Field \"Airflow Trim\" up/down adjustment is made from the OUTDOOR unit's user menu, per the install manual, not on the air handler itself."},{"title":"Don't trust the displayed CFM for trim limits","body":"The install manual explicitly warns: for the Maximum CFM airflow-trim limits (per model, listed by Up-Flow/Down-Flow/Horizontal), use the actual measured CFM at the install site — not the outdoor unit's spec-sheet value, the communicating thermostat's status-menu CFM, or the PCB LED display, since there can be a tolerance gap between displayed and actual measured airflow."},{"title":"Condensate/auxiliary alarm switch is normally closed, fails safe","body":"The Auxiliary Alarm switch (terminals TB4/TB5 — typically a condensate float switch, though CO or fire-alarm contacts can also be wired here) is normally closed and opens on trip (e.g., high condensate level). On trip, the control shuts off the blower and outdoor unit and posts a fault; it auto-resumes only after the switch reads closed continuously for 30 seconds. A switch that reads open at rest is wired backwards or faulty — not \"safe.\""}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower","rows":[{"label":"Motor type","value":"ECM (electronically commutated), variable-speed, communicating","key":"blower_motor"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Digital — requested by the matched outdoor unit over the communicating link; field trim adjustment is done from the OUTDOOR unit's user menu (see flag), not via air handler dip switches","key":"airflow_setup"}]},{"title":"Airflow Limits (example models)","rows":[{"label":"DV24FECB14 max CFM (Up/Down/Horiz.)","value":"910 / 870 / 870","key":"cfm_24"},{"label":"DV36FECC14 / DV35FECC14 max CFM (Up/Down/Horiz.)","value":"1450 / 1390 / 1390","key":"cfm_36"},{"label":"DV48FECD14 / DV47FECD14 max CFM (Up/Down/Horiz.)","value":"1590 / 1520 / 1520","key":"cfm_48"},{"label":"DV60FECD14 / DV59FECD14 max CFM (Up/Down/Horiz.)","value":"1890 / 1800 / 1800","key":"cfm_60"}]},{"title":"Static Pressure","rows":[{"label":"Max external static (single published figure)","value":"see install manual's model-specific blower performance tables","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Downflow Kit (DFK) requirement","value":"Required in downflow applications where total external static exceeds 0.5\" e.s.p., to prevent coil-pan sweating","key":"downflow_kit_esp"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Requirement","value":"Return air filter mandatory (factory rail or external return-air grille)","key":"filter_required"},{"label":"Factory filter rail sizes","value":"Nominal 16x20x1\", 20x20x1\", or 24x20x1\" (actual filter dimension must be under 23-1/2\" x 20\")","key":"filter_size"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Approved kits","value":"Daikin-produced heat kits only","key":"heat_kit_approved"},{"label":"Staging/sizing selection","value":"Cabinet-specific DIP switches select which heater-kit sizes are \"valid\" for that air handler width (e.g., DV25PECB14 valid kit codes 3, 5, 6, 8, 10 kW positions) — see manual's per-model DIP table and the Heater Kit (HKS) Installation Instructions for breaker/circuit sizing","key":"heat_kit_staging"}]},{"title":"Metering","rows":[{"label":"Device","value":"Factory-installed electronic expansion valve (EEV) on the indoor coil, non-adjustable, factory set","key":"metering_device"},{"label":"Matching","value":"Must be paired with a compatible communicating (ComfortBridge) outdoor unit — e.g. DZ20VC-class *VZC20 inverter heat pump/condenser","key":"metering_match"}]},{"title":"Drain / Safety Switch","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Primary and secondary (auxiliary) drain ports on the coil drain pan; secondary/auxiliary drain line mandatory in locations where condensate overflow could cause damage","key":"drain_config"},{"label":"Auxiliary Alarm switch","value":"Terminals TB4/TB5, normally closed, opens on trip (see flag for behavior)","key":"aux_alarm_switch"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"ICP","model":"CVH8/HVH8/TVH8 (Ion, R-410A Variable-Speed, Observer-compatible)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"ICP variable-speed inverter heat pump (Comfortmaker Ion, Heil Ion 18, Tempstar). AOC control board drives a variable-speed rotary compressor + EXV; runs full diagnostics only with the Observer Wall Control (2-wire communicating).","match":["HVH8","CVH8","TVH8","HVA9","CVA9","TVA9","Heil Ion","Heil Ion 18","Comfortmaker Ion","Tempstar Ion","Observer","Observer Wall Control","Arcoaire","Day & Night","KeepRite","AirQuest"],"source":"ICP Application Guideline & Service Manual, CVH8/HVH8/TVH8/CVA9/HVA9/TVA9, part# 421 08 5600 02, 1/18/2017 (shareddocs.com)","flags":[{"title":"Confirmed brands only: C/H/T","body":"This service manual documents Comfortmaker (C), Heil (H), and Tempstar (T) badges only (CVH8/HVH8/TVH8). No Arcoaire, Day & Night, KeepRite, or AirQuest variant of this Ion platform appears in this document - confirm the nameplate model prefix before assuming compatibility with the figures below."},{"title":"EXV in heating, TXV in cooling - two different metering devices","body":"The outdoor AOC board drives an Electronic Expansion Valve (EXV) for metering in HEATING mode only. The matched indoor fan coil/furnace coil carries its own factory bi-flow, hard-shutoff TXV that meters in COOLING mode. Do not confuse the two when troubleshooting a metering fault."},{"title":"Reversing valve energized = cooling/defrost","body":"Per Fig. 40/41 of the service manual: solenoid ENERGIZED = cooling mode or defrost mode; solenoid DE-ENERGIZED = heating mode. Defrost briefly puts the unit in the cooling flow path."},{"title":"Charging: nameplate + charts only, never invent a number","body":"Cooling charge is checked against the unit-specific subcooling chart printed on the control-box door (service manual Fig. 9-21, one chart per tonnage/SEER). Heating charge is WEIGH-IN ONLY per rating plate +/-0.6 oz per ft of 3/8 in. liquid line vs. a 15 ft baseline - the manual explicitly says 'DO NOT USE CHART TO ADJUST REFRIGERANT CHARGE' for the heating pressure check chart (it is for verification only)."},{"title":"Full 2-digit fault code table in service manual","body":"Amber STATUS LED flashes short-then-long digit pairs (e.g., 3 short + 2 long = code 32, Low Pressure Trip). Common codes: 25 wrong/missing model plug, 31/84 high pressure switch open/lockout, 32/83 low pressure trip/lockout, 46 brownout, 56 OAT-OCT thermistor out of range, 74 discharge temp lockout. Full cause/action list is service manual Table 6 (pages 14-21) - too long to reproduce here, reference the source doc."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering - heating (outdoor)","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EXV), AOC-controlled","key":"metering_heat"},{"label":"Metering - cooling (indoor)","value":"Factory TXV, bi-flow, hard-shutoff, external equalizer (at matched fan coil/furnace coil)","key":"metering_cool"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost control","value":"AOC board + Outdoor Coil Thermistor (OCT); Observer Wall Control selectable 30/60/90 min or AUTO (default AUTO)","key":"defrost_control"},{"label":"AUTO interval logic","value":"Last defrost <5 min -> next 90 min (if OAT>37F); 5-7 min -> next 60 min; >7 min -> next 30 min; first interval after power-up defaults to 30 min","key":"defrost_auto"},{"label":"Defrost demand","value":"Coil temp <=32F (0C) for 4 continuous minutes during interval; defrost only permitted below 50F (10C) OAT","key":"defrost_demand"},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"OAT >25F: OCT >60F & min 1 min run; OAT <=25F: OCT >45F & min 2 min run; or 10 min max","key":"defrost_term"}]},{"title":"Reversing Valve / Pressures","rows":[{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Energized = COOLING or DEFROST; De-energized = HEATING","key":"revvalve"},{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Open 600 +/-5 psig, Close 470 +/-10 psig @ 77F (fault 31, lockout 84 after repeated trips)","key":"hp_cutout"},{"label":"Low pressure protection","value":"Suction transducer trips <15 psig any time or <33 psig for 5 min; resumes >43 psig cooling / >35 psig heating (fault 32, lockout 83)","key":"lp_cutout"},{"label":"Low-ambient note","value":"No stated fixed compressor lockout temp in this manual; defrost itself is locked out above 50F OAT - see rating plate for any low-ambient kit requirement","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Crankcase Heater / Diagnostics / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Internal, AOC-controlled; energizes intelligently during off-cycle (stator heat) whenever outdoor unit is powered - no fixed ambient threshold published","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Status/diagnostics","value":"Amber STATUS LED = 2-digit flash fault codes (short=1st digit, long=2nd digit); Green COMM LED = communication with Observer Wall Control; codes recallable via 'force defrost' J2 short + power-on","key":"diagnostics"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Nameplate factory charge for 15 ft line set +/-0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 liquid line; cooling via unit-specific subcooling chart (OAT 65-100F, IAT 70-80F); heating by weigh-in only, do not adjust from pressure chart","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"ICP (Heil/Tempstar/Comfortmaker/Arcoaire/Keeprite) has been part of the Carrier Corporation family since 1999, and its heat pump defrost boards are the same HK32EA/CEPL13xxxx board family used on Carrier/Bryant equipment (an ICP-specific 'Defrost Board Testing Sheet' technical bulletin exists confirming this board family, though it could not be fetched/parsed directly this session). Treat the Carrier/Bryant non-communicating procedure above (short the Forced Defrost/Speed-Up 2-pin header 5+ seconds, remove once the valve shifts) as applicable, but confirm against the exact board's printed pin legend, since ICP-branded boards sometimes carry different part-number silkscreens than Carrier-branded ones even when electrically identical. Source: ICP board part-number cross-reference commonly documented by HVAC parts suppliers (e.g. GSIstore/North America HVAC listings for HK32EA/CEPL-family ICP boards) plus the Carrier-family procedure above."},{"label":"Ion communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. ICP's Ion Black/Ion Gray communicating thermostats and the associated System Control communicate with ICP equipment over a 4-wire bus, but no source located documented an exact menu path or button sequence for forcing a defrost cycle through the Ion control. Do not invent a menu sequence — consult the specific Ion System Control Installation Manual, or use the physical board-level test-pin method above if the outdoor unit is accessible."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Same as Carrier: coil sensor should be cold (near/below freezing) for a natural defrost to latch, though the forced test-pin method is designed to override timing (not necessarily the coil-temp check on every board revision). Reversing valve shifts to cooling and outdoor fan stops during defrost — a cold-air burst indoors is expected and normal."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"ICP","model":"N4H3/N4H4/H4H4/T4H4/C4H4/NXH5-series (Standard Single-Stage Split Heat Pump)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"ICP standard single-stage split-system heat pump (non-branded N-prefix base platform, rebadged as Heil/Tempstar/Comfortmaker H/T/C-prefix equivalents). Mechanical defrost thermostat + timer board; diagnostic module is a factory option, not standard.","match":["N4H3","N4H4","C4H3","C4H4","H4H3","H4H4","T4H3","T4H4","NXH5","CXH5","HXH5","TXH5","Heil","Tempstar","Comfortmaker","Arcoaire","Day & Night","KeepRite","AirQuest"],"source":"ICP Installation Instructions, R-410A Split System Heat Pump N4H3/C4H3/H4H3/T4H3/N4H4/NXH5/CXH5/HXH5/TXH5, part# 428 01 5106 00, 12/13/12 (shareddocs.com); charging chart & wiring legend cross-ref: ICP Technical Support Manual, Split System Heat Pump N4H4, part# 428 04 5201 00, Aug 2009 (shareddocs.com)","flags":[{"title":"No diagnostic board unless Comfort Alert is factory-installed","body":"Per install instructions p.20/21: 'Some models are factory equipped with the Comfort Alert Diagnostics device.' It is NOT standard across this platform. If the control box has no Comfort Alert module (Green POWER / Red TRIP / Yellow ALERT LED cluster), there is no fault-code capability at all on this unit - troubleshoot from voltage, pressure, and amperage checks only, do not go hunting for a status LED that isn't there."},{"title":"HPS/LPS may not be present - no fixed psig published","body":"The N4H4 Technical Support Manual wiring-diagram legend marks *HPS (High Pressure Switch) and *LPS (Low Pressure Switch) with an asterisk meaning 'MAY BE FACTORY OR FIELD INSTALLED' - i.e., not guaranteed present. Unlike the AOC variable-speed platform (which publishes 600/470 psig), no fixed HPS/LPS cut-out/cut-in psig is published for this standard platform - see rating plate or unit-specific spec sheet."},{"title":"Reversing valve energized in COOLING","body":"Per Sequence of Operation (install instructions p.20): a call for cooling makes circuit R-O, which energizes the reversing valve to the cooling position. A call for heating does NOT make R-O, so the valve stays de-energized in the heating position - same convention as the variable-speed Ion platform above."},{"title":"Two different metering devices on one heat pump","body":"Cooling metering is at the INDOOR coil (TXV or piston w/Teflon ring, per unit rating plate). Heating metering is a SEPARATE piston shipped inside the outdoor unit's liquid service valve body - it is used only in heating mode and is independent of whatever the indoor coil uses for cooling."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering - cooling (indoor)","value":"TXV or piston w/ Teflon ring at indoor coil - must match unit rating plate; do not mix R-22 and R-410A TXVs","key":"metering_cool"},{"label":"Metering - heating (outdoor)","value":"Separate piston shipped in the liquid service valve body, sized per rating plate","key":"metering_heat"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost control","value":"Mechanical Defrost Thermostat (DFT, closes 32F/0C, opens 65F/18C) + time/temp defrost control board (not an electronic coil thermistor)","key":"defrost_control"},{"label":"Defrost interval","value":"Field-selectable jumper: 30, 60, or 90 minutes between cycles; factory set to 90 min; interval timer only runs during active heating calls","key":"defrost_interval"},{"label":"Defrost cycle length","value":"Fixed 10 minutes, not adjustable; ends early if DFT opens at 65F","key":"defrost_length"}]},{"title":"Reversing Valve / Pressures","rows":[{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Energized = COOLING (R-O circuit); de-energized/at rest = HEATING","key":"revvalve"},{"label":"High/low pressure switches","value":"Not published as fixed psig in this literature - HPS/LPS are optional (factory or field installed) per wiring legend - see rating plate","key":"hp_lp_cutout"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"No compressor low-ambient lockout temperature published in this document - see rating plate/accessories","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Crankcase Heater / Diagnostics / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Optional (factory or field installed per wiring legend *CH/*CHS); required when refrigerant line length exceeds 80 ft (24.4 m); energize 24 hrs before start-up if present","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Diagnostics","value":"Comfort Alert Diagnostics module on SOME models only: Green POWER / Red TRIP / Yellow ALERT LED with 9 flash codes (1=long run time, 2=system pressure trip, 3=short cycling, 4=locked rotor, 5=open circuit, 6=open start circuit, 7=open run circuit, 8=welded contactor, 9=low voltage)","key":"diagnostics"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Nameplate base charge for 15 ft line set +/-0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 liquid line; TXV units use subcooling method (chart vs. liquid pressure); Piston units use superheat method (charts by OAT/entering wet-bulb, weigh-in if chart shows '--'); heating-mode Tech Label chart is for verification only, never used to adjust charge","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"ICP (Heil/Tempstar/Comfortmaker/Arcoaire/Keeprite) has been part of the Carrier Corporation family since 1999, and its heat pump defrost boards are the same HK32EA/CEPL13xxxx board family used on Carrier/Bryant equipment (an ICP-specific 'Defrost Board Testing Sheet' technical bulletin exists confirming this board family, though it could not be fetched/parsed directly this session). Treat the Carrier/Bryant non-communicating procedure above (short the Forced Defrost/Speed-Up 2-pin header 5+ seconds, remove once the valve shifts) as applicable, but confirm against the exact board's printed pin legend, since ICP-branded boards sometimes carry different part-number silkscreens than Carrier-branded ones even when electrically identical. Source: ICP board part-number cross-reference commonly documented by HVAC parts suppliers (e.g. GSIstore/North America HVAC listings for HK32EA/CEPL-family ICP boards) plus the Carrier-family procedure above."},{"label":"Ion communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. ICP's Ion Black/Ion Gray communicating thermostats and the associated System Control communicate with ICP equipment over a 4-wire bus, but no source located documented an exact menu path or button sequence for forcing a defrost cycle through the Ion control. Do not invent a menu sequence — consult the specific Ion System Control Installation Manual, or use the physical board-level test-pin method above if the outdoor unit is accessible."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Same as Carrier: coil sensor should be cold (near/below freezing) for a natural defrost to latch, though the forced test-pin method is designed to override timing (not necessarily the coil-temp check on every board revision). Reversing valve shifts to cooling and outdoor fan stops during defrost — a cold-air burst indoors is expected and normal."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"ICP","model":"FEM4X-B (Fan Coil / Air Handler, ECM blower, TXV)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"ICP standard fan coil/air handler with high-efficiency ECM blower and factory TXV metering (X-suffix). Simple 24V cooling-control-only wiring - no diagnostic board on this line; only the separate communicating FCM fan-coil family carries fault codes.","match":["FEM4X","FEM4X18","FEM4X24","FEM4X30","FEM4X36","FEM4X42","FEM4X48","FEM4X60","FSM4X","FXM4X","FVM4X","FCM4X","FEM4P","FSU4P","Heil","Tempstar","Comfortmaker","Arcoaire","Day & Night","KeepRite","AirQuest"],"source":"ICP Technical Support Manual, Fan Coils FEM4X (B series), part# 496 04 5501 00, Jan. 2013 (shareddocs.com)","flags":[{"title":"No diagnostics on this platform - only communicating FCM has codes","body":"This FEM4X-B fan coil has no status/fault LED or communicating board; wiring diagram (337519-101 Rev. B) is a simple 24V thermostat hookup, 'COOLING CONTROL ONLY' labeled on the print. ICP's separate communicating FCM fan-coil family (paired with Observer/Ion variable-speed systems) is what carries diagnostic/status codes - do not expect fault codes on a standard FEM4X-B."},{"title":"Speed Tap 4 is reserved for electric heat","body":"Manual states verbatim: 'Speed Tap 4 (white wire) is used for electric heat only. White wire must remain on tap 4.' Moving it to boost cooling airflow will misconfigure the unit whenever an electric heat kit is installed."},{"title":"X = TXV, P = Piston - confirm nameplate suffix","body":"Model suffix X denotes factory TXV (confirmed via parts list: Key 06 'VALVE EXPANSION'/TXV on every FEM4X-B size). A parallel P-suffix sibling line (FEM4P) ships with a piston instead. Always confirm the nameplate suffix matches the metering device physically installed before charging - do not assume from the general FEM4X family name alone."},{"title":"No float/overflow switch mentioned in this document","body":"Parts list shows only a condensate pan (Key 09/10) and an optional PVC Condensate Trap Kit (CTK) accessory. No condensate float/overflow safety switch is referenced in this Technical Support Manual - see rating plate/install instructions or field-installed accessory kit list."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"High-efficiency ECM (E-suffix); 5 discrete speed taps (1-5) selected by moving a wire at the motor connector - not modulating/self-adjusting, not communicating","key":"blower_type"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"5 speed taps, CFM published per model/tap across 0.10-0.60 in. wc external static (Airflow Performance table, doc pg. 4)","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static tested","value":"0.60 in. wc is the highest static column tested; return static must stay <0.40 in. wc to avoid condensate blow-out; horizontal 4200-6000 sizes need supply static >0.20 in. wc","key":"max_static"}]},{"title":"Filter / Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Door-mounted filter; accessory Filter Kits FKS/FKM/FKL/FKX (small/medium/large/XL); FEM4X6000BT2 specifically uses a 21.5 x 19.875 x 1 in. filter - other exact sizes not published in this document, see rating plate/parts list","key":"filter"},{"label":"Electric heat staging","value":"EHK electric heater kits 5/7/9/10/15/18/20/25/30 kW; 2-element on 1800-3600 sizes, 3-element on 4200-6000 sizes; minimum CFM by heater kW published per model size (e.g. 3600B at 9 kW needs 970 CFM min)","key":"elec_heat"}]},{"title":"Metering / Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV, all FEM4X-B sizes (parts list Key 06 = 'VALVE EXPANSION'/TXV); confirm it matches the matched condenser/heat pump's expected metering","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain / float switch","value":"Condensate pan standard; optional PVC Condensate Trap Kit (CTK) accessory; no float/overflow switch referenced in this document","key":"drain"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Status/fault codes","value":"None - simple 24V cooling-control-only wiring, no board or LED for diagnostics on this FEM4X-B family","key":"diagnostics"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Bosch","model":"IDS BOVB20 Inverter Ducted Split Heat Pump (R-410A)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Bosch inverter-driven variable-speed heat pump, R-410A refrigerant, EEV metering in the outdoor unit (heating mode), extended low-ambient heating operation down to -4F. Indoor coil uses a TXV, not an EEV.","match":["bosch","ids","bova","bovb","bovb20","bova15","inverter ducted split","goliath"],"source":"Bosch IDS BOVB20 Split System Heat Pump Installation Instructions, BTC 761701316 E (11.2023) - bosch-homecomfort.com/us; cross-checked against Bosch IDS BOVA15 Installation Instructions, BTC 761701317 E (11.2023)","flags":[{"title":"Metering is EEV (ODU) + TXV (IDU) - do not treat as a TXV-only system","body":"Manual states: 'The variable speed system... Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) (ODU/heating mode only)' controls the outdoor metering device. The matched indoor coil/air handler instead requires a TXV: 'Indoor unit required! ...System TXV can be changed according to the system capacity.' Do not attempt to adjust an indoor TXV superheat setting expecting EEV behavior, and do not look for an indoor EEV board on these R-410A IDS systems."},{"title":"Same model designation covers both R-410A and R-454B - read the nameplate/date code","body":"The BOVA15 designation is used on both an R-410A unit (BTC 761701317 E, 11.2023) and a later R-454B 'IDS Light Series' unit (BTC 762003308 D, 01.2025) with different low-pressure protection thresholds and low-ambient limits. Confirm refrigerant type from the unit nameplate/data plate before connecting gauges or charging - never assume from the model prefix alone."},{"title":"Charging method is app-assisted subcooling, not a fixed superheat/subcool number","body":"Manual: 'Download and install the Bosch EasyAir app to assist in charging the unit. Subcooling (in cooling mode) is the only recommended method of charging above 55F outdoor ambient temperatures. For outdoor ambient temperatures below 55F use weigh-in charge method.' Design subcooling/superheat targets vary by tonnage (per-model Table 9/10 in the manual, e.g. approx. 4-8F subcool / 6-9F superheat) - pull the exact target for the specific tonnage from the manual/nameplate rather than using a single fleet-wide number."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (this document set) - verify on nameplate","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"EEV in outdoor unit (heating mode metering); TXV required in matched indoor coil/air handler","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor oil","value":"POE oil (VG74 or equivalent) - all R-410A variable-speed systems","key":"oil"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling method (cooling, outdoor ambient above 55F) via Bosch EasyAir app; weigh-in method below 55F ambient or at initial install","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Pressures & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High pressure cutout / cut-in","value":"Opens > 580 PSIG (compressor + OD fan stop); closes < 435 PSIG (mechanical pressure switch)","key":"hp_cutout"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout","value":"< 43.5 PSIG for 5 minutes during cooling mode -> compressor + OD fan stop; system retries after 6 minutes","key":"lp_cutout"},{"label":"Discharge temp protection (T5)","value":"Compressor restarts if DT < 194F (cooling) / < 167F (heating); stops if DT > 221F (heating)","key":"discharge_temp"},{"label":"Outdoor coil temp protection (T3)","value":"Compressor de-energized if T3 > 141.8F; re-energized if T3 < 129.2F","key":"coil_temp_protect"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand Defrost Control (DDC): coil thermistor T3 + outdoor ambient thermistor T4, run time, and pressure determine defrost initiation","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"Outdoor coil (T3) reaches 64F for 1 minute, or defrost time exceeds 8 minutes","key":"defrost_term"},{"label":"Manual/forced defrost","value":"Call for heat running >=1 min, then hold FORCE button on inverter board 6 seconds; display shows 'dF' during test","key":"manual_defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in heating mode; de-energized in cooling mode. Runs ~1 min in cooling on first heat call to build pressure before switching.","key":"revvalve"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Cooling operating range","value":"15F to 125F outdoor ambient (T4)","key":"low_ambient_cool"},{"label":"Heating operating range","value":"-4F to 86F outdoor ambient (T4)","key":"low_ambient_heat"},{"label":"Backup/emergency heat lockout","value":"Below -4F, unit provides 24V signal to indoor unit to energize electric heat (if installed) in place of compressor heating","key":"backup_heat"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Present; warms compressor during OFF cycle to prevent refrigerant migration/bearing washout. Wait 1 hour before start-up on initial install if ambient is below 70F.","key":"crankcase"}]},{"title":"Board / Fault Codes","rows":[{"label":"Code format","value":"2-character alphanumeric on inverter board display (H-, P-, E- prefixes); e.g. P1 = high pressure switch, P2 = low pressure, P4 = high discharge temp, H8 = pressure transducer fault, H5 = system lockout after 5x P2 in 100 min","key":"fault_codes"},{"label":"'b'-prefix codes","value":"Reserved for indoor-unit-side faults on Bosch IDS boards (e.g. sensor/communication faults reported at the indoor control) - see fault code table in matched indoor unit/air handler manual","key":"b_codes"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Not applicable in the traditional sense — Bosch's current residential heat pump lineup (IDS 2.0 / BOVA / BVA outdoor units) is inverter-controlled with no separate legacy timer/demand defrost board; defrost logic lives on the inverter/outdoor control board itself. See the Force button procedure below, which is the manufacturer's documented method regardless of comm status."},{"label":"Inverter board Force button","value":"On the outdoor unit's inverter control board, press and hold the 'Force' button for 6 seconds to begin a forced defrost test. Wait roughly 40 seconds for defrost to actually initiate — once it does, the board's display shows 'dF'. The test terminates automatically; afterward the display returns to showing running compressor speed. If a second forced-defrost test is needed, wait at least 5 minutes after the first before repeating. Source: Bosch IDS 2.0 / BOVA-BVA Service Manual, official Bosch Home Comfort technical documentation (bosch-homecomfort.com service manual, external rev.3) — page could not be parsed directly this session via automated fetch, so this is drawn from indexed manual text; confirm against the printed manual before a customer-facing test."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Bosch's Demand Defrost Control (DDC) normally triggers based on a calculated temperature difference between outdoor coil (T3) and outdoor ambient (T4) sustained for 3 minutes, or after a minimum run time keyed to ambient temp — a warm coil may prevent the forced test from actually completing even after the Force button is pressed. Expect the reversing valve to shift to cooling and the outdoor fan to stop during defrost; a burst of cold air from supply registers is normal, not a fault."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Bosch","model":"IDS Light BOVA15 Inverter Ducted Split Heat Pump (R-454B)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Newer-generation Bosch inverter heat pump using mildly-flammable A2L refrigerant R-454B. Same BOVA15 model designation as an earlier R-410A unit, so refrigerant must be confirmed from the nameplate/red refrigerant-line tag, not the model number. Pressure protection setpoints differ meaningfully from the R-410A generation.","match":["bosch","ids light","bova15","r454b","r-454b","a2l","inverter ducted split"],"source":"Bosch IDS Heat Pump Light Series Condensing Unit, Installation and Operating Instructions, BTC 762003308 D (01.2025) - bosch-homecomfort.com/us","flags":[{"title":"A2L mildly flammable refrigerant - certification and handling rules apply","body":"Manual: 'Mildly flammable refrigerant used. Follow handling instructions carefully in compliance with national regulations... Work on the refrigerant circuit with mild flammable refrigerant in safety group A2L may only be carried out by authorized heating contractors... trained in accordance with UL 60335-2-40.' All R-454B units ship with 'a red tag on the refrigerant lines to indicate the product is charged with A2L refrigerant. It should not be removed.'"},{"title":"Low-pressure cutout threshold is drastically different from the R-410A BOVA15/BOVB20 - do not reuse the old number","body":"R-454B low pressure protection trips at < 22 PSIG for 3 seconds (cooling mode), vs. < 43.5 PSIG for 5 minutes on the R-410A generation of the same BOVA15/BOVB20 chassis. High pressure cutout/cut-in (580 PSIG open / 435 PSIG close) is unchanged between refrigerants. Confirm which refrigerant/manual revision applies before troubleshooting a low-pressure trip."},{"title":"Model number does not tell you the refrigerant - check the nameplate and manual revision/date","body":"This R-454B unit is documented under the same 'BOVA15' designation used for the earlier R-410A unit (BTC 761701317, 11.2023). The R-454B version is documented separately as 'IDS Light Series' (BTC 762003308, 01.2025). Always verify refrigerant type from the data plate before connecting gauges, recovering, or charging."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-454B (A2L, mildly flammable) - verify on nameplate/red line tag","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"EEV in outdoor unit (heating mode metering); indoor coil requires an R-454B-rated TXV ('must be matched with R-454B TXV')","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling method (cooling, outdoor ambient above 55F) via Bosch EasyAir app; weigh-in method below 55F ambient. Design subcool/superheat target varies by tonnage (manual table shows approx. 6-10F subcool / 8-10F superheat for larger tonnages)","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Pressures & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High pressure cutout / cut-in","value":"Opens > 580 PSIG (compressor + OD fan stop); closes < 435 PSIG","key":"hp_cutout"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout","value":"< 22 PSIG for 3 seconds during cooling mode -> compressor + OD fan stop; retries after 6 minutes","key":"lp_cutout"},{"label":"Discharge temp protection (T5)","value":"Compressor restarts if DT < 185F; stops if DT > 230F (cooling or heating)","key":"discharge_temp"},{"label":"Low discharge superheat protection","value":"Trips if head discharge superheat (HDSH) < 9F for last 40 minutes","key":"low_dsh"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand Defrost Control (DDC) using coil thermistor T3 + outdoor ambient T4, run time, and pressure","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"Outdoor coil (T3) reaches 64F for 1 minute, or defrost time exceeds 8 minutes","key":"defrost_term"},{"label":"Manual/forced defrost","value":"Call for heat running >=8 minutes, then hold FORCE button on control board 6 seconds; display shows 'dF'","key":"manual_defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in heating mode; de-energized in cooling mode","key":"revvalve"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Cooling operating range","value":"40F to 120F outdoor ambient (T4)","key":"low_ambient_cool"},{"label":"Heating operating range","value":"3F to 86F outdoor ambient (T4)","key":"low_ambient_heat"},{"label":"Backup/emergency heat lockout","value":"Below 1.4F, unit provides 24V signal to indoor unit to energize electric heat (if installed)","key":"backup_heat"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Energizes on first power-up if compressor discharge T5 < 53.6F, or after compressor is off 3 hrs with T4 < 41F or T5 < 53.6F; de-energizes once T5 >= 60.8F and compressor runs. Recommend 12 hrs CCH energized before start-up after extended cold-weather shutdown.","key":"crankcase"}]},{"title":"Board / Fault Codes","rows":[{"label":"Code format","value":"2-character codes on control board display; e.g. E7 = compressor discharge sensor fault (T5), E81 = EEV coil fault, EA = program/drive mismatch","key":"fault_codes"},{"label":"'b'-prefix codes","value":"Indoor-unit-side faults, including A2L refrigerant sensor codes specific to this refrigerant: b3 = indoor A2L sensor fault, b4 = A2L sensor communication fault, b7 = R-454B refrigerant leakage fault (indoor), b8 = A2L sensor past service life","key":"b_codes"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Not applicable in the traditional sense — Bosch's current residential heat pump lineup (IDS 2.0 / BOVA / BVA outdoor units) is inverter-controlled with no separate legacy timer/demand defrost board; defrost logic lives on the inverter/outdoor control board itself. See the Force button procedure below, which is the manufacturer's documented method regardless of comm status."},{"label":"Inverter board Force button","value":"On the outdoor unit's inverter control board, press and hold the 'Force' button for 6 seconds to begin a forced defrost test. Wait roughly 40 seconds for defrost to actually initiate — once it does, the board's display shows 'dF'. The test terminates automatically; afterward the display returns to showing running compressor speed. If a second forced-defrost test is needed, wait at least 5 minutes after the first before repeating. Source: Bosch IDS 2.0 / BOVA-BVA Service Manual, official Bosch Home Comfort technical documentation (bosch-homecomfort.com service manual, external rev.3) — page could not be parsed directly this session via automated fetch, so this is drawn from indexed manual text; confirm against the printed manual before a customer-facing test."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Bosch's Demand Defrost Control (DDC) normally triggers based on a calculated temperature difference between outdoor coil (T3) and outdoor ambient (T4) sustained for 3 minutes, or after a minimum run time keyed to ambient temp — a warm coil may prevent the forced test from actually completing even after the Force button is pressed. Expect the reversing valve to shift to cooling and the outdoor fan to stop during defrost; a burst of cold air from supply registers is normal, not a fault."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Bosch","model":"BVA Series Air Handler, 2-5 Ton (R-410A)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Bosch BVA-series air handler matched to IDS BOVA/BOVB condensers. Multi-tap constant-torque ECM blower (5 speed taps), TXV metering at the indoor coil (not EEV), field-supplied filter only, field-installed electric heat kits from 5-20 kW.","match":["bosch","bva","bva 2.0","ids air handler","bosch air handler"],"source":"Bosch BVA Series Air Handler 2-3-4-5 Ton Capacity R410A, Installation Instructions, BTC 761701101 A (09.2015) - bosch-homecomfort.com/us","flags":[{"title":"No factory filter and no factory float switch mentioned - verify field accessories are installed","body":"Manual: 'External filter or other means of filtration is required. Units should be sized for a maximum of 300 feet/min. air velocity...' and filter is explicitly 'not factory-installed.' The base install manual does not document a factory condensate float/safety switch; it instead recommends field-installed 'Secondary drain pan kits... when the unit is [installed above finished space]' - confirm whether a safety switch was field-added before troubleshooting a nuisance shutdown blamed on 'float switch.'"},{"title":"Metering is TXV at the indoor coil, matched to outdoor unit tonnage - not an EEV","body":"Unlike the outdoor IDS condenser (which uses an EEV for heating-mode metering), the BVA air handler's indoor coil uses a TXV: 'Use a wet rag or an approved heat paste to protect the TXV sensing [bulb]...' Do not look for EEV wiring/board at the air handler on this R-410A generation - if the job has an EEV-equipped indoor coil, it's a different (newer/IDS Ultra) air handler family, not the BVA."},{"title":"5-speed ECM is constant-torque, selected by dip/tap wiring, not auto-sensed","body":"'The mult-tap ECM motor is a constant torque motor... Airflow at 208V is approximately the same as 230V.' Speed/tap selection is a field wiring choice (Tap 1-5) matched to tonnage and static pressure - verify tap wiring against the airflow table for the installed tonnage rather than assuming factory default."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Multi-tap constant-torque ECM, 5 field-selectable speed taps (Tap 1-5)","key":"blower"},{"label":"Rated airflow","value":"350-450 CFM per ton (400 CFM nominal) per manual airflow tables; shaded/excluded ranges in tables are outside 300-450 cfm/ton","key":"airflow"},{"label":"Max external static (per airflow tables)","value":"Performance tables list operation from 0 to 0.8 in. w.c. ESP depending on tonnage/tap - use the specific tonnage table, do not apply a single fleet-wide max","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Airflow test basis","value":"Tables are 'based on cooling performance with a dry coil and no filter in place' - field ESP will typically run higher once filter/coil wet resistance is added","key":"airflow_basis"}]},{"title":"Filter & Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Not factory installed - field-supplied external filter or filter grille required, sized for max 300 ft/min face velocity","key":"filter"},{"label":"Filter cabinet size (24k model)","value":"18 x 20 in. filter opening","key":"filter_size_24k"},{"label":"Filter cabinet size (36/48/60k models)","value":"20 x 22 in. filter opening","key":"filter_size_big"},{"label":"Condensate drain","value":"Primary + auxiliary drain connections; unit must be slightly inclined toward drain connection; trap must be field-formed and tested by pouring water into pan/line","key":"drain"},{"label":"Secondary drain pan / safety switch","value":"Secondary drain pan kit recommended (not always factory-installed) for installs where a leak could cause property damage - see rating plate/parts list for whether a float switch was ordered","key":"float_switch"}]},{"title":"Metering & Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV (thermostatic expansion valve) at indoor coil, matched to system tonnage","key":"metering"},{"label":"Electric heat kits","value":"Field-installed kits: EHK05A (5 kW), EHK08A (7.5 kW), EHK10A (10 kW), EHK15B (15 kW, 36/48/60 only), EHK20B (20 kW, 48/60 only) - double-pole breaker style, MCA/MOP per kit table in manual","key":"heat_kits"},{"label":"Torque spec - drain connections","value":"Do not exceed 15 ft-lbs on drain fitting connections","key":"drain_torque"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SL280V / SL280NV","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Two-stage, variable-speed, communicating (iComfort/S40-capable) 80% gas furnace, SureLight integrated control. Covers SL280UHV, SL280DFV (dual fuel), SL280UHNV (Canada low-NOx).","match":["SL280V","SL280NV","SL280UHV","SL280DFV","SL280UHNV","SL280UH","two-stage","variable speed","communicating","icomfort","80%","furnace"],"source":"Lennox SL280UHV Installation Instructions, Corp. 508245-01 (02/2022); Lennox SL280UHNV Service Literature, Corp. 1601-L8 (2021), tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"No fixed flame-sense µA pass/fail threshold published","body":"This is a communicating (SureLight/iComfort) integrated control, not an older fixed-threshold board. The control's Flame Signal Mode (menu 'F') displays LIVE flame current on the 7-segment LED in microamps, but Corp. 1601-L8 does not publish a numeric normal/low/dropout table - diagnosis is by comparing the live reading before/after cleaning the sensor rather than to a fixed spec. Do not assume a generic µA cutoff for this board family."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"SureLight integrated control (communicating)","value":"Live µA readout only via Flame Signal Mode (menu 'F') on 7-seg LED - no fixed normal/low/dropout numbers published","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG (low/high fire), 0-4500 ft","value":"1.7 in. w.g. low fire / 3.5 in. w.g. high fire","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure NG, 4500-7500 ft (derate)","value":"~1.5-1.6 in. w.g. low fire / 2.8-3.4 in. w.g. high fire (size-dependent, see Table 19)","key":false},{"label":"Manifold pressure LP/propane (low/high fire)","value":"4.5 in. w.g. low fire / 10.0 in. w.g. high fire (LP changeover kit required)","key":true},{"label":"Supply line pressure NG","value":"4.5 in. w.g. min / 13.0 in. w.g. max"},{"label":"Supply line pressure LP","value":"10.0-11.0 in. w.g. min / 13.0 in. w.g. max"},{"label":"Orifice, NG (070/090/110)","value":".063 / .055 (size-specific, high-altitude kit swaps this - see Table 21)"},{"label":"Orifice, LP/propane","value":".034 / .032"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Two-stage redundant valve, factory-set, non-adjustable regulator; 1/8 NPT test ports at valve for manifold/supply pressure"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.8 in. w.g. heating / 1.0 in. w.g. cooling - do not exceed heating ESP, causes erratic limit operation","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-size specific; not consolidated in Corp. 508245-01)"},{"label":"Blower","value":"Variable-speed ECM, DIP-switch selectable heat/cool speeds (+24% to -18% of factory default)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"SureLight silicon nitride hot-surface ignitor, 39-70 Ω across terminals 1-5 (5-pin plug), 120VAC ±10% regulated, 20-sec warm-up","key":true},{"label":"Primary/secondary limits","value":"Auto-reset, factory-set, no published trip temperature ('not published' in Corp. 508245-01/1601-L8)"},{"label":"Flame rollout switches (2)","value":"Manual-reset, factory-set, no published trip temperature"},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Factory-set, non-adjustable; high-altitude kits 69W56/73W33/73W34/73W35 swap switch per altitude band (see Table 20)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"No change 0-4500 ft; NG manifold pressure/orifice derate 4500-7500 ft; high-altitude NG orifice kit required 7500-10,000 ft"},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (SL280UHNV, all sizes)","value":"0.20 in. w.c. — same trip point for low fire and high fire, same across all SL280UHNV sizes (single proving switch near the gas valve). Confirmed only in the SL280UHNV literature; the communicating SL280UHV/DFV installation instructions (Corp. 508245-01) don't carry this service-checkout table, so treat as unconfirmed for that variant."}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SL297NV","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Two-stage, variable-speed, communicating (iComfort/S40-capable) 97% condensing gas furnace, SureLight integrated control. Natural gas only - no LP/propane conversion kit published.","match":["SL297NV","SL297UHNV","97%","two-stage","variable speed","communicating","icomfort","condensing","furnace"],"source":"Lennox SL297UHNV Installation Instructions, Corp. 507760-02 (02/2018); Lennox SL297UHNV Service Literature, Corp. 1802-L1 (rev. 02/2021), lennox.com / tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Natural gas only - do not attempt an LP conversion","body":"Corp. 507760-02 contains no LP/propane orifice or conversion-kit table for the SL297UHNV (unlike the SL280V family, which has one). The gas piping/CSA references to 'Natural Gas and Propane' in this literature are generic code citations, not a model-specific LP option. Confirm fuel type against the model/rating plate before ordering parts - do not substitute an SL280 LP kit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"SureLight integrated control (communicating)","value":"Live µA readout only via Flame Signal Mode push-button/menu - no fixed normal/low/dropout numbers published in Corp. 1802-L1","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG (low/high fire), all models","value":"1.7 in. w.g. low fire / 3.5 in. w.g. high fire","key":true},{"label":"Supply line pressure NG","value":"4.5 in. w.g. min / 13.0 in. w.g. max"},{"label":"LP/propane","value":"Not offered - see flag"},{"label":"Combustion CO2% (NG, low/high fire)","value":"040: 6.3-7.8% | 060: 6.5-8.2% | 080: 7.2-8.4%"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Redundant two-stage valve; 1/8 NPT manifold/supply test ports"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.8 in. w.g. heating / 1.0 in. w.g. cooling"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"45-75°F (-040 low-input) / 40-70°F (-040 high-input, -060, -080) per Corp. 1802-L1 spec tables - confirm against rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Blower","value":"Variable-speed ECM; continuous-fan selectable 28/38/70/100% of 2nd-stage cool speed, min 250 cfm"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"SureLight silicon nitride hot-surface ignitor, 39-70 Ω across terminals 1-5, 120VAC ±10%, 20-sec warm-up","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit / rollout switches","value":"Auto-reset limit, manual-reset flame rollout; factory-set, no published trip temperature"},{"label":"Pressure switch / inducer calibration","value":"Control self-calibrates combustion-air-inducer prove switch each heat cycle; calibration-failure codes E229/watchguard calibration failure logged if it can't complete"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"NOT approved for installations above 4500 ft (Corp. 507760-02) - no high-altitude kit published for this model"},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (all sizes)","value":"0.15 in. w.c. low heat / 0.50 in. w.c. high heat — Table 17 prints one shared set point across -040/-060/-080, factory-set and non-adjustable.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL296V / EL296E","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Two-stage 96% condensing gas furnace, SureLight integrated control. EL296UHV is variable-speed/communicating (iComfort); EL296UHE is constant-torque, non-communicating. Flame-sense µA thresholds below are keyed to the EL296UHE control (103699) - the UHV communicating control shows live µA only, no fixed thresholds published.","match":["EL296V","EL296E","EL296UHV","EL296UHE","EL296DFV","96%","two-stage","condensing","elite series","furnace"],"source":"Lennox EL296UHV(X) Service Literature, Corp. 1125-L5 (2021); Lennox EL296UHE Service Literature, Corp. 1246-L10 (2014), tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Flame-sense µA table is EL296UHE (board 103699) only - EL296UHV communicating control has no fixed threshold","body":"Corp. 1246-L10 (EL296UHE) publishes a fixed flame-signal table keyed to integrated control 103699: Normal 2.6 µA or greater, Low 2.5 µA or less, Drop Out ~0.6 µA. The EL296UHV/EL296DFV (iComfort communicating SureLight control) only displays a LIVE µA reading in Flame Signal Mode ('F' menu) per Corp. 1125-L5 - no numeric pass/fail table is published for that board. Confirm which control is installed before applying the EL296UHE numbers."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board 103699 (EL296UHE, non-communicating)","value":"Normal 2.6 µA or greater / Low 2.5 µA or less / Drop Out ~0.6 µA","key":true},{"label":"EL296UHV/DFV communicating SureLight control","value":"Live µA readout only via Flame Signal Mode - no fixed thresholds published"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG (low/high fire), 0-4500 ft","value":"1.7 in. w.g. low fire / 3.5 in. w.g. high fire","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure NG, derated bands to 7500 ft","value":"As low as 1.5/3.1 in. w.g. depending on size - see Table 31, Corp. 1125-L5"},{"label":"Manifold pressure LP/propane (low/high fire)","value":"4.5 in. w.g. low fire / 10.0 in. w.g. high fire (changeover kit required)","key":true},{"label":"Supply line pressure NG","value":"4.5 in. w.g. min / 13.0 in. w.g. max"},{"label":"Supply line pressure LP","value":"11.0 in. w.g. min / 13.0 in. w.g. max"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Two-stage redundant valve, internally regulated, 1/8 NPT test ports"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.8 in. w.g. heating / 1.0 in. w.g. cooling","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (ranges from 20-50°F to 55-85°F across sizes per Corp. 1125-L5/1246-L10 spec tables)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"SureLight silicon nitride hot-surface ignitor, 39-70 Ω across terminals, 20-sec warm-up","key":true},{"label":"Flame rollout switch (S47)","value":"N.C. SPST manual-reset, one per side of burner box, factory-set trip temp not published"},{"label":"Primary/secondary limits","value":"Auto-reset, factory-set, no published trip temperature"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Approved 0-10,000 ft with manifold pressure/pressure-switch adjustment per Table 31/32 - no hard altitude ceiling like SL297NV"},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (EL296UHE, 0-4500 ft)","value":"-045: Low 0.40 / High 0.70 in. w.c. · -070/-090/-110: Low 0.50 / High 0.90 in. w.c. · -135: Low 0.45 / High 0.90 in. w.c. Dual first/second-stage switch on the CEHB, factory-set, non-adjustable. Confirmed only in the EL296UHE literature — not independently verified for the EL296UHV/DFV communicating control (same CEHB hardware is likely but unconfirmed in Corp. 1125-L5)."}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL297UHE","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Elite Series two-stage 97% AFUE condensing gas furnace (Category IV, upflow/horizontal), SureLight two-stage integrated control 103699-XX/107048-XX. Constant-torque 'Power Saver' DC brushless blower (5 speed taps) - NOT variable-speed, non-communicating (standard 24V R/W1/W2/Y1/Y2/G/C/DS). Nomenclature EL297UH070XE36B: EL=Elite, 2=two-stage, 97=97% AFUE, UH=upflow/horizontal, 070=66,000 Btuh input (43,000 low fire), X=Low NOx, E=constant-torque blower, 36=1.5-3 ton cooling add-on, B=17-1/2 in. cabinet.","match":["EL297UHE","EL297UH","EL297","EL297UHXE","EL297UH070XE36B","97%","two-stage","condensing","elite series","furnace"],"source":"Lennox EL297UHE Installation Instructions 508386-01 (04/2024); Lennox EL297UHE Unit Information 100093 (04/2024); Lennox EL297UHE Product Specifications Bulletin 211032 (07/2024), lennox.com; Lennox EL297UHE Unit Information / service manual 100093 (public: s7d9.scene7.com/is/content/lennoxinternational/100093-01-000pdf), spec column EL297UH070XE36B; flame drop-out per EL297UHEK manual 100170.","flags":[{"title":"Not an EL296 - static and pressure-switch figures differ","body":"EL297UHE max external static is 0.5 in. w.g. (heating and cooling design) where the EL296 is rated 0.8 in. w.g. heating / 1.0 in. w.g. cooling, and the EL297UHE -070 pressure switch is High 0.95 / Low 0.55 in. w.c. where the EL296UHE -070 is 0.90 / 0.50. Do not carry EL296 figures over to this furnace - use the rating plate and the EL297UHE literature."}],"groups":[{"title":"Ratings (-070, EL297UH070XE36B)","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"97%","key":true},{"label":"Input high / low fire","value":"66,000 / 43,000 Btuh","key":true},{"label":"Output high / low fire","value":"65,000 / 42,000 Btuh"},{"label":"Other sizes","value":"-045 44,000/29,000 in · -090 88,000/57,000 in; -110 and -135 on UI 100093 p.2"}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"SureLight two-stage integrated control 103699-XX / 107048-XX","value":"SureLight two-stage integrated control 103699-XX / 107048-XX: Normal 2.6 µA or greater / Low 2.5 µA or less / Drop Out 0.6 µA (UI 100093 p.19 Table 9 prints '.06'; Lennox's later EL297UHEK manual 100170 Table 11 prints 0.6). Read it in the control's Field Test Mode 'F' menu.","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG (low/high fire)","value":"1.7 in. w.g. low fire / 3.5 in. w.g. high fire","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure LP/propane (low/high fire)","value":"4.5 in. w.g. low fire / 10.0 in. w.g. high fire (LP conversion kit 11K51)","key":true},{"label":"Supply line pressure NG","value":"4.5 in. w.g. min / 13.0 in. w.g. max"},{"label":"Supply line pressure LP","value":"11.0 in. w.g. min / 13.0 in. w.g. max"},{"label":"Manifold by altitude, NG low/high fire","value":"0-4,500 ft 1.7/3.5 · 4,501-5,500 1.6/3.3 · 5,501-6,500 1.5/3.2 · 6,501-7,500 1.5/3.1 · 7,501-10,000 1.7/3.5 with orifice kit (UI 100093 Table 23)"},{"label":"Manifold by altitude, LP low/high fire","value":"0-4,500 ft 4.5/10.0 · 4,501-5,500 4.2/9.4 · 5,501-6,500 4.0/9.1 · 6,501-7,500 3.9/8.9 · 7,501-10,000 4.5/10.0 (Table 23)"},{"label":"Clock the meter (-070)","value":"Natural: 55 s per rev on a 1 cu ft dial (110 s on 2 cu ft) · LP: 136 s (272 s). Time 2 revs, divide by 2; shut off other gas appliances (Table 21)","key":true},{"label":"Combustion CO2% (-070)","value":"Natural 5.3-6.3 low fire / 7.4-8.4 high fire · LP 6.3-7.3 / 8.7-9.7 · CO max 100 ppm, after 15 min run (Table 22)","key":true},{"label":"Connections","value":"Gas pipe 1/2 in. IPS · intake/exhaust 2 in. PVC · condensate trap 3/4 in."}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.5 in. w.g. (heating and cooling design); heating not certified above 0.8 in. w.g. - see flag","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"-070: 35-65°F high fire / 25-55°F low fire (EHB 211032 p.10); other sizes see rating plate"},{"label":"Blower","value":"Constant-torque 'Power Saver' DC brushless, 5 speed taps - not variable-speed"},{"label":"Blower (-070)","value":"1/2 hp DC brushless constant-torque, 10 x 8 wheel, 550-1,380 CFM; 1.5-3 tons add-on cooling"},{"label":"Filter (B-width cabinet, e.g. -070)","value":"Field-supplied. End/bottom rack kit 87L96 = 18 x 25 x 1 · side-return rack kit 44J22 = 16 x 25 x 1 (C-width end rack 20 x 25 x 1, D-width 25 x 25 x 1)","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"SureLight silicon nitride hot-surface ignitor, 39-70 Ω (UI 100093 pp.19, 21)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (-070)","value":"0-4,500 ft: High 0.95 / Low 0.55 in. w.c. · 4,501-7,500 ft: 0.85 / 0.50 · 7,501-10,000 ft: 0.75 / 0.45 (UI 100093 p.22 Tables 11-13). Other sizes: see rating plate / UI p.22.","key":true},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Rated to 10,000 ft; pressure switch kit 14A48 (4,501-7,500 ft) or 14A54 (7,501-10,000 ft); NG orifice kit 73W37 / LP orifice kit 11K46 above 7,500 ft (IOM 508386-01 p.50 Tables 16-17)"},{"label":"Flame rollout switches (S47)","value":"Two, one each side on top of the burner box; N.C. manual reset, factory set to open at 210 °F (not adjustable). Tripped = E223 hard lockout","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit (S10)","value":"Heating vestibule; auto-reset. Must reset within 3 min or the control goes to 1-hr Watchguard. Set point is model-specific and not printed in UI 100093; see the Lennox Repair Parts Handbook"}]},{"title":"Electrical (-070)","rows":[{"label":"Supply","value":"120 V / 60 Hz / 1-ph","key":true},{"label":"Blower motor full load amps","value":"6.8 A","key":true},{"label":"Maximum overcurrent protection","value":"15 A"},{"label":"Control transformer","value":"40 VA, 120 V primary / 24 V secondary"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL280","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Two-stage 80% non-condensing gas furnace (upflow/horizontal EL280UH(X)(E), dual-fuel EL280DF(E)), SureLight integrated control 103699-XX/107048-XX family. Notably low max external static (0.5 in. w.g.) vs. the 90%+ Lennox lines.","match":["EL280","EL280UH","EL280UHX","EL280UHE","EL280DF","EL280DFE","80%","two-stage","non-condensing","furnace"],"source":"Lennox EL280UH(X)E Installation Instructions, Corp. 507908-02 (04/2024); Lennox EL280DF Service Literature, Corp. 1139-L11 (rev. 06/2016), tech.lennoxintl.com / lennox.com","flags":[{"title":"Max external static is only 0.5 in. w.g. - notably lower than SL/EL condensing lines","body":"Both EL280UH(X) and EL280DF spec tables (Corp. 507908-02, 1139-L11) list 0.5 in. w.g. as the high-static/max ESP rating for heating AND cooling - well below the 0.8/1.0 in. w.g. figures on the SL280V/EL296V condensing furnaces. On a duct system sized for a condensing replacement, verify actual static against this lower EL280 ceiling before assuming the blower can handle it."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board 103699-XX / 107048-XX","value":"Normal 1.9 µA or greater / Low 1.4 µA or less / Drop Out ~0.20 µA (per Corp. 1139-L11 EL280DF service literature)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG (low/high fire), 0-7500 ft","value":"1.7 in. w.g. low fire / 3.5 in. w.g. high fire","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure NG, 4500-7500 ft derate","value":"As low as 1.5/2.8 in. w.g. depending on size"},{"label":"Manifold pressure LP/propane (low/high fire)","value":"4.5 in. w.g. low fire / 10.0 in. w.g. high fire (changeover kit required)","key":true},{"label":"Supply line pressure NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 in. w.g. (NG) / 11.0-13.0 in. w.g. (LP)"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Two-stage redundant valve, 1/8 NPT test ports"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.5 in. w.g. (heating and cooling) - see flag","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (ranges 20-50°F to 40-70°F across sizes per Corp. 1139-L11 spec tables)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"SureLight silicon nitride hot-surface ignitor, 39-70 Ω, 20-sec warm-up","key":true},{"label":"Rollout/limit switches","value":"Factory-set, auto/manual-reset per switch type; no published trip temperature"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"NG orifice/manifold pressure adjustment 4500-7500 ft; high-altitude NG orifice kit required 7500-10,000 ft"},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (EL280DF)","value":"-070/-090: High 0.55 / Low 0.25 in. w.c. · -110: High 0.60 / Low 0.25 in. w.c. Factory-set, non-adjustable.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ME180 / ML180","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Single-stage 80% non-condensing gas furnace (ML180UH/UHE/UHV upflow-horizontal, ML180DF/DFE dual-fuel). SureLight integrated control shares the same flame-signal table as ML196UHE. 'ME180' commercial-brand/model-alias figures not independently found in Lennox literature - treat as ML180 platform and confirm off the rating plate.","match":["ME180","ML180","ML180UH","ML180UHE","ML180UHV","ML180DF","ML180DFE","80%","single-stage","non-condensing","merit series","furnace"],"source":"Lennox ML180DFE Service Literature, Corp. 1121-L4 (2017); Lennox ML180UHA Service Literature, Corp. 1218-L4 (2017), tech.lennoxintl.com / lennox.com","flags":[{"title":"'ME180' not confirmed as a distinct Lennox literature model","body":"No ME180-specific installation or service literature was located on tech.lennoxintl.com or lennox.com during this research - only ML180 family documents. If a unit is nameplated 'ME180', treat the figures below as a starting point only and verify every value (especially manifold pressure and temp rise) against that unit's own rating plate before servicing."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"ML180DFE / ML180UH(X)(E) SureLight control","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or greater / Low 0.5-1.4 µA / Drop Out ~0.4 µA (per Corp. 1121-L4)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG (single-stage, all sizes, 0-10,000 ft)","value":"3.5 in. w.g. - does not step down with altitude (pressure-switch kit swap used instead)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure LP/propane","value":"10.0 in. w.g. (changeover kit required)","key":true},{"label":"Supply line pressure NG","value":"4.5-13.0 in. w.g."},{"label":"Supply line pressure LP","value":"11.0-13.0 in. w.g."},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Single-stage redundant valve, 1/8 NPT test ports"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure (high static)","value":"0.5 in. w.g.","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-size specific per Corp. 1121-L4/1218-L4 spec tables)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Nitride hot-surface ignitor, 39-70 Ω, 20-sec warm-up","key":true},{"label":"Rollout/primary limit switches","value":"Factory-set, auto/manual-reset per switch type; trip temperature not published"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Approved 0-10,000 ft; NG manifold pressure essentially unchanged by altitude, high-altitude pressure-switch kit required above 4500-7500 ft (size-dependent) - see Table 13, Corp. 1121-L4"},{"label":"Pressure switch set point (ML180UHA, all sizes)","value":"0.60 in. w.c. (150 Pa) — same trip point across -070/-090/-110/-135, factory-set and non-adjustable. Confirmed only for ML180UHA; not independently checked against the ML180DFE dual-fuel literature (Corp. 1121-L4), and 'ME180' remains unconfirmed as a distinct Lennox document per the existing flag on this entry.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XP21","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"2-5 ton two-stage scroll heat pump (SilentComfort Technology), R-410A. Note: Lennox literature classifies XP21 as a TWO-STAGE compressor unit, not a variable-speed/inverter model - correcting a common assumption. Optional iComfort S30 communicating control; also runs as a conventional multi-stage unit.","match":["XP21"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications XP21 (ehb_xp21_2010.pdf) and Corp. 507217-02 Installation Instructions, tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Confirm compressor staging before quoting repairs","body":"Lennox literature lists the XP21 as a Two-Stage Scroll Compressor (SilentComfortTM), not a fully variable-capacity/inverter unit. Don't assume inverter-drive board diagnostics apply - use the standard two-stage IFC/defrost board fault codes (Five-Strike lockout) instead."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV (field-matched via TXV Usage/Substitution tables to indoor coil)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit rating plate / factory charging chart - charge is line-set-length and indoor-coil dependent; do not use a flat charge weight","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost control","value":"IntelliFrostTM Adaptive (demand) Defrost - outdoor temp, coil temp & compressor run-time inputs; field jumper selectable at 50°F/70°F/90°F/MAX, default 50°F","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Factory-installed 4-way valve, pressure-differential operated; energized state not specified in reviewed literature - verify against unit wiring diagram","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switches","value":"Both present, automatic reset, monitored by control board with 5-Strike lockout; exact cutout/cutin psig not published - see rating plate/switch part label","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"No specific °F threshold published; Compressor Low Ambient Cut-Off + Freezestat recommended when Low Ambient Kit (68M04) is installed","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Yes, factory-installed w/ thermostat (S40) - energize 24 hrs before startup","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Optional iComfort S30 Wi-Fi communicating; also operates as a conventional 2-stage unit with standard thermostats","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Lennox Demand Defrost Control boards have a 2-pin 'TEST' header. With the unit running a heating call, jumper the TEST pins for 2–5 seconds then remove — this forces one defrost event. If the jumper stays on TEST longer than 5 seconds, the control ignores it and reverts to normal operation (won't force). To repeat the test, remove the jumper for at least 1 second before reapplying. Source: Lennox heat pump unit service literature (tech.lennoxintl.com/.../507633-01.pdf, 'Demand Defrost Control' section) and corroborating field write-ups."},{"label":"iComfort communicating","value":"From the iComfort Touch/S30 installer Tests screen (Installer program > Tests), select the test set and press Start; the built-in defrost test is a short, self-terminating routine (~30 seconds) distinct from the other 30-minute component tests, per the iComfort Touch Setup manual's troubleshooting/tests section. Exact on-screen menu wording for current S30 firmware not independently re-verified this session — confirm live on the thermostat before using with a customer present. Source: Lennox iComfort Touch Setup Manual, 'Troubleshooting Tips' (lennox.com/dA/3c5cd2b3e6/Lennox_icomfortTouch_Manual.pdf, p.31 via ManualsLib)."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Outdoor coil sensor must be cold enough to be below the board's defrost cut-in (near/below freezing) for the forced cycle to actually engage and hold — on a warm coil the TEST short may be ignored or terminate immediately. Expect the reversing valve to shift to cooling and the outdoor fan to stop when defrost engages; a cold-air burst from supply registers during the test is normal."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XP20 / EL22XPV / EL18XPV / SL22XPV","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"2-5 ton variable-capacity heat pumps (DC Inverter, Precise ComfortTM Technology), R-410A, spanning the Signature (SL), Elite (EL) and XP tiers. Share the same DC-inverter variable rotary/scroll compressor platform and control logic. iComfort Communicating Thermostat is REQUIRED (not furnished) - these are not compatible with conventional non-communicating thermostats.","match":["XP20","EL22XPV","EL18XPV","SL22XPV"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications: XP20 (ehb_xp20_2010.pdf), EL18XPV (ehb_el18xpv_2104.pdf), SL25XPV (ehb_sl25xpv_2109.pdf), tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Communicating thermostat is mandatory, not optional","body":"Unlike XP21/XP17-class units, XP20/EL22XPV/EL18XPV/SL25XPV/SL22XPV literature explicitly states an iComfort Communicating Thermostat is required and is NOT furnished with the unit. A conventional stat will not run the outdoor unit correctly - confirm the correct iComfort stat is on the job before committing to a repair/replacement quote."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV/EEV per TXV Usage table (field-matched to indoor coil)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit rating plate / factory charging chart - do not use a flat charge weight","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost control","value":"Demand defrost using outdoor ambient, coil temp & compressor run-time; selectable termination temp 50°F/70°F/90°F, 14-minute maximum defrost time (XP20 literature)","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Factory-installed 4-way valve; energized state not specified in reviewed literature - verify against unit wiring diagram","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switches","value":"Both present with 5-Strike lockout protection; exact cutout/cutin psig not published - see rating plate","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Built-in low ambient control - cooling mode rated to operate down to 0°F outdoor air temp (no field kit required per EL18XPV/XP20 literature)","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Yes, factory-installed","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"iComfort S30 Communicating Thermostat REQUIRED - order separately, not furnished","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Lennox Demand Defrost Control boards have a 2-pin 'TEST' header. With the unit running a heating call, jumper the TEST pins for 2–5 seconds then remove — this forces one defrost event. If the jumper stays on TEST longer than 5 seconds, the control ignores it and reverts to normal operation (won't force). To repeat the test, remove the jumper for at least 1 second before reapplying. Source: Lennox heat pump unit service literature (tech.lennoxintl.com/.../507633-01.pdf, 'Demand Defrost Control' section) and corroborating field write-ups."},{"label":"iComfort communicating","value":"From the iComfort Touch/S30 installer Tests screen (Installer program > Tests), select the test set and press Start; the built-in defrost test is a short, self-terminating routine (~30 seconds) distinct from the other 30-minute component tests, per the iComfort Touch Setup manual's troubleshooting/tests section. Exact on-screen menu wording for current S30 firmware not independently re-verified this session — confirm live on the thermostat before using with a customer present. Source: Lennox iComfort Touch Setup Manual, 'Troubleshooting Tips' (lennox.com/dA/3c5cd2b3e6/Lennox_icomfortTouch_Manual.pdf, p.31 via ManualsLib)."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Outdoor coil sensor must be cold enough to be below the board's defrost cut-in (near/below freezing) for the forced cycle to actually engage and hold — on a warm coil the TEST short may be ignored or terminate immediately. Expect the reversing valve to shift to cooling and the outdoor fan to stop when defrost engages; a cold-air burst from supply registers during the test is normal."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XP17 / EL17XP1 / EL16XP1 / ML17XP1","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"1.5-5 ton single-stage scroll heat pumps (SilentComfort Technology on XP17; Elite/Merit equivalents on EL17XP1, EL16XP1, ML17XP1), R-410A. Fixed-capacity PSC compressor, works with any standard or communicating thermostat.","match":["XP17","EL17XP1","EL16XP1","ML17XP1"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications XP17 (ehb_xp17_1512.pdf), tech.lennoxintl.com (single-stage EL/ML platform siblings share the same IntelliFrost defrost control logic)","flags":[{"title":"Single-stage - no inverter/EEV diagnostics apply","body":"These are fixed-capacity scroll compressors (PSC motor, no VFD/inverter board). Don't chase variable-speed fault codes on this platform - use the standard IntelliFrost defrost board and 5-Strike HP/LP lockout diagnostics."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV per TXV Usage table (field-matched to indoor coil)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit rating plate / factory charging chart - do not use a flat charge weight","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost control","value":"IntelliFrostTM Adaptive (demand) Defrost - outdoor temp, coil temp & compressor run-time inputs; field jumper 50°F/70°F/90°F/MAX, default 50°F","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Factory-installed 4-way valve, pressure-differential operated; energized state not specified in reviewed literature - verify against unit wiring diagram","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switches","value":"Both present, automatic reset; exact cutout/cutin psig not published - see rating plate","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Cooling mode operates satisfactorily down to 45°F outdoor air without extra controls; optional field Low Ambient Kit extends to 30°F (add Freezestat + Compressor Low Ambient Cut-Off)","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Available/factory-installed depending on size - confirm on rating plate","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Works with iComfort Communicating Control or conventional thermostats (not communicating-mandatory)","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Lennox Demand Defrost Control boards have a 2-pin 'TEST' header. With the unit running a heating call, jumper the TEST pins for 2–5 seconds then remove — this forces one defrost event. If the jumper stays on TEST longer than 5 seconds, the control ignores it and reverts to normal operation (won't force). To repeat the test, remove the jumper for at least 1 second before reapplying. Source: Lennox heat pump unit service literature (tech.lennoxintl.com/.../507633-01.pdf, 'Demand Defrost Control' section) and corroborating field write-ups."},{"label":"iComfort communicating","value":"From the iComfort Touch/S30 installer Tests screen (Installer program > Tests), select the test set and press Start; the built-in defrost test is a short, self-terminating routine (~30 seconds) distinct from the other 30-minute component tests, per the iComfort Touch Setup manual's troubleshooting/tests section. Exact on-screen menu wording for current S30 firmware not independently re-verified this session — confirm live on the thermostat before using with a customer present. Source: Lennox iComfort Touch Setup Manual, 'Troubleshooting Tips' (lennox.com/dA/3c5cd2b3e6/Lennox_icomfortTouch_Manual.pdf, p.31 via ManualsLib)."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Outdoor coil sensor must be cold enough to be below the board's defrost cut-in (near/below freezing) for the forced cycle to actually engage and hold — on a warm coil the TEST short may be ignored or terminate immediately. Expect the reversing valve to shift to cooling and the outdoor fan to stop when defrost engages; a cold-air burst from supply registers during the test is normal."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XC25 / XC20","equip":"Condenser","summary":"2-5 ton variable-capacity air conditioners (DC Inverter, Precise ComfortTM Technology), R-410A. Top-tier Signature/XC platform units - iComfort Communicating Thermostat is REQUIRED and not furnished.","match":["XC25","XC20"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications: XC25 (ehb_xc25_1711.pdf), XC20 (ehb_xc20_2010.pdf), tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Communicating thermostat is mandatory, not optional","body":"Both XC25 and XC20 literature explicitly states an iComfort Communicating Thermostat is required (order separately - not furnished). These will not run correctly on a conventional non-communicating stat; verify equipment on the job before quoting a stat swap or condenser replacement."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV per TXV Usage table (field-matched to indoor coil)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit rating plate / factory charging chart - do not use a flat charge weight","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switches","value":"Both present with monitoring & lockout provisions; exact cutout/cutin psig not published - see rating plate","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Built-in low ambient control (no field kit stated in reviewed literature); Freezestat recommended for extra low-ambient protection","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Yes, factory-installed - prevents refrigerant migration during low ambient","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"iComfort Communicating Thermostat REQUIRED - order separately, not furnished","key":"communicating"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XC21 / XC16","equip":"Condenser","summary":"2-5 ton two-stage air conditioners, R-410A. XC21 is iComfort-enabled (works communicating OR with ComfortSense 7500 / other conventional thermostats); XC16 (Elite tier) is the same two-stage-compressor class.","match":["XC21","XC16"],"source":"Lennox Installation & Service Literature XC21 (Corp. 1007-L2), XC16 Guide Specifications (guidespecs_XC16_1408.pdf), tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Two-stage, communicating-optional - confirm thermostat compatibility","body":"XC21 explicitly supports non-communicating operation (Lennox ComfortSense 7500 or other conventional stats) in addition to full iComfort communicating mode - unlike the XC25/XC20 tier. Don't assume a communicating stat swap is required for this platform."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV (metering valve device only per XC21 literature)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit rating plate / factory charging chart - do not use a flat charge weight","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switches","value":"Both present with 5-Strike lockout on high/low pressure switches and discharge temp sensor; exact cutout/cutin psig not published - see rating plate","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"XC16: optional Low Ambient Kit extends operation down to 30°F, plus Compressor Low Ambient Cutoff; XC21 threshold not stated in reviewed literature","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"XC16: standard on 048-060 models, optional (field kit) on 024-036; XC21: crankcase thermostat (S40) present - confirm on rating plate","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Compatible with iComfort Communicating Control or conventional/ComfortSense 7500 thermostats","key":"communicating"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"XC17 / XC13 / XC14 / EL17XC1 / EL16XC1 / ML14XC1","equip":"Condenser","summary":"1.5-5 ton single-stage scroll air conditioners spanning Signature (XC17), base (XC13/XC14) and Elite/Merit (EL17XC1, EL16XC1, ML14XC1) tiers, R-410A. Fixed-capacity scroll compressor, works with any standard or communicating thermostat.","match":["XC17","XC13","XC14","EL17XC1","EL16XC1","ML14XC1"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications: XC17 (ehb_xc17_1511.pdf), XC14 (ehb_xc14_1706.pdf), EL16XC1 (ehb_el16xc1_2010.pdf), tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Single-stage, no inverter diagnostics","body":"All models in this group use a fixed-capacity (single stage) scroll compressor per Lennox literature - not variable-speed. Use standard high/low pressure switch and crankcase-heater troubleshooting; don't chase DC-inverter-board fault codes on this platform."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV per TXV Usage table (field-matched to indoor coil)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit rating plate / factory charging chart (EL16XC1 example: factory charge ranges ~4 lb 9 oz to 7 lb 1 oz by tonnage) - confirm actual unit charge on its own nameplate, do not reuse another size's figure","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switches","value":"Both present, automatic reset; exact cutout/cutin psig not published - see rating plate","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Standard cooling rated to ~45°F outdoor air without extra controls; optional Low Ambient Kit extends to 30°F w/ Freezestat + Compressor Low Ambient Cut-Off (platform convention per XC16/XP17-family literature)","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"EL16XC1: standard 018-048 models, add-on kit for larger; confirm presence/size on individual model's rating plate","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Works with iComfort Communicating Control or conventional thermostats (not communicating-mandatory)","key":"communicating"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL18XCV / SL28XCV","equip":"Condenser","summary":"2-5 ton variable-capacity air conditioners (DC Inverter Rotary/Scroll Compressor, Precise ComfortTM Technology), R-410A, Elite and Signature tiers. Same DC-inverter platform as EL18XPV/SL25XPV heat pumps.","match":["EL18XCV","SL28XCV"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications EL18XCV (ehb_el18xcv_2109.pdf), tech.lennoxintl.com","flags":[{"title":"Verify communicating-thermostat requirement before quoting","body":"Unlike XC25/XC20, the EL18XCV bulletin does not carry an explicit 'iComfort Communicating Thermostat required' note - but variable-capacity Lennox platforms generally need a compatible iComfort communicating control to run properly. Confirm required thermostat model against the specific unit's spec sheet/nameplate before committing to a repair plan."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory TXV per TXV Usage/Substitution table (field-matched to indoor coil)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit rating plate / factory charging chart - do not use a flat charge weight","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/Low pressure switches","value":"Both present with high/low pressure switch monitoring; exact cutout/cutin psig not published - see rating plate","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Built-in low ambient operation control; specific °F threshold not stated in reviewed literature - Freezestat recommended for extra protection","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Yes, factory-installed - prevents refrigerant migration during low ambient","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Pairs with iComfort Communicating Control - confirm exact thermostat requirement on unit's own spec sheet/nameplate","key":"communicating"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBX40UHV","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Dave Lennox Signature Collection variable-speed ECM air handler, 2-5 ton, multi-position (upflow/horizontal, downflow with kit), iComfort Communicating capable.","match":["CBX40UHV","CBX40UHV-024","CBX40UHV-030","CBX40UHV-036","CBX40UHV-042","CBX40UHV-048","CBX40UHV-060"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications Bulletin 210521 (Nov 2017), tech.lennoxintl.com/.../ehb_cbx40uhv_1711.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Lennox note","body":"Blower speeds (HEAT/COOL, 4 taps each) are set by jumper pins on the control board, not dip switches; an ADJUST jumper trims speed +/-10%. First-stage cooling airflow is auto-set to 70% of the selected COOL speed. Continuous fan (DELAY jumper) runs ~28/38/70/100% of COOL speed, min 380 cfm."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower","rows":[{"label":"Motor type","value":"ECM variable-speed, 1/2-1 hp depending on size","key":"motor"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Jumper-selectable HEAT/COOL speed taps (1-4) + ADJUST trim jumper; no dip switches","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static (published)","value":"0.80 in. w.g. (rated blower performance range, all sizes)","key":"max_static"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Type/size","value":"Disposable frame, MERV 16, 20x20x5 (-024/030/036) or 20x25x5 (-042/048/060)","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"2.5-25 kW field-installed ECB40 kits","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Staging","value":"2.5-6 kW kits are single-stage/single-breaker; 8 kW and larger are 2-stage, split across two circuit breakers (e.g. 12.5 kW = 30A+45A, 15 kW = 35A+60A) - staging sequenced by the control board, no separate field sequencer","key":"heat_staging"}]},{"title":"Metering / Coil","rows":[{"label":"Metering","value":"Factory wide-range R-410A check/expansion valve (TXV) standard; model-number digit also allows fixed orifice or outdoor-unit-side TXV - match device to outdoor unit per AHRI combination","key":"metering"},{"label":"Coil","value":"3-row copper tube/aluminum fin twin 'A' coil","key":"coil"}]},{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Pan","value":"Deep corrosion-resistant plastic dual-position drain pan (upflow/downflow/horizontal), dual (2x 3/4 in fpt) pipe drains","key":"drain_pan"},{"label":"Trap / float switch","value":"Not published as factory-standard in this bulletin - field-fabricated trap and any safety float switch per local code/install instructions; see rating plate/IOM for jurisdiction requirements","key":"drain_trap"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBX32MV","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Dave Lennox Signature Collection variable-speed ECM air handler, 1.5-5+ ton, multi-position, iComfort Communicating capable (Signature tier below CBX40UHV).","match":["CBX32MV","CBX32MV-018/024","CBX32MV-024/030","CBX32MV-036","CBX32MV-048","CBX32MV-060","CBX32MV-068"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications Bulletin 210352 (Feb 2018), tech.lennoxintl.com/.../ehb_cbx32mv_1802b.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Lennox note","body":"Same jumper-pin airflow architecture as CBX40UHV (HEAT/COOL taps 1-4 + ADJUST trim), but filters are 1 in. disposable (not the 5 in. MERV 16 media filter used on CBX40UHV) - do not cross-stock filters between the two lines."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower","rows":[{"label":"Motor type","value":"ECM variable-speed, 1/2 hp (-018/024 thru -036) or 1 hp (-048/060/068)","key":"motor"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Jumper-selectable HEAT/COOL speed taps (1-4) + ADJUST trim jumper; no dip switches","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static (published)","value":"0.80 in. w.g. (rated blower performance range)","key":"max_static"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Type/size","value":"Disposable frame, 1 in., size by tonnage: 15x20x1 (-018/024) up to 20x25x1 (-068)","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"2.5-25 kW field-installed kits (see Electric Heat Data tables)","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Same pattern as CBX40UHV: lower-kW kits single-stage, 8 kW+ kits 2-stage across two breakers, sequenced by control board","key":"heat_staging"}]},{"title":"Metering / Coil","rows":[{"label":"Metering","value":"Factory wide-range R-410A check/expansion valve (TXV) standard; model number also codes fixed orifice or outdoor-unit-side TXV options - match to outdoor unit per AHRI combination","key":"metering"},{"label":"Coil","value":"3-row copper tube/aluminum fin coil, 12 fins/in.","key":"coil"}]},{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Pan","value":"Deep corrosion-resistant plastic dual-position drain pan (upflow/downflow/horizontal), dual (2x 3/4 in fpt) pipe drains","key":"drain_pan"},{"label":"Trap / float switch","value":"Not published as factory-standard in this bulletin - field-fabricated trap and any safety float switch per local code/install instructions; see rating plate/IOM for jurisdiction requirements","key":"drain_trap"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBX27UH","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Elite Series constant-torque, multi-tap blower air handler, 1.5-5 ton, upflow/horizontal, 5-speed 'high efficiency' motor (not variable-speed ECM).","match":["CBX27UH","CBX27UH-018","CBX27UH-024","CBX27UH-030","CBX27UH-036","CBX27UH-042","CBX27UH-048","CBX27UH-060"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications Bulletin 210581 (Oct 2017), tech.lennoxintl.com/.../ehb_cbx27uh_1710.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Lennox note","body":"Airflow is set by choosing one of 5 fixed motor taps (Tap 1-5) wired at the board per the blower-performance table for the target CFM/ESP - there is no ECM jumper/dip-switch profile on this line. Published blower tables only go to 0.80 in. w.g. ESP; taps 1-2 drop out (N/A) above ~0.60-0.70 in. w.g. on smaller sizes."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower","rows":[{"label":"Motor type","value":"High-efficiency multi-tap PSC-type motor, 5 speed taps, 1/2 hp (-018 thru -036) or 1 hp (-042/048/060)","key":"motor"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Field-selected motor tap (1-5) per blower-performance CFM table; no jumpers/dip switches","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static (published)","value":"0.80 in. w.g. (table range; usable airflow narrows at high static on lower taps)","key":"max_static"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Type/size","value":"Disposable frame, 1 in., 20x20x1 (-018 thru -036) or 20x24x1 (-042/048/060)","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"2.5-20 kW (sizes -018/024/030/036) or 5-25 kW (-042/048/060) field-installed kits","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Not captured in the pages reviewed - confirm stage count/sequencer per specific kW kit in the Electric Heat Data tables of this bulletin before quoting","key":"heat_staging"}]},{"title":"Metering / Coil","rows":[{"label":"Metering","value":"Model-number digit codes fixed orifice, indoor-side TXV, or outdoor-unit-side TXV - match metering device to outdoor unit per AHRI combination","key":"metering"},{"label":"Coil","value":"3-row copper tube/aluminum fin coil, 12 fins/in.","key":"coil"}]},{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Pan","value":"Deep corrosion-resistant plastic dual-position drain pan (upflow/downflow/horizontal), dual (2x 3/4 in fpt) pipe drains","key":"drain_pan"},{"label":"Trap / float switch","value":"Not published as factory-standard in this bulletin - field-fabricated trap and any safety float switch per local code/install instructions; see rating plate/IOM for jurisdiction requirements","key":"drain_trap"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBX25UH","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Merit Series entry-level multi-tap PSC air handler, 1.5-5 ton, upflow/horizontal (downflow with kit) - base offering below CBX27UH.","match":["CBX25UH","CBX25UH-018","CBX25UH-024","CBX25UH-030","CBX25UH-036","CBX25UH-042","CBX25UH-048","CBX25UH-060"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications Bulletin 210770 (Dec 2018, -10 revision), tech.lennoxintl.com/.../ehb_cbx25uh-10_1812.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Lennox note","body":"3-speed PSC motor (High/Medium/Low) wired at the board per the blower table - no ECM jumpers/dip switches. Published blower-performance tables only extend to 0.50 in. w.g. ESP (lower static rating than CBX27UH/32MV/40UHV) - do not oversize ductwork static budget for this model."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower","rows":[{"label":"Motor type","value":"PSC, 3 fixed speed taps (High/Med/Low), 1/3 hp (-018 thru -036, -042) or 1/2 hp (-048/060)","key":"motor"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Field-selected tap (High/Med/Low) wired per blower-performance CFM table; no jumpers/dip switches","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static (published)","value":"0.50 in. w.g. (top of published blower-performance table, all sizes)","key":"max_static"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Type/size","value":"Disposable (non-pleated) frame, 1 in.; size by tonnage from 12x20x1 (-018) up to 18x24x1 (-042/048/060)","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"2.5-20 kW field-installed kits","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Not captured in the pages reviewed - confirm stage count/sequencer per specific kW kit in the Electric Heat Data tables of this bulletin before quoting","key":"heat_staging"}]},{"title":"Metering / Coil","rows":[{"label":"Metering","value":"Factory wide-range R-410A check/expansion valve (TXV) standard for cooling; unlike CBX27UH/32MV/40UHV, model number carries no separate field-selectable metering-device digit - match orifice/piston needs to outdoor unit per AHRI combination","key":"metering"},{"label":"Coil","value":"3-row copper tube/aluminum fin coil, 14 fins/in.","key":"coil"}]},{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Pan","value":"Factory-installed anti-microbial dual-position polymer drain pan (upflow/downflow/horizontal), dual pipe drains","key":"drain_pan"},{"label":"Trap / float switch","value":"Not published as factory-standard in this bulletin - field-fabricated trap and any safety float switch per local code/install instructions; see rating plate/IOM for jurisdiction requirements","key":"drain_trap"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59MN7","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Infinity Modulating 4-Way Multipoise condensing gas furnace, up to 98.3% AFUE. Modulating gas valve set at two points (Max Heat / Min Heat); communicating Infinity control with Status Code LED. Bryant twin: 987M (Evolution Modulating).","match":["59MN7","59MN7A","59MN7B","Bryant 987M","987M"],"source":"Carrier 59MN7B Installation, Start-Up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions, Form 59MN7B-02SI — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0D/59MN7B-02SI.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Two different manifold pressure tables — do not mix them up","body":"Manual states verbatim: 'Use Table 18 for all models EXCEPT 59MN7B060C21--20. Use Table 19 for all models 59MN7B060C21--20 ONLY.' Grabbing the wrong table on that one 060 unit throws both Max Heat and Min Heat manifold pressure off. Confirm full model/suffix off the rating plate before pulling a table."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"Table (18 or 19 per model suffix — see flag), by input rate + altitude. Table basis: 20,000 BTUh Max-Heat/8,000 BTUh Min-Heat per burner (std.) or 20,200/8,000 per burner (060C21-20). Sea-level example: 3.4 in. w.c. max heat / 0.55 in. w.c. min heat, No. 44 orifice.","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure NG","value":"Min 4.5 in. w.c. / Max 13.6 in. w.c. at furnace inlet, checked with burners firing at max heat.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure LP","value":"Max 13.8 in. w.c. published; minimum not clearly resolved from this manual — see rating plate / gas pressure table.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Factory No. 44 (example, 0-2000 ft, 1050 Btu/cu ft, 0.62 SG) — verify per Table 19/20 for actual altitude and gas heat value; never assume, always check.","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Modulating 2-stage-setpoint gas valve; brand/model not stated in SI text — confirm on rating plate/parts list.","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot surface igniter (HSI). Cold reading (room temperature) should be 40 to 70 ohms; resistance increases as the igniter heats. Check across both igniter leads with power off.","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"Blower performance (Table 7, Air Delivery CFM) published in 0.1 in. w.c. increments up to 1.0 in. w.c. ESP by unit size/cooling switch setting — no single max ESP figure stated.","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Certified range is PER FIRE STAGE (it modulates). Size 100 (e.g. 59MN7A100): Max Heat 45-75 °F (25-42 °C), Intermediate 50-80 °F (28-44 °C), Min Heat 35-65 °F (19-36 °C) — Carrier PD 59MN7C-01PD. Other sizes differ; read the rating plate. Verify with duct thermometers against the stage the unit is actually running.","key":true}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/flame","rows":[{"label":"Status LED","value":"Amber Status Code LED on blower door: solid ON = normal, rapid flash = lockout, or 2-digit flash code (digit 1 = number of flashes group 1, pause, digit 2 = flashes group 2). Stores last 7 codes in memory, survives power loss.","key":"led"},{"label":"Flame current","value":"Normal 4.0-6.0 microamps DC (nominal); lockout/flame-sense fault if signal drops below 0.5 microamps DC.","key":"flame_current"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"Manual-reset limit switch in burner assembly opens on flame rollout/overheat. Manual explicitly warns: correct the root cause (inadequate combustion air, gas pressure, orifice, or venting) before resetting — 'DO NOT jumper this switch.'","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Table 16 multiplier, ~2%/1000 ft above 2000 ft: 1.00 (0-2000 ft) down to 0.87 (6001-7000 ft), 0.85 (7001-8000 ft), 0.83 (8001-9000 ft), 0.81 (9001-10,000 ft). NG manifold pressure tables (18/19) already build in altitude + heating-value compensation — do not apply an additional derate on top of the table value.","key":"altitude"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59TN6","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Infinity Two-Stage, Variable-Speed 4-Way Multipoise condensing gas furnace, up to 96%+ AFUE. Communicating Infinity control, Status Code LED. Bryant twin: 986T (Evolution Two-Stage).","match":["59TN6","59TN6A","59TN6B","Bryant 986T","986T"],"source":"Carrier 59TN6B Installation, Start-up, Operating, Service and Maintenance Instructions, Form 59TN6B-01SI — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/05/59TN6B-01SI.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Flame-sense/limit lockout requires root-cause fix, not a reset","body":"Manual: 'These furnaces are equipped with a manual reset limit switch...opens and shuts off power to the gas valve if an overheat condition (flame rollout) occurs.' Same as other 59-series: correct inadequate combustion air, gas pressure, orifice sizing, or venting before resetting — do not jumper."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"Table 20, by input rate + altitude (two-stage: separate high-fire/low-fire settings). BTUh-per-burner table basis not confirmed in this pass — verify against unit's Table 19/20 heading.","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure NG","value":"Min 4.5 in. w.c. / Max ~13.6 in. w.c. at furnace inlet (same inlet-pressure-check procedure as 59MN7/59SC2 platform).","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure LP","value":"Max 13.8 in. w.c. published; minimum not clearly resolved from this manual — see rating plate.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Factory-sized by model; verify per Table 20 for altitude/gas heat value — never assume, always check and verify.","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Two-stage gas valve; brand/model not stated in SI text — confirm on rating plate/parts list.","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot surface igniter (HSI). Cold reading should be 40 to 70 ohms at room temperature; resistance rises with igniter temperature. Same spec as 59MN7/59SC2/59TP6 platform-family igniter.","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"Blower performance tables published in 0.1 in. w.c. increments to 1.0 in. w.c. ESP by unit size — no single max ESP figure stated.","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Varies by unit size — printed on furnace rating plate; verify with duct thermometers.","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/flame","rows":[{"label":"Status LED","value":"Amber Status Code LED, blower door: solid ON = normal, rapid flash = lockout, or 2-digit flash code; stores last 7 codes.","key":"led"},{"label":"Flame current","value":"Normal 4.0-6.0 microamps DC (nominal); lockout if signal drops below 0.5 microamps DC.","key":"flame_current"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"Manual-reset limit switch + rollout switch(es) in burner assembly — see flag.","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Table 18 multiplier, ~2%/1000 ft above 2000 ft (same schedule as 59MN7: 1.00 at 0-2000 ft to 0.81 at 9001-10,000 ft). Manifold pressure table already compensates for altitude — do not double-derate.","key":"altitude"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59SC2 / 59SC5 / 59SP5 / 59SP2","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Comfort/Performance single-stage 4-way multipoise condensing gas furnace platform, up to ~96.5% AFUE depending on size/series (59SP2 runs lower, to ~91.1% AFUE on some sizes). NOTE: 59SC5 is single-stage per its own product data ('59SC5B...Single-Stage'), not 2-stage — corrected from initial assumption. Bryant twins: 915S and 925S (Legacy single-stage family), per Carrier/Bryant cross-reference service bulletin.","match":["59SC2","59SC2D","59SC2E","59SC5","59SC5A","59SC5B","59SP5","59SP5A","59SP2","Bryant 915S","Bryant 925S","915S","925S"],"source":"Carrier 59SC2D Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions, Form 59SC2D-03SI — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/09/59SC2D-03SI.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Check inlet pressure under firing load, not just static","body":"Manual: confirm inlet gas pressure is between 4.5 in. w.c. and 13.6 in. w.c. WHILE the furnace is calling for max heat (burners firing) — 'if pressure is too low, you will not be able to adjust the manifold pressure to obtain the proper input rate.' A supply that reads fine at idle can sag below 4.5 in. w.c. once the burners and any other gas load pull simultaneously."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"Table 19, by input rate + altitude. Sea-level example given in manual: 0-2000 ft, 1050 Btu/cu ft, 0.62 SG => No. 44 orifice, 3.4 in. w.c. (847 Pa).","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure NG","value":"Min 4.5 in. w.c. / Max 13.6 in. w.c. (1125-3388 Pa), checked at max-heat call — see flag.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure LP","value":"Max 13.8 in. w.c. published; minimum not clearly resolved from this manual — see rating plate.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Factory No. 44 at sea level (example); verify per Table 19 for actual altitude/gas heat value — never assume, always check.","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Single-stage gas valve; brand/model not stated in SI text — confirm on rating plate/parts list.","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot surface igniter (HSI). Cold reading (nominal) 40 to 70 ohms at room temperature; stable over the life of the igniter.","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"Blower performance (Table 21, Air Delivery CFM) published in 0.1 in. w.c. increments to 1.0 in. w.c. ESP by unit size — no single max ESP figure stated.","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Must fall within range on furnace rating plate; verify per instructions using duct thermometers in supply/return.","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/flame","rows":[{"label":"Status LED","value":"Amber Status Code LED, blower door: solid ON = normal, rapid flash = lockout, or 2-digit flash code; stores last 7 codes in memory.","key":"led"},{"label":"Flame current","value":"Normal 4.0-6.0 microamps DC (nominal); lockout if signal drops below 0.5 microamps DC.","key":"flame_current"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"Manual-reset limit switch in burner assembly opens on flame rollout/overheat; correct root cause before reset, do not jumper.","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Table 17 multiplier, ~2%/1000 ft above 2000 ft (same schedule as 59MN7/59TN6). Manifold pressure table (19) already compensates for altitude + gas heating value — do not double-derate.","key":"altitude"},{"label":"Pressure switch trip","value":"Nominal break point 0.68 in. w.c.; maximum make point is 0.10 in. w.c. above the maximum break point. Figures from the 59SC2C manual — confirm against the specific unit's switch (differs by model/size/altitude kit); not independently re-verified for 59SC5/59SP5/59SP2.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"58CTA / 58CTX / 58CTW / 58CTY","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Performance 80 Two-Stage, induced-combustion, hot-surface-ignition, non-condensing 4-way multipoise gas furnace, 80% AFUE, 45,000-155,000 Btuh (Series 140). 58CTA/58CTX use a PSC blower; 58CTW/58CTY use an ECM variable-speed blower with ComfortHeat technology on the same gas train/combustion platform. 58CTX/58CTY are Low-NOx (40 ng/J) versions for AQMD areas.","match":["58CTA","58CTX","58CTW","58CTY","Bryant 820TB (variable-speed twin — Preferred 80 two-stage, size-matched; PSC-blower 58CTA/CTX twin unconfirmed)"],"source":"Carrier 58CTW/58CTY Product Data, Form 58CTW-06PD — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0C/58CTW-06PD.pdf (58CTA/58CTX-specific installation/service manual, Form 58CT-12SI, could not be located at a direct shareddocs.com URL in this pass — same combustion platform, verify furnace-specific figures against rating plate)","flags":[{"title":"Main limit switch is mounted behind the gas valve","body":"Furnace-components diagram in the product data places the MAIN LIMIT SWITCH behind the gas valve, separate from the manual-reset limit switches on the burner box and the flame rollout switch. When troubleshooting a limit-related lockout, there are multiple limit/rollout switches on this platform — identify which one tripped from the wiring diagram/LED code before condemning a part."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG/LP)","value":"Not obtained from Product Data (PD sheets on this platform don't carry the adjustment table) — see Table in Series 140 installation instructions (Form 58CT-12SI), by input rate + altitude; use value on furnace rating plate.","key":"manifold"},{"label":"Supply pressure NG","value":"Min 4.5 in. w.c. / Max 13.6 in. w.c. at furnace gas valve inlet.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Factory-installed, sized by model/altitude/heat value — see Installation Instructions for usage table (part numbers e.g. LH32DB0xx series listed in PD, no single drill size published).","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers, redundant, slow-opening two-stage gas valve (reduces ignition noise, regulates gas flow, electric shutoff).","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"Ignition","value":"Hot Surface Igniter, Size 43 (Power Heat igniter).","key":"ignition"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"Blower performance tables published in 0.1 in. w.c. increments to 1.0 in. w.c. ESP by unit size — no single max ESP figure stated; guide-spec boilerplate references 0.50 in. w.c. as a nominal design point.","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Certified Temperature Rise Range published per unit size in PD table (High/Low columns by model) — pull the exact deg F range for the specific model/size off that table or the rating plate; values did not extract cleanly in this pass.","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/flame","rows":[{"label":"Status LED","value":"Enhanced diagnostics via LED and reflective sight glass; stores fault codes through power outages (per PD features list).","key":"led"},{"label":"Flame current","value":"Not published in the documents reviewed this pass — see rating plate/service label.","key":"flame_current"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"Manual-reset limit switch(es) on burner box, separate MAIN LIMIT SWITCH behind gas valve, plus flame rollout switch — see flag.","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Not extracted from the documents reviewed this pass — see Series 140 installation instructions altitude derate table / rating plate.","key":"altitude"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"58UVB / 58MVC","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Variable-speed, variable-capacity (high/medium/low heat) condensing gas furnace. NOTE: corrected from the originally assumed 80% tier — 58UVB is documented as 'Performance 96, 95% AFUE Upflow-Only Variable-Speed'; 58MVC is the Infinity ICS 4-way-multipoise variable-speed sibling (up to ~96.6% AFUE on some sizes). Both are condensing units, not 80% non-condensing. Bryant twin not confirmed in this research pass — do not assume a specific Bryant model number without checking a parts cross-reference.","match":["58UVB","58MVC","58MVB"],"source":"Carrier 58MVC Installation Instructions, Form 58MVC-4SI — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/03/58MVC-4SI.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Never redrill orifices, and hold medium-heat pressure to a narrow band","body":"Manual, verbatim: 'DO NOT redrill orifices. Improper drilling (burrs, out-of-round holes, etc.) can cause excessive burner noise and misdirection of burner flames... resulting in heat exchanger failures.' Also: 'DO NOT set medium-heat manifold pressure less than 1.3 in. w.c. or more than 1.7 in. w.c. for natural gas' — a much tighter band than the high/low setpoints."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"3-point setpoint (High/Medium/Low heat), by input rate + altitude — worked example in manual for 80,000 Btuh high-heat input at sea level: 3.8 in. w.c. high heat / 1.6 in. w.c. medium heat / 0.6 in. w.c. low heat, No. 45 orifice. Medium-heat band restricted to 1.3-1.7 in. w.c. — see flag.","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure","value":"Not clearly extracted in this pass — see rating plate/gas piping section of manual.","key":"supply"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Factory No. 45 (sea-level example); verify per installation-instructions usage table for altitude/gas heat value — never redrill (see flag).","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"3-stage (high/medium/low) gas valve; brand/model not stated in extracted text — confirm on rating plate/parts list.","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"Design guidance in manual: avoid duct configurations causing static pressure greater than 0.5 in. w.c.; full blower ESP table not isolated in this pass — see rating plate/blower table.","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Must fall within range on furnace rating plate; adjustable via setup switch SW1-4 (rise-range selection) and airflow speed taps.","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/flame","rows":[{"label":"Status LED","value":"Control status code indicator light: rapid flash = fault/no-run condition; flashes 2-digit codes (e.g., code 12 during 90-sec vent-RPM evaluation, code 24 = fuse needs replacement, codes 11/25/41/42 = component-test results). Stores up to 7 codes.","key":"led"},{"label":"Flame current","value":"Not published as a specific microamp figure in the sections reviewed — see rating plate/service label.","key":"flame_current"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"Flame rollout manual-reset switch (verify continuity before restart); de-energizes gas valve, throttling valve, and humidifier terminal when R-to-W circuit opens.","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"2% derate per 1000 ft above 2000 ft (US), per Table 11 multiplier — simpler flat-rate schedule than the 59-series table-per-range format.","key":"altitude"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"25VNA0","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Infinity Series variable-speed (Greenspeed) heat pump, 1.5-5 tons. Variable-speed scroll compressor, communicating Infinity control, TXV for cooling / EXV for heating. Runs with adaptive (AUTO) or field-fixed defrost intervals.","match":["25VNA0","Infinity 20","Greenspeed","Bryant 280A","Evolution Extreme"],"source":"Carrier Product Data 25VNA-05PD (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/01/25VNA-05PD.pdf); Service Manual 24VNA0-25VNA0-1SM (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0B/24VNA0-25VNA0-1SM.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Low-pressure protection is software, not a discrete switch","body":"This platform uses a suction pressure transducer (0-200 psig range) feeding the control board, not a mechanical low-pressure switch. When troubleshooting nuisance low-pressure trips, pull the reading from the Infinity Control diagnostics / abnormal system status screen rather than assuming a failed physical switch."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Variable-speed scroll","key":"compressorType"},{"label":"Metering - cooling","value":"TXV (Puron hard shutoff)","key":"meteringCool"},{"label":"Metering - heating","value":"Electronic expansion valve (EXV)","key":"meteringHeat"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch (mechanical)","value":"Trips ~610 ±20 psig discharge; standard","key":"hpsCutout"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout - cooling (3-min)","value":"≤ 55 psig (software, via suction transducer)","key":"lpCutoutCool3min"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout - heating (3-min)","value":"< 23 psig (software)","key":"lpCutoutHeat3min"},{"label":"Low pressure cutout - instantaneous (either mode)","value":"< 13 psig (software)","key":"lpCutoutInstant"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Time/temperature with AUTO adaptive mode, selected via Infinity Control UI (no dip switches)","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Defrost intervals","value":"AUTO (adaptive 30/60/90/120 min based on prior defrost duration), or field-fixed 30, 60, 90, or 120 min; factory default AUTO; first defrost after power-up defaults to 30 min","key":"defrostInterval"},{"label":"Defrost enable condition","value":"Only below 50°F outdoor coil temp","key":"defrostEnableTemp"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling (O), de-energized in heating; outdoor fan turns on 15 sec before valve switches at defrost termination","key":"reversingValve"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase / Communicating","rows":[{"label":"Low-ambient cooling","value":"Standard down to 0°F with Infinity Control (no field kit needed)","key":"lowAmbient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Standard; energized during off-cycle below 75°F outdoor temp","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Full Greenspeed variable-capacity operation requires Infinity System Control","key":"communicating"},{"label":"Charging","value":"See rating plate / product data charge table by unit size - do not use a generic charge weight","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Standard demand-defrost boards (HK32EA/HK61EA-series, CEPL13xxxx — same family used on Bryant and ICP/Heil/Tempstar). Remove the small plastic cap over the 2-pin 'Forced Defrost' / 'Speed-Up' (TP1/TP2) test header and short the pins with a jumper wire. Momentarily short-and-release once first to clear any compressor anti-short-cycle delay, then re-short and HOLD 5+ seconds — board commands defrost. You should hear the reversing valve shift and see the outdoor fan stop; verify 24V C-to-W2 with a meter. Pull the jumper the instant the valve shifts or the board will hold in speed-up (60x) mode and cycle continuously — don't leave it shorted. If the valve doesn't shift within ~10 sec of the sustained short, board or valve is suspect. Bryant boards are identical; confirm exact pin silkscreen against the installed board revision, since older CEPL revisions label the header 'TEST' and only speed timing rather than instant-force. Source: Carrier/HVAC-Talk field discussion + HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board walkthrough (hvac-talk.com thread 993331; hvactrainingsolutions.net/heat-pump-defrost-control-boards-step-step)."},{"label":"Infinity communicating","value":"On the Infinity touch thermostat, enter the installer 'Checkout' diagnostic (Menu > Setups > Advanced, press and hold Advanced ~10 sec until Install/Service menu appears), then step through the heat pump Checkout routine, which commands the outdoor unit into defrost as part of the sequence. NOT independently re-verified against a current Infinity outdoor-unit Installation Instructions manual for this session, so confirm the exact menu path on the specific control/thermostat model in front of you before relying on it — menu wording has changed across Infinity System Control generations. The physical 2-pin Forced Defrost header on the outdoor board (same as non-comm procedure above) also still works on Infinity outdoor units independent of the thermostat. Source: Carrier documentation as summarized by Hunker 'How To Enter Diagnostic Mode On A Carrier Infinity Thermostat' and JustAnswer HVAC Q&A — treat menu path as a starting point, not gospel."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Coil temperature sensor (DFT) must read cold — Carrier defrost boards generally need the coil sensor closed (roughly below freezing, board-dependent ~30±3°F) before a forced defrost will actually initiate/hold; forcing on a warm coil may not take. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux/W2 heat may energize — a burst of cold air from supply registers is normal, not a fault. Warn occupants if testing with the system live."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"25HPB6","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Performance 16 heat pump, 1.5-5 tons, single-stage scroll compressor with hard-shutoff TXV. Time/temperature defrost, field-selectable interval. Non-communicating (standard 24V or Thermidistat).","match":["25HPB6","Performance 16","Bryant Preferred single-stage"],"source":"Carrier Product Data 25HPB6-04PD (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/07/25HPB6-04PD.pdf); Installation Instructions 25HCC-HPB-03SI (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/09/25HCC-HPB-03SI.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"This is a single-stage unit, not 2-stage","body":"Carrier's own literature (25HPB6-04PD, 25HCC-HPB-03SI) documents 25HPB6 as a single scroll-compressor, single-stage heat pump. The true 2-stage 16 SEER Performance model is 25HCB6 (already covered separately) - don't confuse the two on a service call."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Single-stage scroll","key":"compressorType"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Hard-shutoff TXV, standard all sizes","key":"metering"},{"label":"High/low pressure switch cutout","value":"See rating plate - exact psig not published for this platform","key":"pressureSwitchCutout"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Time/temperature electronic defrost control","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Defrost intervals","value":"Field-selectable 30, 60, 90, or 120 min; factory set to 90 min; defrost thermostat closes ~32°F, terminates on thermostat open or automatically after 10 min","key":"defrostInterval"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"O terminal, energized in cooling / de-energized in heating","key":"reversingValve"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase","rows":[{"label":"Max outdoor ambient - heating mode","value":"66°F published operating ceiling (not a lockout switch setting)","key":"maxHeatAmbient"},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling control","value":"Accessory (Motormaster / low-ambient switch) - factory standard only on smallest size group; verify nameplate","key":"lowAmbient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Standard on smaller size groups, not present on largest; confirm against nameplate","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Charging","value":"Subcooling method (hard-shutoff TXV) - see charging chart in install instructions / rating plate","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Standard demand-defrost boards (HK32EA/HK61EA-series, CEPL13xxxx — same family used on Bryant and ICP/Heil/Tempstar). Remove the small plastic cap over the 2-pin 'Forced Defrost' / 'Speed-Up' (TP1/TP2) test header and short the pins with a jumper wire. Momentarily short-and-release once first to clear any compressor anti-short-cycle delay, then re-short and HOLD 5+ seconds — board commands defrost. You should hear the reversing valve shift and see the outdoor fan stop; verify 24V C-to-W2 with a meter. Pull the jumper the instant the valve shifts or the board will hold in speed-up (60x) mode and cycle continuously — don't leave it shorted. If the valve doesn't shift within ~10 sec of the sustained short, board or valve is suspect. Bryant boards are identical; confirm exact pin silkscreen against the installed board revision, since older CEPL revisions label the header 'TEST' and only speed timing rather than instant-force. Source: Carrier/HVAC-Talk field discussion + HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board walkthrough (hvac-talk.com thread 993331; hvactrainingsolutions.net/heat-pump-defrost-control-boards-step-step)."},{"label":"Infinity communicating","value":"On the Infinity touch thermostat, enter the installer 'Checkout' diagnostic (Menu > Setups > Advanced, press and hold Advanced ~10 sec until Install/Service menu appears), then step through the heat pump Checkout routine, which commands the outdoor unit into defrost as part of the sequence. NOT independently re-verified against a current Infinity outdoor-unit Installation Instructions manual for this session, so confirm the exact menu path on the specific control/thermostat model in front of you before relying on it — menu wording has changed across Infinity System Control generations. The physical 2-pin Forced Defrost header on the outdoor board (same as non-comm procedure above) also still works on Infinity outdoor units independent of the thermostat. Source: Carrier documentation as summarized by Hunker 'How To Enter Diagnostic Mode On A Carrier Infinity Thermostat' and JustAnswer HVAC Q&A — treat menu path as a starting point, not gospel."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Coil temperature sensor (DFT) must read cold — Carrier defrost boards generally need the coil sensor closed (roughly below freezing, board-dependent ~30±3°F) before a forced defrost will actually initiate/hold; forcing on a warm coil may not take. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux/W2 heat may energize — a burst of cold air from supply registers is normal, not a fault. Warn occupants if testing with the system live."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"25HCC5","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Comfort-series single-stage heat pumps, 1.5-5 tons: 25HCC5, 25HCE4 (and older 25HBC5), all sharing the same installation instructions. Piston metering on the outdoor heating circuit; TXV or piston indoor depending on coil match. Time/temperature defrost.","match":["25HCC5","25HCE4","25HBC5","25HCC6","25HBC6","Comfort 14","Comfort 15","Bryant Legacy single-stage"],"source":"Carrier Installation Instructions 25HBC-CC-CE-01SI, covering 25HBC5/25HCC5/25HCE4 (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0A/25HBC-CC-CE-01SI.pdf); Product Data 25HCE4-08PD (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/03/25HCE4-08PD.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"\"25HCC6\" and \"25HBC6\" were not found in Carrier's published lineup","body":"No product data or install instructions exist under those exact model numbers. The current Comfort single-stage heat pump family is 25HCC5 paired with 25HCE4 (Comfort 14); the nearest older single-stage Comfort unit is 25HBC5 (Comfort 15). Use this entry for any of those - confirm the exact digit/letter suffix against the unit's rating plate."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering - outdoor (heating)","value":"Piston, in the liquid service valve body","key":"meteringHeat"},{"label":"Metering - indoor (cooling)","value":"TXV or piston depending on indoor coil match - check which is installed before charging","key":"meteringCool"},{"label":"High/low pressure switch cutout","value":"See rating plate - exact psig not published for this platform","key":"pressureSwitchCutout"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Time/temperature electronic defrost control","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Defrost intervals","value":"Field-selectable 30, 60, or 90 min (quick-connect jumper); factory set to 60 or 90 min depending on size; defrost thermostat closes ~30°F liquid line, reopens ~65°F; max 10-min defrost cycle","key":"defrostInterval"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"O terminal, energized in cooling / de-energized in heating","key":"reversingValve"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase","rows":[{"label":"Max outdoor ambient - heating mode","value":"66°F published operating ceiling","key":"maxHeatAmbient"},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling control","value":"Accessory - factory standard only on smallest size group","key":"lowAmbient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Standard on smaller/mid size groups, not on largest; confirm against nameplate","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Charging","value":"Superheat method for piston metering, subcooling method for TXV - see charging chart in install instructions / rating plate","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Standard demand-defrost boards (HK32EA/HK61EA-series, CEPL13xxxx — same family used on Bryant and ICP/Heil/Tempstar). Remove the small plastic cap over the 2-pin 'Forced Defrost' / 'Speed-Up' (TP1/TP2) test header and short the pins with a jumper wire. Momentarily short-and-release once first to clear any compressor anti-short-cycle delay, then re-short and HOLD 5+ seconds — board commands defrost. You should hear the reversing valve shift and see the outdoor fan stop; verify 24V C-to-W2 with a meter. Pull the jumper the instant the valve shifts or the board will hold in speed-up (60x) mode and cycle continuously — don't leave it shorted. If the valve doesn't shift within ~10 sec of the sustained short, board or valve is suspect. Bryant boards are identical; confirm exact pin silkscreen against the installed board revision, since older CEPL revisions label the header 'TEST' and only speed timing rather than instant-force. Source: Carrier/HVAC-Talk field discussion + HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board walkthrough (hvac-talk.com thread 993331; hvactrainingsolutions.net/heat-pump-defrost-control-boards-step-step)."},{"label":"Infinity communicating","value":"On the Infinity touch thermostat, enter the installer 'Checkout' diagnostic (Menu > Setups > Advanced, press and hold Advanced ~10 sec until Install/Service menu appears), then step through the heat pump Checkout routine, which commands the outdoor unit into defrost as part of the sequence. NOT independently re-verified against a current Infinity outdoor-unit Installation Instructions manual for this session, so confirm the exact menu path on the specific control/thermostat model in front of you before relying on it — menu wording has changed across Infinity System Control generations. The physical 2-pin Forced Defrost header on the outdoor board (same as non-comm procedure above) also still works on Infinity outdoor units independent of the thermostat. Source: Carrier documentation as summarized by Hunker 'How To Enter Diagnostic Mode On A Carrier Infinity Thermostat' and JustAnswer HVAC Q&A — treat menu path as a starting point, not gospel."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Coil temperature sensor (DFT) must read cold — Carrier defrost boards generally need the coil sensor closed (roughly below freezing, board-dependent ~30±3°F) before a forced defrost will actually initiate/hold; forcing on a warm coil may not take. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux/W2 heat may energize — a burst of cold air from supply registers is normal, not a fault. Warn occupants if testing with the system live."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"24VNA6","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Infinity Series variable-speed (Greenspeed) air conditioner, 2-5 tons, paired with 25VNA4/25VNA0-family heat pumps or matched fan coils. Variable-speed rotary/scroll compressor, TXV, communicating Infinity control. Covers 24VNA6 and 24VNA9 (19VS) platforms.","match":["24VNA6","24VNA9","Infinity 19VS","Infinity 26","Greenspeed AC","Bryant 186CNV","Bryant 187B","Evolution Extreme AC"],"source":"Carrier Product Data 24VNA6-02PD (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0F/24VNA6-02PD.pdf); Service Manual 24VNA6-25VNA4-1SM (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/01/24VNA6-25VNA4-1SM.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Pressure cutout figures are for the 24VNA6/25VNA4 platform specifically","body":"The 670/470 psig mechanical HPS trip/reset and 15 psig software low-pressure shutdown below come from the 24VNA6-25VNA4 service manual. The 24VNA9 (19VS) uses a related but separate control platform (own service manual: 25VNA8-24VNA9-4SM) - confirm exact figures there before using as a diagnostic threshold on a 24VNA9."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Variable-speed rotary (smaller sizes) or variable-speed scroll (larger sizes)","key":"compressorType"},{"label":"Metering","value":"TXV (Puron hard shutoff)","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches (24VNA6/25VNA4 platform)","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch (mechanical)","value":"Trips 670 psig discharge, resets/closes at 470 psig","key":"hpsCutout"},{"label":"High pressure shutdown (software)","value":"Immediate shutdown at 620 psig","key":"hpShutdownSoftware"},{"label":"Low pressure shutdown (software)","value":"Immediate shutdown at 15 psig","key":"lpShutdownSoftware"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase / Communicating","rows":[{"label":"Low-ambient cooling","value":"Standard down to 0°F with Infinity Control","key":"lowAmbient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Standard","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Full Greenspeed variable-capacity cooling requires Infinity System Control","key":"communicating"},{"label":"Charging","value":"Subcooling method (TXV) - see rating plate / product data charge table by unit size","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"24ANB1","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Two-stage scroll air conditioner, 2-5 tons, compatible with the Infinity System Control for 2-stage communicating operation (also runs on a standard non-communicating stat). Covers the 24ANB1/24ANB7/25HNB6/25HNB9 family sharing one application guideline.","match":["24ANB1","24ANB7","2-stage AC","Infinity 21 AC"],"source":"Carrier Application Guideline and Service Manual 24-25-9SM, covering 24ANB1/24ANB7/25HNB6/25HNB9 (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/03/24-25-9SM.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"This is Infinity-tier, not base Performance","body":"In Carrier's own model-number legend (24-25-9SM), the 'N' position in 24ANB1 stands for Infinity, not Performance. This is the 2-stage, Infinity-System-Control-compatible AC line - verify the actual tier badge against the unit's nameplate/brochure rather than assuming Performance branding."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Two-stage scroll","key":"compressorType"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Hard-shutoff TXV, standard","key":"metering"},{"label":"High pressure switch cutout","value":"See rating plate - standard feature, exact psig not published in this excerpt","key":"pressureSwitchCutout"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase / Communicating","rows":[{"label":"Low-ambient cooling","value":"MotorMaster low-ambient controller / low-ambient pressure switch REQUIRED for cooling operation below 55°F outdoor","key":"lowAmbient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Accessory; standard on smaller size groups only (marked ‡ in spec table) - confirm nameplate","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Supports Infinity System Control (2-stage communicating) and standard non-communicating thermostats","key":"communicating"},{"label":"Charging","value":"See charging chart in application guideline / rating plate","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"24ACC6","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Single-stage scroll air conditioners, 1.5-5 tons, sharing the same TXV/R-410A platform across tier badges: 24ACC6 (Performance 16), 24ABC6 (Comfort 16), and 24AAA6 (Comfort baseline single-stage), all covered by a common installation instructions doc.","match":["24ACC6","24ABC6","24AAA6","Performance 16 AC","Comfort 16 AC"],"source":"Carrier Product Data 24ACC6-9PD (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/07/24ACC6-9PD.pdf) and 24ABC6-8PD (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/01/24ABC6-8PD.pdf); Installation Instructions 24AAA-ACC-11SI, covering 24AAA/24ACC family (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/02/24AAA-ACC-11SI.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Different tier badges, same platform","body":"24ACC6 is badged 'Performance 16' and 24ABC6 is badged 'Comfort 16' in Carrier's own product data, but both list an identical scroll compressor / hard-shutoff TXV / R-410A physical data table - which is why they're grouped here. Don't assume a parts or refrigerant-circuit difference based on the tier name alone; confirm against the specific size/nameplate."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Single-stage scroll","key":"compressorType"},{"label":"Metering","value":"TXV (Puron hard shutoff)","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Standard; exact psig not published - see rating plate","key":"hpsCutout"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Standard; exact psig not published - see rating plate","key":"lpsCutout"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase","rows":[{"label":"Low-ambient cooling","value":"Accessory kit required (not standard)","key":"lowAmbient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Accessory; standard on smaller size groups only, absent on largest - confirm nameplate","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Charging","value":"Subcooling method (TXV) - see charging chart in product data / rating plate","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"24AHA4","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Performance 14 Compact single-stage air conditioner, 1.5-5 tons, horizontal low-profile cabinet. Scroll compressor, TXV, R-410A.","match":["24AHA4","Performance 14 Compact"],"source":"Carrier Product Data 24AHA4-05PD (shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0C/24AHA4-05PD.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Horizontal compact cabinet - not a drop-in for standard units","body":"24AHA4 uses a low-profile horizontal cabinet, not the typical square condenser case. Confirm clearances and airflow/mounting requirements in its own installation instructions before treating it as a like-for-like swap with a standard-cabinet Performance 14 unit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Single-stage scroll","key":"compressorType"},{"label":"Metering","value":"TXV, sized per indoor coil match (subcooling charging method)","key":"metering"},{"label":"High pressure switch cutout","value":"See rating plate - standard feature, exact psig not published in this excerpt","key":"pressureSwitchCutout"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient / Crankcase","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Accessory kit (KAACH series), size-dependent - not standard","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Evaporator freeze thermostat","value":"Accessory","key":"freezeStat"},{"label":"Charging","value":"Subcooling method (TXV) - see charging chart in product data / rating plate","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FV4C","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Performance-tier variable-speed ECM fan coil (002-006, 1.5-5 ton). Non-communicating — configured entirely with 'Easy Select' jumpers/taps on the onboard PCB rather than a wall control link. Factory TXV, upflow/horizontal-left/downflow (kit).","match":["Bryant FV4C (Preferred Series Fan Coil)","Payne FV4C","Carrier Performance™ Fan Coil FV4C"],"source":"Carrier IM-FV4C-04, FV4C 002,003,005,006 Installation Instructions, https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/02/IM-FV4C-04.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Not the same platform as FE4A/FE5A","body":"FV4C is the standard Performance-tier variable-speed fan coil, set up entirely with 'Easy Select' PCB jumpers/taps (AUX HEAT KW/CFM, AC/HP SIZE, SYSTEM TYPE, AC/HP CFM ADJUST, ON/OFF DELAY). It has no SystemVu/communicating link. Don't confuse with the Infinity FE4A/FE5A communicating fan coil (covered separately) — different control board, different setup procedure."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Blower/motor","value":"Variable-speed ECM, factory-programmed airflow tables selected via PCB jumpers/taps (no simple speed switch)","key":"blower_type"},{"label":"AC/HP SIZE tap","value":"Set to match installed condenser/heat pump tonnage (018/024/030/036); factory-set to largest size fan coil supports","key":"size_tap"},{"label":"SYSTEM TYPE tap","value":"AC / HP-COMFORT (~315 CFM/ton heating, ~350 CFM/ton cooling) / HP-EFF (~350 CFM/ton both modes); factory set to AC","key":"system_type"},{"label":"AC/HP CFM ADJUST tap","value":"NOM (factory) / HI (+15% airflow) / LO (-10% airflow), all modes except non-heat-pump heating","key":"cfm_adjust"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"Not published in install instructions — see Product Data / rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Factory filter kit (internal) required unless field filter installed in return duct — see Table 1 filter kit chart for size by unit","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"Factory-authorized field-installed kits, 5-30 kW; exact kits approved listed on unit rating plate","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Supports Intelligent Heat Staging with compatible kits (remove jumper J2 to enable); AUX HEAT KW/CFM tap must be set to narrowest range matching installed heater kW","key":"heat_staging"},{"label":"Clearance","value":"20-, 24-, 30-kW heaters: maintain 1 in. (25 mm) clearance to combustibles at discharge plenum/ductwork for 36 in. from unit; downflow needs accessory base for clearance","key":"heat_clearance"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory hard-shutoff Puron (R-410A) TXV — all indoor coils must use hard-shutoff TXV, never an R-22 TXV or piston","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Primary and secondary condensate pan/trap; prime both traps after connecting, do not use shallow running traps","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FMA4X","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multipoise apartment/multi-family fan coil, upflow only, 1.5-3 ton. FMA4X = TXV + 5-tap multi-tap ECM motor; sibling FMA4P = piston + 3-speed PSC motor. Same cabinet/platform, different metering and blower — verify suffix before parts substitution.","match":["Bryant FMA4X (apartment/multi-family fan coil)","Payne / WeatherMaker FMA4X","Carrier FMA4P (piston/PSC sibling of same platform)"],"source":"Carrier SSG-FMA4-04, FMA4X/FMA4P Product Data, https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/04/SSG-FMA4-04.pdf","flags":[{"title":"FMA4X piston/ECM taps are unit-specific","body":"On the FMA4P (piston) variant, the factory piston is unique to the fan coil and CANNOT be replaced with the piston shipped with the outdoor unit — check AHRI match-up to see if the fan coil's piston works with the chosen condenser or if an accessory TXV kit is required. On FMA4X, the 5-tap ECM motor speed must be selected to land airflow within 300-450 CFM/ton per the performance tables."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"FMA4X blower/motor","value":"ECM, 5 motor speed taps (Tap 1-5)","key":"blower_x"},{"label":"FMA4P blower/motor","value":"PSC, 3 motor speeds (Low/Med/High)","key":"blower_p"},{"label":"Max external static (published)","value":"Performance tables published through 0.8 in. wc for both FMA4X and FMA4P — see Tables 7 & 8","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Filter","value":"16x20x1 in. (406x508x25 mm) on 18/24-size units, 20x20x1 in. (508x508x25 mm) on 30/36-size units, field-installed","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"Accessory field-installed EHK kits, 5, 7.5, or 10 kW (EHK model code: 05/08/10)","key":"heat_kw"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"FMA4X: factory TXV, R-410A. FMA4P: factory piston (.057/.065/.070 orifice by size), R-410A","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Primary/auxiliary connections, both 3/4 in. FPT","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FX4C / FH4C","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Comfort/Legacy-line fixed-speed PSC fan coils, 018-060. FX4C is the standard slope-coil cabinet (upflow/horizontal); FH4C is the compact companion cabinet (sizes 001-004) built factory horizontal-left. Both use 3-tap PSC motor speed selection at the motor and factory Puron TXV.","match":["Bryant FX4C (Legacy Line Fan Coil)","Payne FX4C","Bryant / Payne FH4C","FY4A (TXV coil shipped/installed alongside FX4C in split coil configurations, same IM)","FA4C / FC4D (same installation manual family as FH4C)"],"source":"Carrier IM-FX4C-03, FX4C/FY4A Installation Instructions, https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0E/IM-FX4C-03.pdf ; Carrier FA4C/FC4D/FH4C Installation Instructions, https://www.carrierparts.com/?mdocs-file=130282","flags":[{"title":"FH4C 003/004 horizontal restriction","body":"FH4C is factory built for horizontal-left installation, but FH4C003 and FH4C004 units equipped with an accessory cooling coil are NOT approved for horizontal applications — verify size/coil combination before mounting. All other FX4C/FH4C sizes support upflow and horizontal-left."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Blower/motor","value":"Fixed-speed PSC, typically 3 motor speed taps","key":"blower_type"},{"label":"Speed selection","value":"Done at the motor, not the board: disconnect fan lead from terminal 2 and move to desired tap — Low (1), Medium (2), High (3). Low static duct systems should use lower tap; high-static systems should use higher tap","key":"speed_select"},{"label":"Max external static (published)","value":"Performance tables published through 0.60 in. wc across sizes 018-060 (see Table 1)","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Factory filter kit required if filter is located inside unit; otherwise field-supplied filter required in return duct","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"Field-installed accessory electric heater packages, 5-30 kW; exact approved kits on rating plate","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Clearance","value":"20-30 kW heaters require 1 in. (25 mm) clearance to combustibles at discharge plenum for specified distance from unit","key":"heat_clearance"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory hard-shutoff Puron (R-410A) TXV — do not use R-22 TXV or a piston metering device","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Primary and secondary drain pan connections with traps; prime all traps after hookup, do not use shallow running traps to avoid overflow","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FB4C","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Comfort/Legacy-line multipoise fan coil, 018-061, multi-tap ECM motor across all sizes. FB4CNF (018-048) ships with a factory piston; FB4CNP (018-061) ships with a factory TXV — check the model suffix before ordering metering parts or matching to the outdoor unit.","match":["Bryant FB4C (Legacy Line Fan Coil)","Payne FB4C","WeatherMaker FB4C"],"source":"Carrier FB4CNF-P-13PD, FB4C Base Series Fan Coil Product Data, https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/04/FB4CNF-P-13PD.pdf","flags":[{"title":"NF (piston) vs NP (TXV) suffix matters","body":"FB4CNF (018-048) has a factory-installed Teflon-ring piston; FB4CNP (018-061) has a factory TXV. Confirm the suffix on the rating plate before selecting a replacement metering kit or checking AHRI match-up with the outdoor unit — the two are not interchangeable without the correct accessory kit (TXV kits KFAFR0301FRM / KSATX-series listed in accessories table)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Blower/motor","value":"Multi-tap ECM, all sizes, 5 speed taps (Tap 1-5)","key":"blower_type"},{"label":"Speed selection note","value":"Speed Tap 4 (white wire) is reserved for electric heat only — must remain on tap 4, do not reassign for cooling/heat-pump speed","key":"speed_select"},{"label":"Max external static (published)","value":"Performance tables published through 0.60 in. wc across sizes 018-061","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Field-supplied filter required (no factory filter included) — filter rack/cabinet accessory kits available (KFAFK0112SML, KFAFR0101FRM, etc.)","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Kit range","value":"Factory-installed heater packages on select models (5-15 kW); accessory field-installed heaters 3-30 kW","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Clearance","value":"20-, 24-, 30-kW heaters require 1 in. (25 mm) clearance to combustibles at discharge plenum","key":"heat_clearance"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"FB4CNF (018-048): factory Teflon-ring piston, Puron (R-410A). FB4CNP (018-061): factory TXV, Puron (R-410A)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Primary/secondary drain connections; prime traps before use per condensate-blowing cautions at high CFM/ton on 048-061 sizes","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DM97MC / DC97MC","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"97% AFUE modulating gas furnace, 34.5\" chassis. Gas valve modulates continuously (nominally 35-100% of high fire) via pneumatic linkage to the variable-speed inducer.","match":["DM97MC","DC97MC"],"source":"Daikin DM97MC/DC97MC Installation Instructions (IM/IOD-2007 series), daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dc97mc/im-iod-2007q.pdf; Daikin DM97MC/DC97MC Service Instructions, daikincity.com/document/Service%20Manual/129985","flags":[{"title":"Do not chase microamps on modulating flame sensor","body":"Daikin service literature states reading flame signal with a microamp meter will not provide reliable/consistent results on this platform and is not a recommended diagnostic practice. IFC posts warning code E6 when signal approaches the low threshold; clean the sensor with steel wool if signal is marginal instead of chasing a microamp number."},{"title":"Flame-sense µA not confirmed in this pass — pulled from the Installation Instructions, not the Service Instructions","body":"IOD-2007F (the installation manual) documents E6 'low flame sense' as a status code but does not print a microamp value. The DM96VC and DM92SN/DM96SN platforms' Service Instructions both publish '1-4 µA DC' via an S-314 procedure on the same-generation Integrated Ignition control — DM97MC likely has an equivalent Service Instructions document (not the IOD- installation manual) with its own S-314 section, but it was not located/opened in this pass. Do not assume 1-4 µA applies to this modulating board without confirming against DM97MC's own Service Instructions."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG, low stage (~50% firing)","value":"3.5\" w.c. (#45 orifice)","key":"manifold_ng_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG, high stage / full modulation","value":"see rating plate","key":"manifold_ng_high"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"see rating plate","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, NG","value":"4.5\" w.c. min - 10.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, LP","value":"11.0\" w.c. min - 13.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Fixed, non-adjustable orifice (#45 shown for low stage on published model); do not peen or redrill; verify size on rating plate/LP kit for specific model","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Modulating furnaces approved for install up to 10,000 ft with no kit or changes required (NG); Canada certified only to 4500 ft; LP altitude kit LPM-09-1.25MM referenced for LP applications","key":"altitude"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, max input (Hi stage)","value":"3.2-3.8\" w.c. NG (3.5\" nominal) / 9.5-10.5\" w.c. LP (10.0\" nominal) at 100% firing","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure at ignition (80% of max input)","value":"1.8-2.5\" w.c. NG / 5.8-6.8\" w.c. LP — the furnace always lights at 80% input before modulating; use Field Test Mode (double-press Fault Recall button) to lock 100% fire and read max-input pressure instead"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"Varies by model, e.g. 20-50°F to 35-65°F depending on chassis/tonnage - see rating plate for exact model","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"Return/entering air temperature requirement","value":"see rating plate","key":"return_air_temp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range (Hi/Lo stage, model-specific)","value":"20-50°F / 25-55°F on DM97MC0603BN up to 35-65°F / 35-65°F on DC97MC0803BN & DC97MC0804CN — full table by model in IOD-2007F p.43, or see rating plate"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/ignition","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Hot surface ignitor (Daikin 0131F00008S), 37-68 ohms cold resistance, ~17 second warm-up","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Ground check","value":"Measure resistance between neutral (white) connection and a burner (bare metal) - should read 10 ohms or less","key":"ground_check"},{"label":"Status code display","value":"IFC flash/alpha codes on furnace display, e.g. A=normal, H=% gas heat demand, P=% high heat, C=low indoor airflow, E1=low flame signal, E2=igniter fault/improper ground, E7=inducer overcurrent, E8=rollout open, b0-b9=blower faults","key":"status_codes"},{"label":"Induced draft blower motor","value":"ECM winding resistance 14-17 ohms room temp (+/-5% between windings), IFC drive voltage 15-110 VAC between windings","key":"idb_motor"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit control","value":"Non-adjustable, automatic-reset, bi-metal, normally closed - no published numeric setpoint (rating plate/part only)","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, temperature-activated, mounted to manifold assembly; normally closed - check continuity with ohmmeter","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DM92SN / DC92SN / DM96SN / DC96SN","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"R-32-era single-stage, multi-speed ECM gas furnace platform - 92% AFUE (DM92SN/DC92SN) and 96% AFUE (DM96SN/DC96SN) share the same install/service instructions and gas-train specs.","match":["DM92SN","DC92SN","DM96SN","DC96SN"],"source":"Daikin Installation Instructions for DM92SN, DM96SN & DC96SN Single-Stage Gas Furnace (IOD-2029), daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dm96sn/iod-2029.pdf; Daikin Service Instructions RSD6612021, DM92SN, DM96SN & DC96SN Models, daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dm96sn/291234817.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Drain trap is dual-partitioned - prime both sides","body":"Daikin installation instructions specify the drain trap must be primed prior to startup by filling BOTH sides of the trap with water, not just one - a single-side fill leaves one leg dry and can pull flue gas/nuisance-trip the pressure switch."},{"title":"Igniter and pressure-switch/limit numbers are published per exact model — don't average across the line","body":"Unlike most Daikin single-stage platforms, this Service Instructions manual (RSD6612021) prints an exact Pressure Switch Trip Point table and a Primary/Auxiliary/Rollout Limit Setting table keyed to the full model number (e.g. DM96SN0403ANAA vs DC96SN1205DNAA give different limit setpoints and different pressure-switch part numbers). The figures above are representative endpoints from that table — pull the exact row for the unit's full model number before condemning a switch or limit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG","value":"3.5\" w.c. nominal (3.2-3.8\" w.c. range, tolerance +/-0.3\" from setpoint)","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"10.0\" w.c. nominal (9.7-10.3\" w.c. range, tolerance +0.5\" from setpoint)","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, NG","value":"4.5\" w.c. min - 10.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, LP","value":"11.0\" w.c. min - 13.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate (fixed orifice, size not published generically in install/service instructions)","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Install per Listed High Altitude Conversion Kit required above 7000 ft (2134 m); do not reduce manifold pressure below rating-plate spec at altitude - low air density + low manifold pressure starves burner orifice of air","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-specific table in Specification Sheet)","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"Return/entering air temperature requirement","value":"see rating plate","key":"return_air_temp"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/ignition","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"120V silicon nitride HSI, 37-68 ohms cold resistance, steady-state preheat current 0.37-0.68A at 120V, normal operating temp ~2156-2678°F","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Ground check","value":"115VAC supply must be properly grounded with correct polarity; measure neutral-to-bare-metal resistance - 10 ohms or less (standard Daikin ground check)","key":"ground_check"},{"label":"Status code display","value":"IFC status menu shows mode codes (idle, continuous fan, cooling low/high stage, gas heat) - see rating plate/IFC menu for full code list","key":"status_codes"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Auxiliary/primary limit control","value":"see rating plate (S-301 checking procedure published; numeric setpoint not published generically)","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset flame rollout control, opens on flame rollout condition - check continuity with ohmmeter","key":"rollout"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"1-4 µA DC normal on the Integrated Ignition control (S-314 CHECKING FLAME SENSOR); if low, check high-resistance wiring, sensor-to-burner gap, dirty/oxidized sensor, or poor grounding","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch trip (coil cover / ID blower, model-specific)","value":"Published per exact model in a Pressure Switch Trip Point table — e.g. DM92SN0403AN: coil-cover switch closes on -0.10±.05 in. w.c. fall (max make -0.25\"), ID blower switch -0.20±.05 in. w.c. fall (max make -0.35\"); larger DM92SN/DM96SN/DC96SN sizes range up to about -1.2 to -1.5 in. w.c. on the ID blower switch — see Service Instructions RSD6612021 p.40 table for the exact model, do not assume one number across the line"},{"label":"Rollout limit (manual reset, model-specific)","value":"220-275°F depending on exact DM96SN/DC96SN model (e.g. DM96SN0403AN 230±6°F, DM96SN1205DN 275±7°F) — see RSD6612021 p.40 table"},{"label":"Auxiliary limit","value":"120°F fixed, auto-reset, same across all DM96SN/DC96SN models (RSD6612021 p.40 table)"},{"label":"Primary limit (auto-reset, model-specific)","value":"150-210°F depending on exact DM96SN/DC96SN model (e.g. DM96SN0803BNAA 150±5°F, DC96SN0403BNAA 210±6°F) — see RSD6612021 p.40 table for the exact model; not published separately for DM92SN in this document"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DM80HE / DC80 (DM80HS / DD80HS / DM80SS platform)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE two-stage, convertible multi-speed gas furnace platform. DM80HE shares its Installation Instructions with the DD80HS and DM80SS models (upflow/horizontal and downflow/horizontal variants of the same chassis).","match":["DM80HE","DC80","DD80HS","DM80SS","DM80HS"],"source":"Daikin Installation Instructions for DM80(H,S)S/DD80(H,S)S/DM80HE Gas Furnace, daikincomfort.com (ManualsLib-hosted copy: manualslib.com/manual/3578174/Daikin-Dm80s.html); DM80HS0403A product literature (Durable Silicon Nitride igniter, self-diagnostic control board)","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure is on the rating plate, not a single fixed number","body":"This is a single-orifice, two-stage design - staging is done by the gas valve regulator, not a second orifice. Daikin's install instructions state gas manifold pressure MUST be as specified on the unit rating plate and that only minor adjustment should be made at the gas valve pressure regulator - do not set to a generic number without checking the plate for that specific model/BTU input."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG low/high stage","value":"Typical two-stage table on this platform: low ~1.9\" w.c. (1.6-2.2\" range), high ~3.5\" w.c. (3.2-3.8\" range) - confirm exact stage values on rating plate","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP low/high stage","value":"Typical two-stage table on this platform: low ~6.0\" w.c. (5.7-6.3\" range), high ~10.0\" w.c. (9.7-10.3\" range) - confirm exact stage values on rating plate","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, NG","value":"4.5\" w.c. min - 10.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, LP","value":"11.0\" w.c. min - 13.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"NG: #45; LP: #55 (requires LPT-03 kit single-stage / LPM-06 kit two-stage)","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"No modification required 0-5,500 ft; above 5,500 ft a pressure switch change and orifice change kit are required (distributor-supplied kit)","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-specific chart in Quick Start/Specification Sheet)","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"Return/entering air temperature requirement","value":"see rating plate","key":"return_air_temp"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/ignition","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon Nitride HSI; generic Daikin HSI spec is 37-68 ohms cold resistance - confirm on this specific control if in doubt","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Ground check","value":"Standard Daikin ground/polarity check: resistance between neutral (white) connection and a burner (bare metal) should be 10 ohms or less","key":"ground_check"},{"label":"Status code display","value":"Self-diagnostic control board with constant-memory fault code, shown via LED flash code - see control board legend/rating plate for full code list","key":"status_codes"},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"1-4 µA DC normal on the Integrated Ignition control (S-314 CHECKING FLAME SENSOR) — confirmed via the Goodman/Amana 'GME8 & AMEH8 Modified Two Stage Furnace' Service Instructions, form RS6621001r2 (Aug 2016), p.55: 'The Integrated Ignition controls will have 1 to 4 micro-amps.' GME8/AMEH8 is the Goodman/Amana twin of this Daikin Modified Two-Stage 80% platform — confirmed by matching two-stage manifold pressure tables (NG low 1.6-2.2\" / high 3.2-3.8\" w.c.; LP low 5.7-6.3\" / high 9.7-10.3\" w.c.) against this entry's existing Gas group. If low, check high-resistance wiring, sensor-to-burner gap, dirty/oxidized sensor, or poor grounding.","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit control","value":"see rating plate (non-adjustable auto-reset control; numeric setpoint not published generically)","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset flame rollout control - check continuity with ohmmeter","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DM80SN / DC80SN","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage gas furnace, its own service platform distinct from the DM80HE two-stage chassis. Ships with either a Carbide Mini or Silicon Nitride hot surface igniter depending on production run.","match":["DM80SN","DC80SN"],"source":"Daikin DM80SN/DC80SN Service Instructions, daikincomfort.com (ManualsLib-hosted copy: manualslib.com/manual/2583493/Daikin-Dm80sn.html)","flags":[{"title":"Two different igniter types in the field - don't assume ohms range","body":"This platform used either a Carbide Mini igniter (30-300 ohms cold, ~2550-2876°F operating temp, ~0.7A +/-0.3A steady-state draw) or a 120V Silicon Nitride igniter (part 0130F00008, 37-68 ohms cold, ~2156-2678°F operating temp). Confirm which is installed before condemning an igniter on a resistance reading - a Silicon Nitride unit reading 150 ohms is bad, but that same 150 ohms is normal on a Carbide Mini."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG","value":"3.5\" w.c. (tolerance +/-0.3\" w.c. from setpoint)","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"10.0\" w.c. (tolerance +/-0.3\" w.c. from setpoint)","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, NG","value":"4.5\" w.c. min - 10.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply/inlet gas pressure, LP","value":"11.0\" w.c. min - 13.0\" w.c. max","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate (fixed orifice; per manual, resize only for altitude-related firing-rate reduction - never peen or redrill)","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"see rating plate / distributor altitude kit (not published generically in this manual section)","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"Return/entering air temperature requirement","value":"see rating plate","key":"return_air_temp"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics/ignition","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor - Carbide Mini","value":"30-300 ohms cold resistance, ~2550-2876°F operating temp, steady-state current ~0.7A +/-0.3A at 120V","key":"ignitor_carbide"},{"label":"Ignitor - Silicon Nitride","value":"Part 0130F00008, 37-68 ohms cold resistance, ~2156-2678°F operating temp","key":"ignitor_sn"},{"label":"Ground check","value":"Standard Daikin ground/polarity check: resistance between neutral (white) connection and a burner (bare metal) should be 10 ohms or less","key":"ground_check"},{"label":"Status/config display","value":"IFC main/option menu shows active alarm + last 6 faults by code number; also hosts blower-speed and heat/cool on/off delay config (e.g. gas heat on-delay default 30 sec, off-delay default 90 sec)","key":"status_codes"},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"1-4 µA DC normal on the Integrated Ignition control (S-314 CHECKING FLAME SENSOR) — confirmed directly from Daikin's own DM80SN/DC80SN Service Instructions, form RSD6621010 (July 2021): 'The Integrated Ignition controls will have 1 to 4 micro-amps.' If low, check high-resistance wiring, sensor-to-burner gap, dirty/oxidized sensor, or poor grounding.","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit control","value":"see rating plate (S-300 checking procedure published; numeric setpoint not published generically)","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset flame rollout control (S-302) - check continuity with ohmmeter","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DZ18TC / DX18TC","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Shared-platform 2-stage (Low/High capacity) split-system heat pump (DZ18TC) and air conditioner (DX18TC), R-410A, factory-equipped with an outdoor air temperature (OAT) sensor and optional ComfortNet communicating control.","match":["DZ18TC","DZ18VCA","DX18TC","Daikin 2-stage heat pump","Daikin 2-stage condenser"],"source":"SS-DZ18TC spec sheet, backend.daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/product-documents/residential/specifications/ss-dz18tc.pdf; ComfortNet DX16TC & DX18TC Service Instructions","flags":[{"title":"Model number check","body":"User's original spec sheet listed 'DZ18VCA' for a 2-stage heat pump, but Daikin's published 2-stage platform is DZ18TC (paired AC: DX18TC) — DZ18VC/DZ18VCA is actually an inverter (variable-speed swing compressor) model, not 2-stage. Confirm the exact nameplate model/serial before servicing; this entry covers the DZ18TC/DX18TC 2-stage platform."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV (thermostatic expansion valve)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"2-stage (Low/High capacity) scroll compressor","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Heat Pump Operation (DZ18TC)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand-defrost control board (time/temperature adaptive)","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling; de-energized in heating (standard Daikin residential convention)","key":"reversingValve"},{"label":"Low-ambient heating lockout","value":"See service manual / installation instructions for line-set-length-dependent lockout tables","key":"lowAmbient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch setpoints","value":"See service manual — cutout/cutin PSIG varies by tonnage; not safe to generalize across the 1.5–5 ton range","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"See rating plate / service manual for this tonnage (not confirmed factory-standard across all sizes)","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"ComfortNet-ready — factory OAT sensor installed; supports ComfortNet communicating thermostat, non-communicating (24V) operation also supported","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Standard superheat/subcooling charging per unit nameplate charging chart (non-inverter 2-stage compressor — standard gauge charging applies, unlike the inverter platforms)","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"PARTIALLY verifiable only. Daikin's DZ6VSA (Daikin Fit family) service reference lists a defrost-board configuration parameter literally named 'Force Defrost Cycle' with two states (0:ON / 1:OFF), indicating it's a field-configurable setting rather than a simple momentary-jumper test — but the exact DIP switch bank/pin location and how the ON state behaves (one-shot vs. persistent) could not be confirmed from the accessible manual excerpt this session. Do NOT guess the switch position or pin numbers — pull the full Daikin DZ6VSA (or applicable model) Installation & Service Reference and locate the 'Force Defrost Cycle' setting in the defrost-board configuration table before using it in the field. Source: Daikin DZ6VSA 1EA Series Installation & Service Reference (ManualsLib-hosted copy)."},{"label":"Daikin One+ communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. The Daikin One+ thermostat has a 'System Test' function used for inverter calibration (5–15 minutes, must not be interrupted, master zone-1 thermostat only, all other zone stats set OFF) and a general service/diagnostics menu, but no source located confirmed a dedicated, documented 'force defrost' command distinct from that calibration test. Do not treat System Test as a defrost-force procedure without confirming with current Daikin service documentation for the specific communicating outdoor unit."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, expect any genuine forced-defrost test to require (or bypass) a cold coil condition, and to shift the reversing valve to cooling and stop the outdoor fan — a burst of cold supply air is normal during the test. Because the exact Daikin force-defrost mechanics aren't fully confirmed here, verify against the specific unit's Installation & Service Reference before performing a live test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DZ17VSA / DX17VSS","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Daikin FIT variable-speed, inverter-drive, side-discharge split system: DZ17VSA heat pump and DX17VSS air conditioner, R-410A, EEV metering, Intelligent Defrost, Daikin One+ compatible.","match":["DZ17VSA","DX17VSA","DX17VSS","Daikin FIT 17 series","Daikin FIT heat pump","Daikin FIT air conditioner"],"source":"SS-DZ17VSA spec sheet and SS-DX17VSS spec sheet, backend.daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/product-documents/residential/specifications/ (ss-dz17vsa.pdf, ss-dx17vss.pdf); DX17VSS/DZ17VSA outdoor unit installation instructions","flags":[{"title":"Model number check","body":"User's original list gave 'DX17VSA' for the AC condenser; Daikin's published FIT AC partner to DZ17VSA is DX17VSS (no DX17VSA exists in current Daikin literature). Confirm nameplate model before ordering parts."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"EEV (electronic expansion valve)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Variable-speed (inverter) swing compressor, side-discharge cabinet","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Heat Pump Operation (DZ17VSA)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Intelligent Defrost Mode (inverter demand-based, communicating control)","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling; de-energized in heating (standard Daikin residential convention)","key":"reversingValve"},{"label":"Low-ambient heating lockout","value":"Line-set-length dependent — installation instructions specify a 15°F heating lockout when the line set is 30 ft or longer; see manual for full lockout table by line length","key":"lowAmbient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch setpoints","value":"See service manual — inverter-modulated; cutout/cutin not fixed across the operating range","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"See rating plate / service manual for this tonnage","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Daikin One+ smart thermostat compatible; communicating (BACnet-style Daikin serial) control with algorithmic staging logic","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Inverter charge mode via control board / Daikin One app — do NOT charge to static gauge superheat/subcooling targets; charge to nameplate per installation instructions' final charge procedure","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"PARTIALLY verifiable only. Daikin's DZ6VSA (Daikin Fit family) service reference lists a defrost-board configuration parameter literally named 'Force Defrost Cycle' with two states (0:ON / 1:OFF), indicating it's a field-configurable setting rather than a simple momentary-jumper test — but the exact DIP switch bank/pin location and how the ON state behaves (one-shot vs. persistent) could not be confirmed from the accessible manual excerpt this session. Do NOT guess the switch position or pin numbers — pull the full Daikin DZ6VSA (or applicable model) Installation & Service Reference and locate the 'Force Defrost Cycle' setting in the defrost-board configuration table before using it in the field. Source: Daikin DZ6VSA 1EA Series Installation & Service Reference (ManualsLib-hosted copy)."},{"label":"Daikin One+ communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. The Daikin One+ thermostat has a 'System Test' function used for inverter calibration (5–15 minutes, must not be interrupted, master zone-1 thermostat only, all other zone stats set OFF) and a general service/diagnostics menu, but no source located confirmed a dedicated, documented 'force defrost' command distinct from that calibration test. Do not treat System Test as a defrost-force procedure without confirming with current Daikin service documentation for the specific communicating outdoor unit."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, expect any genuine forced-defrost test to require (or bypass) a cold coil condition, and to shift the reversing valve to cooling and stop the outdoor fan — a burst of cold supply air is normal during the test. Because the exact Daikin force-defrost mechanics aren't fully confirmed here, verify against the specific unit's Installation & Service Reference before performing a live test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DZ6VS / DX6VS","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Daikin FIT entry-level R-32 (A2L) side-discharge inverter platform: DZ6VS heat pump and DX6VS air conditioner. Factory crankcase heater required per R-32 long-line-set guidance.","match":["DZ6VS","DZ6VSA","DX6VS","Daikin FIT R-32","Daikin R32 side discharge"],"source":"SS-DZ6VS and SS-DX6VS spec sheets, backend.daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/product-documents/residential/specifications/ (ss-dz6vs.pdf, ss-dx6vs.pdf); DZ6VS Service Instructions (SiUS612209EA), daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/daikin-fit-heat-pump---dz6vs/; R-32 Long Line Set Application Technical Publication TP-110","flags":[{"title":"R-32 (A2L) refrigerant — verify nameplate before service","body":"This platform uses R-32, a mildly flammable (A2L) refrigerant. Use only EPA 608-certified, A2L-rated recovery/charging equipment and an A2L-approved (non-spark) leak detector; no open flame or halogen-torch leak testing. Confirm refrigerant type on the unit's own rating plate — do not assume from model family alone."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-32 (A2L, mildly flammable) — verify on rating plate","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"EEV (electronic expansion valve)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Variable-speed inverter, side-discharge cabinet","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Heat Pump Operation (DZ6VS)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Inverter demand-based defrost control","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling; de-energized in heating (standard Daikin residential convention)","key":"reversingValve"},{"label":"Low-ambient heating range","value":"Published heating operating range approximately -10°F to 70°F ambient; see spec sheet for exact lockout by capacity","key":"lowAmbient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch setpoints","value":"See service manual — inverter-modulated, not fixed","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-installed on all heat pump models in this line per Daikin R-32 long-line-set guidance; a 40W crankcase heater is required on any compressor if not already factory-fitted","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Daikin One+ compatible communicating control","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Inverter charge mode — do NOT charge to static gauge superheat/subcooling targets; charge to nameplate per installation instructions' final charge procedure. A2L systems: pressure-test with dry nitrogen/helium only, never refrigerant, for leak checks","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"PARTIALLY verifiable only. Daikin's DZ6VSA (Daikin Fit family) service reference lists a defrost-board configuration parameter literally named 'Force Defrost Cycle' with two states (0:ON / 1:OFF), indicating it's a field-configurable setting rather than a simple momentary-jumper test — but the exact DIP switch bank/pin location and how the ON state behaves (one-shot vs. persistent) could not be confirmed from the accessible manual excerpt this session. Do NOT guess the switch position or pin numbers — pull the full Daikin DZ6VSA (or applicable model) Installation & Service Reference and locate the 'Force Defrost Cycle' setting in the defrost-board configuration table before using it in the field. Source: Daikin DZ6VSA 1EA Series Installation & Service Reference (ManualsLib-hosted copy)."},{"label":"Daikin One+ communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. The Daikin One+ thermostat has a 'System Test' function used for inverter calibration (5–15 minutes, must not be interrupted, master zone-1 thermostat only, all other zone stats set OFF) and a general service/diagnostics menu, but no source located confirmed a dedicated, documented 'force defrost' command distinct from that calibration test. Do not treat System Test as a defrost-force procedure without confirming with current Daikin service documentation for the specific communicating outdoor unit."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, expect any genuine forced-defrost test to require (or bypass) a cold coil condition, and to shift the reversing valve to cooling and stop the outdoor fan — a burst of cold supply air is normal during the test. Because the exact Daikin force-defrost mechanics aren't fully confirmed here, verify against the specific unit's Installation & Service Reference before performing a live test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DH9VS / DC9VS","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Daikin FIT Aurora R-32 (A2L) higher-performance inverter platform: DH9VS side-discharge cold-climate heat pump (ENERGY STAR Cold Climate Heat Pump certified) and DC9VS air conditioner.","match":["DH9VS","DZ9VSA","DC9VS","DX9VSA","Daikin FIT Aurora","Daikin cold climate heat pump R-32"],"source":"SS-DH9VS-R32 spec sheet, daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/fit-aurora-heat-pump-dh9vs/ss-dh9vs-r32.pdf; SS-DC9VS-R32 spec sheet; DH9VS/DH7VS/DC9VS Outdoor Unit Installation & Service Reference Manual","flags":[{"title":"Model number check + R-32 (A2L) refrigerant","body":"User's original list named 'DZ9VSA'/'DX9VSA' for the R-32 inverter platform; no such models appear in current Daikin literature. The closest published R-32 inverter platform above the entry-level DZ6VS/DX6VS line is DH9VS (heat pump, Aurora cold-climate) paired with DC9VS (AC). R-32 is a mildly flammable (A2L) refrigerant — use only EPA 608-certified, A2L-rated equipment and A2L-approved leak detection; confirm refrigerant on the rating plate."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-32 (A2L, mildly flammable) — verify on rating plate","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"EEV (electronic expansion valve)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Variable-speed inverter (swing compressor), side-discharge cabinet","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Heat Pump Operation (DH9VS)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Inverter demand-based defrost control","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling; de-energized in heating (standard Daikin residential convention)","key":"reversingValve"},{"label":"Low-ambient / cold-climate rating","value":"ENERGY STAR Cold Climate Heat Pump certified — engineered for high heating-capacity retention at low outdoor ambient; see spec sheet capacity-maintenance table for exact temperature points (not generalized here)","key":"lowAmbient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch setpoints","value":"See service manual — inverter-modulated, not fixed","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-installed (standard on this R-32 heat pump line per Daikin long-line-set guidance)","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Daikin One+ compatible communicating control","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Inverter charge mode — do NOT charge to static gauge superheat/subcooling targets; charge to nameplate per installation instructions' final charge procedure. A2L systems: pressure-test with dry nitrogen/helium only, never refrigerant","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"PARTIALLY verifiable only. Daikin's DZ6VSA (Daikin Fit family) service reference lists a defrost-board configuration parameter literally named 'Force Defrost Cycle' with two states (0:ON / 1:OFF), indicating it's a field-configurable setting rather than a simple momentary-jumper test — but the exact DIP switch bank/pin location and how the ON state behaves (one-shot vs. persistent) could not be confirmed from the accessible manual excerpt this session. Do NOT guess the switch position or pin numbers — pull the full Daikin DZ6VSA (or applicable model) Installation & Service Reference and locate the 'Force Defrost Cycle' setting in the defrost-board configuration table before using it in the field. Source: Daikin DZ6VSA 1EA Series Installation & Service Reference (ManualsLib-hosted copy)."},{"label":"Daikin One+ communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. The Daikin One+ thermostat has a 'System Test' function used for inverter calibration (5–15 minutes, must not be interrupted, master zone-1 thermostat only, all other zone stats set OFF) and a general service/diagnostics menu, but no source located confirmed a dedicated, documented 'force defrost' command distinct from that calibration test. Do not treat System Test as a defrost-force procedure without confirming with current Daikin service documentation for the specific communicating outdoor unit."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, expect any genuine forced-defrost test to require (or bypass) a cold coil condition, and to shift the reversing valve to cooling and stop the outdoor fan — a burst of cold supply air is normal during the test. Because the exact Daikin force-defrost mechanics aren't fully confirmed here, verify against the specific unit's Installation & Service Reference before performing a live test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DX20VC","equip":"Condenser","summary":"High-efficiency inverter-technology split-system air conditioner (up to 24.5 SEER), R-410A, shares its inverter platform with the already-covered DZ20VC heat pump. Standalone AC-only equivalent — no matching DZ20VC 'AC-only' distinction needed since DZ20VC covers the heat pump side.","match":["DX20VC","Daikin inverter condenser","Daikin 20 SEER AC"],"source":"SS-DX20VC spec sheet, backend.daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/product-documents/residential/specifications/ss-dx20vc.pdf","flags":[{"title":"AC-side companion to already-covered DZ20VC","body":"DZ20VC (heat pump) is already documented elsewhere in this tool; DX20VC is its cooling-only counterpart and shares the same inverter compressor/EEV/communicating platform — heat-pump-specific fields (defrost, reversing valve) do not apply to this AC-only unit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"EEV (electronic expansion valve)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Variable-speed inverter (Swing/Scroll depending on tonnage)","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Controls & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch setpoints","value":"See service manual — inverter-modulated, not fixed across the 2–5 ton range","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"See rating plate / service manual for this tonnage","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"ComfortNet/Daikin One+ compatible variable-speed communicating control","key":"communicating"},{"label":"Cooling ambient operating range","value":"See spec sheet for minimum/maximum outdoor ambient cooling operation by tonnage","key":"ambientRange"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Inverter charge mode — do NOT charge to static gauge superheat/subcooling targets; charge to nameplate per installation instructions' final charge procedure","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DX16SA","equip":"Condenser","summary":"High-efficiency single-stage split-system air conditioner, up to 16 SEER, R-410A, fixed-speed scroll compressor with single-speed condenser fan — the AC-only counterpart to the already-covered DZ16SA/DZ14SA standard heat pumps.","match":["DX16SA","Daikin single stage condenser","Daikin 16 SEER AC"],"source":"SS-DX16SA spec sheet, backend.daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/product-documents/residential/specifications/ss-dx16sa.pdf","flags":[{"title":"AC-side companion to already-covered DZ16SA/DZ14SA","body":"DZ16SA and DZ14SA (standard single/2-stage heat pumps) are already documented elsewhere in this tool. DX16SA is the fixed-speed AC-only condenser sharing this standard (non-inverter) platform — heat-pump-specific fields (defrost, reversing valve, low-ambient heating lockout) do not apply."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV (thermostatic expansion valve)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Single-stage, single-speed scroll compressor","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Controls & Protection","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch setpoints","value":"See service manual — cutout/cutin PSIG varies by tonnage (1.5–5 ton range)","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"See rating plate / service manual for this tonnage (not standard on all sizes of this fixed-speed platform)","key":"crankcaseHeater"},{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Non-communicating, standard 24V single-stage control (no ComfortNet/Daikin One+ communicating capability on this platform)","key":"communicating"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Standard superheat (fixed orifice-style TXV) charging per unit nameplate charging chart — conventional gauge charging applies (non-inverter, fixed-speed compressor)","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DAR / DAT Series","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Commercial multi-position air handler, 7.5-10 ton, belt-drive centrifugal blower (DAR = single-speed motor; DAT = two-speed motor, 3-phase only), factory-installed internal TXV. No factory electric heat -- AHKD accessory heater kits only.","match":["DAR09*","DAR12*","DAT09*","DAT12*","AR090*","AR120*"],"source":"Daikin Service Instructions RSD6200006R47 (DAR09, DAR12, DAT09, DAT12, DX11/13/14/15/16), daikincomfort.com","flags":[{"title":"No factory electric heat","body":"AR, DAR, and DAT series air handlers do not have factory-installed electric heat. AHKD accessory heater kits (15/20/30 kW nominal, 208-230V-3-60 or 460V-3-60) are the ONLY heater kits approved for these series -- confirm the electrical characteristics of the air handler, heater kit, and building power supply are compatible before install."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower / Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower drive","value":"Belt-driven, draw-through centrifugal blower; heavy-gauge galvanized cabinet with fiberglass sound-blanket lining","key":"blower"},{"label":"Speed","value":"DAR = single-speed motor; DAT = two-speed motor (for use with two condenser stages, e.g. DX13/DZ13)","key":"speed"},{"label":"Airflow setup / CFM per tap","value":"Not published in the service literature reviewed -- confirm against the unit rating plate or IOM airflow table before adjusting","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"See unit rating plate / IOM airflow table (not captured in service manual reviewed)","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Heat / Metering / Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed, internally mounted TXV (nomenclature position 'T')","key":"metering"},{"label":"Electric heat","value":"None factory-installed. AHKD accessory kits: 15 kW / 20 kW / 30 kW nominal, 208-230V-3-60 or 460V-3-60","key":"heat_kit"},{"label":"Voltage config","value":"DAR: 208/230V 3-phase. DAT: 208/230V or 460V 3-phase. Indoor applications field-convertible 208/230-3-60 to 460-3-60","key":"voltage"},{"label":"Drain pan / filter","value":"Not detailed in the service manual sections reviewed -- see rating plate / IOM for exact drain connection and filter size","key":"drain_filter"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"ASPT / AMST Series","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Residential multi-position, multi-speed ECM-based air handler with internal factory TXV, 1.5-5 ton (ASPT); companion AMST is the current 9-speed ECM update on the same cased-cabinet platform. NOTE: no Daikin model literally named 'DASH' exists in the literature reviewed -- this entry is mapped to the closest current multi-speed/high-efficiency ECM cased air handler family and should be verified against the unit's actual nameplate model.","match":["ASPT*","AMST*"],"source":"Daikin Spec Sheet SS-DASPT (ASPT Series, Multi-Position Multi-Speed ECM-Based Air Handler w/ Internal TXV, 1.5-5 Tons), daikincomfort.com","flags":[{"title":"Confirm heater kit vs. minimum CFM","body":"The blower speed tap selected must meet or exceed the minimum CFM required for the installed heater kit (see the Heat Kit Data / Minimum CFM Required table) -- an undersized tap on a heat-kit-equipped unit can trip the high-limit or damage the heater."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower / Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Direct-drive, multi-speed ECM, field speed-tap selectable","key":"blower"},{"label":"Cabinet","value":"SmartFrame cabinet, 21\" depth for attic access, DecaBDE-free thermoplastic drain pan w/ secondary drain connections","key":"cabinet"},{"label":"Airflow example (ASPT25B14 @ 0.3\" ESP)","value":"1,295 CFM (tap 1); full per-model, per-tap, per-static table published in SS-DASPT for all 13 cabinet sizes","key":"airflow"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"Table-driven per model/tap (0.1-1.0 in. w.c. range published in spec sheet); confirm exact max for installed model on rating plate","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Heat / Metering / Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Internal, factory-installed TXV for cooling and heat pump applications","key":"metering"},{"label":"Electric heat","value":"3 kW - 25 kW HKS heater kits, staged: 03=3.0kW, 05=4.5kW, 06=6.0kW, 08=8.0kW, 10=9.6kW, 15=14.4kW, 19=19.2kW (150F limit), 20=19.2kW (170F limit), 25=25.0kW","key":"heat_kit"},{"label":"Coil drain connect","value":"3/4\" FPT on most cabinet sizes","key":"drain"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Tool-less filter access; exact filter size not published in the spec-sheet pages captured -- confirm on rating plate/cabinet label","key":"filter"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"MBVC Series","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position, variable-speed ECM-based modular blower -- a blower-only chassis matched to a separately-ordered cased coil -- ComfortNet-communicating capable, with advanced airflow/tonnage auto-configuration in communicating mode.","match":["MBVC*"],"source":"Daikin Spec Sheet SS-DMBVC (MBVC Series, Multi-Position Variable-Speed ECM-Based Modular Blower -- Communicating), daikincomfort.com","flags":[{"title":"Blower-only chassis -- metering lives in the coil","body":"MBVC is a modular blower section only; there is no factory metering device on the blower itself. TXV or piston selection is set by the matched cased coil ordered separately -- verify the coil's metering device matches the outdoor unit, not the MBVC nameplate."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower / Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Variable-speed ECM, direct drive","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow delivered (nomenclature)","value":"08 = 800 CFM, 12 = 1200 CFM, 16 = 1600 CFM, 20 = 2000 CFM","key":"airflow"},{"label":"Airflow behavior","value":"Constant CFM held across a wide static-pressure range independent of duct system; adjustable low CFM for fan-only operation; CFM indicator and fault recall (last 6 faults) on control","key":"airflow_behavior"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"Not present in the spec-sheet pages captured -- see rating plate / full airflow table","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Heat / Cabinet / Drain","rows":[{"label":"Electric heat","value":"3 kW - 21 kW heater kits (HKR/HKA/HKP families): 4.75 kW, 7.00 kW, 9.50 kW, 14.25-15.00 kW, 19.00-19.60 kW steps","key":"heat_kit"},{"label":"Cabinet","value":"21\" deep, foil-faced insulation, galvanized leather-grain finish; blower section itself is usable as the electric heater enclosure","key":"cabinet"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"None on the blower chassis -- set by the matched cased coil (TXV or piston per coil model)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan / filter","value":"Not present in the spec-sheet pages captured -- see rating plate / IOM","key":"drain_filter"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DHG Series","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Packaged rooftop gas/electric unit, 3-12.5 ton (separate 3-6 ton and 7.5-12.5 ton platforms). NOTE: this is a self-contained packaged unit, not a matched indoor air handler section -- covered here for its integrated supply-air/blower section per request. 3-6 ton platform: direct-drive multi-speed blower (10 speed taps), two-stage gas heat, factory TXV.","match":["DHG*"],"source":"Daikin Installation Instructions IM-IOD-1075 (DHG Series 3-6 Ton Packaged Gas/Electric Unit, Direct Drive), daikincomfort.com","flags":[{"title":"Never operate without the condensate trap","body":"Manual states explicitly: install the condensate drain trap (3/4\" drain line and fittings minimum, 4\" minimum trap depth recommended) before operating -- 'do not operate without trap.' Running the unit untrapped lets flue draft pull air backward through the drain pan."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower / Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Direct-drive, multi-speed motor -- 10 speed taps on standard/high-static gas 3-6 ton models; CFM set via low-voltage leads on terminal block TB1","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Speed-tap selection at TB1 per the Appendix A blower-performance tables; standard-static and high-static gas versions have different allowable tap ranges","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"Model/tap-dependent -- see Appendix A blower performance tables in IM-IOD-1075","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Filter section behind access panels -- note airflow-direction arrows on filter frames when replacing; exact size not published in pages captured, see rating plate","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Heat / Metering / Drain","rows":[{"label":"Gas heat staging","value":"Two-stage heating (low/high stage regulator); example unit natural-gas manifold pressure: low stage 1.7 in. w.c. minimum, high stage 2.7-3.3 in. w.c. -- verify exact figures against the specific model's rating plate","key":"gas_stage"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV -- field superheat adjustment: clockwise (in) increases superheat, counterclockwise (out) decreases superheat","key":"metering"},{"label":"Condensate drain","value":"3/4\" drain line and fittings minimum; install trap per detail drawing (4\" minimum trap recommended); do not operate without trap","key":"drain"},{"label":"Combustion air","value":"Power venter supplies combustion air -- keep air passageways and unit clearances free of obstruction","key":"combustion_air"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"S9X2 / S9X1","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96% AFUE condensing furnace platform, upflow/horizontal/dedicated downflow, direct/non-direct vent, high-efficiency motor. S9X2 is two-stage, S9X1 is single-stage; both share the same IFC, gas valve and orifice spec. American Standard twins AUH2 (two-stage) / AUD2 (single-stage).","match":["S9X2","S9X1","AUH2","AUD2"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide 18-CE12D1-1D-EN (Sep 2020) - https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation/18-CE12D1-1D-EN_09162020.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Adjust 2nd stage before 1st stage","body":"Per the Installer's Guide gas valve adjustment procedure: always set the 2nd stage (HI) manifold pressure first, then the 1st stage (LO). Setting ISD (Interstage Delay) to 000 via the IFC menu/option buttons will force 2nd stage immediately after the 1st-stage blower-on delay, shortening setup time."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure - NG (2nd Stg HI / 1st Stg LO)","value":"3.5\" / 1.7\" W.C.","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure - LP (2nd Stg HI / 1st Stg LO)","value":"10.0\" / 6.0\" W.C.","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - NG","value":"min 5.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - LP","value":"min 11.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Main burner orifice (all models, all inputs)","value":"NG drill #45, LP drill #56","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J (two-stage, toggle on/off)","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"High altitude derate","value":"Reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft; re-check clocked input after orifice/pressure change","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see Service Facts (model-specific CFM vs. ESP tables in IOM)","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-specific)","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sensing current","value":"0.75 - 3.0 microamps DC (1 VDC = 1 microamp on IFC flame-sense test pads \"FP\")","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"Hot surface ignitor; warm-up ~17 sec (resistance not published in this IOM - see rating plate/Service Facts)","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Ignitor cold resistance","value":"37–70 Ω at ~75°F (silicon nitride HSI) — cross-verified from same-generation Trane/Ameristar platform; not itself printed in the S9X2/S9X1 Installer's Guide","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Limit switch","value":"Main thermal limit, fixed, checked by blocking return air - see rating plate for max outlet temp setpoint","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch(es)","value":"Flame roll-out switches (FRS 1 & 2); trip = error code e11 \"Open Limit (Main Thermal, Rollout Switch, or Reverse Airflow Switch)\"","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"S9B1","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96% AFUE single-stage condensing furnace, upflow/horizontal/dedicated downflow, direct/non-direct vent, high-efficiency motor. Shares the same IFC, gas train and orifice spec as S9X1/S9X2 (documented together in the same Installer's Guide).","match":["S9B1"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide 18-CE12D1-1D-EN (Sep 2020) - https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation/18-CE12D1-1D-EN_09162020.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Do not touch ignitor","body":"Hot surface ignitor warning printed in the IOM: \"Do NOT touch igniter. It is extremely hot.\" Allow full cool-down before servicing the burner box."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure - NG","value":"3.5\" W.C.","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure - LP","value":"10.0\" W.C.","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - NG","value":"min 5.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - LP","value":"min 11.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Main burner orifice (all inputs)","value":"NG drill #45, LP drill #56","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J single-stage / redundant combination valve (per platform wiring diagrams)","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"High altitude derate","value":"Reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see Service Facts (model-specific CFM vs. ESP tables in IOM)","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-specific)","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sensing current","value":"0.75 - 3.0 microamps DC (1 VDC = 1 microamp on IFC flame-sense test pads \"FP\")","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"Hot surface ignitor; warm-up ~17 sec (resistance not published in this IOM - see rating plate/Service Facts)","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Ignitor cold resistance","value":"37–70 Ω at ~75°F (silicon nitride HSI) — cross-verified from same-generation Trane/Ameristar platform; not itself printed in the shared S9X1/S9X2/S9B1 Installer's Guide","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Limit switch","value":"Main thermal limit, fixed - see rating plate for max outlet temp setpoint","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch(es)","value":"Flame roll-out switches (FRS 1 & 2); trip = error code e11 \"Open Limit (Main Thermal, Rollout Switch, or Reverse Airflow Switch)\"","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"S8V2 / S8X2","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE two-stage induced-draft furnace platform. S8X2 uses a high-efficiency fixed-speed motor; S8V2(-C) uses a variable-speed/communicating motor. Both share the same gas train, orifice spec and manifold pressure settings. American Standard twins ADH2 / AUH2.","match":["S8V2","S8X2","ADH2","AUH2"],"source":"Trane IOM S8XB-SVX001-1D-EN (Aug 2024, covers S8B1/S8X1/S8X2) - https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation%20Operation%20and%20Maintenance/S8XB-SVX001-1D-EN_08092024.pdf | Trane IOM FNR-SVX003A-EN (Oct 2025, S8V2-C) - https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation%20Operation%20and%20Maintenance/FNR-SVX003A-EN_10312025.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Adjust 2nd stage before 1st stage","body":"Gas valve adjustment procedure requires setting the 2nd stage (HI) manifold pressure first, then 1st stage (LO); confirm 2nd stage is active by verifying 24VAC between C and HI on the gas valve before adjusting."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure - NG (2nd Stg HI / 1st Stg LO)","value":"3.5\" / 1.6\" W.C. (D120 models: 3.5\" / 1.8\" W.C.)","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure - LP (2nd Stg HI / 1st Stg LO)","value":"10.0\" / 6.0\" W.C. (D120 models: 10.0\" / 7.5\" W.C.)","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - NG","value":"min 5.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - LP","value":"min 11.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Main burner orifice (all models)","value":"NG drill #45, LP drill #56","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J two-stage","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"High altitude derate","value":"Reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see Service Facts (model-specific CFM vs. ESP tables in IOM)","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-specific)","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sensing current","value":"0.75 - 3.0 microamps DC (1 VDC = 1 microamp)","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Ignitor type / resistance","value":"120V SiNi (silicon nitride) hot surface ignitor; 37-70 ohms cold resistance at ~75F","key":"ignitor"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Limit switch","value":"Main thermal limit - error code E04 \"Open Thermal Limit, Rollout Switch, or Reverse Airflow Switch\"","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch(es)","value":"Flame rollout switch(es) (FRS), wired in series with main thermal limit - same E04 fault code","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XR95 / XV95 / XC95m","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Older-generation 95% AFUE \"Fan Assisted Combustion System\" condensing furnace (pre-2012 platform, Trane model prefixes CUB1/CDB1). Still common in the field on 15+ year old installs; White-Rodgers gas valve, hot surface ignition, Category I fan-assisted venting.","match":["XR95","XV95","XC95m","CUB1","CDB1"],"source":"Trane/American Standard Installation, Operation, and Maintenance Guide 41-5010-25 (2011) - https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/trane-history/Literature/Installation/41-5010-25_03012011","flags":[{"title":"Not for use as a construction heater","body":"IOM warns: low return-air temperatures during finishing phases of construction can cause condensate formation even though this is a non-condensing model, and chlorides/fluorides from paints, adhesives, and cleaning compounds create a corrosive condition that can rapidly deteriorate the heat exchanger."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure - NG","value":"3.5\" W.C. (adjustable min 3.0\" - max 3.7\" W.C.)","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure - LP","value":"10.5\" W.C.","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - NG","value":"min 5.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - LP","value":"min 11.0\" - max 13.8\" W.C.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Main burner orifice (all inputs, 2-7 burners)","value":"NG drill #45, LP drill #56","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers gas valve model 36G or 36J","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"High altitude derate","value":"Ratings based on sea level, no change needed to 2,000 ft; above 2,000 ft see orifice correction Table 21; High Altitude Kit (BAYHALT***) required above 4,000 ft (pressure switch change)","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see Service Facts (model-specific CFM vs. ESP tables in IOM)","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-specific CFM vs. temp rise tables in IOM)","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sensing current","value":"not published in this IOM - see rating plate/Service Facts","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"Hot surface ignition; warm-up ~17 sec (resistance not published in this IOM)","key":"ignitor"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Limit switch","value":"Closes gas valve on overheat; checked by blocking return air until burners shut off at rating-plate max outlet temp - not separately adjustable","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch(es)","value":"Not called out as a discrete switch in this IOM - see rating plate/Service Facts for this specific model/vintage","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"TUD / AUD (legacy upflow, shared platform with TDD/TUH)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Legacy 80% AFUE non-condensing, fan-assisted-combustion, induced-draft furnace. Source document covers the upflow *UD chassis (Trane TUD / American Standard AUD, first letter A or T per nameplate); downflow (TDD) and horizontal (TUH) share the same generation gas train per Trane parts commonality but should be confirmed against the unit's own Service Facts/rating plate.","match":["TUD","AUD","TDD","TUH"],"source":"Trane/American Standard Installer's Guide 18-CD19D1-2 (Aug 1992, reposted 2011) - https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/trane-history/Literature/Installation/18-CD19D1-2_08012011","flags":[{"title":"Flame roll-out fusible link is not resettable","body":"All models are equipped with a fusible link on the burner cover. In case of flame roll-out, the link opens (melts) and cuts the circuit, shutting off all gas flow. Unlike a manual-reset rollout switch, this link must be replaced, not reset, before the furnace can run again."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure - NG (final setting)","value":"3.0\" - 3.5\" W.C.","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure - LP (final setting)","value":"10.0\" - 10.5\" W.C.","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - NG","value":"min 5.0\" - max 10.5\" W.C.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure - LP","value":"min 11.0\" - max 13.0\" W.C.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Main burner orifice (all inputs, 2-7 burners)","value":"NAT GAS drill #44, LP drill #55","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Automatic gas valve with manual shutoff (brand/model not specified in this IOM - see rating plate)","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"High altitude derate","value":"Reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft; use Table 21 orifice correction; High Altitude Kit required above 4,000 ft (pressure switch change)","key":"altitude"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see Service Facts (model-specific)","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate (model-specific)","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sensing current","value":"not published in this IOM - see rating plate/Service Facts","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"Hot surface ignition; warm-up ~17 sec (resistance not published in this IOM)","key":"ignitor"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Limit switch","value":"Closes gas valve on overheat, checked by blocking return air until burners shut off at rating-plate max outlet temp","key":"limit"},{"label":"Rollout switch(es)","value":"Fusible link on burner cover (see flag above) - not a resettable switch on this platform","key":"rollout"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XR17 / 4TWR7 & 4TTR7 (Two-Stage Heat Pump & AC Condenser)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Conventional 24V two-stage CLIMATUFF scroll platform (70-100% capacity modulation), non-communicating. TXV-Non-Bleed metering, Comfort \"R\" mode for better dehumidification, internal compressor high/low pressure protection with no published cutout/cutin PSIG. Low ambient cooling rated to 55°F as shipped.","match":["XR17","4TWR7","4TTR7","American Standard 4A7H7 (HP)","4A7A7 (AC)"],"source":"Trane Product Data 22-1886-6C-EN, 'Split System Heat Pump XR17 4TWR7, 2-5 Tons' (June 2019); Trane Product Data 22-1942-1B-EN, 'Split System Cooling XR17 4TTR7048B' (May 2019)","flags":[{"title":"Defrost logic and reversing-valve energized state not published","body":"Unlike the XR14/XR16 literature, the XR17 4TWR7 Product Data sheet (22-1886-6C-EN) does not use the words 'defrost' or 'demand defrost' anywhere, and neither document states whether the reversing (switchover) valve is energized in heating or cooling. Confirm defrost behavior and SOV energized-state from the wiring diagram inside the control box or the unit's Service Facts before servicing."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV - Non-Bleed (per Model Nomenclature, Refrigerant Control code 3)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"CLIMATUFF 2-stage scroll, 1-2 stages, 70-100% capacity modulation","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost / Reversing Valve (Heat Pump)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type/interval","value":"Not stated in Product Data 22-1886-6C-EN — see rating plate / Service Facts / Installer's Guide","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Not stated — see rating plate / wiring diagram in control box","key":"reversingValve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"\"Internal compressor high/low pressure & temperature protection\" — no cutout/cutin PSIG published; see rating plate","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling lockout","value":"55°F as shipped; below 55°F requires Application Guide APP-APG013-EN (see also BAYLOAM103 Low Ambient Kit)","key":"lowAmbientLockout"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Accessory — BAYCCHT301 (smaller tons) / BAYCCHT302 (larger tons) kit; not standard as shipped","key":"crankcaseHeater"}]},{"title":"ComfortLink / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Conventional 24V staging — not ComfortLink II communicating","key":"controlPlatform"},{"label":"Charge verification","value":"Subcooling method against nameplate design subcooling + R-410A charging chart (standard Trane split-system method); exact target not printed in Product Data excerpt — see rating plate","key":"chargeMethod"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Trane/American Standard defrost boards use a TEST_COMMON pin plus separate FRC_DFT and TST pins. Short TEST_COMMON to FRC_DFT for 2 seconds and release to command a forced defrost (remove the short once defrost initiates). Shorting TEST_COMMON to TST instead speeds up all board timings rather than forcing an immediate defrost. Trane boards terminate defrost by their own coil/ambient sensor logic (not a fixed 30/60/90-min accumulator like some other brands), typically within a few minutes once coil temp recovers. Exact pin count/labeling should be confirmed against the board silkscreen for the model in hand. Source: field/trade synthesis of Trane installer manuals (corroborated pin function, not independently re-verified against a specific current PDF this session) — cross-check against the unit's own Installer's Manual defrost-control section before relying on it."},{"label":"ComfortLink II communicating","value":"Verified directly from a Trane variable-speed heat pump Installer's Manual: on the CDA/communicating thermostat (XL824/XL850/XL1050 or ComfortLink II control), navigate CONFIG > CONTROL MENU > FRC DFT > ENTER. System must already be running with an active heat demand from the thermostat — 'FRC DFT TEST' can only be initiated in heat mode. The test has a maximum override/runtime of 15 minutes if it doesn't self-terminate sooner. Source: Trane 4TWV0024A1000A Installer's Manual (assets.unilogcorp.com service manual family), 'Defrost Control (Heat Pump Only)' section, p.26."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Per the same Trane manual, demand defrost is only enabled when the coil temperature sensor (CBS) reports coil temperature at or below 35°F — above that, a forced-defrost command may not actually engage the cycle. When defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, and a burst of cold air from the supply registers is normal and expected, not a malfunction."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XR16 / 4TTR6 (Two-Stage AC Condenser)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Cooling-only companion to the XR16 heat pump platform. CLIMATUFF 2-stage scroll, TXV-Non-Bleed metering, internal compressor high/low pressure protection, low ambient cooling to 55°F as shipped with staged accessory kits for lower ambients.","match":["XR16","4TTR6","American Standard 4A6A6"],"source":"Trane Product Data 22-1916-1J-EN, 'Split System Cooling 4TTR6'","flags":[{"title":"No published HP/LP cutout PSIG — internal to compressor","body":"Like every other XR-series cooling sheet reviewed, 22-1916-1J-EN states only that high/low pressure controls are 'inherent to the compressor' — there is no field-serviceable pressure switch with a printed cutout/cutin PSIG. Do not assume a number; check the rating plate or Service Facts if a specific setpoint is needed for diagnostics."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV - Non-Bleed (per Model Nomenclature, Refrigerant Control code 3)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"CLIMATUFF 2-stage scroll, 1-2 stages","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Pressure Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"Internal to compressor — no cutout/cutin PSIG published; see rating plate","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling lockout","value":"55°F as shipped; see Application Guide APP-APG013-EN for operation below 55°F","key":"lowAmbientLockout"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Accessory kit (BAYCCHT302 / BAYCCHT301 depending on tonnage) — not standard as shipped","key":"crankcaseHeater"}]},{"title":"ComfortLink / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Conventional 24V staging — not ComfortLink II communicating","key":"controlPlatform"},{"label":"Charge verification","value":"Subcooling method against nameplate design subcooling + R-410A charging chart","key":"chargeMethod"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XR15 / 4TWR5 (Single-Stage Heat Pump)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Single-stage CLIMATUFF scroll heat pump, non-communicating. Metering device is model-dependent (TXV/EEV on some tonnages, fixed orifice on others) — the Product Data explicitly instructs verifying charge method (subcooling vs. superheat) per unit nameplate. Built-in demand defrost control is standard (accessory 'Evaporator Defrost Control' column reads N/A because it's not needed).","match":["XR15","4TWR5","American Standard 4A7H5","XB14 (builder-tier furnace/air-handler pairing name — NOT a separate outdoor condensing model; XB14 systems use the same 4TWR5/4TTR5 outdoor units)"],"source":"Trane Product Data 22-1832-14J-EN, 'Split System Heat Pump 4TWR5-H' (August 2020)","flags":[{"title":"Metering device is not fixed across the model line — always check the nameplate","body":"22-1832-14J-EN tells the tech to 'verify proper system charge via subcooling (TXV/EEV) or superheat (fixed orifice) per the unit nameplate' — meaning some 4TWR5 tonnages ship with fixed-orifice metering and require the superheat charging method instead of subcooling. Do not default to a TXV/subcooling assumption on this model line."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Model-dependent: TXV/EEV or fixed orifice — confirm on nameplate before choosing subcooling vs. superheat charge method","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"CLIMATUFF single-stage scroll","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost / Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type/interval","value":"Built-in demand defrost control standard (accessory 'Evaporator Defrost Control' listed N/A — not required); exact delta-T/interval logic not printed in this Product Data — see Service Facts","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Not stated — see rating plate / wiring diagram","key":"reversingValve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"Not detailed in this excerpt — see rating plate / Service Facts","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling lockout","value":"Not stated in this compact Product Data format — see rating plate / Application Guide APP-APG013-EN","key":"lowAmbientLockout"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Accessory kit BAYCCHT302 — not standard as shipped","key":"crankcaseHeater"}]},{"title":"ComfortLink / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Conventional 24V staging — not ComfortLink II communicating","key":"controlPlatform"},{"label":"Charge verification","value":"Subcooling (TXV/EEV models) or superheat (fixed-orifice models) per nameplate — do not assume one method for the whole line","key":"chargeMethod"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Trane/American Standard defrost boards use a TEST_COMMON pin plus separate FRC_DFT and TST pins. Short TEST_COMMON to FRC_DFT for 2 seconds and release to command a forced defrost (remove the short once defrost initiates). Shorting TEST_COMMON to TST instead speeds up all board timings rather than forcing an immediate defrost. Trane boards terminate defrost by their own coil/ambient sensor logic (not a fixed 30/60/90-min accumulator like some other brands), typically within a few minutes once coil temp recovers. Exact pin count/labeling should be confirmed against the board silkscreen for the model in hand. Source: field/trade synthesis of Trane installer manuals (corroborated pin function, not independently re-verified against a specific current PDF this session) — cross-check against the unit's own Installer's Manual defrost-control section before relying on it."},{"label":"ComfortLink II communicating","value":"Verified directly from a Trane variable-speed heat pump Installer's Manual: on the CDA/communicating thermostat (XL824/XL850/XL1050 or ComfortLink II control), navigate CONFIG > CONTROL MENU > FRC DFT > ENTER. System must already be running with an active heat demand from the thermostat — 'FRC DFT TEST' can only be initiated in heat mode. The test has a maximum override/runtime of 15 minutes if it doesn't self-terminate sooner. Source: Trane 4TWV0024A1000A Installer's Manual (assets.unilogcorp.com service manual family), 'Defrost Control (Heat Pump Only)' section, p.26."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Per the same Trane manual, demand defrost is only enabled when the coil temperature sensor (CBS) reports coil temperature at or below 35°F — above that, a forced-defrost command may not actually engage the cycle. When defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, and a burst of cold air from the supply registers is normal and expected, not a malfunction."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XR13 / XR14 — 4TWR3 / 4TWR4 & 4TTR3 / 4TTR4 (Older Single-Stage HP & AC)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Older single-stage CLIMATUFF scroll tier, R-410A, non-communicating. XR14 heat pump (4TWR4) carries 'Demand Defrost with Diagnostics' as a stated feature and model/tonnage-dependent factory Compressor Sump Heat. XR14/XR13 AC condensers (4TTR4/4TTR3) use an SPST 'Evaporator Defrost Control' accessory purely for low-ambient cooling protection (not heat-pump defrost).","match":["XR14","XR13","4TWR4","4TWR3","4TTR4","4TTR3","American Standard 4A6H4/4A6H3 (HP)","4A6A4/4A6A3 (AC)"],"source":"Trane Product Data 22-1765-10, 'Split System Heat Pump XR14 4TWR4, 1½-5 Tons' (©2015 Trane); Trane Product Data 22-1904-1M-EN, 'Split System Cooling 4TTR4-L Models' (April 2020); Trane Product Data 22-1842-8R-EN, 'Split System Cooling XR13 4TTR3'","flags":[{"title":"Compressor Sump Heat (crankcase heater) is model/tonnage-dependent — never assume it's standard","body":"The XR14 heat pump electrical table shows 'Compressor Sump Heat' as YES on some tonnage columns and NO on others (not a blanket standard feature) — confirm per the specific model number's electrical data row or the nameplate before assuming crankcase heat is present. XR13 heat pump (4TWR3) specifics were not independently pulled this session — treat as same-generation platform to XR14 but verify defrost/reversing-valve/PSIG details from its own nameplate or Service Facts."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV - Non-Bleed (per Model Nomenclature, Refrigerant Control code 3)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"CLIMATUFF single-stage scroll","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost / Reversing Valve (Heat Pump — XR14 4TWR4 confirmed)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand Defrost with Diagnostics (stated feature, 4TWR4); exact delta-T logic/interval not printed in Product Data — see Service Facts","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Not stated — see rating plate / wiring diagram","key":"reversingValve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"High pressure switch present; \"internal compressor high/low pressure & temperature protection\" — no cutout/cutin PSIG published; see rating plate","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling (HP, as shipped)","value":"55°F as shipped; 20°F with AY28X084 accessory (evaporator defrost control) added","key":"lowAmbientCoolingHP"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling (AC, 4TTR4/4TTR3)","value":"55°F as shipped → 40°F with evaporator defrost control accessory → 30°F with evaporator defrost control + TXV → 20°F with BAYLOAM107A low ambient kit","key":"lowAmbientCoolingAC"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Model/tonnage-dependent — YES on some 4TWR4 electrical-table columns, NO on others; accessory kit (BAYCCHT301/302) on units where not factory-installed","key":"crankcaseHeater"}]},{"title":"ComfortLink / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Conventional 24V staging — not ComfortLink II communicating","key":"controlPlatform"},{"label":"Charge verification","value":"Subcooling method against nameplate design subcooling + R-410A charging chart","key":"chargeMethod"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Trane/American Standard defrost boards use a TEST_COMMON pin plus separate FRC_DFT and TST pins. Short TEST_COMMON to FRC_DFT for 2 seconds and release to command a forced defrost (remove the short once defrost initiates). Shorting TEST_COMMON to TST instead speeds up all board timings rather than forcing an immediate defrost. Trane boards terminate defrost by their own coil/ambient sensor logic (not a fixed 30/60/90-min accumulator like some other brands), typically within a few minutes once coil temp recovers. Exact pin count/labeling should be confirmed against the board silkscreen for the model in hand. Source: field/trade synthesis of Trane installer manuals (corroborated pin function, not independently re-verified against a specific current PDF this session) — cross-check against the unit's own Installer's Manual defrost-control section before relying on it."},{"label":"ComfortLink II communicating","value":"Verified directly from a Trane variable-speed heat pump Installer's Manual: on the CDA/communicating thermostat (XL824/XL850/XL1050 or ComfortLink II control), navigate CONFIG > CONTROL MENU > FRC DFT > ENTER. System must already be running with an active heat demand from the thermostat — 'FRC DFT TEST' can only be initiated in heat mode. The test has a maximum override/runtime of 15 minutes if it doesn't self-terminate sooner. Source: Trane 4TWV0024A1000A Installer's Manual (assets.unilogcorp.com service manual family), 'Defrost Control (Heat Pump Only)' section, p.26."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Per the same Trane manual, demand defrost is only enabled when the coil temperature sensor (CBS) reports coil temperature at or below 35°F — above that, a forced-defrost command may not actually engage the cycle. When defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, and a burst of cold air from the supply registers is normal and expected, not a malfunction."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XL18i / XL16i — 4TWX8 & 4TTX8 (Two-Stage HP & AC, older premium tier)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Two-stage CLIMATUFF scroll platform (predecessor to XR17), non-communicating 24V, WEATHERGUARD II top shields. AC condenser (4TTX8) uses TXV-Non-Bleed metering with internal compressor pressure protection. Heat pump (4TWX8, confirmed on the 060/5-ton via Service Facts) uses a demand-defrost board with outdoor-ambient + coil sensors and delta-T logic — the same board family later reused on XR16 (47°F termination as shipped, 70°F if Jumper J2 is cut below 30°F ambient).","match":["XL18i","XL16i","4TWX8","4TTX8","American Standard 4A7X8 (HP)","4A7X8 (AC, cooling variant)"],"source":"Trane Product Data 22-1885-2E-EN, 'Product Data 4TTX8024A/036A/048B/060A' (October 2020); Trane Service Facts 4TWX8060A-SF-1E-EN, 'Split System Heat Pump 4TWX8060A1000C'","flags":[{"title":"Heat pump defrost/board details confirmed only on the 5-ton (060) model","body":"The Demand Defrost details (delta-T logic, 47°F/70°F termination, Jumper J2) come from the Service Facts for the specific 4TWX8060A1000C (5-ton) unit. Other 4TWX8 tonnages are assumed to share the same board family but were not independently confirmed this session — verify against the Service Facts shipped with the specific unit. XL16i-specific literature was not pulled; treat as a related earlier-generation two-stage sibling and confirm specifics from its own nameplate/Service Facts."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"AC (4TTX8): TXV - Non-Bleed. HP (4TWX8, per Service Facts): outdoor EEV control board present (fault codes reference EEV/superheat/pressure-transducer faults) — confirm exact metering configuration on nameplate","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"CLIMATUFF 2-stage scroll, 1-2 stages","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost / Reversing Valve (Heat Pump)","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand defrost: outdoor ambient sensor + outdoor coil sensor, delta-T logic determines need for defrost; coil sensor also terminates the cycle","key":"defrostType"},{"label":"Defrost termination — as shipped","value":">22°F ambient: 47°F | 10-22°F: ODT + 25°F (per table)","key":"defrostTermAsShipped"},{"label":"Defrost termination — Jumper J2 cut","value":"70°F termination when ambient is at or below 30°F","key":"defrostTermJumperCut"},{"label":"Forced defrost test","value":"Short TEST_COMMON to FRC_DFT pin for 2 seconds to initiate a forced defrost","key":"forcedDefrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"Not stated in the Service Facts excerpt reviewed — see wiring diagram in control box","key":"reversingValve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Protection & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"No cutout/cutin PSIG published; unit uses a suction-line pressure transducer (EEV control board) for diagnostics, not a simple switch with a fixed setpoint — see Service Facts pressure curves for expected PSIG by operating condition","key":"pressureSwitch"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling lockout","value":"55°F as shipped (AC, per 22-1885-2E-EN); see Application Guide APP-APG013-EN for lower","key":"lowAmbientLockout"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"AC: accessory kit (BAYECMT023 / BAYCAKT001 depending on tonnage) — not standard. HP (060 model): 'Compressor Heat' row present in Service Facts electrical table but value not legible in the copy reviewed — see rating plate","key":"crankcaseHeater"}]},{"title":"ComfortLink / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating status","value":"Conventional 24V staging — not ComfortLink II communicating","key":"controlPlatform"},{"label":"Charge — cooling, 55-120°F OD ambient","value":"Subcooling method (high stage only), target 10-15°F subcooling; use R-410A Refrigerant Charging Chart (liquid line temp vs. PSIG) in Service Facts","key":"chargeCooling"},{"label":"Charge — below 55°F OD ambient","value":"Weigh in nameplate charge plus line-length adders in heating mode; do NOT use the cooling subcooling method below 55°F","key":"chargeBelow55"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Trane/American Standard defrost boards use a TEST_COMMON pin plus separate FRC_DFT and TST pins. Short TEST_COMMON to FRC_DFT for 2 seconds and release to command a forced defrost (remove the short once defrost initiates). Shorting TEST_COMMON to TST instead speeds up all board timings rather than forcing an immediate defrost. Trane boards terminate defrost by their own coil/ambient sensor logic (not a fixed 30/60/90-min accumulator like some other brands), typically within a few minutes once coil temp recovers. Exact pin count/labeling should be confirmed against the board silkscreen for the model in hand. Source: field/trade synthesis of Trane installer manuals (corroborated pin function, not independently re-verified against a specific current PDF this session) — cross-check against the unit's own Installer's Manual defrost-control section before relying on it."},{"label":"ComfortLink II communicating","value":"Verified directly from a Trane variable-speed heat pump Installer's Manual: on the CDA/communicating thermostat (XL824/XL850/XL1050 or ComfortLink II control), navigate CONFIG > CONTROL MENU > FRC DFT > ENTER. System must already be running with an active heat demand from the thermostat — 'FRC DFT TEST' can only be initiated in heat mode. The test has a maximum override/runtime of 15 minutes if it doesn't self-terminate sooner. Source: Trane 4TWV0024A1000A Installer's Manual (assets.unilogcorp.com service manual family), 'Defrost Control (Heat Pump Only)' section, p.26."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Per the same Trane manual, demand defrost is only enabled when the coil temperature sensor (CBS) reports coil temperature at or below 35°F — above that, a forced-defrost command may not actually engage the cycle. When defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, and a burst of cold air from the supply registers is normal and expected, not a malfunction."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"XV20i / 4TTV0 (Variable-Speed ComfortLink II AC Condenser)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Cooling-only companion to the already-covered XV20i/4TWV0 variable-speed heat pump. Same Integrated Variable Speed Control (IVSC) board + Communicating Display Assembly (CDA) platform, EEV metering, ComfortLink II communicating control. Charging is via the 'Charging Mode-Cooling' subcooling test ONLY, with the indoor blower mandatorily set to 400 CFM/ton.","match":["XV20i","4TTV0","TTV0","American Standard 4A7V0","A7V0"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide 18-BC89D1-1H-EN, 'Variable Speed ComfortLink II Heat Pumps and Air Conditioners' (models incl. 4TTV0024/036B/048/060/061A1000B), June 2018 — same document already used for the companion XV20i/4TWV0 heat pump entry","flags":[{"title":"High/low pressure cutout PSIG and other HP-only rows do not apply / are not published for this AC","body":"This Installer's Guide states only 'internal compressor high/low pressure & temperature protection' for the platform — no numeric cutout/cutin PSIG values are given for the 4TTV0 AC any more than for its 4TWV0 heat pump sibling. See rating plate or the unit's Service Facts (shipped inside the outdoor unit control box) for actual setpoints. Defrost rows are not applicable — this is a cooling-only condenser."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (PVE oil — variable-speed compressor)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) — EEV Test available in CDA Control Menu","key":"metering"},{"label":"Oil hygroscopic warning","value":"If system open to atmosphere >4 hrs, compressor oil must be replaced","key":"oilNote"}]},{"title":"Operating Range & Pressure Protection","rows":[{"label":"Cooling operating range","value":"55°F to 120°F outdoor ambient","key":"coolingRange"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling lockout","value":"55°F (per Table 1 Operating Range)","key":"lowAmbientLockout"},{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"Internal compressor high/low pressure & temperature protection — no cutout/cutin PSIG published; see rating plate / Service Facts","key":"pressureSwitch"}]},{"title":"Crankcase Heater / Startup","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater wait","value":"Wait 3 HOURS before starting unit if outdoor ambient is below 85°F","key":"crankcaseWait"},{"label":"400VDC hazard","value":"Wait 2 minutes after disconnecting power; verify <42VDC at +VDC/-VDC test points before servicing IVSC board","key":"highVoltageHazard"}]},{"title":"ComfortLink II / Communicating Status","rows":[{"label":"Control platform","value":"Integrated Variable Speed Control (IVSC) board + Communicating Display Assembly (CDA), pairs with 850/950/1050 comfort controls","key":"controlPlatform"},{"label":"Status LED (green)","value":"Slow=Standby/Idle, Medium=Call for Capacity, Fast=Power-up delay, Solid=Test Mode, 1 flash/4 sec=Hard Lockout","key":"statusLed"},{"label":"COMM LED (amber)","value":"Slow=device count, Fast (5x/sec)=loss of communication","key":"commLed"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Approved subcooling method","value":"'Charging Mode-Cooling' test in comfort control Technician Menu ONLY — outdoor 55-120°F, indoor 70-80°F, indoor blower at 400 CFM/ton (mandatory)","key":"chargingMethod"},{"label":"Design subcooling value","value":"See rating plate or Service Facts (not a fixed figure in this guide) — used with the R-410A charging chart, 8-14°F subcooling columns, 55-125°F liquid temp rows","key":"designSubcooling"},{"label":"Line length/lift limits","value":"150 ft max length / 50 ft max lift on 5/8\"-7/8\" lines; larger 1-1/8\" vapor line models limited to 80 ft length / 10-25 ft lift depending on model","key":"lineLimits"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"TAM7 / 4TEC3","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Convertible variable-speed communicating air handler (2-5 ton) with an Airflow Control (AFC) board driving an ECM blower, electronic expansion valve (EEV) metering, and dip-switch commissioning for tonnage/airflow. Cabinet accepts an optional hot-water (hydronic) coil accessory in place of electric heat.","match":["TAM7","4TEC3","TAM7A0A24H21SD","TAM7A0A24H21EA","TAM7A0B30H21SD","TAM7A0B30H21EA","TAM7A0C36H31SD","TAM7A0C36H31EA","TAM7A0C42H31SD","TAM7A0C42H31EA","TAM7A0C48H41SD","TAM7A0C48H41EA","TAM7B0C60H51SC","TAM7B0C60H51EA"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide, Convertible Air Handlers 2-5 Ton TAM7, pub. 18-GJ06D2-2F-EN (trane.com/content/dam/.../Small Splits/Air Handlers/18-GJ06D2-2F-EN.pdf); hydronic coil accessory per Trane Installer's Guide, Hydronic Coil Accessory (Fits Hyperion/ForeFront air handlers), pub. 18-GJ21D1-2A-EN (elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/trane-history/Literature/Installation/18-GJ21D1-2A-EN_08052020.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Trane: dip switches must be set with power OFF","body":"S1/S2 airflow-control (AFC) dip switches (tonnage/OD-multiplier, AC vs HP, stages, compressors, CFM/ton, blower-off delay, Torque vs Constant-CFM mode) only take effect after power is cycled off and re-applied. Changing switches with power on will not update the AFC."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Variable-speed ECM, direct drive, controlled by the Airflow Control (AFC) board","key":"blowerType"},{"label":"Airflow commissioning","value":"Dip switch S1: OD tonnage multiplier (S1-1/S1-2), AC/HP (S1-3), OD stages (S1-4), # compressors (S1-5). Dip switch S2: cooling & heating CFM/ton (S2-1/S2-2), blower-off delay (S2-3/S2-4), Torque vs Constant-CFM airflow mode (S2-5)","key":"airflowSetup"},{"label":"Torque mode static threshold","value":"Torque mode starts reducing airflow above approx. 0.3\" w.c. (2-ton), 0.35\" w.c. (2.5-3.5 ton), 0.4\" w.c. (4-5 ton) static; cooling only, all heating modes default to Constant CFM","key":"torqueThreshold"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"See airflow performance tables for the specific model / rating plate (varies by tonnage and speed-tap/torque setting)","key":"maxESP"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) on the Electronic Expansion Valve Control (EVC) board, field-selectable R-410A/R-22 via J7 jumper (factory default R-410A)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Match to outdoor unit","value":"EEV is electronically controlled (not a fixed TXV) - confirm compatibility/charge per the matched outdoor unit's System Charge Adjustments (subcooling) table","key":"meteringMatch"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Integral filter channel at bottom of blower/filter compartment (no remote filter required); size set by cabinet letter (A=16x20, B=20x20, C=22x20, 1\" throwaway), per 7th digit of model number","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat / Hydronic Heat","rows":[{"label":"Electric heat kits","value":"Field-installed BAYHTR-series kW heater kits (wiring diagrams ship with the heater); see heater kit literature or rating plate for exact kW/staging by model","key":"heatKit"},{"label":"Hydronic (hot water) coil option","value":"Optional BAYWAxx/BAYWVxx hydronic coil accessory (pub. 18-GJ21D1-2A-EN) slides into the heater compartment in place of electric heat; 7/8\" OD x 3/4\" ID copper field water piping, max entering water temp 180F, two vertical or two horizontal pipe runs (entering-water pipe always farthest from blower); usable upflow, downflow, or horizontal","key":"hydronicCoil"}]},{"title":"Drain / Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan/trap","value":"Factory condensate connections; Trane states a P-trap is NOT required for drainage because the cabinet runs at positive pressure, but a trap is still recommended to prevent conditioned-air loss/efficiency loss. No factory float switch documented - see rating plate/accessory kit for float-switch option","key":"drainPan"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"TEM4 / 4TEM4 (incl. TEM8 platform)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Convertible multi-speed air handler (1.5-5 ton) sharing the same painted-steel cabinet, drain-pan, and heater-kit platform as TEM6/TEM8. Smaller tonnages use a multi-speed PSC/direct-drive blower; larger tonnages (and the higher-tier TEM8 communicating variant) use a constant-torque (basic ECM) motor. Factory bleed TXV metering; remote/external filter required.","match":["TEM4","4TEM4","TEM8","TEM4A0B18S21SA","TEM4A0B30S31SA","TEM4A0C48S41SA","TEM4A0C60S51SA"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide, Convertible Air Handlers 1-1/2-5 Ton TEM4, pub. 18-GF73D1-1C-EN (trane.com/content/dam/.../Small Splits/Air Handlers/18-GF73D1-1C-EN.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Trane: disconnect power before changing blower speed taps","body":"Unit ships with factory-set cooling and heating speed taps (High/Med/Low). Always disconnect all power before moving a motor speed tap, then verify airflow and evaporator coil temperature drop after any change."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Multi-speed, direct-drive blower - PSC on most models, constant-torque motor (basic ECM) on larger tonnages / TEM8 platform; confirm on rating plate","key":"blowerType"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Factory-set High/Med/Low speed taps for cooling and heating (field-selectable at the motor plug); airflow performance tables give CFM at 0.1-0.7\" w.c. external static for 230V and 208V taps","key":"airflowSetup"},{"label":"Max external static (tested)","value":"Airflow tables published through 0.7\" w.c. external static (e.g., TEM4A0B30S31SA: High tap 1066 CFM @ 0.7\" w.c., 230V); downflow airflow must not exceed 1200 CFM due to condensate blow-off","key":"maxESP"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed, internally-checked bleed TXV (R-410A) for AC or heat pump duty; pressures equalize after shutdown. Some outdoor units may require a start-assist kit - verify against the matched condensing unit","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"No integral filter rack - a remote/external filter must be field-installed ahead of the coil; optional Slim Fit Filter Box Kit accessories BAYSF1185AAA / BAYSF1235AAA","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heater kW range","value":"4, 5, 8, 10, 15, 19, 20, 21 kW single-phase (BAYHTR15xx series); 10 & 15 kW three-phase (BAYHTR35xx, lug terminal); single-point power entry kit for 15/19/20/21 kW heaters","key":"heatKit"},{"label":"Downflow heat requirement","value":"Downflow condensate management kit BAYTEMDFKT1A required for 5-ton downflow applications; downflow sub-base kits TAYBASE185/TAYBASE235 available","key":"downflowKit"}]},{"title":"Drain / Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Factory-installed sturdy polycarbonate drain pan, shipped configured for upflow/horizontal-left; primary + auxiliary condensate connections are 3/4\" NPT. Primary drain must be trapped outside the unit and pitched 1/4\"/ft minimum. No factory float switch documented","key":"drainPan"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"GAM5","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Modular multipoise convertible air handler with a Vortica direct-drive blower on a high-efficiency ECM motor (5 speed taps), factory R-410A TXV metering, and a molded 1\" integral filter rail (filter not furnished). Two-piece modular cabinet with integrated horizontal drain pans and a safety door switch.","match":["GAM5","GAM5B0A18M11SB","GAM5B0A24M21SB","GAM5B0B30M21SB","GAM5B0B36M31SB","GAM5B0C42M31SB","GAM5B0C48M41SB","GAM5B0C60M51SB"],"source":"Trane Product Data, Modular Multi-position Air Handlers GAM5B Models, pub. 22-1845-14 (trane.com/content/dam/.../Small Splits/Air Handlers/GAM5.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Trane: airflow speed-tap change required for 2-stage","body":"On 2-stage AC/HP matches, the factory speed tap must be reset per the 2-Stage Airflow Adjustment tables (High tap for stage 2, Low tap for stage 1) - the unit does not auto-adjust airflow between stages."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Vortica centrifugal blower, direct drive, High-Efficiency ECM motor, 5 speed taps, soft-start operation with built-in fan-delay modes","key":"blowerType"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Field-selectable speed taps (low-voltage pigtail connections); 2-stage AC/HP applications require resetting the tap per the published High/Low CFM & ESP tables for the matched outdoor unit (e.g., GAM5B0C48M41 with 4TTR7048A: High tap 1475 CFM @ 0.449\" w.c., Low tap 1390 CFM @ 0.399\" w.c.)","key":"airflowSetup"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory R-410A thermal expansion valve (TXV); R-22 conversion TXV kit sold as accessory","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Not furnished - molded 1\" throwaway filter rail integral to cabinet; recommended size 1x throwaway per model (16x20 up to 22x20 depending on cabinet width) - see General Data table for the specific model","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Electric heat kits","value":"Slide-in electric heaters sold as accessory with polarized plug connections; see the GAM5 air handler/heater allowable-combinations matrix or rating plate for exact kW-to-model pairing","key":"heatKit"}]},{"title":"Drain / Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Integrated horizontal drain pans (both orientations), 3/4\" NPT drain connection; safety door switch cuts power when a cabinet door is opened. No factory condensate float switch documented - see rating plate/accessory options","key":"drainPan"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"TEM3 / TWE","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Standard-efficiency convertible air handler (1.5-5 ton) with a multi-speed direct-drive PSC blower (constant-torque motor optional per rating plate) and factory bleed TXV metering. Same cabinet/heater-kit template as TEM4/TEM6/TEM8; requires a remote/external filter.","match":["TEM3","TWE","ATEM3","TEM3A0B18S21SA","TEM3A0B30S21SA","TEM3A0B30S31SA","TEM3A0C36S31SA","TEM3A0C48S41SA","TEM3A0C60S51SA"],"source":"Trane Installer's Guide, Convertible Air Handlers 1-1/2 to 5 Ton TEM3 Models, pub. 18-GJ65D1-1D-EN (trane.com/content/dam/.../Small Splits/Air Handlers/18-GJ65D1-1D-EN.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Trane: model-number nomenclature caveat","body":"This Trane installer's guide documents the TEM3 (and American Standard ATEM3) family only; a distinct 'TWE-E' PSC single-phase air handler line (1.5-5 ton) is referenced in Trane product handbooks but was not independently confirmed in an elibrary.tranetechnologies.com or trane.com/content/dam document during this research. Confirm the exact TWE model's specs against its own rating plate before servicing."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow Setup","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Multi-speed, direct-drive blower; PSC standard, constant-torque motor version also referenced in sequence-of-operation - confirm on rating plate","key":"blowerType"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Factory-set High/Med/Low speed taps (field-adjustable at the motor plug, power off); airflow tables published 0.1-0.7\" w.c. external static for 230V/208V taps","key":"airflowSetup"},{"label":"Max external static (tested)","value":"Airflow tables published through 0.7\" w.c. (e.g., TEM3A0B30S31SA/TEM3A0B36S31SA: High tap 1066/997 CFM @ 0.7\" w.c., 230V); downflow airflow must not exceed 1200 CFM due to condensate blow-off; TEM3A0B36S31SA recommended tap is Medium at 0.4\" w.c.","key":"maxESP"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed, internally-checked bleed TXV (R-410A) for AC or heat pump duty; pressures equalize after shutdown - some outdoor units may need a start-assist kit","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"No integral filter rack - remote/external filter must be field-installed; optional Slim Fit Filter Box Kit BAYSF1185AAA / BAYSF1235AAA","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heater kW range","value":"4, 5, 8, 10, 15, 19, 20 kW single-phase (BAYHTR15xx series); 10 & 15 kW three-phase lug-terminal heaters (BAYHTR35xx); single-point power entry kit for 15/19/20 kW heaters","key":"heatKit"}]},{"title":"Drain / Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Factory-installed polycarbonate drain pan shipped for upflow/horizontal-left; primary + auxiliary condensate 3/4\" NPT, primary trapped outside the unit, 1/4\"/ft minimum pitch. No factory float switch documented","key":"drainPan"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"TM9V / TM9E / TM9M","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"95-96% AFUE ECM condensing platform: TM9V (2-stage variable-speed ECM), TM9E (single-stage standard ECM), TM9M (modulating). Same cabinet/heat-exchanger family, sold under the same model numbers across York and Fraser-Johnston nameplates (confirmed on york.com for TM8E/this platform); no distinct Coleman/Luxaire prefix could be verified in yorknow.com literature within this pass.","match":["TM9V","TM9V*C","TM9E","TM9E*MP","TM9M","TM9M*MP"],"source":"yorknow.com TM9V_Install.pdf (5402851-UIM-A-0917); yorknow.com tm9etech.pdf; yorknow.com tm9e_installguide.pdf / tm9v_installguide.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Two-stage: set high fire before low fire","body":"TM9V install manual: high-fire manifold pressure MUST be set/verified before adjusting low-fire pressure — low fire is a percentage of the high-fire tap."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board / control","value":"York integrated furnace control (IFC), LED self-diagnostics","key":"board"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA (normal/warning/lockout)","value":"see rating plate — not published in TM9V/TM9E install literature reviewed","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — confirmed (normal/warning/lockout)","value":"Normal ~3.7 µA DC; low-signal warning starts at 1.5 µA; lockout at 0.1 µA DC. Confirmed independently in the TM9V, TM9E, and TM9M install manuals (same wording in each) — supersedes the earlier \"see rating plate\" placeholder row above.","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — NG (TM9V high/low fire)","value":"3.5 in. w.c. high fire / 1.7 in. w.c. low fire (0-7,999 ft, 800-900 Btu/cu ft gas) — Table 5/6","key":"manifold_ng_tm9v"},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP (TM9V high/low fire)","value":"9.8 in. w.c. high fire / 4.1 in. w.c. low fire (sea level)","key":"manifold_lp_tm9v"},{"label":"Manifold pressure — NG (TM9E single-stage, nominal)","value":"3.5 in. w.c. (0-7,999 ft) — Table 4","key":"manifold_ng_tm9e"},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP (TM9E)","value":"9.8 in. w.c. (sea level-7,999 ft)","key":"manifold_lp_tm9e"},{"label":"Modulating (TM9M) range + lock procedure","value":"see rating plate / unit-specific commissioning sheet — modulating range and low-fire lockout procedure not found in literature reviewed","key":"manifold_mod_tm9m"},{"label":"Supply pressure — NG/LP","value":"Max downstream to gas valve 0.5 psig (14 in. w.c.); full min/max supply table not located — see rating plate","key":"supply_pressure"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate — manual states \"do not attempt to drill out any orifices\"","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"see rating plate — model/manufacturer not published in literature reviewed","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate (\"within the allowable range as specified on the furnace rating plate\")","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"30-65°F depending on model/tap (TM9V Table 7: 35-65°F; TM9E Table 5 varies by model)","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type/ohms","value":"Hot surface ignition (type per literature); resistance in ohms not published — see rating plate","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Limit switch (TM9E, per parts list)","value":"250°F manual-reset limit switch","key":"limit_switch"},{"label":"Rollout/limit fault code","value":"5 RED FLASHES = limit circuit open (TM9V diagnostics)","key":"rollout_limit_code"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"see rating plate — not tabulated in literature reviewed for this platform","key":"altitude_derate"},{"label":"Pressure switch fault codes","value":"2 RED FLASHES = switch closed when it should be open (stuck/wiring); 3 RED FLASHES = switch open when it should be closed (inducer/vent/hose); numeric trip setpoint in in. w.c. not published — see rating plate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"TG9S","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"95.5% AFUE single-stage PSC multi-position condensing furnace. Same platform sold as Coleman-network GG9S (confirmed by combined manual title \"TG9S-GG9S\").","match":["TG9S","TG9S*MP","GG9S"],"source":"yorknow.com TG9S_Install.pdf (JCI doc 1083287-UIM-H-0817)","flags":[{"title":"Verify altitude table before setting manifold pressure","body":"Nominal NG manifold pressure varies 2.4-3.5 in. w.c. by altitude/gas heating value — confirm the correct column for the install altitude before final adjustment, not just sea-level spec."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board / control","value":"York integrated furnace control (IFC), LED self-diagnostics","key":"board"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — normal","value":"~3.7 µA DC typical","key":"flame_ua_normal"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — warning","value":"Continuous amber flash below 1.5 µA — clean/inspect flame sensor","key":"flame_ua_warning"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — lockout","value":"see rating plate — exact lockout threshold not confirmed from yorknow.com excerpt reviewed","key":"flame_ua_lockout"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — lockout (confirmed)","value":"0.1 µA DC — confirmed in the TG9S install manual (same IFC diagnostics text as TM9V/TM9E/TM9M/TG8S/TM8E); supersedes the earlier \"not confirmed\" placeholder row above.","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — NG","value":"2.4-3.5 in. w.c. (varies by altitude/gas Btu content, see rating plate for exact column)","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP","value":"9.8 in. w.c. (sea level)","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply pressure — NG/LP","value":"Max downstream to gas valve 0.5 psig (14 in. w.c.); full min/max table — see rating plate","key":"supply_pressure"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Sized for 1030 Btu/ft³ natural gas heating value; specific drill number — see rating plate","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"see rating plate — model/manufacturer not published in literature reviewed","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"30-60°F (smallest models) up to 45-75°F (130 MBH models) — model-specific table","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type/ohms","value":"Hot surface ignition; resistance in ohms not published — see rating plate","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Rollout switch fault code","value":"5 RED FLASHES = rollout/limit circuit fault","key":"rollout_code"},{"label":"Main limit switch fault code","value":"4 RED FLASHES = main limit switch fault","key":"limit_code"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Manifold pressure table adjusts above 5,000 ft (Table 5) — see rating plate for exact percentage","key":"altitude_derate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"TG8S","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage PSC multi-position furnace, non-condensing. Confirmed twin standard/low-NOx variant TGLS.","match":["TG8S","TG8S*MP","TGLS","TGLS*MP"],"source":"yorknow.com TG8S_Install.pdf (JCI doc 998491-UIM-C-0616)","flags":[{"title":"Confirm LP supply pressure floor before firing","body":"Manual publishes a hard LP minimum supply of 8.0 in. w.c. (vs. 4.5 in. w.c. for NG) — a marginal LP regulator that would pass on natural gas can starve this furnace and cause nuisance ignition lockouts."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board / control","value":"York integrated furnace control (IFC), LED self-diagnostics","key":"board"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA thresholds","value":"see rating plate — not published in TG8S install manual reviewed","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA (normal/warning/lockout, confirmed)","value":"Normal ~3.7 µA DC; low-signal warning starts at 1.5 µA; lockout at 0.1 µA DC — same IFC platform figures as TM9V/TG9S/TM8E.","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — NG","value":"3.5 in. w.c.","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP","value":"10.0 in. w.c.","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply pressure — NG (min/max)","value":"4.5 in. w.c. minimum / 10.5 in. w.c. maximum","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure — LP (min/max)","value":"8.0 in. w.c. minimum / 13.0 in. w.c. maximum","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate — drill size not published in excerpt reviewed","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"see rating plate — model/manufacturer not published in literature reviewed","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"25-55°F (smallest models) up to 40-70°F (largest models) — model-specific, Table 6","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type/ohms","value":"Hot surface ignition; resistance in ohms not published — see rating plate","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Rollout/limit switch","value":"see rating plate — temperature ratings not published in excerpt reviewed","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Manifold pressure adjustment referenced above 5,000 ft (Table 5) — see rating plate for exact value","key":"altitude_derate"},{"label":"Pressure switch fault codes","value":"2 RED FLASHES = stuck closed at start; 3 RED FLASHES = won't close (inducer/vent/hose); 6 RED FLASHES = switch cycled open 4x during a call for heat, 1-hr soft lockout; numeric trip setpoint in in. w.c. not published — see rating plate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"TM8E","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage ECM multi-position furnace (standard and Ultra-Low NOx TMLE variant). Same model number sold under the Fraser-Johnston nameplate per york.com product pages.","match":["TM8E","TM8E*MP","TMLE","TMLE*MP"],"source":"yorknow.com technical guide (JCI doc 5597956-YTG-C-1219)","flags":[{"title":"Low-NOx TMLE variant may need altitude kit sooner","body":"Tech guide flags separate altitude kits (S1-1PS3301 / S1-1PS3302) required above 5,000 ft — confirm the correct kit p/n for standard TM8E vs. low-NOx TMLE before ordering."},{"title":"TM8E's published LP manifold pressure (8.0\" w.c.) is lower than other 80% York platforms","body":"Table 11 in the TM8E install manual gives LP manifold pressure as 8.0\" w.c. (1.99 kPa) — most other York/JCI 80% single-stage furnaces (TG8S, TM8Y) publish 9.8-10.0\" w.c. for LP. Value is quoted directly from the TM8E manual's own table; confirm against the specific unit's rating plate before final adjustment rather than assuming a typo."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board / control","value":"York integrated furnace control (IFC), LED self-diagnostics (per shared platform)","key":"board"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA thresholds","value":"see rating plate — not published in TM8E technical guide reviewed","key":"flame_ua"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA (normal/warning/lockout, confirmed)","value":"Normal ~3.7 µA DC; low-signal warning starts at 1.5 µA; lockout at 0.1 µA DC — same IFC platform figures as TM9V/TG9S/TG8S.","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — NG/LP","value":"see rating plate — not published in technical guide reviewed (install manual not located on yorknow.com in this pass)","key":"manifold"},{"label":"Supply pressure — NG/LP","value":"see rating plate","key":"supply_pressure"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"see rating plate","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"Manifold pressure — NG (confirmed)","value":"3.5\" w.c. (Table 11)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP (confirmed)","value":"8.0\" w.c. (Table 11 — see flag re: this being lower than other 80% York platforms)"},{"label":"Supply pressure — NG (min/max)","value":"4.5\" w.c. minimum / 10.5\" w.c. maximum; 7\" w.c. minimum to reach rated input (Table 10)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.8 in. H₂O (from blower performance tables)","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"20-50°F (40 MBH model) up to 40-70°F (largest models) — model-specific table","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"Max outlet air temperature","value":"190°F (all models)","key":"max_outlet_temp"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type/ohms","value":"see rating plate — not published in technical guide reviewed","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Rollout/limit switch","value":"see rating plate — not published in technical guide reviewed","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Altitude kit required above 5,000 ft (S1-1PS3301 std / S1-1PS3302 low-NOx); exact derate % — see rating plate","key":"altitude_derate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"GY9S / GF9S / GM9S (legacy Stellar/Latitude platform, incl. Affinity PS9)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Legacy 90%+ single-stage condensing \"Stellar/Latitude\" tubular heat-exchanger platform (superseded by TG9S). GY9S=York, GF9S=Fraser-Johnston, GM9S=Coleman-network nameplate per upgnet.com archive folder structure; PS9 is the Affinity-branded version of the same generation. LED flash codes for this platform are already covered elsewhere — this entry is MAINT figures only.","match":["GY9S","GF9S","GM9S","PS9"],"source":"upgnet.com Source1 archive — York Affinity PS9 Technical Guide (doc 036-21578-002-b-0205)","flags":[{"title":"Confirm capacity derate before altitude conversion","body":"PS9 tech guide: reduce input capacity 4% for each 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft elevation — recompute BTU input before selecting a high-altitude orifice/pressure-switch kit on a replacement in the mountains."}],"groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Board / control","value":"Legacy York integrated control — codes covered separately; MAINT figures only here","key":"board"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA thresholds","value":"see rating plate — not published in the PS9 technical guide reviewed","key":"flame_ua"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — NG/LP","value":"see rating plate — not published in PS9 technical guide reviewed (dimensional/performance guide only, no combustion table)","key":"manifold"},{"label":"Supply pressure — NG/LP","value":"see rating plate","key":"supply_pressure"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"see rating plate","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.5 in. w.g. (per PS9 technical guide)","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"35-65°F (40 MBH model example) — model-specific table","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type/ohms","value":"see rating plate — not published in PS9 technical guide reviewed","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Rollout/limit switch","value":"see rating plate — not published in PS9 technical guide reviewed","key":"rollout_limit"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Reduce capacity 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft elevation","key":"altitude_derate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YZH018-060 (Affinity 2-Stage Heat Pump)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"18 SEER two-stage scroll-compressor heat pump (Affinity series); factory-matched to TXV-equipped indoor coils with on-demand microprocessor defrost control.","match":["York YZH024/036/048/060 (and 'C' communicating-ready suffix)","Coleman/Luxaire 18 SEER 2-stage Affinity-platform twin — brand-specific model code not confirmed in reviewed literature, verify rating plate"],"source":"York Technical Guide 561927-YTG-A-0410, 'Affinity Split-System Heat Pumps 18 SEER - R-410A', Models YZH024 thru 060(C) — JCI/York service literature distributed via upgnet.com Source1 / yorknow.com documentation library","flags":[{"title":"No Factory Crankcase Heater on This Platform","body":"All YZH024-060 models ship WITHOUT a crankcase heater per the Physical & Electrical Data table — don't assume one is present. Follow standard oil-return/soak precautions on cold-soaked startups and long off-cycles."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering Device","value":"TXV — system-matched (e.g. 1TVM4G1/4H1/4K1 by size); required, not field-selected","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"2-stage scroll (Multi-stage Compressor: Yes)","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost Type/Interval","value":"On-demand microprocessor defrost (adaptive balance-point control); not a fixed timer — exact algorithm not detailed in this guide","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing Valve Energized Mode","value":"Not stated in this guide. Standard York/JCI convention is energized-in-cooling / de-energized-in-heating — confirm against the unit wiring diagram before relying on it","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Protections & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in Technical Guide — see rating plate or IFC/board label","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in Technical Guide — see rating plate or IFC/board label","key":"lps"},{"label":"Low Ambient Lockout","value":"No standard rating stated. Accessory kits extend cooling operation to +20°F (Standard Low Ambient Kit S1-2LA06700424) or -20°F (Advanced Low Ambient Kit S1-2LA04701024)","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase Heater","value":"No (all sizes)","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"System Charge","value":"See nameplate / System Charge for Various Matched Systems table (base factory charge + evaporator adder + lineset adder) — do not invent a charge value","key":"charge"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"York/Coleman/Luxaire (Johnson Controls) Demand Defrost Control boards have a 'TEST' pin pair (P3 on some revisions). With a heating call active, jumper the TEST pins for 6+ seconds — defrost engages and continues for as long as the jumper stays in place. While TEST is jumpered, the control ignores actual coil (liquid-line) temperature and outdoor ambient — the coil does NOT need to be cold for the forced test to run. After removing the jumper, defrost terminates normally on its own logic: liquid-line temp reaches 80°F, or after 8 minutes of defrost run time, whichever comes first. Source: Johnson Controls Unitary Products 'Demand Defrost Control' Operation Instructions, part 031-09178-000 / doc 501062-UAI (cdn.master.ca and us-ac.com hosted copies), plus corroborating HVAC-Talk field posts."},{"label":"ComfortNet/Affinity communicating","value":"NOT independently verified this session. The S1-TTSCC01/S1-TTSCC02 Affinity/ComfortNet touchscreen control has a service/diagnostics area, and York field literature references being able to force a defrost cycle through it, but no source located gave the exact on-screen menu path or button sequence. Do not guess the menu steps — pull the specific control's Installation/Operation guide or use the physical TEST-pin method above (works regardless of comm status) if the outdoor unit's board is accessible."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"On normal (non-forced) operation, coil temp must be below the board's frost/cut-in threshold before a defrost demand will latch; the TEST-pin forced method above deliberately bypasses that check. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may lock in — warn of a normal burst of cold supply air during the test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YHM024-060 (LX Series Modulating Heat Pump)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"14-17.75 SEER inverter-driven modulating heat pump (50-100% capacity, operated from a conventional 2-stage thermostat, non-communicating); hybrid demand/time-temperature defrost control.","match":["York YHM","Coleman CH16","Luxaire TH16"],"source":"Johnson Controls Unitary Products Installation Manual 5156631-UIM-G-0417, 'YHM, CH16, TH16 Series' 16 SEER Heat Pump, 2-5 Tons 1-Phase — yorknow.com/pub/media/documentationMatched/YHM48B21S_InstallGuide.pdf","flags":[{"title":"LPS Is Intentionally Ignored Below 15°F Ambient","body":"The control electronically ignores the Low Pressure Switch input during defrost, for 120 seconds after defrost ends, and whenever outdoor ambient is below 15°F. A low-suction condition without an LPS fault in cold weather is expected behavior on this platform, not a stuck or bypassed switch."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering Device","value":"TXV (bulb-mounted, R-410A TXV per install manual)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Inverter-driven, modulates 50-100% of nominal capacity in 10% steps from a conventional 2-stage thermostat signal","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost Type/Interval","value":"Hybrid Time/Temperature + Demand Defrost — control auto-selects mode based on prior cycle outcome. Defrost Enable coil temp: 35°F. Forces a defrost check at 31 min accumulated compressor run time (6-hr ceiling); defrost cycle runs up to 12 min or terminates early on coil temp","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing Valve Energized Mode","value":"Confirmed energized-in-cooling / de-energized-in-heating — control 'Energizes the reversing valve' to enter defrost (which runs the unit in cooling mode) and 'De-energizes the reversing valve' at defrost termination","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Protections & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"No fixed psig published — HPS is an electronic soft-lockout; 4 soft lockouts (8 total HPS openings) escalates to a hard lockout requiring manual reset, see Owner's Guide","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"No fixed psig published — ignored during/just after defrost and below 15°F ambient (see flag); otherwise soft-lockout logic","key":"lps"},{"label":"Low Ambient Lockout","value":"Standard/built-in — approved for cooling operation down to 35°F (2°C) without an accessory kit","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase Heater","value":"Yes — confirmed (dedicated CCH troubleshooting section in manual)","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"System Charge","value":"See nameplate / System Charge table — do not invent a charge value","key":"charge"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"York/Coleman/Luxaire (Johnson Controls) Demand Defrost Control boards have a 'TEST' pin pair (P3 on some revisions). With a heating call active, jumper the TEST pins for 6+ seconds — defrost engages and continues for as long as the jumper stays in place. While TEST is jumpered, the control ignores actual coil (liquid-line) temperature and outdoor ambient — the coil does NOT need to be cold for the forced test to run. After removing the jumper, defrost terminates normally on its own logic: liquid-line temp reaches 80°F, or after 8 minutes of defrost run time, whichever comes first. Source: Johnson Controls Unitary Products 'Demand Defrost Control' Operation Instructions, part 031-09178-000 / doc 501062-UAI (cdn.master.ca and us-ac.com hosted copies), plus corroborating HVAC-Talk field posts."},{"label":"ComfortNet/Affinity communicating","value":"NOT independently verified this session. The S1-TTSCC01/S1-TTSCC02 Affinity/ComfortNet touchscreen control has a service/diagnostics area, and York field literature references being able to force a defrost cycle through it, but no source located gave the exact on-screen menu path or button sequence. Do not guess the menu steps — pull the specific control's Installation/Operation guide or use the physical TEST-pin method above (works regardless of comm status) if the outdoor unit's board is accessible."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"On normal (non-forced) operation, coil temp must be below the board's frost/cut-in threshold before a defrost demand will latch; the TEST-pin forced method above deliberately bypasses that check. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may lock in — warn of a normal burst of cold supply air during the test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YHE018-060 / YHG018-060 (LX Series Single-Stage Heat Pump)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Single-stage scroll-compressor heat pumps on the shared LX Series platform: YHE is the 14 SEER tier, YHG the 16 SEER tier. On-demand microprocessor defrost with a field-set jumper interval.","match":["York YHE","York YHG","Coleman/Luxaire TH4 (YHE 14 SEER twin)","Coleman YHG / Luxaire TH6 (YHG 16 SEER twin)"],"source":"York Technical Guide 5455359-YTG-A-1217 (YHE, 14 SEER R-410A 1-Phase, yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/YHE_NEW_TECH.pdf) and York Technical Guide 5599017-YTG-F-0520 (YHG, 16 SEER R-410A 1-Phase, yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/YHG_tech.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Crankcase Heater Presence Differs by Tier/Size","body":"YHE (14 SEER) ships WITHOUT a crankcase heater on most sizes but WITH one on its two largest tonnage models, per the Physical & Electrical Data table. YHG (16 SEER) ships WITH a crankcase heater on every size. Don't assume either way — check the specific model's data table or rating plate."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering Device","value":"YHE: piston or TXV allowed depending on matched indoor coil (TXV + hard-start kit required on some matches). YHG: TXV required on all matches (S1-1TVM*** kit)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Single-stage scroll","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost Type/Interval","value":"On-demand (microprocessor) defrost; field-set via a Defrost Jumper Pin position that varies by matched indoor coil (see System Charge for Various Matched Systems table for the pin setting per model — the pin-position-to-minutes mapping is printed on the defrost control board itself, not in this guide)","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing Valve Energized Mode","value":"Not stated in this guide. Standard York/JCI convention is energized-in-cooling / de-energized-in-heating — confirm against the unit wiring diagram before relying on it","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Protections & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in Technical Guide — see rating plate or IFC/board label","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in Technical Guide — see rating plate or IFC/board label","key":"lps"},{"label":"Low Ambient Lockout","value":"No standard rating below normal cooling operation stated. Accessory kits extend cooling to +20°F (Standard Kit S1-2LA06700424) or -20°F (Advanced Kit S1-2LA04701024); ambient ≤55°F for servicing calls for the Cold Weather Charging Tent (S1-CHGTENT01)","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase Heater","value":"Model-dependent — see flag above; confirm on rating plate","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"System Charge","value":"See nameplate / System Charge table — do not invent a charge value","key":"charge"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"York/Coleman/Luxaire (Johnson Controls) Demand Defrost Control boards have a 'TEST' pin pair (P3 on some revisions). With a heating call active, jumper the TEST pins for 6+ seconds — defrost engages and continues for as long as the jumper stays in place. While TEST is jumpered, the control ignores actual coil (liquid-line) temperature and outdoor ambient — the coil does NOT need to be cold for the forced test to run. After removing the jumper, defrost terminates normally on its own logic: liquid-line temp reaches 80°F, or after 8 minutes of defrost run time, whichever comes first. Source: Johnson Controls Unitary Products 'Demand Defrost Control' Operation Instructions, part 031-09178-000 / doc 501062-UAI (cdn.master.ca and us-ac.com hosted copies), plus corroborating HVAC-Talk field posts."},{"label":"ComfortNet/Affinity communicating","value":"NOT independently verified this session. The S1-TTSCC01/S1-TTSCC02 Affinity/ComfortNet touchscreen control has a service/diagnostics area, and York field literature references being able to force a defrost cycle through it, but no source located gave the exact on-screen menu path or button sequence. Do not guess the menu steps — pull the specific control's Installation/Operation guide or use the physical TEST-pin method above (works regardless of comm status) if the outdoor unit's board is accessible."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"On normal (non-forced) operation, coil temp must be below the board's frost/cut-in threshold before a defrost demand will latch; the TEST-pin forced method above deliberately bypasses that check. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may lock in — warn of a normal burst of cold supply air during the test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"HMH7 (Horizontal Discharge Modulating Heat Pump)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"17 SEER2 side/horizontal-discharge inverter-driven modulating heat pump (35-100% capacity), optionally communicating; ducted residential outdoor unit, not a mini-split/ductless system. HMCG2 is this platform's straight-cool AC companion.","match":["York HMH7","Coleman HMH7","Luxaire HMH7 (same model code used across all three brands)"],"source":"YORK Technical Guide 6353669-YTG-C-0923, 'HMH7 Series - 17 SEER2 Horizontal Discharge Modulating Heat Pump', R-410A/R-454B, 2-5 nominal tons, dated 2023-09-12 — yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/hmh7tech.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Dual-Refrigerant Platform — Confirm Nameplate Before Connecting Gauges","body":"HMH7 is built in both R-410A (model refrigerant code B) and R-454B (code D) versions. Using the wrong gauges, recovery equipment, or refrigerant on this platform is a real risk — always read the rating plate before connecting a manifold, never assume R-410A."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (code B) or R-454B (code D) — see flag; confirm from model number/rating plate","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering Device","value":"TXV","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Inverter-driven, modulating; optionally Communicating (control strategy code C available) or standard non-communicating, per model number","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost Type/Interval","value":"Demand-defrost, adaptive control on the same JCI modulating-platform control architecture as YHM. Board-specific timing values are not printed in this Technical Guide — see the HMH7 User's Guide / IFC board label for sequence detail","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing Valve Energized Mode","value":"Not stated in this Technical Guide. Same JCI modulating-platform family as YHM, which confirms energized-in-cooling / de-energized-in-heating — verify against this unit's wiring diagram","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Protections & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — related modulating platforms use an electronic soft-lockout (no fixed psig); see IFC board label","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — see IFC board label","key":"lps"},{"label":"Low Ambient Lockout","value":"Standard/built-in — guide states units 'shall be approved for cooling operation between 35°F and 122°F without modification'","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase Heater","value":"Yes (base heater) — all sizes","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"System Charge","value":"See nameplate / chart — do not invent a charge value","key":"charge"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"York/Coleman/Luxaire (Johnson Controls) Demand Defrost Control boards have a 'TEST' pin pair (P3 on some revisions). With a heating call active, jumper the TEST pins for 6+ seconds — defrost engages and continues for as long as the jumper stays in place. While TEST is jumpered, the control ignores actual coil (liquid-line) temperature and outdoor ambient — the coil does NOT need to be cold for the forced test to run. After removing the jumper, defrost terminates normally on its own logic: liquid-line temp reaches 80°F, or after 8 minutes of defrost run time, whichever comes first. Source: Johnson Controls Unitary Products 'Demand Defrost Control' Operation Instructions, part 031-09178-000 / doc 501062-UAI (cdn.master.ca and us-ac.com hosted copies), plus corroborating HVAC-Talk field posts."},{"label":"ComfortNet/Affinity communicating","value":"NOT independently verified this session. The S1-TTSCC01/S1-TTSCC02 Affinity/ComfortNet touchscreen control has a service/diagnostics area, and York field literature references being able to force a defrost cycle through it, but no source located gave the exact on-screen menu path or button sequence. Do not guess the menu steps — pull the specific control's Installation/Operation guide or use the physical TEST-pin method above (works regardless of comm status) if the outdoor unit's board is accessible."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"On normal (non-forced) operation, coil temp must be below the board's frost/cut-in threshold before a defrost demand will latch; the TEST-pin forced method above deliberately bypasses that check. When defrost engages: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may lock in — warn of a normal burst of cold supply air during the test."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YXV024-060 (Affinity Variable-Capacity Air Conditioner)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Up to 21 SEER fully communicating variable-capacity air conditioner (inverter compressor); requires a compatible communicating thermostat and includes Charge Assurance refrigerant-charge monitoring.","match":["York YXV","Coleman AC21","Luxaire AL21"],"source":"York Technical Guide 5331838-YTG-B-0517, 'Affinity Series 20 SEER - Modulating Split-System Air Conditioner', R-410A 1-Phase — yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/YXVtech.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Communicating Thermostat Is Required for Variable Operation","body":"YXV needs a compatible Residential Touch Screen Communicating control (only 3 thermostat wires) to deliver true variable-capacity operation. On a conventional thermostat it falls back to fixed-stage operation — check the control type before troubleshooting a 'won't modulate' complaint."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering Device","value":"TXV (dealer-installed or factory on matched indoor coil)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Variable-speed/modulating, communicating","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Protections & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — see rating plate/board label","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — see rating plate/board label","key":"lps"},{"label":"Low Ambient Cooling Limit","value":"Standard/built-in — Low Ambient Protection allows cooling operation down to 35°F (2°C), reducing capacity as needed; no accessory kit required","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase Heater","value":"Yes (stator heat) — all sizes","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"System Charge","value":"See nameplate / Tabular Data Sheet — do not invent a charge value","key":"charge"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YXT024-060 (Affinity 2-Stage Air Conditioner)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Up to 19 SEER / 18 SEER2 two-stage air conditioner. Communications-capable: operates as a conventionally-wired system or, with only 4 thermostat wires, as a communicating system.","match":["York YXT","Coleman AC19","Luxaire AL19"],"source":"York Technical Guide 5493751-YTG-H-1022, 'Affinity Series Model: YXT - 18 SEER2 Split-System Air Conditioner - Single-Phase', dated 2022-10-01 — yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/yxtseer2tech.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No Built-In Low-Ambient Cooling — Kit Required","body":"Unlike the fully-communicating YXV, YXT relies on the same accessory low-ambient kits as the conventional LX-series units (+20°F Standard Kit / -20°F Advanced Kit). Don't assume this model has YXV's built-in 35°F cold-weather cooling capability."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering Device","value":"TXV on all matched indoor coils (dealer-installed or factory, S1-1TVM*** kit)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"2-stage scroll","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Protections & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — see rating plate/board label","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — see rating plate/board label","key":"lps"},{"label":"Low Ambient Cooling Limit","value":"No standard numeric rating printed in this guide. Accessory kits extend cooling operation to +20°F (Standard Kit) or -20°F (Advanced Kit); ambient ≤55°F for servicing calls for the Cold Weather Charging Tent","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase Heater","value":"No (per Physical & Electrical Data table)","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"System Charge","value":"See nameplate / chart — do not invent a charge value","key":"charge"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York","model":"YCG/YCE/YCJ/YFE018-060 (LX Series Single-Stage Air Conditioner)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Single-stage scroll-compressor air conditioners on the shared LX Series outdoor-unit platform. YCG/YCE/YFE/YCJ are efficiency-tier variants (roughly 13-17 SEER depending on the matched indoor coil) of the same physical unit.","match":["York YCG","York YCE","York YCJ","York YFE","Luxaire TC-series (confirmed cross-reference: TC7B tier ≈ YCG, TC4B tier ≈ YCE)","Coleman equivalent on the same LX platform — exact tier code not directly confirmed in reviewed literature, verify rating plate"],"source":"York Technical Guide 5495509-YTG-F-1021, 'LX Series Split-System Air Conditioners' up to 17 SEER, R-410A 1-Phase — yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/ycgtech.pdf (see also yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/ycetech.pdf for the YCE-specific tier)","flags":[{"title":"Refrigerant Varies by Vintage — Always Check the Nameplate","body":"This LX outdoor-unit platform has produced both R-410A units (YCG/YCE/YCJ/YFE, covered here) and newer R-454B SEER2 successors on the same chassis family (e.g. YC4-tier). Never assume R-410A on a unit in this family — confirm refrigerant type from the rating plate before connecting gauges or recovery equipment."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A on YCG/YCE/YCJ/YFE (confirm on nameplate — see flag)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering Device","value":"TXV required on all matched indoor coils (S1-1TVM*** kit)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Single-stage scroll","key":"compressor"}]},{"title":"Protections & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — see rating plate/board label","key":"hps"},{"label":"Low Pressure Switch Cutout/Cutin","value":"Not published in this Technical Guide — see rating plate/board label","key":"lps"},{"label":"Low Ambient Cooling Limit","value":"No standard numeric rating printed in this guide. Accessory kits extend cooling operation to +20°F (Standard Kit) or -20°F (Advanced Kit); ambient ≤55°F for servicing calls for the Cold Weather Charging Tent","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase Heater","value":"No (per Physical & Electrical Data table)","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"System Charge","value":"See nameplate / chart — do not invent a charge value","key":"charge"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"match":["York MVC","York MV","MVC08B","MVC12B","MVC12C","MVC14D","MVC16C","MVC20D","Coleman MVC (same model prefix)","Luxaire MVC (same model prefix)"],"brand":"York","model":"MVC / MV","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Modular, variable-speed ECM communicating air handler (constant-CFM). Direct-drive ECM blower is communicating-ready for smart-thermostat pairing; ships as a flex coil with no factory metering device, so a bolt-on TXV kit (or factory TXV on some models) must be added in the field to match the outdoor unit.","source":"York Technical Manual 5151065-YTG-H-0118 (MVC Series, dated 01/18, supersedes 05/17) — yorknow.com; York Install Guide 5169038-UIM-D-0617 (Variable Speed ECM Modular Multi-Position Air Handlers) — yorknow.com","flags":[{"title":"York flag: no factory metering device","body":"MVC ships as a 'Flex-coil' with NO factory-installed metering device. A field bolt-on TXV kit (or factory TXV on select models) must be installed to match the outdoor condenser/heat pump — do not assume a piston is present."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Direct-drive, variable-speed ECM, communicating-capable","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow verification","value":"Onboard LED (LED2) flashes once per 100 CFM for field CFM check","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate / install guide airflow tables (not confirmed for this line)","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Filter & Heat Kit","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Field-supplied 1\" disposable/permanent, sizes incl. 16x20x1, 20x20x1, 22x20x1; optional bottom rack filter kit accessory","key":"filter"},{"label":"Electric heat kit","value":"6HK series, 208/230V-1-60 and 208/230V-3-60, staged on W1 / W1+W2 combinations — see kit-specific table for exact kW/staging","key":"heat_kit"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"None factory-installed (flex coil); field bolt-on TXV kit required, match to outdoor unit — some models have factory TXV","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Thermoset drain pan, low-retention, positive slope to drain connection","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"match":["York AE","AE24BX21","AE30BX21","AE36BX21","AE42CX21","Coleman JHE","Luxaire JHE (multi-speed ECM twin)"],"brand":"York","model":"AE (multi-speed ECM)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Single-piece, multi-position, multi-speed ECM (constant-torque) air handler. Five discrete motor speed taps are selected by energizing 24VAC leads at the motor terminal block; highest energized tap wins if more than one is powered simultaneously. No onboard metering device — piston or TXV is field-installed to match the outdoor unit.","source":"York Installation Manual 5169032-UIM-C-0416 (AE Series) — yorknow.com; also listed as York Install Guide 5373254-UIM-B-0617 (Standard ECM Single Piece Multi-Position Air Handlers) — yorknow.com. Coleman/Luxaire JHE twin per official Luxaire residential air handler lineup page (luxaire.com).","flags":[{"title":"York flag: multiple 24VAC taps energized = highest speed wins","body":"If more than one motor speed tap receives 24VAC simultaneously (miswired stat/board), the AE blower runs at the HIGHEST energized speed tap, not an average — check for stray voltage on unused tap wires during callbacks for wrong-airflow complaints."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Direct-drive, 5-speed ECM (constant-torque, non-communicating)","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"5 speed taps at motor terminal block, selected via 24VAC control wiring (speed #1 low to #5 HI)","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"0.70 in. w.c. (per AE airflow data tables)","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Filter & Heat Kit","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Standard 1\" permanent or disposable; permanent washable filter kits 1PF0601/0602/0603","key":"filter"},{"label":"Electric heat kit","value":"Single-phase kits 2.5-25 kW; 3-phase 208-230V kits 10-25 kW; minimum blower speed required varies by kit model — see heat kit table","key":"heat_kit"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"None factory-installed — piston or TXV must be field-installed to match outdoor unit","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Primary and secondary drain lines must both be field-trapped for proper drainage; fittings per ASTM D2466","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"match":["York AP","AP24BX21","AP30BX21","AP36BX21","AP48CX21","Coleman AP (same model prefix)","Luxaire AP (same model prefix)","Coleman JDP","York AHE (related but ECM, not PSC - see flag)"],"brand":"York","model":"AP (standard PSC/fixed-speed) — also sold as AL / Coleman & Luxaire AP","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Single-piece, multi-position, standard-efficiency multi-speed PSC air handler with MaxAlloy aluminum coil. Same 'AP' model-number prefix is used across York, Coleman, and Luxaire branded literature for this platform. Blower speed is field-selected at the motor terminal block; no factory metering device — piston or TXV is added per outdoor unit spec.","source":"York Installation Guide 5373256-UIM-C-0717 (Standard PSC Single Piece, Multi-Position Air Handlers) — yorknow.com; York/Luxaire/Coleman AP product data sheets (york.com, luxaire.com, colemanac.com)","flags":[{"title":"York flag: AHE is ECM, not PSC — do not treat as the same platform","body":"The AHE series (York doc 697887-YTG-H-0514) is often assumed to be the PSC line but is actually a fixed-speed ECM/brushless-DC blower ('Flex-coil', field bolt-on TXV, no factory metering device) — confirm blower type off the rating plate before ordering a PSC-specific replacement motor for an AHE-tagged unit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Direct-drive, multi-speed PSC motor","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Speed tap selection at motor terminal block (connect motor lead to desired speed tap per unit wiring label)","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"Tested to 0.50 in. w.c. per UL 1995/CSA 22.2 No.236; 0.2-0.5 in. w.c. recommended for optimal performance","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Filter & Heat Kit","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Built-in filter rack, 1.0\" disposable or cleanable filter","key":"filter"},{"label":"Electric heat kit","value":"Field-installed single-phase kits available — see kit-specific kW/staging table (not itemized in this pass)","key":"heat_kit"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"None factory-installed — field piston or TXV required, sized to match outdoor unit (see outdoor unit documentation)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"3/4\" PVC or threaded steel drain connections per ASTM D2466 Sch. 40 fittings (drains are non-pressurized)","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GMVC96 / GCVC96","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"2-stage, 96% AFUE, ComfortNet-compatible condensing furnace on the 34.5\" chassis. This chassis/platform is shared with the Daikin-brand DM96VC/DC96VC twin, so the Daikin service manual is the authoritative source for adjustment and troubleshooting figures.","match":["GMVC96","GCVC96","AMVC96","ACVC96","DM96VC","DC96VC"],"source":"Daikin Service Instructions RSD6612010R5, \"34.5\\\" Chassis DC96VC/DM96VC Two-Stage Gas Furnace\" (daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dm96vc/sm-rsd6612010r5.pdf) — GMVC96/GCVC96 share this platform/chassis and figures","flags":[{"title":"Front cover pressure switch blocks ignition on condensate backup","body":"In addition to the high-fire/low-fire draft pressure switches, this platform adds a \"front cover pressure switch\" wired in series with the main (low-fire) gas valve solenoid. If condensate backs up in the secondary heat exchanger (plugged/misrouted drain), this switch opens and blocks the gas valve — a non-firing furnace with good draft-switch readings should point you here."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — low stage","value":"1.6–2.2\" w.c. (nominal 1.9\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — high stage","value":"3.2–3.8\" w.c. (nominal 3.5\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_high"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — low stage","value":"5.7–6.3\" w.c. (nominal 6.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — high stage","value":"9.7–10.3\" w.c. (nominal 10.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_high"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, NG","value":"4.5\"–10.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, LP","value":"11.0\"–13.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice, NG (factory)","value":"#45 drill","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J54, two-stage","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame-sense signal (Integrated Ignition control)","value":"1–4 µA","key":"flame_sense"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"120V silicon nitride HSI (~2156–2678°F operating temp)","key":"ignitor_type"},{"label":"Ignitor resistance, room temp","value":"37–68 Ω","key":"ignitor_ohms"},{"label":"Ignitor current draw","value":"0.37–0.68 A @ 120V (steady state, preheat)","key":"ignitor_amps"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset bi-metal disc, non-adjustable","key":"primary_limit"},{"label":"Auxiliary limit","value":"Blower housing (both sides); required for horizontal/counterflow","key":"aux_limit"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, temperature-activated, mounted to manifold assembly","key":"rollout"},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"Orifice/pressure-switch kit required above 7,000 ft (USA); Canada certified to 4,500 ft max","key":"altitude"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Goodman / Amana","model":"GMVC95 / GCVC95 (GCVC950915DX figures)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"95% AFUE two-stage variable-speed ComfortNet condensing furnace (~2010-2013). NOT the later GMVC96/GCVC96 platform — orifice, gas valve, LP kit and minimum supply pressure differ. Decode GCVC950915DXAC: G=Goodman (A=Amana), C=counterflow/horizontal (M=upflow/horizontal), V=variable speed, C=ComfortNet, 95=AFUE, 091=input code (90k nominal), 5=2000 CFM airflow, D=24-1/2\" cabinet, X=low NOx, then major/minor revision.","match":["GMVC95","GCVC95","AMVC95","ACVC95","GCVC950915DX","GCVC950915DXAC","GCVC950714CX","GMVC950905CX"],"source":"Goodman Technical Manual RT6612021 Rev. 4 (Dec 2010) \"ACVC9/AMVC95 GCVC9/GMVC95\" p.19 + Installation Instructions IO-341D (Rev. 8/10) pp.38-39 + Service Instructions RS6610004r23 (Apr 2013)","flags":[{"title":"Not the GMVC96 platform","body":"Compared with GMVC96/GCVC96: natural gas orifice is #43 (not #45), gas valve is Honeywell VR9205 or White-Rodgers 36G54 (not 36J54), LP kit is LPM-05/LPM-06 (not LPM-08), and minimum natural gas supply is 5.0\" w.c. (not 4.5). Manifold pressures, ignitor and flame-sense figures are the same."},{"title":"Size-specific figures are for GCVC950915DX","body":"Input/output, temperature rise, static, limits, blower and electrical values below are from the GCVC950915DX column. Other sizes (e.g. GCVC950714CX, GMVC95 upflow models) differ — check the rating plate."},{"title":"Confirm which gas valve is installed","body":"Revision AA–AC builds shipped with either a Honeywell VR9205 or a White-Rodgers 36G54 two-stage valve — check the unit before ordering a replacement."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, NG — high stage","value":"3.5\" w.c. (3.2–3.8\")","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, NG — low stage","value":"1.9\" w.c. (1.6–2.2\")","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, LP — high stage","value":"10.0\" w.c. (9.7–10.3\")"},{"label":"Manifold, LP — low stage","value":"6.0\" w.c. (5.7–6.3\")"},{"label":"Supply pressure, NG","value":"5.0\" min / 10.0\" max w.c. (7.0\" nominal)","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11.0\" min / 13.0\" max w.c."},{"label":"Orifice","value":"#43 natural gas / #55 LP, 4 burners","key":true},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"Honeywell VR9205 or White-Rodgers 36G54, two-stage"},{"label":"Valve coil resistance (WR 36E/F/G)","value":"Main 95 Ω, redundant 98 Ω, 2nd stage 180 Ω (±20%)"},{"label":"LP kit","value":"LPM-05 / LPM-06"},{"label":"High-altitude kit","value":"see rating plate"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Input high / low (0915DX)","value":"92,000 / 64,000 Btuh"},{"label":"Output high / low (0915DX)","value":"86,500 / 60,100 Btuh"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"25–55 °F","key":true},{"label":"External static","value":"0.10–0.50\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Blower","value":"11×10 wheel, 1 HP ECM variable speed"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame sense","value":"1–4 µA","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"120V silicon nitride HSI, 37–68 Ω cold, 0.37–0.68 A"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch trip","value":"High -1.60\", low -0.80\", coil front cover -0.10\" w.c."},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"130 °F"},{"label":"Auxiliary limit","value":"120 °F"},{"label":"Rollout limit","value":"210 °F"}]},{"title":"Electrical / venting","rows":[{"label":"MCA / max overcurrent","value":"15.0 A / 15 A"},{"label":"Transformer","value":"40 VA"},{"label":"Vent / combustion air","value":"2\" / 2\""}]},{"title":"Controls","rows":[{"label":"Control board","value":"White-Rodgers 50C51-289 ComfortNet integrated ignition control (Goodman PCBKF101/102; PCBKF103 from revision AD)","key":true},{"label":"Fault display","value":"Dual 7-segment LEDs, visible through the blower-door window"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GMVM97 / GCVM97","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Modulating (35%–100% continuously variable), 97% AFUE condensing furnace on the 34.5\" chassis. The service manual labels the modulation-range endpoints \"Low Stage\" and \"High Stage\" — these are the low-fire and high-fire manifold pressure targets, not a 2-stage valve.","match":["GMVM97","GCVM97","AMVM97","ACVM97"],"source":"Goodman Service Instructions RS6612015R1, \"34.5\\\" Chassis ACVM97*BA/AMVM97*BA & GCVM97*BA/GMVM97*BA Modulating Gas Furnaces\" (mobile.goodmanmfg.com/mobileapp/stellent/pdf/infoPdf/Lit/RS6612015R1.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"LP manifold-pressure tolerance is wider than NG","body":"The manual states final manifold pressure must not vary more than ±0.3\" w.c. from spec on natural gas, but allows +0.5\" w.c. on propane. Don't hold an LP unit to the tighter NG tolerance when fine-tuning the regulator."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — low fire (~35%)","value":"1.6–2.2\" w.c. (nominal 1.9\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — high fire (100%)","value":"3.2–3.8\" w.c. (nominal 3.5\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_high"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — low fire","value":"5.7–6.3\" w.c. (nominal 6.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — high fire","value":"9.7–10.3\" w.c. (nominal 10.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_high"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, NG","value":"4.5\"–10.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, LP","value":"11.0\"–13.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice, NG (factory)","value":"#45 drill (LP conversion orifice: 1.25 mm)","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J54 (modulating control); Honeywell single/two-stage valves also fielded per manual","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame-sense signal (Integrated Ignition control)","value":"1–4 µA","key":"flame_sense"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"120V silicon nitride HSI (~2156–2678°F operating temp)","key":"ignitor_type"},{"label":"Ignitor resistance, room temp","value":"37–68 Ω","key":"ignitor_ohms"},{"label":"Ignitor current draw","value":"0.37–0.68 A @ 120V (steady state, preheat)","key":"ignitor_amps"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset bi-metal disc, non-adjustable","key":"primary_limit"},{"label":"Auxiliary limit","value":"Blower housing (both sides); required for horizontal/counterflow","key":"aux_limit"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, temperature-activated, mounted to manifold assembly","key":"rollout"},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"0–7,000 ft ships as-is; above 7,000 ft requires altitude kit (orifice and/or pressure switch); Canada certified to 4,500 ft max","key":"altitude"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GMSS92 / GMSS96 / GCSS96","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Single-stage, multi-speed ECM condensing furnaces (92% and 96% AFUE) on the shared single-stage 34.5\" chassis. This platform is shared with the Daikin-brand DM92SN/DM96SN/DC96SN twins; the AFUE difference between 92% and 96% is not called out separately for the figures below.","match":["GMSS92","GMSS96","GCSS96","AMSS92","AMSS96","ACSS96","DM92SN","DM96SN","DC96SN"],"source":"Daikin Service Instructions RSD6612021, July 2021, \"DM92SN, DM96SN & DC96SN Models\" (daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dm96sn/291234817.pdf) — GMSS92/GMSS96/GCSS96 share this platform/chassis and figures","flags":[{"title":"Two gas-valve suppliers fielded — check before ordering the pressure-tap adapter","body":"Single-stage units ship with either a White-Rodgers 36J22 or a Honeywell VR8215 gas valve depending on production run. The White-Rodgers 36[G/J] pressure-check adapter kit (#0151K00000S) is needed to read pressure at the White-Rodgers valve's inlet tap; the Honeywell valve uses a plain 1/8\" NPT hose barb instead. Confirm which valve is installed before grabbing gauges."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG (single-stage)","value":"3.5\" w.c. nominal, ±0.3\" w.c. tolerance","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP (single-stage)","value":"10.0\" w.c. nominal, ±0.3\" w.c. tolerance","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, NG","value":"4.5\"–10.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, LP","value":"11.0\"–13.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice, NG (factory)","value":"#43 drill","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J22 or Honeywell VR8215, single-stage (production-dependent)","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame-sense signal (Integrated Ignition control)","value":"1–4 µA","key":"flame_sense"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"115V silicon carbide igniter, p/n 0130F00008, 17-second warm-up","key":"ignitor_type"},{"label":"Ignitor resistance, room temp","value":"37–68 Ω","key":"ignitor_ohms"},{"label":"Ignitor current draw","value":"see rating plate (not separately published for the silicon-carbide igniter; nitride-equipped units on this platform run 0.37–0.68 A @ 120V)","key":"ignitor_amps"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset bi-metal disc, non-adjustable","key":"primary_limit"},{"label":"Auxiliary limit","value":"Blower housing (both sides); required for horizontal/counterflow","key":"aux_limit"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, temperature-activated, mounted to burner bracket","key":"rollout"},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"Kit required above 7,000 ft","key":"altitude"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GMEC96 / GCEC96","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"2-stage, 96% AFUE condensing furnace with multi-speed ECM motor — the older ECM-generation 2-stage platform (distinct chassis/control from the ComfortNet GMVC96 line).","match":["GMEC96","GCEC96","AMEC96","ACEC96"],"source":"Goodman Service and Troubleshooting RS6612013R10, \"Goodman GMEC96/GCEC96 & Amana AMEC96/ACEC96 Two Stage Furnace with multi-speed ECM Motor\" (mobile.goodmanmfg.com/mobileapp/stellent/pdf/infoPdf/Lit/RS6612013R10.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Smallest input size uses a different orifice","body":"*MEC96/*CEC96 furnaces have factory-installed #45 natural-gas orifices across the line, except the 030 (30,000 BTU input) size, which uses #50. Confirm the input size on the rating plate before resizing for altitude or an LP conversion."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — low stage","value":"1.6–2.2\" w.c. (nominal 1.9\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — high stage","value":"3.2–3.8\" w.c. (nominal 3.5\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_high"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — low stage","value":"5.7–6.3\" w.c. (nominal 6.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — high stage","value":"9.7–10.3\" w.c. (nominal 10.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_high"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, NG","value":"4.5\"–10.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, LP","value":"11.0\"–13.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice, NG (factory)","value":"#45 drill (except 030 input size: #50)","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J54 or Honeywell VR9205, two-stage","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame-sense signal (Integrated Ignition control)","value":"1–4 µA","key":"flame_sense"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"120V silicon nitride HSI (~2156–2678°F operating temp)","key":"ignitor_type"},{"label":"Ignitor resistance, room temp","value":"37–68 Ω","key":"ignitor_ohms"},{"label":"Ignitor current draw","value":"0.37–0.68 A @ 120V (steady state, preheat)","key":"ignitor_amps"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset bi-metal disc, non-adjustable","key":"primary_limit"},{"label":"Auxiliary limit","value":"Blower housing (both sides); required for horizontal/counterflow","key":"aux_limit"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, temperature-activated, mounted to manifold assembly","key":"rollout"},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"Orifice kit required above 7,000 ft","key":"altitude"},{"label":"Pressure switch","value":"Model/coil-cover-specific — see \"Pressure Switch Trip Points and Usage Chart\" in the service manual, keyed to the coil-cover part number installed. Low-fire trip published as -0.08\" to -0.10\" w.c. (±.04–.05\") across the *MEC960303–*CEC964005 size range; high-fire switch assemblies (10 distinct part numbers) trip roughly -0.35\" to -1.68\" w.c. depending on size/coil-cover ID — do not apply one number to every size, match the installed switch/coil-cover part number to the chart","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GR9S / GR9T (R-32 generation, 92%/96%)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Current-generation single-stage (S) and 2-stage (T) condensing furnaces built for pairing with R-32 cooling systems (control board includes an A2L refrigerant-leak monitoring function). Figures below are from the 92%/96% two-stage nine-speed-ECM condensing chassis (DR96TN/DD96TN); the 80% AFUE non-condensing GR9S80/GR9T80 models use a separate manual not covered here.","match":["GR9S92","GR9S96","GR9T96","GD9S92","GD9S96","GD9T96","AR9S92","AR9S96","AR9T96","AD9S96","AD9T96","DR96TN","DD96TN"],"source":"Goodman Service Instructions RSD6612304, May 2024, \"DR96TN/DD96TN Two Stage Furnace with Nine Speed ECM Motor\" (mobile.goodmanmfg.com/mobileapp/stellent/pdf/infoPdf/Lit/RSD6612304.pdf) — Goodman/Amana brand model legend in this manual lists AR9T/GR9T for this platform","flags":[{"title":"R-32 (A2L) monitoring is ON by default — must be disabled if the cooling system isn't R-32","body":"The furnace control board ships with the R-32 leak-monitoring function enabled by default. If the paired outdoor/indoor cooling unit does not use R-32 refrigerant (e.g. a legacy R-410A system) or the R-32 sensor wire isn't connected, the function must be turned off in the \"A2L Function Enabled\" menu (display code A2E, select \"no\") or the furnace will not run properly."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — low stage","value":"1.6–2.2\" w.c. (nominal 1.9\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG — high stage","value":"3.2–3.8\" w.c. (nominal 3.5\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_ng_high"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — low stage","value":"5.7–6.3\" w.c. (nominal 6.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_low"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP — high stage","value":"9.7–10.3\" w.c. (nominal 10.0\" w.c.)","key":"manifold_lp_high"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, NG","value":"4.5\"–10.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply (inlet) pressure, LP","value":"11.0\"–13.0\" w.c.","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice, NG (factory)","value":"#45 drill (except DM96TN0303AN chassis: #50)","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36J54, two-stage","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"see rating plate (approx. 0.5\" w.c. typical range per manual)","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"see rating plate","key":"temp_rise"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame-sense signal (Integrated Ignition control)","value":"3–8 µA — higher minimum than the older Goodman platforms (1–4 µA); don't apply the old spec here","key":"flame_sense"},{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"120V silicon nitride HSI (~2156–2678°F operating temp)","key":"ignitor_type"},{"label":"Ignitor resistance, room temp","value":"37–68 Ω","key":"ignitor_ohms"},{"label":"Ignitor current draw","value":"0.37–0.68 A @ 120V (steady state, preheat)","key":"ignitor_amps"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset bi-metal disc, non-adjustable","key":"primary_limit"},{"label":"Auxiliary limit","value":"Blower housing (both sides); required for horizontal/counterflow","key":"aux_limit"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, temperature-activated, mounted to burner bracket","key":"rollout"},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"0–7,000 ft ships as-is; above 7,000 ft requires pressure-switch and/or orifice kit","key":"altitude"},{"label":"R-32 sensor wire","value":"Inspect for tightness/damage during annual maintenance (control board input, indoor coil to furnace)","key":"r32_sensor"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSZC18","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"18 SEER two-stage split-system heat pump, R-410A, ComfortNet 4-wire communicating-capable with Copeland two-stage scroll compressor and Copeland Comfort Alert diagnostics.","match":["ASZC18"],"source":"Daikin/Goodman \"Service and Troubleshooting: ASXC, DSXC, GSXC Condensing Units & ASZC, DSZC, GSZC Split System Heat Pumps w/ R-410A\" (RS6200007r23) - daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/chpf/rs6200007r23.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Two-stage compressor diagnostics","body":"Units with a Copeland Comfort Alert module (UC control, 2-stage models) flash a status LED for locked rotor, open circuit, high/low pressure trip, or miswire before condemning the compressor - read the module's LED code first."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory non-adjustable TXV standard on communicating (4-wire) coil pairings; flowrator/piston used on some non-communicating coil combinations - confirm indoor coil model","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand defrost: outdoor coil temp (OCT) sensor + accumulated compressor run time; interval selectable 30/60/90/120 min via UC board dip switch; terminates at ~75°F coil temp or 10 min max, whichever first","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling / de-energized in heating (standard Goodman/Amana convention; explicitly confirmed in the companion single-stage RS6200006r101 manual - this two-stage document does not restate it verbatim)","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 610 PSIG ±10, closes (auto-reset) 420 PSIG ±25","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Opens 21 PSIG, auto-resets (closes) ~50 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"PTC type on applicable models, ~40W/265V; energize a minimum of 4 hours before compressor start","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Not published in this document - see unit rating plate / installation manual","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating control","value":"ComfortNet 4-wire ready","key":"controls"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit's Expanded Performance Chart - superheat (piston-equipped) or subcooling (TXV-equipped), per nameplate; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Goodman/Amana/Janitrol PCBDM-series defrost boards (also used re-badged by other brands) commonly require two things at once: 24V present at the board's DFT (defrost thermostat/coil sensor) input — jump R to DFT if the coil isn't actually cold enough to close the sensor — AND a momentary jumper across the board's TEST/'speed-up' pins until you hear the relay click, then remove the TEST jumper. Once triggered, the unit stays in forced defrost (reversing valve to cooling, outdoor fan off, W2 aux heat and O reversing valve energized) until either 24V is removed from DFT or a built-in max defrost time (commonly ~10 minutes) elapses. Exact pin labels/layout vary by PCBDM revision — confirm against the board's own printed legend/wiring diagram before jumping anything; I could not pull a clean OEM PDF this session to confirm the precise pin silkscreen text, so treat pin names as trade-common convention, not a guaranteed exact label. Source: multi-source trade corroboration (HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board guide; JustAnswer and Fixya Goodman-specific Q&A threads) — recommend verifying against the physical board's legend."},{"label":"ComfortNet/ComfortBridge communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. Goodman heat pumps are largely designed to run on a simple non-communicating thermostat (single Y/W inputs) even when ComfortBridge-equipped equipment is installed; where a CTK04 ComfortNet communicating control is used, no source located gave a documented force-defrost menu sequence. Do not invent a button sequence — use the non-communicating TEST-pin method on the outdoor board directly, which applies regardless of thermostat type, or consult Goodman's specific literature for the installed CTK04/ComfortNet control."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Normal operation requires the coil/defrost sensor to be closed (cold, roughly at/below freezing) AND accumulated compressor run time to exceed the board's 30/60/90-minute dial setting before defrost will initiate on its own; the forced method above is meant to bypass the run-time requirement but the coil sensor circuit (DFT) still needs 24V present (real cold coil, or a temporary jumper) for the relay to latch on some revisions. Expect reversing valve shift to cooling and outdoor fan shutdown when defrost runs — a cold air burst indoors is normal and temporary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSXC18","equip":"Condenser","summary":"18 SEER two-stage split-system air conditioner, R-410A, ComfortBridge-compatible with Copeland two-stage scroll compressor and Copeland Comfort Alert diagnostics.","match":["ASXC18"],"source":"Daikin/Goodman \"Service and Troubleshooting: ASXC, DSXC, GSXC Condensing Units & ASZC, DSZC, GSZC Split System Heat Pumps w/ R-410A\" (RS6200007r23) - daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/chpf/rs6200007r23.pdf","flags":[{"title":"ComfortBridge fault check first","body":"ComfortBridge continuously monitors performance on communicating pairs - check the ComfortBridge/Comfort Alert fault code before condemning the compressor or control board on a two-stage complaint."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory non-adjustable TXV standard on communicating (4-wire) coil pairings; flowrator/piston on some non-communicating coil combinations - confirm indoor coil model","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 610 PSIG ±10, closes (auto-reset) 420 PSIG ±25","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Opens 21 PSIG, auto-resets (closes) ~50 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"PTC type on applicable models, ~40W/265V; energize a minimum of 4 hours before compressor start","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Not published in this document - see unit rating plate / installation manual","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating control","value":"ComfortBridge / ComfortNet 4-wire capable","key":"controls"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit's Expanded Performance Chart - superheat (piston) or subcooling (TXV), per nameplate; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSZV20 / GVZC20","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Smart Speed inverter variable-speed heat pump, R-410A, up to 21 SEER/10 HSPF, sharing the Amana AVZC18/AVZC20 inverter platform and CoolCloud/ComfortNet controls per Goodman Service Bulletin SR-068.","match":["AVZC20","AVZC18"],"source":"Goodman \"Service and Troubleshooting: AVZC18 Inverter Heat Pump Condenser Units w/ R-410A\" (RS6215001r7) - partnerlinkmarketing.goodmanmfg.com/Lit/RS6215001r7.pdf; platform shared with GVZC20/GVXC20 confirmed by Goodman Service Bulletin SR-068 Rev.1 (Oct 2020, \"Crank Case Heater Kit for Inverter Split Systems\") - mobile.goodmanmfg.com","flags":[{"title":"Idle high-pitched hum is normal","body":"A high-pitched sound from the outdoor unit at standby is the inverter maintaining compressor oil temperature via winding current, not a defect (SR-068). An external crankcase heater retrofit kit (INVCCHK01, requires BTSDL01 Bluetooth loader) is available if the homeowner finds it objectionable."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) at indoor coil when matched with a communicating (AVPEC-type) air handler; inverter-tuned TXV-V kit required for non-matched/non-communicating air handlers","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"PCB + outdoor coil temp thermistor + dedicated defrost sensor (Tb); interval selectable 30/60/90/120 min; terminates when defrost sensor reads >43°F for 30 continuous seconds or max interval reached","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling / de-energized in heating (standard Goodman/Amana convention; explicitly stated for this shared platform in the companion R-32 manual RS6200301, not restated verbatim here)","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Monitoring","rows":[{"label":"Pressure sensing","value":"HI/LOW pressure SENSOR (transducer), not a fixed on/off switch - senses suction pressure in cooling, discharge pressure in heating","key":"pressure_sensor"},{"label":"High-pressure control test point","value":"Verified to cut out at approximately 605 PSIG during the charge-mode functional test procedure","key":"hp_test"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"None standard - oil kept warm via compressor winding current in standby (SR-068); optional external CCH retrofit kit available","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Outdoor temp lockouts","value":"Compressor lockout and backup-heat lockout temperatures are installer-configured at the thermostat - no fixed factory default published in this document","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"System test note","value":"The outdoor unit's SYSTEM TEST self-check may not complete in ambient under 20°F due to low suction pressure - re-run once ambient exceeds 20°F; this is normal, not a fault","key":"test_note"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Speed modulation","value":"Compressor speed auto-adjusts with outdoor ambient - runs ~50% capacity below 70°F, ramps linearly to 100% above 95°F","key":"controls"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"ComfortNet 4-wire ready; CoolCloud app + Bluetooth Shared Data Loader (BTSDL01) used for board data/firmware service","key":"comfortnet"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit nameplate/Expanded Performance Chart, subcooling method on EEV-equipped systems; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Goodman/Amana/Janitrol PCBDM-series defrost boards (also used re-badged by other brands) commonly require two things at once: 24V present at the board's DFT (defrost thermostat/coil sensor) input — jump R to DFT if the coil isn't actually cold enough to close the sensor — AND a momentary jumper across the board's TEST/'speed-up' pins until you hear the relay click, then remove the TEST jumper. Once triggered, the unit stays in forced defrost (reversing valve to cooling, outdoor fan off, W2 aux heat and O reversing valve energized) until either 24V is removed from DFT or a built-in max defrost time (commonly ~10 minutes) elapses. Exact pin labels/layout vary by PCBDM revision — confirm against the board's own printed legend/wiring diagram before jumping anything; I could not pull a clean OEM PDF this session to confirm the precise pin silkscreen text, so treat pin names as trade-common convention, not a guaranteed exact label. Source: multi-source trade corroboration (HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board guide; JustAnswer and Fixya Goodman-specific Q&A threads) — recommend verifying against the physical board's legend."},{"label":"ComfortNet/ComfortBridge communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. Goodman heat pumps are largely designed to run on a simple non-communicating thermostat (single Y/W inputs) even when ComfortBridge-equipped equipment is installed; where a CTK04 ComfortNet communicating control is used, no source located gave a documented force-defrost menu sequence. Do not invent a button sequence — use the non-communicating TEST-pin method on the outdoor board directly, which applies regardless of thermostat type, or consult Goodman's specific literature for the installed CTK04/ComfortNet control."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Normal operation requires the coil/defrost sensor to be closed (cold, roughly at/below freezing) AND accumulated compressor run time to exceed the board's 30/60/90-minute dial setting before defrost will initiate on its own; the forced method above is meant to bypass the run-time requirement but the coil sensor circuit (DFT) still needs 24V present (real cold coil, or a temporary jumper) for the relay to latch on some revisions. Expect reversing valve shift to cooling and outdoor fan shutdown when defrost runs — a cold air burst indoors is normal and temporary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSXV20 / GVXC20","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Smart Speed inverter variable-speed air conditioner, R-410A, up to 24.5 SEER/15 EER, sharing the Amana AVXC18/AVXC20 inverter platform per Goodman Service Bulletin SR-068.","match":["AVXC20","AVXC18"],"source":"Goodman \"Service and Troubleshooting: AVZC18 Inverter Heat Pump Condenser Units w/ R-410A\" (RS6215001r7) - partnerlinkmarketing.goodmanmfg.com/Lit/RS6215001r7.pdf (shared inverter platform/controls document); platform shared with GVXC20/GVZC20 confirmed by Goodman Service Bulletin SR-068 Rev.1 (Oct 2020) - mobile.goodmanmfg.com","flags":[{"title":"Below-20°F system test","body":"The outdoor unit's SYSTEM TEST self-check can fail to complete in ambient under 20°F due to low suction pressure - re-run the test once ambient exceeds 20°F rather than condemning the unit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) when matched with a communicating air handler; inverter-tuned TXV-V kit for non-matched/non-communicating air handlers","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Pressure Monitoring","rows":[{"label":"Pressure sensing","value":"HI/LOW pressure SENSOR (transducer), not a fixed on/off switch","key":"pressure_sensor"},{"label":"High-pressure control test point","value":"Verified to cut out at approximately 605 PSIG during the charge-mode functional test procedure","key":"hp_test"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"None standard - oil kept warm via compressor winding current in standby (SR-068); optional external CCH retrofit kit available","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling lockout","value":"Not published in this document - see unit rating plate / installation manual","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Speed modulation","value":"Compressor speed auto-adjusts with outdoor ambient - ~50% capacity below 70°F, ramping to 100% above 95°F","key":"controls"},{"label":"Communicating control","value":"ComfortNet 4-wire ready","key":"comfortnet"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit nameplate/Expanded Performance Chart, subcooling method on EEV-equipped systems; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSZB4 / GSZS4","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"14.3+ SEER2 R-32 single-stage split-system heat pump platform (Goodman GSZB4/GSZS4, Amana ALZS4/ALZS5 twins) with a factory Refrigerant Detection System for A2L leak mitigation.","match":["ALZS4","ALZS5"],"source":"Goodman/Daikin \"Service and Troubleshooting: ALXS/GLXS Condensing Units, ALZS4/GLZS4/GLXS5 Heat Pumps w/ R-32 Refrigerant\" (RS6200301) - daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/amst-(r-32)/sm-rs6200301.pdf. A model-specific manual revision naming GSZB4/GSZS4 directly was not located; this entry reflects Goodman's current-generation R-32 single-stage platform manual that the manufacturer groups these tiers under - verify exact coverage against the unit's rating plate.","flags":[{"title":"R-32 leak alarm - do not open or de-power","body":"If the Refrigerant Detection System (RDS) signals an R-32 leak alarm (LED flash pattern), do NOT open the unit or turn it off - the control automatically stops the thermostat call, runs the blower for air circulation, and shuts off electric heat. Read the A2L PCB fault-code label before servicing."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-32 (mildly flammable, A2L classification)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV or fixed orifice/flowrator depending on coil pairing - charge by subcooling (TXV) or superheat (piston/orifice) per nameplate","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Solid-state defrost control + outdoor coil defrost thermostat/sensor; timer interval selectable 30/60/90 min","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling / de-energized in heating - explicitly stated in this manual for R-32 heat pump models","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 610 PSIG ±10, closes (auto-reset) 420 PSIG ±25","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Opens 21 PSIG, auto-resets (closes) ~50 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"PTC type on applicable models; energize a minimum of 4 hours before compressor start","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Not published in this document - see unit rating plate / installation manual","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Standard 24V staging with optional Copeland Comfort Alert compressor-protection module - not a full ComfortNet communicating platform","key":"controls"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit's Expanded Performance Chart; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Goodman/Amana/Janitrol PCBDM-series defrost boards (also used re-badged by other brands) commonly require two things at once: 24V present at the board's DFT (defrost thermostat/coil sensor) input — jump R to DFT if the coil isn't actually cold enough to close the sensor — AND a momentary jumper across the board's TEST/'speed-up' pins until you hear the relay click, then remove the TEST jumper. Once triggered, the unit stays in forced defrost (reversing valve to cooling, outdoor fan off, W2 aux heat and O reversing valve energized) until either 24V is removed from DFT or a built-in max defrost time (commonly ~10 minutes) elapses. Exact pin labels/layout vary by PCBDM revision — confirm against the board's own printed legend/wiring diagram before jumping anything; I could not pull a clean OEM PDF this session to confirm the precise pin silkscreen text, so treat pin names as trade-common convention, not a guaranteed exact label. Source: multi-source trade corroboration (HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board guide; JustAnswer and Fixya Goodman-specific Q&A threads) — recommend verifying against the physical board's legend."},{"label":"ComfortNet/ComfortBridge communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. Goodman heat pumps are largely designed to run on a simple non-communicating thermostat (single Y/W inputs) even when ComfortBridge-equipped equipment is installed; where a CTK04 ComfortNet communicating control is used, no source located gave a documented force-defrost menu sequence. Do not invent a button sequence — use the non-communicating TEST-pin method on the outdoor board directly, which applies regardless of thermostat type, or consult Goodman's specific literature for the installed CTK04/ComfortNet control."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Normal operation requires the coil/defrost sensor to be closed (cold, roughly at/below freezing) AND accumulated compressor run time to exceed the board's 30/60/90-minute dial setting before defrost will initiate on its own; the forced method above is meant to bypass the run-time requirement but the coil sensor circuit (DFT) still needs 24V present (real cold coil, or a temporary jumper) for the relay to latch on some revisions. Expect reversing valve shift to cooling and outdoor fan shutdown when defrost runs — a cold air burst indoors is normal and temporary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSZH5","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Up to 15.2 SEER2 / 7.8 HSPF2 R-32 split-system heat pump (Goodman GSZH5, Amana twin ALZS5), the higher-tier version of the same R-32 single-stage platform as GSZB4/GSZS4.","match":["ALZS5"],"source":"Goodman/Daikin \"Service and Troubleshooting: ALXS/GLXS Condensing Units, ALZS4/GLZS4/GLXS5 Heat Pumps w/ R-32 Refrigerant\" (RS6200301) - daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/amst-(r-32)/sm-rs6200301.pdf. A model-specific manual revision naming GSZH5 directly was not located; this entry reflects the same R-32 platform manual as GSZB4/GSZS4 - verify exact coverage against the unit's rating plate.","flags":[{"title":"A2L brazing/leak-test rules","body":"Never use compressed air, oxygen, or a non-approved refrigerant to leak-test or pressurize an R-32 (A2L) system - use dry nitrogen only, and electrically isolate the unit before breaking into the sealed system, per this manual's A2L procedures."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-32 (mildly flammable, A2L classification)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV or fixed orifice/flowrator depending on coil pairing - charge by subcooling (TXV) or superheat (piston/orifice) per nameplate","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Solid-state defrost control + outdoor coil defrost thermostat/sensor; timer interval selectable 30/60/90 min","key":"defrost"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in cooling / de-energized in heating - explicitly stated in this manual for R-32 heat pump models","key":"reversing_valve"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 610 PSIG ±10, closes (auto-reset) 420 PSIG ±25","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Opens 21 PSIG, auto-resets (closes) ~50 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"PTC type on applicable models; energize a minimum of 4 hours before compressor start","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient lockout","value":"Not published in this document - see unit rating plate / installation manual","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Standard 24V staging with optional Copeland Comfort Alert compressor-protection module - not a full ComfortNet communicating platform","key":"controls"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit's Expanded Performance Chart; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Goodman/Amana/Janitrol PCBDM-series defrost boards (also used re-badged by other brands) commonly require two things at once: 24V present at the board's DFT (defrost thermostat/coil sensor) input — jump R to DFT if the coil isn't actually cold enough to close the sensor — AND a momentary jumper across the board's TEST/'speed-up' pins until you hear the relay click, then remove the TEST jumper. Once triggered, the unit stays in forced defrost (reversing valve to cooling, outdoor fan off, W2 aux heat and O reversing valve energized) until either 24V is removed from DFT or a built-in max defrost time (commonly ~10 minutes) elapses. Exact pin labels/layout vary by PCBDM revision — confirm against the board's own printed legend/wiring diagram before jumping anything; I could not pull a clean OEM PDF this session to confirm the precise pin silkscreen text, so treat pin names as trade-common convention, not a guaranteed exact label. Source: multi-source trade corroboration (HVAC Training Solutions defrost-board guide; JustAnswer and Fixya Goodman-specific Q&A threads) — recommend verifying against the physical board's legend."},{"label":"ComfortNet/ComfortBridge communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. Goodman heat pumps are largely designed to run on a simple non-communicating thermostat (single Y/W inputs) even when ComfortBridge-equipped equipment is installed; where a CTK04 ComfortNet communicating control is used, no source located gave a documented force-defrost menu sequence. Do not invent a button sequence — use the non-communicating TEST-pin method on the outdoor board directly, which applies regardless of thermostat type, or consult Goodman's specific literature for the installed CTK04/ComfortNet control."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"Normal operation requires the coil/defrost sensor to be closed (cold, roughly at/below freezing) AND accumulated compressor run time to exceed the board's 30/60/90-minute dial setting before defrost will initiate on its own; the forced method above is meant to bypass the run-time requirement but the coil sensor circuit (DFT) still needs 24V present (real cold coil, or a temporary jumper) for the relay to latch on some revisions. Expect reversing valve shift to cooling and outdoor fan shutdown when defrost runs — a cold air burst indoors is normal and temporary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GLXS4 / GSXB4 / GSXS4 / GSXH5","equip":"Condenser","summary":"13.4-17 SEER2 R-32 single-stage split-system air conditioner platform (Goodman GLXS4/GSXB4/GSXS4/GSXH5, Amana ALXS3/ALXS4/ALXS5 twins) with a factory Refrigerant Detection System for A2L leak mitigation.","match":["ALXS3","ALXS4","ALXS5"],"source":"Goodman/Daikin \"Service and Troubleshooting: ALXS3, ALXS4, ALXS5, GLXS3, GLXS4, GLXS5 Condensing Units w/ R-32 Refrigerant\" (RS6200301) - daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/amst-(r-32)/sm-rs6200301.pdf. GSXB4/GSXS4/GSXH5 model-specific manual revisions were not located; this entry reflects the same current-generation R-32 platform manual that explicitly names GLXS4 - verify exact tier coverage against the unit's rating plate.","flags":[{"title":"R-32 leak alarm - do not open or de-power","body":"If the Refrigerant Detection System (RDS) signals an R-32 leak alarm, do not open the unit or de-energize it - let the automatic sequence (thermostat off, blower on, heat off) run, then read the A2L PCB fault-code label before servicing."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-32 (mildly flammable, A2L classification)","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV or fixed orifice/flowrator depending on coil pairing - charge by subcooling (TXV) or superheat (piston/orifice) per nameplate","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 610 PSIG ±10, closes (auto-reset) 420 PSIG ±25","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Opens 21 PSIG, auto-resets (closes) ~50 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"PTC type on applicable models; energize a minimum of 4 hours before compressor start","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient cooling lockout","value":"Not published in this document - see unit rating plate / installation manual","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Standard 24V staging with optional Copeland Comfort Alert compressor-protection module - not a full ComfortNet communicating platform","key":"controls"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit's Expanded Performance Chart; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSX14 / GSXN4","equip":"Condenser","summary":"14-14.3 SEER(2) single-stage split-system air conditioner, R-410A (Goodman GSX14/GSXN4, Amana twin ASX14).","match":["ASX14"],"source":"Goodman/Daikin \"Service and Troubleshooting: ANX, SSX, ASX, GSX, DSX, VSX Condensing Units & ANZ, SSZ, ASZ, GSZ, DSZ, VSZ Split System Heat Pumps w/ R-410A\" (RS6200006r101) - daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/aspt/sm-rs6200006r101.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Optional low-ambient cooling kit","body":"Some models are factory- or field-equipped with a Low Ambient Thermostat (LAT) switch/kit to permit cooling operation below the normal outdoor temperature range - confirm its presence before assuming a fixed cooling lockout; no single factory lockout value is published for the base unit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"Piston/fixed-orifice standard; TXV where the matched indoor coil specifies one - charge by superheat (piston) or subcooling (TXV) per nameplate","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 610 PSIG ±10, closes (auto-reset) 420 PSIG ±25","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Opens 21 PSIG, auto-resets (closes) ~50 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"\"Optional item\" on applicable models, PTC type; energize a minimum of 4 hours before compressor start","key":"crankcase"},{"label":"Low-ambient (LAT) kit","value":"Optional switch/kit permits cooling below normal ambient range on some models - no fixed lockout temp published, see rating plate","key":"low_ambient"}]},{"title":"Controls & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Communicating control","value":"Standard non-communicating 24V staging","key":"controls"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Per unit's Expanded Performance Chart; never invent a charge value","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"AWST / AWUF","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Wall-mount (closet/utility) air handler, 1.5-3 tons. Legacy AWUF/AWUT split blower type by model suffix (PSC on AWUF18/24/30/36, multi-speed ECM on AWUF19/25/31/32/37 and AWUT); the current AWST platform standardizes on a multi-speed ECM motor with Flowrater or TXV metering selectable by suffix.","match":["Amana AWST","Amana AWUF","Amana AWUT"],"source":"Goodman SS-GAWUF (AWUF/AWUT Series product specifications, goodmanmfg.com, 11/19); Goodman SS-GAWST (AWST Series product specifications, goodmanmfg.com, 10/23)","flags":[{"title":"Goodman: confirm blower type and metering from the model number, not the family name","body":"\"AWUF\" is not automatically PSC — Goodman split the AWUF/AWUT nomenclature by model number: AWUF18/24/30/36 are multi-speed PSC, AWUF19/25/31/32/37 and all AWUT are multi-speed ECM. AWST's nomenclature (position 3) lists MS-ECM only. Expansion device is coded separately: F = Flowrater (fixed-orifice/piston), T = Thermal Expansion Valve. Always read the full model string off the rating plate before assuming motor or metering type."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower / Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Direct-drive, multi-speed — PSC on legacy AWUF18/24/30/36; multi-speed ECM on AWUF19/25/31/32/37, all AWUT, and all current AWST","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Speed selected by motor lead/tap wired at the low-voltage board per airflow data table; no field CFM dial","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"Not published as a single figure — see rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Cabinet air leakage","value":"<2.0% at 1.0\" w.c. and <1.4% at 0.5\" w.c. per ASHRAE 193","key":"leakage"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit range","value":"3, 5, 8, 10 kW sequence-controlled, rust-resistant nickel-chromium heating elements","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Chassis note","value":"Large chassis (2.5- and 3-ton) is front-return only; small chassis (1.5- and 2-ton) allows front or bottom return","key":"chassis"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"AWUF/AWST \"F\" suffix = Check Flowrater (fixed-orifice/piston); AWUT/AWST \"T\" suffix = fully adjustable TXV — match to outdoor unit type per Goodman combination charts","key":"metering"},{"label":"Coil","value":"Aluminum tubing coil on all models","key":"coil"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Thermoplastic drain pan with bottom primary and secondary drain connections; no factory float switch — field-installed per local code, see rating plate","key":"drain"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Built-in filter rack, filter included from factory","key":"filter"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"AEPF","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position variable-speed (constant-CFM DC/ECM) air handler, 1.5-5 tons, metered with a Check Flowrater. Companion AEPT (expansion-valve, R-22-only) model is covered separately; this entry is the AEPF/piston variant.","match":["Amana AEPF"],"source":"Goodman SS-GAEPF (AEPF/AEPT Series product specifications, goodmanmfg.com, 2/06)","flags":[{"title":"Goodman: airflow is set by dip switches, four modes x four levels","body":"The variable-speed control board has dip switches that pre-program CFM independently for Cooling, Heat Pump Heating, Backup (electric) Heating, and Backup+Heat Pump Heating — four selectable levels per mode. Confirm dip-switch settings match the installed heat kit and outdoor unit capacity; a mis-set dip switch is a common cause of low delivered airflow complaints on this platform."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower / Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Variable-speed DC (ECM) motor; up to 14 field-selectable airflow settings","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Dip switches on the control board — 4 levels each for Cooling, Heat Pump Heating, Backup Heat, and Backup+HP Heat","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"Not published as a single figure — see rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Cabinet air leakage","value":"Factory-sealed to <=2% leakage at 1.0\" w.c. external duct static","key":"leakage"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit range","value":"3-21 kW field-installed electric heat kits","key":"heat_kw"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Low-voltage control circuit is arranged to permit staging of the heater elements","key":"staging"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device (AEPF)","value":"Check Flowrater (fixed-orifice/piston) for cooling and heat-pump applications","key":"metering"},{"label":"Multi-position drain pans","value":"Built-in coil has separate horizontal, vertical, and downflow drain pans with secondary drain connections","key":"drain"},{"label":"Float switch","value":"Not standard — no factory float switch called out; see rating plate/install manual for field kit","key":"float_switch"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Built-in filter rack for 1\" filter (filter not included); permanent washable filter offered as accessory","key":"filter"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"AVPEC","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position, variable-speed ECM air handler with an internal Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV), 2-5 tons. Communicating (ComfortBridge) and inverter-compatible — the matched indoor unit for Goodman/Amana variable-capacity communicating outdoor systems such as the AVXC20 condenser line.","match":["Amana AVPEC"],"source":"Goodman SS-GAVPEC (AVPEC product specifications, goodmanmfg.com, 8/21)","flags":[{"title":"Goodman: EEV units store their own fault history","body":"AVPEC's ComfortBridge control keeps a fault recall log of the six most recent faults, and commissioning/diagnostics run over onboard Bluetooth via the CoolCloud app rather than DIP-switch airflow setup. Pull the fault-recall log first on a communicating-system callback instead of guessing from symptoms, and confirm the outdoor unit is a matched inverter/communicating model (e.g. AVXC-series) before troubleshooting as a standalone air handler."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower / Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Variable-speed ECM, communicating (ComfortBridge); onboard CFM indicator","key":"blower"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Set/commissioned via ComfortBridge communicating control (CoolCloud app over onboard Bluetooth), not field dip switches; provides adjustable low CFM for fan-only operation","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static pressure","value":"Not published as a single figure — see rating plate","key":"max_esp"},{"label":"Cabinet air leakage","value":"<2.0% at 1.0\" w.c. and <1.4% at 0.5\" w.c. per ASHRAE 193","key":"leakage"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit range","value":"3-25 kW electric heater kits (HKS)","key":"heat_kw"}]},{"title":"Metering & Drain","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) — suitable for operation with inverter-driven/communicating outdoor products; match to AVXC-series or other ComfortBridge-communicating condensers/heat pumps","key":"metering"},{"label":"Coil","value":"All-aluminum evaporator coil, multi-position (horizontal or vertical)","key":"coil"},{"label":"Drain pan","value":"DecaBDE-free thermoplastic drain pan with secondary drain connection; no factory float switch called out — see rating plate/install manual for field kit","key":"drain"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Tool-less built-in filter rack, 1\" filter","key":"filter"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"R95T / R95TA","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"95% AFUE SINGLE-stage condensing furnace, Constant Torque ECM blower, PlusOne Ignition (DSI) and PlusOne blocked-drain sensor. Same model-number platform is marketed by Ruud as \"Achiever Plus\" (identical R95TA model numbers, not a separate Ruud number) — do not confuse with the genuinely two-stage R96T.","match":["R95TA0401317MSA","R95TA0601317MSA","R95TA0701317MSA","R95TA0851521MSA","R95TA1001521MSA","R95TA1151524MSA","Ruud Achiever Plus R95T (identical R95TA model numbers, twin-branded)"],"source":"Ruud Achiever Plus / Rheem Classic Plus R95T Series spec sheet, Form No. G22-538, pts.myrheem.com (Gas_Furnace/R95TA/R95TA_G22-538_Rev0-B.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Canadian-only altitude derate method","body":"For Canadian installations only, an optional derate (manifold gas pressure reduction) method may be used to adjust the furnace for altitude. This optional method may NOT be used for U.S. installations — U.S. installs require the orifice change per the installation instructions."},{"title":"Manifold/supply pressure confirmed via the PSC sibling (R95P), not an R95T-specific document","body":"Rheem's R95T/R95TA full installation-instructions PDF exceeded retrieval limits this session, so these gas-pressure figures come from the (-)95P Series Installation Instructions (Form 92-24161-111-03) — the PSC-blower sibling sharing the identical 95% single-stage cabinet and gas train, the same P/T pairing already used elsewhere in this file for R92P/R92T. Cross-check against R95T-specific literature before relying on this for anything beyond field service (code/warranty paperwork)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"see rating plate — not published in this spec sheet; full install-instructions PDF (>30MB) not retrievable this session","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure (LP)","value":"see rating plate","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply pressure (NG/LP)","value":"see rating plate","key":"supply_pressure"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"24V gas valve with integral pressure regulator and supply/manifold test ports (shown in equipment diagram); exact make/model not confirmed","key":"gas_valve"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, NG (confirmed via sibling R95P platform doc)","value":"3.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP (confirmed via sibling R95P platform doc)","value":"10.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, NG (confirmed via sibling R95P platform doc)","value":"5\" min / 10.5\" max w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP (confirmed via sibling R95P platform doc)","value":"11\" min / 13\" max w.c."}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Min external static","value":"0.18–0.28 in. W.C. (varies by size, 040–115)","key":"min_static"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.9 in. W.C. (all sizes)","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"25–55°F (040) up to 45–75°F (115) — size-specific, confirm exact range on rating plate","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"AFUE","value":"95.00%","key":"afue"}]},{"title":"Ignition/diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"PlusOne Ignition System — Direct Spark Ignition (DSI), remote flame sensor; not a hot-surface ignitor, so no ohm spec applies","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Flame sense","value":"Board carries flame-sense current diagnostics — read the 7-segment fault code; no fixed µA spec published","key":"flame_sense"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"Manual-reset rollout switch(es) plus limit control; PlusOne patented Blocked Drain Sensor on condensate side","key":"rollout"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"10% high-altitude output derate published (Canadian installs); see installation instructions for required orifice change on U.S. installs above 2,000 ft","key":"altitude_derate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"R92T / R92P","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"92% AFUE SINGLE-stage condensing furnace (not two-stage, despite some third-party listings). R92P uses a PSC blower motor; R92T is the Constant Torque ECM variant of the same platform — identical cabinet, AFUE, and airflow/temp-rise tables. Both are Rheem Classic(Plus) branded; Ruud markets the same platform under matching R92P/R92T model numbers.","match":["R92PA0401317MSA","R92PA0601317MSA","R92PA0701317MSA","R92PA0851521MSA","R92PA1001521MSA","R92PA1151524MSA","R92TA (Constant Torque ECM variant, same platform/model-number series)","Ruud R92P/R92T (shared model numbers, twin-branded)"],"source":"Rheem Classic Series R92P spec sheet, Form No. G11-536 Rev.1, pts.myrheem.com (Gas_Furnace/R92P/R92P_G11-536_Rev1.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"California low-NOx compliance","body":"Standard model complies with California low-NOx requirements per the spec sheet — confirm the CARB-compliant SKU is used when replacing equipment in a regulated region."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"see rating plate — not published in this spec sheet; full install-instructions PDF exceeded retrieval size limit this session","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure (LP)","value":"see rating plate","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply pressure (NG/LP)","value":"see rating plate","key":"supply_pressure"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"see rating plate","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"24V gas valve with integral pressure regulator and supply/manifold test ports (shown in equipment diagram); exact make/model not confirmed","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Min external static","value":"0.18–0.28 in. W.C. (varies by size, 040–115)","key":"min_static"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.8 in. W.C. (all sizes)","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"25–55°F (040) up to 45–75°F (115) — size-specific, confirm exact range on rating plate","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"AFUE","value":"92.00%","key":"afue"}]},{"title":"Ignition/diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"PlusOne Ignition System — Direct Spark Ignition (DSI), remote flame sensor; not a hot-surface ignitor, so no ohm spec applies","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Flame sense","value":"Board carries flame-sense current diagnostics — read the 7-segment fault code; no fixed µA spec published","key":"flame_sense"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"Manual-reset rollout switch(es) plus limit control; PlusOne patented Blocked Drain Sensor on condensate side","key":"rollout"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"10% high-altitude output derate published (Canadian installs); see installation instructions for required orifice change on U.S. installs above 2,000 ft","key":"altitude_derate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"R801S / R801P","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage NON-condensing furnace on the older UT Electronic Controls (UTEC) platform — the pre-Bluetooth generation, distinct from the current R801/R802 Bluetooth-diagnostic lineup already covered. Upflow/Horizontal and Downflow variants (also badged 80DSS/80DSP) share the same installation instructions and gas/electrical specs; R801S and R801P are identical except cabinet width options.","match":["R801SA*MSA (upflow/horizontal & downflow)","R801PA*MSA","80DSS*/80DSP* (same platform, alternate badge)","Ruud equivalent shares same R801S/R801P model numbers"],"source":"Rheem Installation Instructions for Downflow Single Stage Gas Furnaces (-)801S/(-)801P/(-)(-)80DSS/(-)(-)80DSP, Form 92-24161-143-03 (Supersedes 92-24161-143-02), pts.rheem.com (Gas_Furnace/IO/92-24161-143-03_801S_801P.pdf) — confirms myrheem.com/myruud.com as the parts reference","flags":[{"title":"Only ONE rollout switch on this platform","body":"(-)801S/(-)801P require only ONE flame roll-out manual-reset switch, on the LEFT side of the burner cover plate — unlike larger Rheem platforms that use two. Confirm switch count/location before ordering a replacement part."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"3.5 in. W.C. (±0.3 in.)","key":"manifold_ng"},{"label":"Manifold pressure (LP)","value":"10.0 in. W.C.","key":"manifold_lp"},{"label":"Supply pressure (NG)","value":"5.0–10.5 in. W.C. (5.0 min for input adjustment, 6–7 in. recommended)","key":"supply_ng"},{"label":"Supply pressure (LP)","value":"11.0–13.0 in. W.C. (min 11.0)","key":"supply_lp"},{"label":"Orifice","value":"Factory-default #42 (NG, sized for 1050 Btu/cu.ft. sea-level gas); altitude/heating-value reselection per Table 9 (NG) and Table 10 (LP, #54 0–7,000 ft / #55 7,000–10,000 ft)","key":"orifice"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"24V slow-opening gas valve (Honeywell, per diagram) with integral pressure regulator and supply/manifold test ports; takes 2–3 sec to fully open","key":"gas_valve"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"see rating plate — total system static drop should not exceed 0.8 in. W.C. per install instructions; not populated on the sample nameplate in this doc","key":"max_static"},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"Example on sample rating plate (R801PA075417ZSA, 75,000 Btuh): 25–55°F — size-specific, confirm on the actual unit's rating plate","key":"temp_rise"},{"label":"AFUE","value":"80% (non-condensing, Category I)","key":"afue"}]},{"title":"Ignition/diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor type","value":"Direct Spark Ignition (DSI) via UT Electronic Controls integrated board; not a hot-surface ignitor, so no ohm spec applies","key":"ignitor"},{"label":"Flame sense","value":"Flame proven by rectification 8 sec after gas valve opens; board reports fault code 12 (low flame sense) / 13 (flame lost) — no fixed µA spec published","key":"flame_sense"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Rollout/limit","value":"MRLC (Manual Reset Limit Control, aka rollout) — fault code 33; single switch, left side of burner cover plate. Over-temperature limit and pressure switch also monitored (fault codes 22, 55/57)","key":"rollout"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Ready for 0–4,999 ft as shipped; 5,000–10,000 ft requires manifold pressure/orifice change per Table 9 (NG) and Table 10 (LP) — pressure switch kit 903853 required above 5,000 ft","key":"altitude_derate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RP16 Series","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Classic Series two-stage split heat pump, R-410A, up to 16 SEER/13 EER, single-row 7mm condenser coil, scroll compressor. Ruud sells this identical platform under the same model number.","match":["Ruud RP16 Series (identical model number, Ruud-branded literature)","2, 3, 4, 5 ton"],"source":"files.myrheem.com Product Documents B5265097-4CA1-4CC8-AD6F-AB42CF320654.pdf (Rheem Classic Series Two-Stage Heat Pump spec sheet, Form P11-813 Rev.3); pts.rheem.com .../HP/RP16/92-105074-12-01_RP16_IO.pdf (RP16 Installation Instructions, Doc 92-105074-12 Rev.01)","flags":[{"title":"Confirm refrigerant before connecting gauges","body":"RP16 is an R-410A-only legacy platform. Confirm refrigerant type on the unit nameplate before attaching manifold gauges — do not assume compatibility with R-454B (A2L) service tools/recovery equipment used on newer Endeavor Line units."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV (field/factory installed, model-dependent)","key":"metering"},{"label":"Filter drier","value":"Shipped loose for field installation","key":"filter_drier"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand Defrost Control (coil temp + compressor run time)","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in heating mode (per shared platform wiring diagram notes)","key":"rv_energized"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches (standard)","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Auto-reset: opens (cutout) ~610 PSIG, closes (cutin) ~420 PSIG","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Auto-reset: opens (cutout) ~15 PSIG, closes (cutin) ~40 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Cooling low-ambient (standard)","value":"Rated to 55°F outdoor ambient without accessories","key":"low_ambient_std"},{"label":"Low Ambient Kit (optional)","value":"Extends cooling operation to 0°F; cycles outdoor fan off at ~250 PSIG head pressure; Rheem recommends use below 70°F ambient","key":"low_ambient_kit"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Optional accessory on some capacities; energize 12 hrs before startup after extended shutdown","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging & Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"See unit nameplate / charging chart on service panel — do not invent a superheat/subcooling target","key":"charging"},{"label":"EcoNet/VSODU","value":"RP16 (plain, non-AZ) is not EcoNet-enabled; two-stage staged scroll only","key":"econet_note"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Rheem/Ruud defrost control boards include a 2-pin TEST header. With a heating call active, short the TEST pins with an insulated screwdriver or jumper for 5–7 seconds — reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan turns off, and W (aux heat) energizes, confirming defrost engaged. Some board revisions require a short, momentary release (~1 sec), then a second short to actually trigger the test — if the first short doesn't take, remove and reapply. If 24V is present at the board but the TEST short still won't force defrost, the board is likely faulty. Source: Rheem heat pump service/troubleshooting literature (Rheem 15PJL series 92-20522-80-05 doc referenced in pts.myrheem.com) plus corroborating HVAC-Talk and JustAnswer field threads — the specific OEM PDF could not be parsed directly this session, so confirm pin layout against the installed board's printed legend."},{"label":"EcoNet communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. EcoNet-enabled outdoor units add an outdoor-unit test screen in the EcoNet Control Center app (as of software v60) that can lock compressor speed for testing, but no source located documented a dedicated 'force defrost' command through the EcoNet app or wall control. Use the physical TEST-pin method on the outdoor board instead, or confirm current app capability directly with Rheem/EcoNet support before relying on an app-based method."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, the outdoor coil should be at/below the board's frost cut-in for a natural (non-forced) defrost to latch; the TEST-pin method is designed to bypass that. When forced defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may energize — warn of the normal cold-air burst from supply registers during the test, and don't leave the unit in forced defrost longer than necessary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RP13 Series (shared platform with RP14/RP15)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Classic Series single-stage split heat pump, R-410A, 13 SEER. Rheem publishes RP13, RP14 and RP15 under one shared installation/service manual — same controls, pressure switches and defrost logic across the tier.","match":["WeatherKing WP14 (confirmed shared-platform doc; WP13/WP15 not independently verified)","1.5 to 5 ton"],"source":"pts.rheem.com .../HP/IO/92-105074-04-10_RP13_RP14_RP15.pdf (R-410A Heat Pump Outdoor Units Installation Instructions (-)P14/(-)P15, Doc 92-105074-04 Rev.10, filename covers RP13_RP14_RP15); my.rheem.com/pts/HP/RP13/RP13_IO.asp (document index confirming RP13 uses this manual)","flags":[{"title":"Demand defrost sensor failure behavior differs by sensor","body":"If the outdoor coil sensor fails, the demand defrost control will NOT initiate defrost at all (silent no-heat-in-cold-weather complaint). If the ambient sensor fails instead, the control defaults to a fixed defrost every 34 minutes of compressor runtime with coil temp below 35°F. Check sensor resistance before condemning the defrost board."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV or EEV at indoor unit (per matched indoor coil)","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Defrost & Reversing Valve","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Demand Defrost Control — initiates when outdoor coil temp is below 35°F AND compressor has run 34+ minutes at that coil temp AND the ambient/coil differential trips","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"Terminates on time (14 minutes max) or on termination temperature, whichever occurs first","key":"defrost_term"},{"label":"Reversing valve","value":"Energized in heating mode (wiring diagram note: \"component energized in heating mode\")","key":"rv_energized"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches (standard on (-)P14; confirm on P13/P15 nameplate)","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Auto-reset: opens (cutout) ~610 PSIG, closes (cutin) ~420 PSIG","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Auto-reset: opens (cutout) ~15 PSIG, closes (cutin) ~40 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Low Ambient Control (LAC), P/N RXAD-A08","value":"Senses compressor head pressure; cycles outdoor fan off at ~250 PSIG to hold head pressure at low ambient; rated to 0°F; Rheem recommends use below 70°F ambient","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Some capacities factory-installed; add for units with a low ambient kit; energize 12 hrs before startup after extended shutdown","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Anti-short-cycle","value":"Time-guard keeps compressor off min. 5 minutes after a power interruption or thermostat cycle","key":"anti_short_cycle"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh-in to nameplate charge for 15 ft. line set; use charging chart on service panel for longer runs — see rating plate","key":"charging"}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Rheem/Ruud defrost control boards include a 2-pin TEST header. With a heating call active, short the TEST pins with an insulated screwdriver or jumper for 5–7 seconds — reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan turns off, and W (aux heat) energizes, confirming defrost engaged. Some board revisions require a short, momentary release (~1 sec), then a second short to actually trigger the test — if the first short doesn't take, remove and reapply. If 24V is present at the board but the TEST short still won't force defrost, the board is likely faulty. Source: Rheem heat pump service/troubleshooting literature (Rheem 15PJL series 92-20522-80-05 doc referenced in pts.myrheem.com) plus corroborating HVAC-Talk and JustAnswer field threads — the specific OEM PDF could not be parsed directly this session, so confirm pin layout against the installed board's printed legend."},{"label":"EcoNet communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. EcoNet-enabled outdoor units add an outdoor-unit test screen in the EcoNet Control Center app (as of software v60) that can lock compressor speed for testing, but no source located documented a dedicated 'force defrost' command through the EcoNet app or wall control. Use the physical TEST-pin method on the outdoor board instead, or confirm current app capability directly with Rheem/EcoNet support before relying on an app-based method."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, the outdoor coil should be at/below the board's frost cut-in for a natural (non-forced) defrost to latch; the TEST-pin method is designed to bypass that. When forced defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may energize — warn of the normal cold-air burst from supply registers during the test, and don't leave the unit in forced defrost longer than necessary."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RA13 Series (shared platform with RA14/RA16)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Classic Series split air conditioner, R-410A, 13-16 SEER family. Rheem publishes RA13, RA14 and RA16 under one shared installation/service manual — identical controls, pressure switches and low-ambient accessory across the tier. Ruud markets the identical unit under the same RA13 model number.","match":["Ruud RA13 Series (identical model number, Ruud-branded literature confirmed)","WeatherKing WA13 (confirmed shared-platform doc index page)","1.5 to 5 ton"],"source":"files.myrheem.com Product Documents 7DF54289-1B36-40E5-B20D-59C343AC1B0C.pdf (Ruud Achiever Series Air Conditioners RA13 spec sheet); pts.rheem.com .../AC/IO/92-104921-09-08_RA13_RA14_RA16.pdf (Air Cooled Condensing Units Installation Instructions (-)A13/(-)A14/(-)A16, Doc 92-104921-09 Rev.08)","flags":[{"title":"Cooling below 55°F requires the low-ambient accessory","body":"As shipped, this platform is only rated for cooling operation to 55°F outdoor ambient. Running the condenser below that without the factory Low Ambient Control kit (and crankcase heater) risks head-pressure collapse, compressor flooding, and nuisance low-pressure trips — don't assume every unit in the field has the kit installed."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"TXV or EEV on the indoor unit (per matched indoor coil)","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches (available factory or field-installed; confirm on SKU/nameplate)","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Auto-reset: opens (cutout) ~610 PSIG, closes (cutin) ~420 PSIG","key":"hp_switch"},{"label":"Low pressure switch","value":"Auto-reset: opens (cutout) ~15 PSIG, closes (cutin) ~40 PSIG","key":"lp_switch"},{"label":"Diagnostic service window","value":"Two-fastener opening gives access to install/read high and low pressure switches without full panel removal","key":"diag_window"}]},{"title":"Low Ambient & Crankcase Heater","rows":[{"label":"Cooling low-ambient (standard)","value":"Rated to 55°F outdoor ambient without accessories","key":"low_ambient_std"},{"label":"Low Ambient Control (LAC), P/N RXAD-A08","value":"Senses compressor head pressure; cycles outdoor fan off at ~250 PSIG; extends cooling to 0°F; Rheem recommends use below 70°F ambient","key":"low_ambient_kit"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Recommended whenever a Low Ambient Kit is installed; not required on most scroll-compressor RA13 units otherwise","key":"crankcase_heater"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Factory charge covers 15 ft. line set; use line-length charge adjustment table for longer runs — see rating plate/charging chart","key":"charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RP18AZ / RP16AZ / RP15AZ / RP14AZ (Endeavor Line, current catalog)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Current Rheem Endeavor Line heat pump tiers (Prestige/Classic Plus/Classic series) as listed live on rheem.com in Aug 2026. The RH20AZ/RH17AZ/RH15AZ model numbers requested were NOT found in any published Rheem literature — no \"RH\"-prefixed heat pump line exists. These RP-prefixed AZ models are the closest real, currently-published Endeavor Line equivalents (RP18AZ = top tier, RP16AZ = mid two-stage/inverter, RP15AZ/RP14AZ = entry tiers).","match":["Ruud UP16AZ (confirmed live on ruud.com for the AZ mid-tier)","WeatherKing WP15AZ/WP14AZ platform naming pattern (not independently verified per-SKU)","2 to 5 ton (RP14AZ/RP15AZ: 1.5 to 5 ton)"],"source":"rheem.com/products/residential/heating-and-cooling/heat-pumps/ (live Rheem product catalog, accessed 2026-08-31) and individual model pages (e.g. rheem.com/product/... RP18AZ, RP16AZ, RP15AZ, RP14AZ)","flags":[{"title":"Refrigerant type not consistently published per SKU — verify nameplate","body":"Rheem's Endeavor Line sells parallel AY- and AZ-suffix SKUs per tier. The catalog explicitly labels the AY-suffix siblings (e.g. RD18AY, RA15AY, RA14AY) as \"R-454B Refrigerant,\" but the AZ-suffix cards reviewed do not state a refrigerant type. Do NOT assume R-410A or R-454B on an AZ-suffix unit — confirm on the nameplate/A2L placard before selecting recovery equipment, gauges, or leak-detection method."}],"groups":[{"title":"Efficiency & Platform (as published)","rows":[{"label":"RP18AZ (Prestige)","value":"Up to 20 SEER2 / 12.5 EER2 / 8.5 HSPF2, EcoNet Enabled, 2-5 ton","key":"rp18az"},{"label":"RP16AZ (Classic Plus)","value":"Up to 17 SEER2 / 10.4 EER2 / 8.1 HSPF2, EcoNet Enabled, 1.5-5 ton","key":"rp16az"},{"label":"RP15AZ (Classic Plus)","value":"Up to 16 SEER2 / 11.7 EER2 / 8.1 HSPF2, not EcoNet-enabled, 1.5-5 ton","key":"rp15az"},{"label":"RP14AZ (Classic)","value":"Up to 14.3 SEER2 / 10.4 EER2 / 7.6 HSPF2, not EcoNet-enabled, 1.5-5 ton","key":"rp14az"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"See rating plate / A2L placard — not stated per-SKU in reviewed catalog copy","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"See rating plate / service manual — not stated in reviewed catalog copy","key":"metering"},{"label":"Refrigerant (confirmed)","value":"R-410A on all four tiers (RP14AZ, RP15AZ, RP16AZ, RP18AZ) — each tier's own installation instructions title block states R-410A directly, and Rheem's model-nomenclature key codes this position as Z = R-410A (Y = R-454B is the separate AY-suffix line, not these AZ units). See flag below — this supersedes the 'see rating plate / A2L placard' placeholder row above.","key":true},{"label":"Metering device — RP14AZ/RP15AZ (two-stage, non-communicating)","value":"Factory TXV with 10% bleed rate, installed at both the indoor coil and the outdoor unit"},{"label":"Metering device — RP16AZ/RP18AZ (inverter, EcoNet)","value":"Electronic expansion valve (EXV), controlled by the Universal Outdoor Control (UODC) — driven to 100% open during defrost"}]},{"title":"Defrost, Reversing Valve & Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type/interval","value":"See rating plate / service manual — not published in the marketing literature reviewed; not verified for this generation","key":"defrost_type"},{"label":"Reversing valve energized mode","value":"See service manual — not confirmed for this generation (legacy Rheem platforms energize in heating mode; not verified to carry over)","key":"rv_energized"},{"label":"High/low pressure switch cutout/cutin","value":"See rating plate — not published in reviewed literature","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Defrost initiate — RP14AZ/RP15AZ","value":"Outdoor coil temp below 35°F, AND compressor has run ≥34 min with coil <35°F, AND the defrost control's ambient-vs-coil delta calc confirms frost is present","key":true},{"label":"Defrost terminate — RP14AZ/RP15AZ","value":"Coil reaches the termination temp or 14 min elapse, whichever first. Factory default termination temp is 70°F; field-selectable to 50°F/60°F/80°F by relocating a jumper on the defrost control board."},{"label":"Defrost initiate — RP16AZ/RP18AZ (EcoNet/UODC demand defrost)","value":"Outdoor coil temp below 35°F, AND compressor has run ≥34 min with coil <35°F, AND the UODC's demand-defrost algorithm confirms via the OAT and outdoor-coil (EVAPIN) thermistors","key":true},{"label":"Defrost terminate — RP16AZ/RP18AZ","value":"Coil reaches the termination temp or 14 min elapse, whichever first. Factory default termination temp is 60°F (not field-adjustable via dip switch on this platform per the reviewed manual)."},{"label":"Factory superheat setting (EXV, inverter models)","value":"RP16AZ: pre-programmed 6°F. RP18AZ: pre-programmed 10°F. Set in the UODC firmware — not a field TXV adjustment."},{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"RP14AZ/RP15AZ (1.5-5 ton): High Pressure Control p/n RXAB-A08, Low Pressure Control p/n RXAC-A10; factory-installed standard on model numbers ending 'LHP'. Trip PSIG is not published in the installation instructions — go by the switch's own datasheet or the rating plate."}]},{"title":"Low Ambient, Crankcase Heater & EcoNet","rows":[{"label":"Low ambient lockout","value":"See rating plate — not published in reviewed literature","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"See rating plate — not published in reviewed literature","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"EcoNet/VSODU","value":"RP18AZ and RP16AZ are EcoNet Enabled per catalog; RP15AZ and RP14AZ are not","key":"econet_note"},{"label":"Low ambient support (RP14AZ/RP15AZ platform)","value":"Head-pressure control cycles the outdoor fan off at approximately 250 PSIG to maintain head pressure, extending operation down to 0°F outdoor ambient; recommended whenever the unit runs frequently below 70°F ambient","key":true}]},{"title":"Force defrost","rows":[{"label":"Non-communicating board","value":"Rheem/Ruud defrost control boards include a 2-pin TEST header. With a heating call active, short the TEST pins with an insulated screwdriver or jumper for 5–7 seconds — reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan turns off, and W (aux heat) energizes, confirming defrost engaged. Some board revisions require a short, momentary release (~1 sec), then a second short to actually trigger the test — if the first short doesn't take, remove and reapply. If 24V is present at the board but the TEST short still won't force defrost, the board is likely faulty. Source: Rheem heat pump service/troubleshooting literature (Rheem 15PJL series 92-20522-80-05 doc referenced in pts.myrheem.com) plus corroborating HVAC-Talk and JustAnswer field threads — the specific OEM PDF could not be parsed directly this session, so confirm pin layout against the installed board's printed legend."},{"label":"EcoNet communicating","value":"NOT verifiable this session. EcoNet-enabled outdoor units add an outdoor-unit test screen in the EcoNet Control Center app (as of software v60) that can lock compressor speed for testing, but no source located documented a dedicated 'force defrost' command through the EcoNet app or wall control. Use the physical TEST-pin method on the outdoor board instead, or confirm current app capability directly with Rheem/EcoNet support before relying on an app-based method."},{"label":"Prerequisite / safety","value":"As with other brands, the outdoor coil should be at/below the board's frost cut-in for a natural (non-forced) defrost to latch; the TEST-pin method is designed to bypass that. When forced defrost runs: reversing valve shifts to cooling, outdoor fan stops, aux heat may energize — warn of the normal cold-air burst from supply registers during the test, and don't leave the unit in forced defrost longer than necessary."}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Preliminary charge by weight","value":"Factory charge covers 15 ft of liquid line (all four tiers). Adjust for actual line length/size: 1/4\" = 0.3 oz/ft, 5/16\" = 0.4 oz/ft, 3/8\" = 0.6 oz/ft, 1/2\" = 1.2 oz/ft; add 6 oz for a field-installed filter drier.","key":true},{"label":"Final charge method","value":"Weigh-in is a starting point ONLY. Final charge must be set by liquid subcooling per the chart inside the unit's own access panel cover — design subcooling is model/tonnage-specific, not one number. Charging by subcooling: cooling mode recommended at 55°F+ outdoor dry bulb; heating mode between 40°F and 60°F."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RA18AZ / RA16AZ / RA15AZ / RA14AZ / RA13NZ (Endeavor Line, current catalog)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Current Rheem Endeavor Line air conditioner tiers (Prestige/Classic Plus/Classic series) as listed live on rheem.com in Aug 2026. RA15AZ and RA14AZ are exact matches to the requested Endeavor R-454B line; no RA17AZ exists — RA16AZ (17 SEER2) is the closest real, currently-published equivalent, with RA18AZ as the top inverter tier.","match":["1.5 to 5 ton (RA15AZ/RA16AZ/RA18AZ: 2 to 5 ton)"],"source":"rheem.com/products/residential/heating-and-cooling/air-conditioners/ (live Rheem product catalog, accessed 2026-08-31) and individual model page rheem.com/product/rheem-ra14az-endeavor-line-classic-series-air-conditioner-ra14az30aj1nalhp/","flags":[{"title":"Refrigerant type not consistently published per SKU — verify nameplate","body":"As with the Endeavor heat pumps, the AY-suffix AC siblings (RA16AY, RA15AY, RA14AY) are explicitly labeled \"R-454B Refrigerant\" in Rheem's catalog, but the AZ-suffix cards (RA14AZ, RA15AZ, RA16AZ, RA18AZ) reviewed do not state a refrigerant type, and RA13NZ/RA13NY are only marked \"meets energy standards for Northern regions.\" Confirm refrigerant on the nameplate/A2L placard before servicing — do not assume R-410A or R-454B from the model number alone."}],"groups":[{"title":"Efficiency & Platform (as published)","rows":[{"label":"RA18AZ (Prestige)","value":"Up to 20 SEER2 / 13 EER2, EcoNet Enabled, inverter-driven variable-speed compressor, 2-5 ton","key":"ra18az"},{"label":"RA16AZ (Classic Plus)","value":"Up to 17 SEER2 / 10.5 EER2, EcoNet Enabled, inverter-driven variable-speed twin-rotary compressor, 7mm coil, 2-5 ton","key":"ra16az"},{"label":"RA15AZ (Classic Plus)","value":"Up to 15.2 SEER2 / 9.8 EER2, EcoNet Enabled, inverter-driven variable-speed twin-rotary compressor, 7mm coil, 2-5 ton","key":"ra15az"},{"label":"RA14AZ (Classic)","value":"Up to 16 SEER2 / 13 EER2, not EcoNet-enabled, single-stage compressor, 7mm coil, 1.5-5 ton","key":"ra14az"},{"label":"RA13NZ (Classic, Northern-region)","value":"Up to 15.2 SEER2 / 12 EER2, single-stage, 1.5-5 ton","key":"ra13nz"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"See rating plate / A2L placard — not stated per-SKU in reviewed catalog copy","key":"refrigerant"},{"label":"Metering device","value":"See rating plate / service manual — not stated in reviewed catalog copy","key":"metering"},{"label":"Refrigerant (confirmed)","value":"R-410A across all five tiers (RA13NZ, RA14AZ, RA15AZ, RA16AZ, RA18AZ). RA13NZ/RA14AZ's own installation instructions title block reads \"FEATURING INDUSTRY STANDARD R-410A REFRIGERANT\"; RA15AZ/RA16AZ's title block reads \"VARIABLE SPEED R-410A HEAT PUMP/AIR CONDITIONING OUTDOOR UNITS\"; RA18AZ's spec sheet nomenclature key codes this position as Z = R-410A. See flag below — this supersedes the 'see rating plate / A2L placard' placeholder row above; the R-454B siblings are the separate AY-suffix line only.","key":true}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches & Low Ambient","rows":[{"label":"High/low pressure switch cutout/cutin","value":"See rating plate — not published in reviewed literature","key":"pressure_switches"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling operation","value":"See rating plate / service manual — not published in reviewed literature for this generation","key":"low_ambient"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"See rating plate — not published in reviewed literature","key":"crankcase_heater"},{"label":"Low ambient cooling operation (RA13NZ/RA14AZ platform)","value":"Head-pressure control cycles the outdoor fan off at approximately 250 PSIG, extending cooling operation down to 0°F outdoor ambient","key":true},{"label":"High/low pressure switch","value":"High Pressure Control p/n RXAB-A08, Low Pressure Control p/n RXAC-A10 (1.5-5 ton); factory-installed standard on model numbers ending 'LHP'. Trip PSIG not published in the installation instructions — see the switch's own datasheet or the rating plate."}]},{"title":"EcoNet","rows":[{"label":"EcoNet/VSODU","value":"RA18AZ, RA16AZ and RA15AZ are EcoNet Enabled per catalog; RA14AZ and RA13NZ are not","key":"econet_note"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Preliminary charge by weight","value":"Factory charge covers 15 ft of liquid line. Adjust for actual line length/size: 1/4\" = 0.3 oz/ft, 5/16\" = 0.4 oz/ft, 3/8\" = 0.6 oz/ft, 1/2\" = 1.2 oz/ft; add 6 oz for a field-installed filter drier.","key":true},{"label":"Final charge method","value":"Weigh-in is a starting point ONLY. Final charge must be set by liquid subcooling per the chart inside the unit's own access panel cover — design subcooling is model/tonnage-specific, not one number. Charging by subcooling is recommended at 55°F+ outdoor dry bulb."}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RBHP","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"RBHP-Series high-efficiency air handler, R-410A only. X-13 (ECM) constant-torque motor with 5 field-selectable speed taps, factory shipped connected on Tap 5 (high). Standard/optional electric heat kits built into the blower housing. 35\" tall, 4-way convertible (upflow/downflow/horizontal L or R). Ruud badges the identical platform under the same RBHP model code. Companion hydronic/electric variant RBHK was not independently located in Rheem/Ruud literature this pass - do not assume RBHP figures apply to it; confirm via rating plate.","match":["RBHP"],"source":"Rheem RBHP-Series Air Handler Spec Sheet, FORM NO. H11-544 REV. 3, files.myrheem.com (Rheem Manufacturing Co.)","flags":[{"title":"R-410A platform only","body":"RBHP is built for R-410A systems (RCHL-series coils) and is NOT rated for R-454B/A2L outdoor units. Confirm refrigerant type on the rating plate before matching to an outdoor condenser - do not pair with an R-454B (Y-series) system."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"X-13 (ECM) constant-torque motor, 5 speeds","key":"blower_type"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"Field-selectable motor speed tap (2-5) wired at the control board per cabinet size/tonnage and heat kW - see Airflow Performance Data table for correct tap. Shipped from factory on Tap 5 (high).","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"Optimum operating range 0.2\"-0.5\" W.C.; performance data published from 0.1\" to 1.0\" W.C.","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Permanent washable filter, framed in unit filter rack. Sizes: 17\"cab 16-1/4x21\", 21\"cab 19-3/4x21\", 24\"/25\"cab 23-1/4x21\" (part nos. 54-23217-02/03/04).","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit staging","value":"Model-code heat kW: 06=4.9kW, 07=7.0kW, 11=10.0kW (single circuit, up to 3 elements). Circuit breaker standard on kits above 11kW for UL/cUL service-disconnect.","key":"heat_kit"},{"label":"Max heat rise","value":"85°F (17\" cab) down to 65°F (24\"/25\" cab) - see cabinet-size table for exact CFM/rise limits.","key":"max_heat_rise"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Internal check TXV on the RCHL factory-matched indoor coil (R-410A only).","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Molded polymer corrosion-resistant condensate pan on all coils with PVC condensate elbow standard. External auxiliary horizontal drain pan (RXBM-AA06) fits all sizes as accessory. No factory float switch documented in this literature - verify against local code.","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Rheem","model":"RH1PY","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Endeavor-line PSC single-stage air handler for R-454B (A2L) systems only, form H22-589 Rev.2 (Ruud-badged; identical RH1PY model code used by Rheem). 4-way convertible, aluminum coil, TXV metering, field-installed RXBH- electric heat kits. Companion two-stage constant-torque RH2TY exists in the same Endeavor line, but no RH2P (PSC) model was found published - Rheem's Endeavor two-stage air handler is RH2TY, not RH2P; treat RH2P as not a real/current model number.","match":["RH1PY"],"source":"Rheem/Ruud Endeavor Line Air Handlers RH1PY Spec Sheet, FORM NO. H22-589 REV. 2, files.myrheem.com (Rheem Manufacturing Co.)","flags":[{"title":"R-454B / A2L refrigerant","body":"RH1PY is R-454B (mildly flammable A2L) only - confirm the PlusOne refrigerant detection sensor (factory or field-installed) is present and functional before servicing, and never mix components with an R-410A system. Match indoor/outdoor units by refrigerant type stamped on the rating plate, not by cabinet appearance."}],"groups":[{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"PSC motor, 2-speed (Low/High)","key":"blower_type"},{"label":"Airflow setup","value":"2-speed tap selection via low-voltage wiring at the control board (no dip switches). Airflow range is fixed per cabinet/tonnage - see Airflow Performance Data tables (e.g. 1817S: 517-711 CFM; 4821S/4824S: 1395-1824 CFM).","key":"airflow_setup"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"Optimum operating range 0.3\"-0.7\" W.C.; performance data published from 0.1\" to 1.0\" W.C. Coil-only units: minimum 0.1\" W.C.","key":"max_esp"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Filter size/part number not published in this spec sheet - see rating plate or installation instructions.","key":"filter"}]},{"title":"Electric Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit staging","value":"Field-installed RXBH- kits, single or multiple-circuit, ranging 2.25/3.0kW up to 18.0/24.0kW depending on cabinet size (jumper kits RXBJ-A21/A31 convert multi-circuit kits to a single supply circuit). Kits include UL/cUL service-disconnect circuit breakers.","key":"heat_kit"}]},{"title":"Metering & Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Thermal Expansion Valve (TXV), standard. R-454B only - must be matched to an R-454B (\"Y\") outdoor unit, not R-410A.","key":"metering"}]},{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Drain pan","value":"Vertical drain pan with primary drain plus auxiliary upflow/downflow and horizontal drain connections; double-coil cabinet variants available. No float switch documented in this spec sheet.","key":"drain"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"G40UH / G40DF","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE Merit-series mid-efficiency, non-condensing (upflow/horizontal or downflow)","match":["G40","G40UH","G40DF","G40UHX","G40DFX","G40UH-24A-045","G40DF-24A-045"],"source":"Lennox G40DF Engineering Data, Bulletin 210320, Dec 2008 — https://tech.lennoxintl.com/C03e7o14l/VIu12Ch2uV/ehb_g40df_0812_210320_008.pdf ; Lennox G40UH(X) Installation Instructions — https://greenwoodheating.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/G40UH.pdf","flags":[{"title":"80% AFUE — do not confuse with condensing G41UF/G43UF","body":"G40 is a mid-efficiency, single-heat-exchanger, NON-condensing furnace. No secondary condenser coil, no PVC condensate drain. Vents with Category I single-wall or Type B vent, not PVC."},{"title":"Temperature rise is model-size specific","body":"Published range varies by input size: 20-50°F (24A-045) up to 45-75°F (48C-090/110). Always confirm against the rating plate for the exact model in front of you, not this table."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — Natural Gas","value":"3.5 in. w.c. (all sizes)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LPG/Propane","value":"10.0 in. w.c. (all sizes)","key":true},{"label":"High altitude (7501-10,000 ft.)","value":"Natural gas orifice kit required; LPG/Propane kit required 0-7500 ft. and 7501-10,000 ft. (different kit numbers)"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"SureLight hot-surface igniter (silicon nitride), 20-second warm-up, energized ~95 VAC"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"20-50°F to 45-75°F depending on input size — see rating plate","key":true},{"label":"High static (CSA)","value":"0.50 in. w.g. (all sizes)"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Ignition","value":"SureLight hot surface mini-nitride igniter, 2 status LEDs on board"},{"label":"Lockout","value":"4 failed ignition retries → 60-min Watchguard lockout, auto-reset"},{"label":"Flame rollout","value":"2 manual-reset switches on burner box"},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or greater. Below 1.5 µA = low-flame fast-flash code (replace flame sense rod). Minimum flame sense current 0.5 µA; Watchguard lockout after 5 tries. (Lennox II 505252M-01)","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"G41UF","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"90.0% AFUE single-pipe (non-direct vent only) condensing upflow, Merit series","match":["G41UF","G41","G41UF-24B-045"],"source":"Lennox G41UF Merit Series Engineering Data, Bulletin 210369, Feb 2004 — https://tech.lennoxintl.com/C03e7o14l/VIu12Ch2uV/ehb_g41uf_0402.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Single-pipe / non-direct vent only","body":"G41UF draws combustion air from indoors (2-in. or 3-in. PVC exhaust only, no intake pipe). It is NOT a direct-vent (2-pipe) furnace — that's the G43UF successor. Confirm before quoting a sealed-combustion install."},{"title":"Manifold pressure derates with altitude (natural gas only)","body":"3.5 in. w.c. at 0-4500 ft., stepping down to 3.1 in. w.c. at 6501-7500 ft. LPG/Propane stays fixed at 10.0 in. w.c. regardless of altitude. See Table on Page 6 of the bulletin for the full 4-tier breakdown."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — Natural Gas (0-4500 ft.)","value":"3.5 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LPG/Propane","value":"10.0 in. w.c. (all altitudes)","key":true},{"label":"High altitude pressure switch kit","value":"Required above 4500 ft. on -090/-110 models; all models require it 7501-10,000 ft."},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot-surface igniter, 20-second warm-up"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"25-55°F to 50-80°F depending on model size — see rating plate","key":true},{"label":"High static (CSA)","value":"0.50 in. w.g. (all sizes)"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Not furnished — field-provided, side or bottom return"}]},{"title":"Venting/Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Exhaust","value":"2 in. PVC (up to -60D size), min. equivalent vent length 15 ft."},{"label":"Condensate trap","value":"Field-installed, can be relocated up to remote per accessory kit; primary + secondary limit on 90/110/135 models"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Low-flame flash code below 0.18 µA (replace flame sense rod); minimum flame sense current 0.16-0.17 µA. NOTE: this older G41UF board uses a MUCH lower flame threshold than G40/G43 (1.5 µA) — do not cross-apply. (Lennox II 504645M-01)","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"G43UF","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Up to 92.1% AFUE, direct (2-pipe) or non-direct (1-pipe) vent condensing upflow, Merit series — G41UF successor","match":["G43UF","G43","G43UF-24B-045"],"source":"Lennox G43UF Merit Series Engineering Data, Bulletin 210394, Dec 2008 — https://tech.lennoxintl.com/C03e7o14l/VIu12Ch2uV/ehb_g43uf_0812.pdf","flags":[{"title":"AFUE varies 90.0-92.1% by model","body":"Not every G43UF size/config hits 92.1%. Some (e.g. -24B-070, and the Canada-only \"H\" suffix models) are rated 90.0%. Check the specific model suffix on the rating plate before quoting an efficiency number."},{"title":"Can run either Direct Vent or Non-Direct Vent","body":"Unlike the G41UF, this unit supports true 2-pipe direct vent (sealed combustion) as well as 1-pipe non-direct. Confirm which configuration is installed before troubleshooting combustion-air complaints."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — Natural Gas","value":"3.5 in. w.c. (all sizes/models)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LPG/Propane","value":"10.0 in. w.c. (all sizes/models)","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"SureLight hot-surface igniter (silicon nitride), 20-second warm-up, energized ~95 VAC"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"90.0% or 92.1% depending on model — see rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"30-60°F to 50-80°F depending on model size — see rating plate","key":true},{"label":"High static (CSA)","value":"0.50 in. w.g. (all sizes)"}]},{"title":"Venting","rows":[{"label":"Intake/Exhaust","value":"2 in. PVC (most sizes) or 3 in. PVC (60D-135), both same diameter","key":true},{"label":"Configuration","value":"Direct Vent (2-pipe, sealed combustion) or Non-Direct Vent (1-pipe) — field selectable"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or greater. Below 1.5 µA = low-flame fast-flash code (replace flame sense rod). Minimum flame sense current 0.5 µA. (Lennox II 506497-01)","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"G71MPP","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"95% AFUE variable-capacity (1% increments), variable-speed, direct-vent-only, Dave Lennox Signature Collection","match":["G71MPP","G71"],"source":"Lennox G71MPP Dave Lennox Signature Collection Engineering Data, Bulletin 210507, Feb 2010 — https://tech.lennoxintl.com/C03e7o14l/VIu12Ch2uV/ehb_g71mpp_1002.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Variable-capacity gas valve — TWO manifold pressures, not one","body":"Manifold pressure is 3.5 in. w.c. (Nat) / 10.0 in. w.c. (LP) at MAXIMUM input, but drops to only 0.7 in. w.c. (Nat) / 2.0 in. w.c. (LP) at MINIMUM input (~40% turndown). Confirm which firing rate the furnace is on before condemning a pressure reading."},{"title":"Direct Vent (2-pipe) ONLY","body":"This furnace cannot be installed non-direct-vent — combustion air always comes from outdoors via a dedicated intake pipe. There is no 1-pipe configuration."},{"title":"iComfort control — diagnostic LED + DIP switches","body":"7-segment LED shows staging/status; single-stage, two-stage, or icomfort Touch communicating thermostat all change staging behavior via DIP switches (2-stage, 3-stage, or full variable-capacity mode). Verify DIP switch config matches the installed thermostat type before troubleshooting short-cycling."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — Max input (Nat / LP)","value":"3.5 in. w.c. / 10.0 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — Min input (Nat / LP)","value":"0.7 in. w.c. / 2.0 in. w.c.","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"95.0% (all four installation orientations)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise — Max input","value":"50-80°F to 60-90°F depending on model size"},{"label":"Temperature rise — Min input","value":"40-70°F (all model sizes)"},{"label":"High static (CSA)","value":"0.80 in. w.g. — higher than fixed-speed furnaces, note when sizing static budget","key":true}]},{"title":"Venting","rows":[{"label":"Configuration","value":"Direct Vent (2-pipe) only, 2 in. PVC (most sizes) or 3 in. PVC (60D-135)"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Communicating SureLight board — no field microamp spec published. Low flame is reported as fault code E 270 (\"Low flame current\"); measure HSI resistance per the install instructions. (Lennox II 506509-01)","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"G10 / G11 / G12 / G16 / G17 / G19 / G20 / G23 / G24M / G27M / G29M / G25MV (legacy)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Discontinued standing-pilot / early-electronic-ignition G-series (documentation gap — no service figures published)","match":["G10","G11","G12","G16","G17","G19","G20","G23","G24M","G27M","G29M","G25MV","AF80","AF90","AF92","Aire-Flo AF80","Aire-Flo AF90","Aire-Flo AF92"],"source":"No current Lennox Engineering Data or Installation Instructions bulletin was located for these discontinued platforms on tech.lennoxintl.com, lennox.com, or manualslib.com in this research pass.","flags":[{"title":"No published maintenance figures found — work from the rating plate","body":"These are pre-2000s (some pre-1990s) standing-pilot or early hot-surface-ignition furnaces, including the Lennox-family Aire-Flo AF80/AF90/AF92 badge. Manifold pressure, temperature rise, and input/output for the specific unit are stamped on the rating plate inside the burner compartment door. If a printed installation/service manual is on-site or in the customer's paperwork, use it and photograph the rating plate for the record — do not guess a number from a similar-looking newer model."}]},
  {"brand":"Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane","model":"A96UHMV / A96DFMV","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96% modulating variable-speed condensing furnace (upflow/downflow)","match":["A96UHMV","A96DFMV","A96UH","A96DF","A96MV"],"source":"Allied Air A96UHMV Installation Instructions, Form 506550-01 Issue 1028 — https://s7d2.scene7.com/is/content/AlliedAirEnterprises/FLAGSHIP_GASFURNACES_A96MV-UPFLOW_INSTALLATIONMANUALpdf","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure table not machine-readable — read from the manual","body":"Tables 22-24 (form 506550-01, p.49-50) give the modulating low-fire/high-fire in.w.c. values by rate; the source PDF's table digits did not extract cleanly and were NOT guessed. Confirm the actual numbers from Table 22-24 or the rating plate."},{"title":"Altitude threshold differs from the A97/A98 modulating platforms","body":"This unit (older Issue 1028 printing) states no manifold pressure adjustment is required only up to 7,500 ft — the A97MV/A98MV modulating platforms state 10,000 ft. Verify against the issue date/rating plate on the actual unit; a reprinted manual may have updated this."},{"title":"No flame-signal microamp spec found — only Installation Instructions exist for this platform","body":"A96UHMV/A96DFMV (Issue 1028, an older printing) uses the same \"A92 Integrated Control\" board shown on the A97USMV, A97US2V, and A98USMV wiring diagrams, which DO publish Flame Signal in Microamps (Normal ≥2.6, Low ≤2.5, Drop Out 1.1) and a silicon-nitride ignitor spec (39-70 Ω, 120VAC) in their own Service Manuals. No A96UHMV/A96DFMV Service Manual was found on Allied Air's scene7 CDN, manualslib, or elsewhere to confirm the same numbers apply to this specific board revision/platform — do not assume they match without verifying against the rating plate or a pulled control-board spec sheet. Do not add a flame-µA number until an A96UHMV-specific source is found."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Firing rate","value":"Modulating, 35% (low) to 100% (high)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"See Table 22-24 in install manual (rate + altitude dependent) — do not adjust gas valve"},{"label":"Altitude","value":"No manifold adjustment 0-7,500 ft; pressure switch/orifice kit required 7,501-10,000 ft (Table 24)"},{"label":"Pressure switch","value":"Combustion-air-inducer switch is factory set, no field adjustment — no in. w.c. trip number is published in the Installation Instructions"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See rating plate; set blower speed at 100% firing rate","key":true}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot surface, called \"Ignitor\" in Allied Air literature — material/cold-resistance not published in this unit's Installation Instructions (no Service Manual exists for this platform)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane","model":"A97USMV / A97DSMV","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"97% MODULATING variable-speed condensing furnace (upflow/downflow) — not the two-stage A97US2V","match":["A97USMV","A97DSMV","A97UH","A97MV"],"source":"Allied Air A97USMV Installation Instructions, Form 507028-05 Issue 2241 — https://s7d2.scene7.com/is/content/AlliedAirEnterprises/1%20-%20Document%20Updates/FLAGSHIP_GASFURNACES_A97MV-UPFLOW_INSTALLATIONMANUAL.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single manifold pressure number — it modulates","body":"Table 25 gives 3 setpoints (40/70/100% rate); Table 26 gives the low-fire(35%)/high-fire(100%) range used for field checks. Gas valve is not field-adjustable."},{"title":"Pressure switch self-calibrates per installation — it is not a simple fixed trip point","body":"The A92 control runs a Vent Calibration routine (RPM ramp test against the low-fire and high-fire pressure switches) on first call for heat and after venting changes; the 1.00″/0.25″ w.c. figures in Table 18 are the switch set points, not a field-adjustable manifold-style number. See Service Manual pages 28-30 for the calibration sequence and E228/E276 fault codes if calibration fails."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — low fire (35% rate)","value":"0.40-0.60\" NG / 1.2-1.8\" LP","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — high fire (100% rate)","value":"3.2-3.8\" NG / 9.5-10.5\" LP","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — 40/70/100% rate (Table 25, normal)","value":"NG 0.6\" / 1.9\" / 3.5\" — LP 1.6\" / 5.5\" / 10.0\""},{"label":"Gas orifice size (Table 26)","value":"NG .0625\" / LP .034\""},{"label":"Altitude","value":"Manifold pressure unchanged 0-10,000 ft; LP kit 68W77 (all altitudes); pressure switch kit 14T65 required 7,501-10,000 ft"},{"label":"Pressure switch — combustion air inducer (high/low fire set point)","value":"High Fire 1.00±0.05″ w.c. — Low Fire 0.25±0.05″ w.c. (Table 18, 0-7,500 ft; factory calibrated per-installation via the control's vent-calibration routine, not a fixed field-adjustable switch)","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See rating plate; adjust blower speed at 100% firing rate","key":true}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Normal ≥2.6 µA DC — Low ≤2.5 µA — Drop Out 1.1 µA (Table 17). Check via Field Test Mode on the integrated control (push-button menu displays live flame signal), or a DC-microamp meter at the flame-sense terminal.","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride, cold resistance 39-70 Ω (ohm 4-pin plug terminals 2-4 at the control, or the 2-pin jack near the manifold); control supplies 120VAC to igniter but pulses/controls it — use a true RMS meter, a standard digital meter will read low"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"S47, SPST N.C. manual-reset, trips (opens) at 210°F — not adjustable"},{"label":"CO2 — high fire (100% rate)","value":"7.6-8.6% NG / 9.1-10.1% LP"},{"label":"CO2 — low fire (35-40% rate)","value":"5.7% NG / 7.2-8.2% LP (070 size); 5.3-6.3% NG / 6.8-7.8% LP (090/110/135)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane","model":"A97US2V / A97DS2V","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"97% TWO-STAGE variable-speed condensing furnace (upflow/downflow) — a different platform from the modulating A97USMV","match":["A97US2V","A97DS2V","A97US2VK","A97DS2VK","A972V"],"source":"Allied Air A97US2V Installation Instructions, Form 508362-01 Issue 2336 — https://s7d2.scene7.com/is/content/AlliedAirEnterprises/Product%20Materials%20Library/Installation%20&%20Service%20Manuals/Gas%20Furnaces/FLAGSHIP_GASFURNACES_A972V-107046-XX-UPFLOW_INSTALLATIONMANUAL.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure DOES change with altitude on this platform","body":"Unlike the A96/A97MV/A98MV modulating furnaces (manifold fixed 0-10,000 ft), this two-stage unit's Table 19 gives 5 separate altitude bands (0-4500 / 4501-5500 / 5501-6500 / 6501-7500 / 7501-10000 ft) each with its own low-fire/high-fire NG and LP psi. Read the row for the actual install altitude."},{"title":"A97US2VK is a later control-board revision, not re-verified separately","body":"Form 508623-01 (scene7) covers the 'K' revision of this same two-stage platform. Match alias added, but its manifold/pressure-switch figures were not independently pulled for this entry — cross-check 508623-01 if the unit nameplate reads A97US2VK/A97DS2VK."},{"title":"Two different pressure figures on this entry — don't confuse them","body":"The existing altitude-banded rows (\"Manifold pressure 0-4,500 ft\" etc.) are GAS manifold pressure at the burner. The new \"Pressure switch\" row above is the COMBUSTION-AIR INDUCER switch set point (0.25″/1.00″ w.c.), a completely separate measurement point — don't cross-reference them when troubleshooting."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure 0-4,500 ft","value":"Low 1.7\" / High 3.5\" NG — Low 4.5\" / High 10.0\" LP","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure 4,501-5,500 ft","value":"Low 1.6\" / High 3.3\" NG — Low 4.2\" / High 9.4\" LP"},{"label":"Manifold pressure 5,501-6,500 ft","value":"Low 1.5\" / High 3.2\" NG — Low 4.0\" / High 9.1\" LP"},{"label":"Manifold pressure 6,501-7,500 ft","value":"Low 1.5\" / High 3.1\" NG — Low 3.9\" / High 8.9\" LP"},{"label":"Manifold pressure 7,501-10,000 ft","value":"Low 1.7\" / High 3.5\" NG — Low 4.5\" / High 10.0\" LP"},{"label":"Supply line pressure (Table 19)","value":"NG 4.5-13.0\" w.c. / LP 11.0-13.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Altitude kits","value":"Size-specific burner orifice + pressure switch kits above 4,500 ft (Table 20); pressure switch factory-set, no adjustment, 0-4,500 ft"},{"label":"Pressure switch — combustion air inducer (high/low fire set point)","value":"High Fire 1.00±0.05″ w.c. — Low Fire 0.25±0.05″ w.c. — this is the switch set point (see flag on the manifold-pressure-by-altitude rows already on this entry — those are a separate measurement)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See rating plate; adjust blower speed to maintain range (Table 16 heating speeds)","key":true}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Normal ≥2.6 µA DC — Low ≤2.5 µA — Drop Out 1.1 µA (same A92 Integrated Control platform/table as A97USMV and A98USMV)","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride, cold resistance 39-70 Ω; control supplies 120VAC but pulses/controls voltage — use a true RMS meter (digital averaging meters read low)"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"SPST N.C. manual-reset, trips (opens) at 210°F — not adjustable"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane","model":"A98MV / A98MVK","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"98% modulating variable-speed condensing furnace (upflow/downflow)","match":["A98MV","A98MVK","A98USMV","A98DSMV","A98USMVK","A98DSMVK"],"source":"Allied Air A98USMV Service Manual, Form 508420-01 Issue 2346 — https://s7d2.scene7.com/is/content/AlliedAirEnterprises/Product%20Materials%20Library/Installation%20&%20Service%20Manuals/Gas%20Furnaces/FLAGSHIP_GASFURNACES_A98MV-UPFLOW_SERVICEMANUAL.pdf","flags":[{"title":"\"A98MVK\" naming assumed, not independently confirmed in this document","body":"The pulled service manual (508420-01) covers A98USMV/A98DSMV. The 'K' control-board-revision suffix follows the same naming convention Allied Air uses on the A97US2V/A97US2VK platform, but a separate A98MVK document was not located/opened — verify against unit rating plate if servicing a K-suffix unit."},{"title":"Confirmed via cross-platform match, not a full direct read of 508420-01","body":"The 508420-01 PDF would not extract as readable text in this research pass; the flame-µA/igniter/pressure-switch figures above were confirmed instead by (1) a targeted search excerpt of 508420-01 itself quoting \"silicon nitride...39 to 70 ohms,\" and (2) full, independently-read A97USMV (508146-01) and A97US2V (508416-01) Service Manuals — same \"A92 Integrated Control\" platform — which publish byte-identical Table 17/18-style figures. High confidence, but flagging that A98MV's own document wasn't fully read start-to-finish."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — low fire (35% rate)","value":"0.40-0.60\" NG / 1.2-1.8\" LP","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — high fire (100% rate)","value":"3.2-3.8\" NG / 9.5-10.5\" LP","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — 35/70/100% rate (normal)","value":"NG 0.6\" / 1.9\" / 3.5\" — LP 1.6\" / 5.5\" / 10.0\""},{"label":"Gas orifice size","value":"NG .0625\" / LP .034\""},{"label":"CO2 — high fire","value":"7.6-8.6% NG / 9.1-10.1% LP"},{"label":"Altitude","value":"Manifold pressure unchanged 0-10,000 ft; LP kit 68W77 (all altitudes); pressure switch kit 14T65 required 7,501-10,000 ft"},{"label":"Pressure switch — combustion air inducer (high/low fire set point)","value":"High Fire 1.00±0.05″ w.c. — Low Fire 0.25±0.05″ w.c., 0-7,500 ft (14T65 high-altitude switch kit required 7,501-10,000 ft)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See rating plate \"TEMP. RISE °F\"; set blower speed accordingly","key":true}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Normal ≥2.6 µA DC — Low ≤2.5 µA — Drop Out 1.1 µA (same A92 Integrated Control flame-signal table published on the A97USMV/A97US2V service manuals for this control platform)","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride, cold resistance 39-70 Ω; 120VAC supplied but pulsed/controlled — use a true RMS meter"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"SPST N.C. manual-reset, trips (opens) at 210°F — not adjustable"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane","model":"A95UH / A95DF","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"95% single-stage condensing furnace (upflow/downflow), PSC blower on -1D, constant-torque ECM on -1E","match":["A95UH","A95DF","A95UH1D","A95DF1D","A95UH1E","A95DF1E","A93UH","A93UH1D","95G1UH","92G1UH"],"source":"Allied Air A95UH/A93UH/95G1UH/92G1UH Installation Instructions, Form 506724-01 Issue 1108 — https://www.afsupply.com/pub/media/catalog/product/matridtech/armstrong_air/installation/ARMA95UH1D110C20A.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Source document covers the -1D (PSC) variant only","body":"506724-01 is titled for A95UH1D/A93UH1D/95G1UH/92G1UH. The -1E constant-torque ECM variant was not independently pulled/verified for this entry — confirm blower type (PSC vs ECM) from the model suffix/rating plate before assuming PSC-specific service steps."},{"title":"Source is the -1E (ECM) variant; existing entry's other source (506724-01) is the -1D (PSC) variant","body":"This entry already cites Allied Air form 506724-01 for the A95UH1D/A93UH1D PSC variant, which did not publish the flame-µA/igniter/pressure-switch figures. The figures above come from the -1E (constant-torque ECM) service manual (508093-01) instead — both use the same \"Integrated Ignition Control (A92)\" hot-surface ignition system per their own service literature, so the flame-signal/igniter/rollout figures are very likely identical across -1D and -1E, but this was not independently verified against a -1D-specific service manual. Confirm blower type (PSC vs ECM) from the model suffix/rating plate; that only affects blower wiring/troubleshooting, not the gas/ignition figures above."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (single-stage, all sizes)","value":"3.5\" NG / 10.0\" LP","key":true},{"label":"Supply line pressure","value":"NG 4.5-10.5\" w.c. / LP 11.0-13.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Altitude","value":"No manifold change 0-10,000 ft; pressure switch (Table 12) and burner orifice kits change above 4,500 ft"},{"label":"Pressure switch — combustion air inducer (differential, factory set, non-adjustable)","value":"030/045: -0.65″ w.c. (0-7,500 ft), -0.60″ (7,501-10,000 ft) — 070/090/110/135: -0.90″ to -0.80″ w.c. (0-7,500 ft), -0.65″ (7,501-10,000 ft) — size-specific, see Table 6"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See rating plate","key":true}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Normal ≥1.5 µA DC — Low 0.5-1.4 µA — Drop Out ≤0.4 µA. NOTE: this single-stage platform's A92 control uses a DIFFERENT flame-signal table than the A97/A98 modulating/two-stage furnaces (which read Normal ≥2.6/Low ≤2.5/Drop Out 1.1) — do not cross-apply.","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Nitride ignitor (proprietary ceramic), cold resistance 39-70 Ω across the 4-pin plug terminals 2 & 4; voltage 102-132VAC (120V ±10%) during the 20-sec warm-up — use a true RMS meter or ohm it"},{"label":"Flame rollout switch","value":"S47, SPST N.C. manual-reset, factory preset to open at 210°F +12°F (99°C +6.7°C) on temperature rise"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane","model":"7AH1 / 7AH2","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Cased coil / air handler family — AC (PSC), AE (constant-torque), AV (variable-speed), RE (R454B) motor variants","match":["7AH1","7AH2","7AH1AE","7AH1AC","7AH1AV","7AH1RE","7AH2AE"],"source":"Allied Air 7AH1AE Installation Instructions, Form 508441-01 Issue 2516 — https://s7d2.scene7.com/is/content/AlliedAirEnterprises/RESI_AIRHANDLERS_7AH1AE-71_INSTALLATIONMANUAL.pdf","flags":[{"title":"2\" trap is mandatory on the primary drain — negative-pressure coil","body":"The drain sits on the negative-pressure (suction) side of the blower. Without a field-installed 2\" trap in the primary line, the blower pulls air through the condensate line and the pan will not drain — this is the #1 no-cool/water-damage callback on this platform."},{"title":"Variant manuals not individually verified","body":"AC (PSC, 508440-01), AV (variable-speed, 508442-01) and RE (R454B, 508798-01) each have their own form number; only AE (508441-01) and the 7AH2AE product page were pulled for this entry. Trap/drain-pan guidance is confirmed for AE — treat AC/AV/RE the same unless the specific manual says otherwise."}],"groups":[{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Primary drain trap","value":"2\" trap required, as close to unit as practical, top of trap below drain-pan connection","key":true},{"label":"Horizontal drain pan","value":"Reversible front-to-back for left/right air discharge (rotate 180°, swap drain plugs)"}]},{"title":"Metering","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Factory-installed TXV (cooling TXV, \"CTXV\")","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Minimum airflow (RDS/A2L mitigation floor)","value":"350 CFM/ton","key":true},{"label":"Blower speed taps (5-tap direct-drive ECM)","value":"Tap 1: continuous/low-speed fan (2-speed HP/AC), energized by 24V at G. Tap 2: lower-tonnage speed, 1/2 ton below nominal at 0.5\" static (e.g. 3-ton set to 1000 CFM). Tap 3: cooling speed, 400 CFM/nominal ton at 0.5\" static. Tap 4: electric heat — 400 SCFM/ton at 0.5\" static, minimum setting for heat, energized on a heater call, 120-sec OFF delay (vs. 45-sec on the other taps). Tap 5: high-static applications, 1/2 ton above nominal at 0.5\" static.","key":true},{"label":"Filter size","value":"-024/-030: 15\" x 20\" x 1\"; -036/-042/-048/-060: 18\" x 20\" x 1\" — 1\" throwaway, field-installed (not factory furnished)"}]},{"title":"Heat","rows":[{"label":"Electric heat kit range","value":"4, 5, 7.5, 10, 12.5, 15, 20 kW field-installed kits; a jumper is required for single-stage operation on the 12.5kW and 20kW kits","key":true}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane","model":"EFV","equip":"Electric Furnace","summary":"Variable-speed ECM electric furnace / modular air handler with field-installed heat kit","match":["EFV","EFV08BCP","EFV12BCP","EFV16CCP","EFV20DCP"],"source":"Allied Air EFV Electric Furnace Installation Instructions, Form 506265-03 (0650329-56) Issue 1924 — https://s7d2.scene7.com/is/content/AlliedAirEnterprises/1%20-%20Document%20Updates/RESI_ELECTRICFURNACES_EFV_INSTALLATIONMANUAL.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Never remove line power from the variable-speed motor for storage/idle — only during service","body":"The ECM contains DC filter capacitors that surge on power-up. Leave AC power applied to the motor at all times except while actively servicing it, and never install a blower relay that interrupts line voltage to the motor — this can damage the motor control board."},{"title":"2\" trap required on primary drain (negative-pressure side of blower)","body":"Same negative-pressure drain design as the 7AH air handlers — a proper trap is required or the pan will not drain."}],"groups":[{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Primary drain trap","value":"2\" trap required in primary line, below bottom of drain pan","key":true}]},{"title":"Air / Blower","rows":[{"label":"Airflow target","value":"350-450 CFM per ton of cooling capacity (min. 350 CFM/ton)","key":true},{"label":"CFM taps","value":"ADJUST(+) raises table CFM 10%; ADJUST(-) lowers it 12%; TEST runs motor at 70% for troubleshooting"},{"label":"Continuous blower","value":"50% of normal airflow, 350 CFM minimum"},{"label":"Dehumidify mode","value":"10% reduced airflow when HUM terminal sees a closed-to-open humidistat signal"},{"label":"Soft start","value":"Ramps to full speed over up to 7.5 minutes"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Voltage","value":"208-240V single phase; factory-wired 240V — move black transformer lead to 208V terminal if needed"},{"label":"Heat kit","value":"Field heat-kit install discards the factory plug-in high-voltage harness; connections move to the heater kit's field wire points"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Payne","model":"PG9MAB","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"90%+ AFUE 4-way multipoise fixed-capacity condensing gas furnace, 2-pipe direct-vent or 1-pipe non-direct-vent (sizes 040-120 only), sizes 040-140","match":["PG9MAB","PG9M","PG9MAA","PG9"],"source":"Payne PG9MAB Installation, Start-Up and Operating Instructions, Sizes 040-140 Series B & C — Catalog No. IM-PG9MAB-05 — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0D/IM-PG9MAB-05.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single manifold pressure number","body":"Table 14 (040-120 sizes, 20,000 Btuh/burner basis) or Table 15 (140 size only, 23,000 Btuh/burner basis) key orifice size + manifold pressure to installation altitude, average gas heat value, and specific gravity. At sea level the approved range is 3.2-3.8 in. W.C.; above 2000 ft it can be adjusted as low as 2.0 in. W.C. Never bottom out the regulator screw."},{"title":"PG9MAA is an earlier series — verify before applying these tables","body":"This entry's figures come from the current PG9MAB (Series B/C) literature. PG9MAA is an earlier PG9M-family unit; confirm the actual orifice/manifold table and control-board type against that unit's rating plate before assuming PG9MAB data applies as-is."},{"title":"Condensate trap must be primed","body":"Trap has 2 internal chambers and will not drain correctly unless primed with ~1 qt of water into the inducer drain side before first firing. Condensate is mildly acidic (pH ~3.2-4.5)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"Table 14/15, by altitude + gas heat value + specific gravity (3.2-3.8\" W.C. at sea level)","key":true},{"label":"Gas supply pressure","value":"4.5-14 in. W.C. (0.16-0.5 psig)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"US: 2%/1000 ft above 2000 ft; Canada: 5% flat, 2000-4500 ft"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See furnace rating plate — varies by size","key":true},{"label":"Return air temp","value":"60°F min continuous (55°F intermittent) to 80°F max"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"LED status codes","value":"2-digit flash (short-long): 11 no fault, 13 limit lockout, 14 ignition lockout, 21 gas heating lockout, 31/23 pressure switch fault, 33 limit circuit fault, 34 ignition proving failure, 45 control lockout","key":true},{"label":"Rapid continuous flash","value":"Reversed 115V polarity or ungrounded control"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot surface igniter, normal operating temperature exceeds 2000°F (1093°C). Cold reading should be 40 to 70 ohms at room temperature, measured across both igniter leads with power off.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Payne","model":"PG8MAA / PG8JAA","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage 4-way multipoise non-condensing gas furnace with HSI ignition and LED diagnostics (PG8JAA = Low NOx California variant)","match":["PG8MAA","PG8JAA","PG8M","PG8J","PG80","PG8"],"source":"Payne PG8MAA/PG8JAA Series G Installation, Start-Up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions — Catalog No. IM-PG8J-17 — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0D/IM-PG8J-17.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single manifold pressure number","body":"Table 14 (standard, all PG8MAA + PG8JAA in upflow, 22,000 Btuh/burner basis) or Table 15 (PG8JAA Low NOx in downflow/horizontal only, 21,000 Btuh/burner basis) key orifice size + manifold pressure to altitude, gas heat value, and specific gravity. Sea-level range is 3.2-3.8 in. W.C.; orifice #43 is factory-installed on most sizes — verify, never assume."},{"title":"Temperature rise range varies widely by size","body":"Certified rise ranges from 20-50°F on the smallest unit up to 50-80°F on the largest — always use the range printed on that specific unit's rating plate, not a single number."},{"title":"LED diagnostic codes","body":"2-digit flash codes: 11 no fault, 12 blower-on after power-up, 13 limit lockout, 14 ignition lockout, 21 gas heating lockout, 22 abnormal flame-proving, 23/31 pressure switch fault, 24 secondary fuse open, 33 limit circuit fault, 34 ignition proving failure. Rapid continuous flash = reversed 115V polarity."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"Table 14/15, by altitude + gas heat value + specific gravity (3.2-3.8\" W.C. at sea level)","key":true},{"label":"Gas supply pressure","value":"4.5-13.6 in. W.C. (natural gas)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"Input reduced 4%/1000 ft above 2000 ft; Canada 10% flat, 2000-4500 ft"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See furnace rating plate — 20-80°F range across sizes","key":true},{"label":"Blower off delay","value":"Selectable 90/120/150/180 sec, factory-set 120 sec"},{"label":"Filter","value":"External filter rack required — no internal filter provision"}]},{"title":"Venting","rows":[{"label":"Category","value":"Category I fan-assisted, single-wall or Type B vent, 4\" standard connector"},{"label":"Masonry chimney","value":"Requires factory Chimney Adapter Kit — see rating plate for kit number"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"CNPVP / CNPVT","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Cased upflow/downflow N-coil evaporator coil, factory-installed refrigerant-specific TXV, 1.5-5 ton (CNPVT = transition-width variant for one-size-smaller furnace)","match":["CNPVP","CNPVT","CNPVU","CNRVU","CNPV","CNRV","CN*VU"],"source":"Carrier CNPVP, CNPVT, CNPVU, CNRVU Evaporator Coil (N Coil — Cased and Uncased, Upflow/Downflow) Product Data — Catalog No. SS-CNPV-05 — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/08/SS-CNPV-05.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single static pressure number","body":"Dry/wet coil static pressure drop varies by unit size and CFM — see Product Data Table 5 (ranges roughly 0.02-0.54 in. W.C. across the line). Check it before assuming the system blower can handle the coil + duct static."},{"title":"TXV is refrigerant-specific","body":"P models (CNPVP/CNPVT/CNPVU) = Puron/R-410A TXV; R models (CNRVU) = R-22 TXV. Do not mix — factory TXV is matched to the refrigerant in the nomenclature."}],"groups":[{"title":"Coil","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"Puron/R-410A (P models) or R-22 (R models)","key":true},{"label":"TXV","value":"Factory-installed, refrigerant-specific, rated at 10°F superheat leaving coil"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"018 through 061 (1-1/2 to 5 ton)"}]},{"title":"Maintenance","rows":[{"label":"Coil access","value":"Slides out of cabinet after removing access door and service panel","key":true},{"label":"Condensate","value":"Corrosion-resistant sloped drain pan, two 3/4\" female-threaded brass drain connections"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"45MUAA","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Comfort Crossover ducted ductless-style air handler for mini-split systems, sizes 18K-60K, R-454B (A2L mildly flammable) refrigerant","match":["45MUAA","45MUAAQ","45MUAAQ18","45MUAAQ24","45MUAAQ30","45MUAAQ36","45MUAAQ48","45MUAAQ60","45MU"],"source":"Carrier 45MUAA(Q) Crossover Air Handler Owner's Manual, Sizes 18K-60K — Catalog No. 45MUAA-02OM — https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1009/Public/0F/45MUAA-02OM.pdf","flags":[{"title":"R-454B is mildly flammable (A2L)","body":"Servicing requires certified refrigerant-handling training per the manual — no open flame/ignition sources near the unit; do not puncture refrigerant tubing."},{"title":"Extensive error-code list — look up the exact code","body":"EC/EH/EL/PC/FL-prefixed codes cover dozens of faults (e.g., EL0C = system lacks refrigerant, EHC1/EHC2/EHC3 = refrigerant-leak sensor faults). See Owner's Manual Table 7 rather than guessing from memory."}],"groups":[{"title":"System","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-454B (A2L, mildly flammable)","key":true},{"label":"Pairs with","value":"37MUHAQ or 37MURAQ mini-split outdoor condensers, matched by tonnage suffix (e.g. 45MUAAQ24 with 37MUHAQ24AA3)"}]},{"title":"Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Nominal CFM by size","value":"18K/24K: 400 CFM; 30K: 447 CFM; 36K: 541 CFM; 48K: 706 CFM; 60K: 795 CFM","key":true}]},{"title":"Maintenance","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Inspect monthly; clean or replace every 30-90 days depending on thickness/MERV"},{"label":"Coil dust removal","value":"Automatic: on shutoff, outdoor fan reverses for ~70 sec after a 10-sec delay to blow loose dust off the outdoor coil (does not replace manual cleaning)"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Carrier / Bryant","model":"38-Series Legacy Split (documentation-limited)","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Discontinued legacy split-system AC/heat pump condensers (38TX, 38TD, 38YC, 38YZ and similar), mostly R-22 fixed-orifice, circa 1990s-2000s — no current OEM service literature located","match":["38TX","38TD","38YC","38YZ","38-series"],"source":"No current OEM service literature located for these discontinued 38-series platforms. Work from the specific unit's rating plate and any printed installation/service manual shipped with it; do not carry over figures from any modern Carrier/Bryant AC or heat pump entry — today's electronic multi-stage/variable-speed platforms are not the same metering/control system.","flags":[{"title":"No verified service figures for this platform","body":"These are old, largely R-22, fixed-orifice systems on a different platform than every other Carrier/Bryant entry in this library. Get charge, superheat/subcooling target, and airflow from the rating plate and any onboard nameplate charging chart — do not estimate from a similar-looking modern unit."}]},
  {"brand":"ICP","model":"N96MSN / N96VSN","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96% AFUE single-stage gas valve, 4-way multipoise condensing furnace; N96MSN = multi-speed ECM blower, N96VSN = variable-speed ECM blower","match":["N96MSN","N96VSN","N96M","N96V","N96"],"source":"Carrier/ICP N96MSN Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions, Catalog No. N96MSN-01SI REV D, Edition 06/23 — https://hvacdirect.com/media/pdf/ACiQ%20N96MSN%20Installation%20Manual.pdf (mirrors: tempstar.com/comfortmaker.com/heil-hvac.com/arcoaire.com product pages for N96MSN and N96VSN)","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure is a lookup, not a fixed number","body":"Table 25 (all standard models) and Table 26 (26,000 BTUh low-capacity model ONLY, capped at 1.8 in. w.c.) key manifold pressure + orifice size to installed altitude, local gas heating value, and specific gravity. The 26,000 BTUh model is identified by a green label on the gas valve solenoid — using the wrong table will overfire it."},{"title":"Table pressures are already altitude-corrected — do not double-derate","body":"Table 25/26 values are AS-MEASURED AT ALTITUDE (not sea-level reference). Do not additionally apply the Table 23 percent-derate on top of the table lookup."},{"title":"Temperature rise has no single number","body":"Manual explicitly directs techs to the furnace rating plate for the rise range; recommended operating point is the midpoint of that range or slightly above."},{"title":"Nominal flame-sense range not independently confirmed for N96MSN — don't reuse the N80ESN number without checking","body":"The N96MSN's own literature publishes a 0.5 µA DC clean/minimum threshold, but this pass could not locate its normal-operating µA range (the ICP N80ESN on the same GEMINI-family control board publishes 4.0-6.0 µA DC nominal — plausible for N96MSN but NOT confirmed against N96MSN's own service literature, so it is not stated as fact here). Pull the N96MSN Service and Maintenance Instructions Troubleshooting Guide (equivalent to N80ESN Fig. 49, code 6 'Ignition Proving Failure') to confirm before quoting a normal range to a tech."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Inlet (supply) gas pressure","value":"4.5–13.6 in. w.c. NG (0.16–0.5 psig) with burners firing","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure / orifice","value":"Table 25 (standard) or Table 26 (26,000 BTUh model) — by altitude + gas heat value + specific gravity","key":true},{"label":"Altitude derate (input rate)","value":"US: −2%/1000 ft above 2000 ft; Table 23 multiplier 1.00 (0–2000 ft) down to 0.81 (9001–10,000 ft)"},{"label":"26,000 BTUh model cap","value":"Do not adjust NG manifold pressure above 1.8 in. w.c."}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See furnace rating plate — operate at midpoint of range or slightly above","key":true},{"label":"Airflow / CFM","value":"Table 18 (Air Delivery CFM with filter) and Table 19 (Airflow Settings) — model/tap specific"},{"label":"Filter media","value":"1-in. media not recommended due to pressure drop; manual recommends sizing filtration for 2-in. minimum (4-in. cabinet for future IAQ upgrades)"},{"label":"Blower-OFF delay","value":"Field-selectable 90–180 sec, factory default 120 sec"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Status/fault codes","value":"Amber LED flash-code system, Table 20 (System Status Display Codes) — covers pressure switch, limit, flame-proving, ignition, polarity, blower and gas-valve faults"},{"label":"Component self-test","value":"Ct menu on control board runs inducer/igniter/blower test sequence (Table 22) with idle thermostat inputs"},{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"Clean the flame sensor with fine steel wool if the reading is below 0.5 µA DC (published minimum/clean threshold); a normal/nominal µA figure specific to N96MSN was not located in this pass — see flag","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon Nitride hot surface igniter (direct ignition); ohms/current spec not confirmed for this model in this pass"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"ICP","model":"N80ESN / N80ESL","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage, Category I non-condensing, ECM-blower gas furnace (33-1/3 in. cabinet)","match":["N80ESN","N80ESL","N80ES"],"source":"Carrier/ICP N80ESN and N80ESL (Series A) Installation Instructions, Form 441 01 3400 02, Edition 7/12/2019 — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/2378343/Carrier-N80esn-Series.html","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure/orifice not independently confirmed","body":"The install manual publishes Table 12 (Orifice Size and Manifold Pressure, in. w.c., by gas input rate) on p.35-36, but the numeric values could not be verified from available mirrors in this pass. Pull Table 12 from the source form before adjusting — do not assume a number."},{"title":"No published temperature-rise figure confirmed","body":"Work from the furnace rating plate; the specific rise range was not confirmed from available excerpts of this manual."},{"title":"Manifold pressure/orifice table is now confirmed — prior flag in this entry can be cleared","body":"Form 441 01 3400 02 (7/12/2019), Table 12 p.35-36, publishes the full orifice-size/manifold-pressure lookup by altitude, average gas heat value, and specific gravity for standard (22,000 Btuh/burner) models; Table 13 (p.37-38) covers the Low NOx 21,000 Btuh/burner variant. At sea level with typical 1000 Btu/cu ft gas and 0.60 SG the factory-shipped setup is orifice #43 at 3.6\" w.c. — confirmed directly from the source document, not estimated."},{"title":"Temperature rise still has no published fixed number","body":"This Installation Instructions form repeatedly directs the tech to the furnace rating plate for the actual temperature-rise range and does not print a generic range or per-model table — \"see rating plate\" remains accurate, it was not simply unconfirmed research."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure / orifice","value":"Table 12, form 441 01 3400 02 — by gas input rate (values not independently confirmed, see flag)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure & orifice (confirmed, Table 12)","value":"At sea level (0-2000 ft, 1000 Btu/cu ft NG, 0.60 specific gravity): Orifice #43, manifold 3.6\" w.c. nominal (do not set below 3.2\" or above 3.8\" w.c. at sea level). Table 12 (standard, 22,000 Btuh/burner) or Table 13 (Low NOx downflow/horizontal, 21,000 Btuh/burner) key orifice + manifold pressure to installed altitude, gas heat value, and specific gravity — pull the actual row, do not assume #43/3.6\" for a different altitude or gas","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"see rating plate"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"Nominal 4.0-6.0 µA DC; clean the flame sensor with fine steel wool and recheck if current is below 0.5 µA DC (Troubleshooting Guide code 6, \"Ignition Proving Failure\")","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Hot Surface Igniter (direct ignition); resistance/current spec not published in this Installation Instructions form — verify by visible glow or continuity, or check OEM part number"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"ICP","model":"NH4A4 / NH4H4","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"R-410A horizontal-discharge split-system single-stage AC (NH4A4) / heat pump (NH4H4) — distinct chassis from the vertical N4H4 line","match":["NH4A4","NH4H4","NH4A","NH4H"],"source":"ICP NH4H4 R-410A Horizontal Split System Heat Pumps Installation Instructions, Form 428 01 9702 01, 02/25/15 — https://cdn.bakerdist.com/icp_nh4h4_en_ii.pdf (NH4A4 = same-chassis AC-only companion per icptempstarparts.com listing)","flags":[{"title":"Charging method depends on metering device","body":"TXV indoor coils: subcooling method (Table 1 delta from rating-plate value, keyed to indoor unit model + outdoor tonnage). Piston/fixed-orifice indoor coils: superheat method (Table 2 by outdoor temp + evaporator entering wet-bulb, Table 3 to convert to required suction-line temp). Do not use the outdoor unit's Heating Check Chart to adjust charge — reference only."},{"title":"Line-length charge adjustment","body":"Factory charge is for 15 ft of 3/8-in. liquid line; add/remove 0.6 oz/ft above/below 15 ft. Standard limit 80 ft equivalent length / 20 ft vertical separation — beyond that, follow the Residential Piping and Long Line Guideline (not in this document)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling (TXV) or superheat (piston) — see flag","key":true},{"label":"Factory charge / line length","value":"15 ft of 3/8 in. liquid line; 0.6 oz/ft adjustment above/below"},{"label":"Line length limits","value":"80 ft standard equivalent length / 20 ft vertical separation"},{"label":"Compressor oil","value":"POE — Mobil 3MA-POE, factory charge; replace only what is lost"},{"label":"High-pressure switch trip","value":"≈670 ± 10 psig"},{"label":"Gauge manifold rating","value":"700 psig high side / 180 psig low side (550 psig low-side retard)"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost interval","value":"Field-selectable via W1 jumper on defrost control board: 30 / 50 / 90 min accumulated compressor run time","key":true},{"label":"Max defrost period","value":"10 min (timer-limited; terminates early when defrost thermostat contacts open)"}]},{"title":"Coil","rows":[{"label":"Cleaning","value":"Blow-thru design traps dirt between fin rows — inspect monthly, flush/clean annually or as conditions require"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DR96SN","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Single-stage multi-speed ECM 96-97% AFUE condensing gas furnace (R-32 control-board era)","match":["DR96SN","DR92SN","DD96SN","DR9","DD9"],"source":"Daikin Installation Instructions for DR92SN, DR96SN & DD96SN Single-Stage Gas Furnace — Form IM-IOD-2037B — https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dd96sn/im-iod-2037b.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single temperature-rise number — it's model/tap specific","body":"Rise range differs by BTU size and blower speed tap (manual's own tables show e.g. 25-55°F and 35-65°F on different models/taps). Use the range on the rating plate / model-specific Specification Sheet table, not a generic figure."},{"title":"Final manifold pressure tolerance","body":"Once set, manifold pressure must not drift more than ±0.3\" w.c. (Natural) or +0.5\" w.c. (LP) from the specified setting. Never derate by setting pressure below spec — that causes incomplete combustion, not less heat."},{"title":"R-32 leak-sensor menu items are inert on this furnace","body":"The control board carries R-32 mitigation menu items (A2E/A2u) for use when paired with an R-32 indoor coil. This furnace itself burns gas, not refrigerant — ignore those menus unless the furnace is paired with an R-32 cased coil."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — Natural","value":"3.2 - 3.8\" w.c. (nominal 3.5\")","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — Propane","value":"9.7 - 10.3\" w.c. (nominal 10.0\")","key":true},{"label":"Inlet supply pressure — Natural","value":"4.5 - 10.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Inlet supply pressure — Propane","value":"11.0 - 13.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Adjustment","value":"Regulator screw at gas valve outlet pressure tap (White-Rodgers 36J22); CW = increase, CCW = decrease"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See rating plate / spec sheet table (model + tap specific, roughly 25-65°F across the line)","key":true},{"label":"Filter","value":"Field-supplied, required; avoid restrictive 1\" filters (>0.25\" w.c. drop) — size per manual's Minimum Recommended Filter Size chart"}]},{"title":"Altitude","rows":[{"label":"0 - 7,000 ft","value":"No derate — standard #45 orifice","key":true},{"label":"Above 7,000 ft (2134 m)","value":"Listed High Altitude Conversion Kit required (orifices + pressure switch)"},{"label":"Canada","value":"Furnace certified only to 4,500 ft"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Status display","value":"Integrated control module 2-digit alphanumeric code on LED (Main Menu \"Err\" → Option Menu \"Exx\"); last 10 faults under \"F10\"","key":true},{"label":"EE0","value":"Lockout after 3 failed ignition retries — check gas supply"},{"label":"EE1","value":"Pressure switch circuit fault (stuck closed at start, or won't close) — check hose/wiring/blower"},{"label":"EE2","value":"Induced draft blower runs continuously, no operation — blocked flue/intake/drain or weak draft blower"},{"label":"EE3","value":"Circulator blower runs continuously, no operation — open limit circuit, blocked filter/ductwork, or blower speed/motor issue"},{"label":"EE4","value":"Both blowers run continuously, no operation — short to ground in flame-sense circuit or lingering flame/slow gas valve"},{"label":"EE5","value":"Open fuse or short in low-voltage wiring"},{"label":"EE6 / EEL","value":"Weak or lost flame-sense signal — clean/realign flame sensor"},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"1-4 µA DC normal on the Integrated Ignition control (S-314-equivalent CHECKING FLAME SENSOR procedure) — confirmed via the Goodman/Amana 'GM9S92/GM9S96/GC9S96/AM9S92/AM9S96/AC9S96/VM9S96/VC9S96 Single Stage Gas Furnaces' Service and Troubleshooting manual, form RS6612022 (July 2021), p.43: 'The Integrated Ignition controls will have 1 to 4 micro-amps.' GM9S96/GC9S96 (96% AFUE, R-32, nine-speed ECM, single-stage) is the Goodman/Amana twin of this Daikin platform — confirmed by the matching model-suffix scheme (0403A/0603B/0803B/0804C/0805C/1005C/1205D) and matching heating-airflow temperature-rise ranges (see Temperature rise row below) against DR96SN's own Installation Instructions (Form IM-IOD-2037B). If low, check high-resistance wiring, sensor-to-burner gap, dirty/oxidized sensor, or poor grounding.","key":true},{"label":"Igniter","value":"NOT independently confirmed on Daikin's own DR96SN literature this pass. The Goodman/Amana twin's Service Instructions (RS6612022, S-308) lists a 115V igniter, p/n 0130F00008, 37-68 ohms cold resistance, ~17-second warm-up — but that document labels it 'silicon carbide,' while the same part number (0130F00008) is documented as Silicon Nitride HSI elsewhere in Daikin/Goodman literature (e.g. the DM92SN/DM96SN/DC96SN Service Instructions RSD6612021). Confirm the actual igniter material/type against the specific unit before ordering parts — do not assume from this cross-reference alone."}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"CAPEA","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"EEV-metered vertical cased upflow/downflow coil, FIT/ComfortNet communicating, all-aluminum","match":["CAPEA","CAPE"],"source":"Daikin CAPEA, CAPE Series Cased Coil Installation Instructions — Form IM-IO-457 — https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/cape-capea/im-io-457.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No standalone charging chart — charge from the outdoor unit's procedure","body":"The coil's metering device is an EEV driven by the coil's own PCB in communication with the matched outdoor unit, not a field-adjustable TXV. Charge the system per the matched condenser/heat pump's charging instructions — there is no separate superheat/subcool table for the coil alone."},{"title":"Partial-unit certification — do not mix-match","body":"Manual states this is a partial-unit air conditioner that must only be combined with outdoor/indoor pairings Daikin has confirmed comply with matched-system requirements. Installing it with an unconfirmed combination is not permitted."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant / Controls","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Electronic Expansion Valve (EEV) — no field superheat adjustment","key":true},{"label":"Communication","value":"4-wire data/comm bus between coil PCB, outdoor unit, and thermostat (FIT/ComfortNet)"}]},{"title":"Drain","rows":[{"label":"Primary drain","value":"Port (A) on drain pan — condensate line must attach here","key":true},{"label":"Secondary drain","value":"Port (B), optional; if installed, wire its safety switch to cut control voltage on a blocked primary drain"},{"label":"Trap","value":"Required by most local codes — draw-through applications need a trap to prevent air being pulled back through the drain line"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Display","value":"7-segment LED on coil control board","key":true},{"label":"EE","value":"Emergency mode — no 24V power to PCB, blown fuse, or PCB internal fault"},{"label":"d0","value":"Data not yet on network — populate shared data via memory card"},{"label":"70","value":"EEV disconnected / open circuit — check connector, coil resistance"},{"label":"73 / 74","value":"Liquid-side / gas-side thermistor fault"},{"label":"75","value":"Pressure sensor fault"},{"label":"76","value":"Comm loss with outdoor unit, gas furnace, or blower unit during operation"},{"label":"77","value":"Thermostat comm error — hold LEARN button 5+ sec to re-establish network"},{"label":"78","value":"Comm error with outdoor unit/furnace/blower at startup"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DP13GM / DP14GM / DP15GM / DP16GM","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"Single/two-stage gas/electric packaged rooftop unit, ~81% AFUE gas section, EEM blower","match":["DP13GM","DP14GM","DP15GM","DP16GM","DPGM"],"source":"Daikin DP14GM \"M\" Series Gas/Electric Packaged Unit Installation Instructions — Form IM-IOD-3008K — https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dp14gm---m-series/im-iod-3008k.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Confirm exact figures against DP13/15/16GM's own literature","body":"Numbers below were verified only in the DP14GM manual (IM-IOD-3008K). DP13/14/15/16GM share the same \"M\" series platform and White-Rodgers valve family per Daikin's DP13-16GM brochure, but pressures/orifices can shift with AFUE/staging — confirm against the specific unit's rating plate before final adjustment."},{"title":"Manifold pressure differs single-stage vs. two-stage models","body":"Single-stage (White-Rodgers 36G22 valve): Natural 3.2-3.8\" w.c. (nom. 3.5\"), LP 9.7-10.3\" w.c. (nom. 10.0\"). Two-stage (White-Rodgers 36G54 valve): Natural low 1.6-2.2\" w.c. (nom. 2.0\") / high 3.2-3.8\" w.c. (nom. 3.5\"); LP low 5.7-6.3\" w.c. (nom. 6.0\") / high 9.7-10.3\" w.c. (nom. 10.0\"). Manifold pressure must stay within 0.3\" w.c. of nameplate at ANY altitude — never derate by lowering it."},{"title":"Metering device varies by tonnage","body":"5-ton models use a TXV (charge by subcooling, adjust superheat at the valve). Smaller-tonnage models are fixed-orifice, factory-charged for 325 CFM/ton at AHRI test ESP (~0.15-0.28\" w.c.) — charge those by the superheat method instead."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"See flag — staged by single/two-stage valve, table above","key":true},{"label":"Adjustment","value":"Regulator cover screw at outlet pressure tap; CW = increase, CCW = decrease"},{"label":"Input rate check","value":"Time smallest gas-meter dial per revolution; INPUT = gas heating value × 3600 / sec-per-cu-ft; compare to rating plate"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Per rating plate (model/tap-specific; manual's tables span roughly 29-64°F across the tonnage line)","key":true},{"label":"Max external static (heating)","value":"0.5\" w.c."},{"label":"Blower","value":"EEM constant-torque motor, 24V low-voltage speed-tap selection"}]},{"title":"Altitude","rows":[{"label":"Above 2,000 ft","value":"Consult the DP GM spec sheet for the required orifice/kit; do not compensate by changing orifices or raising manifold pressure","key":true}]},{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Superheat formula","value":"Suction line temp − saturated suction temp"},{"label":"Subcool formula","value":"Saturated liquid temp − liquid line temp (5-ton TXV models)"},{"label":"Design targets","value":"See unit's own spec sheet / rating plate"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Display","value":"Single-stage: ignition control diagnostic LED, flash-coded","key":true},{"label":"Off","value":"Internal control failure"},{"label":"1 flash","value":"External lockout"},{"label":"2 flashes","value":"Pressure switch stuck open"},{"label":"3 flashes","value":"Pressure switch stuck closed"},{"label":"4 flashes","value":"Thermal protection device open"},{"label":"5 flashes","value":"Flame detected with gas valve closed"},{"label":"6 flashes","value":"Short-cycle compressor delay (cooling only)"},{"label":"Two-stage fault recall","value":"Hold push-button ~2 sec (NOT past 4 sec — that erases memory) to replay last 5 faults"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Daikin","model":"DP13HM / DP14HM / DP15HM / DP16HM / DP3HM","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"Packaged heat pump — DP13/14/15/16HM legacy R-410A, DP3HM current 13.4 SEER2 R-32 platform","match":["DP13HM","DP14HM","DP15HM","DP16HM","DP3HM","DPHM"],"source":"Daikin DP14HM \"M\" Series Heat Pump Installation Instructions — Form IM-IOD-3007D — https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dp14hm/im-iod-3007d.pdf ; Daikin DP3HM 13.4 SEER2 \"M\" Series R-32 Packaged Heat Pump Installation Instructions — Form IM-IOD-3035A — https://daikincomfort.com/docs/default-source/dp3hm---m-series/im-iod-3035a.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Two different refrigerant platforms share this entry — confirm rating plate","body":"DP13/14/15/16HM (R-410A, legacy): manual gives superheat/subcool formulas only, no printed design-target table — pull the numbers from that unit's own spec sheet. DP3HM (R-32, current): manual DOES publish a Design Superheat & Subcool table (see Refrigerant group) — verify the exact row for your tonnage/stage against the printed table, not this summary."},{"title":"Minimum airflow floor differs by platform","body":"Rule of thumb is ~400 (up to 425) CFM/ton on both. Floor differs: DP3HM manual says never below 300 CFM/ton; DP14HM manual says never below 350 CFM/ton."},{"title":"DP3HM has an R-32 leak-mitigation system","body":"DP3HM carries an R-32 refrigerant sensor that halts HVAC operation (keeping blower running) above 25% LFL, holds mitigation mode 5 minutes, then resumes. See Diagnostics group for the PCB LED patterns."}],"groups":[{"title":"Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Rule of thumb","value":"~400 CFM/ton, up to 425 CFM/ton","key":true},{"label":"Minimum — DP3HM","value":"Never below 300 CFM/ton"},{"label":"Minimum — DP13/14/15/16HM","value":"Never below 350 CFM/ton"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant — DP3HM (R-32)","rows":[{"label":"Design superheat/subcool","value":"Model-specific table in IM-IOD-3035A — e.g. smaller piston models ~7.5-10°F superheat (no subcool, fixed orifice); largest model uses TXV with ~16°F superheat / ~8°F subcool. Confirm exact row for your model on the printed table.","key":true},{"label":"Adjustment limit","value":"TXV screw: no more than 1 full turn CW/CCW from factory setting; wait 15 min between adjustments"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant — DP13/14/15/16HM (R-410A)","rows":[{"label":"Superheat formula","value":"Suction line temp − saturated suction temp"},{"label":"Subcool formula","value":"Saturated liquid temp − liquid line temp"},{"label":"Design targets","value":"See unit's own spec sheet / rating plate — not printed in this IM"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Timing (verified on DP3HM/PCBDM133 board)","value":"Jumper-selectable 30 / 60 / 90-minute accumulation periods","key":true},{"label":"Sensor setpoints","value":"Closes (starts accumulation) ~30°F, opens (terminates defrost) ~60°F on the outdoor-coil feeder tube"},{"label":"Override","value":"12-minute maximum defrost period if the sensor doesn't terminate it first"},{"label":"Compressor delay","value":"PCBDM133 ships with 30-sec contactor de-energize at defrost initiation/termination, plus a 3-min compressor off-cycle delay"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics — DP3HM","rows":[{"label":"Slow LED flash","value":"Normal operation","key":true},{"label":"Fast LED flash","value":"R-32 leak alarm"},{"label":"Solid LED on","value":"Delay/mitigation mode"},{"label":"2 flashes then solid","value":"Control board fault"},{"label":"3 flashes then solid","value":"R-32 sensor comm loss"},{"label":"4 flashes then solid","value":"R-32 sensor internal fault"}]}]},
  {"brand":"American Standard","model":"5A6 / 5A7","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"R-454B variable-speed split heat pump (5A6) / air conditioner (5A7)","match":["5A6","5A7","5A6V0","5A6V8","5A7A4","5A7A7"],"source":"American Standard Variable Speed R-454B Heat Pump/AC Outdoor Units Installation & Operation Manual, Form 11-BC49D1-1E-EN (Aug 2024) — https://www.denverwinair.com/literature/american-standard/submittals-heat-pumps/5A6V8X/install_11-BC49D1-1E-EN.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single subcool/superheat number","body":"Manual gives per-tonnage Subcool Charging Correction charts (line length/lift) plus a full R-454B pressure-temperature Bubble/Dew table (Table 6). Design subcooling value is on the unit rating plate — start there."},{"title":"Subcooling method requires 55°F+ outdoor","body":"Subcooling charging in cooling is not recommended below 55°F ambient. Below that, or for initial/no-power charge, use the weigh-in method."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Type","value":"R-454B (A2L, mildly flammable) — use only R-454B-approved recovery/charging equipment","key":true},{"label":"Charging method (cooling, ≥55°F OD)","value":"Subcooling to nameplate design value, corrected for line length via Table (charts by 2/3/4/5 ton)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method (superheat ref.)","value":"Use Dew Point table (Table 6) when referencing superheat instead of subcool"},{"label":"Weigh-in method","value":"Used for initial install/replacement or when power unavailable"}]},{"title":"Defrost (heat pump)","rows":[{"label":"Control type","value":"Demand Defrost — outdoor coil sensor + outdoor air sensor delta-T","key":true},{"label":"Forced defrost test","value":"Entered through thermostat / American Standard Link interface; terminates on coil temp or timeout"},{"label":"Termination temp","value":"Configurable in Link 'Environment' section — not a fixed field number"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"5HPL / 5HCL","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"R-454B variable-speed inverter side-discharge heat pump (5HPL) / cold-climate HP (5HCL)","match":["5HPL","5HCL","5HPL9","5HCL9"],"source":"Trane 5HPL9 Installer's Guide, Form DLR-SVN004A-EN (May 2025) — https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation/DLR-SVN004A-EN_05012025.pdf ; product data DLR-PSD004A-EN (5HCL9, Feb 2026) — https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation/DLR-PSD004A-EN_02152026.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Factory precharged — do not manually charge to a subcool/superheat target","body":"Refrigerant control is inverter-driven Td/SC (discharge-temp/subcooling) auto-regulation, not a field-set charge. Unit ships precharged for line sets up to 100 ft (30 m); beyond that, add R-454B per the pipe-length chart in the guide — no field subcool/superheat adjustment procedure is published."},{"title":"Defrost is automatic, no field-adjustable settings","body":"Guide does not document a defrost interval/termination table — control is fully automatic via the inverter board."},{"title":"Communicating S1/S2/S3 wiring","body":"Indoor/outdoor communication link takes ~3 minutes to start after power-up. Companion indoor unit is the 5TEM9/5TEM7 multi-position air handler, not a conventional coil."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Type","value":"R-454B, factory charged","key":true},{"label":"Additional charge","value":"Not required ≤100 ft line length; beyond that, chart-based addition (R-454B only)","key":true},{"label":"Max pipe length / height difference","value":"5HPL9036/048/060: max 50 m (165 ft) pipe length, max 30 m (100 ft) height difference. 5HPL6048/6060: max 75 m (245 ft) pipe length, max 30 m (100 ft) height difference.","key":true},{"label":"Additional charge table","value":"Published by pipe length in ~3 m increments — e.g. 5HPL6060 at 34 m (110 ft): 0.17 kg (6 oz); at 75 m (245 ft): 2.10 kg (4 lb 10 oz). No addition needed ≤30 m (100 ft). See the Installer's Guide table for the exact model/length row — do not interpolate by hand."}]},{"title":"Piping test pressure","rows":[{"label":"Leak/strength test","value":"Step-pressurize to 0.5 MPa (73 psig) → 1.5 MPa (218 psig) → 4.15 MPa (602 psig); hold 24 hrs"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Forced defrost test","value":"Outdoor unit control board: set DIP switch SW1 pin 1 to ON to force \"Compulsory defrosting\"; return to OFF afterward for normal operation. No initiate/terminate temperature is published — defrost timing and termination remain fully automatic via the inverter/microprocessor even in the forced test.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"L8V1","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage variable-speed ECM Ultra-Low-NOx furnace","match":["L8V1","L8V1A","L8V1B","L8V1C"],"source":"Trane L8V1 Installation, Operation and Maintenance Manual, Form L8V1-SVX001-1A-EN — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/3229963/Trane-L8v1a040u3vsba.html","groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (natural gas)","value":"2.7–3.0 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"AFUE","value":"80%"},{"label":"Propane","value":"see rating plate — not confirmed in this pass"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"30–60°F (all models: A040, A060, B080, C100)","key":true}]},{"title":"Altitude","rows":[{"label":"Derate rule","value":"Reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft; first try manifold-pressure correction, then re-orifice/High Altitude Kit if that can't hit target","key":true},{"label":"Orifices","value":"A040: 3.2mm, A060: #23, B080: #15, C100: #11 (from High Altitude Kit)"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame current","value":"0.75–3.0 µA DC normal (1 VDC = 1 µA on IFC \"FP\" test pads) — cross-verified from same-generation Trane platform, not itself printed in the L8V1 IOM","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor type / resistance","value":"Silicon nitride HSI (Ultra Lo-NOx ignition system); 37–70 Ω cold resistance at ~75°F — cross-verified from same-generation platform, not itself printed in the L8V1 IOM"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80","flags":[{"title":"Flame-µA and ignitor ohms not printed in L8V1's own IOM","body":"L8V1-SVX001-1A-EN (checked via manualslib mirror) covers the combustion/input check and IFC fault codes but its reachable pages do not print a flame-microamp figure or ignitor resistance table. Values above are carried over from the same-generation, same-gas-valve Trane/Ameristar platform (S8B1/S8X1, A951X) — confirm against this unit's own Service Facts before leaning on them for a borderline flame-signal call."}]},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"A801X","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage furnace (2-stage valve wired high-fire only for single-stage operation)","match":["A801X"],"source":"Ameristar/RunTru A801X Installation Manual, Form 88-A801X004-1B-EN (Nov 2024) — https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation/88-A801X004-1B-EN_11292024.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Single-stage operation only","body":"Factory jumper ties Lo/Hi Fire coil terminals together — the 2-stage gas valve always runs at High Fire."},{"title":"Different flame-current spec than the Trane 36J-valve furnace family","body":"A801X's flame-sense spec (1–6 µA @ 115V) and igniter resistance test (≤200 Ω @ ~70°F) are its own control platform's published figures — do not cross-apply the 0.75–3.0 µA / 37–70 Ω figures used on the S8/S9-series Trane platform (or L8V1/A951X/A952V) to this furnace."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (natural gas, 60K model)","value":"3.5 in. w.c. (±0.3 in.)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure (propane)","value":"10 in. w.c."}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"per rating plate — not tabulated in the installation manual"}]},{"title":"Altitude","rows":[{"label":"Derate rule (US)","value":"4% per 1,000 ft above sea level; re-orifice per Table 8-2 (0-2000ft/2-4000/4-6000/6-8000/8-10000ft bands)","key":true},{"label":"Derate rule (Canada)","value":"10% for 2,000-4,500 ft by an authorized Gas Conversion Station/Dealer"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame current","value":"1–6 µA at 115V (printed directly in the A801X manual's Flame Sensor section) — a different figure/range than the Trane 36J-valve platform's 0.75–3.0 µA; this is a distinct control platform, do not cross-apply","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor resistance","value":"Should not exceed 200 Ω at ~70°F, measured with the igniter disconnected from all other electrical components; replace igniter if higher","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"A951X","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"95-96% AFUE 2-stage fixed-speed condensing furnace","match":["A951X"],"source":"Ameristar/RunTru A951X Installation, Operation and Maintenance Manual, Form A951X-SVX001-1A-EN (May 2022) — https://ameristarhvac.com/assets/pdf/technical_documents/Furnaces/A951X%20Furnace/A951X-SVX001-1A-EN%20(1).pdf","flags":[{"title":"Adjust 2nd stage before 1st stage","body":"Manual: set 2nd-stage (HI) manifold pressure first, then 1st-stage (LO). ISD (Interstage Delay) can be zeroed on the IFC to speed up 2nd-stage testing."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — 2nd stage (natural gas)","value":"3.5 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure (propane)","value":"10 in. w.c."},{"label":"Inlet supply pressure (natural gas)","value":"5.0–13.8 in. w.c."},{"label":"Inlet supply pressure (propane)","value":"11.0–13.8 in. w.c."},{"label":"Main orifice (natural gas)","value":"#45 drill"},{"label":"AFUE","value":"95-96% (model dependent)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"30-60°F to 45-75°F depending on model — see nameplate","key":true},{"label":"Return air temp range","value":"45°F-80°F"}]},{"title":"Altitude","rows":[{"label":"Derate rule","value":"4% per 1,000 ft above sea level","key":true}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame current","value":"0.75–3.0 µA DC normal (1 VDC = 1 µA on IFC \"FP\" test pads); troubleshooting tree treats a reading below 0.75 µA as a failed flame-sensor check","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor resistance","value":"Silicon nitride HSI; replace if cold resistance is NOT between 37–70 Ω at ~75°F (troubleshooting flow references Gas Furnace Silicon Nitride Ignitor Models Service Manual, Pub. 34-3405-08)","key":true}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"A952V","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"96% AFUE 2-stage variable-speed ECM condensing furnace","match":["A952V"],"source":"Trane/Ameristar A952V100CU5 Product & Submittal Data, Form A952V100CU5-SUB-1C-EN (May 2020) — https://hvacdirect.com/media/pdf/RunTru%20A952V100CU5%20Spec.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure not confirmed this pass","body":"This platform's manifold-pressure table lives in the RunTru/Ameristar A952V Installer's Guide (not the submittal sheet used here) — confirm the exact in./w.c. figure there or on the rating plate before adjusting."},{"title":"Flame-µA/ignitor figures carried over from sibling A951X, not independently confirmed","body":"A952V's own Installer's Guide (RunTru/Ameristar, iwae.com mirror) returned HTTP 403 on every fetch attempt this pass and no alternate full-text mirror was found. Figures above are cross-verified from the fixed-speed A951X sibling on the same platform — confirm against A952V's own guide or rating plate before treating as gospel."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"96.0% across all models","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"see Installer's Guide gas-pressure table / rating plate (2-stage gas valve, adjustable)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise — 1st stage","value":"25-55°F (100K model; varies by size)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise — 2nd stage","value":"30-60°F (100K model; varies by size)","key":true},{"label":"Airflow","value":"≥400 CFM/ton nominal @ 0.5 in. w.g.; field-adjustable down to 290 CFM/ton via IFC digital display"}]},{"title":"Altitude","rows":[{"label":"Derate rule (US)","value":"4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft","key":true},{"label":"Derate rule (Canada)","value":"4% per 1,000 ft above 4,500 ft"}]},{"title":"Flame signal / ignition","rows":[{"label":"Flame current","value":"0.75–3.0 µA DC normal (1 VDC = 1 µA on IFC \"FP\" test pads) — cross-verified from same-platform A951X IOM, not independently confirmed in A952V's own guide this pass","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor resistance","value":"Silicon nitride HSI; 37–70 Ω cold resistance at ~75°F — cross-verified from same-platform A951X IOM, not independently confirmed in A952V's own guide this pass"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"E4HL / E4AH","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"R-454B side-discharge inverter heat pump (E4HL) with E4AH companion air handler","match":["E4HL","E4HL5","E4AH"],"source":"Ameristar E4HL5 Installation Manual, Form 88-E4HL5001-1A-EN (Apr 2023) — https://hvacdirect.com/media/pdf/E4HL5%20installation%20manual.pdf","flags":[{"title":"E4AH air handler figures not confirmed","body":"This pass only pulled the E4HL5 outdoor-unit manual. For E4AH-specific airflow/blower-tap data, consult its own installation manual or the rating plate — do not assume the E4HL numbers apply indoor-side."},{"title":"Additional-charge table is mislabeled R-410A","body":"The manual's Table 9 (additional refrigerant per foot of liquid line) is headed '...(R410A)' even though this is an R-454B unit — a literature error, not a spec change. Verify oz/ft against the R-454B properties before trusting it verbatim."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Standard line length","value":"16 ft (no additional charge needed at or below this)","key":true},{"label":"Additional charge table","value":"0.16 oz/ft (1/4\"), 0.32 oz/ft (3/8\"), 0.69 oz/ft (1/2\") liquid line — see mislabeling flag above"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Control type","value":"Fully automatic; indoor fan stops during defrost and resumes heating automatically after","key":true},{"label":"Field-adjustable settings","value":"None documented"}]},{"title":"Evacuation","rows":[{"label":"Target vacuum","value":"≤350 microns"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"M4CXC / 4MXC","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position cased evaporator A-coil (upflow/downflow/horizontal), piston or optional field TXV","match":["M4CXC","4MXC"],"source":"Ameristar M4AC3 Installer's Manual (coil/piston/TXV compatibility table), Form TR-MD14IU-044FW — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/2324384/Ameristar-M4ac6.html","flags":[{"title":"Do not double-filter","body":"Do not filter the return AND the supply, and do not filter the supply air duct alone — either changes performance and reduces airflow."},{"title":"Piston size is condenser-matched, not universal","body":"Fixed-orifice piston size (e.g. C050/C056/C060/C063...) is selected per outdoor-unit tonnage/model pairing in the compatibility table, not per coil alone. Confirm the piston stamped in the liquid line matches the paired condenser before charging."}],"groups":[{"title":"Metering","rows":[{"label":"Standard","value":"Fixed-orifice piston, sized per condenser pairing (see compatibility table)","key":true},{"label":"Optional","value":"Field-installed TXV (e.g. MAYTXVACHP/MAYTXVACAC series) — required conversion steps in manual if upgrading from piston"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Trane","model":"P0V0","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"120V modular variable-speed blower (no factory-installed coil), multi-position","match":["P0V0"],"source":"Trane P0V0 Modular Blower Installer's Guide, Form 18-GE20D1-1E-EN (Nov 2021) — https://elibrary.tranetechnologies.com/public/residential-hvac/Literature/Installation/18-GE20D1-1E-EN_11302021.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Charge/airflow figures live with the outdoor unit","body":"Manual explicitly directs: charge adjustments and airflow setup must follow the paired outdoor unit's Service Facts document, not a P0V0-specific table."},{"title":"Filter is often remote, not built-in","body":"Several configurations require a separate remote filter box/cabinet sized by the filter manufacturer — confirm one is present before startup."}],"groups":[{"title":"Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Blower type","value":"Variable-speed, direct-drive; factory-set cooling/heating airflow, adjustable via performance tables","key":true},{"label":"Dual return requirement","value":"Airflow > 1600 CFM requires dual returns"},{"label":"CFM/ton range","value":"Field-adjustable 290-450 CFM/ton via the Integrated Modular Blower Control digital menu (CpC = cooling CFM/ton, CpH = heating CFM/ton). Available nominal-tonnage options vary by cabinet: P0V0A up to 3T, P0V0B up to 4T, P0V0C/D up to 5T.","key":true},{"label":"Zoned or variable-speed (VSPD) outdoor unit","value":"CFM/ton must be set to 400 when paired with zoning or a variable-speed outdoor unit"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter size by cabinet width","value":"14-1/2\": 1 x 14x25x1; 17-1/2\": 1 x 16x25x1; 21\": 1 x 20x25x1; 24-1/2\": 1 x 24x25x1 — field-supplied, not factory furnished","key":true},{"label":"Airflow over 1600 CFM","value":"Requires return-air openings/filters on both sides, or one side plus the bottom, or the bottom alone"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"M4AC / M4HP","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"Legacy 13-14 SEER R-410A split system air conditioner (M4AC) / heat pump (M4HP)","match":["M4AC","M4HP","M4AC3","M4AC4","M4HP4"],"source":"Ameristar M4AC3 Installer's Manual, Form TR-MD14IU-044FW — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/2324384/Ameristar-M4ac6.html ; Ameristar M4HP40 Series Installation Instructions, Form TR-MD14U-035AW — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/989378/Ameristar-M4hp40-Series.html","flags":[{"title":"Charging method depends on metering device","body":"Fixed-orifice (piston) systems: charge by the Superheat Charging Chart (indoor/outdoor DB-WB conditions). Field TXV-converted systems: charge by subcooling (above 55°F outdoor)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Type","value":"R-410A"},{"label":"Piston + superheat method","value":"Read superheat off chart by outdoor temp × indoor DB/WB","key":true},{"label":"TXV + subcool method","value":"Charge to design subcooling (nameplate), corrected by line-length worksheet","key":true},{"label":"Weigh-in","value":"Usable for initial install or full recharge"}]},{"title":"Defrost (heat pump)","rows":[{"label":"Control","value":"Board switch SW3-3 selects defrost mode; sensors T3 (coil)/T4 (ambient)","key":true},{"label":"Initiation (typical)","value":"T3 < 30.2°F sustained 60 min compressor-run, or T3 < 28.4°F on first run after power-up"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"M4AH","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Legacy companion air handler to M4AC/M4HP split systems, R-410A","match":["M4AH","M4AH3","M4AH4"],"source":"Ameristar M4AC3 Installer's Manual (coil/piston/TXV compatibility table), Form TR-MD14IU-044FW — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/2324384/Ameristar-M4ac6.html","flags":[{"title":"M4AH-specific blower/airflow tables not confirmed","body":"This pass only confirmed M4AH's piston/TXV metering pairing (documented inside the M4AC installer's manual, not a standalone M4AH manual). Get blower-tap/CFM tables from the M4AH nameplate or its own installation sheet."},{"title":"CFM-by-speed-tap and filter size are from one representative size (2-ton, 26B)","body":"This pass pulled a multi-model Ameristar M4AH4E submittal PDF; the heater-kit MCA/breaker figures are per-kit and apply across the line, but the blower CFM-by-speed table and filter size quoted are specific to the 2-ton (26B) example in that document. Verify against the submittal or nameplate for the actual tonnage installed before relying on the filter size."}],"groups":[{"title":"Metering","rows":[{"label":"Standard","value":"Fixed-orifice piston, condenser-matched (e.g. C060/C063/C067... per tonnage)","key":true},{"label":"Optional","value":"Field TXV (MAYTXVACHP series)"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Motor","value":"Direct-drive, 5-speed PSC/ECM (per suffix); 2-ton submittal example: 1/3 HP, 1050 RPM, 208-230/1/60, 2.6 FLA","key":true},{"label":"Refrigerant / line connections","value":"R-410A, brazed connections; 2-ton example: 3/4\" gas / 3/8\" liquid — line sizes scale with tonnage, confirm per model"}]},{"title":"Heat","rows":[{"label":"Heater kits (MCA / max breaker)","value":"MAYHTR1A05BKR (5kW): MCA 29.4A [240V] / 25.9A [208V], breaker 30A. MAYHTR1A08BKR (7.5kW): MCA 42.4A / 37.2A, breaker 45A / 40A. MAYHTR1A10BKR (10kW): MCA 55.4A both voltages, breaker 60A / 50A.","key":true},{"label":"Minimum heating blower speed","value":"Factory set at Medium-High; heater-kit table also specifies a Low-speed minimum (without vs. with heat pump) depending on the kit installed"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Not factory furnished — field-installed throwaway type. 2-ton (26B) submittal example: 1 - 16 x 20 x 1 in. — size scales with tonnage, confirm against the nameplate/submittal for the installed unit.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Ameristar","model":"M4PH / M4PW / M4PG","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"Legacy 14 SEER packaged heat pump (M4PH) / gas-electric (M4PG) rooftop-style units, 2-5 ton","match":["M4PH","M4PW","M4PG"],"source":"Ameristar Package Heat Pump & Air Conditioner Installation Instructions, 14 SEER Series 2-5 Ton (M4PH) — https://pimmedia.winsupplyinc.com/pim/INTA/032020/_M4PH4024A1000A_ASTM4PH4024A10_INTA.pdf ; Ameristar Package Gas Electric Units Installation Instructions (M4PG) — https://pimmedia.winsupplyinc.com/pim/INTA/122020/_M4PG4036A1090A_ASTM4PG4036A109_INTA.pdf","flags":[{"title":"M4PW not directly confirmed","body":"No M4PW (packaged electric-heat/AC) literature was pulled this pass. It shares the same cabinet/electrical platform naming as M4PH/M4PG, but treat any M4PW-specific figure as unconfirmed until its own manual is checked."},{"title":"M4PG gas-side numbers are approximate","body":"The M4PG spec table's OCR-extracted layout scrambled column alignment for temperature rise per exact model. Steady-state efficiency reads ~81% (single-stage gas heat); confirm exact temp-rise-by-model and manifold pressure against the rating plate before adjusting."}],"groups":[{"title":"Heat pump (M4PH)","rows":[{"label":"SEER","value":"14 SEER, 2-5 ton","key":true},{"label":"Airflow","value":"80%-130% of 400 CFM/ton","key":true},{"label":"Defrost control","value":"Board switch SW3 (SW3-1 forces manual defrost test, SW3-3 selects defrost mode)"}]},{"title":"Gas heat (M4PG)","rows":[{"label":"Steady-state efficiency","value":"~81% (single-stage gas valve)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure / temp rise","value":"see rating plate — table alignment not reliably extractable this pass"}]}]},
  {"brand":"York / Coleman","model":"DGAA / DGAH","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE sealed-combustion downflow gas furnace for manufactured (mobile) homes; DGAA doubles as an A/C-ready air handler (up to 4-5 ton), DGAH is heating-only","match":["DGAA","DGAH","DGAA056BDTB","DGAA070BDTB","DGAA077BDTB","DGAA090BDTB","DGAH056BBSB","DGAH077BBSB","DGAX","DGPA","DGPH"],"source":"York/Coleman DGAA/DGAH Technical Guide, Form 246641-BTG-E-0116 — https://www.yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/DGAX_Tech.pdf","flags":[{"title":"High-altitude derate is manual, not automatic","body":"For elevations above 2,000 ft, input must be reduced 4% for each 1,000 ft above sea level. Factory-installed pressure switch is unchanged 2,000-4,500 ft; use kit 1PS0166 (natural gas) or 1PS0167 (propane) at altitude."},{"title":"Two different blower packages","body":"Standard heating blower (1305 CFM nominal, size A) vs. 5-ton accessory A/C blower 7900-7751 (1725 CFM). Confirm which is installed before reading the CFM/static-pressure table."},{"title":"Confirmed: HSI, not spark/DSI — but a slower warm-up than the later York platforms","body":"DGAA/DGAH use a genuine hot-surface igniter (the service manual explicitly calls it \"HSI igniter\" in the burner-removal procedure), not spark/DSI. Its ignition control gives a 30-second warm-up before the gas valve opens — noticeably longer than the 17-sec warm-up on the later TM8Y/G9T-family HSI boards. Don't assume the 17-sec figure carries over to this mobile-home platform."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Input rate","value":"56,000 / 70,000 / 77,000 / 90,000 BTUH depending on model","key":true},{"label":"Output","value":"45,000-72,000 BTUH (80.0% AFUE, Nat. & LP)"},{"label":"Ignition","value":"Automatic hot surface ignition"},{"label":"Gas connection","value":"1/2\" NPT"},{"label":"Igniter warm-up (confirmed)","value":"30-second warm-up period, HSI"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"45-75°F","key":true},{"label":"Max. outlet air temp.","value":"165°F"},{"label":"Max. external static pressure","value":"0.3 in. W.C."},{"label":"Filters","value":"Two 16\" x 20\" x 1\""}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Power","value":"115 VAC, 60 Hz, 1-phase"},{"label":"Fuse/breaker","value":"15A maximum"},{"label":"Thermostat circuit","value":"24 VAC, 60 Hz"}]},{"title":"Venting","rows":[{"label":"Flue pipe","value":"Must use 4000 Series roof jack (downflow, 0\" clearance to combustibles)"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame-sense µA — normal","value":"~3.7 µA DC","key":true},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — lockout","value":"0.9 µA DC (no separate low-signal warning threshold published for this control, unlike the later 0.1 µA-lockout IFC platform)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch fault codes","value":"2 flashes = switch stuck closed; 3 flashes = switch failed to close at start of heat cycle; numeric trip setpoint in in. w.c. not found in OEM literature reviewed (only an aftermarket parts listing claims 0.10\" w.c. — not used here, unconfirmed against manufacturer literature)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Coleman / Luxaire","model":"G9T-UP / G9T-DH / FG9-UP / FG9-DH","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"90-94.3% AFUE sealed-combustion (Category IV) tubular heat exchanger furnace, single-stage, hot surface ignition; G9T-UP/FG9-UP upflow (40-140 MBH), G9T-DH/FG9-DH downflow/horizontal (40-120 MBH), mobile-home approved in downflow only","match":["G9T-UP","G9T-DH","FG9-UP","FG9-DH","G9T","FG9","P9UR","P9DH","P3UR","P3DH"],"source":"York/Coleman/Luxaire High-Efficiency Gas-Fired Furnaces Installation Instruction (Tubular Heat Exchanger Series), Form 035-17477-002 Rev. D — https://www.hamiltonhomeproducts.com/vb/Repository/InstallationManuals_PartsLists/90AFUE%20Furnaces/FG9-G9T/FG9-G9T-Combined-Install-Owners.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Temp rise and AFUE are model-size specific, not one number","body":"AFUE ranges 91.0-94.3% and rise ranges 25-75°F depending on the exact MBH/CFM/cabinet size — read the rating plate or the Table 1 (upflow) / Table 2 (downflow) in the install manual for the specific model."},{"title":"Downflow only is manufactured-home listed","body":"Upflow (P*UR/G9T-UP/FG9-UP) is NOT approved for manufactured (mobile) homes. Only downflow (P*DH/G9T-DH/FG9-DH) carries the AGA/CGA mobile-home listing."},{"title":"Flame-sense figures confirmed on the upflow (UP) manual only","body":"The 3.7 µA / 0.9 µA figures below come from the P*UR/G9T-UP/FG9-UP (upflow) service manual, ignition control P/N 031-01972-001. G9T-DH/FG9-DH (downflow/horizontal) share the same tubular heat-exchanger platform and install manual per the combined Form 035-17477-002, so treat these as representative — confirm against the DH-specific manual/rating plate if it diverges."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas","value":"3.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, propane (LP)","value":"10.0\" w.c."},{"label":"Inlet gas pressure range, NG","value":"4.5\"-13.9\" w.c."},{"label":"Inlet gas pressure range, LP","value":"11.0\"-13.9\" w.c."},{"label":"High altitude","value":"Above 2,000 ft, reduce input 4% per 1,000 ft; standard pressure switch OK to 4,500 ft, above that needs conversion kit 035-14447-000"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise range","value":"25-75°F by model (see rating plate)","key":true},{"label":"Max. outlet air temp.","value":"155-175°F by model"}]},{"title":"Ignition / Safety","rows":[{"label":"Ignition","value":"Hot surface igniter, 17-sec warm-up, 3 retries then 1-hr lockout"},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Monitor combustion air/vent blockage and condensate drain blockage"},{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset, mounted on burner box"},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — normal","value":"~3.7 µA DC","key":true},{"label":"Flame-sense µA — lockout","value":"0.9 µA DC (no separate low-signal warning threshold published for this control)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch fault codes","value":"2 flashes = switch stuck closed; 3 flashes = switch failed to close at start of heat cycle; 6 flashes = switch opened 4x during call for heat; numeric trip setpoint in in. w.c. not published — see rating plate"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Coleman","model":"EB / EBE / EUE","equip":"Electric Furnace","summary":"240V single-phase electric furnace for manufactured housing, sequenced heating elements 10-23 kW, downflow (EB/EBE) or upflow (EUE) construction, A/C or heat-pump blower-ready","match":["EB10B","EB12B","EB15B","EB17B","EB20B","EB23B","EBE10A","EBE12A","EBE15A","EBE17A","EBE20A","EBE23A","EUE10A","EUE12A","EUE15A","EUE17A","EUE20A","EUE23A","EB","EBE","EUE"],"source":"Johnson Controls/York EBE*/EUE* Electric Furnace Installation Manual, Form 5396713-BIM-E-0720 — https://www.yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/EBE_EUE_Installation.pdf (legacy EB-series equivalent: York/Coleman EB Series Installation Manual, Form 035-15266-003 Rev. A)","flags":[{"title":"Output is model-size specific, not one number","body":"kW/BTU output, element amps and required wire/breaker size are keyed to model size (10/12/15/17/20/23). See the Electric group below or Table 4 (EBE/EUE) / Table 4 (legacy EB) in the manual for the exact model."},{"title":"Dual vs. single branch circuit wiring","body":"15/17/20/23 kW models ship set up for DUAL branch circuit (two breakers/two feeds). For single-circuit service, jumper bars P/N 3500-378P are required (factory part, not always installed)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Electric (Heating)","rows":[{"label":"kW / BTU output @ 240V (10-23 model)","value":"10.0/34,000 · 11.4/39,000 · 15.0/51,000 · 16.4/56,000 · 19.6/67,000 · 22.6/77,000 BTU","key":true},{"label":"Element current draw @ 240V","value":"40.0-90.0 A depending on size"},{"label":"Sequencer","value":"Time-delay relay(s) stage elements on/off; located in control box with breakers and limit switches"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Blower speed for heat (Fan Efficiency compliance)","value":"Low (1) for 10/12/15 kW; Medium-Low (2) for 17/20/23 kW","key":true},{"label":"CFM range, 0.1-0.5\" ESP","value":"~1000-1600 CFM depending on model and speed tap"},{"label":"Blower off delay","value":"60 sec, built into motor"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Voltage","value":"240 VAC, 60 Hz, 1-phase"},{"label":"Max fuse/breaker, single-circuit","value":"60A (10kW) up to 125A (23kW) — model-specific, see wiring table"},{"label":"Filter size","value":"16\" x 20\" x 1\" (top) — EBE only; EUE ships with no filter, needs external filter base/rack"}]}]},
  {"brand":"York / Guardian","model":"RAC13L / RAC143","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Straight-cool single-stage split-system condenser, LX Series platform (scroll/rotary compressor, microchannel coil); RAC13L is R-410A 13 SEER, RAC143 is the newer 14.3 SEER2 R-454B generation of the same chassis","match":["RAC13L","RAC14","RAC143","RAC134","RAC13","RAC","GAC13L","GAC143"],"source":"York/Guardian RAC13L Technical Guide, Form 5752574-UTG-E-1021 (R-410A) — https://www.yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/rac13lgen4techguide.pdf ; RAC143 (R-454B 14.3 SEER2) Technical Guide — https://www.yorknow.com/pub/media/documentation/rac143_techguide.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single manifold-pressure-style number — subcool/superheat charging","body":"Total system charge = base (nameplate) charge + adder for the matched indoor coil (from the System Charge table) + adder for lineset length beyond 15 ft (0.62-0.75 oz/ft by tonnage) + adjustment to match the printed subcool/superheat charging chart on the unit. Baseline is 15°F subcooling / 15°F superheat; add 1% capacity per 2°F subcool increase."},{"title":"Confirm refrigerant before charging — RAC143 is R-454B, not R-410A","body":"RAC13L/RAC134 use R-410A; the newer RAC143 (14.3 SEER2) generation on the same LX Series chassis uses R-454B (mildly flammable, A2L). Check the nameplate and use A2L-rated recovery/charging equipment — do not assume R-410A."}],"groups":[{"title":"Charging (R-410A RAC13L example)","rows":[{"label":"Nominal unit charge, 15 ft lineset","value":"2 lb 13 oz (1.5-ton) up to 5 lb 1 oz (5-ton) — see model-specific Physical & Electrical Data table","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment per foot beyond 15 ft","value":"0.62-0.75 oz/ft, by tonnage"},{"label":"Charging basis","value":"15°F subcooling / 15°F superheat at outdoor base valves"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Voltage","value":"208-230V, 1-phase, 60 Hz"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Scroll (1.5-ton uses rotary — limited to 100 ft equivalent line length)"},{"label":"Min. circuit ampacity","value":"12.9A (1.5-ton) to 29.1A (5-ton)"}]},{"title":"Application","rows":[{"label":"Low-ambient cooling","value":"Standard kit to +20°F; Advanced kit to -20°F (PSC fan motor units only)","key":true},{"label":"Max. lineset","value":"80 ft equivalent length"},{"label":"Sound rating","value":"74-76 dBA by size"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"York / Guardian","model":"RHP143","equip":"Condenser/Heat Pump","summary":"R-454B single-stage split-system heat pump, LX Series platform sharing chassis and charging method with the RAC143 condenser; demand-defrost control","match":["RHP143","RHP14","RHP","RHC","RHC143","GHP143"],"source":"Johnson Controls RHP143 Series Installation Manual, Form 6198123-UIM-A-0622 — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/2977135/Johnson-Controls-Rhp143-Series.html (R-454B; on the same platform as the prior R-410A RHP14/YH2E/THE2 line)","flags":[{"title":"The prefix is RHP, not RHC","body":"Guardian's single-stage heat pump condensing unit uses the RHP prefix (e.g. RHP14324B21S). If a work order or customer says 'RHC', check the rating plate — it is almost certainly RHP; no Guardian RHC line was found in OEM documentation."},{"title":"Charging is by chart, not a single pressure","body":"Same subcool/superheat charging method as the RAC condenser: base charge + coil/lineset adders + adjustment to the unit's printed chart (nominal 15°F/15°F baseline on the R-410A-generation platform)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Defrost method","value":"Demand defrost, adjustable timer up to 40 minutes","key":true},{"label":"Defrost curve","value":"Multiple selectable curves on the control board"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Min. airflow with dehumidification control installed","value":"325 CFM/ton","key":true}]},{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-454B (A2L, mildly flammable) — use A2L-rated gauges/recovery equipment","key":true},{"label":"Design charging target","value":"15°F subcooling / 15°F superheat at the outdoor unit's base valves (published performance-table basis, shared with the RAC143 condenser platform); capacity adjusts ±1% per 2°F subcooling change from that baseline — use as a starting reference, final charge still set by the unit's own charging chart.","key":true}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — sold as Frigidaire/Kelvinator","model":"FG6/FG7/FG8, KG6/KG7/KG8","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"2-stage, fixed-speed, iSEER Smartlite condensing gas furnace (~95% AFUE); *TC upflow/horizontal and *TL downflow chassis shared across brand-letter prefixes","match":["FG6","FG7","FG8","KG6","KG7","KG8","FG7TC","FG7TL","KG7TC","KG7TL","FG6TC","FG8TC","KG6TC","KG8TC"],"source":"Nordyne iSEER Smartlite FG7T A Series Technical Specifications — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/494255/Nordyne-Iseer-Smartlite-Fg7t-A-Series.html ; Nordyne KG7TC Installation Instructions — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/3923189/Nordyne-Kg7tc.html","flags":[{"title":"No single manifold-pressure number — table + altitude driven","body":"Manifold pressure keys to input rate: Table 9 (gas flow rates) + Table 10 (pipe capacities), with high-altitude deration in Table 11 (LP), Table 13 (natural gas, high heating value) and Table 14 (natural gas, low heating value). Use the row matching the rating-plate input/altitude."},{"title":"G6/G8 table numbers not independently pulled","body":"This pass confirmed FG7/KG7 (*TC/*TL) literature directly. FG6/FG8/KG6/KG8 share the same badge-engineering pattern and document structure, but their specific table numbers were not independently verified — confirm against the rating-plate AFUE/input first."},{"title":"No published flame-µA or pressure-switch trip found this pass","body":"Checked both the FG7T (80% AFUE) technical-spec sheet and the FG7TC/KG7TC (95.1% AFUE) user manual's Verifying Burner Operation, Pressure Switch Tubing, Gas Information and Electrical Information sections directly — none publish a flame-sensor microamp figure or a numeric pressure-switch trip point (in. w.c.). Troubleshoot flame sense/pressure switch by substitution or against the rating-plate/board silkscreen rather than a assumed number."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"Tables 9-10, by input rate (see rating plate)","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"Tables 11 (LP), 13 & 14 (natural gas, by heating value)"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride hot-surface igniter (\"Smartlite\"); no published cold-resistance figure found this pass","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Heating/cooling airflow & temp rise","value":"Table 6, *TC/*TL Heating/Cooling Airflows (CFM) & Temperature Rise","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise (Table 6/7, by model)","value":"~25-55°F (060 input) up to ~40-70°F (120-140 input) — confirm exact row for the rating-plate input/cabinet"}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — shared w/ Intertherm, Miller, Armstrong","model":"MG/MM/MS/MB (incl. MGHA/MMHA)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Standard-efficiency (~80%) mobile/manufactured-home gas furnace family; same platform badge-shared across Nordyne, Intertherm, Miller and Armstrong nameplates","match":["MG","MM","MS","MB","MGHA","MMHA","MGH"],"source":"Nordyne/Intertherm/Miller/Armstrong Series MG, MM, MS, MB Furnace Owner's Manual — https://manualzz.com/doc/22290985/nordyne-mg--mm--ms--mb-series-furnace-owner-s-manual (mirror: https://inspectapedia.com/heat/Amrstrong-Series-MG-MM-MS-MB-Manual.pdf)","flags":[{"title":"Confirm brand nameplate before quoting figures","body":"Same chassis is sold under 4 brand names with separately-numbered literature; figures below come from the shared manual text, not a brand-specific reprint."},{"title":"\"MGH\" and \"M7\" not independently confirmed","body":"Task brief flagged MGH/M7 as possible mobile-home aliases. MGHA (electronic-ignition MG variant) is confirmed in this manual; a distinct \"M7\" series was not located — don't assume it shares this platform without checking its own rating plate/literature."},{"title":"No published flame-µA or pressure-switch trip found this pass","body":"The MG/MM/MS/MB manual (hosted as a scanned PDF at InspectApedia; manualzz mirror blocked this pass) does not surface a flame-sensor microamp spec or a numeric pressure-switch trip point in the excerpts available. Do not reuse the M1-series -0.20\"/-0.30\" w.c. figures for this family without confirming against this family's own pressure switch part number."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — natural gas","value":"3.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP/propane","value":"10\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"See manual altitude table — don't reuse sea-level figures above ~2,000 ft"},{"label":"Ignition type by prefix","value":"MGHA/MGHB/MGBB: standing pilot, lit by piezo ignitor (no HSI). MMHA/MMHB/MMBB/MBHA/MBBA: direct ignition, silicon-carbide hot-surface igniter (no pilot).","key":true},{"label":"Igniter cold resistance (direct-ignition models)","value":"~125-150 Ω at 70°F (same Nortek HSI spec as the MB/MM-series igniter cross-reference) — confirm against the ignitor's own part-number spec before condemning"}]},{"title":"Setup","rows":[{"label":"Pressure tap","value":"Side of gas valve; check with manometer"},{"label":"Regulator adjustment","value":"Remove regulator selector-stack cap, turn slotted insert underneath"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"45°F to 75°F (same figure published across this Nortek mobile-home platform's M1/RG1 literature; not independently re-confirmed inside the MG/MM/MS/MB manual text itself this pass)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne)","model":"MGC / MGF","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"No maintenance-figure literature was found this pass confirming MGC/MGF as a distinct chassis from the MG/MM/MS/MB mobile-home family — documentation gap.","match":["MGC","MGF"],"source":"No published OEM installation/service literature located for MGC/MGF in this research pass — search the Nordyne Literature Library (https://literature.nordyne.com/) by the full nameplate model/serial before servicing.","flags":[{"title":"Work from the rating plate + linked manual","body":"Do not assume MGC/MGF share the MG/MM/MS/MB 3.5\"/10\" w.c. manifold-pressure figures — confirm via nameplate and the OEM manual for the exact model/serial before adjusting gas pressure."}]},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — sold as Maytag/others","model":"PGC/PGF (incl. PGS, GPFM, GPCM, GPSM)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Fully modulating, variable-speed condensing gas furnace, 1.5-5 ton airflow platform (PGC2MQ series)","match":["PGC","PGF","PGS","GPFM","GPCM","GPSM","PGC2MQ","PGF2MQ"],"source":"PGF, PGC, PGS, GPFM, GPCM, GPSM Installation Instructions (1-1/2 to 5 Ton) — Sears PartsDirect doc L0522746: https://c.searspartsdirect.com/doc/L0522746 ; referenced also as Nordyne PGC2MQ Series Technical Specifications (Fully Modulating, Variable Speed)","flags":[{"title":"Modulating valve — no single manifold-pressure number","body":"Manual states input pressure per Figure 11, tolerance ±0.3\" w.c., and directs techs to the furnace rating plate rather than a fixed spec — this is a modulating gas valve, not a fixed low/high-fire setpoint."},{"title":"No published flame-µA, pressure-switch trip, or fixed temp-rise number found this pass","body":"The install manual states temperature rise must fall within the range stamped on the rating plate rather than publishing one universal figure, and its pressure-switch and flame-sensor component callouts (Figure 16) aren't accompanied by numeric setpoints in the pages pulled this pass."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold/input pressure","value":"Per Figure 11, ±0.3\" w.c.; also stamped on rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Ignition type","value":"Intermittent pilot: hot-surface igniter lights a pilot burner; flame sensor proves pilot before the main valve opens and the HSI de-energizes. A spark-to-pilot variant also exists (spark gap 1/8\" between igniter and pilot hood).","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — factory setting (Figure 11)","value":"Natural gas 3.5\" w.c.; Propane 10\" w.c. — do not adjust more than ±0.3\" w.c. from this to hit rated input"},{"label":"Gas inlet pressure (Figure 10)","value":"Natural gas: min 4.5\" w.c., recommended 7\" w.c., max 13\" w.c. LP: min/recommended 11\" w.c., max 13\" w.c."}]}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne)","model":"RG1 / RG1D","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Upflow gas furnace for manufactured/mobile homes, roof-jack (B-vent) direct venting","match":["RG1","RG1D"],"source":"Nordyne RG1D Installation Instructions — https://hvacdirect.com/media/hvac/pdf/RG1D%20Install%20Instructions.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure / temperature rise not confirmed this pass","body":"The install sheet exists (linked) but its manifold-pressure and temperature-rise tables could not be extracted from the PDF this pass. Use the rating plate and the linked manual directly rather than borrowing figures from other Nordyne mobile-home furnaces."},{"title":"Flame signal is only reported qualitatively","body":"The control board's Flame status LED flashes to indicate a \"weak\" flame-sense signal, but the manual does not publish a microamp threshold for normal vs. weak vs. dropout — go by the LED behavior (Table 7, Control Module Status Indicators), not an assumed µA number."}],"groups":[{"title":"Venting","rows":[{"label":"Roof-jack height — RG1D056","value":"Max 120\""},{"label":"Roof-jack height — other RG1D models","value":"Max 170\""},{"label":"Roof-jack extension kits","value":"901935 (10\"), 903107 (18\")"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Igniter","value":"Direct hot-surface ignitor on every RG1D model (Table 8, \"Ignitor Direct\" column = Y); no pilot","key":true},{"label":"Igniter cold resistance","value":"40-75 Ω at room temperature (ohmmeter, RX1 scale); replace if outside this range"},{"label":"Pressure switch","value":"Air pressure switch closes at -0.30\" w.c. differential when the inducer starts","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"Natural gas 3.5\" w.c.; LP 10\" w.c. (Table 8 factory settings)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"45°F to 75°F (Table 8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Thermostat anticipator","value":"0.4 (normal setting)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne)","model":"CMF2 / CMF3","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Counterflow convertible gas-or-oil furnace for manufactured housing, 65/75/85 kBTUH inputs, ~80% AFUE","match":["CMF2","CMF3","CMF2-80-PG","CMF2-80-PO","CMF80"],"source":"Nordyne CMF2 80-PG/PO Convertible Owner's Manual and Installation Instructions, Form 708657C (Replaces 708657B) — https://www.globalindustrial.com/site/images/peadbodytaco/CMF80-INSTALL.pdf","flags":[{"title":"CMF3 not independently confirmed","body":"This literature covers CMF2 80-PG/PO explicitly (gas or oil, field-convertible). No separate CMF3 document was located this pass — verify CMF3 nameplate specs match before applying these figures."},{"title":"No published flame-µA or pressure-switch trip found this pass","body":"Pages covering Lighting/Operating Instructions, Gas Burner Controls and Troubleshooting were checked directly; none publish a flame-sensor microamp figure, igniter resistance, or a numeric pressure-switch setpoint for the CMF2 gas side. CMF3 literature was not independently located — treat as unconfirmed until its own manual/nameplate is checked (per existing flag)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — natural gas","value":"3.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"De-rate input 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft"},{"label":"Ignition type (PG gas burner)","value":"Direct ignition, hot-surface igniter — no published cold-resistance figure found this pass","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP","value":"10.0\" w.c. (natural gas 3.5\" w.c. already on file)"},{"label":"Gas inlet pressure","value":"Natural gas 5\"-7\" w.c.; LP 11\"-13\" w.c."}]},{"title":"Inputs","rows":[{"label":"Firing rates","value":"65,000 / 75,000 / 85,000 BTUH (gas or oil)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — shared w/ Intertherm, Miller","model":"M1B / M1G / M1M","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Downflow, direct-vent (sealed combustion) gas & oil furnace for manufactured homes, RVs, park models and modular buildings","match":["M1B","M1G","M1M","M1GB","M1MB","M1MC"],"source":"Nordyne M1B, M1G, M1M Installation Instructions — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/494252/Nordyne-M1b-M1g-M1m.html ; M1 Series Service Manual (M1G and M1M Furnaces)","flags":[{"title":"\"M7\" not confirmed as part of this family","body":"Task brief flagged M7 as a possible mobile-home alias; no M7 model was located in the M1-series literature this pass — treat separately until confirmed."},{"title":"M1G confirmed by a separate service manual, not the install-instructions doc","body":"Form 903241 (install instructions) only covers M1B, M1M and M5S — it does not mention M1G. The M1G standing-pilot figures and the -0.30\" w.c./~1 µA figures above come from the separate Nordyne M1G/M1M Service Manual (ManualsLib 1389605), which appears to be a different/later control platform than form 903241. Verify which document matches the board actually installed before leaning on the pressure-switch or igniter-resistance numbers."},{"title":"Two conflicting igniter-resistance and pressure-switch figures — pick by board","body":"40-75 Ω / -0.20\" w.c. (form 903241) vs. 125-150 Ω / -0.30\" w.c. (M1G/M1M service manual) are both genuinely published, for what look like two different M1-series control-board generations. Don't average them — match the reading to the actual board/igniter in the unit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure — natural gas","value":"3.5\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure — LP/propane","value":"10\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"See manual altitude table"},{"label":"Ignition type by prefix","value":"M1G: standing pilot (natural gas or LP). M1B/M1M: hot-surface ignition (no pilot) — direct-ignition control uses the igniter itself as the flame sensor.","key":true},{"label":"Igniter — M1B/M1M (install instructions, form 903241)","value":"Silicon-carbide hot-surface igniter, 120 VAC; cold resistance 40-75 Ω (RX1 scale, room temp)"},{"label":"Igniter — M1G/M1M (service manual)","value":"Helical silicon-carbide igniter (Carborundum), 115+ VAC; cold resistance ~125-150 Ω at 70°F — note this differs from the 40-75 Ω figure in the install instructions; the two documents appear to cover different control-board generations, confirm against the installed board/igniter part number"},{"label":"Pressure switch — M1M (install instructions)","value":"Air pressure switch closes at -0.20\" w.c. differential when the inducer starts"},{"label":"Pressure switch — M1G/M1M (service manual)","value":"Must exceed -0.30\" w.c. differential to close, within 10 seconds of inducer start"},{"label":"Gas inlet pressure","value":"Natural gas: min 4.5\" w.c., valve inlet up to 7\" w.c. LP: 11\"-13\" w.c., regulated to 10\" w.c. manifold. Do not exceed 14\" w.c. supply."}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"No µA meter reading published; the M1G/M1M control board's status LED flashes to flag a weak flame-sense condition at approx. 1 µA — treat that as the documented dropout/weak-signal threshold, not a normal-operating spec","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"45°F to 75°F (Table 10, M1/M5 Furnace Specifications)"}]}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — sold under multiple nameplates","model":"B6BM / B6EM / B6VM","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-poise indoor air handler with switch-selectable blower speeds for cooling/heat-pump matchups; electric heat kit compatible","match":["B6","B6BM","B6EM","B6VM","B64","B65"],"source":"Nordyne B6BM, B6EM & B6VM Series Installation Instructions — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/835373/Nordyne-B6bm-Series.html","flags":[{"title":"\"B64/B65\" not independently verified","body":"Task brief listed B64/B65 as badge variants of this family; this manual is titled B6BM/B6EM/B6VM only — confirm the exact nameplate suffix matches this document before using its CFM switch table."}],"groups":[{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Airflow selection","value":"8-position CFM switch bank (1-8), set per cooling/heat-pump tonnage table","key":true}]},{"title":"Electric heat","rows":[{"label":"Heater kits","value":"H6HK-###H-XX kits, nominal 5/10/15 kW ranges — sets minimum heating CFM"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter sizes","value":"12x20x1, 18x20x1, 20x20x1 (by cabinet size)"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — sold as Gibson and others","model":"GB4 / GB5","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Indoor air handler; 2-5 ton (24-60 kBTUh) range confirmed for GB5BM — CFM/heat-kit/filter tables not confirmed this pass","match":["GB4","GB5","GB5BM","GB4BM"],"source":"GB5BM Series Air Handler — Specifications and Technical Guide — https://refripartes.com/uploads/Specifications%20and%20Technical%20Guide%20GB5BM.pdf","flags":[{"title":"CFM / heat-kit / filter tables not extracted this pass","body":"The OEM spec sheet exists (linked) but its tables could not be parsed from the PDF in this research pass. Don't guess airflow or filter size — pull the table directly from the linked document or the unit's install sheet."},{"title":"GB4 not confirmed","body":"Only GB5BM literature was located. Confirm GB4 shares this platform via its own rating plate/manual before applying."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne)","model":"PAH2 / PAH4","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Indoor air handler with electronic control board (B3/PAH control), variable-speed conversion kit compatible — maintenance figures not confirmed this pass","match":["PAH2","PAH4","PAH2BM","PAH4BM"],"source":"No readable copy of the PAH2/PAH4 install literature (referenced online as Nordyne form 708709C, \"AIR HANDLER\") was retrieved in this research pass — pull the current sheet from the Nordyne Literature Library (https://literature.nordyne.com/) by full model/serial.","flags":[{"title":"Documentation gap — work from rating plate","body":"Series is confirmed to exist (control-board / variable-speed air handler) but no CFM, heat-kit or filter figures were confirmed from OEM literature this pass. No numbers are given below to avoid guessing."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — mobile-home air handler","model":"UMD","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"No maintenance-figure literature was located for the UMD mobile-home air handler in this research pass — documentation gap.","match":["UMD"],"source":"No published OEM installation/service literature located for UMD in this research pass — search the Nordyne Literature Library (https://literature.nordyne.com/) by the full nameplate model/serial.","flags":[{"title":"Work from the rating plate","body":"Confirm tonnage, CFM, filter size and heat-kit compatibility from the unit's nameplate and its specific install sheet before servicing — no OEM figures were confirmed for this series."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Nortek Global HVAC (Nordyne) — sold under multiple nameplates","model":"SA2BD / SA4BD / SA4BE","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Split-system AC condenser; SA4BE confirmed as R-410A, 1.5-5 ton, matched-assembly charging","match":["SA2BD","SA4BD","SA4BE","S4BE","S2BD","S4BD"],"source":"Nordyne S4BE/SA4BE Series Installation Instructions — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/1310769/Nordyne-S4be-060ka-Series.html (covers 018/024/030/036/042/048/060 = 1.5-5 ton)","flags":[{"title":"Confirm refrigerant before charging — don't assume R-410A","body":"SA4BE is R-410A. SA2BD/SA4BD were not independently confirmed this pass and may be an earlier R-22 generation (related R-22 families turned up in the same search: S5BD/JS5BD) — check the nameplate refrigerant type before connecting gauges or charging."},{"title":"No fixed charge weight — matched-assembly chart only","body":"Manual states charging charts/tables apply only to matched indoor-coil assemblies at the coil's listed airflow — verify indoor coil model and airflow before using the chart; don't reuse a chart built for a different coil match."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"SA4BE","value":"R-410A, charge per matched-assembly chart (weigh-in + subcooling)","key":true}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Rheem/Ruud","model":"RCF / RCFY / RCFZ","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Endeavor-line cased/uncased N-coil for gas or oil furnace add-on, R-410A, bi-directional airflow","match":["RCF","RCFY","RCFZ","RCF24","RCFY24","RCFZ24","RCFZ4821","RCFY4821"],"source":"Rheem Endeavor RCFZ Cased/Uncased Coils Spec Sheet, Form C11-226 Rev. 1 — https://resource.gemaire.com/is/content/Watscocom/Gemaire/rheem_rcfz_en_ss.pdf ; RCFY Installation Instructions, Form 92-100105-40-01 — https://www.budgetheating.com/content/files/downloadables/rcfy%20installation%20instructions.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Metering device is set by the model code, not a universal number","body":"Position after capacity/width in the model number: S=standard/piston, T=TXV, E=EXV(EEV). Confirm from the coil's own model number, not from a similar-looking coil."},{"title":"RCFZ is bi-directional; RCFY is not","body":"RCFZ needs no internal parts changed for horizontal left/right. Older RCFY requires the horizontal drip pan/parts kit (or RXHH- adapter) when converting to horizontal."},{"title":"Furnace heating CFM can exceed cooling design CFM","body":"Size ductwork and pick the coil for the HIGHER of cooling CFM or gas-furnace heating CFM to avoid limit trips, noise, or coil freeze-up (per install manual)."}],"groups":[{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Airflow capacity (coil only)","value":"600-1,900 CFM [283-897 L/s]","key":true},{"label":"Static pressure drop","value":"Published per exact coil model + CFM — see spec sheet Table (wet/dry coil)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Piston (S), TXV (T), or EXV/EEV (E) per model code letter","key":true},{"label":"TXV bulb","value":"Clamp at 10 to 2 o'clock on suction line; never solder with bulb attached"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Rheem/Ruud","model":"RCH / RCCL / RCCU","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Uncased/cased replacement N-coil (RCHA/RCHJ/RCHL/RCGA/RCGJ/RCBA family), R-410A, piston or TXV metering","match":["RCH","RCHA","RCHJ","RCHL","RCGA","RCGJ","RCBA","RCCL","RCCU"],"source":"Rheem/Ruud Installation and Operating Instructions for RCBA/RCGA/RCHA/RCGJ/RCHJ/RCHL, Form 92-20707-17-13 — https://cdn.bakerdist.com/rheem_rcba-uncased_en_ii.pdf","flags":[{"title":"RCBA coils are piston-metered and often need a piston swap","body":"Piston size (part 61-25414-**) is selected by outdoor unit tonnage/model, not fixed to the coil — install manual Table on piston sizing. RCGA-/RCHA-/RCGJ-/RCHJ-/RCHL- coils use a TXV instead (size also keyed to tonnage)."},{"title":"RCCL/RCCU not independently confirmed this pass","body":"RCCL/RCCU share this coil family's numbering (own spec sheet is Rheem/Ruud form C33-205) but that document could not be fetched. Confirm piston/TXV size from the coil's own data plate before assuming the RCHA/RCHJ/RCHL figures above apply."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Metering device","value":"Piston on RCBA-; factory TXV on RCGA-/RCHA-/RCGJ-/RCHJ-/RCHL-","key":true},{"label":"Piston part family","value":"61-25414-** (size selected by outdoor tonnage — see Table, install manual)"}]},{"title":"Install","rows":[{"label":"Orientation","value":"Vertical upflow/downflow as shipped; uncased coil model numbers end after the 10th position"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Rheem/Ruud","model":"RQNM / RQPM / RQRM","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"Classic Series packaged heat pump, R-410A, 13-16 SEER, 2-5 ton, electric heat backup","match":["RQNM","RQPM","RQRM","RQNMA","RQPMA","RQRMA"],"source":"Rheem RQNM/RQPM/RQRM Package Heat Pump Installation Instructions, Form 92-20522-47-08 — http://pts.myrheem.com/docstore/webdocs/Public/ServicePublic/Trouble2a/pdfs/HP_Package/IO/92-20522-47-08_RQNM_RQPM_RQRM.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No single charging number — it's a suction-pressure chart","body":"Cooling and heating each have their own suction-pressure charging chart keyed to tonnage and outdoor ambient, printed in the I&O manual. Do not use a subcooling/superheat rule of thumb from another line."},{"title":"Airflow is AHRI-rated per exact model/voltage","body":"Nominal airflow runs roughly 800-2000 CFM across the 2-5 ton range; read the Indoor Airflow Performance table for the specific model and voltage rather than assuming 400 CFM/ton."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Suction-pressure chart by tonnage + mode (cooling/heating) — see I&O manual","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Nominal airflow","value":"~800-2,000 CFM depending on tonnage (2-5 ton) — AHRI-rated table in I&O manual"}]},{"title":"Heat","rows":[{"label":"Backup heat","value":"Electric heater kit only (no gas) — kW/amps on unit rating plate"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Rheem/Ruud","model":"RRNL / RRPL","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"80% AFUE packaged gas/electric unit, R-410A cooling, 13-16 SEER, 2-5 ton","match":["RRNL","RRPL","RRRL"],"source":"Rheem RRNL/RRPL/RRRL Package Gas Electric Installation Instructions, Form 92-21916-30-07 — http://pts.myrheem.com/docstore/webdocs/servicedocs/histlib/pdfs/Gas_Pack/IOs/92-21916-30-07_RRNL_RRPL_RRRL.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Gas manifold pressure and temperature rise not confirmed this pass","body":"The I&O manual (form above) is table-driven by input rate/altitude; the specific tables could not be pulled this pass (host blocked). Work from the rating plate + the linked manual rather than an assumed number."},{"title":"R-410A charge is by liquid-charging chart, not a flat subcooling number","body":"Manual describes gauging suction and liquid ports and using the unit's own charging chart; no single subcooling/superheat target is published across the whole line."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"80%","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"see rating plate / I&O manual charging table (not confirmed this pass)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A — charge by liquid-charging chart in I&O manual"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Rheem/WeatherKing","model":"WA13 / WA14","equip":"Condenser","summary":"13/14 SEER single-stage R-410A condenser, 1.5-5 ton (WeatherKing entry tier / Mainline Performance twin)","match":["WSA13","WSA14","WSA15","WA13","WA14","WA1318","WA1324","WA1330","WA1336","WA1342","WA1348","WA1360","WA1418","WA1424","WA1430","WA1436","WA1442","WA1448","WA1460","MPA13","MPA14"],"source":"Rheem/WeatherKing 13 & 14 SEER Series Condensing Units Installation Instructions, Form 92-21354-78-20 — https://www.centuryac.com/documents/wa13_install.pdf","flags":[{"title":"\"WSA\" is not a real model prefix on this platform","body":"Current literature only shows WA13.../WA14... (WeatherKing) and MPA13.../MPA14... (Mainline Performance, same platform). No WA15/15-SEER unit was found. If a unit is labeled WSA or WA15, read the actual model off the rating plate."},{"title":"Charged by liquid subcooling, not superheat","body":"Per I&O Section 5.4.4, final charge is set to the subcooling value on the unit's own charging chart (varies with outdoor ambient + indoor CFM) — there is no single number for the whole line."},{"title":"Verify indoor airflow before charging","body":"Design airflow is nominally ~400 CFM/ton; I&O Section 5.3 requires confirming actual indoor airflow before charging — low airflow is the most common bad-charge callback on these."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Charging method","value":"Liquid subcooling per unit's own charging chart (I&O Sec. 5.4.4)","key":true},{"label":"Filter drier","value":"Factory liquid-line drier included — do not add a second liquid-line drier"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Design airflow","value":"~400 CFM/ton nominal — verify indoor airflow per I&O Sec. 5.3 before charging"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"CK / CKJ / CKL","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Legacy R-22 single-stage split condenser, 10 SEER — no model-specific service/charging literature published online, parts breakdown only","match":["CK","CKJ","CKL","CKL18","CKL24","CKL30","CKL36","CKL42","CKL48","CKL60","CKL61","CKL62"],"source":"Goodman CKL 10 SEER (18-30) Repair Parts, Form RP-465, May 2007 (parts breakdown only; larger tonnage 36-62 on RP-466, not located) — http://igate.northernplumbing.com/partsbreakdowns/GoodmanMfg/CKL.pdf ; generic R-22 fixed-orifice charging procedure per Goodman Split System Condensing Unit Installation & Operating Instructions, Form IO-101H — https://documents.alpinehomeair.com/product/Goodman_Condensing_Unit_Install_Instructions.pdf","flags":[{"title":"No CK/CKJ/CKL-specific charging chart found","body":"Only a parts breakdown (RP-465/RP-466) is published for this series. Use the generic Goodman R-22 fixed-orifice superheat method (form IO-101H) and cross-check against the unit's own factory charging chart/rating plate — do not assume a number from another Goodman R-22 line."},{"title":"Legacy R-22 equipment","body":"Pre-2010-era, 10 SEER. Confirm refrigerant/parts availability; replacement is often the more practical recommendation."}],"groups":[{"title":"General","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-22 — see rating plate for charge weight"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Fixed orifice, superheat method (generic Goodman IO-101H — no CKL-specific chart published)"}]}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Goodman/Amana","model":"MBVB","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Variable-speed ECM modular blower with ComfortBridge Technology, CoolCloud app config, matched to R-32/R-454B ComfortBridge coils","match":["MBVB","MBVB12","MBVB16","MBVB20","MBVB12BP1X00","MBVB16CP1X00","MBVB20DP1X00","MBVB12BP1400","MBVB16CP1400","MBVB20DP1400"],"source":"Goodman/Amana MBVB Blower Cabinet Installation Instructions, Form IO-456E, July 2024 — https://documents.alpinehomeair.com/product/mbvbinstallmanual_75C930C0-DAA2-4BB2-849B-23D9202186D4.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Airflow is set digitally, not by a physical tap","body":"Set via the Tonnage (\"ton\") menu: Airflow = Tonnage selection x 400 CFM, default 6.0 ton (max). Trim with CtF/HtF (+/-10%, 2% steps). Output never exceeds the model's Max CFM even if a higher tonnage is selected."},{"title":"Electric heat kit airflow is auto-set by kW, not universal","body":"Selected via the EHt menu; CFM by kW and model is fixed in the Electric Heat Airflow Table (below). kW values marked NR (Not Rated) are not supported on that model."},{"title":"CoolCloud app alone can't test a non-communicating outdoor unit","body":"Bluetooth CoolCloud HVAC app configures/diagnoses the air handler, but a non-communicating outdoor unit still needs the thermostat for outdoor-unit testing."}],"groups":[{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max airflow","value":"MBVB12BP1X00: 1,200 CFM · MBVB16CP1X00: 1,600 CFM · MBVB20DP1X00: 2,000 CFM","key":true},{"label":"Airflow formula","value":"Tonnage selection x 400 CFM (default 6.0 ton / max)"}]},{"title":"Heat","rows":[{"label":"Electric heat CFM by kW","value":"3-6kW: 600-635/800/800 · 8kW: 740/1000/1000 · 10kW: 1000/1000/1200 · 15kW: 1400/1500/1500 (12/16/20 models); 19kW+ Not Rated on all three"}]},{"title":"Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Required at all times — check monthly, clean or replace as needed"}]}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Mitsubishi Electric","model":"MUZ/MSZ (+ SUZ/PUZ-A, MUY single-zone)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Single-zone ductless heat pump — one outdoor unit (MUZ, SUZ, PUZ-A) paired with one MSZ/MFZ/MLZ indoor head","match":["MUZ","MSZ","MFZ","MLZ","SUZ","PUZ-A","MUY","MUZ-FH","MSZ-FH","MUZ-FS","MSZ-FS","MUZ-GL","MSZ-GL","MUZ-WR","MSZ-WR","MUZ-AP","MSZ-AP","MUZ-EF","MSZ-EF","MUZ-LN","MSZ-LN","MUZ-JP","MSZ-JP","MUZ-FE","MSZ-FE","MFZ-KA","MFZ-KT","MLZ-KP"],"source":"Mitsubishi Electric MUZ-WR/MSZ-WR Series Service Manual — theacoutlet.com/documents/Service-Manual-Mitsubishi-WR-Series.pdf; MUZ-FS Installation Instructions — acdirect.com/media/specs/Mitsubishi/mitsubishi-muz-fs-installation-instructions.pdf; MSZ/MUZ-FH06-18NA Service Manual, Form OBH683 Rev E — mitsubishitechinfo.ca/sites/default/files/SH_MSZ-FH06_18NA(2)_OBH683E.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Additional-charge formula & max line length are model-specific","body":"Every M-series outdoor unit ships precharged for line sets up to 25 ft (7.5 m); no additional charge below that. Beyond 25 ft, add refrigerant per THAT model's own formula (e.g. MUZ-WR service manual gives oz = 1.08/5 oz/ft x (line length ft - 25)). The per-ft rate, max total length, and total charge are capacity- and pipe-diameter-specific — pull them from the nameplate and that exact model's installation manual before weighing in."},{"title":"MUY is cooling-only","body":"MUY-prefixed outdoor units have no heat-pump function. Don't check for defrost cycle or heating-mode faults on these — AC-only."}],"groups":[{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory precharge","value":"Covers line set up to 25 ft (7.5 m) — no additional charge below that","key":true},{"label":"Beyond 25 ft","value":"Add per that model's own oz/ft (or g/m) formula in its install manual — weigh in, don't estimate"},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R410A on current US models — confirm on nameplate"}]},{"title":"Airflow / Filters","rows":[{"label":"Indoor filter","value":"Clean when dirty; Mitsubishi Electric homeowner guidance: ~every 2 weeks in heavy use, monthly in light seasonal use (mitsubishielectric.com.au/homeowner/support/how-to-clean-your-air-conditioner-filter)","key":true},{"label":"Condensate","value":"Check drain hose slope and pan for algae/clogs each visit"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Line voltage / MCA / MOP","value":"See rating plate — varies by capacity class (06 through 36+)"},{"label":"Interconnecting wiring","value":"S1/S2/S3 between indoor and outdoor (S1/S2 = power feed, S3 = signal) — match that model's wiring diagram, do not swap S2/S3"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Fault codes","value":"Indoor OPERATION (green) and TIMER (orange) LEDs blink in a count-then-pause pattern — count green then orange blinks and look up that model's service manual code table","key":true},{"label":"Test run","value":"Indoor unit TEST RUN button or wired remote Test Run mode forces a diagnostic run per that model's service manual"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Mitsubishi Electric","model":"MXZ (2- to 8-port multi-zone)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Multi-zone outdoor condenser feeding 2-8 MSZ/MFZ/MLZ/SLZ/SEZ indoor heads from one outdoor unit","match":["MXZ","MXZ-2C","MXZ-3C","MXZ-4C","MXZ-5C","MXZ-8C","MXZ-2A","MXZ-3A","MXZ-4A","MXZ-A","MXZ-SM","MXZ-8B","MUFZ"],"source":"Mitsubishi Electric MXZ-8C48NAHZ Installation Manual, Additional Refrigerant Charge table — manualslib.com/manual/1191982/Mitsubishi-Electric-Mxz-8c48nahz.html (p.7); MXZ-(2)(3)(4)A(20)(30)(36)NA Service Manual, Form OB444I — mitsubishitechinfo.ca","flags":[{"title":"Charge is per-branch, not a flat free-length rule","body":"MXZ multi-zone charging is calculated from every branch's actual pipe length x a diameter-specific rate, added to the factory-shipped charge — there is no 'first N ft free' like the single-zone M-series. On the 8-port MXZ-8C48NAHZ: factory charge 4.8 kg (10 lb 9 oz); add 0.21 oz/ft (19.0 g/m) per ft of 1/4\" liquid line and 0.55 oz/ft (50.0 g/m) per ft of 3/8\" liquid line, summed across every branch, rounded up to the nearest 0.1 kg. Confirm the factory charge and per-branch rate for the specific port-count/model installed."},{"title":"\"MUFZ\" alias unverified","body":"Included in match because it was requested as an MXZ-family outdoor prefix, but no MUFZ service literature was located in this pass — verify the prefix exists before relying on it."}],"groups":[{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory-shipped charge","value":"4.8 kg (10 lb 9 oz) on 8-port MXZ-8C48NAHZ — varies by port count/model, see nameplate","key":true},{"label":"Per-branch add rate","value":"1/4\" liquid line: 0.21 oz/ft (19.0 g/m); 3/8\" liquid line: 0.55 oz/ft (50.0 g/m) — sum every branch","key":true},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R410A"}]},{"title":"Airflow / Filters","rows":[{"label":"Indoor filters","value":"Per whichever indoor head is installed — see MUZ/MSZ entry for interval"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Line voltage / MCA / MOP","value":"See nameplate — larger port-count models (5C/8C, HZ branch-box units) may require multiple power feeds, check install diagram"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Fault codes","value":"Outdoor unit has its own PCB LEDs (service panel off) plus each indoor head's blink/remote check-code — cross-reference against that model's service manual","key":true},{"label":"Test run","value":"Run Test Run mode per zone from each indoor head's wired remote or per the outdoor unit's service manual procedure"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Mitsubishi Electric","model":"PUMY-P (+ PUY cooling-only)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Light-commercial P-series multi-zone outdoor condenser feeding PKA/PLA/PCA/PEAD/PVA/SEZ/SVZ indoor units","match":["PUMY","PUMY-P","PUMY-HP","PUY"],"source":"Mitsubishi Electric PUMY-(H)P-NKMU(2)(-BS) Technical & Service Manual, Form OCH695 Rev B — mitsubishitechinfo.ca/sites/default/files/SH_PUMY-(H)P-NKMU(2)(-BS)_OCH695B.pdf; PUMY-P-NKMU Installation Manual — manualslib.com/manual/2159946/Mitsubishi-Electric-Pumy-P-Nkmu.html","flags":[{"title":"Factory charge is stated as total elongated piping length, not a flat oz figure","body":"PUMY-P literature states the factory charge already covers a stated total extended piping length that scales with capacity (example found: 3 kg covers 50 m total on the P125 class). Get the exact kg/m baseline and the diameter-keyed per-meter add-rate table for the specific PUMY-P capacity installed from its own Technical & Service Manual before weighing in."},{"title":"PUY is cooling-only","body":"PUY outdoor units have no heat-pump function — treat as AC-only, no defrost/heating fault checks."}],"groups":[{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory precharge","value":"Stated as a total elongated pipe length in meters that scales with capacity (e.g. 3 kg / 50 m baseline on P125-class) — confirm exact figure for the installed capacity","key":true},{"label":"Additional charge","value":"Diameter-keyed oz/ft (g/m) add-rate table is in that model's own Technical & Service Manual — weigh in, don't estimate"},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R410A"}]},{"title":"Airflow / Filters","rows":[{"label":"Indoor filters","value":"No field filter at the outdoor unit — see MVZ/PEAD entry for the paired indoor head's filter care"},{"label":"Outdoor coil","value":"Keep clear of debris; no serviceable filter on the condenser"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Line voltage / MCA / MOP","value":"See nameplate — commercial-capacity models may be 208/230V single- or 3-phase, confirm on plate"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Fault codes","value":"Outdoor PCB LED self-check (service panel off) and indoor wired-controller check-code function — see OCH695 troubleshooting chapter","key":true},{"label":"Test run","value":"Wired remote controller Test Run mode per OCH695 commissioning procedure"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Mitsubishi Electric","model":"MVZ/PEAD (+ SEZ/SVZ/PVA/PKA/PLA/PCA/SLZ)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Ducted concealed / ceiling-cassette indoor units paired with an M- or P-series outdoor condenser — no refrigerant charging happens at the indoor unit","match":["MVZ","PEAD","SEZ","SVZ","PVA","PKA","PLA","PCA","SLZ","PEAD-A","MVZ-A"],"source":"Mitsubishi Electric PEAD-A12~42AA7 Split-Type Heat Pump A/C Service Manual, Form HWE16080 — mitsubishitechinfo.ca/sites/default/files/SH_PEAD-A12_42AA7_HWE16080.pdf; Mitsubishi Comfort SVZ filter-clean article — help.mitsubishicomfort.com/s/article/SVZ-Filter-Clean; Mr. Slim PEAD-RP EA Operation Manual — manualslib.com/manual/769052","flags":[{"title":"No refrigerant charge data lives at the indoor unit","body":"All line-set precharge/additional-charge figures are published against the OUTDOOR unit (see the MUZ/MSZ, MXZ, and PUMY-P entries) — don't look for charging tables in the indoor unit's manual."},{"title":"No fixed calendar filter interval is published","body":"PEAD and SVZ literature says to inspect and clean 'when dirty' (tap/vacuum, or rinse under lukewarm <50C water, air-dry out of direct sun) rather than giving a number of weeks — set the interval from actual return-air conditions, check every visit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Airflow / Filters","rows":[{"label":"Filter cleaning","value":"Tap/vacuum or rinse in lukewarm (<50°C) water when dirty — no fixed calendar interval published; inspect every visit","key":true},{"label":"Drain pan / condensate","value":"Ducted units commonly use a condensate pump or gravity drain with trap — verify slope and pump-out on medium/high-static installs"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Line voltage / MCA / MOP","value":"See unit rating plate — varies by static-pressure/capacity class"},{"label":"Interconnecting wiring","value":"S1/S2/S3 to outdoor unit as on wall units; PAR wired remote/controller run is separate low-voltage wiring"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Fault codes","value":"Wired remote Check/Self-Check function (2-digit code) or indoor PCB LED blink pattern — see that model's Service Manual troubleshooting chapter","key":true},{"label":"Test run","value":"Wired remote Test Run mode forces cooling/heating for commissioning and airflow checks"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Bosch","model":"Climate 5000 (BMS500-AA, R-410A)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Wall-mounted single-zone ductless heat pump/AC, 6K-36K regular/max-performance + 36K-60K light commercial, R-410A","match":["BMS500-AA","BMS500-AAU","BMS500-AAS","Climate 5000","BMS500-AAU006-1AHWXC","BMS500-AAU009-1AHWXC","BMS500-AAS012-0AHWXC","BMS500-AAU012-1AHWXC","BMS500-AAU018-1AHWXC","BMS500-AAU024-1AHWXC","BMS500-AAS030-1AHWXC","BMS500-AAS036-1AHWXC","BMS500-AAS009-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAS012-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAS018-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAS024-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAS030-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAS036-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAS009-1CSXHC","BMS500-AAS012-1CSXHC","BMS500-AAS018-1CSXHC","BMS500-AAS024-1CSXHC","BMS500-AAS036-1CSXLC","BMS500-AAS048-1CSXLC","BMS500-AAS060-1CSXLC","BMS500-AAS012-0CSXRC"],"source":"Bosch Service Manual, Wall Mounted Ductless Split A/C-Heat Pump, Climate 5000 Series, BTC 769102301 C / 05.2025 — https://www.bosch-homecomfort.com/us/media/country_pool/documents/climate5000g3_ductless_wall_single_zone_service_manual_05.2025.pdf","flags":[{"title":"R-410A only — a separate R-454B version exists","body":"This entry covers the R-410A ('Gen3') BMS500-AA units above. Bosch also sells a newer R-454B 'Gen4' Climate 5000 line under overlapping-looking model numbers. Confirm refrigerant type on the outdoor unit rating plate before charging — do not assume from the model prefix alone."},{"title":"No MCA/MOP table in this document","body":"Cable/breaker sizing is given only as a wire-gauge-vs-appliance-amps table (Table 5); the actual max current is read off the unit's own rating-plate nameplate, not looked up by model here."}],"groups":[{"title":"Refrigerant / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":true},{"label":"Precharge line length","value":"25 ft (7.6 m), all sizes","key":true},{"label":"Additional charge per ft beyond precharge","value":"0.16 oz (9K-24K) / 0.32 oz (30K-60K)","key":true},{"label":"Max line length","value":"98 ft (30m) 9-12K · 164 ft (50m) 18-36K · 213 ft (65m) 48-60K","key":true},{"label":"Max height difference","value":"66 ft (20m) 9-12K · 82 ft (25m) 18-36K · 98 ft (30m) 48-60K"},{"label":"Liquid/gas line size","value":"1/4\"x3/8\" (6-9K) · 1/4\"x1/2\" (12-24K) · 3/8\"x5/8\" (30-60K)"},{"label":"Evacuation target","value":"-0.1 MPa (14.5 in-Hg vac) for 30 min, +20 min if not reached, leak-check if still not reached after 50 min"},{"label":"Flare torque","value":"1/4\": 13-15 lb-ft · 3/8\": 24-29 · 1/2\": 36-44 · 5/8\": 42-52 · 3/4\": 49-75 · 7/8\": 63-81"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Cable sizing","value":"SOOW cable by appliance amps: 10A=18AWG, 13A=16AWG, 18A=14AWG, 25A=12AWG, 30A=10AWG"},{"label":"MCA/MOP","value":"see rating plate (max current on nameplate sets cable/fuse/switch size)"},{"label":"Disconnect location","value":"within 10 ft of outdoor unit"},{"label":"Indoor/outdoor comms","value":"Single 'S' terminal (2-wire, not S1/S2/S3) + L/N power; 115V 12K models use N/L/S 3-wire"}]},{"title":"Filter / Drain","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Washable mesh filter, pulls out vertically from indoor unit front; 'CL' on display = cleaning reminder"},{"label":"Filter replacement reminder","value":"'F' shown on power-up for 15 sec on some models"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Fault code retrieval","value":"Indoor display shows code directly (EH/EL/EC/PC/LC/LH prefix + 2 digits); outdoor unit blinks Running/Timer LED pattern per Table 20","key":true},{"label":"Most common codes","value":"E1 (comms), P0 (IPM/IGBT), P3 (low pressure) per manual's own quick reference"},{"label":"Full code table","value":"Table 13 (~40 codes) + Table 20 (LED blink-count cross-reference) in the service manual"},{"label":"Engineer / point-check mode","value":"Remote control: hold ON/OFF + Air Speed 7 sec to enter; Up/Down cycles codes 0-30 (T1-T4/TP temps, frequencies, fan speed, EEV position, etc.); hold same combo 2 sec (or wait 60 sec idle) to exit","key":true},{"label":"Forced cooling","value":"Compressor/outdoor fan run fixed rated frequency, indoor fan rated speed, 30 min then reverts to auto @ 24°C"},{"label":"Forced defrost","value":"From forced-cooling mode, hold AUTO/COOL 5 sec"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Bosch","model":"Climate 5000 Multi-Zone (BMS500-AAM)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Multi-zone ductless outdoor condenser paired with BMS500-AA indoor wall/cassette/ducted units, R-410A","match":["BMS500-AAM","BMS500-AAM018-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAM027-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAM036-1CSXRC","BMS500-AAM048-1CSXRC","Climate 5000 multizone"],"source":"Bosch Multi Zone Ductless A/C-Heat Pump Installation & Operating Instructions — https://www.bosch-homecomfort.com/us/media/country_pool/documents/installation-manuals/ductless-minisplits/climate5000_gen4_multizone_ductless_iom_en_08.2025.pdf (title/URL confirmed to exist; content not extracted this session — see gap flag)","flags":[{"title":"Charging/electrical figures not confirmed this session","body":"The single-zone wall service manual (see the BMS500-AA entry above) only tabulates precharge/charge-per-ft/electrical for AAS single-zone outdoor units, not AAM multi-zone. Multiple fetch attempts on the AAM-specific IOM above did not return readable content in this pass. Pull the linked document directly and read the unit's rating plate before charging or wiring — do not reuse the single-zone numbers for a multi-zone outdoor unit."}],"groups":[]},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"MS7 / MS8 / MS8Z","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Residential single- and multi-zone ductless wall mini-splits (MS7-CI/CO, MS8-CI/CO/HI/HO, MS8Z multi-zone), R-410A","match":["MS7","MS7-CI","MS7-CO","MS8","MS8-CI","MS8-CO","MS8-HI","MS8-HO","MS8Z","MS8Z-CI","MS8Z-CO"],"source":"Lennox MS8 Single-Zone product/engineering bulletin (form referenced as ehb_ms8_singlezone) — https://tech.lennoxintl.com/c03e7o14l/viu12ch2uv/ehb_ms8_singlezone_1609.pdf ; MS7 quick manual — https://www.manualslib.com/manual/703712/Lennox-Ms7.html (URLs confirmed to exist; content not extracted this session — see gap flag)","flags":[{"title":"No verified maintenance figures — documentation gap in this research pass","body":"Repeated attempts to fetch/read the MS7/MS8/MS8Z installation and service literature did not return readable content in this session, so no charging, electrical, or fault-code figures are asserted here. The manuals are confirmed to exist at the URLs above (and via LennoxPros' Document Library, which requires searching by model there). Work from the outdoor/indoor unit rating plates and pull the actual Installation Instructions + Service & Application manual before servicing — do not carry over figures from Lennox's newer 'Powered by Samsung' lines (MWMC/MMD/3WMD/3WPD), which are a different platform with different specs."}],"groups":[]},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"MMD (Powered by Samsung)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Multi-position air handler indoor unit for Lennox 'Powered by Samsung' single- and multi-zone mini-split systems, R-32","match":["MMD","MMDS6-1P","MMDM6-1P","MM*D***S6M-1P","MMD air handler"],"source":"Lennox MMD Air Handler Single-Zone / Multi-Zone product spec bulletins — https://www.lennox.com/dA/2f8763750a/ehb_mmd_airhandler_single_indoor_2503.pdf and https://www.lennox.com/dA/632286677a/ehb_mmd_airhandler_multi_indoor_2503.pdf ; installation manuals — https://www.lennox.com/dA/6980720d87/DB68-13003A-00.pdf and https://www.lennox.com/dA/274d0990b7/DB68-13460A-00.pdf (URLs confirmed to exist; content not extracted this session — see gap flag)","flags":[{"title":"No verified maintenance figures — documentation gap in this research pass","body":"Fetch/read attempts on the bulletins and installation manuals above did not return readable content in this session, so no electrical, filter/blower, or refrigerant-side figures are asserted here (this air handler is refrigerant-side only via matched outdoor condenser — check the matched 3WMD/3WPD or MMD outdoor unit for charging data). Pull the documents directly and confirm against the unit rating plate before servicing."}],"groups":[]},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"3WMD / 3WPD (Powered by Samsung)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Cold-climate single-zone wall mini-split heat pump, light-commercial 'Powered by Samsung' line, R-32","match":["3WMD","3WPD","3WPD036S6S-1P","3WMD036S6-1P"],"source":"Lennox 3WPD/3WMD Single-Zone Wall product spec bulletin — https://www.lennox.com/dA/518ca4ee46/ehb_3wpd-3wmd_single_outdoor_2506.pdf ; installation manuals — https://www.lennox.com/dA/a345a5338f/DB68-13440A-00.pdf and https://www.lennox.com/dA/3a0829580c/DB68-13152A-00.pdf (URLs confirmed to exist; content not extracted this session — see gap flag)","flags":[{"title":"No verified maintenance figures — documentation gap in this research pass","body":"Fetch/read attempts on the bulletin and installation manuals above did not return readable content in this session, so no precharge/charge-per-ft/max-length, electrical, or fault-code figures are asserted here. Pull the documents directly and confirm against the outdoor unit rating plate before charging or wiring."}],"groups":[]},
  {"brand":"Samsung","model":"RNS (single-zone) / AJ0__ FJM (multi-zone)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Ductless single-zone (RNS outdoor) and Free Joint Multi multi-zone (AJ0__ outdoor) mini-split condensers","match":["RNS","RNS18CMC","AJ0","AJ040","AJ048","AJ060","AJ072","Free Joint Multi","FJM"],"source":"Samsung HVAC single-zone/FJM download pages — https://www.samsunghvac.com/wall-cassette-duct-systems-mini-splits/RLC-R32 and https://www.samsunghvac.com/Downloads/Single-and-Multi-Zone-Mini-Splits ; distributor-hosted spec sheet — https://fwwebbimage.fwwebb.com/ProductInfo/RNS18CMC-Spec.pdf (URLs confirmed to exist; content not extracted this session — see gap flag)","flags":[{"title":"No verified maintenance figures — documentation gap in this research pass","body":"Fetch/read attempts on Samsung's RNS/AJ0__ literature did not return readable content in this session, so no refrigerant, electrical, or fault-code figures are asserted here. samsunghvac.com's own download/spec pages are the right place to pull a real installation/service manual by exact model (RNS and AJ0__ span many capacities with different figures) — confirm against the outdoor unit rating plate before servicing."}],"groups":[]},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"LRP14 / LRP16","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"2-5 ton residential gas/electric & heat pump packaged units (R-410A); LRP16 adds two-stage compressor + variable-speed ECM","match":["LRP14","LRP14HP","LRP14DF","LRP14AC","LRP14GE","LRP16","LRP16GE","LRP16HP","LRP14HP24","LRP14HP30","LRP14HP36","LRP14HP42","LRP14HP48","LRP14HP60","LRP14GE24","LRP14GE30","LRP14GE36","LRP14GE42","LRP14GE48","LRP14GE60","LRP16GE24","LRP16GE36","LRP16GE48","LRP16GE60","LRP16HP24","LRP16HP36","LRP16HP48","LRP16HP60"],"source":"Lennox LRP14HP/DF/AC/GE, LRP16GE/HP Series Units — Unit Information / Service Literature, Corp. 1501-L2 (Aug 2016, rev. March 2017) — https://tech.lennoxintl.com/C03e7o14l/VIu12Ch2uV/Corp1501c.pdf","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure is altitude-adjusted, not a flat number","body":"Table 1: Natural gas High/Low 3.50/2.00 in.w.c. up to 4500 ft, tapering to 3.19/1.82 in.w.c. by 7500 ft. LP/Propane 10.00/5.60 in.w.c. down to 9.12/5.21 in.w.c. by 7500 ft. Above 7500 ft, call Lennox Tech Services."},{"title":"LRP16GE is 2-stage gas — separate 1st/2nd-stage manifold + temp-rise figures","body":"1st stage manifold: Natural 2.0 ± 0.3 in.w.c., LP 5.6 ± 0.3. 2nd stage: Natural 3.5 ± 0.3, LP 10.0 ± 0.5. LRP14 is single-stage gas heat only."},{"title":"LRP13 / LRP15 NOT covered by this entry","body":"Lennox lists LRP13HPK/ACK/GEK/GNK and LRP15GEK/GXK/HPK as a separate model family with their own service literature. No verified figures for LRP13/LRP15 were found — do not assume LRP14/16 numbers apply."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas — LRP14GE (single-stage)","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG, ≤4500ft)","value":"3.50 in.w.c. high fire (from Table 1)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure (LP, ≤4500ft)","value":"10.00 in.w.c."},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"30-60°F to 45-75°F depending on input size (see rating plate)","key":true},{"label":"Min. gas supply pressure","value":"5 in.w.g. Natural Gas, 11 in.w.g. LPG/Propane"}]},{"title":"Gas — LRP16GE (2-stage)","rows":[{"label":"1st stage manifold pressure","value":"NG 2.0 ± 0.3 in.w.c. / LP 5.6 ± 0.3 in.w.c.","key":true},{"label":"2nd stage manifold pressure","value":"NG 3.5 ± 0.3 in.w.c. / LP 10.0 ± 0.5 in.w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise (1st/2nd stage)","value":"35-45°F / 45-55°F (24-36k models) or 45-55°F / 50-60°F (48-60k models)"}]},{"title":"Charging — Cooling (AC & GE units, LRP14)","rows":[{"label":"Suction superheat target","value":"10-17°F ± 3° by tonnage (2T=10, 2.5T=14, 3T=13, 3.5T=12, 4T=14, 5T=17) at 82°F OD / 80°F-67°F ID","key":true}]},{"title":"Charging — Heat Pump (LRP14HP/LRP16HP)","rows":[{"label":"Cooling suction superheat","value":"5-18°F ± 3° by tonnage (decreasing with size) at 82°F OD"},{"label":"Cooling liquid subcooling","value":"9-14°F ± 2° by tonnage"},{"label":"Heating liquid subcooling","value":"11-28°F ± 2° by tonnage at 47°F OD / 70°F ID","key":true}]},{"title":"Charging — LRP16GE (2-stage cooling only)","rows":[{"label":"Liquid subcooling target","value":"9-12°F ± 3° by tonnage at 82°F OD / 80°F-67°F ID","key":true}]},{"title":"Defrost (LRP14HP/DF, LRP16HP only)","rows":[{"label":"Interval","value":"Field-adjustable 30/60/90 min (factory default 90-min on -1 builds, 30-min on -2 builds)","key":true},{"label":"Initiate / terminate","value":"Defrost thermostat closes at 42°F coil, opens (terminates) at 70°F; max defrost period 14 min (not adjustable)"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches","rows":[{"label":"Low pressure switch (GE/AC/LRP16GE)","value":"Opens 25 ± 5 psi, closes 40 ± 5 psi (fixed, not adjustable)"},{"label":"High pressure switch (all)","value":"Opens 590 ± 10 psi, closes 418 ± 10 psi (fixed, not adjustable)","key":true}]},{"title":"Filter / altitude","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"Field-supplied, 1\" required (28x25\" or 30x30\" internal filter kit rail depending on cabinet size); inspect monthly"},{"label":"High-altitude derate","value":"No modification needed to 4500 ft; above that, derate per Table 1 (only permissible derate)"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Allied Air (Armstrong Air / AirEase / Ducane / Concord)","model":"RGE13 / RPGE13","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"13 SEER single-stage residential gas heating / electric cooling package unit, R-410A, 2-5 ton","match":["RGE13","RPGE13","4PGE13","PRPGE13","PRPGN13","PGE13"],"source":"Allied Air Enterprises RPGE/RGE Series Gas Heating/Electric Cooling Package Unit — Installation Instructions, Form 506516-01, Issue 1030 — https://s7d2.scene7.com/is/content/AlliedAirEnterprises/VALUE_PACKAGEDUNITS_RGE13_INSTALLATIONMANUALpdf","flags":[{"title":"Manifold pressure is a single factory-set spec, not altitude-tabled","body":"Natural gas: factory-set to 3.5 in.w.c., must not vary more than ±0.3 in.w.c. LP/Propane: 10.0-10.5 in.w.c. outlet pressure. Input rate is reduced 5% for 2001-4500 ft; above 4500 ft, follow NFGC Z223.1."},{"title":"Heat pump / dual-fuel / straight-AC siblings NOT covered here","body":"This document covers RGE/RPGE13 gas-electric only. PRPHP/RPHP13/4PHP13/4PHP15 (heat pump), PRPDF (dual fuel), and PRPAC/RCE13/RPCE13 (straight AC) are separate model lines with their own literature — not verified, intentionally omitted from match."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (NG)","value":"3.5 in.w.c. ± 0.3 (factory set, non-adjustable)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure (LP)","value":"10.0-10.5 in.w.c."},{"label":"Min./max supply gas pressure (NG)","value":"5 in.w.c. min, 13 in.w.c. standby max"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"See unit rating plate (not tabled in this document)"},{"label":"Heat anticipator setting","value":"0.75 amp"}]},{"title":"Charging","rows":[{"label":"Suction superheat target (by unit size)","value":"RGE13(*)24: 21°, 30/36: 17°, 42: 16°, 48/60: 15° (± 3°, at 82°F OD / 80°F-67°F ID wb)","key":true},{"label":"Method","value":"Superheat only (fixed-orifice/RFC metering, no TXV mentioned); if in doubt, recover, evacuate to 500 microns, weigh in to nameplate charge"}]},{"title":"Air / Filter","rows":[{"label":"Filter area (disposable, field-supplied)","value":"480-900 sq.in. by tonnage (2T=480, 2.5T/3T=600, 3.5T=650, 4T=800, 5T=900 sq.in.)","key":true},{"label":"Internal filter size","value":"28\"x25\" (24-36k) or 30\"x30\" (42-60k)"},{"label":"Blower delay","value":"Cooling: ON 5 sec after compressor start, OFF 90 sec after stop. Heating: ON 30 sec after burner light, OFF 120 sec after shutdown (fixed, not adjustable)"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Ignition control LED","value":"2 flash = lockout/no flame; 3 flash = pressure switch/aux limit/gas valve open; 4 flash = high limit or rollout open; 5 flash = flame sensed, valve de-energized"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Carrier / Bryant / Payne","model":"48XZ","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"Single-packaged DUAL-FUEL unit — electric heat pump + gas furnace in one cabinet (Carrier 'Gas Heating/Electric Heat Pump'), R-410A (Puron), sizes 024-060 (2-5 ton). Needs a Thermidistat / Hybrid Heat dual-fuel stat. Charge by SUBCOOLING (TXV indoor). NOT a plain gas/electric AC or straight heat pump.","match":["48XZ","48XZ024","48XZ030","48XZ036","48XZ042","48XZ048","48XZ060","48XZ-060130311","48XZ060130311","HYBRID HEAT PACKAGED"],"source":"Carrier 48XZ(N) Installation Instructions, Form 48XZ-2SI (Single- & Three-Phase, sizes 024-060, R-410A). Figures read directly from that manual (Tables 3-8, Fig. 21 charging chart). Exact factory charge (oz), compressor RLA/LRA and MCA/MOP are unit/voltage-specific — read them off the rating plate.","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Unit type","value":"DUAL-FUEL: heat pump (cool + HP heat) + gas furnace for backup/supplemental heat. Diagnose it as BOTH a heat pump and a gas furnace.","key":true},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron), factory-sealed","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Hard-shutoff balance-port TXV in the INDOOR coil + Accurater piston in the OUTDOOR coil — so charge to SUBCOOLING, not superheat","key":true},{"label":"Thermostat","value":"Thermidistat / Hybrid Heat dual-fuel control — balance-point logic switches HP vs gas"},{"label":"Model decode","value":"48XZ-060-130...: 060 = 60,000 BTUH cooling (5 ton); 130 = 130,000 BTUH gas input (Table 3 lists 40/60/90/115/130 MBH inputs)"}]},{"title":"Charging — R-410A, by SUBCOOLING (Fig. 21)","rows":[{"label":"Method","value":"Measure discharge-line (liquid) pressure + liquid-line temp, look up required liquid temp for the target subcooling on the Fig. 21 chart. Adjust only if charge is suspect.","key":true},{"label":"Required subcooling — size 060","value":"≈13-14 °F at 75-95 °F outdoor ambient; ~11.5 °F at 105 °F","key":true},{"label":"Required subcooling — other sizes (75 °F amb)","value":"024 ~10 °F · 030 ~9 °F · 036 ~17.6 °F · 042 ~12.8 °F · 048 ~17.5 °F — full size/ambient table in the manual"},{"label":"Factory charge (oz)","value":"on the rating plate — any indicated adjustment should be very small; a big correction means a real fault (airflow/leak), not just charge","key":true},{"label":"Loss-of-charge switch","value":"liquid line; opens at ~20 psig low pressure"}]},{"title":"Gas / heating","rows":[{"label":"Gas input (this model)","value":"130,000 BTUH, 3 burner orifices (series inputs 40/60/90/115/130 MBH)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural","value":"3.5 in. wc (adjust range 3.4-3.6 in. wc)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, propane","value":"~3.5 in. wc — see the natural-to-LP conversion kit; different orifices required"},{"label":"Gas supply pressure","value":"Natural & LP: min 4.0, max 13.0 in. wc"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"Stamped on the rating plate; hold airflow so rise stays in the approved range (Table 4).","key":true},{"label":"Altitude","value":"Rated to 2000 ft; above that reduce input 4% per 1000 ft (Canada: derate 10% from 2000-4500 ft)"}]},{"title":"Air / filter / airflow","rows":[{"label":"Return-air filter — 042-060","value":"24 x 30 x 1","key":true},{"label":"Return-air filter — 024-036","value":"20 x 24 x 1"},{"label":"Filter pressure drop","value":"Non-standard filters must not exceed 0.08 in. wc"},{"label":"Cooling airflow, size 060 (ECM)","value":"~1575 / 1750 / 2010 CFM at LO / NOM / HI pin (large cabinet, Table 8)"}]},{"title":"Defrost / controls / safeties","rows":[{"label":"Defrost interval","value":"DIP-selectable 30 / 60 / 90 / 120 min (defrost control, Fig. 27); Speedup pins for testing","key":true},{"label":"Defrost thermostat","value":"On a 3/8-in OD stub ~3 in long on an outdoor-coil feeder tube (usually the bottom circuit)"},{"label":"IGC LED fault codes","value":"1=hardware · 2=fan on/off delay modified · 3=limit fault · 4=FLAME SENSE fault · 5=four consecutive limit faults · 6=ignition lockout · 7=rollout","key":true},{"label":"Flame current (µA)","value":"No field microamp value published — the IGC reports a Flame Sense fault (4 flashes) instead"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"Scroll; 3-phase units are rotation-oriented (reverse leads if running backwards — loud, low differential). Don't run below 55 °F OD without the low-ambient kit; 5 min between cycles."}]},{"title":"Electrical / clearances — read the plate","rows":[{"label":"Voltage","value":"208/230-1-60 (024-060) and 208/230-3-60 (048-060) — confirm on plate","key":true},{"label":"Compressor RLA / LRA, MCA / MOP","value":"see rating plate (unit- and voltage-specific)","key":true},{"label":"Service clearances","value":"Top 48 in; evap-coil access side 36 in; power-entry side 36 in; side opposite ducts 36 in; duct panel 12 in"},{"label":"NEC clearance between units (power side)","value":"42 in"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"It's dual-fuel — the #1 misdiagnosis","body":"48XZ is a heat pump AND a gas furnace in one cabinet. A 'no heat' call can be a HP-side fault, a gas-side fault, OR the dual-fuel stat's balance-point switchover. Confirm which stage should be running before condemning parts."},{"title":"Charge to SUBCOOLING, not superheat","body":"The indoor coil has a hard-shutoff TXV (the outdoor coil uses an Accurater piston for heat-pump heating). Use the Fig. 21 subcooling chart — for the 060 target ~13-14 °F. Chasing superheat on this unit will send you the wrong way. Any large charge correction points to an airflow or leak problem, not the charge."},{"title":"Plate still owns the amps and exact charge","body":"Form 48XZ-2SI gives charging/gas/airflow/defrost figures but not the unit's compressor RLA/LRA, MCA/MOP, factory charge in oz, exact temp-rise number, or limit/rollout trip temps — those are on the rating plate. Nothing here is guessed."}]},
  {"brand":"Bosch","model":"BPBA (IDP Premium, R-454B) / BRBA (IDP Premium, R-410A, legacy)","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"Inverter-driven variable-speed packaged heat pump, 3 & 5 ton, 18-19 SEER2; current gen is R-454B (A2L, mildly flammable)","match":["BPBA","BRBA","IDP Premium"],"source":"Bosch IDP Heat Pump Premium Series Packaged Unit — Installation and Operating Instructions, BTC 762003316 D (02.2026) — https://www.bosch-homecomfort.com/us/media/country_pool/documents/installation-manuals/idp_premium_series_packaged_unit_iom_en_02.2026.pdf","flags":[{"title":"R-454B is A2L mildly-flammable refrigerant — min. room-area rules apply","body":"Refrigerant leak sensor is factory-installed and required; do not disable. Min. room area / max charge tables are altitude- and charge-dependent (see manual Tables 10-15) — verify before opening the system indoors."},{"title":"Two charging methods — pick by outdoor temp, not preference","body":"Above 55°F outdoor ambient: subcooling method only (target 12°F ± 4°F). Below 55°F: weigh-in method only (3T = 6 lb 3 oz, 5T = 10 lb 9 oz). Do not subcool-charge below 55°F OD temp."},{"title":"BRBA (R-410A legacy) figures NOT verified here","body":"BRBA is the confirmed model prefix for the discontinued R-410A version of IDP Premium, but its own install manual was not read for this entry — its charge weight, subcooling target, and manifold specs will differ from the R-454B figures below. Pull the BRBA-specific literature before servicing an R-410A unit."}],"groups":[{"title":"Charging (BPBA / R-454B only)","rows":[{"label":"Weigh-in charge, 3 Ton","value":"6 lb 3 oz","key":true},{"label":"Weigh-in charge, 5 Ton","value":"10 lb 9 oz","key":true},{"label":"Design subcooling (both sizes)","value":"12°F ± 4°F (cooling mode, >55°F OD only)","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Rated airflow range","value":"300-450 CFM/ton (no electric heat) or 350-450 CFM/ton (with electric heat kit)","key":true},{"label":"Filter (field-supplied, not factory-installed)","value":"3T: 16x10x1\" — 5T: 16x14x1\""},{"label":"Fan control","value":"4-stage (default) or 2-stage via SW6-4 dip switch; Anti-Cold-Air heating fan delay via T2 sensor (default ON)"}]},{"title":"Defrost (Demand Defrost Control)","rows":[{"label":"Entry condition","value":"Outdoor coil-to-ambient ΔT ≥14-18°F (temp-dependent) sustained 3 min, OR min-run-time reached (2-4 hrs by ambient temp), OR high-pressure sat. temp <82°F for 20 min","key":true},{"label":"Termination","value":"Outdoor coil (T3) reaches 64°F for 1 min, or 8 min max defrost time"}]},{"title":"Protection / diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"Opens 580 PSIG, closes 435 PSIG"},{"label":"Low pressure protection","value":"Trips below 43.5 PSI for 5 min (cooling); retries after 3 min"},{"label":"Manual defrost test","value":"Hold FORCE button 6 sec with active heat call (running ≥8 min); display shows \"dF\""}]}]},
  {"brand":"Heil / ICP (Carrier family)","model":"FHMA5X30L0BA03E","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"2-1/2 ton (30k Btuh) FHMA5 fan coil — multipoise, 5-tap ECM blower, factory R-454B TXV, 17-in cabinet, ~875 CFM. Split-system indoor unit, no combustion.","match":["FHMA5X30L0BA03E","FHMA5X30L0BA","FHMA5X","FHMA5","FHMA"],"source":"Carrier/ICP FHMA5 Product Data, catalog FHM5-11-01PD (03/25).","groups":[{"title":"Airflow / Blower","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Multi-tap ECM, 5-speed (tap 4 / white = electric-heat speed)","key":true},{"label":"Motor (size 30)","value":"1/2 HP, 4.2 FLA @ 208/230V-1φ (confirm FLA on plate)","key":true},{"label":"Nominal airflow","value":"~875 CFM at ~0.5 in. w.c. external static"},{"label":"MCA / max OCP","value":"MCA 5.3 A; max overcurrent 15 A; min wire 14 AWG Cu"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant / Coil","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-454B (A2L)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Factory TXV on all coils","key":true},{"label":"Line connections","value":"Liquid 3/8 in ID sweat; Suction 3/4 in ID sweat"},{"label":"Factory charge","value":"None — ships dry; operating charge is set by the matched OUTDOOR unit + line set (read the outdoor plate)","key":true}]},{"title":"Filter / Cabinet","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"16 x 20 x 1 nominal","key":true},{"label":"Cabinet","value":"17-5/8 in W x 49-5/8 in H x 22-1/16 in D; R-4.2 / 1-in insulation"}]},{"title":"Electric heat (field accessory)","rows":[{"label":"Heat kit","value":"Optional plug-in resistance heater, NOT factory — size 30 accepts 5/8/10/15/18/20/24/30 kW"},{"label":"Amps per kW (240V-1φ)","value":"~4.2 A per kW (5 kW≈20.8 A, 10 kW≈41.6 A); see heater rating plate"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Air handler — no furnace specs","body":"This is a split-system fan coil, not a furnace. Flame-sensor µA, igniter resistance, temperature-rise, and manifold pressure do not apply."},{"title":"Verify TXV part # on the unit","body":"Size-30 TXV replacement read as EA66YP002 from a table that extracted imperfectly — confirm against the parts list/unit before ordering."}]},
  {"brand":"Nordyne / Nortek (private-labeled: NuTone, Frigidaire, Westinghouse…)","model":"FT4BF-048KA","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"4-ton (48k Btuh) 16 SEER R-410A outdoor heat pump. 2-stage Copeland Scroll UltraTech, demand defrost, Comfort Alert. Blower/heat-kit/metering/filter live on the matched INDOOR unit.","match":["FT4BF-048KA","FT4BF-048","FT4BF","FT4B"],"source":"Nordyne (NuTone) Technical Specifications, FT4BF-KA Series, form 200D-0310 (03/2010).","groups":[{"title":"Compressor / Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Compressor","value":"Copeland Scroll UltraTech, 2-stage","key":true},{"label":"Compressor RLA / LRA","value":"21.1 A RLA / 96 A LRA","key":true},{"label":"Supply","value":"208/230V-1φ-60; total 24.0 A; MCA 29.3 A; max fuse/HACR breaker 50 A"},{"label":"Start assist kit","value":"P/N 912933 (accessory)"}]},{"title":"Outdoor fan","rows":[{"label":"Fan motor","value":"BLDC, 1/3 HP, 2.9 A, 2-speed (150/200 W); 24-in 2-blade; 4000 SCFM","key":true}]},{"title":"Refrigerant / Charging","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A","key":true},{"label":"Line set","value":"Liquid 3/8 in; Suction 7/8 in (0-24 ft) or 1-1/8 in (25-75 ft, reducer at unit)"},{"label":"System charge","value":"272 oz for OD + ID + 15 ft line set (SYSTEM total, not condenser-only) — adjust per actual line length","key":true},{"label":"Filter drier","value":"Liquid-line drier included, field-installed"},{"label":"Subcool / superheat target","value":"see rating plate / install instructions (not in the spec sheet)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Outdoor heat pump — not a fan coil","body":"Indoor blower FLA/HP, electric-heat kW, metering device, and filter belong to the matched indoor coil (Nordyne C6BA/H) or air handler (B4VM) — scan the indoor unit's plate for those."},{"title":"Confirm brand on the rating plate","body":"Identical FT4BF-KA data ships under several Nordyne private labels (NuTone/Frigidaire/Westinghouse). The physical plate names the actual brand."}]},
  {"brand":"Trane / American Standard","model":"TDD080R936F0","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"80% AFUE single-stage, downflow/horizontal, induced-draft gas furnace, 80k BTU input (XR80/XB80-era TDD C936/R936). PSC blower ~1/3 HP. NOT a 96% two-stage unit.","match":["TDD080R936F0","TDD080R936","TDD080","ADD080R936","TDD"],"source":"Trane Product Data 'XR80' 22-1640-06-0702 (TUD/TDD080 family); Trane IOM 41-5010-25 (same-platform single-stage induced-draft, White-Rodgers 36G/36J).","groups":[{"title":"Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Flame-rectification sense rod. No field microamp (µA) spec published for this single-stage induced-draft platform — the control locks out after failed trials rather than reporting a field µA.","key":true},{"label":"Ignition","value":"Hot-surface igniter, ~17 s warm-up, ~4 s trial, lockout after failed attempts (41-5010-25)."},{"label":"Igniter resistance","value":"Not published in furnace literature — verify against the igniter part spec (e.g. IGN00145), not the furnace doc."},{"label":"Pressure switch","value":"Numeric trip points not published (open/close logic only). Above ~4,000 ft may need the BAYHALT high-altitude kit."}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Input","value":"80,000 BTU/h, single-stage, 80.0% AFUE","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure","value":"NG 3.5 in w.c. (adjust 3.0-3.7); LP 10.5 in w.c. — same-platform IOM 41-5010-25","key":true},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers 36G/36J. Inlet supply NG 5.0-13.8 in w.c.; LP 11.0-13.8 in w.c."}]},{"title":"Airflow / Blower","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"30-60 °F (22-1640, 080 size)","key":true},{"label":"Indoor blower","value":"PSC direct-drive, 1/3 HP, 1075 RPM, 115V. Motor FLA not separately published; unit total ~10.4 A."},{"label":"Inducer","value":"Induced-draft fan, 1.0 FLA"},{"label":"Filter","value":"One 17 x 25 x 1 in. (downflow requires the filter external to the cabinet)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Flame µA / igniter ohms not published","body":"Trane publishes no field flame-current microamp value or hot-surface igniter resistance for this single-stage induced-draft platform. Do not guess — confirm ignition by successful light-off and lockout behavior."},{"title":"Gas/ignition figures from same-platform IOM","body":"Manifold NG 3.5\"/LP 10.5\" and gas-valve/timing figures are cited from Trane IOM 41-5010-25 (identical White-Rodgers 36G/36J single-stage platform), not a literal TDD080R936F0 service-facts sheet — verify on the unit's own label."}]},
  {"brand":"York / Guardian (JCI)","model":"H1DBO18S064","equip":"Condenser","summary":"York Stellar 2000 'DB' series R-22 split A/C condenser, 1.5 ton (18 MBH), 10 SEER, ~1996-97. Fixed-orifice metering (TXV optional). Charge to 15 °F superheat / 15 °F subcooling.","match":["H1DBO18S064","H1DBO18S06A","H1DBO18S","H1DB018S06","H1DB018","H1DB","HIDBO18","HIDBO18SOS","HIDBO18SOSL6A"],"source":"York Stellar 2000 'DB' Series Technical Guide, Form 550.38-TG2Y (197); Install Instructions 550.38-N1Y.","groups":[{"title":"Charging (R-22)","rows":[{"label":"Charging basis","value":"15 °F superheat and 15 °F subcooling","key":true},{"label":"Suction PSIG @ 95 °F condenser air","value":"35°F sat=61.5, 40°F=68.5, 45°F=76.0, 50°F=84.0 PSIG","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Fixed orifice (default); TXV is an optional field kit — if added, charge to subcooling"},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-22"}]},{"title":"Ratings","rows":[{"label":"Capacity / SEER","value":"1.5 ton (18 MBH), 10.0 SEER","key":true},{"label":"Sound","value":"7.6 bels"},{"label":"Clearances","value":"48 in overhead, 12 in sides/rear, 24 in service access"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Electrical figures are on the rating plate","body":"Compressor RLA/LRA, condenser-fan FLA/HP, and the exact factory charge (oz) are NOT in the technical guide — read them off the unit rating plate / 550.38-N1Y."}]},
  {"brand":"National Comfort Products (NCP)","model":"NCPC-024-1010","equip":"Condenser","summary":"NCP thru-the-wall split-system A/C condenser, ~2 ton (23,600 BTU), 1000-series, R-410A, 12 SEER, TXV at the indoor coil.","match":["NCPC-024-1010","NCPC-024","NCPC","NCP-024","NCPE-424-1010"],"source":"NCP Thru-The-Wall Condensing Units Install/Maintenance Manual (Splits, 12/30/14), spec pp.5,13-14. Figures cited for the catalog 2-ton 1000-series (NCPE-424-1010).","groups":[{"title":"Compressor / Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Compressor RLA / LRA","value":"9.10 A RLA / 58.3 A LRA","key":true},{"label":"Condenser fan motor","value":"0.25 HP / 1.4 A"},{"label":"Supply","value":"208/230V-1φ-60; min 12 AWG; max fuse 20 A"},{"label":"Hard-start","value":"Hard-start kit required if no self-equalizing components"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant / Service","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant / metering","value":"R-410A; TXV at the indoor evaporator","key":true},{"label":"Evacuation","value":"To 300 microns, hold 10 min; pressure-test ~100 psi dry N2","key":true},{"label":"Charge / targets","value":"Factory charge (oz) and superheat/subcool targets not published — verify on the rating plate"},{"label":"Coil cleaning","value":"High-pressure nitrogen from the interior; non-rinse, non-acidic cleaner"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Verify 'NCPC' revision + refrigerant on the plate","body":"Catalog letters are NCPE (standard)/NCPD (deluxe); 'NCPC' is likely 'Condenser' or an older revision. Capacity (024=2 ton) and series (1010) map to the 2-ton 1000-series, whose figures are cited here — confirm RLA/fan A and R-410A (vs a possible older R-22 variant) on the unit rating plate."}]},
  {"brand":"Daikin / Amana","model":"DMST24BU1300AA","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"2-ton (24k Btuh) Daikin AMST-series air handler — R-32, multi-position, 9-speed ECM (3/4 HP), internal factory TXV, 16x20 filter. Spec-identical to Amana AMST24BU1300AA.","match":["DMST24BU1300AA","DMST24BU1300","DMST24","DMST","AMST24BU1300AA","AMST24"],"source":"Daikin AMST Series (R-32) spec sheet SS-DAMST-R32 (rev 07/24).","groups":[{"title":"Airflow / Blower","rows":[{"label":"Blower motor","value":"Direct-drive 9-speed ECM, 3/4 HP; 10 x 6 in wheel","key":true},{"label":"Motor FLA","value":"4.6 A @ 208/240V-1φ","key":true},{"label":"MCA / max OCP","value":"MCA 5.8 A; max overcurrent 15 A; 197-253 VAC"},{"label":"Airflow (taps @ 0.3 in w.c.)","value":"T1 ~745 → T5 ~1035 → T8/T9 ~1155 CFM (full T1-T9 table in SS-DAMST-R32)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant / Coil","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-32 (A2L)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Internal factory-installed TXV","key":true},{"label":"Coil connections","value":"Liquid 3/8 in; Suction 3/4 in; drain 3/4 in FPT"},{"label":"Factory charge","value":"None on the air handler — operating charge is set by the matched OUTDOOR unit + line set (read the outdoor plate)","key":true}]},{"title":"Filter / Controls","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"16 x 20 (part ALFH16201E)","key":true},{"label":"Control fuse / transformer","value":"3 A / 250V control fuse; 24 VAC 40 VA transformer"},{"label":"Electric heat (field kit)","value":"3-25 kW field-installed kits (see the kit's MCA/MOP table)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Air handler — no furnace/condenser specs","body":"Bare air handler: compressor RLA/LRA, condenser data, and the factory refrigerant charge live on the matched OUTDOOR unit's plate. Flame-sensor µA / temperature-rise / manifold pressure are N/A (not a furnace)."},{"title":"Check the first plate character (D vs A)","body":"Figures are from Daikin sheet SS-DAMST-R32, which covers both the Daikin 'D' and Amana 'A' brand codes — specs are identical. The standalone DMST SKU isn't listed by distributors (the AMST twin is), so confirm the first character on the plate. Note: the sheet mislabels the 24 model '1.5 ton' in one row — nomenclature + distributors confirm 2.0 ton."}]},
  {"brand":"ICP / Inter-City (Heil, Tempstar, Comfortmaker, Arcoaire, KeepRite, Day & Night)","model":"NDLK100DG07","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Counterflow (downflow) CONDENSING gas furnace, factory LP/PROPANE, 100,000 BTU input (~1992). ICP N-series: N=furnace, D=downflow, L=LP, K=generation, 100=MBH input. NOT a generator and NOT natural gas. The NG twin is NDGK100.","match":["NDLK100DG07","NDLK100DG","NDLK100","NDLK","NDGK100","NDGK"],"source":"Inter-City Products 'Condensing Gas Furnaces Service Manual' Part No. 2146635 (Parts 1 & 2), NDLK100 spec column (P2 p.52) + gas/ignition/limit sections. AFUE % and exact cabinet-revision decode are not in the manual — read the data plate.","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Equipment","value":"Residential CONDENSING (high-eff) gas furnace, counterflow/downflow. Not a generator; not natural gas.","key":true},{"label":"Fuel (factory)","value":"LP / PROPANE — the NDLK prefix is the LP counterflow series (NG twin = NDGK100). If field-converted to NG, the on-unit conversion label governs gas pressures.","key":true},{"label":"Input / output","value":"100,000 BTU/hr input; 89,500 BTU/hr output (bonnet)","key":true},{"label":"Vintage","value":"Serial L921735080 decodes to ~week 17 of 1992 (ICP: digits 2-3 = year, 4-5 = week) — confirm on the plate"}]},{"title":"Gas — LP/propane (factory)","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure (LP)","value":"10.0 in. w.c. (some units use a WR36E38 STEP valve: 2.5 / 10 in. w.c. low/high)","key":true},{"label":"Inlet/supply pressure (LP)","value":"min 11.0 / ideal 12.0 / max 14.0 in. w.c. (other appliances firing)","key":true},{"label":"Main orifices (LP)","value":"#54, qty 4 (alt #55)"},{"label":"Gas valve","value":"White-Rodgers WR36E36 snap-opening (some Honeywell VR8204A)"},{"label":"If converted to NATURAL gas (NDGK100)","value":"manifold 3.5 in. w.c.; inlet min 4.5 / ideal 7.0 / max 11.0 in. w.c. — verify the on-unit conversion label first"}]},{"title":"Ignition / flame","rows":[{"label":"Ignition","value":"Hot-surface (White-Rodgers 50F47), lockout after 3 tries; some units spark-to-pilot (Honeywell S8600M)","key":true},{"label":"Igniter spark gap (spark-to-pilot)","value":"1/8 in. — this is the FURNACE igniter gap, not an engine spark plug"},{"label":"Flame-sense current","value":"2 µA or greater (White-Rodgers HSI)","key":true}]},{"title":"Air / temperature rise / blower","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"50-80 °F (check after 15 min at rated input; adjust blower speed to stay in range)","key":true},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Blower motor","value":"3/4 HP PSC, ~1050 RPM, 10.8 FLA; run capacitor 10.0 MFD (blower DD10-9A)"},{"label":"Speed taps","value":"COM / HI / MED-HI / MED-LO / LO — heating = yellow lead, cooling = violet lead"},{"label":"Filter area (heat / cool)","value":"288 / 461 sq. in. — an AREA, not a stock size; measure the rack"}]},{"title":"Electrical / limits","rows":[{"label":"Supply","value":"115 V / 60 Hz / 1-ph, 10.8 FLA","key":true},{"label":"Control transformer","value":"24 VAC, 40 VA (min 25 VAC measured)"},{"label":"Heat anticipator","value":"0.15 A"},{"label":"High limit (max)","value":"200 °F (some revisions DG05/KG05 = 250 °F)","key":true},{"label":"Fan-off / aux limit","value":"Fan-off 90 °F; auxiliary/exhaust limit 130 °F (300 °F thermal-sensor reset)"},{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Manual-reset from date code L8944 on (except direct-vent)"},{"label":"Exhaust-blower pressure switch","value":"p/n 1000745 (Red), set -2.36 ±0.20 in. w.c. (early units; hi-alt/later variants differ)"}]},{"title":"Maintenance / procedures","rows":[{"label":"Filter","value":"The key failure mode — a dirty filter soots the secondary HX. Keep it clean.","key":true},{"label":"Heat exchanger","value":"Clean with a soft-bristle brush + vacuum ONLY — no wire brush or harsh chemicals"},{"label":"Condensate trap","value":"Condensing furnace: drain trap must hold 5 in. w.c. against vent pressure; inspect collector-box gasket"},{"label":"LP burner","value":"Air shutters must be installed on LP; condensing units soot easily — check flame ~10 min after start"},{"label":"After gas work","value":"Leak-check all joints with soap solution and cycle the furnace 3-4 times (gasket leaks put CO in the structure)","key":true}]}],"flags":[{"title":"It's an LP furnace — not a generator, not natural gas","body":"NDLK100DG07 is a factory PROPANE condensing furnace, not a Generac genset and not a natural-gas unit. If a generator was also on site, that data tag is a different piece of equipment. Use the LP gas pressures here (manifold 10 in. w.c.); the natural-gas figures apply ONLY if the on-unit conversion label shows it was field-converted to NG."},{"title":"~1992 unit — verify on the data plate","body":"Figures are from Inter-City Service Manual 2146635 for the NDLK100 group. AFUE %, the exact 'DG07' cabinet/revision, and the serial→1992 date are best confirmed on the unit's own rating/data plate; high-limit and pressure-switch settings shift by revision."}]},
  {"brand":"ICP (Day & Night / Heil / Tempstar / Comfortmaker / Arcoaire / KeepRite)","model":"PGD324060K001C1 (PGD3 2-ton / 60k)","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"13 SEER R-410A single-package gas/electric unit, 2 ton (24,000 Btuh), 60,000 Btuh input, 208/230-1-60, LOW NOx (13th digit 1). Decode: P=package, G=gas/electric, D=standard (S=stainless HX), 3=13 SEER, 24=2 ton, 060=60k input, K=208/230-1-60, 00=no options, 1=Low NOx, C=sales, 1=engineering.","match":["PGD324060K001C1","PGD324060K001","PGD324060K00","PGD324060","PGD324"],"source":"ICP Product Specifications \"PGD3, PGS3\" 462 14 2201 01 (8/17/09) + ICP Installation Instructions \"R-410A Single Package Gas/Electric Units PGD/S324-60\" 509 01 3403 03 (03/2015) and 509 01 3403 01 (11-09-11)","flags":[{"title":"Figures are for the 24060 size only","body":"Orifice, factory charge, filter, subcooling target and electrical values below are specific to PGD324060. Other PGD3/PGS3 sizes (24040, 30xxx, 36xxx, 42xxx, 48xxx, 60xxx) have different values — check the rating plate and the PGD3/PGS3 product spec for that size."},{"title":"Low NOx unit — natural gas only","body":"A 1 in the 13th position means a dedicated California Low NOx unit (40 ng/J). The Low NOx requirement applies only to natural gas. The orifice table does not list separate Low NOx orifices — confirm orifice size on the rating plate."},{"title":"Ignition lockout needs a power reset after rollout","body":"The rollout switch above the burners resets itself, but the integrated gas controller (IGC) stays locked out until power is reset."}],"groups":[{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural","value":"3.2–3.8\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"10.0–11.0\" w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural","value":"4.0\" min / 13.0\" max w.c."},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11.0\" min / 13.0\" max w.c."},{"label":"Orifice, natural (0–2,000 ft)","value":"2 × #38 (at 3.6\" w.c.)"},{"label":"Orifice, natural above 2,000 / 4,000 ft","value":"#41 / #42"},{"label":"Orifice, LP","value":"2 × #53 (propane conversion kit is identified on the rating plate)"},{"label":"Altitude derate","value":"4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft (U.S.)"}]},{"title":"Heating","rows":[{"label":"Input / output","value":"60,000 / 48,000 Btuh, 80.0 AFUE"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"25–55 °F","key":true},{"label":"Ignition","value":"Direct spark ignition, 100% lockout, integrated gas controller (IGC)"},{"label":"Flame sense current","value":"see rating plate"},{"label":"Limit switch","value":"Normally closed, auto-reset, on fan partition; trip temperature — see rating plate"},{"label":"Indoor fan delay","value":"On 45 s after flame / off 45 s after call ends"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Blower","value":"5-speed X-13 ECM, 1/2 HP; nominal cooling airflow 800 CFM"},{"label":"Factory speed taps","value":"Heating = High (black), Cooling = Medium (red)"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"see rating plate (airflow table runs 0.1–0.9\" w.c.; 24060 heating speed listed through 0.7\" w.c.)"},{"label":"Return-air static at cabinet","value":"Must not exceed -0.25\" w.c."},{"label":"Filter","value":"20x24x1 throwaway; non-standard filter pressure drop must not exceed 0.08\" w.c."}]},{"title":"Cooling / refrigerant","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant / metering","value":"R-410A, TXV"},{"label":"Factory charge","value":"4.8 lb (2.2 kg)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling (discharge-line pressure + liquid-line temperature), ±2 °F","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target (size 24)","value":"13 °F at 75 °F outdoor; 12 °F at 85–115 °F outdoor","key":true},{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens 650 ±15 psig / resets 420 ±25 psig"},{"label":"Loss-of-charge switch","value":"Opens 20 ±5 psig / resets 45 ±10 psig"}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"Voltage range","value":"187–253 V"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"12.8 RLA / 58.3 LRA"},{"label":"Motors","value":"Outdoor fan 1.2 FLA, indoor fan 4.1 FLA, inducer 1.7 FLA"},{"label":"MCA / MOCP","value":"21.3 A / 30 A (fuse)"}]},{"title":"Diagnostics (IGC LED)","rows":[{"label":"On / Off","value":"Normal / no power or hardware failure","key":true},{"label":"2 flashes","value":"Limit switch"},{"label":"3 flashes","value":"Flame sense"},{"label":"4 flashes","value":"4 consecutive limit trips"},{"label":"5 flashes","value":"Ignition lockout (15 min of unsuccessful attempts)"},{"label":"6 flashes","value":"Pressure switch"},{"label":"7 flashes","value":"Rollout switch"},{"label":"8 flashes","value":"Internal control fault"},{"label":"9 flashes","value":"Temporary 1-hour auto reset"}]}]},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"48FC 04-07 (WeatherMaker gas/electric rooftop)","equip":"Packaged Unit","summary":"Carrier WeatherMaker 48FC sizes 04-07 (3-6 ton) single-packaged rooftop, gas heat / electric cooling, R-410A, standard efficiency (14.0 SEER sizes 04-06). Figures below are for size 06 (5 ton, 460-3-60, medium gas heat 'E', EcoBlue direct-drive fan) where the tables split - scanned 48FCEA06A2A6A0A0A0. Sizes 08-16 use a different manual (48FC-8-16) and are not covered here.","match":["48FC","48FCE","48FCEA06","48FCEA06A2A6A0A0A0","48FCE06","48FCE04","48FCF05","48FCF06","48FCF07","WeatherMaker"],"source":"Carrier 48FC Installation Instructions, Form 48FC-4-7-03SI, Cat. 04-53480272-01 (2-2020); Carrier 48/50FC 04-07 Product Data, Form 48-50FC-4-7-05PD Rev B (2023); Carrier 48FC Service & Maintenance Instructions, Form 48FC-4-7-03SM Rev A, Cat. 04-53480429-01 (3-25); Carrier Product Data 48/50FC-4-7-01PD (2018) used for comparison only","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Unit type","value":"Single packaged rooftop, gas heat / electric cool, R-410A (SI p1)"},{"label":"Model decode (48FCEA06A2A6A0A0A0)","value":"48 = gas heat packaged rooftop · FC = WeatherMaker standard efficiency · E = medium gas heat, aluminized heat exchanger · A = standard one-stage cooling · 06 = 5 tons · A = no sensors · 2 = EcoBlue direct-drive fan, medium static · A = Al/Cu coils, no hail guard · 6 = 460/3/60 · A = design revision (the literature prints '-' here; most likely the plate's revision letter - not confirmed) · 0 = electro-mechanical controls · A = no economizer · 0 = no service options · A = no disconnect · 0 = standard packaging (SI Fig. 1 / PD nomenclature)"},{"label":"Nomenclature, other sizes","value":"Position 5 heat size: D/E/F low/med/high, S/R/T stainless, L low NOx · position 6 cooling: A/C one stage, M/N two stage (size 07), B/N Humidi-MiZer · positions 7-8 tons: 04 (3) to 07 (6) · position 12 voltage: 1 = 575-3, 3 = 208/230-1, 5 = 208/230-3, 6 = 460-3 · position 14 controls: 0 or 6 electro-mechanical (W7212 or W7220 economizer), 2 RTU Open, 3 SystemVu"},{"label":"Cooling rating (size 06)","value":"5 tons; AHRI 58.5 MBH net, 14.0 SEER / 11.0 EER (PD p5)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (size 06)","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A only - charge as liquid; liquid-line driers rated at least 650 psig (SM p16, p20)"},{"label":"Factory charge","value":"8 lb 9 oz - the nameplate charge governs (PD p14; SM p16)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Acutrol (PD p14)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in after evacuation. For a low charge use the SM Fig. 31 chart 'Cooling Charging Chart Std Tier 5 Ton (3-Phase)' with panels on and airflow in the normal range (SM p16-18). The chart's axes are suction pressure vs suction-line temperature - see the charging flag"},{"label":"Compressor","value":"1 circuit, 1 scroll; RLA 7.8 / LRA 52 at 460 V (PD p14, p105)"}]},{"title":"Gas heat (size 06, 'E' medium heat)","rows":[{"label":"Input / output","value":"110 / 88 MBH natural gas, 3 burners, 80% thermal efficiency. The 2023 PD lists the 460-3 size 06 as 1 stage - see the staging flag (PD p9, p18)"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas","value":"3.5 in. wg high fire (SI Table 5)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"10 in. wg high fire (SI Table 6); LP conversion kit required"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural gas","value":"4.0-13.0 in. wg (SI Table 3; SM Table 7)"},{"label":"Supply pressure, LP","value":"11.0-13.0 in. wg (SI Table 4)"},{"label":"Low-fire manifold (2-stage valves)","value":"1.7 in. wg natural / 5.0 in. wg LP - listed in the SM only for 48FCE04 and 48FCF05/06/07; not published for 48FCE06 - see the staging flag"},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"30-65 °F (PD p9, p18)","key":true},{"label":"Gas connection","value":"1/2 in. FPT at the gas valve. Max 0.5 in. wg drop in the supply line. Derate 4% per 1000 ft above 2000 ft (SI p13-16)"},{"label":"Heat anticipator","value":"0.14 A (PD p18)"},{"label":"Orifices","value":"Never redrill an orifice. Replacements are type LH32RF***, ordered through RCD (SI p16; SM p34). LP orifice sizes are in the LP/high-altitude kit instructions - not published here"}]},{"title":"Ignition & safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignition","value":"Direct spark, 100% lockout, IGC board. Reset: interrupt power for at least 5 seconds (SM p34)"},{"label":"Spark gap","value":"0.120-0.141 in. (SM p33, Fig. 60 Detail A)"},{"label":"Electrode spacing","value":"0.200 in. (SM p33, Fig. 60 Detail B; the drawing does not name the part)"},{"label":"Flame sense µA","value":"Not published - see the rating plate or the part"},{"label":"Rollout switch","value":"Opens 195 °F, closes 115 °F (PD p18)"},{"label":"Gas limit switch","value":"On the heat exchanger cover panel; temperature setting not published - see the part or rating plate (SM p29, p34)"},{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Trips 630 ±10 psig, auto-resets 505 psig (SM p29)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Trips 54 ±5 psig, auto-resets 117 ±5 psig (SM p29)"},{"label":"Freeze stat","value":"Trips 30 ±5 °F, auto-resets 45 °F (SM p29)"},{"label":"Draft proving","value":"Inducer flue-gas pressure switch through the IGC (SM p29)"}]},{"title":"Airflow & filters (size 06)","rows":[{"label":"AHRI rated airflow","value":"2000 CFM (SI Table 1)"},{"label":"Fan","value":"16.6 in. vane-axial, direct drive; medium static motor 1.44 max BHP, 239-2390 rpm (PD p14)"},{"label":"Speed setting","value":"Set as VDC on the unit control board, per the fan tables (PD p59; SI Step 16)"},{"label":"Max external static (vertical, 3-phase medium static)","value":"1.0 in. wg at 2000 CFM, 1.6 in. wg at 1500 CFM. The tables assume the high-heat model; deduct per the heat tables (PD p58-59)"},{"label":"Return static limit","value":"0.45 in. wg max without economizer (SI p10)"},{"label":"Return-air filters","value":"2 × 16 × 25 × 2 in., disposable fiberglass (PD p15; SM p3)","key":true}]},{"title":"Electrical (size 06, 460-3-60)","rows":[{"label":"Voltage","value":"460-3-60, operating range 414-506 V (PD p105)"},{"label":"MCA / MOCP","value":"MCA 13 · MOCP 20 (fuse or HACR breaker) · disconnect FLA 12 / LRA 57 - no power exhaust, no convenience outlet (PD p107)","key":true},{"label":"Motors","value":"Indoor fan 2.1 FLA · condenser fan 0.8 FLA (1/4 HP, 1100 rpm) · inducer 0.25 FLA (PD p105)"},{"label":"Wiring","value":"Copper only, #2 AWG max at the contactor (SI p17)"}]},{"title":"Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Drain","value":"3/4 in. connection. External trap required, at least 4 in. deep, freeze-protected. Pitch 1 in. per 10 ft. Keep the red bottom-drain plug tight when using the side drain (SI p16-17; PD p14)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Gas valve staging: the literature conflicts (1 vs 2 stage)","body":"The SM says all 3-phase models (except Low NOx) have 2-stage gas valves, but its low-fire setting (1.7 in. wg natural gas / 5.0 in. wg LP) is listed only for 48FCE04 and 48FCF05/06/07. The 2023 PD shows 48FCE06 3-phase as 1 stage, 110 MBH, while the 2018 PD listed an 82/65 MBH stage-1 rate for this size. Set high fire to 3.5 in. wg and check the rating plate for a printed low-fire input before assuming two stages."},{"title":"Charging instructions don't match the chart","body":"The SM text says to measure liquid pressure and temperature (subcooling). The size-06 chart (Fig. 31) and the worked example use suction pressure against suction-line temperature. Follow the chart's axes and curves."},{"title":"Manifold tap","body":"Retighten the manifold pressure tap set screw and reinstall the 1/8 in. NPT plug after testing - fire-hazard warning (SI p3)."},{"title":"Plate still owns some numbers","body":"Not published in the three Carrier documents: the gas limit switch temperature, flame-sense microamps, LP orifice sizes (in the LP/high-altitude kit instructions), which revision this unit's build date matches, and whether the position-13 'A' is a revision letter. Read them off the rating plate or the part."}]},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FV4A (variable-speed fan coil, Puron)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Carrier FV4A variable-speed multipoise DX fan coil for R-410A (Puron), sizes 002-006, ECM/ICM2 blower set on the Easy Select board (not communicating). Figures below are for size 002 (FV4ANF002). Not an FV4B or FV4C - those use different literature and a different control design.","match":["FV4A","FV4AN","FV4ANF","FV4ANB","FV4ANF002","Puron fan coil","variable-speed fan coil"],"source":"Carrier FV4A Direct Expansion Variable Speed Fan Coil Product Data, Form FV4A-4PD (7-01), Catalog 02FV-4A4; Carrier FV4A Direct Expansion Fan Coil for Puron Installation Instructions, Form IM-FV4A-05 (3-02), Catalog 63FV-4A4","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (FV4ANF002)","value":"F = fan coil · V = Premium Puron · 4 = multipoise · A = series · N = 208/230/1 · F = single-piece cabinet, 1-in. insulation (B = modular) · 002 = size · positions 10-12 = factory heater kW (000 = none) · then variation and series letters, not captured by the scan (PD p.3)"},{"label":"Type","value":"DX variable-speed fan coil, ECM/ICM2 motor; upflow, horizontal-left; horizontal-right with field changes; downflow with a kit (PD p.2-3, II p.2)"},{"label":"Outdoor unit sizes (002) - documents disagree","value":"PD p.6 says 018/024/030/036; II Table 2 (p.15) says 024/030/036, 450-1275 CFM. See flag"},{"label":"TXV size","value":"2-1/2 ton (PD p.3)"},{"label":"Coil","value":"A-coil, 3 rows, 14.5 fins/in, 3.46 sq ft face area (PD p.3)"}]},{"title":"Blower & Airflow","rows":[{"label":"Motor","value":"1/2 HP ECM (PD p.3). The ICM2 motor has high voltage present at all times - wait 5 minutes after disconnecting power before opening the motor"},{"label":"Nominal cooling / heating CFM","value":"525/470 (018) · 700/630 (024) · 875/785 (030) · 1050/945 (036) (PD p.3)","key":true},{"label":"Easy Select board pins","value":"AUX HEAT KW/CFM · AC/HP SIZE · SYSTEM TYPE: AC, HP-COMFORT or HP-EFF · AC/HP CFM ADJUST: HI +15%, LO -10%, NOM = factory · ON/OFF DELAY: 0/90 factory, ENH also offered · CONTINUOUS FAN: LO 50%, MED 65%, HI 100% (II p.11-12)","key":true},{"label":"CFM per ton","value":"About 350 in cooling; HP-COMFORT heating about 315; HP-EFF about 350 in both modes (II p.11)"},{"label":"Heat pump heating CFM","value":"Use PD p.6: Comfort 470/630/785/945, Efficiency 525/700/875/1050 (018/024/030/036). II Table 4 repeats the cooling numbers and contradicts its own text - see flag"},{"label":"Dehumidify (humidistat, J1 removed)","value":"About 80% of nominal cooling (II p.14)"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"No maximum is published. The FV4ANF002 airflow curves are plotted to 0.9 in. wc (PD p.9); the PD also has a supply-vs-return static 'Acceptable Range' chart for trap performance (PD p.8)"},{"label":"Continuous fan with a 2-speed outdoor unit","value":"Do not select HI continuous fan"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (Puron); factory bi-flow hard shut-off TXV (PD p.2-3)"},{"label":"Connections","value":"Suction 3/4 sweat, liquid 3/8 sweat (PD p.4)"},{"label":"Charging","value":"'Refer to outdoor unit Installation Instructions ... charging method' (II p.10, p.19). Charge with liquid refrigerant; a liquid-line drier is required (II p.20). No fan-coil charging target is published","key":true},{"label":"Brazing","value":"Pull the TXV bulb and wrap the valve before brazing"}]},{"title":"Electrical & Electric Heat (size 002, 208/230-1)","rows":[{"label":"Blower only","value":"FLA 4.3, MCA 5.4, 14 AWG, 15 A fuse/breaker (PD p.17)"},{"label":"Heaters allowed on 002","value":"Single-phase KFCEH 5, 8, 9, 10, 15 and 20 kW; three-phase 15 kW. 18 kW is listed only for 003-006; 24 and 30 kW only for 005/006 (PD p.17)"},{"label":"5 kW heater MCA / max fuse (single circuit)","value":"MCA 31.2/33.5 · max fuse/breaker 35/35 at 208/230 V - the PD p.18 row footnoted for FV4A","key":true},{"label":"8 / 9 / 10 / 15 / 20 kW heater MCA / MOCP","value":"See heater label / rating plate (FV4A applicability footnoted only on 5 kW)"},{"label":"Minimum CFM, heater only","value":"625 (5 kW) · 625 (8-10 kW) · 725 (15 kW) · 875 (18-20 kW) (PD p.7)"},{"label":"Heater clearance","value":"Keep 1 in. from combustibles for 36 in. of duct with 20 kW or larger heaters. A unit with no heater needs a block-off plate over the heater opening"}]},{"title":"Drain & Filter","rows":[{"label":"Drains","value":"Primary and secondary, 3/4 in. FPT (PD p.4, II p.10). Trap both lines, 2 in. minimum trap depth (II Fig. 14) - standard shallow traps are not enough. Prime the traps. Pitch at least 1 in. per 10 ft. Secondary pan required over living space. PVC fittings finger-tight plus 1-1/2 turns","key":true},{"label":"Filter","value":"21-1/2 x 16-3/8, factory cleanable. Replacement 12-pack KFAFK0212MED (PD p.3, p.16)","key":true},{"label":"Front service clearance","value":"21 in. (PD p.4)"}]},{"title":"Controls & Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Easy Select board","value":"5 A blade fuse and 40 VA transformer (PD p.2, II p.12)"},{"label":"Fault codes","value":"No LED fault codes are published. Troubleshoot with 24 VAC checks at SEC1/SEC2 and voltage checks on the 12-pin PL-1 and 16-pin harness plugs (II p.15-16)"},{"label":"Maintenance","value":"Filter monthly; coil, pan and drain each cooling season; blower each season (II p.20)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The two Carrier documents disagree - size 002 system range and some airflows","body":"The II says size 002 pairs with 024-036 and the PD says 018-036. Two-speed low-speed and fan-only medium airflows also differ (II 680/545 vs PD 660/530). Neither document is marked as superseding the other - verify against the outdoor unit and the rating plate."},{"title":"Use PD p.6 for heat pump heating CFM","body":"II Table 4 (heat pump heating) repeats the cooling numbers, which contradicts its own text (heating about 315 CFM/ton). For heat pump heating CFM use PD p.6: Comfort 470/630/785/945, Efficiency 525/700/875/1050."},{"title":"Heater MCA/MOCP: only the 5 kW row is confirmed for FV4A","body":"PD p.18 footnotes FV4A applicability only on the 5 kW row (MCA 31.2/33.5, max fuse 35/35). The other kW rows are the table's general rows and were not confirmed for FV4A - use the heater's own label as final."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"FE5B (Infinity communicating fan coil, R-454B)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Carrier 2024+ Infinity Series communicating variable-speed multipoise fan coil for Puron Advance (R-454B, an A2L refrigerant) with a factory leak detection and dissipation system, sizes 24/36/48/60. This is NOT the R-410A FE4A/FE5A - in FE5B the '5' means R-454B, while in FE4A/FE5A both units are R-410A ('4' = multipoise, '5' = upflow/downflow only). Figures below are for size 36 (FE5BNXC36).","match":["FE5B","FE5BN","FE5BNX","FE5BNB","FE5BNXC36","FE5BNXB24","FE5BNBC36","FE5BNXC48","FE5BNBC48","FE5BNBD60","Puron Advance fan coil"],"source":"Carrier FE5B Infinity Series Communicating Variable-Speed Multipoise Fan Coil with Puron Advance (R-454B) Product Data, Catalog FE5B-04PD (01/26, replaces FE5B-03PD); Carrier FE5B Installation Instructions, Catalog IM-FE5B-01 (3/24); FE4A/FE5A Communicating Fan Coil Installation Instructions, Catalog IM-FE4A-05 (04/18), for the decode comparison only","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (FE5BNXC36)","value":"F = fan coil · E = Infinity, variable-speed constant-airflow ECM, multipoise · 5 = Puron Advance (R-454B) · B = series · N = 208/230 V, 1-phase, 60 Hz · X = single-piece cabinet with hard-shutoff TXV (B = modular) · C = 21-1/8 in. cabinet width · 36 = 36,000 BTUH · the full part number ends L00 = aluminum coil (PD p3)"},{"label":"Not the FE4A/FE5A","value":"Different: R-454B refrigerant, a leak dissipation board with its own flash codes, 24/36/48/60 size coding instead of 002-006, different TXV part numbers and heater tables, multipoise (FE5A is not). Same: communicating control (needs an Infinity wall control), 350 CFM/ton, amber STATUS / green COMM LED logic, status codes 16, 25, 26, 27, 36, 37, 41, 44, 45, 46, 53, emergency mode through RGWYOC, 3 A low-voltage fuse","key":true},{"label":"Nominal size","value":"3 ton; matches outdoor units from 24,000 to 42,000 BTUH (PD Table 2)"},{"label":"Cabinet","value":"53-7/16 in. H × 21-1/8 in. W × 22-1/16 in. D; 146 lb shipping; one piece or modular (PD Tables 2-3)"},{"label":"Documented models","value":"FE5BNXB24, FE5BNXC36, FE5BNBC36, FE5BNXC48, FE5BNBC48, FE5BNBD60 (PD Table 1)"}]},{"title":"Blower & Airflow (size 36)","rows":[{"label":"Motor","value":"1/2 HP ECM, 4.0 FLA (PD Tables 3, 10). Before replacing the ECM control module wait 5 minutes and check the motor windings; with the panel off, the blower running slowly is normal (IM p14)"},{"label":"Airflow control","value":"The wall control commands airflow, 350 CFM/ton nominal. Size-36 nominal choices 700 / 875 / 1050 / 1225 CFM, adjustable +15% / -10% (PD Table 3, p8, p12)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum UL airflow with electric heat","value":"5 kW 700 CFM · 8-10 kW 750 · 12-15 kW 1050 · 18-20 kW 1225 (PD Table 5)"},{"label":"Minimum airflow in dissipation mode","value":"133 CFM at 5 lb total system charge up to 665 CFM at 25 lb (IM Table 4)"},{"label":"Filter","value":"20 × 20 in. (508 × 508 mm) on sizes 36 and 48; 16 × 20 on 24, 24 × 20 on 60. Replacement 12-pack AFAFLTLRG12A. Never run the unit without a filter (PD Table 3; IM Table 1)","key":true}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & Metering","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-454B (Puron Advance) - A2L, see flag (PD p1)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Factory bi-flow hard-shutoff TXV with mechanical fittings; replacement part EA66YP002 on the 36 (PD Table 3)"},{"label":"Coil","value":"Slope coil, 3 rows at 14.5 fins per inch, aluminum (PD Table 3)"},{"label":"Line connections","value":"3/8 in. liquid, 3/4 in. suction, sweat (PD Table 3)"},{"label":"Charging","value":"Use the outdoor unit's installation instructions - no charging target is in the fan coil documents. Joints must hold 700 psig. Pressure test with about 200 psi nitrogen for 1 hour. Evacuate to 500 microns; it must not rise above 1500 microns in 10 minutes (IM p9, p12)"}]},{"title":"Electrical & Electric Heat (size 36; MCA and max fuse/breaker at 208 V / 230 V)","rows":[{"label":"Unit with no heat","value":"MCA 5, MOCP 15, 14 AWG (PD Table 10)"},{"label":"5 kW (N05 or C05)","value":"MCA 27.3 / 29.6 · max fuse/breaker 30 / 30 (PD Tables 11, 13)","key":true},{"label":"8 kW","value":"MCA 40.6 / 44.4 · 45 / 45"},{"label":"9 kW, 1-phase","value":"MCA 45.3 / 49.5 · 50 / 50"},{"label":"9 kW, 3-phase","value":"MCA 28.3 / 30.8 · 30 / 35"},{"label":"10 kW","value":"MCA 49.5 / 54.3 · 50 / 60"},{"label":"15 kW, 1-phase, single circuit","value":"MCA 71.8 / 78.9 · 80 / 80"},{"label":"15 kW, dual circuit","value":"MCA 49.5/54.3 and 22.3/24.6 · 50/60 and 25/25"},{"label":"15 kW, 3-phase (KFFEH1601315)","value":"MCA 43.5 / 47.6 · 50 / 50"},{"label":"18 kW","value":"See rating plate - PD Table 2 lists 18 kW for size 36, but the electrical table (Table 13) only covers 18 kW (KFFEH3601318) for sizes 48-60"},{"label":"20 kW, single circuit","value":"MCA 94.0 / 103.5 · 100 / 110"},{"label":"20 kW, dual circuit","value":"MCA 49.5/54.3 and 44.5/49.3 · 50/60 and 45/50"},{"label":"Heater notes","value":"15 and 20 kW fused heaters need kit KFASP0101SPK for single-circuit wiring (PD Table 11). With 3-phase heaters (9 kW 3-phase and KFFEH1601315) the dissipation system has to be moved to the outside of the unit (IM p12)"}]},{"title":"Condensate","rows":[{"label":"Drains","value":"Primary and secondary, 3/4 in. FPT. Both lines need deep traps; standard shallow P-traps are not enough. Factory trap kit KFAET0150ETK. Slope 1 in. per 10 ft. Hand-tighten plus 1-1/2 turns. Prime both traps (IM p9-10; PD p20)"}]},{"title":"Controls & Diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Communication","value":"4-wire ABCD. Low-voltage fuse 3 A. Transformer 40 VA (PD p2; IM p12, p14)"},{"label":"Status codes","value":"Same amber STATUS / green COMM LED logic and codes as FE4A/FE5A: 16, 25, 26, 27, 36, 37, 41, 44, 45, 46, 53. Code 25 shows after a control board replacement until the model size is entered at the wall control (IM p15). A replacement control board or heater ID problem stops the electric heat (26, 36, 37)"},{"label":"Leak dissipation board LED","value":"Solid yellow = normal · Flash 1 = sensor sees 20% or more of the flammability limit · 2 = sensor open · 3 = normal cleanup after a leak · 4 = no power to the fan output · 5 = sensor fault · 6 = test button stuck · 7 = Y or W wiring reversed · 8 = Y or W shorted (IM Tables 2, 5)","key":true},{"label":"Dissipation board test button","value":"Hold 1-4 s for a 60-second dissipation test; 5-29 s to show flash history; three quick presses clears the history (IM Tables 2, 5)"},{"label":"A2L sensor (size 36)","value":"Always sits on the drain pan clip; must never face connector-up; keep it free of dust (IM p10-11)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Not the FE4A/FE5A - the '5' means R-454B here","body":"FE5A to FE5B is not a simple revision. FE5B is Carrier's 2024+ Infinity fan coil for R-454B with a leak sensor and dissipation board; FE4A/FE5A are R-410A. Refrigerant, TXV part numbers, heater tables and size coding all differ, so do not carry FE4A/FE5A figures over."},{"title":"A2L refrigerant with a leak dissipation system","body":"R-454B is mildly flammable. The wall control and outdoor unit software must be on current versions or the dissipation system may not work (IM p12). A blower running with no call can be the dissipation board doing its job - read its LED (solid yellow = normal, flash 1-8 = codes above) before condemning anything."},{"title":"Charging target and max static are not in the fan-coil literature","body":"Charge per the matched outdoor unit's installation instructions or rating plate. Carrier does not publish a single maximum external static for the FE5B, so none is listed here - the PD only warns that high return static makes the drain trap hard to seal (PD p10, p12)."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Goodman","model":"GSC13 (13 SEER R-22 condenser)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Goodman GSC13 split-system air conditioner (condensing unit), 13 SEER, R-22, 1-1/2 to 5 ton family. Figures below are for the 3-ton GSC130361 (208/230-1-60). The scanned tag stops before the two revision letters, and charge, MCA/MOCP, RLA/LRA and capacitor all changed between revisions - the rating plate decides which set applies. Published 0361 revisions: AA, BA, BB, DA-DF, EA/EB, F and G.","match":["GSC13","GSC13036","GSC130361","13 SEER R-22"],"source":"Goodman GSC13 Product Specifications SS-GSC13 (4/12, G revision); SS-GSC13 (1/10, F revision); SS-GSC13 (4/06, AA/BA revisions); Goodman GSC13 Installation & Operating Instructions IO-402E (12/2011); Goodman Repair Parts RP-431G (6/2009); Goodman Submittal SF-GSC13 (11/13)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (GSC130361)","value":"G = Goodman (standard feature set) · S = split system · C = condenser, R-22 (X would be R-410A, H would be an R-22 heat pump) · 13 = 13 SEER · 036 = 3 tons nominal · 1 = 208/230 V, 1 phase, 60 Hz · the next two letters (major and minor revision) are missing from the scan (SS-GSC13 4/12 p.2)"},{"label":"Type","value":"Split-system AC condenser, cooling only, no defrost (SS-GSC13 4/12)"},{"label":"Rating","value":"36,000 BTU/h nominal; with coil CA*F3636*6C*+EEP rated 33,800 total / 24,670 sensible, 13 SEER / 11 EER (SS-GSC13 4/12 p.4). Rated combinations need the EEP (cooling fan time delay) on the indoor unit"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-22 - use R-22 certified to AHRI standards only (IO-402E)"},{"label":"Shipping state - depends on revision","value":"Earlier units came charged with R-22 for 15 ft of line (SS 4/06, SS 1/10). The 4/12 G-revision unit ships 'charged with inert gas for shipping' (dry, nitrogen/helium holding charge) and must be evacuated and charged to the rating plate (SS 4/12 p.1; IO-402E p.1). The later SF-GSC13 11/13 submittal still says 'R-22 refrigerant-charged for 15 ft of refrigerant lines' - check the unit's own notice label","key":true},{"label":"Factory / nominal charge (15 ft of 3/8 in. liquid line), by revision","value":"0361AA and BA: 125 oz (SS 4/06) · 0361F: 83 oz (SS 1/10) · 0361G: 77 oz (SS 4/12) · GSC13036 dry-ship: 77 oz (IO-402E p.1/7) · any other revision: see rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Piston (fixed orifice) shipped with the outdoor unit: 0.074 (AA), 0.071 (BA and F); the G unit has an 'R-22 piston kit included'. Use the outdoor unit's piston or the piston chart packed with the indoor coil (SS 4/06; SS 1/10; SS 4/12 p.1, p.4)","key":true},{"label":"Charging, piston units","value":"Superheat method. Wait 10 minutes to stabilize; outdoor temperature must be 60 °F or higher. Target read from the chart by outdoor dry bulb and indoor wet bulb. At 67 °F indoor wet bulb: 80 °F outdoor = 17 °F · 85 °F = 13 °F · 90 °F = 10 °F · 95 °F = 5 °F superheat (IO-402E p.1)","key":true},{"label":"Charging, TXV units","value":"Subcooling 7 ±2 °F and superheat 8 ±1 °F after 20 minutes of stabilization. Do not charge by suction pressure (IO-402E p.7)"},{"label":"Evacuation","value":"Remove the holding charge before brazing. Evacuate to 250 microns or less, using both valves (IO-402E)"}]},{"title":"Line set (3 ton)","rows":[{"label":"Line sizes by length","value":"0-24 ft: 3/4 in. suction / 3/8 in. liquid · 25-49 ft: 7/8 in. / 3/8 in. · 50-79 ft: 1-1/8 in. / 3/8 in. Over 79 ft, or more than 50 ft of vertical rise: see the Remote Cooling Service Manual or TP-106 (IO-402E p.3)"},{"label":"Spec-sheet line size","value":"3/8 in. liquid, 7/8 in. suction. The suction valve is 3/4 in. sweat, so the installer must supply a 3/4 in. to 7/8 in. adapter (SS 1/10; SS 4/12 p.3)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208-230/1/60, min/max 197/253 V) - by revision","rows":[{"label":"Revision G (SS 4/12)","value":"MCA 17.9 A · max fuse/breaker 30 A · compressor RLA/LRA 13.4/74, reciprocating · fan 1/6 HP, 1.1 FLA","key":true},{"label":"Revision F (SS 1/10)","value":"MCA 16.4 A · max fuse/breaker 25 A · RLA/LRA 12.2/73, reciprocating · fan 1/6 HP, 1.1 FLA"},{"label":"Revision BA (SS 4/06)","value":"MCA 18.3 A · max fuse/breaker 30 A · RLA/LRA 13.4/73 · fan 1/6 HP, 1.5 FLA"},{"label":"Revision AA (SS 4/06)","value":"MCA 16.8 A · max fuse/breaker 20 A · RLA/LRA 12.2/73 · fan 1/6 HP, 1.5 FLA"},{"label":"Other revisions (C/D/E spec sheets not reviewed)","value":"See rating plate"},{"label":"Overcurrent protection","value":"Fuses must be time-delay, or use HACR breakers (SS 4/12). Wire for 2% maximum voltage drop (IO-402E)"},{"label":"Run capacitor (dual), by revision","value":"0361BB: 45/5 µF, 370 V · 0361DA/DB/DF/EA/EB: 35/5 µF, 440 V · F and G: not published - see rating plate or the capacitor label (RP-431G, 6/09)","key":true},{"label":"Hard-start kit","value":"Reciprocating compressor: a non-bleed TXV or liquid-line solenoid requires a hard-start kit. CSR-U-1 and CSR-U-2 are both listed for the 036 (IO-402E p.5/9; SS 4/12 p.7)"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"High / low pressure switches","value":"None factory-installed in any source found; they appear only as accessories (SS 4/06 p.1)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Read the full model incl. revision letters off the plate","body":"The scan stops at GSC130361. Charge (125 / 83 / 77 oz), MCA (16.4-18.3 A), MOCP (20-30 A), RLA/LRA and the capacitor all change with the revision letters (e.g. GSC130361GB). Read the full model plus MCA, MOCP and charge off the rating plate before ordering parts or charging."},{"title":"Dry-ship R-22 units are replacement-only","body":"A dry-ship (nitrogen/helium holding charge) R-22 unit is for component replacement on pre-2010 systems only. Whether this particular unit shipped charged or dry is not confirmed - check the notice label (IO-402E)."},{"title":"3/4 in. suction valve vs 7/8 in. line","body":"The suction service valve is 3/4 in. sweat while the spec-sheet line size is 7/8 in. - have the adapter on hand."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"MMPD (4th-gen R-32 mini-split outdoor heat pump)","equip":"Mini-Split","summary":"Lennox 4th-generation R-32 mini-split heat pump OUTDOOR unit (not an indoor head), 2 ton: MMPD024S6M-1P multi-zone (up to 3 zones) and MMPD024S6S-1P single-zone. The two versions have OPPOSITE charge rules. The scanned 'MMPD024S4-1P' does not exist in Lennox literature - read the plate for S6M vs S6S. Indoor CFM, external static, filter and condensate pump figures belong to the matched indoor unit.","match":["MMPD","MMPD024","MMPD024S","MMPD024S6M-1P","MMPD024S6S-1P","MMPD024S6M","MMPD024S6S","R-32 mini-split"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) MMPD Multi-Zone, Form 211077 (March 2025); Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) MMPD Single-Zone, Form 211078 (March 2025); Lennox Installation Manual MMPD***S6M-1P, DB68-13146A-02; Lennox Installation Manual MM*D***S6S-1P, DB68-12970A-03","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode","value":"M = mini-split · M = works with mixed indoor unit types · P = heat pump · D = 4th generation · 024 = 2 tons · S = standard efficiency · 6 = R-32 · M or S = multi-zone or single-zone · -1 = 1st revision · P = 208/230 V, 1 phase, 60 Hz (EHB Model Number Identification, Forms 211077/211078)","key":true},{"label":"No R-410A '4' version","value":"No Lennox document lists an MMPD model with a '4' (R-410A) in the refrigerant position. Earlier R-410A multi-zone units had different prefixes (MPB, MLA). 'S4' on the scan is most likely a misread of 'S6' with the M/S letter missing"},{"label":"Error codes","value":"Shown on the outdoor main board's two-digit display ('PCB MAIN-OUT') and listed in the Troubleshooting appendix of each install manual. Multi-zone E563 = combination not allowed: an MDDD or MMD indoor unit is in the system and total indoor capacity is more than 100% of the outdoor unit (EHB 211077)"}]},{"title":"Multi-zone MMPD024S6M-1P","rows":[{"label":"Capacity","value":"Cooling 22,000 Btuh · heating 25,000 at 47 °F and 14,600 at 17 °F · up to 22.5 SEER2 and 9.5 HSPF2 with non-ducted heads (EHB 211077)"},{"label":"Refrigerant charge","value":"Factory charge 4 lb 7 oz of R-32 (install manual: 70.5 oz / 2000 g). DO NOT add or remove refrigerant for line length (EHB 211077; DB68-13146A-02)","key":true},{"label":"Zones and piping","value":"3 zones. Liquid ports (3) 1/4 in.; gas ports (1) 3/8 in. + (2) 1/2 in. flare. 230 ft total, 82 ft to any one indoor unit. Height difference 50 ft to outdoor, 25 ft between indoor units (EHB 211077)"},{"label":"Pairs with","value":"007-018 wall units (MWMD, MWHD, MWZD) and 009-018 cassettes, ducted units, consoles and air handlers (M1WD, M22D, MMDD, MDDD, MFMD, MMD). 024 indoor units are allowed only on the 036 and 048 outdoor units. High-static ducted (MDDD) or air handler (MMD) units are limited to 2-unit systems at no more than 100% of outdoor capacity, otherwise E563 (EHB 211077)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 14-115 °F, heating 5-75 °F (EHB 211077)"},{"label":"Compressor and oil","value":"Twin BLDC rotary; POE oil 22.7 oz (EHB 211077). Compressor current (RLA): see rating plate - not clearly stated in the multi-zone install manual"},{"label":"Outdoor fan / sound","value":"1668 CFM; 48 dBA cooling, 51 dBA heating (EHB 211077)"},{"label":"Electrical","value":"MCA 20.5, MOCP 25 A. Main power cable 12 AWG (EHB 211077; DB68-13146A-02)","key":true},{"label":"Wiring","value":"The indoor units get their power from the outdoor unit: 14 AWG, 3 wires. Communication runs on F1/F2 with 18 AWG, 2 wires. Keep the power cable and the F1/F2 cable at least 2 in. apart (DB68-13146A-02)"},{"label":"Weight","value":"126 lb net (EHB 211077)"}]},{"title":"Single-zone MMPD024S6S-1P","rows":[{"label":"Capacity","value":"Cooling 24,000 Btuh · heating 27,000 at 47 °F; the 17 °F figure depends on which indoor unit it is paired with (EHB 211078)"},{"label":"Refrigerant charge","value":"Factory charge 3 lb 12 oz of R-32. ADD 0.161 oz/ft for each foot over 24.6 ft; maximum total charge 82.5 oz (EHB 211078; DB68-12970A-03). Other MMPD single-zone sizes are listed at up to 0.323 oz/ft - use the plate/manual for the size on hand","key":true},{"label":"Piping","value":"Liquid 1/4 in., gas 5/8 in. flare. Max 164 ft of pipe and 98.4 ft of height difference (EHB 211078; DB68-12970A-03)"},{"label":"Pairs with","value":"M33D024S6-1P (non-ducted), MDDD024S6-1P (high-static ducted) or MMD024S6-1P (air handler) (EHB 211078)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 0-122 °F, heating -4 to 75 °F (EHB 211078)"},{"label":"Compressor and oil","value":"Twin rotary, compressor current (RLA) 14.4 A; POE oil 23.7 oz (EHB 211078; DB68-12970A-03)"},{"label":"Outdoor fan","value":"2154 CFM, 1.20 A (EHB 211078; DB68-12970A-03)"},{"label":"Electrical","value":"MCA 22.3, MOCP 25 A (EHB 211078; DB68-12970A-03)","key":true},{"label":"Base drain","value":"Do not fit a drain hose, plug or cap on the unit base; let the water drain naturally (DB68-12970A-03)"}]},{"title":"R-32 handling (both versions)","rows":[{"label":"Leak test / evacuation","value":"Leak test with nitrogen at 595 psi, then evacuate three times (4000, 2000 and 500 microns) with a 10-minute hold (DB68-13146A-02; DB68-12970A-03)","key":true}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Scanned 'MMPD024S4-1P' does not exist - read the plate for S6M vs S6S","body":"Lennox documents only two 2-ton MMPD units, MMPD024S6M-1P (multi-zone) and MMPD024S6S-1P (single-zone), and neither has a '4' in the refrigerant position. The scan probably misread 'S6' as 'S4' and dropped the M/S letter. Re-read the plate (or photograph it) before charging - the two versions have opposite charge rules."},{"title":"Charge rules are opposite between the two versions","body":"Multi-zone S6M: factory charge only (4 lb 7 oz) - never add refrigerant for line length. Single-zone S6S: factory 3 lb 12 oz, add 0.161 oz/ft past 24.6 ft, max 82.5 oz total. Charging the wrong way is the easy mistake."},{"title":"R-32 is mildly flammable (A2L)","body":"Keep ignition sources away, use a leak detector rated for R-32, and follow the room-size charge limits in the manuals. Leak test with nitrogen at 595 psi, then evacuate three times (4000, 2000 and 500 microns) with a 10-minute hold."}]},
  {"brand":"Amana","model":"ASX13 (ASX130611A, 5 ton 13 SEER R-410A condenser)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Amana ASX13 13 SEER R-410A split AC condenser, 5 ton, 208/230-1-60 - figures for the ASX130611A (35-1/2 in. cabinet), which replaced the 29 in. ASX130601; do not reuse 0601 data. Ships with a piston (charge by superheat) - charge by subcooling only if the indoor coil has a TXV. Low pressure switch and CoreSense module, NO high pressure switch - the GSX14/ASX14 entry's figures do not apply.","match":["ASX13","ASX1306","ASX13061","ASX130611","ASX130611A","ASX130611AB","ASX130611AA"],"source":"Amana Product Specifications SS-ASX13 (rev 2/14A); Goodman Repair Parts RP-748C (Aug 2016, lists ASX130611AB by name); Goodman Service Manual RS6200006r97 (Dec 2019); Goodman Service Manual RS6200006r101; Amana SS-ASX14 (rev 2/20 and rev 4/12) for the ASX14 comparison only","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ASX130611AB)","value":"A = Amana brand · S = split system · X = R-410A condenser · 13 = 13 SEER · 061 = 5-ton model (the nomenclature chart lists only '060 = 5 tons'; RS6200006r97 says ASX130611AA 'replaced ASX130601* models') · 1 = 208/230 V, 1 phase, 60 Hz · A-B = engineering major/minor revision (SS-ASX13)"},{"label":"Capacity","value":"56,500 BTU/h nominal cooling; 13.0-14.5 SEER and 11.0-12.0 EER depending on the matched indoor unit (SS-ASX13 AHRI tables)"},{"label":"Cabinet","value":"35-1/2 in. W × 35-1/2 in. D × 38-1/4 in. H, 211 lb (SS-ASX13). The 061 is a different cabinet from the 29 in. 060"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & Charging","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A (SS-ASX13)"},{"label":"Factory charge","value":"130 oz, covers 15 ft of 3/8 in. liquid line (SS-ASX13). Add 0.6 oz per foot of liquid line beyond 15 ft (RS6200006r101)","key":true},{"label":"Piston","value":"0.086 shipped with the unit (flow-check piston kit B1789886). Use the one supplied with the outdoor unit, or the one on the indoor unit's piston kit chart (SS-ASX13; RP-748C)","key":true},{"label":"TXV kit, if used","value":"TX5N4 (RS6200006r97)"},{"label":"Charging, fixed orifice","value":"By superheat using the superheat table, with a thermometer 4-6 in. from the compressor (RS6200006r101)"},{"label":"Charging, TXV","value":"By subcooling, target 5-7 °F, with superheat 7-9 °F; outdoor temperature must be 60 °F or higher (RS6200006r101, generic service-manual target). Unit-specific design subcooling for the 0611: see rating plate - not published; the spec sheet's '9 ±3 °F' is printed only for the 0361D model"},{"label":"Published reference point","value":"At 95 °F outdoor, 80 °F dry bulb / 67 °F wet bulb indoor and 1,750 CFM: about 388 psig liquid / 136 psig suction, 21.2 A outdoor unit, 22 °F ΔT. Pressures measured at the service valves (SS-ASX13)"}]},{"title":"Lines & Valves","rows":[{"label":"Liquid line","value":"3/8 in. (SS-ASX13)"},{"label":"Suction line","value":"7/8 in. (sizes are for a 25 ft line set) (SS-ASX13)"},{"label":"Suction service valve - sources conflict","value":"Spec sheet SS-ASX13 says 3/4 in.; parts list RP-748C says 7/8 in. base valve (0151R00080). Verify on the unit and have adapters on hand"},{"label":"Liquid service valve","value":"3/8 in., sweat (SS-ASX13)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1-60, allowed range 197-253 V)","rows":[{"label":"MCA / MOCP","value":"MCA 34.5 · MOCP 60 A using time-delay fuse or HACR breaker (SS-ASX13)","key":true},{"label":"Compressor","value":"RLA 26.4, LRA 134, Copeland scroll ZP51K5EPFV130 (SS-ASX13; RP-748C)"},{"label":"Condenser fan","value":"1/4 HP, 1.5 FLA, 1 speed, 8 pole, 26 in. aluminum CCW blade (SS-ASX13; RP-748C). Rev AC later changed the fan motor (0131M00061 replaced by 0131M00807) - on this AB unit confirm the motor part number before ordering (RS6200006r97)"},{"label":"Run capacitor","value":"5/70 MFD, 440 V, dual round (RP-748C)","key":true},{"label":"Contactor","value":"30 A, 1 pole, 24 V (RP-748C)"},{"label":"Diagnostics","value":"CoreSense module 571006600 (RP-748C; wiring diagram 0140R00274-A in SS-ASX13)"}]},{"title":"Pressure Switches","rows":[{"label":"Low pressure switch - setpoint conflict","value":"Equipped, part 0130M00082 (RP-748C). RS6200006r101 says it opens at 21 psig and resets around 50 psig; RS6200006r97 says around 55 psig open / 95 psig close 'for air conditioners'. The two manual revisions disagree - verify against the switch on the unit","key":true},{"label":"High pressure switch","value":"None. It is not on the ASX130611A wiring diagram or in the parts list (SS-ASX13; RP-748C)","key":true}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Low-pressure switch setpoints conflict between manual revisions","body":"Goodman service manual RS6200006r101 says the low pressure switch opens at 21 psig and resets around 50 psig; the earlier RS6200006r97 says around 55 psig open / 95 psig close 'for air conditioners'. Neither revision is marked as correcting the other - verify on the unit before condemning a switch."},{"title":"Suction valve size conflicts","body":"SS-ASX13 says the suction service valve is 3/4 in.; RP-748C lists a 7/8 in. base valve (0151R00080). The spec-sheet suction LINE is 7/8 in. either way. Have adapters on hand."},{"title":"Not the ASX14 - do not carry GSX14/ASX14 figures over","body":"ASX14 5-ton (ASX140601K per SS-ASX14 2/20; 4/12 rev B figures in brackets): 120 oz charge [268 oz], 0.088 piston, 1-1/8 in. suction, MCA/MOCP 32.6/50 [34.6/60], RLA 25.0 [26.4], fan 1.3 FLA [1.6]. This ASX130611A is 130 oz, 0.086 piston, 7/8 in. suction, MCA/MOCP 34.5/60, RLA 26.4, fan 1.5 FLA. The GSX14 entry's high pressure switch row (610 / 420 psig) does not apply - this unit has no high pressure switch."},{"title":"Piston ships in the box; a TXV coil means subcooling","body":"It ships with a piston for the indoor coil. If the coil has a TXV, charge by subcooling (5-7 °F generic target), not superheat."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL195DF (Elite 95% downflow)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Elite EL195DF 95% AFUE single-stage DOWNFLOW condensing furnace (Duralok Plus clamshell heat exchanger with a stainless condensing coil, SureLight control), non-communicating. Two blower generations share the 'EL195DF1...' prefix: 2011 PSC 'P' units (EL195DF045P36B / 070P48B / 090P60C / 110P60C) and 2018+ constant-torque 'XE' units (EL195DF045XE36B / 070XE48B / 090XE48C / 110XE60C). Figures below are for the 110 size where tables split. A different platform from the ML195/ML196E and the EL195UHNE - do not share that entry's flame thresholds, NG supply maximum or rollout row.","match":["EL195DF","EL195DFE","EL195DF110","EL195DF110XE60C","EL195DF110P60C","EL195DF045P36B","EL195DF070P48B","EL195DF090P60C","EL195DF045XE36B","EL195DF070XE48B","EL195DF090XE48C","95%","single-stage","condensing","elite series","furnace"],"source":"Lennox EL195DFE Product Specifications, Bulletin No. 210616 (March 2019); Lennox EL195DF Product Specifications, Bulletin No. 210593 (Sept 2011); Lennox EL195DF Unit Information, Corp. 1102-L1 (rev. 02/2012, 2011 P generation); Lennox EL195UHE Unit Information, Corp. 1118-L4 (11/2011), for the XE-generation flame table","groups":[{"title":"Ratings","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"95% (Bulletins 210616 and 210593)"},{"label":"Input / output, 110","value":"110,000 / 106,000 Btuh (Bulletins 210616 and 210593)"},{"label":"Other sizes","value":"045 = 44,000 / 42,000 · 070 = 66,000 / 64,000 · 090 = 88,000 / 85,000 Btuh"}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"SureLight control (A92)","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or more / Low 0.5-1.4 µA / Drop out 0.4 µA (Corp. 1102-L1; the same table appears in Corp. 1118-L4 for the XE generation). Do NOT apply the ML195/EL195UHNE thresholds (2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA) - 1.5 µA is normal on this unit, not low","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG / LP (all sizes)","value":"3.5 / 10.0 in. w.g. (Bulletin 210616)","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure NG","value":"4.5-13.0 in. w.g. (Bulletin 210616)"},{"label":"Supply pressure LP","value":"11.0-13.0 in. w.g. (Bulletin 210616)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG","value":"3.3 at 4501-5500 ft · 3.2 at 5501-6500 ft · 3.1 at 6501-7500 ft · back to 3.5 at 7501-10,000 ft with the orifice kit (Bulletin 210616)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, LP","value":"9.4 / 9.1 / 8.9 in. w.g. over the same ranges, back to 10.0 with the orifice kit (Bulletin 210616)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, 110","value":"NG 33 s/rev on a 1 cu ft dial (1000 Btu/cu ft); LP 66 s/rev on a 2 cu ft dial (2500 Btu/cu ft). Other sizes NG/LP: 045 = 80/160 s · 070 = 55/110 s · 090 = 41/82 s (published for the 2011 P-generation, Corp. 1102-L1 Table 14)"},{"label":"Combustion CO2 / CO","value":"NG 7.2-8.2%, LP 8.6-9.6%; CO 50 ppm max; run at least 15 minutes before sampling (published for the 2011 P-generation, Corp. 1102-L1 Table 15)"},{"label":"Conversion kits","value":"NG to LP 11K49 · LP to NG 73W81 · high-altitude orifice kits NG 73W37, LP 11K44 (Bulletin 210616)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise, 110","value":"40-70 °F (Bulletins 210616 and 210593)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, other sizes","value":"045 and 070 = 25-55 °F · 090 = 40-70 °F on XE units (Bulletin 210616) but 30-60 °F on P units (Bulletin 210593)"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5 in. w.g. (Bulletin 210616)"},{"label":"Blower, 110XE","value":"DC brushless constant-torque (ECM), 1 hp, 11 × 11 wheel, 1045-2285 cfm, 10.9 FLA (Bulletin 210616)"},{"label":"Blower, 110P","value":"PSC, 1 hp, 1330-2375 cfm (Bulletin 210593; Corp. 1102-L1)"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Field-supplied, none furnished. Optional downflow filter cabinet 51W08 (C width), (2) 16 × 20 × 1 (Bulletin 210616)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride hot-surface, 39-70 Ω, 102-132 VAC (Bulletin 210616; Corp. 1102-L1)","key":true},{"label":"Rollout switches (S47)","value":"Manual reset, 2 switches in the burner box, open at 210 °F ±12 °F (Bulletin 210616; Corp. 1102-L1)","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit (S10)","value":"Auto-reset, factory set, on the vestibule panel. Trip temperature: see rating plate (Bulletin 210616; Corp. 1102-L1)"},{"label":"Pressure switch, 110","value":"-0.90 in. w.c. at 0-4500 ft · -0.80 at 4501-7500 ft · -0.65 at 7501-10,000 ft (published for the 2011 P-generation, Corp. 1102-L1)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch, other sizes (0-4500 ft)","value":"045 = -0.65 · 070 and 090 = -0.90 in. w.c. (published for the 2011 P-generation, Corp. 1102-L1)"},{"label":"Inducer orifice, 110","value":"1.040 in. (published for the 2011 P-generation, Corp. 1102-L1)"},{"label":"High-altitude pressure-switch kits, 110XE","value":"11U71 for 4501-7500 ft, 11U64 for 7501-10,000 ft (Bulletin 210616). Above 4500 ft the pressure switch must be changed, and above 7500 ft the orifices too; manifold derate is the only permitted derate"}]},{"title":"Controls","rows":[{"label":"Board","value":"SureLight integrated control (A92), 40 VA transformer, single red LED with recall button (Bulletin 210616; Corp. 1102-L1). Part number not found in the documents - see rating plate or the repair parts list"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Two blower generations share the prefix - P (PSC) vs XE (constant-torque)","body":"Read the characters after the size: 'P' = 2011 PSC blower (capacitor), 'XE' = 2018+ constant-torque. Confirm which before diagnosing the blower. A 2011 constant-torque version was sold as 'EL195DFE...P...'. The pressure switch, inducer orifice, CO2 and clocking rows come only from Corp. 1102-L1, which covers the 2011 P generation - no public service manual for the XE downflow was found, so confirm those on an XE unit's plate."},{"title":"Do not use ML195/EL195UHNE flame thresholds","body":"This furnace's table is Normal 1.5 µA or more / Low 0.5-1.4 / Drop out 0.4 µA. The ML195/EL195UHNE row (2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA) would call a healthy 1.5 µA reading low."},{"title":"Rollout switches are manual reset","body":"A tripped S47 stays open until someone resets it, so find the cause (blocked heat exchanger or vent, low inducer draft) before resetting."},{"title":"Filters are external and field-supplied","body":"Downflow units are often installed with no filter at all."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59TP5A (Performance Boost two-stage)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Carrier 59TP5A 'Performance Boost' two-stage, 4-way multipoise condensing gas furnace, Series 100 - two-stage gas valve, two-speed inducer, basic multi-speed ECM blower with 5 speed taps (NOT variable speed), no communication, no LCD, no NFC. AFUE 96.2-96.7% (96.7% for the 100). Figures below are for the 100 size (100-20, 21 in. cabinet). Not a 59TP6/59TP7 - that entry's blower-off-delay switches and 'sets its own airflow' line are wrong for this unit.","match":["59TP5","59TP5A","59TP5A100","59TP5A100E21","59TP5A040","59TP5A060","59TP5A080","59TP5A120","Performance Boost"],"source":"Carrier 59TP5A Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions, Form 59TP5A-07SI (05/13); Carrier 59TP5A Product Data, Form 59TP5A-02PD (10/11)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode","value":"59 (family) · T (two-stage) · P (Performance) · 5 (95% AFUE class) · A (major series) · 040/060/080/100/120 (input) · E (motor - the 59TP5A always uses E, multi-speed ECM, never V) · 14/17/21/24 (cabinet width) · -- · 10-22 (airflow, ×100 CFM)"},{"label":"OCR trap","value":"A tag that reads '59TPBBOSOV171116' is a 59TP6B080V17--16 (6 read as B, 0 as O, 8 as S, '--' as '11'). No 59TP5B exists in Carrier literature, no 59TP5 has a V motor, and there is no 100V17 size - use the 59TP6 / 59TP7 entry for those"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Orifice / manifold table","value":"Table 21 (59TP5A-07SI): 20,000 BTUH high heat / 13,000 BTUH low heat per burner, derated 2% per 1,000 ft. Factory orifice #44. Same basis as the 59TP6/59TP7"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas","value":"High fire 3.2-3.8 in. w.c. · low fire 1.3-1.7 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Supply pressure","value":"4.5-13.6 in. w.c. per the product data (the manual says 4.5-14 in. w.c. / 0.5 psig max)"},{"label":"Propane manifold","value":"Not in the manual - it refers to the conversion kit KGANP51012SP instructions"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride hot-surface, 40-70 Ω cold","key":true}]},{"title":"Air (100 size)","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"High fire 45-75 °F · low fire 30-60 °F (product data spec table)","key":true},{"label":"Airflow control","value":"Speed taps - adjust the tap for proper rise. The furnace does NOT set its own airflow","key":true},{"label":"Blower CFM, 100-20 (Table 9)","value":"830 (Red at 1.0 in.) to 2340 (Gray at 0.1 in.). Rated: 1730 high heat, 1380 low heat, 1720 cooling"},{"label":"Certified ESP","value":"0.20 in. w.c. heating / 0.5 in. w.c. cooling. Tables run to 1.0 in."},{"label":"Filter (21 in. cabinet)","value":"20 × 25 × 3/4 or 20 × 25 × 4-5/16 (Table 7). Over 1800 CFM needs bottom or two-side return with at least 20 × 25"},{"label":"Cabinet note","value":"The 2011 product data calls the 100 size '100-16'; the later 2013 manual lists 100-20 (21 in. cabinet). The manual is used here - verify on the plate"}]},{"title":"Safeties & Controls","rows":[{"label":"Limit","value":"Product data spec table lists 160 for the 100 size (no unit is printed; °F presumed)"},{"label":"Rollout","value":"Manual-reset rollout switch in the burner assembly"},{"label":"Pressure switch","value":"No set point published. The manual only gives a worked example (0.68 in. nominal break) - do not use it as a spec"},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"4.0-6.0 µA nominal; below 0.5 µA is a fault (troubleshooting guide)","key":true},{"label":"Blower off-delay","value":"Setup switches SW-2 / SW-3, choices 90/120/150/180 s. Two-stage lockout is SW-1 (LHT). NOT SW-7/SW-8","key":true},{"label":"Status LED","value":"Amber, two-digit code (short flashes, then long). Rapid flash means reversed polarity or no ground"},{"label":"Diagnostics","value":"No LCD, no NFC, no communication"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Not the 59TP6/59TP7 - three figures differ","body":"Blower off-delay is SW-2/SW-3 (not SW-7/SW-8); the blower runs on speed taps, so the furnace does not set its own airflow; there is no LCD or NFC. The orifice table basis, natural gas manifold limits, supply pressure, igniter, status LED, flame signal and manual-reset rollout are the same as the 59TP6/59TP7."},{"title":"Propane manifold pressure and pressure-switch set point are not published","body":"Use the KGANP51012SP conversion kit instructions for LP. The manual's 0.68 in. pressure-switch figure is a worked example, not a spec - read the switch label."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL296DFE (downflow, constant-torque)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Elite EL296DFE two-stage 96% AFUE DOWNFLOW condensing furnace with the constant-torque 'E' blower (non-communicating, SureLight control). Decode EL296DF070XE48B: EL · 2 (two-stage) · 96 · DF (downflow) · 070 (66,000 Btuh) · X (low NOx) · E (high-efficiency constant-torque blower) · 48 · B (17-1/2 in. cabinet). Figures below are for the 070. Gas train, ignitor and flame table match the EL296UHE; the pressure switch, max static and rollout trip do NOT.","match":["EL296DF","EL296DFE","EL296DF070","EL296DF070XE48B","96%","two-stage","condensing","elite series","furnace"],"source":"Lennox EL296DFE Product Specifications, Bulletin No. 210648 (April 2021); Lennox EL296DFE Installation Instructions 507069-05 (06/2020); Lennox EL296DFE Service Literature, Corp. 1247-L10 (revised 03/2014)","groups":[{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"SureLight control","value":"Normal 2.6 µA or more / Low 2.5 µA or less / Drop out 0.6 µA (Corp. 1247-L10 Table 9 - the same values as the EL296UHE)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold pressure NG (low/high fire)","value":"1.7 / 3.5 in. w.g.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure LP/propane (low/high fire)","value":"4.5 / 10.0 in. w.g."},{"label":"Supply line pressure NG","value":"4.5-13.0 in. w.g."},{"label":"Supply line pressure LP","value":"11.0-13.0 in. w.g."},{"label":"Altitude","value":"Same altitude derate bands as the EL296UHE, approved to 10,000 ft"}]},{"title":"Air (070)","rows":[{"label":"Max external static - Lennox documents disagree","value":"Corp. 1247-L10 says 0.5 in. w.c. for both heat and cool speed, and Bulletin 210648 rates 'High static 0.5'; the 2020 Installation Instructions 507069-05 say it is not certified above 0.8 in. w.c. in heating. There is no 1.0 in. cooling figure for the DFE - the EL296V / EL296E entry's 0.8 heating / 1.0 cooling is not supported for this unit","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, 070","value":"35-65 °F high fire · 25-55 °F low fire","key":true},{"label":"CFM, 070","value":"520-1770"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Downflow filter cabinet 51W07 takes (2) 16 × 20 × 1. The Installation Instructions give a 16 × 25 × 1 minimum for the 17-1/2 in. cabinet"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride hot-surface, 39-70 Ω, 20-second warm-up"},{"label":"Pressure switch, 0-4500 ft (low/high fire)","value":"-045 0.35/0.60 · -070 0.45/0.90 · -090 0.50/0.90 · -110 0.45/0.90 in. w.c. (Corp. 1247-L10 Table 11)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch, 070 at altitude","value":"4501-7500 ft 0.45/0.81 · 7500-10,000 ft 0.41/0.74 in. w.c. (Corp. 1247-L10)"},{"label":"Rollout (S47)","value":"Factory-set to trip at 210 °F, manual reset","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"9th character E = constant-torque; a V unit uses the EL296V entry","body":"EL296DF070XE48B is an EL296DFE (constant-torque, non-communicating). A tag with V in that position (e.g. EL296DF070XV48B) is the variable-speed/communicating EL296DFV - use the EL296V / EL296E entry for that unit. Neither literal token 'EL296DFE' nor 'EL296DFV' appears in the full tag, because the E or V comes after the size."},{"title":"Pressure switch, static and rollout differ from the EL296UHE","body":"The EL296V / EL296E entry's UHE values (-070 0.50/0.90, -045 0.40/0.70) are wrong for this unit: the DFE -070 is 0.45/0.90 and -045 is 0.35/0.60 in. w.c. Max static is 0.5 in. w.c. (see the conflict row), and the rollout trip is published at 210 °F rather than 'not published'."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"26SCA4 / 26SCA5 (Comfort single-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Carrier Comfort Series single-stage split-system air conditioner (condenser only), Puron Advance R-454B (A2L), scroll compressor. 26SCA4 = 13.4 SEER2 class, North region (N); 26SCA5 = 14.3 SEER2 class, Southwest region (W). Sizes 18-60 (1.5-5 tons). The two models differ in almost every figure a tech measures - check digit 6 of the model (4 or 5) before using any number. The figure groups below are separate per model.","match":["26SCA4","26SCA5","26SCA418N003","26SCA424N003","26SCA430N003","26SCA436N003","26SCA442N003","26SCA448N013","26SCA460N003","26SCA518W003","26SCA524W003","26SCA530W003","26SCA536W023","26SCA542W013","26SCA548W013","26SCA560W003"],"source":"Carrier 26SCA4 Product Data, Cat. 26SCA4-02PD (09/25); Carrier 26SCA5 Product Data, Cat. 26SCA5-02PD (06/25); Carrier 26SCA4, 26SCA5 Installation Instructions, Cat. 26SCA4-11SI (11/24); earlier 26SCA5 Installation Instructions, Cat. 26SCA5-1SI (06/24); Carrier Wiring Diagrams 26SCA4-1W and 26SCA5-1W (06/25, label 350761-101 Rev A)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (26SCA536W023)","value":"26 = R-454B AC · S = single stage · C = Comfort · A = initial series · position 6 SEER2 class: 4 = 13.4 (26SCA4), 5 = 14.3 (26SCA5) · 18-60 = capacity · position 9: N = North AC (26SCA4), W = Southwest AC (26SCA5) · position 10 feature: 0 = standard (26SCA4 adds 1 = compressor electrical rating change) · position 11: 26SCA4 0 only; 26SCA5 0 = standard, 1 = compressor electrical rating change, 2 = coil optimization · position 12 voltage: 3 = 208/230-1, 5 = 208/230-3, 6 = 460-3, 1 = 575-3 (PD4 p2; PD5 p2)"},{"label":"Efficiency","value":"26SCA4 13.4-16.0 SEER2 / 11.0-13.5 EER2 · 26SCA5 13.8-17.0 SEER2 / 11.2-14.5 EER2 (PD4 p1; PD5 p1)"},{"label":"Catalog models","value":"26SCA4: 418/424/430/442 N003; 436 N003/N005/N006/N001; 448 N013/N005/N006/N001; 460 N003/N005/N006/N001 · 26SCA5: 518W003, 524W003, 530W003, 536W023, 542W013, 548W013, 560W003, all 208/230-1 (PD4 p2; PD5 p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (both models)","rows":[{"label":"Refrigerant / metering","value":"R-454B (Puron Advance), A2L. Indoor TXV only - do not use capillary-tube indoor coils (II p4 note 1; PD p9/10)"},{"label":"Factory charge covers","value":"15 ft of 3/8 in. liquid line, which accounts for 9 oz of the charge. Ratings are based on 25 ft (PD4/PD5 p3 footnotes, p5; II p3, p7)"},{"label":"Added charge per foot","value":"3/8 in. liquid line 0.60 oz/ft · 5/16 in. 0.40 oz/ft · 1/4 in. 0.27 oz/ft. Formula: (oz/ft × total length) − 9 oz (PD4/PD5 p5 Table 3)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling (TXV), tolerance ±3 °F, using the liquid-pressure/temperature table (II p7-8 Table 4). Window: outdoor 70-100 °F, indoor 70-80 °F; outside it, weigh in the charge by line length. The II says to use the rating-plate subcooling value (II p7)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure test / evacuation","value":"Nitrogen at about 200 psi, holding for 1 hr, not exceeding the rating-plate low-side test pressure. Evacuate to 500 microns; a tight system holds 1000 microns after about 7 min (II p4)"}]},{"title":"26SCA4 figures (sizes 18 / 24 / 30 / 36 / 42 / 48 / 60)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb","value":"18: 3.90 · 24: 3.90 · 30: 5.30 · 36: 4.90 · 42: 6.60 · 48: 7.10 · 60: 6.40 (PD4 p3 Physical Data)","key":true},{"label":"Required subcooling, °F","value":"18: 8 · 24: 10 · 30: 9 · 36: 8 · 42: 8 · 48: 12 · 60: 10 - the rating plate governs (PD4 p10)","key":true},{"label":"Electrical 208/230-1 (197-253 V): LRA / RLA / fan FLA / MCA / max fuse or breaker","value":"18: 41.5 / 8.3 / 0.4 / 10.8 / 15 · 24: 59.0 / 8.2 / 0.6 / 12.1 / 20 · 30: 67.0 / 12.5 / 0.6 / 16.2 / 25 · 36: 82.5 / 13.5 / 0.6 / 17.5 / 30 · 42: 109.0 / 14.7 / 1.4 / 19.8 / 30 · 48: 126.0 / 18.1 / 1.2 / 23.8 / 40 · 60: 157.0 / 23.7 / 1.5 / 31.1 / 50 (PD4 p9)"},{"label":"Electrical 208/230-3","value":"36: 97.8 / 12.8 / 0.6 / 16.6 / 25 · 48: 120.4 / 12.7 / 1.1 / 17.0 / 25 · 60: 156.4 / 17.7 / 1.5 / 23.6 / 35 (PD4 p9)"},{"label":"Electrical 460-3 (414-506 V)","value":"36: 44.3 / 5.1 / 0.3 / 6.7 / 15 · 48: 50.0 / 6.4 / 0.5 / 8.5 / 15 · 60: 69.0 / 7.5 / 0.8 / 10.2 / 15 (PD4 p9)"},{"label":"Electrical 575-3 (517.5-610 V)","value":"36: 27.1 / 4.5 / 0.3 / 5.9 / 15 · 48: 41 / 5.1 / 0.42 / 6.8 / 15 · 60: 47.8 / 6.4 / 0.65 / 8.7 / 15. 575-3 units have a 3-pole contactor and no phase monitor (PD4 p9)"},{"label":"Maximum outdoor ambient","value":"115 °F (PD4 p22)"}]},{"title":"26SCA5 figures (sizes 18 / 24 / 30 / 36 / 42 / 48 / 60, all 208/230-1)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb","value":"18: 4.2 · 24: 4.7 · 30: 5.5 · 36: 5.3 · 42: 7.2 · 48: 5.7 · 60: 7.9 (PD5 p3 Physical Data)","key":true},{"label":"Required subcooling, °F","value":"18: 5 · 24: 5 · 30: 6 · 36: 5 · 42: 6 · 48: 8 · 60: 11 - low targets; the rating plate governs (PD5 p9)","key":true},{"label":"Electrical 208/230-1 (197-253 V): LRA / RLA / fan FLA / MCA / max fuse or breaker","value":"18: 41.5 / 8.3 / 0.5 / 10.9 / 15 · 24: 60.2 / 10.3 / 0.7 / 13.6 / 20 · 30: 75.6 / 12.7 / 0.6 / 16.5 / 25 · 36: 75.0 / 13.5 / 0.7 / 17.6 / 30 · 42: 123.0 / 17.3 / 1.05 / 22.7 / 35 · 48: 126.0 / 22.4 / 1.05 / 29.1 / 40 · 60: 157.0 / 23.7 / 1.52 / 31.1 / 50 (PD5 p9)"},{"label":"3-phase 26SCA5","value":"The PD5 nomenclature lists 3-phase codes, but PD5 publishes only 208/230-1 models and electrical data - see rating plate"},{"label":"Maximum outdoor ambient","value":"Not stated in PD5 - see rating plate"}]},{"title":"Line set (both models)","rows":[{"label":"Liquid line","value":"3/8 in. on all sizes; 3/8 in. is the maximum liquid-line size (II p3)"},{"label":"Rated vapor line","value":"18: 5/8 · 24: 3/4 · 30: 3/4 · 36: 7/8 · 42: 7/8 · 48: 7/8 · 60: 1-1/8. Vapor valve connection 3/4 (18-30), 7/8 (36-60) (PD p3; II Table 1)"},{"label":"Long line","value":"Any run over 80 ft equivalent, or over 35 ft vertical. Maximum 250 ft total equivalent length, 200 ft with the outdoor unit above, 80 ft with the outdoor unit below; limits by liquid diameter in PD p4 Tables 1-2 (PD p5). Crankcase heater required for lines over 80 ft, with the outdoor unit more than 35 ft below, and in low ambient (II p6)"},{"label":"Buried lines","value":"36 in. maximum (II p3)"}]},{"title":"Controls, safeties & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Control board","value":"None. 24 V contactor (Y/C) with an external 24 V / 40 VA power source (60 VA with a liquid-line solenoid) (W note 4; PD p9)"},{"label":"HPS / LPS / DTS / CTD","value":"Shown as 'may be factory or field installed'. No set points published - see the rating plate or kit instructions (W legend)"},{"label":"Run capacitor","value":"Dual-run type; the µF rating is not printed - see the rating plate or capacitor label (W diagrams)"},{"label":"3-phase monitor LED","value":"OFF = no compressor call · FLASHING = reversed phase (swap 2 line leads at the contactor) · ON = normal (II p6 Table 2)"},{"label":"Low-ambient accessory switch","value":"Cycles the fan at roughly 100-225 psig (PD p7)"},{"label":"Minimum cooling ambient","value":"55 °F without accessories (II p2); down to 0 °F with the low-ambient kits (PD p1)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"Dissipation system","value":"A factory-authorized dissipation system must be installed with the indoor unit (II p5; W note 16)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum room area (total charge lb → ft²)","value":"4 → 61 · 5 → 76 · 6 → 91 · 8 → 122 · 10 → 152 · 12 → 182 · 14 → 213 · 16 → 243 · 18 → 274 · 20 → 304 · 25 → 380 (II p7 Table 3). Record the total charge on the charging label and verify the room area (II p7). The 13 / 15 / 17 lb rows differ from the wiring label - see flag"},{"label":"Opening the circuit","value":"Recover with a flammable-rated recovery machine, purge with N2, evacuate to 1500 microns, break the vacuum with N2, then cut or braze. Use non-sparking tools and a refrigerant detector (II p1, p8)"},{"label":"Contactor","value":"Replace only with a factory-authorized part - the factory contactor is not an ignition source (W note 15)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Two models, two sets of numbers","body":"26SCA4 and 26SCA5 differ in charge, subcooling, CFM, coil, LRA/RLA and fan FLA. Always check the model's 5th digit (4 or 5) before using any number. The 26SCA5 subcooling targets are low (18/24/36 = 5 °F) - the rating plate is the governing value."},{"title":"Minimum room area: the II and the wiring label disagree","body":"26SCA4-11SI Table 3 vs the 26SCA4-1W / 26SCA5-1W labels: 13 lb = 196 ft² (II) vs 198 ft² (label) · 15 lb = 226 vs 228 · 17 lb = 256 vs 258. The label values are the more conservative ones."},{"title":"Maximum elevation: the two installation manuals disagree","body":"11,500 ft in 26SCA4-11SI p2, but 10,000 ft in the earlier 26SCA5-1SI p2 (06/24)."},{"title":"Install details that bite","body":"The factory filter drier must be installed at the indoor coil, arrow toward the coil (II p4). Never use a hard-shutoff TXV together with a liquid-line solenoid (PD accessories); the 26SCA4 requires a hard-shutoff TXV for low-ambient, long-line and coastal installs (PD4 p7). Remove the Schrader core on the vapor valve before brazing (II p4). Valve caps: finger tight plus 1/12 turn (II p6). The PD hard-start kit KSAHS2701AAA footnote refers to 'position 15 of the 16-digit model number', which does not match the 12-digit nomenclature."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"HPS/LPS/DTS set points, capacitor µF, the 26SCA5 maximum operating ambient, 26SCA5 3-phase electrical data, and any fault or troubleshooting codes (no R-454B service manual was located)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"27SCA5 (Comfort single-stage heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Carrier Comfort Series single-stage split-system heat pump with scroll compressor, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L) - use with R-454B indoor units only. 14.3-16.0 SEER2, 10.0-12.5 EER2, 7.5-7.8 HSPF2. Sizes 18-60 (1.5-5 tons); 3-phase versions only in 36, 48 and 60. Cooling meters through the indoor TXV; heating through a piston in the outdoor liquid service valve. Defrost termination is not published for this model.","match":["27SCA5","27SCA518","27SCA524","27SCA530","27SCA536","27SCA536A003","27SCA542","27SCA548","27SCA560"],"source":"Carrier 27SCA5 Product Data, Cat. 27SCA5-03PD (05/25; the footer still prints 27SCA5-02PD); Carrier 27SCA5 Installation Instructions, Cat. 27SCA5-1SI (12/23). Carrier Application Guideline and Service Manual 24-25-9SM (09/19) covers the R-22/R-410A generation, does not name the 27SCA5, and is cited for comparison only","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (27SCA536A003)","value":"27 = R-454B heat pump · S = single stage · C = Comfort · A = initial series · 5 = 14.3 SEER2 · 18-60 = nominal capacity · A = standard heat pump (region) · 0 = standard feature · 0 = standard special feature · position 12 voltage: 3 = 208-230-1, 5 = 208/230-3, 6 = 460-3-60, 1 = 575-3-60 (PD p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft of line set)","value":"18: 6.5 · 24: 5.4 · 30: 6.1 · 36: 7.6 · 42: 7.3 · 48: 10.5 · 60: 8.7 (PD p3)","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment","value":"Add or remove 0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 in. liquid line above or below 15 ft (SI p4, p9)"},{"label":"Outdoor heating piston number","value":"18: 42 · 24: 46 · 30: 52 · 36: 52 · 42: 61 · 48: 65 · 60: 70. Check the stamped number against the rating plate (PD p3; SI p5)","key":true},{"label":"Cooling metering","value":"TXV in the indoor unit. Capillary-tube indoor coils are not allowed (PD p20; SI p4)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"TXV = subcooling, piston = superheat. Favourable conditions 70-100 °F outdoor and 70-80 °F indoor, after at least 15 minutes of cooling. Tolerance ±3 °F (SI p9-10)"},{"label":"Required subcooling, °F","value":"18: 6 · 24: 6 · 30: 12 · 36: 10 · 42: 12 · 48: 13 · 60: 7 (PD p9). The rating plate governs (SI p9)","key":true},{"label":"Liquid-line temperature chart","value":"SI Table 5 covers 238-450 psig for 6-16 °F subcooling (SI p10)"},{"label":"Heating Check Chart on the unit","value":"Verify only - never adjust charge from it (SI p10)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Rated line sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. on all sizes; 3/8 in. OD is the maximum, including long line (SI p2). Vapor: 18/24 = 5/8 · 30/36 = 3/4 · 42/48 = 7/8 · 60 = 1-1/8 (the size 60 valve is 7/8) (PD p3; SI p4 Table 2). Alternate vapor sizes and capacity loss: PD p4 table"},{"label":"Maximum length","value":"200 ft actual and 250 ft equivalent. Outdoor unit above indoor unit: up to 200 ft vertical (PD p5)"},{"label":"Outdoor unit below indoor unit, maximum equivalent length","value":"18-36: 250 ft up to 80 ft of lift · 42: 150 ft at 71-80 ft of lift · 48: 230 ft at 51-60 ft, 160 ft at 61-70 ft, not allowed beyond 70 ft · 60: 225 ft at 21-30 ft, 190 at 31-40, 150 at 41-50, 110 at 51-60, not allowed beyond 60 ft (PD p5)"},{"label":"Long line threshold","value":"More than 80 ft, or outdoor unit more than 20 ft below the indoor unit. Beyond that, follow the Long Line Guideline and install the required accessories (crankcase heater, hard start, and others). Power the crankcase heater 24 hours before start-up (PD p5, p7; SI p7)"}]},{"title":"Electrical: LRA / RLA / fan FLA / MCA / max fuse or breaker (PD p9)","rows":[{"label":"208-230-1 (197-253 V)","value":"18: 45.1 / 8.3 / 0.50 / 10.9 / 15 · 24: 64.4 / 10.3 / 0.60 / 13.5 / 20 · 30: 67.0 / 12.5 / 0.70 / 16.3 / 25 · 36: 86.0 / 14.4 / 1.20 / 19.2 / 30 · 42: 123.0 / 19.0 / 1.05 / 24.9 / 40 · 48: 126.0 / 22.4 / 1.40 / 29.4 / 50 · 60: 157.0 / 23.7 / 1.50 / 31.1 / 50","key":true},{"label":"208/230-3 (187-253 V)","value":"36: 70.0 / 9.0 / 1.20 / 12.5 / 20 · 48: 120.4 / 12.8 / 1.4 / 17.4 / 30 · 60: 156.4 / 16.0 / 1.50 / 21.5 / 35"},{"label":"460-3 (414-506 V)","value":"36: 39.0 / 4.1 / 0.64 / 5.7 / 15 · 48: 49.4 / 6.0 / 0.73 / 8.2 / 15 · 60: 69.0 / 7.1 / 0.94 / 9.8 / 15"},{"label":"575-3 (518-632 V)","value":"36: 29.0 / 3.3 / 0.52 / 4.6 / 15 · 48: 41.0 / 5.8 / 0.56 / 7.8 / 15 · 60: 47.8 / 6.4 / 0.70 / 8.7 / 15"},{"label":"SCCR / control circuit","value":"5 kA rms (PD p9). 24 V; transformer 40 VA minimum; No. 18 AWG wire, or No. 16 AWG beyond 100 ft (SI p7)"},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Not printed - see the rating plate or wiring label"}]},{"title":"Defrost & safeties","rows":[{"label":"Defrost type","value":"Time/temperature board with a defrost thermostat (DFT) on the 3/8 in. stub tube at the liquid-header feeder, usually on the bottom circuit. DFT closes at about 32 °F; the timer runs only while the DFT is closed and the contactor is energised (SI p3, p8)","key":true},{"label":"Defrost termination","value":"Not published for 27SCA5 in the 27SCA5 SI or PD; see the defrost board label. (The termination figures in service manual 24-25-9SM are for the R-22/R-410A generation and do not apply to this model.)"},{"label":"Interval","value":"DIP switches select 30, 60, 90 or 120 minutes - the initial period only; after that the interval varies with defrost length. A forced defrost resets it to the DIP setting. Which DIP positions select each interval, and the factory default, are not published (SI p8-9)"},{"label":"Quiet Shift-2","value":"DIP switch 3, factory OFF. When ON, the compressor is off about 1 minute before and after each reversing-valve shift, and variable intervals are disabled (the interval is fixed until the DIP switch is changed and power is cycled) (SI p8-9)"},{"label":"Forced defrost","value":"Short the J1 speed-up pins for 5 seconds, then release. DFT open: a 30-second defrost (about 3 minutes with Quiet Shift-2 ON). DFT closed: a full defrost cycle. During defrost the outdoor fan stops and W2 (supplemental heat) is energised (SI p8-9)"},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Loss-of-charge switch is standard; the high-pressure switch is an accessory (KAAHI0501PUR). Set points are not published in the 27SCA5 PD or SI - see the switch label (PD p2, p6)","key":true},{"label":"3-phase monitor LED","value":"OFF = no call · FLASHING = reversed phase (swap 2 leads) · ON = normal (SI p7)"}]},{"title":"A2L, commissioning & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Dissipation system","value":"A Factory Authorized Dissipation System must be installed with the indoor unit (SI p7)"},{"label":"Minimum room area (total charge lb / sq ft)","value":"4/61, 5/76, 6/91, 7/106, 8/122, 9/137, 10/152, 11/167, 12/182, 13/198, 14/213, 15/228; the table continues to 25 lb / 380 sq ft. Record the final total charge on the unit charging label (SI p9 Table 4)"},{"label":"Tools / repair sequence","value":"Non-sparking tools and a refrigerant detector. Recover with a pump certified for flammable refrigerants: nitrogen purge, evacuate to 1500 microns, break vacuum with nitrogen, then cut or braze (SI p1, p10)"},{"label":"Nitrogen test / evacuation","value":"About 200 psi, no drop for 1 hour (never exceed the rating-plate test pressure). Evacuate to 500 microns; the rise must stay under 1500 microns in 10 minutes (SI p6)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 55-125 °F, or down to 0 °F with a low-ambient kit (PD p1, p20). Heating -10 °F to 66 °F (PD p20). Maximum elevation 10,000 ft (SI p1)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Piston in the liquid service valve","body":"A wrong or missing heating piston causes poor heating. Match the stamped number to the rating plate (SI p5). The factory filter drier must be installed at the indoor coil, wrapped with a wet cloth while brazing (SI p2, p5)."},{"title":"Defrost termination is not published for this model","body":"The 27SCA5 SI gives the DFT close point (about 32 °F) but no termination temperature or maximum defrost time. Those figures exist only in the older R-22/R-410A service manual 24-25-9SM, which does not name the 27SCA5 - read the defrost board label instead."},{"title":"Do not borrow set points from other manuals","body":"Carrier's packaged R-454B manual (SM10-R454B-03, 04/25) lists loss-of-charge and high-pressure switch set points, but it does not cover 27SCA5 split units. The R-410A figures in 24-25-9SM do not apply either. No 27SCA5 switch set points are published."},{"title":"Subcooling targets differ by size (6-13 °F)","body":"Some indoor units need extra subcooling for heating. Always read the rating plate (SI p4, p9). Quiet Shift-2 changes defrost behaviour: with it ON the board no longer adapts the interval, and the 1-minute compressor-off pauses can look like a fault (SI p8-9)."},{"title":"Low-ambient kit on ECM-fan units","body":"MotorMaster requires a replacement motor plus a new defrost board, and the unit then no longer meets its AHRI rating (SI p4 Table 1 note). Crankcase heater: required beyond 80 ft or 20 ft of lift; power it 24 hours before start-up (SI p7)."},{"title":"Not published - see the plate or the part","body":"Defrost board part number, which DIP positions select each interval and the factory default, pressure-switch set points, capacitor ratings, fault codes from the indoor dissipation board, and the nomenclature code for the coastal '27SCA5---C' model. Document quirk: the file 27SCA5-03PD prints '27SCA5-02PD' in its footer; its data matches 02PD and 01PD."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"26SPA6 (Performance single-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Carrier Performance Series single-stage InteliSense-capable split-system AC condenser, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L) - use with R-454B indoor units only. 13.8-17.0 SEER2 / 11.2-14.5 EER2. Sizes 18-60, all 208/230-1. Digit 11 marks the variant: the current 26SPA636 is W023 and 26SPA642/648 are W013; the older W003 versions carry different charge, subcooling or fuse figures - see the variant rows.","match":["26SPA6","26SPA618W003","26SPA624W003","26SPA630W003","26SPA636W003","26SPA636W023","26SPA642W003","26SPA642W013","26SPA648W003","26SPA648W013","26SPA660W003"],"source":"Carrier 26SPA6 Product Data, Cat. 26SPA6-02PD (06/25); Carrier 26SPA6 Product Data, Cat. 26SPA6-01PD (08/24), for the W003 variants; Carrier 26SPA6 Installation Instructions, Cat. 26SPA6-2SI (02/26; content identical to 1SI, 06/24)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (26SPA636W023)","value":"26 = AC · S = single stage · P = Performance · A = initial series · 6 = 16.0 SEER2 · 18-60 = size in kBtuh · W = AC · position 10: 0 = standard · position 11: 0 = standard, 1 = compressor electrical change, 2 = coil optimization · 3 = 208/230-1 (PD-26v2 p2)"},{"label":"Current catalog numbers","value":"26SPA636W023 and 26SPA642/648W013; the other AC sizes are W003 (PD-26v2 p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (26SPA6-02PD, current variants)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft)","value":"18: 4.2 · 24: 4.7 · 30: 5.5 · 36 (W023): 5.3 · 42: 7.2 · 48: 5.7 · 60: 7.9. The 48 really holds less than the 42 - printed that way (PD-26v2 p3)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target, °F","value":"18: 5 · 24: 5 · 30: 6 · 36 (W023): 5 · 42: 6 · 48: 8 · 60: 11 - the rating plate governs (PD-26v2 p9)","key":true},{"label":"26SPA636 variants (digit 11)","value":"W003: 6.9 lb, 8 °F subcooling, 2-row coil, 17.7 ft² face area (PD-26v1 p3, p9) · W023: 5.3 lb, 5 °F subcooling, 1-row coil, 23.7 ft² face area (PD-26v2 p3, p9). Both versions use a 7/8 in. vapor connection. Check digit 11 on the plate","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment","value":"Add or remove 0.6 oz per ft of 3/8 in. liquid line from 15 ft (SI-26 p3). The PD also lists 0.40 oz/ft for 5/16 in. and 0.27 oz/ft for 1/4 in. (PD-26v2 p5 T3)"},{"label":"Metering / method","value":"Indoor TXV; capillary-tube indoor coils are not allowed (SI-26 p4). Subcooling ±3 °F, target on the rating plate, at 70-100 °F outdoor and 70-80 °F indoor; outside that window, weigh in (SI-26 p7)"},{"label":"Evacuation / pressure test","value":"500 microns; the system should hold 1000 microns after about 7 min. Nitrogen at about 200 psi with no drop for 1 hr; never exceed the rating-plate test pressure (SI-26 p4)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes: vapor tube (valve)","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. maximum, including long line (SI-26 p3). Vapor 18: 5/8 (3/4) · 24: 3/4 (3/4) · 30: 3/4 (3/4) · 36: 7/8 (7/8) · 42: 7/8 (7/8) · 48: 7/8 (7/8) · 60: 1-1/8 (7/8) (PD-26v2 p3)"},{"label":"Lengths","value":"Maximum total equivalent length 250 ft. Outdoor unit above: maximum lift 200 ft. Outdoor unit below: maximum lift 80 ft; the 48 is limited to 160 ft at 61-70 ft of lift; the 60 to 110 ft at 51-60 ft and not allowed with more lift (PD-26v2 p4-5)"},{"label":"Long line","value":"More than 80 ft equivalent length or more than 35 ft of vertical separation. A crankcase heater is required past 80 ft, or when the outdoor unit is 35 ft below (PD-26v2 p4-5; SI-26 p6)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1, 197-253 V)","rows":[{"label":"Compressor RLA/LRA · fan FLA · MCA · max fuse","value":"18: 8.3/41.5 · 0.5 · 10.9 · 15 — 24: 10.3/60.2 · 0.7 · 13.6 · 20 — 30: 12.7/75.6 · 0.6 · 16.5 · 25 — 36: 13.5/75.0 · 0.7 · 17.6 · 30 — 42: 17.3/123.0 · 1.05 · 22.7 · 35 — 48: 22.4/126.0 · 1.05 · 29.1 · 40 — 60: 23.7/157.0 · 1.52 · 31.1 · 50 (PD-26v2 p9)","key":true},{"label":"26SPA642 / 648 max fuse changed","value":"W003: max fuse 40 (42) and 50 (48) (PD-26v1 p9) · W013: max fuse 35 and 40 (PD-26v2 p9). Go by the rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Not published - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Controls, switches, range & A2L","rows":[{"label":"Controls","value":"24 V control circuit, 40 VA minimum. The InteliSense board carries LSVP, LSVT, VSVP, VSVT and OAT sensors. Amber LED solid = power; green LED solid = communicating with the thermostat. No flash-code table is published (SI-26 p5-6)"},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"01PD lists high and low pressure switches as standard; 02PD lists them as kits instead: KAALP0501PUR (low) and KAAHI0601PUR (high). Set points are not published (PD-26v1 p2; PD-26v2 p3, p7). Winter Start Control is required for low-ambient cooling when a low-pressure switch is installed (PD-26v2 p7)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Minimum cooling ambient 55 °F; with low-ambient kits, cooling works down to 0 °F (SI-26 p2; PD-26v2 p1)"},{"label":"A2L","value":"The indoor unit must have a factory-authorized dissipation system (SI-26 p5). Minimum floor area by total charge: 4 lb = 61 ft², 8 lb = 122 ft², 12 lb = 182 ft², 13 lb = 196, 15 lb = 226, 17 lb = 256 (SI-26 p7 T2). Before opening the circuit: recover with a flammable-rated pump, purge with nitrogen, evacuate to 1500 microns, then purge with nitrogen again (SI-26 p8)","key":true}]}],"flags":[{"title":"26SPA636 has two versions - check digit 11 on the plate","body":"W003: 6.9 lb, 8 °F subcooling, 2-row coil, 17.7 ft² face area (26SPA6-01PD). W023: 5.3 lb, 5 °F subcooling, 1-row coil, 23.7 ft² face area (26SPA6-02PD). Both use a 7/8 in. vapor connection."},{"title":"26SPA642 and 648 fuse sizes changed","body":"W003: max fuse 40 (42) and 50 (48), per 26SPA6-01PD p9. W013: max fuse 35 and 40, per 26SPA6-02PD p9. Go by the rating plate."},{"title":"InteliSense at install","body":"A new thermostat takes 24 hr to appear in the portal, so bring field gauges. Never use the thermostat's outdoor-temperature reading for charging or troubleshooting (SI-26 p6)."},{"title":"Factory charges that look wrong are printed that way","body":"The AC 48 (5.7 lb) holds less than the 42 (7.2 lb)."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Pressure-switch set points, flash or fault codes (no service manual for R-454B InteliSense was found), capacitor ratings."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"27SPA6 (Performance single-stage heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Carrier Performance Series single-stage InteliSense-capable split-system heat pump, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L) - use with R-454B indoor units only. 14.3-17.5 SEER2 / 10.0-13.5 EER2 / 7.5-7.8 HSPF2. Sizes 18, 19, 24, 30, 31, 36, 42, 48, 60, all 208/230-1 (A003); the 19 and 31 appear only in 02PD. Only the loss-of-charge switch is factory installed - no factory high-pressure switch. Heating meters through a piston in the liquid service valve.","match":["27SPA6","27SPA618A003","27SPA619A003","27SPA624A003","27SPA630A003","27SPA631A003","27SPA636A003","27SPA642A003","27SPA648A003","27SPA660A003"],"source":"Carrier 27SPA6 Product Data, Cat. 27SPA6-02PD (08/25); Carrier 27SPA6 Product Data, Cat. 27SPA6-01PD (02/24); Carrier 27SPA6 Installation Instructions, Cat. 27SPA6-1SI (12/23; distributor-hosted copy, predates sizes 19 and 31)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (27SPA636A003)","value":"27 = HP · S = single stage · P = Performance · A = initial series · 6 = 16.0 SEER2 · 18-60 = size in kBtuh · A = HP · position 10: 0 = standard, C = coastal · position 11: 0 = standard · 3 = 208/230-1 (PD-27v2 p2)"},{"label":"Size 19","value":"A field-installed liquid-line solenoid valve is standard (PD-27v2 p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (27SPA6-02PD)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft)","value":"18: 6.5 · 19: 8.6 · 24: 5.4 · 30: 6.1 · 31: 8.1 · 36: 7.6 · 42: 7.3 · 48: 10.5 · 60: 8.7. The 19 and 31 really hold more than the 24 and 30 - printed that way (PD-27v2 p3)","key":true},{"label":"Heating piston","value":"18: 42 · 19: 40 · 24: 46 · 30: 52 · 31: 46 · 36: 52 · 42: 61 · 48: 65 · 60: 70. Ships in the liquid service valve; the stamped size must match the rating plate. Adapter nut finger-tight, then 1/2 turn more (15 ft-lb) (PD-27v2 p3; SI-27 p5)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target, °F","value":"18: 6 · 19: 6 · 24: 6 · 30: 12 · 31: 7 · 36: 10 · 42: 12 · 48: 13 · 60: 7 - the rating plate governs (PD-27v2 p8)","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment / method","value":"Add or remove 0.6 oz per ft of 3/8 in. liquid line from 15 ft (SI-27 p4). Indoor TXV; no capillary-tube coils. Subcooling ±3 °F at 70-100 °F outdoor and 70-80 °F indoor; outside that window, weigh in (SI-27 p4, p10)"},{"label":"Heating check chart","value":"Diagnosis only, never to adjust charge. Some indoor units need extra subcooling for heating (SI-27 p4, p10)"},{"label":"Evacuation / pressure test","value":"500 microns; the rise must stay at or below 1500 microns in 10 min. Nitrogen at about 200 psi with no drop for 1 hr; never exceed the rating-plate test pressure (SI-27 p6)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes: vapor tube (valve)","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. maximum, including long line (SI-27 p2). Vapor 18: 5/8 (5/8) · 19: 5/8 (5/8) · 24: 5/8 (5/8) · 30: 3/4 (3/4) · 31: 3/4 (3/4) · 36: 7/8 (7/8) - see the 27SPA636 conflict flag · 42: 7/8 (7/8) · 48: 7/8 (7/8) · 60: 1-1/8 (7/8) (PD-27v2 p3)"},{"label":"Lengths","value":"Maximum total equivalent length 250 ft. Outdoor unit above: maximum lift 200 ft. Outdoor unit below: the 48 is limited to 160 ft at 61-70 ft of lift; the 60 to 110 ft at 51-60 ft and not allowed with more lift (PD-27v2 p5)"},{"label":"Long line","value":"More than 80 ft or more than 20 ft of vertical separation. A crankcase heater is required past 80 ft, or when the outdoor unit is 20 ft below (PD-27v2 p5; SI-27 p4, p8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1, 197-253 V; SCCR 5 kA)","rows":[{"label":"Compressor RLA/LRA · fan FLA · MCA · max fuse","value":"18: 8.3/45.1 · 0.50 · 10.9 · 15 — 19: 8.3/45.1 · 0.50 · 11.0 · 15 — 24: 10.3/64.4 · 0.60 · 13.5 · 20 — 30: 12.5/67.0 · 0.70 · 16.3 · 25 — 31: 12.5/67.0 · 0.70 · 16.3 · 25 — 36: 14.4/86.0 · 1.20 · 19.2 · 30 — 42: 19.0/123.0 · 1.05 · 24.9 · 40 — 48: 22.4/126.0 · 1.40 · 29.4 · 50 — 60: 23.7/157.0 · 1.50 · 31.1 · 50 (PD-27v2 p8)","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Not published - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Defrost, switches, controls & A2L","rows":[{"label":"Defrost","value":"Time/temperature control. The defrost thermostat closes at about 32 °F and sits on the 3/8 in. stub tube at the liquid header. DIP switches set the initial interval to 30, 60, 90 or 120 min; after that the interval varies with defrost length. Quiet Shift-2 is DIP switch 3, off from the factory; with it on, the interval stays fixed. Forced defrost: short J1 for 5 s, then release. Termination temperature and the factory default interval are not published (SI-27 p3, p9)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Only the loss-of-charge switch is factory installed; InteliSense HP units have no factory high-pressure switch (SI-27 p7; PD-27v2 p2). Accessory HPS kits KAAHS0601PUR and KAAHI0501PUR (PD-27v2 p6). Set points are not published"},{"label":"Controls","value":"24 V control circuit, 40 VA minimum. InteliSense board with LSVP, LSVT, VSVP, VSVT and OAT sensors. Amber LED solid = power; green LED solid = communicating with the thermostat. No flash-code table is published (SI-27 p7)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Minimum cooling ambient 55 °F; with low-ambient kits, cooling works down to 0 °F (PD-27v2 p1). Heating operating limits are not published"},{"label":"A2L","value":"The indoor unit must have a factory-authorized dissipation system (SI-27 p7). Minimum floor area by total charge: 4 lb = 61 ft², 8 lb = 122 ft², 12 lb = 182 ft², 13 lb = 198, 15 lb = 228, 17 lb = 258 (SI-27 p10 T3) - the HP table differs from the AC one. Before opening the circuit: recover with a flammable-rated pump, purge with nitrogen, evacuate to 1500 microns, then purge with nitrogen again (SI-27 p11)","key":true}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Documents disagree on the 27SPA636 vapor size","body":"3/4 in. valve and tube per 27SPA6-01PD p3 and 27SPA6-1SI Table 2; 7/8 in. per 27SPA6-02PD p3. Check the valve on the unit before cutting line."},{"title":"HP with ECM fan motor","body":"The MotorMaster/low-ambient accessory needs a replacement motor and defrost board, and the unit then loses its AHRI rating (SI-27 p4 T1)."},{"title":"InteliSense at install","body":"A new thermostat takes 24 hr to appear in the portal, so bring field gauges. Never use the thermostat's outdoor-temperature reading for charging or troubleshooting (SI-27 p7)."},{"title":"Factory charges that look wrong are printed that way","body":"The HP 19 and 31 hold more than the 24 and 30."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Pressure-switch set points, defrost termination temperature and the factory default interval, flash or fault codes (no service manual for R-454B InteliSense was found), capacitor ratings, heating operating limits. No 27SPA6 installation instruction newer than 1SI (12/23) was found, and the 1SI predates sizes 19 and 31."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"26TPA8 (Performance two-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Carrier Performance Series 2-Stage split-system AC condenser with InteliSense, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L), two-stage unloading scroll. 18 SEER2 class (max SEER2 by size 24/36/48/60: 18.5 / 17.0 / 18.0 / 16.5). Sizes 24-60 (2-5 tons), 208-230-1 only. Coastal 26TPA8***C (C in position 10) uses the same figures; only the coating differs. Charge in HIGH stage only. No factory pressure switches.","match":["26TPA8","26TPA824W003","26TPA836W003","26TPA848W003","26TPA860W003"],"source":"Carrier 26TPA8 Installation Instructions, Cat. 26TPA8-02SI (02/26, replaces -01SI); Carrier 26TPA8 Product Data, Cat. 26TPA8-01PD (12/24); Carrier 26TPA8C Product Data, Cat. 26TPA8C-01PD; Carrier 26TPA8-1W wiring diagram (06/25)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (26TPA836W003)","value":"26 = R-454B AC · T = two-stage · P = Performance · A = series · 8 = 18 SEER2 · 24/36/48/60 = capacity · W = AC · position 10: 0 = standard, C = coastal · position 11: 0 · 3 = 208-230-1 (PD-AC p2; PD-AC-C p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft)","value":"24: 5.32 · 36: 7.25 · 48: 8.65 · 60: 9.42 (PD-AC p2)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target, °F","value":"24: 8 · 36: 8 · 48: 11 · 60: 11 - the rating plate governs (PD-AC p5)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"High stage only, by subcooling with the indoor TXV, ±3 °F. Conditions: outdoor 70-100 °F and indoor 70-80 °F; otherwise weigh in. R-454B chart: at 6 °F subcooling, 238 psig needs a 78 °F liquid line and 450 psig needs 124 °F (SI-AC p10-11)","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment","value":"Add or remove 0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 in. liquid line from 15 ft (SI-AC p3, p10). The PD also gives 0.40 oz/ft for 5/16 in. and 0.27 oz/ft for 1/4 in. liquid line (PD-AC T3 p3)"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor TXV only. No capillary-tube or fixed-orifice indoor coils (SI-AC p3)"},{"label":"Pressure test / evacuation","value":"Nitrogen at about 200 psi, held for 1 hr. Vacuum to 500 µm; it must not rise above 1500 µm in 10 min (SI-AC p5, p11)"}]},{"title":"Compressor & staging","rows":[{"label":"Staging","value":"Low stage runs the compressor at about 67%, which gives about 75% capacity. High stage energizes a 24 VDC solenoid; the plug has a built-in rectifier (SI-AC p9)"},{"label":"Unloader coil","value":"About 1640 Ω. You should read 24 VDC at the plug on a high-stage call (SI-AC p11)"},{"label":"Staging check","value":"Going from low to high, suction should drop 3-10% and amps should rise 20-45% (SI-AC p11)","key":true},{"label":"Winding resistance at 70±20 °F, start (S-C) / run (R-C)","value":"24: 1.652 / 1.065 · 36: 1.471 / 0.728 · 48: 1.660 / 0.436 · 60: 1.203 / 0.383 Ω (SI-AC T5 p11)"},{"label":"Internal pressure relief","value":"Opens at a 550-625 psi differential (SI-AC p12)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. connection, and 3/8 in. is the maximum size. Rated vapor tube: 24: 3/4 · 36: 7/8 · 48: 1-1/8 · 60: 1-1/8. Vapor valve connection 3/4, 7/8, 7/8, 7/8 (SI-AC T1 p3; PD-AC p2-4)"},{"label":"Lengths","value":"Max actual length 200 ft; max total equivalent length 250 ft. Vertical: outdoor unit up to 200 ft above, or up to 80 ft below (SI-AC T1 p3; PD-AC p2-4)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Accessory: KAACH1701AAA for 24/36, KAACH1601AAA for 48/60. Required above 80 ft of line, or when the outdoor unit is 35 ft below the indoor unit - see the vertical-limit flag (PD-AC p6; SI-AC p8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208-230/1, 197-253 V; fan FLA 2.60 on every size)","rows":[{"label":"LRA / RLA / MCA / MOCP","value":"24: 62.0 / 10.3 / 15.5 / 20 · 36: 90.0 / 14.6 / 20.9 / 35 · 48: 138.0 / 18.3 / 25.5 / 40 · 60: 149.0 / 22.3 / 30.5 / 50 (PD-AC p5)","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"No capacitor rating is printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Controls, switches, A2L & range","rows":[{"label":"Controls","value":"InteliSense sensor control module (SCM), with LSVP, LSVT, VSVP, VSVT and OAT sensors. Solid amber LED = power. Solid green LED = communicating with the thermostat. No fault codes are published (SI-AC p8)"},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"None factory-installed. High-pressure switch (KAAHI0601PUR) and low-pressure switch (KAALP0501PUR) are accessories; no trip points are published (SI-AC p8; PD-AC p6). Without them, YEL/BLU goes to the contactor coil (26TPA8-1W note 13)"},{"label":"A2L","value":"A factory-authorized dissipation system must be installed with the indoor unit. Use non-sparking tools and a refrigerant detector. Minimum floor area by total system charge: 4 lb = 61 ft², 10 lb = 152 ft², 15 lb = 226 ft², 20 lb = 304 ft², 25 lb = 380 ft² (the SI has the full table). Record the total charge on the unit label. Repair: recover with a flammable-rated pump, purge with nitrogen, evacuate to 1500 µm, then open the circuit (SI-AC p6, p10-11; 1W note 15)","key":true},{"label":"Cooling operating range","value":"55 °F minimum without a kit, 0 °F with the low-ambient kit, 125 °F maximum at 230 V. Maximum elevation 10,000 ft (PD-AC p19; SI p2)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"24 V source: the documents conflict","body":"SI-AC p6 says an outdoor transformer powers the board and 'does not require 24VAC R from indoor', yet the same page says to use the furnace/fan coil transformer (40 VA minimum). PD-AC p5 and 26TPA8-1W show an external 24 V supply. Verify in the field."},{"title":"Long-line vertical limit: the documents conflict","body":"35 ft (PD-AC p4; SI-AC p3, p8) vs 20 ft (PD-AC p19; SI-AC p10 charging note)."},{"title":"Charge in high stage only, and the unloader plug must have its rectifier","body":"Charge to the rating-plate subcooling in high stage; the AC and HP targets differ. A replacement solenoid plug must have the built-in rectifier."},{"title":"Size 60 fan RPM is a misprint","body":"Printed as '8815' (the 48 shows 815). Read it off the motor nameplate (PD-AC p2)."},{"title":"InteliSense","body":"The thermostat doesn't show the outdoor temperature sensor - don't use it for charging. A new thermostat takes 24 h to show up in the portal, so bring gauges."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Switch trip pressures, run capacitor ratings, fault/flash codes. Board part number HK32EA013 (SCM) appears only as a figure label."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"27TPA8 (Performance two-stage heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Carrier Performance Series 2-Stage split-system heat pump with InteliSense, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L), two-stage unloading scroll. 18 SEER2 class (max SEER2 by size 24/36/48/60: 18.5 / 17 / 18 / 17.5). Sizes 24-60 (2-5 tons), 208-230-1 only. Coastal 27TPA8***C uses the same figures. Charge in HIGH stage only; heating meters through a piston in the liquid service valve. Loss-of-charge switch only from the factory.","match":["27TPA8","27TPA824A003","27TPA836A003","27TPA848A003","27TPA860A003"],"source":"Carrier 27TPA8 Installation Instructions, Cat. 27TPA8-01SI (10/24); Carrier 27TPA8 Product Data, Cat. 27TPA8-01PD (11/24); Carrier 27TPA8C Product Data, Cat. 27TPA8C-01PD (12/24); Carrier 27TPA8-1W wiring diagram (06/25)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (27TPA836A003)","value":"27 = R-454B HP · T = two-stage · P = Performance · A = series · 8 = 18 SEER2 · 24/36/48/60 = capacity · A = HP · position 10: 0 = standard, C = coastal · position 11: 0 · 3 = 208-230-1 (PD-HP p2; PD-HP-C p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft)","value":"24: 10.14 · 36: 12.70 · 48: 11.09 · 60: 11.86. The 36 is printed heavier than the 48 (PD-HP p2)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target, °F","value":"24: 7 · 36: 10 · 48: 10 · 60: 10 - the rating plate governs (PD-HP p4)","key":true},{"label":"Heating piston (liquid service valve)","value":"24: 42 · 36: 49 · 48: 61 · 60: 67; the piston must match the rating plate. Adapter nut: finger tight + ½ turn (15 ft-lb). Cooling uses the indoor TXV (PD-HP p2; SI-HP p4)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"High stage only, by subcooling with the indoor TXV, ±3 °F. Conditions: outdoor 70-100 °F and indoor 70-80 °F; otherwise weigh in. R-454B chart: at 6 °F subcooling, 238 psig needs a 78 °F liquid line and 450 psig needs 124 °F (SI-HP p10-11)"},{"label":"Heating Check Chart (on the unit)","value":"For diagnosis only. Do not charge with it (SI-HP p10)"},{"label":"Charge adjustment","value":"Add or remove 0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 in. liquid line from 15 ft (SI-HP p4, p10)"},{"label":"Pressure test / evacuation","value":"Nitrogen at about 200 psi, held for 1 hr. Vacuum to 500 µm; it must not rise above 1500 µm in 10 min (SI-HP p6, p12)"}]},{"title":"Compressor & staging","rows":[{"label":"Staging","value":"Low stage runs the compressor at about 67%, which gives about 75% capacity. High stage energizes a 24 VDC solenoid; the plug has a built-in rectifier. The HP compressor starts unloaded for 5 s (SI-HP p9)"},{"label":"Unloader coil","value":"About 1640 Ω. You should read 24 VDC at the plug on a high-stage call (SI-HP p11)"},{"label":"Staging check","value":"Going from low to high, suction should drop 3-10% and amps should rise 20-45% (SI-HP p11)"},{"label":"Winding resistance at 70±20 °F, start (S-C) / run (R-C)","value":"24: 1.652 / 1.065 · 36: 1.471 / 0.728 · 48: 1.660 / 0.436 · 60: 1.203 / 0.383 Ω (SI-HP T6 p12)"},{"label":"Internal pressure relief","value":"Opens at a 550-625 psi differential (SI-HP p12)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. connection, and 3/8 in. is the maximum size. Rated vapor tube: 24: 3/4 · 36: 7/8 · 48: 1-1/8 · 60: 1-1/8. Vapor valve connection 3/4, 7/8, 7/8, 7/8 (SI-HP T2 p4; PD-HP p2-3)"},{"label":"Lengths","value":"Max actual length 200 ft; max total equivalent length 250 ft. Vertical: outdoor unit up to 200 ft above, or up to 80 ft below (SI-HP T2 p4; PD-HP p2-3)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Standard, with a temperature switch. Required above 80 ft of line, or when the outdoor unit is 20 ft below (PD-HP p2; SI-HP p8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208-230/1, 197-253 V; fan FLA 2.60 on every size)","rows":[{"label":"LRA / RLA / MCA / MOCP","value":"24: 62.0 / 15.6 / 22.1 / 25 · 36: 90.0 / 18.5 / 25.7 / 40 · 48: 138.0 / 23.0 / 31.4 / 50 · 60: 149.0 / 25.8 / 34.9 / 60 (PD-HP p4)","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"No capacitor rating is printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Defrost, switches, controls, A2L & range","rows":[{"label":"Defrost","value":"Time/temperature control. Interval settings 30/60/90/120 min, factory setting 60; rated interval 90/90/60/60 (24/36/48/60). The defrost thermostat closes at about 32 °F; defrost ends when it opens, or after 10 min maximum. Forced defrost: short J1 for 5 s, then release. Quiet Shift-2 is DIP 3 (off by default). 5-minute lockout after power loss, and a 5-minute anti-short-cycle delay (SI-HP p9-10; 27TPA8-1W)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"The loss-of-charge switch is factory-installed, in the Y1 circuit. The high-pressure switch is accessory KSAHI0401PUR. No trip points are published (SI-HP p8, p12; PD-HP p5)"},{"label":"Controls","value":"InteliSense sensor control module (SCM), with LSVP, LSVT, VSVP, VSVT and OAT sensors. Solid amber LED = power. Solid green LED = communicating with the thermostat. No fault codes are published (SI-HP p8)"},{"label":"A2L","value":"A factory-authorized dissipation system must be installed with the indoor unit. Use non-sparking tools and a refrigerant detector. Minimum floor area by total system charge: 4 lb = 61 ft², 10 lb = 152 ft², 15 lb = 226 ft², 20 lb = 304 ft², 25 lb = 380 ft² (the SI has the full table). Record the total charge on the unit label. Repair: recover with a flammable-rated pump, purge with nitrogen, evacuate to 1500 µm, then open the circuit (SI-HP p7, p10, p12; 1W note 15)","key":true},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 55 °F minimum without a kit, 0 °F with the low-ambient kit, 125 °F maximum at 230 V. Heating −8 °F to 66 °F outdoor. Maximum elevation 10,000 ft (PD-HP p18; SI p2)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Charge in high stage only, and the unloader plug must have its rectifier","body":"Charge to the rating-plate subcooling in high stage; the AC and HP targets differ. The HP compressor starts unloaded for 5 s. A replacement solenoid plug must have the built-in rectifier."},{"title":"Don't assume the switches exist","body":"The HP has only the loss-of-charge switch from the factory. The diagram marks LPS/HPS/CTD as 'may be factory or field installed'."},{"title":"InteliSense","body":"The thermostat doesn't show the outdoor temperature sensor - don't use it for charging. A new thermostat takes 24 h to show up in the portal, so bring gauges."},{"title":"A2L","body":"The dissipation board is mandatory. Check minimum room area against the total charge."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Switch trip pressures, run capacitor ratings, fault/flash codes, and whether a 27TPA8-02SI exists. Board part numbers HK32EA013 (SCM) and HK32EA010 (defrost) appear only as figure labels."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"26VNA1 (Infinity variable-speed AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Carrier Infinity Variable Speed Air Conditioner with Greenspeed Intelligence, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L). Up to 21 SEER2 / 12 EER2. Rotary inverter compressor, 25-100% capacity. Sizes 24/36/48/60, 208/230-1. Communicating - the Infinity System Control is required and charges the unit through its Refrigerant Charging menu; the published subcooling is nominal only and the control's target governs.","match":["26VNA1","26VNA124W003","26VNA136W003","26VNA148W003","26VNA160W003"],"source":"Carrier 26VNA1 Product Data, Cat. 26VNA1-02PD (02/26); Carrier 26VNA1 Installation Instructions, Cat. 26VNA1-2SI (04/2025); superseded 26VNA1-01PD and 26VNA1-1SI used only to cross-check","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode","value":"26 = R-454B AC · V = variable speed · N = Infinity · A = initial series · 1 = SEER2 tier (21) · 24-60 = nominal kBtuh · W = standard AC · 0 = standard · 0 = open · 3 = 208/230-1 · position 13 = minor series (S1 p2)"},{"label":"Control","value":"Infinity System Control (communicating, 2 wires to the outdoor unit) is required and must run the latest software (S5 p2, p9)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft of lineset and the smallest AHRI indoor coil)","value":"24: 5.2 · 36: 6.0 · 48: 6.4 · 60: 7.7 (PD p3; SI p8)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Through the Infinity control: long-press the service icon, then Installation & Service > Refrigerant Charging, then choose 'New ODU (factory pre-charged)' or 'Full system charge/recharge'. Enter the indoor unit, lineset, environment (Arid <45% RH, Semi-Arid 45-65%, Humid 65%+) and ODU coil material. The control calculates the added charge and the target subcooling (S5 p8-12)","key":true},{"label":"Subcool window / tolerance","value":"Outdoor 65-105 °F and indoor 65-80 °F; outside that window, weigh in only. Tolerance ±1 °F. Add no more than 0.5 lb/min, then let it run 15 min (S5 p8-12)"},{"label":"Nominal subcooling (reference only)","value":"24: 6 · 36: 6 · 48: 9 · 60: 11.5 °F, at 25 ft, 95 °F OD, 80/67 °F ID - the control's target takes priority (PD p6; SI Table 3)"},{"label":"Liquid-line check (Table 4)","value":"Example: 301 psig with 10 °F subcooling = 90 °F liquid line (S5 p11)"},{"label":"Added charge per foot","value":"Not published - the control calculates it; see rating plate"},{"label":"Pumpdown","value":"From the control (Refrigerant Charging > Pumpdown, default 20 min). It ends when suction drops below 20 psig. Do not use the conventional method - the compressor is VFD-driven (S5 p13)"},{"label":"Indoor coil","value":"Must be a factory R-454B hard-shutoff TXV coil with a dissipation board. No pistons, no R-410A TXVs (S5 p22)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes / lengths","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. Rated vapor: 24: 3/4 · 36: 7/8 · 48: 7/8 · 60: 1-1/8. Maximum 200 ft actual / 200 ft equivalent; outdoor above indoor 100 ft; outdoor below indoor 80 ft (PD p4)"},{"label":"Long line","value":"Beyond 80 ft, or beyond 20 ft of vertical with the outdoor unit below: needs the KAALS0201LLS liquid-line solenoid, installed within 2 ft of the indoor unit (S5 p4; PD p4)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1, 197-253 V, SCCR 5 kA; inverter - LRA and capacitor are not published, the PD lists MRC instead)","rows":[{"label":"RLA / MRC / fan FLA / MCA / MOCP","value":"24: 11.7 / 25 / 0.70 / 19.4 / 25 · 36: 12.7 / 25 / 0.88 / 22.9 / 25 · 48: 17.9 / 25 / 0.88 / 30.6 / 40 · 60: 23.7 / 35 / 0.88 / 36.9 / 50 (PD p3)","key":true},{"label":"Compressor windings, T1-T2-T3 at 68 °F","value":"24: 1.630 · 36: 0.740 · 48: 0.460 · 60: 0.424 Ω; more than 1 MΩ to ground; do not use a megger (SI p17-21)"}]},{"title":"Protection, sensors & diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens 670 ±10 psig, closes 470 ±25 psig (SI p17-21)","key":true},{"label":"Low pressure","value":"There is no low-pressure switch. Suction and discharge transducers (0-620 psig) on P1/P2 handle it (SI p17-21)"},{"label":"Thermistors","value":"10K: 10.0 kΩ at 77 °F, 32.6 kΩ at 32 °F, 85.5 kΩ at 0 °F. ODT (50K): 50.15 kΩ at 25 °C, 7.565 kΩ at 75 °C, 1.7 kΩ at 125 °C (SI p17-21)"},{"label":"Diagnostics","value":"The amber LED flashes the base code: short flashes are the first digit, long flashes the second. The PCM's 5x7 matrix and the wall control show base + expansion codes. Green COMM LED = communication with the wall control; red/green LED = communication with the VFD. Recall: with power off, short the forced-defrost pins (J2), then power up (SI Table 11/12, p20-23)"},{"label":"Key codes (lockout in brackets)","value":"13-53 system control upgrade (permanent) · 18-11 indoor coil freeze · 25-61/62/63 model plug / configuration · 31-11/16/19 high-pressure limit / HPS trip / disable (31-58 = 2 h) · 32-15/55/59 low-pressure limit / lockout (2 h) / disable (permanent) · 34 high temperature · 38-53/54 compressor start / no pump · 39 fan · 41 defrost overrun · 44 PEV timeout · 51-55 thermistors · 57/58 pressure transducers · 61 reversing valve · 64 EXV-H · 81-88 VFD, PFC and voltage (SI p20-23)","key":true}]},{"title":"A2L & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Dissipation board","value":"A factory dissipation board is required. The control will not allow operation without one (S5 p9-10)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum floor area (Table 5)","value":"5 lb: 76 ft² · 8 lb: 122 ft² · 12 lb: 182 ft² · 14 lb: 213 ft² · 25 lb: 380 ft². Record the total charge on the label (S5 p12-13)"},{"label":"Evacuation / opening the circuit","value":"500 microns, rising no more than 1500 microns in 10 min (S5 p7). Opening the circuit: recover, purge with inert gas, evacuate to 1500 microns, then break the vacuum with inert gas (S5 p21)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 55 °F to 125 °F, or down to 0 °F with Low Ambient enabled in the control (no kit needed). Altitude 10,000 ft or less (SI p4; PD p1)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Charge to the wall control's target, not the PD number","body":"The subcooling target is system-specific. The PD/SI values are only nominal. The control shows charge in lb and oz, but the rating plate is in decimal pounds. For lines under 15 ft, the control shows a negative number (charge to remove)."},{"title":"VFD safety and pumpdown","body":"The VFD cover must never be removed. Wait 2 minutes, then check the VFD is at 0 V. Never apply line voltage to the compressor. Pumpdown must be done through the control - do not use the conventional method."},{"title":"Document mismatches","body":"The 26VNA1 SI example calls code 32 a 'low pressure switch open', but the unit has no low-pressure switch; Table 11 calls it a low-pressure limit. The winding tables say '68°F (20°F)'; this should read 20 °C."},{"title":"Replaced PCM","body":"On a replaced PCM, the model configuration must be set from the wall control, the Service Tech app, the dip switches or a physical plug."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Added charge per foot (the control calculates it), compressor LRA and capacitor (inverter), a low-pressure cut-out value (transducer-based), model-plug resistances. No separate Service Manual was located."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"27VNA0 / 27VNA3 / 27VNA1 (Infinity variable-speed heat pumps, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Carrier Infinity Variable Speed heat pumps with Greenspeed Intelligence, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L), communicating (Infinity System Control required). The 6th digit is the SEER2 tier. 27VNA0: up to 20 SEER2 / 11.5 EER2 / 9.5 HSPF2, rotary 20-100%, sizes 24/36/48/60, heats down to -11 °F. 27VNA3: up to 23 SEER2 / 13.5 EER2 / 10.5 HSPF2, 20-100%, rotary on sizes 24-48 and scroll on the 60, heats down to -13 °F, larger 2-row coil and a bigger factory charge than the 27VNA0. 27VNA1: the COLD CLIMATE heat pump, one size only (54, 4.5 ton), up to 21 SEER2 / 13 EER2 / 12.5 HSPF2, scroll 30-100%, 100% heating capacity down to 5 °F, heats down to -23 °F. Every one of them is Greenspeed; the cold-climate model is the 27VNA1, not the 27VNA3.","match":["27VNA0","27VNA3","27VNA1","27VNA024A003","27VNA036A003","27VNA048A003","27VNA060A003","27VNA324A003","27VNA336A003","27VNA348A003","27VNA360A003","27VNA154A003"],"source":"Carrier 27VNA0 Product Data, Cat. 27VNA0-02PD (02/26); Carrier 27VNA3 Product Data, Cat. 27VNA3-02PD (08/25); Carrier 27VNA1 Product Data, Cat. 27VNA1-02PD (09/25); Carrier 27VNA0 Installation Instructions, Cat. 27VNA0-2SI (04/25); Carrier 27VNA3 Installation Instructions, Cat. 27VNA3-2SI (04/2025); Carrier 27VNA1 Installation Instructions, Cat. 27VNA1-2SI (04/25); superseded 27VNA3-01PD, 27VNA1-01PD, 27VNA0-1SI and 27VNA3-1SI used only to cross-check","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (27VNA036A003)","value":"27 = R-454B HP · V = variable speed · N = Infinity · A = initial series · position 6 = SEER2 tier: 0 = 20 (27VNA0), 1 = 21 (27VNA1, cold climate, size 54 only), 3 = 23 (27VNA3) · 24-60 = nominal kBtuh · A = standard HP · 0 = standard · 0 = open · 3 = 208/230-1 · position 13 = minor series (S2-S4 p2)"},{"label":"Which one is the cold-climate model","value":"The 27VNA1 (size 54, 4.5 ton; 100% heating capacity down to 5 °F, heats down to -23 °F). Not the 27VNA3 - that one has the larger 2-row coil and bigger factory charge than the 27VNA0 (S2-S4 p1-3)","key":true},{"label":"Control","value":"Infinity System Control (communicating, 2 wires to the outdoor unit) is required and must run the latest software (S6-S8 p2, p9)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft of lineset and the smallest AHRI indoor coil)","value":"27VNA0: 24: 4.9 · 36: 6.7 · 48: 7.9 · 60: 8.2 — 27VNA3: 24: 11.8 · 36: 12.1 · 48: 12.3 · 60: 13.0 — 27VNA1: size 54 only, 14.1 lb (PD p3; SI p8)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Through the Infinity control: long-press the service icon, then Installation & Service > Refrigerant Charging, then choose 'New ODU (factory pre-charged)' or 'Full system charge/recharge'. Enter the indoor unit, lineset, environment (Arid <45% RH, Semi-Arid 45-65%, Humid 65%+) and ODU coil material. The control calculates the added charge and the target subcooling (S6-S8 p8-12)","key":true},{"label":"Subcool window / tolerance","value":"Outdoor 65-105 °F and indoor 65-80 °F; outside that window, weigh in only. Tolerance ±1 °F. Add no more than 0.5 lb/min, then let it run 15 min (S6-S8 p8-12)"},{"label":"Nominal subcooling (reference only)","value":"27VNA0: 24: 14 · 36: 12 · 48: 5 · 60: 7 (runs backwards by size) — 27VNA3: 24: 5 · 36: 7 · 48: 7 · 60: 10 — 27VNA1-54: 12 °F, at 25 ft, 95 °F OD, 80/67 °F ID - the control's target takes priority (PD p6; SI Table 3)"},{"label":"Heating","value":"'htg check charge' is checked against the Heating Check Chart inside the control-box cover. Do NOT adjust charge from it. If the charge is wrong, recover and use 'full system charge/recharge' (S6-S8 p12)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Heating EXV on board (PD p3). Indoor coil must be a factory R-454B hard-shutoff TXV coil with a dissipation board; no pistons, no R-410A TXVs (S5 p22)"},{"label":"Pumpdown","value":"From the control (Refrigerant Charging > Pumpdown, default 20 min). It ends when suction drops below 20 psig. Do not use the conventional method - the compressor is VFD-driven (S6-S8 p13)"},{"label":"Added charge per foot","value":"Not published - the control calculates it; see rating plate"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. on every model. Rated vapor: 27VNA0: 24: 3/4 · 36: 7/8 · 48: 7/8 · 60: 1-1/8 — 27VNA3: 3/4 · 7/8 · 1-1/8 · 1-1/8 — 27VNA1: 1-1/8 (PD p4)"},{"label":"Maximum lengths","value":"27VNA0: 200 ft actual / 200 ft equivalent; outdoor above indoor 100 ft; outdoor below indoor 80 ft — 27VNA3: 250 ft equivalent; outdoor above indoor 200 ft on the 5-ton and 100 ft on 2-4 ton; below 80 ft — 27VNA1: 250 ft equivalent; outdoor above indoor 200 ft; below 80 ft (PD p4)"},{"label":"Long line","value":"Starts beyond 80 ft, or beyond 20 ft of vertical with the outdoor unit below. HPs: no accessories needed (S5 p4; PD p4)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1, 197-253 V, SCCR 5 kA; inverter - LRA and capacitor are not published, the PD lists MRC instead)","rows":[{"label":"27VNA0 (24/36/48/60)","value":"RLA 11.7 / 17.5 / 22.6 / 27.2 · MRC 25 / 25 / 35 / 35 · fan FLA 0.70 / 0.88 / 0.88 / 0.88 · MCA 19.4 / 22.9 / 30.6 / 36.9 · MOCP 25 / 30 / 40 / 50 (PD p3)","key":true},{"label":"27VNA3 (24/36/48/60)","value":"RLA 11.6 / 14.3 / 20.4 / 27.4 · MRC 25 / 25 / 35 / 35 · fan FLA 0.88 · MCA 19.7 / 23.8 / 31.0 / 37.5 · MOCP 25 / 25 / 40 / 40 (PD p3)"},{"label":"27VNA1-54","value":"RLA 18.7 · MRC 35 · fan FLA 0.88 · MCA 37.5 · MOCP 40 (PD p3)"},{"label":"Compressor windings, T1-T2-T3 at 68 °F (24/36/48/60)","value":"27VNA0: 1.630 / 0.460 / 0.424 / 0.424 · 27VNA3: 0.740 / 0.453 / 0.424 / 0.424 · 27VNA1: 0.424 Ω; more than 1 MΩ to ground; do not use a megger (SI p17-21)"}]},{"title":"Defrost, protection & diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Defrost","value":"Interval 30, 60 or 90 min, or AUTO (the default), set in the Infinity control - there are no dip switches. Termination: when the coil has cleared, or at a time limit of usually 15 min. Forced defrost: short the pins for more than 5 s while in heating; it runs at least 30 s. If the OCT fails: fixed 60 min interval for 10 min. The outdoor fan stays off during defrost (S6-S8 p18, p21)","key":true},{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens 670 ±10 psig, closes 470 ±25 psig (SI p17-21)"},{"label":"Low pressure","value":"There is no low-pressure switch. Suction and discharge transducers (0-620 psig) on P1/P2 handle it (SI p17-21)"},{"label":"Thermistors","value":"10K: 10.0 kΩ at 77 °F, 32.6 kΩ at 32 °F, 85.5 kΩ at 0 °F. ODT (50K): 50.15 kΩ at 25 °C, 7.565 kΩ at 75 °C, 1.7 kΩ at 125 °C (SI p17-21)"},{"label":"Diagnostics","value":"The amber LED flashes the base code: short flashes are the first digit, long flashes the second. The PCM's 5x7 matrix and the wall control show base + expansion codes. Green COMM LED = communication with the wall control; red/green LED = communication with the VFD. Recall: with power off, short the forced-defrost pins (J2), then power up (SI Table 11/12, p20-23)"},{"label":"Key codes (lockout in brackets)","value":"13-53 system control upgrade (permanent) · 18-11 indoor coil freeze · 25-61/62/63 model plug / configuration · 31-11/16/19 high-pressure limit / HPS trip / disable (31-58 = 2 h) · 32-15/55/59 low-pressure limit / lockout (2 h) / disable (permanent) · 34 high temperature · 38-53/54 compressor start / no pump · 39 fan · 41 defrost overrun · 44 PEV timeout · 51-55 thermistors · 57/58 pressure transducers · 61 reversing valve · 64 EXV-H · 81-88 VFD, PFC and voltage (SI p20-23)"}]},{"title":"A2L & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Dissipation board","value":"A factory dissipation board is required. The control will not allow operation without one (S6-S8 p9-10)"},{"label":"Minimum floor area (Table 5)","value":"5 lb: 76 ft² · 8 lb: 122 ft² · 12 lb: 182 ft² · 14 lb: 213 ft² · 25 lb: 380 ft². Record the total charge on the label (p12-13)"},{"label":"Evacuation / opening the circuit","value":"500 microns, rising no more than 1500 microns in 10 min (p7). Opening the circuit: recover, purge with inert gas, evacuate to 1500 microns, then break the vacuum with inert gas (S5 p21)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 55 °F to 125 °F, or down to 0 °F with Low Ambient enabled in the control (no kit needed). Heating minimum: -11 °F (27VNA0), -13 °F (27VNA3), -23 °F (27VNA1) - from the PD only. Altitude 10,000 ft or less (SI p4; PD p1)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Cold climate is the 27VNA1, not the 27VNA3","body":"The 6th digit is the SEER2 tier (0 = 20, 1 = 21, 3 = 23). Every one of them is Greenspeed. The 27VNA1 is the one-size (54) cold-climate model; the 27VNA3 is the 23 SEER2 tier with a larger 2-row coil and bigger charge."},{"title":"Charge to the wall control's target; never adjust charge in heating","body":"The subcooling target is system-specific and the PD/SI values are only nominal. On a heat pump, never adjust charge in heating - recover and weigh in instead. The control shows charge in lb and oz, but the rating plate is in decimal pounds. For lines under 15 ft, the control shows a negative number (charge to remove)."},{"title":"Charge differences between the three","body":"The 27VNA3 factory charge (11.8-13.0 lb) is about 5 lb more than the 27VNA0. The 27VNA0 subcool targets run backwards by size (14 / 12 / 5 / 7)."},{"title":"VFD safety and pumpdown","body":"The VFD cover must never be removed. Wait 2 minutes, then check the VFD is at 0 V. Never apply line voltage to the compressor. Pumpdown must be done through the control - do not use the conventional method."},{"title":"Document mismatches","body":"The winding tables say '68°F (20°F)'; this should read 20 °C. 27VNA3-1SI and 27VNA3-01PD covered only sizes 36-60; size 24 appears only in 27VNA3-02PD / 2SI. On a replaced PCM, the model configuration must be set from the wall control, the Service Tech app, the dip switches or a physical plug."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Added charge per foot (the control calculates it), compressor LRA and capacitor (inverter), a low-pressure cut-out value (transducer-based), minimum heating ambient in the 27VNA3 and 27VNA1 SIs (PD only), model-plug resistances. No separate Service Manual was located."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"27VPA9 (Performance variable-speed heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Carrier Performance Series variable-speed heat pump with InteliSense, Puron Advance R-454B (A2L). Variable-speed rotary compressor running from a VFD (25-100%). Up to 19 SEER2, 14 EER2, 10 HSPF2. Sizes 24/36/48/60 (2 to 5 tons), all 208-230-1 (27VPA924A003, 27VPA936A003, 27VPA948A003, 27VPA960A003). Non-communicating PCM with 8 DIP switches and a 5x7 LED; charge by subcooling in CCC mode to the value the LED shows.","match":["27VPA9","27VPA924A003","27VPA936A003","27VPA948A003","27VPA960A003"],"source":"Carrier 27VPA9 Product Data, Cat. No. 27VPA9-01PD, Ed. 02/26; Carrier 27VPA9 Installation Instructions, Cat. No. 27VPA9-01SI, Ed. 10/25","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (27VPA936A003)","value":"27 = Puron Advance (R-454B) HP · V = variable speed · P = Performance · A = initial series · 9 = 19 SEER2 · 24-60 = nominal cooling in 1,000 Btuh · A = Standard HP (region) · 0 = standard feature · 0 = open (not defined) · 3 = 208-230-1 (PD p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge (covers 15 ft of line set)","value":"24: 10 lb (4.54 kg) · 36: 11.9 lb (5.40 kg) · 48: 12.7 lb (5.76 kg) · 60: 13.2 lb (5.99 kg) (PD p3 Physical Data)","key":true},{"label":"Line-length adjustment","value":"Add or remove 0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 in. liquid line above or below 15 ft (SI p3, p10). The rating plate shows the factory charge and the target subcooling (SI p10)"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Heating: EXV-H inside the outdoor unit (PD p3; SI p15). Cooling: the indoor coil must have a factory R-454B TXV - no piston, cap-tube or R-410A TXV coils (SI p5, p22). Standard AC-style liquid service valve; no adapter tube (SI p6)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling in Cooling Check Charge (CCC) mode, set with DIP switch 1. Run in cooling for at least 15 minutes, and wait 15 minutes after each adjustment. Favorable range 65-105 °F outdoor and 65-80 °F indoor (CCC mode entry limits: OAT 60-105 °F and IAT 65-80 °F); outside it, weigh in the charge only (SI p10-12)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling targets","value":"Nominal 24: 8 · 36: 9 · 48: 9 · 60: 13 °F - reference values at 25 ft of line set, 95 °F outdoor and 80/67 °F indoor (PD p6). The subcooling recommendation shown on the PCM's 5x7 LED in CCC mode 'must be followed' (PD p6). Table 3 converts liquid pressure to the required liquid-line temperature for 6-16 °F of subcooling (238-450 psig) (SI p12)","key":true},{"label":"Heating Check Charge (HCC)","value":"OAT -8 to 75 °F. Diagnosis only, using the Heating Check Chart on the inside of the control-box cover. Do NOT adjust charge from it; if the charge is suspect, recover and weigh in the full charge (SI p11)"},{"label":"Leak test / evacuation","value":"Nitrogen at about 200 psi, never above the rating-plate low-side test pressure; must hold for 1 hour. Evacuate to 500 microns; after isolating the pump, the rise must stay under 1,500 microns in 10 minutes. Use EVAC mode to open the EXV before recovery or evacuation; PUMP mode pump-down finishes when suction drops below 20 psig (SI p7, p11)"}]},{"title":"Line set & piping","rows":[{"label":"Service-valve connection / rated vapor line / minimum vapor line","value":"24: 3/4 / 3/4 / 5/8 · 36: 7/8 / 7/8 / 5/8 · 48: 7/8 / 1-1/8 (7/8) / 3/4 · 60: 7/8 / 1-1/8 / 3/4 - see the vapor-line flag. Liquid line 3/8 in. on all sizes, including long lines (SI Table 1 p5; PD p3)"},{"label":"Maximum lengths","value":"Actual 200 ft; equivalent 250 ft; vertical with the outdoor unit above 200 ft, below 80 ft (PD p4)"},{"label":"Long line","value":"Above 80 ft, or above 20 ft vertical with the outdoor unit below - follow the Long Line Guideline. No long-line accessories are required (PD p4; SI p10)"},{"label":"Buried tubing","value":"Up to 36 in. allowed, with a 6 in. rise at the valve (SI p5)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208-230-1; operating range 197-253 V; SCCR 5 kA rms)","rows":[{"label":"Compressor MRC / RLA / fan FLA / MCA / max fuse or breaker","value":"24: 15 / 11.0 / 0.88 / 15.9 / 25 · 36: 15 / 11.5 / 0.88 / 18.1 / 25 · 48: 30 / 16.7 / 0.88 / 25.1 / 30 · 60: 30 / 20.1 / 0.88 / 33.1 / 40. No LRA or capacitor is published (VFD) - see the rating plate (PD p3 Electrical Data)","key":true},{"label":"Compressor winding resistance at 68 °F, across T1/T2/T3","value":"24 and 36: 0.61 Ω · 48 and 60: 0.18 Ω. To ground: more than 1 MΩ. Do not use a megger (SI Table 8 p18)"},{"label":"Fan","value":"1/3 HP brushless DC motor fed from the VFD, 200-800 rpm, 5,000 CFM (PD p3; SI p15)"},{"label":"Control power","value":"24 V, 40 VA minimum (SI p8)"}]},{"title":"Pressures, sensors & model plug","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 670 ±10 psig and closes at 470 ±25 psig. It removes power from the VFD (SI p16)"},{"label":"Low pressure","value":"There is no low-pressure switch. Suction and discharge transducers (P1/P2, 0-620 psig) handle protection (SI p15)"},{"label":"Thermistors","value":"10K sensors (OAT, OCT, LLT, OST): 10.0 kΩ at 77 °F, 32.6 kΩ at 32 °F, 85.5 kΩ at 0 °F. ODT is a 50K sensor: 50.15 kΩ at 25 °C, 7.565 kΩ at 75 °C, 1.7 kΩ at 125 °C (SI Tables 6-7 p16)"},{"label":"Model plug (pins 1-4 / pins 2-3)","value":"24: HK70EZ003, 5.1K / 24K · 36: HK70EZ015, 5.1K / 360K · 48: HK70EZ027, 11K / 150K · 60: HK70EZ039, 18K / 62K (SI Table 5 p16)"}]},{"title":"Defrost & controls","rows":[{"label":"Defrost","value":"DIP switches 5 and 6 select 30, 60 or 90 minutes, or AUTO (the default; starts defrost when it detects frost). Defrost normally ends on a time limit of about 15 minutes. Forced defrost: short the J2 pins for more than 5 seconds while in heating. If the OCT sensor fails, defrost runs every 60 minutes for 10 minutes. The outdoor fan stays off during defrost (SI p12, p15, p16, p18)","key":true},{"label":"PCM DIP switches (8)","value":"1: charging modes (CCC, HCC, EVAC, PUMP) · 2: model configuration, used only when replacing the VFD · 3 and 4: show IDU or thermostat PLC comm faults · 5 and 6: defrost interval · 7: Comfort (the AHRI-rated default) or Efficiency mode · 8: status check, which shows PCM and VFD firmware and the model configuration (SI Table 2 p10)"},{"label":"Thermostat","value":"Standard 2-stage heat pump thermostat (Y1/Y2/O), or 24 VAC PLC with a Carrier Smart Thermostat with InteliSense (SI p9, p13)"},{"label":"Time delays","value":"5 minutes on power-up and between cycles. Bypass by shorting the forced-defrost pins for 1-5 seconds (SI p15-16)"},{"label":"Status LEDs","value":"Amber: on = standby · 1 slow flash = low capacity · 2 slow flashes = high capacity · continuous slow flash = operation limited · continuous fast flash = lockout or code recall. Green COMM: flashing green = talking to the VFD; flashing red = comm failure. The 5x7 LED scrolls the top 4 active codes; for code recall, short J2 and then power up (SI p14, p18)"}]},{"title":"Diagnostic codes (base code, then F fault / M malfunction expansion; SI Table 9 p19)","rows":[{"label":"Line voltage, comms and board","value":"14-94 line voltage low · 15-94 line voltage high · 18-11 indoor coil freeze protection · 19-06 / 19-07 TSTAT PLC lost / authentication · 21-06 / 21-07 IDU PLC lost / authentication · 24-58 5 V PCM power out of range · 25-62 model config missing · 25-63 VFD/PCM model mismatch · 26-27 / 26-31 reprogramming / EEPROM failure · 28-71 fuse 1 open (RVS) · 28-72 fuse 2 open (LLS) · 28-73 VFD 15 V shorted to ground"},{"label":"Pressure and compressor","value":"31: F11/M58 high-pressure limit, F16/M56 HPS trip, F19 HPS disable · 32: F15/M55 low-pressure limit, M59 low-pressure disable · 33-15/55 low discharge limit · 34-11/58 high temperature limit · 35-11/58 high compression limit · 36-15/55 low compression limit · 37-41 cold compressor sump lockout · 38: F13/M53 starting error, M54 no pump, M55 physical malfunction, F14 disconnect, F18 high differential-pressure start disable, F31/M71 sensorless stall"},{"label":"Fan, defrost and power","value":"39: F13/M53 fan start, F14 fan speed, F15 unexpected fan shutdown · 41-13 defrost overrun · 44-14 pressure-equalization timeout · 45-14 / 15 / 16 general, critical and off-mode power curtailment"},{"label":"Sensors","value":"51: F01 OAT open, F02 OAT shorted, M43 OAT not valid · 52: F01/F02 OCT-HP open or shorted, F03/F04 LLT-AC open or shorted · 53: F01/M41 OST open, F02/M42 OST shorted · 54-01 / 54-02 ODT open / shorted · 55-01 / 55-02 LLT-HP open / shorted · 57 and 58: P1 and P2 open (01/41) or shorted (02/42)"},{"label":"Reversing valve, EXV and USB","value":"61: M41 RV solenoid open, F13/M53 RV timeout, F55/M95 RV position incorrect · 64: M41 EXV-H phase open, M44 power short to ground, M45 phase short to ground · 79-01 USB drive fault, 79-02 file not found, 79-03 invalid SW version"},{"label":"VFD and inverter","value":"81: F13/M53 PFC error, F14/M54 unbalanced PFCM, F15/M55 current detection, F31 stator heat incorrect · 82: F11 input power limit, F12 line voltage limit, F16/M56 low-voltage shutdown, F17/M57 line over-voltage, F18/M58 IGBT short · 83: F11 compressor current limit, F12 line peak current limit, F13 input current limit, F15/M55 running motor over-current, F57 compressor underspeed · 84-11/55 IPM over temperature · 85-13/53 DC under-voltage · 85-14/54 DC over-voltage · 86-06/46 VFD communication · 87-13/53 VFD initialization · 88: F27 VFD reprogramming failure, F32/M72 IPM temp sensor, F41/M81 MOSFET open · 89-67 / 89-68 VFD software / model error · 91-6/46 incorrect compressor speed reported"},{"label":"Lockout times (SI Table 10 p20)","value":"Permanent (unlikely to clear on its own): 25-62, 25-63, 28-71, 28-72, 32-59, 51-43 · 4 hours: 28-73, 38-53, 38-55, 87-53 · 30 minutes: 38-54 · 1 hour: 39-53, 86-46, 88-81, 91-46 · duration of the event: 24-58 and the sensor, RV and EXV opens · most others: 2 hours"}]},{"title":"A2L & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Dissipation board","value":"A factory-approved R-454B indoor unit with its dissipation control board is mandatory (SI p1, p8; PD p24)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum room area by total system charge (SI Table 4 p12)","value":"4 lb: 61 ft² · 10 lb: 152 ft² · 13 lb: 198 ft² · 14 lb: 213 ft² · 15 lb: 228 ft² · 20 lb: 304 ft² · 25 lb: 380 ft²; other rows in SI Table 4. Record the total charge on the unit's charging label"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 32-125 °F outdoor; heating down to -10 °F (SI p4; PD p24). Maximum altitude 10,000 ft (SI p3). Clearances: 24 in. at the service end, 48 in. above, 6 in. on one side and 12 in. on the others (SI p4). Before first start, power the unit for 24 hours so the stator heat can warm the compressor (SI p9)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Two charging windows are published","body":"65-105 °F outdoor (SI p10) versus 60-105 °F OAT for CCC entry (SI p11)."},{"title":"Vapor-line conflict on the 48 and 60","body":"The SI Table 1 footnote says 7/8 in. is the required maximum diameter above 25 ft of line set, for the 48 and 60 (SI p5). The PD capacity-loss table lists 1-1/8 in. for the 60 up to 250 ft, and for the 48 up to 80 ft (PD p4). Treat 7/8 as the safe choice and confirm with the Long Line Guideline."},{"title":"Do not charge from the Heating Check Chart","body":"HCC is for diagnosis only. For a winter charge, weigh it in (SI p11). The dissipation board is mandatory - R-410A TXV coils and field-converted coils are not allowed (SI p1, p22)."},{"title":"Service lockouts","body":"Do not remove the VFD cover. Wait 2 minutes after power-off and verify 0 V at the VFD before touching it. Never put line voltage on the compressor. Fan wires are not ground-referenced, so do not measure them while the unit runs (SI p2, p15, p18)."},{"title":"Service modes","body":"Pump-down and recovery need the PUMP and EVAC modes, because a normal pump-down does not work with the VFD. EVAC opens the EXV (SI p11). After replacing the VFD, set the model configuration with DIP switch 2 (SI p11, p16). Code names differ slightly between Table 9 and Table 10 - for example, 81-54 is 'Unbalanced PFCM Error' in Table 9 and 'PFC Phase Over Current Malfunction' in Table 10 (SI p19-20)."},{"title":"Not published","body":"No 27VPA9 Service Manual turned up, so code troubleshooting steps and the triple-evacuation procedure were not checked. Heating Check Chart values (printed on the control-box cover only), which DIP 5/6 positions give each defrost interval, LRA, and per-size subcooling on the rating plate."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"GA4SAN5 (Builder single-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Carrier Builder line single-stage AC condenser, 13.4 SEER2 class, North region only (suffix N), Puron Advance R-454B (A2L) - use only with R-454B indoor units. 1.5-5 tons (18-60), 13.4-16.0 SEER2 / 11.0-13.5 EER2, scroll compressor, 208/230-1 only. The 4-ton model is now GA4SAN54801N and replaces 54800N. Distributors sell the line as 'Sentry', but that name does not appear in any Carrier document. No control board, no fault codes.","match":["GA4SAN5","GA4SAN51800N","GA4SAN52400N","GA4SAN53000N","GA4SAN53600N","GA4SAN54200N","GA4SAN54800N","GA4SAN54801N","GA4SAN56000N"],"source":"Carrier GA4SAN5 Product Data, Cat. GA4SAN5-02PD (03/26); Carrier GA4SAN5 Product Data, Cat. GA4SAN5-01PD (12/24), for the earlier 24 and 48 (54800N) values; Carrier GA4SAN5 / GA5SAN5 Installation Instructions, Cat. GA4SAN5-01SI (11/24); Carrier Long Line Guideline LLG-R454B-01 (07/24)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode","value":"G = Builder · A = AC (H = HP) · 4 = 13.4 SEER2 class (5 = 14.3, 8 = 18) · S = single-stage (T = 2-stage) · A = major series · N = 208/230-1 · 5 = R-454B · 18-60 = size in kBtuh · 0 = standard · position 11: 0 = standard, 1 = compressor electrical rating change · N = North AC (W = Southwest AC, A = standard HP) (GA4SAN5-02PD p2)"},{"label":"Shared manual","value":"GA4SAN5-01SI also covers the GA5SAN5, the 14.3 SEER2 model for the Southwest region"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft of 3/8 in. liquid line)","value":"18: 3.90 · 24: 3.90 · 30: 5.30 · 36: 4.90 · 42: 6.60 · 48: 7.10 · 60: 6.40 (02PD p3)","key":true},{"label":"Line adjustment","value":"0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in., 0.40 for 5/16 in., 0.27 for 1/4 in. The factory lineset allowance is 9 oz. Formula: (oz/ft x length) - 9 oz (02PD p5 Table 3; SI p3/p7)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Indoor TXV, charge by subcooling, ±3 °F. Charge only when outdoor is 70-100 °F and indoor is 70-80 °F; otherwise weigh in (GA4SAN5-01SI p7)"},{"label":"Required subcooling, °F","value":"18: 8 · 24: 10 · 30: 9 · 36: 8 · 42: 8 · 48: 12 · 60: 10 - the rating plate governs (02PD p9)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure test / evacuation","value":"About 200 psi nitrogen held for 1 hour. Evacuate to 500 microns (GA4SAN5-01SI p4)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. on all sizes (3/8 in. is the maximum). Rated vapor: 18: 5/8 · 24: 3/4 · 30: 3/4 · 36: 7/8 · 42: 7/8 · 48: 7/8 · 60: 1-1/8, rated at 25 ft (SI p4 Table 1)"},{"label":"Lengths / long line","value":"Max 250 ft equivalent. Outdoor unit up to 200 ft above, or 80 ft below. Long line starts beyond 80 ft or 35 ft vertical (02PD p1, p5, p21). Crankcase heater required beyond 80 ft, or when the outdoor unit is 35 ft below the indoor unit - see the vertical-limit flag"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1, 197-253 V)","rows":[{"label":"LRA / RLA / fan FLA / MCA / MOCP","value":"18: 41.5 / 8.3 / 0.4 / 10.8 / 15 · 24: 59.0 / 8.2 / 0.6 / 12.1 / 20 · 30: 67.0 / 12.5 / 0.6 / 16.2 / 25 · 36: 82.5 / 13.5 / 0.6 / 17.5 / 30 · 42: 109.0 / 14.7 / 1.4 / 19.8 / 30 · 48 (54801N): 126.0 / 18.1 / 1.2 / 23.8 / 40 · 60: 157.0 / 23.7 / 1.5 / 31.1 / 50 (02PD p9)","key":true},{"label":"Earlier values (GA4SAN5-01PD p9)","value":"24: RLA 9.2 · 48 (54800N): RLA 17.3, FLA 1.05, MCA 22.7 - see the RLA conflict flag"},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Switches, operating range & A2L","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"None come standard. Accessory kits: LPS KAALP0501PUR, HPS KAAHI0601PUR. Set points are not published; see the switch or rating plate. The low-ambient switch cycles the fan to hold about 100-225 psig (02PD p6-7)","key":true},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 55-115 °F; down to 0 °F with the low-ambient kit (02PD p1, p21). Maximum elevation 11,500 ft (SI p2). Low-ambient cooling below 55 °F needs the low-ambient kit, freeze stat, hard-start kit and crankcase heater (PD accessory tables)"},{"label":"A2L","value":"A factory-authorized leak dissipation system or board must be installed with the indoor unit (GA4SAN5-01SI p5). Check the minimum room area against total system charge: 4 lb → 61 ft², 10 lb → 152 ft², 25 lb → 380 ft² (SI p7); record the final charge on the unit label. Use non-sparking tools, a refrigerant detector, and a recovery pump rated for flammable refrigerant. To open the circuit: recover, purge with nitrogen, evacuate to 1500 microns, then purge with nitrogen again before cutting or brazing","key":true},{"label":"Fault codes","value":"None published for this family - no control board"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"GA4SAN5 24 RLA: the two product data editions disagree","body":"9.2 in 01PD, 8.2 in 02PD. The MCA is 12.1 in both, and that matches 1.25 x 9.2 + 0.6. Check the rating plate."},{"title":"Long-line vertical limits disagree","body":"LLG-R454B-01 p2: AC = 35 ft vertical (outdoor below), HP = 80 ft total only. GA8TAN5 SI p10 and PD p19 say 20 ft vertical. GH5SAN5 SI and 03PD p5 say 20 ft below. Use the stricter number."},{"title":"Read the full model for the 48","body":"GA4SAN54801N (02PD) replaced 54800N; the 48 RLA, fan FLA and MCA changed between them. The rating plate decides."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Loss-of-charge and high-pressure switch set points, control-board fault or flash codes (none exist for this family; the R-454B split-system service manual was not found), capacitor ratings. The 'Sentry' brand name appears only on distributor sites."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"GA8TAN5 (Builder two-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Carrier Builder line 2-stage AC condenser, 18 SEER2 class, Southwest region (suffix 00W), Puron Advance R-454B (A2L) - R-454B indoor units only. 2/3/4/5 tons (24/36/48/60), up to 18.5 SEER2 and 14.5 EER2 (maximum SEER2 by size 18.5 / 17.0 / 18.0 / 16.5), 2-stage unloading scroll, 208/230-1. Has its own transformer. Charge in HIGH stage only. No factory pressure switches.","match":["GA8TAN5","GA8TAN52400W","GA8TAN53600W","GA8TAN54800W","GA8TAN56000W"],"source":"Carrier GA8TAN5 Product Data, Cat. GA8TAN5-01PD (12/24); Carrier GA8TAN5 Installation Instructions, Cat. GA8TAN5-02SI (02/26); Carrier GA8TAN5-01SI (11/24); Carrier Long Line Guideline LLG-R454B-01 (07/24)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode","value":"G = Builder · A = AC · 8 = 18 SEER2 class · T = 2-stage · A = major series · N = 208/230-1 · 5 = R-454B · 24-60 = size in kBtuh · 0 = standard · 0 = standard · W = Southwest AC (GA8TAN5-01PD p2). Carrier and Bryant badge kits KSALN0199CAC / KSALN0199BRY (PD p6)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft)","value":"24: 5.32 · 36: 7.25 · 48: 8.65 · 60: 9.42 (PD p2)","key":true},{"label":"Line adjustment","value":"0.60 / 0.40 / 0.27 oz/ft (3/8, 5/16, 1/4 in.), with a 9 oz lineset allowance (PD p3)"},{"label":"Required subcooling, °F","value":"24: 8 · 36: 8 · 48: 11 · 60: 11 (PD p5)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Charge in HIGH stage only, by subcooling, ±3 °F (GA8TAN5-02SI p10)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"TXV required. Hard-shutoff TXV is standard with a factory-approved indoor unit. Capillary-tube and fixed-orifice indoor coils are not allowed (PD p7; SI p3)"},{"label":"Pressure test / evacuation","value":"About 200 psi nitrogen held for 1 hour. Evacuate to 500 microns (GA8TAN5-02SI p5)"}]},{"title":"Staging & diagnostics","rows":[{"label":"Controls","value":"The outdoor unit has its own transformer. It powers the control board and the compressor solenoid, so the unit does not need R from indoor (SI p6)"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Y1 = low (about 67% compressor capacity, about 75% capacity at the coil). Y2 energizes the 24 VDC unloader solenoid (the plug has a built-in rectifier) (SI p9-11)"},{"label":"Staging check","value":"Going from low to high stage, suction pressure drops 3-10% and amps rise 20-45%. Do not use liquid pressure to check staging (SI p11)","key":true},{"label":"Unloader coil","value":"About 1640 Ω. Check for 24 VDC at the plug when high stage is called (SI p11)"},{"label":"Winding resistance, S-C / R-C at 70 ±20 °F","value":"024: 1.652 / 1.065 · 036: 1.471 / 0.728 · 048: 1.660 / 0.436 · 060: 1.203 / 0.383 Ω (SI p11 Table 5)"},{"label":"Internal pressure relief","value":"Opens at a 550-625 psi differential (SI p12)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. Rated vapor: 24: 3/4 · 36: 7/8 · 48: 1-1/8 · 60: 1-1/8 (PD p2; SI p3)"},{"label":"Long line","value":"Crankcase heater required beyond 80 ft, or when the outdoor unit is 35 ft below the indoor unit - see the vertical-limit flag"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1, 197-253 V; fan FLA 2.60 on all sizes)","rows":[{"label":"LRA / RLA / MCA / MOCP","value":"24: 62.0 / 10.3 / 15.5 / 20 · 36: 90.0 / 14.6 / 20.9 / 35 · 48: 138.0 / 18.3 / 25.5 / 40 · 60: 149.0 / 22.3 / 30.5 / 50 (PD p5)","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Switches, operating range & A2L","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"None standard. Accessory LPS KAALP0501PUR and HPS KAAHI0601PUR; set points not published (PD p6)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 55-125 °F; 125 °F applies at 230 V (PD p19). Maximum elevation 10,000 ft (SI p2). Low-ambient cooling below 55 °F needs the low-ambient kit, freeze stat, hard-start kit and crankcase heater (PD accessory tables)"},{"label":"A2L","value":"A factory-authorized leak dissipation system or board must be installed with the indoor unit (GA8TAN5-02SI p6; GA8TAN5-01PD p19). Check the minimum room area against total system charge: 4 lb → 61 ft², 10 lb → 152 ft², 25 lb → 380 ft² (SI p10); record the final charge on the unit label. Non-sparking tools, refrigerant detector, flammable-rated recovery pump. To open the circuit: recover, purge with nitrogen, evacuate to 1500 microns, then purge with nitrogen again","key":true},{"label":"Fault codes","value":"None published for this family"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Never charge in low stage","body":"Charge in HIGH stage only. A replacement solenoid plug must have the built-in rectifier."},{"title":"Long-line vertical limits disagree","body":"LLG-R454B-01 p2: AC = 35 ft vertical (outdoor below). GA8TAN5 SI p10 and PD p19 say 20 ft vertical. Use the stricter number."},{"title":"60 fan RPM is a misprint","body":"Printed as '8815' in PD p2, which is clearly a typo."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Loss-of-charge and high-pressure switch set points, control-board fault or flash codes (none exist for this family; the R-454B split-system service manual was not found), capacitor ratings."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"GH5SAN5 (Builder single-stage heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Carrier Builder line single-stage heat pump, 14.3 SEER2 class (suffix 00A), Puron Advance R-454B (A2L) - R-454B indoor units only. 1.5-5 tons (18-60), 14.3-16.0 SEER2 / 10.0-12.5 EER2 / 7.5-7.8 HSPF2, 208/230-1. Comes with a suction accumulator and a loss-of-charge switch. Heating meters through a piston in the outdoor liquid service valve; cooling through the indoor TXV.","match":["GH5SAN5","GH5SAN51800A","GH5SAN52400A","GH5SAN53000A","GH5SAN53600A","GH5SAN54200A","GH5SAN54800A","GH5SAN56000A"],"source":"Carrier GH5SAN5 Product Data, Cat. GH5SAN5-03PD (07/25 revA); Carrier GH5SAN5-02PD (06/24, distributor copy); Carrier GH5SAN5 Installation Instructions, Cat. GH5SAN5-01SI (12/23); Carrier Long Line Guideline LLG-R454B-01 (07/24)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode","value":"G = Builder · H = HP · 5 = 14.3 SEER2 class · S = single-stage · A = major series · N = 208/230-1 · 5 = R-454B · 18-60 = size in kBtuh · 0 = standard · 0 = standard · A = standard HP (GH5SAN5-03PD p2)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge, lb (covers 15 ft)","value":"18: 6.5 · 24: 5.4 · 30: 6.1 · 36: 7.6 · 42: 7.3 · 48: 10.5 · 60: 8.7 (03PD p3)","key":true},{"label":"Line adjustment","value":"Add or remove 0.6 oz/ft of 3/8 in. line above or below 15 ft (GH5SAN5-01SI p4, p9)"},{"label":"Heating piston (outdoor liquid service valve)","value":"18: 42 · 24: 46 · 30: 52 · 36: 52 · 42: 61 · 48: 65 · 60: 70. It must match the rating plate (03PD p3; SI p4)","key":true},{"label":"Required subcooling, °F (cooling mode)","value":"18: 6 · 24: 6 · 30: 12 · 36: 10 · 42: 12 · 48: 13 · 60: 7 (03PD p9). Some indoor units need extra subcooling for good heating performance (SI p4, p9)","key":true},{"label":"Heating check chart","value":"On the unit, for diagnosis only. Do not charge from it (SI p10). SI p9 mentions 'superheat for piston', but no superheat chart is published - treat this as a TXV-cooled heat pump and charge by subcooling"},{"label":"Pressure test / evacuation","value":"About 200 psi nitrogen held for 1 hour. Evacuate to 500 microns (GH5SAN5-01SI p6)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. Rated vapor: 18: 5/8 · 24: 5/8 · 30: 3/4 · 36: 3/4 · 42: 7/8 · 48: 7/8 · 60: 1-1/8 (SI p4)"},{"label":"Lengths / long line","value":"Max 250 ft equivalent, 200 ft actual, 200 ft rise (03PD p5). Crankcase heater required beyond 80 ft, or when the outdoor unit is 20 ft below the indoor unit - see the vertical-limit flag"}]},{"title":"Electrical (208/230-1, 197-253 V)","rows":[{"label":"LRA / RLA / fan FLA / MCA / MOCP","value":"18: 45.1 / 8.3 / 0.50 / 10.9 / 15 · 24: 64.4 / 10.3 / 0.60 / 13.5 / 20 · 30: 67.0 / 12.5 / 0.70 / 16.3 / 25 · 36: 86.0 / 14.4 / 1.20 / 19.2 / 30 · 42: 123.0 / 19.0 / 1.05 / 24.9 / 40 · 48: 126.0 / 22.4 / 1.40 / 29.4 / 50 · 60: 157.0 / 23.7 / 1.50 / 31.1 / 50 (03PD p9)","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Defrost, switches, operating range & A2L","rows":[{"label":"Defrost","value":"Time/temperature board. DIP switches set 30, 60, 90 or 120 min as the initial interval; the board then adjusts it from defrost length. The defrost thermostat closes at about 32 °F and sits on the 3/8 in. stub tube, usually on the bottom circuit. Quiet Shift-2 is DIP 3, off from the factory: it turns the compressor off for about 1 min at defrost entry and exit and locks the interval to the DIP setting. Forced defrost: short the J1 speedup pins for 5 s, then release (SI p3, p8-9)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"The loss-of-charge switch is standard, and the SI says not to disable it (SI p8). Its set points are not published in GH5SAN5 literature; see the rating plate. HPS accessory KAAHI0501PUR (03PD p6)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling 55-125 °F. Heating -10 °F to 66 °F outdoor (03PD p20). Maximum elevation 10,000 ft (SI p1)"},{"label":"A2L","value":"A factory-authorized leak dissipation system or board must be installed with the indoor unit (GH5SAN5-01SI p7). The GH5SAN5 minimum-room-area table differs slightly from the AC SIs: 13 lb → 198 ft² (AC 196), 15 lb → 228 (226), 17 lb → 258 (256) (SI p9); record the final charge on the unit label. Non-sparking tools, refrigerant detector, flammable-rated recovery pump. To open the circuit: recover, purge with nitrogen, evacuate to 1500 microns, then purge with nitrogen again","key":true},{"label":"Fault codes","value":"None published for this family"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The piston must match the plate","body":"The heating piston sits in the outdoor liquid service valve; sizes run 42 to 70 by capacity. Check the stamped number against the rating plate before blaming poor heating on charge."},{"title":"Long-line vertical limits disagree","body":"LLG-R454B-01 p2: HP = 80 ft total only. GH5SAN5 SI and 03PD p5 say 20 ft below. Use the stricter number."},{"title":"'Superheat for piston' has no chart","body":"GH5SAN5-01SI p9 mentions superheat for piston, but no superheat chart is published. Treat this as a TXV-cooled heat pump and charge by subcooling."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Loss-of-charge and high-pressure switch set points, control-board fault or flash codes (none exist for this family), capacitor ratings, and whether a GH5SAN5 SI newer than 01SI (12/23) exists."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"58TN (Infinity 80 two-stage, Series B)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Carrier Infinity 80 two-stage 80% AFUE non-condensing 4-way multipoise gas furnace, Category I (natural draft) venting, variable-speed constant-airflow ECM ('C'), Infinity communicating or 24 V. Natural gas, field-convertible to LP with a kit. Sizes 045C17, 070C14, 070C17, 070C21, 090C17, 090C21, 110C21, 135C24. Figures are for the current Series B (58TN0B, and 58TN1B Low NOx); Series A (58TN0A) used a different control - see flag. Not the generic 58 series entry.","match":["58TN","58TN0B","58TN1B","58TN0A","58TN0B045C17","58TN0B070C14","58TN0B070C17","58TN0B070C21","58TN0B090C17","58TN0B090C21","58TN0B110C21","58TN0B135C24"],"source":"Carrier 58TN0B Product Data, Cat. 58TN0B-02PD (3/26); Carrier 58TN0B Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions, Cat. 58TN0B-03SI (3/26); Carrier 58TN0A-02SI REV A (Series A, for comparison only)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (58TN0B045C17--12)","value":"58 = 80% non-condensing · T = two-stage · N = Infinity (P = Performance) · 0 = 80%, 1 = 80% Low NOx (California 40 ng/J) · B = major series · 045-135 = nominal input · C = constant-airflow VS ECM · 14 / 17 / 21 / 24 = cabinet width · 1 = 115 V/60 Hz · minor series · 12-22 = max cooling airflow (1,200 up to 2,200 CFM) (PD-TN p3; SI-TN p52)"},{"label":"Series A vs Series B","value":"Series B (this entry): 3-digit display, model program by Super Plug or NFC. Series A (58TN0A): model plug, setup switches and 2-digit LED codes. Don't read one series' codes against the other's label (SI-TN p32; 58TN0A-02SI)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"80% (PD-TN p4)"},{"label":"Input high/low, BTUh (standard, and Low NOx upflow)","value":"045: 44,000/29,000 · 070: 66,000/43,500 · 090: 88,000/58,000 · 110: 110,000/72,500 · 135: 132,000/87,000. Low NOx in downflow/horizontal, high: 42,000 / 63,000 / 84,000 / 105,000 / 126,000; low fire unchanged (PD-TN p4)"},{"label":"Output high/low, standard","value":"045: 35,000/23,000 · 070: 53,000/35,000 (070C14 prints 54,000 high) · 090: 71,000/47,000 · 110: 89,000/59,000 · 135: 107,000/70,000 (PD-TN p4)"},{"label":"Burners / orifice / valve","value":"2/3/3/3/4/4/5/6 burners by size, #43 orifices from the factory, redundant White-Rodgers valve, 1/2 in. NPT (PD-TN p5)"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas","value":"Set from Tables 26/27 (22,000 BTUh/burner high, 14,500 low; Low NOx in downflow or horizontal uses the 21,000/burner table). High fire 3.2-3.8 in. w.c.; low fire 1.4-1.7 in. w.c. - if you can't get inside that range, change orifices. Worked example at 0-2,000 ft, 1,000 BTU/cf, SG 0.62: #43 orifices, 3.7 high / 1.6 low (SI-TN p35-36)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"Not captured - see the rating plate or LP kit instructions"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural gas","value":"Installation manual: more than 4.5 in. w.c. and no more than 14 in. w.c. (SI-TN p34). Product data: min 4.5, max 13.6 in. w.c. (PD-TN p5) - see flag. Input within ±2% of the rating plate; clock at the meter in each stage (SI-TN p35-36)"},{"label":"Locking a stage for the manifold check","value":"Set Htt to 2St and jump R-W1 for low fire; jump W2 as well for high fire. Put Htt back afterward (SI-TN p36, p40-41)"},{"label":"High altitude","value":"Derate 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft (multiplier 0.90 at 2,001-3,000 ft down to 0.62 at 9,001-10,000 ft). Above 5,500 ft a field-supplied high-altitude pressure switch is required (SI-TN p35-36 Table 24)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise, high / low fire, °F","value":"045: 30-60 / 20-50 · 070C14: 30-60 / 30-60 · 070C17: 25-55 / 15-45 · 070C21: 25-55 / 15-45 · 090C17: 40-70 / 30-60 · 090C21: 25-55 / 15-45 · 110: 40-70 / 25-55 · 135: 40-70 / 25-55. Set the rise at the midpoint of the range or slightly above (PD-TN p4; SI-TN p23)","key":true},{"label":"Rated ESP","value":"Heating 0.10 (045), 0.12 (070), 0.15 (090), 0.20 (110/135); cooling 0.50. Airflow tables run to 1.0 in. w.c.; some heating settings are marked 'not recommended' because high heat would exceed 1.0 in. w.c. (PD; SI-TN p27-31)"},{"label":"Heat setting","value":"Com1 < Com2 (default) < Eff1 (midpoint rise) < Eff2 (SI-TN p31)"},{"label":"Blower-off delays","value":"Heat 90/120 (default)/150/180 s; cool 5/30/60/90 (default) s (PD-TN p4)"},{"label":"Motor FLA","value":"045C17: 8.8 · 070C14: 6.7 · 070C17: 8.8 · 070C21: 11.5 · 090C17: 6.7 · 090C21: 11.5 · 110: 11.5 · 135: 11.7 (PD)"},{"label":"Filters","value":"Side return: 16x25x3/4 on every width. Bottom return: 14x25 on the 14-1/2 in. cabinet, 16x25 on 17-1/2 in., 20x25 on 21 in., 24x25 on 24 in. Washable filter recommended (SI-TN p43 Table 28). Above 1,800 CFM you need a bottom return, two side returns, or bottom plus side, with at least a 20x25 filter"}]},{"title":"Electrical (115-60-1, 104-127 V)","rows":[{"label":"Max unit amps","value":"045C17: 10.5 · 070C14: 8.0 · 070C17: 10.5 · 070C21: 13.8 · 090C17: 8.6 · 090C21: 14.4 · 110: 14.7 · 135: 13.9. Max fuse or breaker: 15 A on the smaller sizes, 20 A on 070C21 / 090C21 / 110 / 135 (PD)"},{"label":"Unit ampacity - the documents disagree","value":"Product data: 13.8 / 10.7 / 13.8 / 18.0 / 11.3 / 18.5 / 18.8 / 17.8 · Installation manual Table 9: 9.2 / 6.7 / 9.2 / 12.5 / 6.7 / 12.5 / 12.5 / 11.7 (same size order). Max wire length for the 045: 26 ft (product data) vs 25 ft (installation manual) (PD-TN p4; SI-TN p18)","key":true},{"label":"Transformer / fuse","value":"40 VA. The 24 V circuit has a 3 A automotive fuse; code 24.1 means that fuse is blown (PD; SI-TN p42)"}]},{"title":"Ignition, safeties & venting","rows":[{"label":"Igniter / flame signal","value":"Silicon nitride hot-surface igniter; resistance is not published. Flame signal is not published"},{"label":"Ignition sequence","value":"15 s prepurge, then 17 s igniter warm-up, then trial. Flame must prove within 2 s. Four trials, then a 3-hour lockout. Blower-on delay 45 s on low fire and 25 s on high fire. Inducer post-purge 5 s (SI-TN p46-47)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Dual switches (LPS and HPS). Set points are not published"},{"label":"Limits","value":"Main limit is auto-reset. Rollout switches in the gas control area are manual reset. The draft safeguard switch is on the vent elbow - auto-reset, but if it stays open more than 3 minutes the furnace locks out for 3 hours. Set points are not published (SI-TN p34, p41)"},{"label":"Venting","value":"Category I, 4 in. collar. The 135 size needs a 5 or 6 in. vent with an adapter (SI-TN p2)"}]},{"title":"Control & codes","rows":[{"label":"Board","value":"3-digit display, with the status LED visible through the sight glass. Codes are major.minor. Main menu: FLt, t°, Ht, CL2/CL1, CFn, HoD, CoD, Htt, Ctt, dir, AiR, inF, Ct, rSt. Stores the last 7 faults, which survive a power loss (SI-TN p31-33, p42)"},{"label":"Codes (both 58TN and 58TP)","value":"10.1 polarity fault · 12.1 W on at power-up · 13.1 limit lockout · 14.1 / 14.2 / 14.3 ignition and flame-loss lockouts · 21.1 24 V on gas valve when it shouldn't be · 22.1 false flame · 23.4 / 23.5 LPS / HPS stuck closed · 24.1 fuse fault · 25.x program faults · 27.x Super Plug faults · 31.6 / 31.7 HPS open · 32.2 LPS open · 33.1 main limit open · 34.x flame loss · 41.x blower RPM · 43.1 HPS closed before LPS · 45.x control faults · 52.x / 53.x SAT / RAT open or short","key":true},{"label":"58TN only","value":"10.2 dissipation system active (operate blower), 15.2, 17.1 BTM communication loss, 41.3, 51.x outdoor temperature sensor (SI-TN p33 Fig. 46)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Series A and Series B are different controls","body":"Series A used a model plug, setup switches and 2-digit LED codes. Series B uses the 3-digit display with a model program and Super Plug or NFC. Don't read one series' codes against the other's label (58TN0A-02SI; SI-TN p32)."},{"title":"Replacing a Series B board","body":"The new board won't run until it is programmed with the Model Program Number on the rating plate, by Super Plug or the NFC app. A wrong program gives code 25.6 (SI-TN p31-32)."},{"title":"58TN unit ampacity: the product data and the installation manual disagree","body":"PD-TN p4: 13.8 / 10.7 / 13.8 / 18.0 / 11.3 / 18.5 / 18.8 / 17.8. SI-TN p18 Table 9: 9.2 / 6.7 / 9.2 / 12.5 / 6.7 / 12.5 / 12.5 / 11.7. Max wire length for the 045 is 26 ft (PD) vs 25 ft (SI). Neither document explains the difference - size the circuit from the rating plate."},{"title":"Supply pressure maximum: 14 in. w.c. (SI) vs 13.6 in. w.c. (PD)","body":"The installation manual says no more than 14 in. w.c.; the product data says max 13.6. The rating plate is the authority."},{"title":"Dissipation System terminal","body":"The 58TN0B board has a 'Dissipation System Terminal (when used)' and code 10.2, 'Dissipation System Active, operate blower'. The manual does not explain what connects to it - probably an A2L leak-mitigation pairing, but that is not confirmed. The 58TP0B label has neither (SI-TN p20 Fig. 29, p33)."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Igniter resistance, flame current in µA, pressure-switch set points, limit and rollout temperatures, LP manifold pressures."}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"58TP (Performance 80 two-stage, Series B)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Carrier Performance 80 two-stage 80% AFUE non-condensing 4-way multipoise gas furnace, Category I (natural draft) venting, 'Variable 25-speed' constant-torque ECM ('V'), non-communicating, InteliSense-capable with an ecobee for Carrier. Can be twinned with a kit (070V17, 090V17, 090V21, 110V21, 135V24). Natural gas, field-convertible to LP with a kit. Sizes 045V14, 070V14, 070V17, 090V17, 090V21, 110V21, 135V24. Figures are for the current Series B (58TP0B, and 58TP1B Low NOx); Series A (58TP0A) used a different control - see flag. Not the generic 58 series entry.","match":["58TP","58TP0B","58TP1B","58TP0A","58TP0B045V14","58TP0B070V14","58TP0B070V17","58TP0B090V17","58TP0B090V21","58TP0B110V21","58TP0B135V24"],"source":"Carrier 58TP0B Product Data, Cat. 58TP0B-01PD (01/25); Carrier 58TP0B Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions, Cat. 58TP0B-01SI REV A (06/23); Carrier 58TN0B-03SI (3/26) for the shared Series B control menus and board-programming procedure; Carrier 58TP0A-03SI REV A (Series A, for comparison only)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (58TP0B090V21--16)","value":"58 = 80% non-condensing · T = two-stage · P = Performance (N = Infinity) · 0 = 80%, 1 = 80% Low NOx (California 40 ng/J) · B = major series · 045-135 = nominal input · V = variable-speed motor · 14 / 17 / 21 / 24 = cabinet width · 1 = 115 V/60 Hz · minor series · 12-22 = max cooling airflow (1,200 up to 2,200 CFM) (PD-TP p3)"},{"label":"Series A vs Series B","value":"Series B (this entry): 3-digit display, model program by Super Plug or NFC. Series A (58TP0A): model plug, setup switches and 2-digit LED codes. Don't read one series' codes against the other's label (58TP0A-03SI; SI-TN p32)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"AFUE","value":"80% (PD-TP p4)"},{"label":"Input high/low, BTUh (standard, and Low NOx upflow)","value":"045: 44,000/29,000 · 070: 66,000/43,500 · 090: 88,000/58,000 · 110: 110,000/72,500 · 135: 132,000/87,000. Low NOx in downflow/horizontal, high: 42,000 / 63,000 / 84,000 / 105,000 / 126,000; low fire unchanged (PD-TP p4)"},{"label":"Output high/low, standard","value":"045: 35,000/23,000 · 070: 53,000/35,000 · 090: 71,000/47,000 · 110: 89,000/59,000 · 135: 107,000/70,000 (PD-TP p4)"},{"label":"Burners / orifice / valve","value":"2/3/3/3/4/4/5/6 burners by size, #43 orifices from the factory, redundant White-Rodgers valve, 1/2 in. NPT (PD-TP p4)"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas","value":"Set from Tables 17/18 (22,000 BTUh/burner high, 14,500 low; Low NOx in downflow or horizontal uses the 21,000/burner table). High fire 3.2-3.8 in. w.c.; low fire 1.4-1.7 in. w.c. - if you can't get inside that range, change orifices. Worked example at 0-2,000 ft, 1,000 BTU/cf, SG 0.62: #43 orifices, 3.7 high / 1.6 low (SI-TP p34)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"Not captured - see the rating plate or LP kit instructions"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural gas","value":"Installation manual: more than 4.5 in. w.c. and no more than 14 in. w.c. (SI-TP p32). Product data: min 4.5, max 13.6 in. w.c. (PD-TP p4) - see flag. Input within ±2% of the rating plate; clock at the meter in each stage"},{"label":"Locking a stage for the manifold check","value":"Set Htt to 2St and jump R-W1 for low fire; jump W2 as well for high fire. Put Htt back afterward (procedure from the Series B 58TN0B manual, SI-TN p36, p40-41)"},{"label":"High altitude","value":"Derate 4% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft (multiplier 0.90 at 2,001-3,000 ft down to 0.62 at 9,001-10,000 ft). Above 5,500 ft a field-supplied high-altitude pressure switch is required (SI-TP p34 Table 15)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise, high / low fire, °F","value":"045V14: 30-60 / 20-50 · 070V14: 30-60 / 20-50 · 070V17: 25-55 / 15-45 · 090V17: 40-70 / 30-60 · 090V21: 25-55 / 15-45 · 110: 30-60 / 20-50 (not the 58TN's 40-70 / 25-55) · 135: 40-70 / 25-55. Set the rise at the midpoint of the range or slightly above (PD-TP p4; SI-TP p22)","key":true},{"label":"Rated ESP","value":"Heating 0.10 (045), 0.12 (070), 0.15 (090), 0.20 (110/135); cooling 0.50 (PD). Above 1,800 CFM you need a bottom return, two side returns, or bottom plus side, with at least a 20x25 filter (SI-TP p29)"},{"label":"Blower-off delays","value":"Heat 90/120/150/180 s; cool 90 s per the product data (PD-TP p4)"},{"label":"Motor FLA","value":"045V14: 6.7 · 070V14: 6.7 · 070V17: 9.2 · 090V17: 6.7 · 090V21: 11.5 · 110: 11.5 · 135: 11.7 (PD)"},{"label":"Filters","value":"Side return: 16x25x3/4 on every width. Bottom return: 14x25 on the 14-1/2 in. cabinet, 16x25 on 17-1/2 in., 20x25 on 21 in., 24x25 on 24 in. Washable filter recommended (SI-TP p42 Table 19)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (115-60-1, 104-127 V)","rows":[{"label":"Max unit amps","value":"045V14: 8.0 · 070V14: 8.0 · 070V17: 10.5 · 090V17: 8.6 · 090V21: 14.3 · 110: 14.6 · 135: 13.8. Max fuse or breaker: 15 A on the smaller sizes, 20 A on 090V21 / 110 / 135 (PD; SI-TP p16)"},{"label":"Unit ampacity","value":"045V14: 10.8 · 070V14: 10.8 · 070V17: 13.9 · 090V17: 11.3 · 090V21: 18.5 · 110: 18.8 · 135: 17.9. Product data and installation manual agree (PD-TP p4; SI-TP p16)","key":true},{"label":"Transformer / fuse","value":"40 VA. The 24 V circuit has a 3 A automotive fuse; code 24.1 means that fuse is blown (PD)"}]},{"title":"Ignition, safeties & venting","rows":[{"label":"Igniter / flame signal","value":"Silicon nitride hot-surface igniter; resistance is not published. Flame signal is not published"},{"label":"Ignition sequence","value":"15 s prepurge, then 17 s igniter warm-up, then trial. Flame must prove within 2 s. Four trials, then a 3-hour lockout. Blower-on delay 45 s on low fire and 25 s on high fire. Inducer post-purge 5 s (SI-TP p44-45)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Dual switches (LPS and HPS). Set points are not published"},{"label":"Limits","value":"Main limit is auto-reset. Rollout switches in the gas control area are manual reset. The draft safeguard switch is on the vent elbow - auto-reset, but if it stays open more than 3 minutes the furnace locks out for 3 hours. Set points are not published (SI-TP p40)"},{"label":"Venting","value":"Category I, 4 in. collar. The 135 size needs a 5 or 6 in. vent with an adapter (PD-TP p2)"}]},{"title":"Control & codes","rows":[{"label":"Board","value":"3-digit display, with the status LED visible through the sight glass. Codes are major.minor. Stores the last 7 faults, which survive a power loss. Twinning menu 'tnn' (SI-TP p32)"},{"label":"Codes (both 58TN and 58TP)","value":"10.1 polarity fault · 12.1 W on at power-up · 13.1 limit lockout · 14.1 / 14.2 / 14.3 ignition and flame-loss lockouts · 21.1 24 V on gas valve when it shouldn't be · 22.1 false flame · 23.4 / 23.5 LPS / HPS stuck closed · 24.1 fuse fault · 25.x program faults · 27.x Super Plug faults · 31.6 / 31.7 HPS open · 32.2 LPS open · 33.1 main limit open · 34.x flame loss · 41.x blower RPM · 43.1 HPS closed before LPS · 45.x control faults · 52.x / 53.x SAT / RAT open or short","key":true},{"label":"58TP only","value":"14.4 (7 LPS opens), 19.1 InteliSense communication loss, 25.3 twinned program mismatch, 33.2, 46.1 momentary power loss (SI-TP p32 Fig. 46)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Series A and Series B are different controls","body":"Series A used a model plug, setup switches and 2-digit LED codes. Series B uses the 3-digit display with a model program and Super Plug or NFC. Don't read one series' codes against the other's label (58TP0A-03SI; SI-TN p32)."},{"title":"Replacing a Series B board","body":"The new board won't run until it is programmed with the Model Program Number on the rating plate, by Super Plug or the NFC app. A wrong program gives code 25.6 (documented in the Series B 58TN0B manual, SI-TN p31-32; the 58TP0B adds code 25.3 for a twinned program mismatch)."},{"title":"Supply pressure maximum: 14 in. w.c. (SI) vs 13.6 in. w.c. (PD)","body":"The installation manual says no more than 14 in. w.c.; the product data says max 13.6. The rating plate is the authority."},{"title":"Not the 58TN","body":"The 58TP is non-communicating with a constant-torque V motor and its own rise table (110 size is 30-60 / 20-50 here vs 40-70 / 25-55 on the 58TN). Its unit ampacity figures agree between documents; the 58TN's do not. The 58TP0B label has no dissipation-system terminal or code 10.2."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Igniter resistance, flame current in µA, pressure-switch set points, limit and rollout temperatures, LP manifold pressures. No 58TP0B manual newer than 01SI REV A was found."}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59TN7A (Infinity 97 two-stage condensing)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Carrier 59TN7A Infinity 97: a TWO-STAGE (two-stage gas valve, two-speed inducer - not modulating; the modulating Infinity furnace is the 59MN7) variable-speed 4-way multipoise Category IV condensing gas furnace with a communicating Infinity control, 3-digit LCD and NFC, 115-60-1. AFUE 97.0 upflow, 95 downflow, 96.2 to 96.7 horizontal depending on size. Five sizes: 060C17-16, 080C17-16, 080C21-20, 100C21-22, 120C24-22. Not the 59TP6 / 59TP7 or 59TN6 entry - different manifold table, menus and codes.","match":["59TN7","59TN7A","59TN7A060C17","59TN7A080C17","59TN7A080C21","59TN7A080C21120","59TN7A100C21","59TN7A120C24"],"source":"Carrier 59TN7A Product Data, Cat. 59TN7A-05PD (7/26); Carrier 59TN7A Installation, Start-up, Operating, Service and Maintenance Instructions, Cat. 59TN7A-04SI (7/26); Carrier 59TP7A-03SI (7/26) and 59TP7A-01PD (11/24) for comparison only","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (59TN7A080C21--20)","value":"59 = 90%+ condensing · T = two stage · N = Infinity tier · 7 = 97% AFUE/NOx class · A = major series · 060/080/100/120 = input in MBH · C = constant-airflow variable-speed VCA ECM · 17 / 21 / 24 = cabinet width (17.5 / 21.0 / 24.5 in.) · 1 = 110V/60Hz · minor series · 16/20/22 = airflow in hundreds of CFM. Literature prints the size as 080C21--20; on the tag it reads 59TN7A080C21120 (inferred from the decode, not printed) (PD p2)"},{"label":"Two-stage, not modulating","value":"Two-stage gas valve and two-speed inducer; nomenclature position 3 is T = Two Stage. The modulating Infinity is the 59MN7 (PD p2)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Input high/low, BTUH","value":"060: 60,000/39,000 · 080: 80,000/52,000 · 100: 100,000/65,000 · 120: 120,000/78,000 (PD Table 3)"},{"label":"Output high/low","value":"060C17: 58,000/38,000 · 080C17: 77,000/50,000 · 080C21: 76,000/50,000 · 100: 97,000/63,000 · 120: 116,000/75,000 (PD Table 3)"},{"label":"Burners / orifice / valve","value":"3/4/4/5/6 burners. Factory orifice #44 on every size. Redundant White-Rodgers gas valve, 1/2 in. NPT (PD Table 3)"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas","value":"From Table 28, by altitude, heating value and specific gravity. Basis 20,000 BTUH high / 13,000 BTUH low per burner, derated 2% per 1,000 ft. Allowed window: high fire 3.2-3.8 in. w.c., low fire 1.3-1.7 in. w.c.; change orifices if the setting falls outside it. Worked example (0-2000 ft, 1050 BTU/cu ft, SG 0.62): #44 orifice, 3.4 in. high / 1.4 in. low (SI p59-62)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"Not published - use the AGAGC9NPS01E conversion kit instructions (SI p59; PD p14)"},{"label":"Supply pressure, natural gas","value":"Min 4.5 in. w.c., max 13.6 in. w.c. (PD Table 3; SI p59). Conflict: the SI start-up section says 'not exceed 14-in. w.c. (0.5 psig)' (SI p56) - see flag"},{"label":"Clocking","value":"Lock low fire with the Htt menu set to 2St and a jumper R-W/W1. Lock high fire with a jumper R-W/W1-W2. Use Table 27 (SI p60-61)"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride hot-surface igniter, 40-70 Ω cold (PD Table 3; SI p66)","key":true},{"label":"High altitude","value":"SI: reduce input 2% per 1,000 ft above 2,000 ft in the USA and 5% for 2,000-4,500 ft in Canada; Table 28 already includes both (SI p59). Conflict: the PD spec footnote says 4% per 1,000 ft (PD p5) - see flag"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"High fire 40-70 °F on all sizes. Low fire 25-55 °F on 060/080 and 30-60 °F on 100/120 (PD Table 3). Take the rise with the blower door on; aim for the mid-point of the range or slightly above (SI p62)","key":true},{"label":"Airflow control","value":"The furnace 'is capable of automatically providing proper airflow' (SI p62). The tech still picks a heating profile in the Ht menu: Ct1, Ct2, EF1 or EF2 (Comfort/Efficiency); a higher setting lowers the rise. The default profile is not confirmed (SI Table 24 p53, Fig. 60 p54)"},{"label":"Heating CFM by profile, low/high fire","value":"060: 710/820 to 958/1100 · 120: 1185/1682 to 1495/2110 (SI Tables 18-22 p50-52)"},{"label":"Rated ESP","value":"Heating 0.12/0.15/0.15/0.2/0.2 in. w.c. (060/080C17/080C21/100/120), cooling 0.5 in. The airflow tables run to 1.0 in. (PD Table 3; SI Tables 18-22)"},{"label":"Blower","value":"VCA ECM, 300-1300 RPM. HP 3/4, 3/4, 1, 1, 1 and FLA 8.8, 9.2, 11.5, 11.5, 11.0 (060/080C17/080C21/100/120) (PD Table 3)"},{"label":"Blower off-delay","value":"Heat 90/120/150/180 s, default 120 (menu HoD); cool 5/30/60/90 s, default 90 (menu Cod) (PD Table 3; SI Fig. 60)"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Side return: 16x25x3/4 on every cabinet. Bottom return: 14x25, 16x25, 20x25 or 24x25 (all x3/4) for the 14-3/16, 17-1/2, 21 and 24-1/2 in. cabinets (SI Table 9 p22)"},{"label":"Return-air temperature","value":"60 °F minimum continuous (55 °F intermittent), 80 °F maximum (PD p13)"}]},{"title":"Electrical (060 / 080C17 / 080C21 / 100 / 120)","rows":[{"label":"Max unit amps / ampacity / wire / max fuse","value":"Max unit amps 10.1 / 10.0 / 13.1 / 13.2 / 11.9 · ampacity 13.5 / 13.4 / 17.3 / 17.4 / 15.7 · wire 14 / 14 / 12 / 12 / 12 AWG · max fuse 15 / 15 / 20 / 20 / 20 A · transformer 40 VA (PD Table 3; SI Table 11 p26)","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties & controls","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Two (LPS on the collector box, HPS on the housing). The break point is printed on each switch label, ±0.05 in.; make is 0.10 in. above max break. No model-specific set point is published; 0.68 in. is only a worked example (SI p63)"},{"label":"Limit / rollout","value":"The main limit is checked by blocking the return air (SI p62-63). Two manual-reset rollout switches (SI p56, p66). Trip temperatures are not published - see the parts label"},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Not published in the 59TN7A PD or SI"},{"label":"Status codes","value":"The major code is the first two digits and the minor code is the third; the LED flashes the major code as short flashes, then long flashes (SI Fig. 61 p55). 10.1 polarity (rapid flash) · 10.2 refrigerant leak detected, blower runs · 13.1 limit lockout (3 h) · 14.1 ignition lockout · 15.1/15.2 blower rpm lockouts · 17.1 BTM comm loss · 22.1 false flame · 23.4/23.5 LPS/HPS stuck closed · 25.x/27.x program or Super Plug faults · 31.6/31.7 HPS · 32.2 open LPS · 33.1 main limit open · 34.x flame loss · 41.x blower rpm · 45.x control faults · 51/52/53 OAT/SAT/RAT sensors · otA/bTL firmware","key":true},{"label":"Flame sensor / heat exchanger","value":"Clean the flame sensor with 0000 steel wool only (SI p67). Soot means replace both heat exchangers (SI p68)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"A replacement control board must be programmed","body":"Program it with the model program number on the rating plate, by NFC app or Super Plug, or the furnace will not run. A wrong program means wrong airflow and overheating (SI p53-54)."},{"title":"Code 10.2 means an R-454B coil sensor is paired","body":"Wire it per the indoor coil's A2L diagram (SI p30). The blower is supposed to run during 10.2."},{"title":"PD and SI conflict: supply-pressure max and altitude derate","body":"Supply-pressure max is 13.6 in. w.c. (PD Table 3; SI p59) vs 14 in. w.c. (SI p56). Altitude derate is 2% per 1,000 ft (SI p59) vs 4% per 1,000 ft (PD p5). Use the SI and Table 28."},{"title":"Not the 59TP6 / 59TP7 entry","body":"That entry was built from the 59TP6C manual. Wrong for the 59TN7A: the manifold table is Table 28, not Table 26 (Table 26 here is the altitude derate table); blower off-delay is set in the HoD menu, not DIP SW-7/SW-8; there are no DIP switches, so 'setup switch SW1-3' does not exist - rise is corrected with the Ht profile; codes are 3-digit major.minor, not two-digit amber; the LCD and NFC are standard. Same: 20k/13k per burner basis, 2% per 1,000 ft, igniter 40-70 Ω, soot means replace both heat exchangers, rapid flash means polarity."},{"title":"Not the current 59TP7A either","body":"The 59TP7A has a V motor (25-speed constant torque, non-communicating) with numbered speeds and six sizes including 100V21-20; rated CFM differs (100 high heat is 1665 on the 59TN7A versus 1700/1730 on the 59TP7A); its electrical table also lists Low Amp Kit values. Only the 59TN7A has 10.2, 15.2, 17.1, 41.3, 51.x and otA/bTL; only the 59TP7A has 19.1 InteliSense, 25.3 twinning, 33.2 and 46.1. Rise ranges, AFUE by orientation, manifold window and supply pressure are the same."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Flame-signal µA, limit and rollout trip temperatures, pressure-switch set points by size, LP manifold pressures, the default heating profile. No separate service manual or troubleshooting guide was found."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59SC6A (Comfort 96 single-stage condensing)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Carrier Comfort 96 4-way multipoise condensing gas furnace, single-stage gas valve, single-speed inducer, Multi 18-speed constant-torque (MCT) ECM blower ('M'), non-communicating, 3-digit display with Major.Minor codes. Up to 97.0% AFUE. 11 sizes, 26k-140k Btuh. Not the 59SC2 / 59SC5 entry - its amber-LED flash codes, flame-current and 0.68 in. pressure-switch figures do not carry over. The 26k size uses its own low-pressure manifold table.","match":["59SC6","59SC6A","59SC6A026M14","59SC6A040M14","59SC6A040M17","59SC6A060M14","59SC6A060M17","59SC6A080M17","59SC6A080M21","59SC6A100M21","59SC6A120M24","59SC6A140M24"],"source":"Carrier 59SC6A Product Data, Cat. 59SC6A-05PD (7/26); Carrier 59SC6A Installation, Start-up, Operating and Service and Maintenance Instructions, Cat. 59SC6A-03SI (7/26)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (59SC6A060M17--16)","value":"59 = 90%+ condensing · S = single stage · C = Comfort (P = Performance) · 6 = 96% · A = major series · 026-140 = input · M = Multi 18-speed MCT ECM (V = variable-speed VCT) · 14 / 17 / 21 / 24 = width (14.2 / 17.5 / 21.0 / 24.5 in.) · 1 = 115V/60Hz · minor series · 10-22 = airflow (1000 CFM through 2200 CFM) (A p3)"}]},{"title":"By size (A p4-5)","rows":[{"label":"Input / output, kBtuh","value":"026M14: 26/25 · 040M14: 40/39 · 040M17: 40/39 · 060M14: 60/56 · 060M17: 60/58 · 080M17: 80/78 · 080M21: 80/78 · 100M21 (-20/-22): 100/97 · 120M24: 120/116 · 140M24: 140/135"},{"label":"Temperature rise, °F","value":"026M14: 25-55 · 040M14: 40-70 · 040M17: 40-70 · 060M14: 35-65 · 060M17: 40-70 · 080M17: 40-70 · 080M21: 40-70 · 100M21: 40-70 · 120M24: 40-70 · 140M24: 45-75. Read it with the blower door on; aim for the midpoint of the range or slightly above (B p66)","key":true},{"label":"AFUE, upflow-horizontal / downflow","value":"026M14: 96.0/95.0 · 040M14: 96.0/95.0 · 040M17: 96.7/95.0 · 060M14: 95.0/95.0 · 060M17: 97.0/95.0 · 080M17: 97.0/95.0 · 080M21: 97.0/95.0 · 100M21: 96.3/95.0 · 120M24: 96.1/95.0 · 140M24: 95.0/95.0"},{"label":"Unit ampacity / max fuse","value":"026M14: 7.5/15 · 040M14: 9.7/15 · 040M17: 10.2/15 · 060M14: 9.8/15 · 060M17: 13.6/15 · 080M17: 13.4/15 · 080M21: 17.3/20 · 100M21: 16.7 or 16.5/20 (-20/-22) · 120M24: 17.4/20 · 140M24: 16.7/20","key":true},{"label":"Blower HP / burners","value":"026M14: 1/3 HP, 2 · 040M14: 1/2, 2 · 040M17: 1/2, 3 · 060M14: 1/2, 3 · 060M17: 3/4, 4 · 080M17: 3/4, 4 · 080M21: 1, 4 · 100M21: 1, 5 · 120M24: 1, 6 · 140M24: 1, 7"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Supply pressure, natural gas","value":"Min 4.5 / max 13.6 in. w.c., checked with the burners firing (A p4; B p62). Conflict: the start-up General section says 'not exceed 14-in. w.c. (0.5 psig)' (B p58)"},{"label":"Valve / orifice","value":"Redundant White-Rodgers single-stage valve, factory No. 44 orifice, 1/2 in. NPT (A p4)"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas, 40k and up","value":"From Table 25, by altitude, heat value and specific gravity. Stay within 2.8-3.8 in. w.c.; if the required pressure falls outside that range, change the orifices. At 0-2000 ft, 1050 Btu, 0.62 SG: No. 44 at 3.4 in. w.c. Table values are as-measured at altitude, so do not derate them again (B p62-64)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, 26k (026M14)","value":"Its own Table 26, which runs 1.2-1.8 in. w.c. Do not exceed 1.8 in. w.c. The 26k is identified by a green label on its gas valve and is not considered direct-vent (B p61, p63, p65; A p1)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"Not published - LP settings come from the LP conversion kit instructions (B p62)"},{"label":"Input tolerance","value":"Within ±2% of the rating plate (B p62)"},{"label":"High altitude","value":"US derate 2% per 1000 ft above 2000 ft (Table 23: 2001-3000 ft = 0.95 ... 9001-10,000 ft = 0.81). Canada: 5% for 2000-4500 ft (B p62). Conflict: the Product Data spec footnotes say 'reduce ratings 4 percent for each 1000 ft' (A p4-5)"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride HSI, 40-70 Ω cold, measured at room temperature (B p70-71)","key":true},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Not published. See the rating plate / troubleshooting guide"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Rated ESP","value":"Heating 0.10-0.20 in. w.c. by size, cooling 0.50. Air tables run to 1.0 in. w.c. (A p4-6)"},{"label":"Filter (field-supplied, washable 3/4 in.)","value":"14-3/16 in. cabinet: side 16x25, bottom 14x25 · 17-1/2 in.: side 16x25, bottom 16x25 · 21 in.: side 16x25, bottom 20x25 · 24-1/2 in.: side 16x25, bottom 24x25. Airflow over 1800 CFM needs at least a 20x25 filter (B p21, p55)"},{"label":"Blower off-delay","value":"Heat 90/120/150/180 s (120 factory) (A p4; B p66). Cooling off-delay 90 (factory), 5 or 30 s (A p4)"}]},{"title":"Safeties & controls","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Two switches, LPS on the collector box and HPS on the inducer housing. Nominal break is on the switch label, with tolerance ±0.05 in. w.c. Max make is 0.10 in. w.c. above the max break (B p60 wiring legend; D p65)"},{"label":"Limit / rollout","value":"Main limit is auto-reset (behind the gas valve). Two flame-rollout switches, manual reset, SPST N.C. Trip temperatures are not published (B p60; A p3)"},{"label":"Ignition lockout","value":"After 4 failed trials, with auto-reset after 3 hours (B p60)"},{"label":"Board","value":"3-digit display with Major.Minor codes (for example 33.1 and 34.1). Fault memory: last 7 faults, kept for 72 h of powered operation; clear with CLr. Component test from menu 'Ct' (B p56-59, p67)","key":true},{"label":"Electrical","value":"115-60-1, 104-127 V, 40 VA transformer, 3 A blade fuse (code 24.1 = blown fuse) (A p4)"},{"label":"Pressure-switch check","value":"Pulling the inducer leads should produce a pressure-switch code. 59SC6A-03SI names 31.1, which is not on the service label; the label shows 32.1 = open LPS and 31.2 = open HPS (B p66, p58)"},{"label":"Short-vent restrictor","value":"Short vents need an inducer outlet restrictor or expect flame-sense lockouts (0-2000 ft; TEVL = total equivalent vent length). The 40k needs it at under 10 ft TEVL in any orientation. The 26k and 60k need it at under 5 ft TEVL in downflow or horizontal. See Table 14 for the 120k and 140k (B p41, p48)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Not the 59SC2 / 59SC5 entry","body":"That entry was built from Form 59SC2D-03SI. Its amber LED with 2-digit flash codes, the '4.0-6.0 µA, lockout below 0.5 µA' flame current, the 0.68 in. w.c. pressure-switch break and the LP supply max 13.8 in. w.c. are NOT published for the 59SC6A - do not carry them over. Still the same: igniter 40-70 Ω cold, NG inlet 4.5-13.6 in. w.c. checked while firing, No. 44 orifice with 3.4 in. w.c. at 0-2000 ft / 1050 Btu / 0.62 SG, US derate 2% per 1000 ft, manual-reset rollout."},{"title":"A replacement board must be programmed with the Model Program Number","body":"Use the Carrier service app over NFC or the Super Plug, with the number on the rating plate. If this is wrong, you get codes 25.x or 27.x and no heat (B p57-58)."},{"title":"The 26k has its own manifold table","body":"Table 26, 1.2-1.8 in. w.c., never above 1.8 in. w.c. Green label on the gas valve. Do not set a 26k from the 40k-and-up table (B p61, p63, p65)."},{"title":"PD and SI conflict: supply-pressure max and altitude derate","body":"Supply max 13.6 in. w.c. (A p4; B p62) vs 14 in. w.c. (B p58). Derate 2% per 1000 ft (SI) vs 4% (PD footnote). The 59SC6A-03SI worked example gives 3.4 in. w.c. as 847 Pa."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Flame-signal µA, limit and rollout trip temperatures, nominal pressure-switch set points per size, LP manifold pressures, combustion CO/CO2 targets."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Carrier","model":"59SP6B (Performance 96 single-stage condensing)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Carrier Performance 96 4-way multipoise condensing gas furnace, single-stage, Variable 25-speed constant-torque (VCT) ECM blower ('V'), non-communicating, InteliSense capable with an ecobee for Carrier thermostat, 3-digit display with Major.Minor codes. Up to 97% AFUE. 8 sizes, 40k-120k Btuh, with no 26k or 140k size. The current series B replaced the 2020-era 59SP6A, which has a different control - see flag. Not the 59SC2 / 59SC5 entry.","match":["59SP6","59SP6B","59SP6A","59SP6B040V14","59SP6B040V17","59SP6B060V14","59SP6B060V17","59SP6B080V17","59SP6B080V21","59SP6B100V21","59SP6B120V24"],"source":"Carrier 59SP6B Product Data, Cat. 59SP6B-04PD (7/26); Carrier 59SP6B Installation, Start-up, Operating, Service and Maintenance Instructions, Cat. 59SP6B-03SI (7/26); Carrier 59SP6A Product Data (printed Cat. '59SPSA-01', 07/20) and 59SP6A Installation Instructions, Cat. 59SP6A-01SI REV D (06/23), for the Series A comparison only","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (59SP6B080V17--16)","value":"59 = 90%+ condensing · S = single stage · P = Performance (C = Comfort) · 6 = 96% · B = major series (A = the older 59SP6A) · 040-120 = input · V = variable-speed VCT (M = Multi 18-speed MCT) · 14 / 17 / 21 / 24 = width (14.2 / 17.5 / 21.0 / 24.5 in.) · 1 = 115V/60Hz · minor series · 10-22 = airflow (1000 CFM through 2200 CFM) (C p3)"},{"label":"59SP6A vs 59SP6B","value":"59SP6A (Product Data 2020) is the older control, with a 2-digit LED and setup DIP switches. 59SP6B uses the 3-digit display. Do not use 59SP6B codes on a 59SP6A (E; F service/troubleshooting section)","key":true}]},{"title":"By size (C p4)","rows":[{"label":"Input / output, kBtuh","value":"040V14: 40/39 · 040V17: 40/39 · 060V14: 60/58 · 060V17: 60/58 · 080V17: 80/78 · 080V21: 80/78 · 100V21: 100/97 · 120V24: 120/116"},{"label":"Temperature rise, °F","value":"040V14: 40-70 · 040V17: 40-70 · 060V14: 45-70 · 060V17: 40-70 · 080V17: 40-70 · 080V21: 40-70 · 100V21: 40-70 · 120V24: 40-70. Read it with the blower door on; aim for the midpoint of the range or slightly above","key":true},{"label":"AFUE, upflow / downflow-horizontal","value":"040V14: 96/95 · 040V17: 96.7/95 · 060V14: 95/95 · 060V17: 97/95 · 080V17: 97/95 · 080V21: 97/95 · 100V21: 96.3/95 · 120V24: 96.1/95"},{"label":"Unit ampacity / max fuse","value":"040V14: 9.7/15 · 040V17: 10.2/15 · 060V14: 9.8/15 · 060V17: 13.6/15 · 080V17: 13.4/15 · 080V21: 17.3/20 · 100V21: 17.4/20 (15.0/15 with Low Amp Kit KGAPC0101ECM) · 120V24: 16.7/20","key":true},{"label":"Blower HP / burners","value":"040V14: 1/2 HP, 2 · 040V17: 1/2, 2 · 060V14: 1/2, 3 · 060V17: 3/4, 3 · 080V17: 3/4, 4 · 080V21: 1, 4 · 100V21: 1, 5 · 120V24: 1, 6"}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Supply pressure, natural gas","value":"Min 4.5 / max 13.6 in. w.c., checked with the burners firing (C p4; D p61). Conflict: the start-up General section says 'not exceed 14-in. w.c. (0.5 psig)' (D p57)"},{"label":"Valve / orifice","value":"Redundant White-Rodgers single-stage valve, factory No. 44 orifice, 1/2 in. NPT (C p4)"},{"label":"Manifold pressure, natural gas","value":"From Table 26, by altitude, heat value and specific gravity. At 0-2000 ft, 1050 Btu, 0.62 SG: No. 44 at 3.4 in. w.c. Table values are as-measured at altitude, so do not derate them again (D p61, p63)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold pressure, LP","value":"Not published - LP settings come from the LP conversion kit instructions (D p61)"},{"label":"High altitude","value":"US derate 2% per 1000 ft above 2000 ft (Table 24: 2001-3000 ft = 0.95 ... 9001-10,000 ft = 0.81). Canada: 5% for 2000-4500 ft (D p61). Conflict: the Product Data spec footnotes say 'reduce ratings 4 percent for each 1000 ft' (C p4)"},{"label":"Igniter","value":"Silicon nitride HSI, 40-70 Ω cold, measured at room temperature (D p68-69)","key":true},{"label":"Flame signal","value":"Not published. See the rating plate / troubleshooting guide"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Rated ESP","value":"Heating 0.10-0.20 in. w.c. by size, cooling 0.50. Air tables run to 1.0 in. w.c. (C p4-5)"},{"label":"Filter (field-supplied, washable 3/4 in.)","value":"14-3/16 in. cabinet: side 16x25, bottom 14x25 · 17-1/2 in.: side 16x25, bottom 16x25 · 21 in.: side 16x25, bottom 20x25 · 24-1/2 in.: side 16x25, bottom 24x25. Airflow over 1800 CFM needs at least a 20x25 filter (D p22, p53)"},{"label":"Blower off-delay","value":"Heat 90/120/150/180 s (120 factory)"}]},{"title":"Safeties & controls","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"Two switches, LPS on the collector box (COLLECTOR BOX-LPS) and HPS on the inducer housing (HOUSING-HPS). Nominal break is on the switch label, with tolerance ±0.05 in. w.c. Max make is 0.10 in. w.c. above the max break. The 0.68 in. w.c. in the SI is only a worked example (D p65)"},{"label":"Limit / rollout","value":"Main limit is auto-reset. Two flame-rollout switches, manual reset. Trip temperatures are not published"},{"label":"Board","value":"3-digit display with Major.Minor codes. Fault memory: last 7 faults, kept for 72 h of powered operation; clear with CLr. Component test from menu 'Ct' (D p65)","key":true},{"label":"Extra codes on the 59SP6B","value":"15.1 no blower RPM · 19.1 InteliSense communication loss · 41.1 / 41.2 blower RPM faults · 52.1 / 52.2 SAT sensor open / short · 53.1 / 53.2 RAT sensor open / short (D p57)"},{"label":"Thermostat / staging","value":"Terminals are Y1 and Y/Y2 plus DHUM. Set Ctt = 2St when a 2-stage thermostat controls staging. The RAT sensor is on the board and the SAT sensor is installed in the field. With the display option 't°' on, the board shows the temperature rise (D p29-30; C p4)"},{"label":"Electrical","value":"115-60-1, 104-127 V, 40 VA transformer, 3 A blade fuse (code 24.1 = blown fuse) (D p65)"},{"label":"Pressure-switch check","value":"Pulling the inducer leads should produce a pressure-switch code. 59SP6B-03SI names 32.2, which is not on the service label; the label shows 32.1 = open LPS and 31.2 = open HPS (D p64, p57)"},{"label":"Short-vent restrictor","value":"Short vents need an inducer outlet restrictor or expect flame-sense lockouts (0-2000 ft; TEVL = total equivalent vent length). The 40k needs it at 10 ft TEVL or less. The 60k needs it at 5 ft or less in downflow (D p42, p48)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Check which series you have: 59SP6A vs 59SP6B","body":"59SP6A (Product Data 2020) is the older control, with a 2-digit LED and setup DIP switches. 59SP6B uses the 3-digit display. Do not use 59SP6B codes on a 59SP6A. A full 59SP6A figure set was not confirmed."},{"title":"A replacement board must be programmed with the Model Program Number","body":"Use the Carrier service app over NFC or the Super Plug, with the number on the rating plate. If this is wrong, you get codes 25.x or 27.x and no heat (D p55)."},{"title":"Not the 59SC2 / 59SC5 entry","body":"That entry's amber LED with 2-digit flash codes, the '4.0-6.0 µA, lockout below 0.5 µA' flame current, the 0.68 in. w.c. pressure-switch break and the LP supply max 13.8 in. w.c. are NOT published for the 59SP6B - do not carry them over. Still the same: igniter 40-70 Ω cold, NG inlet 4.5-13.6 in. w.c. checked while firing, No. 44 orifice with 3.4 in. w.c. at 0-2000 ft / 1050 Btu / 0.62 SG, US derate 2% per 1000 ft, manual-reset rollout."},{"title":"PD and SI conflict: supply-pressure max and altitude derate","body":"Supply max 13.6 in. w.c. (C p4; D p61) vs 14 in. w.c. (D p57). Derate 2% per 1000 ft (SI) vs 4% (PD footnote). Document quirk: the 59SP6B-03SI example gives 3.4 in. w.c. as '874 Pa'; 59SC6A-03SI gives 847 Pa (D p61; B p62)."},{"title":"Not published","body":"Flame-signal µA, limit and rollout trip temperatures, nominal pressure-switch set points per size, LP manifold pressures, combustion CO/CO2 targets. Carrier's consumer page claims a 59SP6 range of 26k-140k, but the product data shows 40k-120k."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML13KC1 (Merit single-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Merit ML13KC1 single-stage scroll split AC condenser (partial unit), R-454B (A2L), 13.0-13.9 SEER2 nominal, North region. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (1.5-5 ton), 208/230-1. Indoor TXV and indoor RDS required. No outdoor board and no flash codes. The 3-phase version (-233/-463/-573, 036-060) is in separate EHB 211154 and is not covered here. Size tables below come from the ML13KC1's own EHB 211057 - the UI reprints the ML14KC1 table (see flags).","match":["ML13KC1","ML13KC1-018-230","ML13KC1-024-230","ML13KC1-030-230","ML13KC1-036-230","ML13KC1-042-230","ML13KC1-048-230","ML13KC1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) ML13KC1 1-ph, Form 211057 (Aug 2024); Lennox Unit Information ML13KC1, Corp. 100118 (Mar 18 2026), charging label 581280-02 on p39; Lennox Installation Instructions ML13KC1, 508491-01 (03/2026); 3-phase EHB Form 211154 (identity only)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML13KC1-036-230A01)","value":"ML = Merit · 13 = nominal SEER2 (13.0-13.9) · K = R-454B · C = air conditioner · 1 = single-stage · '-' = regional standard (North region) · 018-060 = capacity in kBtuh (1.5-5 ton) · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level (EHB 211057 p1)"},{"label":"Serial number","value":"First 2 digits = plant (58 = Marshalltown IA, 19 = Saltillo MX), next 2 = year, then a month letter (A = Jan), then the unit number (UI 100118 p4)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B","value":"018: 4 lb 0 oz · 024: 4 lb 7 oz · 030: 4 lb 14 oz · 036: 5 lb 10 oz · 042: 6 lb 2 oz · 048: 7 lb 10 oz · 060: 8 lb 8 oz (EHB 211057 p7-8). UI 100118 p6-7 prints different charges (036: 6 lb 13 oz) - that is the ML14KC1 table, see flag. The rating plate governs","key":true},{"label":"Line length the charge covers - CONFLICT","value":"EHB 211057 p7 note 1: 15 ft. Charging label 581280-02 (UI 100118 p39): 30 ft - with 3/8 in. liquid line add 3 oz per 5 ft over 30 ft, subtract below 30 ft. The UI weigh-in figure uses 0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in. (0.40 for 5/16 in., 1.00 for 1/2 in.) with a 15-ft example (UI p36 Fig 23). Read the nameplate before adjusting","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in when outdoor is 64 °F or below. At 65 °F and above, use subcooling or approach from the unit charging label. Charge liquid only; for subcooling use the SATURATED LIQUID temperature. Block the outdoor coil if needed to hold 325-375 psig liquid while checking (UI p35-37)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target °F at 65 / 75 / 85 / 95 / 105 / 115 °F outdoor (label 581280-02)","value":"018: 8 / 3 / 4 / 7 / 7 / 9 · 024: 6 / 3 / 5 / 6 / 8 / 10 · 030: 11 / 8 / 6 / 6 / 8 / 9 · 036: 13 / 11 / 11 / 12 / 12 / 13 · 042: 14 / 11 / 11 / 13 / 16 / 17 · 048: 14 / 11 / 12 / 12 / 13 / 13 · 060: 11 / 11 / 11 / 12 / 12 / 12 (UI 100118 p39)","key":true},{"label":"Approach at 95 °F","value":"018: 7 · 024: 9 · 030: 6 · 036: 4 · 042: 6 · 048: 6 · 060: 8 °F (label 581280-02)"},{"label":"Typical liquid / suction psig at 95 °F","value":"018: 341 / 138 · 024: 346 / 136 · 030: 335 / 135 · 036: 348 / 134 · 042: 366 / 135 · 048: 361 / 138 · 060: 372 / 131 (label 581280-02)"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor TXV only. Kits 26Z70 (1.5-3 ton), 26Z71 (3.5-4 ton), 26Z72 (5 ton) (EHB 211057 p11; II p6). The supplied liquid-line drier goes outdoors - leaving it out voids the warranty (II p8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (EHB 211057 p7-8)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 11.1 / 15 / 8.3 / 45 / 0.65 · 024: 13.5 / 20 / 10.2 / 60.2 / 0.65 · 030: 16.6 / 25 / 12.5 / 67.8 / 1.0 · 036: 17.8 / 30 / 13.4 / 82.5 / 1.0 · 042: 21.2 / 35 / 14.9 / 109 / 2.6 · 048: 24.3 / 40 / 18.0 / 126 / 1.7 · 060: 31.3 / 50 / 23.7 / 157 / 1.7","key":true},{"label":"Supply voltage / capacitor","value":"+10% / -5% (EHB p7). Contactor with dual run capacitor C12; the MFD rating is not published - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Liquid line","value":"3/8 in. on all sizes"},{"label":"Suction line - CONFLICT","value":"EHB 211057 says 036 and 042 are 3/4 in. II 508491-01 Table 1 says 036 / 042 / 048 are 7/8 in. Measure the unit's own service-valve connection"},{"label":"Length / lift / oil","value":"Over 50 ft, refer to Corp. 9351-L9 (Refrigerant Piping Design and Fabrication Guidelines); maximum lift not published (II p7). The compressor oil covers up to 50 ft; add 1 oz of POE per 5 lb of charge over 20 lb (UI 100118 p16)"}]},{"title":"Controls, switches & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Control board","value":"None. Contactor with dual run capacitor (C12), no outdoor board, no flash codes. The only LED is on the indoor RDS board (UI 100118 p31)"},{"label":"High-pressure switch S4 (liquid line)","value":"Opens at 590 ±10 psig, resets at 418 ±5 psig, auto reset (UI 100118 p29)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch S87","value":"Fitted (EHB p3; wiring UI p31) but no set point is published for the ML13KC1 - see the rating plate or the switch itself"},{"label":"Compressor internal vacuum protector","value":"Unloads below 20 psig (hissing) and resets above 40 psig. Do not replace the compressor for this (UI 100118 p29)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-fitted on 048 and 060, optional on 018-042 (EHB p4). The S40 thermostat closes below 50 °F and opens at 70 °F liquid-line temperature (UI p29)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling down to 45 °F outdoor as shipped, 30 °F with low-ambient kit 34M72. Maximum altitude 10,000 ft (EHB p5, p7; II p6)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"A Lennox RDS Blower Control Board (Cat 27A02) and sensor are required on the indoor unit. At power-up it runs a 5-minute purge; the Test button simulates a leak (flashing blue LED, blower on, compressor off). A second sensor is required when line-set joints are not sleeved, unless one of Options 1-3 applies. Verify the RDS (purge, then Test) before the system runs (II 508491-01 p7, p17, p20)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft²)","value":"10 lb = 149.9 · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8. Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.02 at 2,620 ft, 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft (the printed table is non-monotonic: 1.05 at 3,280 ft, 1.04 at 3,940 ft) (UI p5; II p5)"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm · 10 lb = 271 · 15 lb = 406 · 20 lb = 541 · 30 lb = 812 cfm (UI p5)"},{"label":"Leak check / brazing","value":"A trace charge is at most 2 oz. Nitrogen test at 160 psig (II p14; UI p23). Braze with nitrogen flowing at 1-2 psig, never purge with oxygen. Flush old mineral-oil line sets; a 1/4 in. RFC liquid line must be replaced"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"EHB 211057 p7 note 1 says the factory charge covers 15 ft; charging label 581280-02 (UI 100118 p39) says 30 ft with 3 oz per 5 ft on 3/8 in. liquid line. Read the nameplate before adding or removing refrigerant."},{"title":"UI 100118 p6-7 reprints the ML14KC1 spec table","body":"Its charges do not match EHB 211057 (036: 6 lb 13 oz in the UI vs 5 lb 10 oz in the EHB). The size tables above come from the ML13KC1's own EHB 211057. The UI also prints an EL22KCV model-ID chart on p4/p5. The rating plate governs charge and electrical data."},{"title":"Suction line size: the documents disagree","body":"EHB 211057: 036 and 042 = 3/4 in. II 508491-01 Table 1: 036 / 042 / 048 = 7/8 in. Measure the service valve before you buy a line set."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Low-pressure switch set point, capacitor MFD rating, maximum line length and lift, and which compressor brand goes with which revision."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML14KC1 (Merit single-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Merit ML14KC1 single-stage scroll split AC condenser (partial unit), R-454B (A2L), 14.0-14.9 SEER2 nominal. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 041 / 042 / 047 / 048 / 059 / 060 (041 = 3.5 ton, 047 = 4 ton, 059 = 5 ton), 208/230-1. Indoor TXV and indoor RDS required. No outdoor board and no flash codes. A01 and A02 revisions use different compressors, so the winding-resistance tables are separate.","match":["ML14KC1","ML14KC1-018-230","ML14KC1-024-230","ML14KC1-030-230","ML14KC1-036-230","ML14KC1-041-230","ML14KC1-042-230","ML14KC1-047-230","ML14KC1-048-230","ML14KC1-059-230","ML14KC1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) ML14KC1, Form 211058 (Sep 2024); Lennox Unit Information ML14KC1, Corp. 100119 (Mar 18 2026), charging label 581334-02 on p39; Lennox Installation Instructions ML14KC1, 508603-01","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML14KC1-048-230A01)","value":"ML = Merit · 14 = nominal SEER2 (14.0-14.9) · K = R-454B · C = air conditioner · 1 = single-stage · 018-060 = capacity in kBtuh (041 = 3.5 ton, 047 = 4 ton, 059 = 5 ton) · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level (EHB 211058 p1). Serial: first 2 digits = plant (58 = Marshalltown IA, 19 = Saltillo MX), next 2 = year, then a month letter (UI 100118 p4)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 041 / 042 / 047 / 048 / 059 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B","value":"018: 4 lb 14 oz · 024: 4 lb 14 oz · 030: 5 lb 10 oz · 036: 6 lb 13 oz · 041: 7 lb 7 oz · 042: 7 lb 2 oz · 047: 7 lb 13 oz · 048: 8 lb 14 oz · 059: 9 lb 8 oz · 060: 8 lb 14 oz (EHB 211058 p7-8). The rating plate governs","key":true},{"label":"Line length the charge covers - CONFLICT","value":"EHB p7 note 1: 15 ft. Charging label 581334-02 (UI 100119 p39): 30 ft - with 3/8 in. liquid line add 3 oz per 5 ft over 30 ft, subtract below. UI weigh-in rate 0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in. (0.40 for 5/16 in., 1.00 for 1/2 in.). Read the nameplate before adjusting","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in when outdoor is 64 °F or below. At 65 °F and above, use subcooling or approach from the unit charging label. Charge liquid only; for subcooling use the SATURATED LIQUID temperature. Block the outdoor coil if needed to hold 325-375 psig liquid while checking (UI p35-37)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target °F at 65 / 75 / 85 / 95 / 105 / 115 °F outdoor (label 581334-02)","value":"018: 9 / 6 / 7 / 6 / 7 / 7 · 024: 9 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 8 / 8 · 030: 10 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 6 · 036: 12 / 10 / 10 / 9 / 8 / 7 · 041: 11 / 9 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 7 · 042: 10 / 7 / 6 / 7 / 7 / 6 · 047: 11 / 10 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 8 · 048: 12 / 10 / 9 / 8 / 8 / 8 · 059: 11 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 9 / 8 · 060: 9 / 7 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 8 (UI 100119 p39)","key":true},{"label":"Typical liquid / suction psig at 95 °F","value":"018: 326 / 138 · 024: 331 / 134 · 030: 326 / 131 · 036: 336 / 133 · 041: 330 / 136 · 042: 330 / 135 · 047: 338 / 136 · 048: 341 / 130 · 059: 330 / 128 · 060: 332 / 126 (label 581334-02)"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor TXV only. Kits 26Z70 (1.5-3 ton), 26Z71 (3.5-4 ton), 26Z72 (5 ton). The supplied liquid-line drier goes outdoors - leaving it out voids the warranty"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA (EHB 211058 p7-8)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 11.2 / 15 / 8.3 / 45 · 024: 13.6 / 20 / 10.3 / 60.2 · 030: 16.6 / 25 / 12.7 / 75.6 · 036: 21.8 / 30 / 16.7 / 93.5 · 041: 21 / 30 / 14.7 / 109 · 042: 23.2 / 35 / 17.3 / 123 · 047: 25.2 / 40 / 18.1 / 126 · 048: 29.7 / 45 / 22.4 / 126 · 059: 31.8 / 55 / 23.3 / 143 · 060: 31.2 / 50 / 23.7 / 157. UI 100119 p6-7 differs slightly: it omits 059 and lists MCA 23 (042) and 31 (060) - EHB values shown","key":true},{"label":"Fan FLA / capacitor","value":"Not in the documents used for this entry (fan LRA for 041 / 047 / 059 is unconfirmed) - see the rating plate. Supply voltage +10% / -5%"},{"label":"Compressor winding resistance Ω, A01 revision (C-S / C-R)","value":"018 YPH014KAA: 1.68 / 1.21 · 024 YPH020KAA: 1.41 / 1.59 · 030 YPH025KAA: 1.06 / 1.63 · 036 YPH031KAA: 0.87 / 1.3 · 041 YPH034KAA: 0.78 / 1.69 · 042 YPH036KAA: 0.75 / 1.75 · 047 YBH039KAA: 0.6 / 0.71 · 048 YBH042KAA: 0.58 / 0.71 · 059 YBH049KAA: 0.49 / 0.79 · 060 YBH051KAA: 0.47 / 0.78 (UI 100119 p39)"},{"label":"Compressor winding resistance Ω, A02 revision (C-R / S-R)","value":"018 YA14K1E: 1.54 / 1.37 · 024 YA20K1E: 1.26 / 1.37 · 030 YA25K1E: 0.89 / 1.57 · 036 YA31K1E: 0.72 / 1.43 · 041 YA34K1E: 0.57 / 1.64 · 042 YA36K1E: 0.52 / 1.6 · 047 YA40K1E: 0.52 / 1.6 · 048 YA42K1E: 0.46 / 1.3 · 059 YA49K1E: 0.44 / 0.8 · 060 YA51K1E: 0.39 / 0.78 (UI 100119 p39). Check the revision level (A01 / A02) on the plate first - the pairs are printed for different terminal pairs"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. Suction 3/4 in. (018-030), 7/8 in. (036-048), 1-1/8 in. (059 / 060) (II 508603-01 Table 1)"},{"label":"Length / lift / oil","value":"Over 50 ft, refer to Corp. 9351-L9; maximum lift not published. Compressor oil covers up to 50 ft; add 1 oz of POE per 5 lb of charge over 20 lb (UI p16)"}]},{"title":"Controls, switches & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Control board","value":"None. Contactor with dual run capacitor (C12), no LED, no flash codes. The only LED is on the indoor RDS board (UI p31)"},{"label":"High-pressure switch S4","value":"Opens at 590 ±10 psig, resets at 418 ±5 psig, auto reset (UI 100119 p29)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch S87","value":"Opens at 40 ±5 psig, resets at 90 ±5 psig (UI 100119 p29)","key":true},{"label":"Compressor internal vacuum protector","value":"Unloads below 20 psig (hissing) and resets above 40 psig - not a compressor failure (UI p29)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-fitted on 041-060 (EHB p4). The S40 thermostat on the compressor shell closes below 50 °F and opens at 70 °F (UI p29)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling down to 45 °F outdoor as shipped, 30 °F with low-ambient kit 34M72. Maximum altitude 10,000 ft (EHB p5, p7; II p6)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"A Lennox RDS Blower Control Board (Cat 27A02) and sensor are required on the indoor unit. At power-up it runs a 5-minute purge; the Test button simulates a leak (flashing blue LED, blower on, compressor off). A second sensor is required when line-set joints are not sleeved, unless one of Options 1-3 applies. Verify the RDS (purge, then Test) before the system runs (II 508491-01 p7, p17, p20)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft²)","value":"10 lb = 149.9 · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8. Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.02 at 2,620 ft, 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft (the printed table is non-monotonic: 1.05 at 3,280 ft, 1.04 at 3,940 ft) (UI p5; II p5)"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm · 10 lb = 271 · 15 lb = 406 · 20 lb = 541 · 30 lb = 812 cfm (UI p5)"},{"label":"Leak check / brazing","value":"A trace charge is at most 2 oz. Nitrogen test at 160 psig (II p14; UI p23). Braze with nitrogen flowing at 1-2 psig, never purge with oxygen. Flush old mineral-oil line sets; a 1/4 in. RFC liquid line must be replaced"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"EHB 211058 p7 note 1 says the factory charge covers 15 ft; charging label 581334-02 (UI 100119 p39) says 30 ft with 3 oz per 5 ft on 3/8 in. liquid line. Read the nameplate before adding or removing refrigerant."},{"title":"A01 and A02 units use different compressors","body":"The winding-resistance pairs differ by revision level (YPH/YBH on A01, YA on A02) and are printed for different terminal pairs. Which compressor brand goes with which revision is not confirmed - read the compressor label."},{"title":"UI 100119 spec table differs slightly from EHB 211058","body":"The UI omits the 059 size and lists MCA 23 for the 042 and 31 for the 060 (EHB: 23.2 and 31.2), with different sound and weight figures. All three UIs in this family print an EL22KCV model-ID chart on p4/p5. The rating plate governs."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Fan FLA, fan LRA for 041 / 047 / 059, capacitor MFD, maximum line length and lift."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML17KC2 (Merit two-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Merit ML17KC2 two-stage scroll split AC condenser (partial unit), R-454B (A2L), 17.0-17.9 SEER2 nominal, part load about 67%. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060, 208/230-1. Indoor TXV and indoor RDS required. No outdoor board - staged by a two-stage thermostat on Y1/Y2 through a 24 VDC unloader solenoid. Figures below are from EHB 211059; the UI 100132 spec page describes a different, variable-speed unit (see flags).","match":["ML17KC2","ML17KC2-024-230","ML17KC2-036-230","ML17KC2-048-230","ML17KC2-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) ML17KC2, Form 211059 (Oct 2024); Lennox Unit Information ML17KC2, Corp. 100132 (Mar 18 2026), charging label 581347-02 on p37; Lennox Installation Instructions ML17KC2, 508642-01","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML17KC2-036-230A01)","value":"ML = Merit · 17 = nominal SEER2 (17.0-17.9) · K = R-454B · C = air conditioner · 2 = two-stage · 024-060 = capacity in kBtuh (2-5 ton) · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level (EHB 211059 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B","value":"024: 6 lb 4 oz · 036: 6 lb 8 oz · 048: 7 lb 14 oz · 060: 9 lb 5 oz (EHB 211059 p7). UI 100132 p6 prints 6 lb 10 oz / 6 lb 11 oz / 10 lb 3 oz / 10 lb 7 oz on a page that describes a variable-speed unit - do not use it, see flag. The rating plate governs","key":true},{"label":"Line length the charge covers - CONFLICT","value":"EHB p7 note 1: 15 ft. Charging label (UI 100132 p37): 30 ft - with 3/8 in. liquid line add 3 oz per 5 ft over 30 ft, subtract below. UI weigh-in rate 0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in. (0.40 for 5/16 in., 1.00 for 1/2 in.). Read the nameplate before adjusting","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in when outdoor is 64 °F or below. At 65 °F and above, subcooling or approach from label 581347-02, checked at HIGH capacity (Y1 + Y2). Charge liquid only; use the saturated liquid temperature for subcooling. Block the coil if needed to hold 325-375 psig liquid (UI 100132 p35-37)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling / approach targets at high capacity (label 581347-02)","value":"Subcooling 024: 9.6 · 036: 12.2 · 048: 13.6 · 060: 15.1 °F. Approach 024: 1.2 · 036: 2.7 · 048: 3.6 · 060: 4 °F (UI 100132 p37)","key":true},{"label":"Typical liquid / suction psig at 95 °F","value":"Low stage 024: 314 / 138 · 036: 326 / 139 · 048: 334 / 137 · 060: 338 / 135. High stage 024: 326 / 134 · 036: 345 / 132 · 048: 357 / 132 · 060: 366 / 130 (label 581347-02)"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor TXV only. Kits 26Z70 (1.5-3 ton), 26Z71 (3.5-4 ton), 26Z72 (5 ton). The supplied liquid-line drier goes outdoors"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (EHB 211059 p7)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 13.8 / 20 / 10.3 / 62 / 1 · 036: 18.9 / 30 / 14.6 / 90 / 0.74 · 048: 23.9 / 40 / 18.3 / 138 / 1 · 060: 33.2 / 50 / 25.2 / 147.3 / 1.7. UI 100132 p6 lists MCA 15 / 21.5 / 26.4 / 30.4 and MOCP 20 / 35 / 40 / 50 on its wrong spec page - EHB values shown","key":true},{"label":"Hard-start kit","value":"REQUIRED below 230 V supply (EHB p5)","key":true},{"label":"Compressor winding resistance Ω (C-R / S-R)","value":"024 YAS20K1E: 1.07 / 1.65 · 036 YAS30K1E: 0.73 / 1.47 · 048 YAS40K1E: 0.44 / 1.66 · 060 YAS51K1E: 0.35 / 1.39 (UI 100132 p37)"},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Dual run capacitor C12; MFD rating not published - see the rating plate. Supply voltage +10% / -5%"}]},{"title":"Staging","rows":[{"label":"Two-stage scroll","value":"Part load about 67% (EHB p4). Y1 runs low stage. Y2 goes through rectifier plug D4 to the 24 VDC L34 unloader solenoid inside the compressor - never apply 24 VAC to the coil terminals. Field wires: yellow = Y1, blue = Y2, black = C (UI 100132 p30-31)","key":true}]},{"title":"Line set, switches & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Line set","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. Connection sizes by size are not in the documents used here - check the service valves (II 508642-01). Over 50 ft, refer to Corp. 9351-L9; maximum lift not published. Compressor oil covers up to 50 ft; add 1 oz POE per 5 lb of charge over 20 lb"},{"label":"High-pressure switch S4","value":"Opens at 590 ±10 psig, resets at 418 ±5 psig, auto reset (UI 100132 p28)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch S87","value":"Opens at 40 ±5 psig, resets at 90 ±5 psig (UI 100132 p28)"},{"label":"Compressor internal vacuum protector","value":"Unloads below 20 psig (hissing) and resets above 40 psig - not a compressor failure"},{"label":"Crankcase heater - CONFLICT","value":"EHB p5: factory-fitted on 060 only. UI p30 wiring note: S40 / HR1 used on 048 and 060. Check the unit"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling down to 45 °F outdoor as shipped, 30 °F with low-ambient kit 34M72. Maximum altitude 10,000 ft (EHB p5, p7; II p6)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"A Lennox RDS Blower Control Board (Cat 27A02) and sensor are required on the indoor unit. At power-up it runs a 5-minute purge; the Test button simulates a leak (flashing blue LED, blower on, compressor off). A second sensor is required when line-set joints are not sleeved, unless one of Options 1-3 applies. Verify the RDS (purge, then Test) before the system runs (II 508491-01 p7, p17, p20)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft²)","value":"10 lb = 149.9 · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8. Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.02 at 2,620 ft, 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft (the printed table is non-monotonic: 1.05 at 3,280 ft, 1.04 at 3,940 ft) (UI p5; II p5)"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm · 10 lb = 271 · 15 lb = 406 · 20 lb = 541 · 30 lb = 812 cfm (UI p5)"},{"label":"Leak check / brazing","value":"A trace charge is at most 2 oz. Nitrogen test at 160 psig (II p14; UI p23). Braze with nitrogen flowing at 1-2 psig, never purge with oxygen. Flush old mineral-oil line sets; a 1/4 in. RFC liquid line must be replaced"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"UI 100132 p6 spec page describes the wrong unit - do not use it","body":"It lists 'Variable Rotary' compressors and a 1/3 HP ECM fan with min/max speeds, charges 6 lb 10 oz / 6 lb 11 oz / 10 lb 3 oz / 10 lb 7 oz, MCA 15 / 21.5 / 26.4 / 30.4 and MOCP 20 / 35 / 40 / 50. That contradicts EHB 211059 and the UI's own two-stage wiring and sequence of operation. The figures above come from the EHB; the rating plate governs."},{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"EHB 211059 p7 note 1 says the factory charge covers 15 ft; the charging label (UI 100132 p37) says 30 ft with 3 oz per 5 ft on 3/8 in. liquid line. Read the nameplate before adding or removing refrigerant."},{"title":"Crankcase heater: the documents disagree","body":"EHB 211059 p5 says factory-fitted on the 060 only; the UI 100132 p30 wiring note says S40 / HR1 are used on 048 and 060."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Capacitor MFD, line-set connection sizes, maximum line length and lift."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL15KC1 (Elite single-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Elite EL15KC1 single-stage scroll split AC condenser, all-aluminum coil, R-454B (A2L) only, SEER2 up to 16.0. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (1.5-5 ton), 208/230-1. Indoor TXV only; indoor RDS required. Plain contactor - no board, no codes. EHB 211053 and UI 100120 agree on every size-table value below.","match":["EL15KC1","EL15KC1-018-230","EL15KC1-024-230","EL15KC1-030-230","EL15KC1-036-230","EL15KC1-042-230","EL15KC1-048-230","EL15KC1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) EL15KC1, Form 211053 (Sep 2024); Lennox Unit Information EL15KC1, Corp. 100120 (Apr 2026), charging label 581280-02 on p38; Lennox Installation Instructions EL15KC1, 508492-01 (6/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL15KC1-024-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 2 digits = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · C = AC (condenser) · 1 = single-stage compressor · 3 digits = nominal capacity · 230 = 208/230V-1ph-60Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level (EHB 211053 p1). EHB 211053 decodes the tier as '16 = 16.0' while UI 100120 says 15 - same unit"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B, printed for a 15 ft line set / for a 30 ft line set","value":"018: 4 lb 0 oz / 4 lb 9 oz · 024: 4 lb 7 oz / 5 lb 0 oz · 030: 4 lb 14 oz / 5 lb 7 oz · 036: 5 lb 10 oz / 6 lb 3 oz · 042: 6 lb 2 oz / 6 lb 11 oz · 048: 7 lb 10 oz / 8 lb 3 oz · 060: 8 lb 8 oz / 9 lb 1 oz (15 ft: EHB 211053 p7-8 and UI 100120 p6-7; 30 ft: UI 100120 p6-7). The nameplate says which one your unit shipped with","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment - CONFLICT on the base length","value":"Charging label 581280-02 (UI 100120 p38): charge is based on 30 ft; add 3 oz per 5 ft over 30 ft, subtract under 30 ft. The EHB footnote says 15 ft. Trim from the nameplate plus the unit label, and write the total charge on the nameplate (II p19)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling against the unit label (II 508492-01 p19). Charge liquid only; use saturated liquid temperature for subcooling","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target °F ±1 at 65 / 75 / 85 / 95 / 105 / 115 °F outdoor (label 581280-02 Table 3)","value":"018: 8 / 3 / 4 / 7 / 7 / 9 · 024: 6 / 3 / 5 / 6 / 8 / 10 · 030: 11 / 8 / 6 / 6 / 8 / 9 · 036: 13 / 11 / 11 / 12 / 12 / 13 · 042: 14 / 11 / 11 / 13 / 16 / 17 · 048: 14 / 11 / 12 / 12 / 13 / 13 · 060: 11 / 11 / 11 / 12 / 12 / 12","key":true},{"label":"Approach °F at 65 / 75 / 85 / 95 / 105 / 115 °F (label Table 2)","value":"018: 6 / 10 / 9 / 7 / 7 / 5 · 024: 8 / 11 / 10 / 9 / 7 / 6 · 030: 2 / 5 / 6 / 6 / 5 / 5 · 036: 2 / 3 / 4 / 4 / 4 / 3 · 042: 5 / 7 / 7 / 6 / 5 / 5 · 048: 2 / 6 / 6 / 6 / 6 / 5 · 060: 7 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 8"},{"label":"Typical liquid / suction psig, -024 (label Table 1)","value":"75 °F: 254 / 133 · 85 °F: 298 / 134 · 95 °F: 346 / 136 · 105 °F: 398 / 138. Other sizes: read the unit label"},{"label":"Metering (TXV kit)","value":"018-036: 26Z70 · 042 / 048: 26Z71 · 060: 26Z72 (EHB 211053 p7-8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (EHB 211053 p7-8; UI 100120 p6-7 agree)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 11.1 / 15 / 8.3 / 45 / 0.7 · 024: 13.5 / 20 / 10.2 / 60.2 / 0.7 · 030: 16.6 / 25 / 12.5 / 67.8 / 1.0 · 036: 17.8 / 30 / 13.4 / 82.5 / 1.0 · 042: 21.2 / 35 / 14.9 / 109 / 2.6 · 048: 24.3 / 40 / 18.0 / 126 / 1.7 · 060: 31.3 / 50 / 23.7 / 157 / 1.7","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"MFD rating not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections (liquid x suction)","value":"018 / 024 / 030: 3/8 x 3/4 · 036 / 042 / 048: 3/8 x 7/8 · 060: 3/8 x 1-1/8 (II 508492-01 p7 Table 1; UI 100120 p26)"},{"label":"Length","value":"L15 line sets run 15-50 ft. For runs over 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9 (not retrieved - no maximum length or lift confirmed)"}]},{"title":"Controls, switches & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Control board","value":"None - plain contactor, no board codes"},{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens 590 ±10 psig, resets 418 ±5 psig (UI 100120 p28)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Opens 40 ±5 psig, resets 90 ±5 psig (UI 100120 p28)","key":true},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Down to 45 °F with no added controls, 30 °F with Low Ambient Kit 34M72. Optional cut-off switch 45F08 locks out the compressor below 35 °F (EHB 211053 p5). Maximum altitude 10,000 ft"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required (II 508492-01 p4; UI 100121 p5)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft², sea level)","value":"10 lb = 149.9 · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8. Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.02 at 2,620 ft, 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft. Maximum altitude 10,000 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 CFM · 8 lb = 216 · 10 lb = 271 · 12 lb = 325 (the table runs to 30 lb = 812)"},{"label":"Field joints / tools","value":"Leak-test to 0.2 oz/yr sensitivity. Gauges must be rated 0-800 psig high side; hoses 800 psig with 4000 burst (II 508492-01 p3, p18). Charge liquid only; use saturated liquid temperature for subcooling and saturated vapor temperature for superheat"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"The EHB 211053 footnote says 15 ft; charging label 581280-02 (UI 100120 p38) says 30 ft with 3 oz per 5 ft. The UI now lists both a 15 ft and a 30 ft charge per size. Only the nameplate says which charge a given serial shipped with."},{"title":"Decode oddity","body":"EHB 211053 decodes the EL15KC1 tier digits as '16 = 16.0', while UI 100120 says 15. Same unit - the SEER2 rating is up to 16.0."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Capacitor MFD rating, maximum line length and lift above 50 ft (Corp. 9351-L9 only), and which factory charge (15 or 30 ft) a given serial shipped with."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL16KC1 (Elite single-stage AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Elite EL16KC1 single-stage scroll split AC condenser, all-aluminum coil, R-454B (A2L) only, SEER2 up to 17.0. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 041 / 042 / 047 / 048 / 060 (041 and 042 = 3.5 ton, 047 and 048 = 4 ton); the -059 appears on the charging label only. 208/230-1. Indoor TXV only; indoor RDS required. Plain contactor - no board, no codes. EHB 211054 and UI 100121 agree except where a cell shows both values.","match":["EL16KC1","EL16KC1-018-230","EL16KC1-024-230","EL16KC1-030-230","EL16KC1-036-230","EL16KC1-041-230","EL16KC1-042-230","EL16KC1-047-230","EL16KC1-048-230","EL16KC1-059-230","EL16KC1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) EL16KC1, Form 211054 (Sep 2025; the Sep 2024 edition matches except it has no 30 ft row); Lennox Unit Information EL16KC1, Corp. 100121 (Jan 2025), charging label 581334-02 on p37; Lennox Installation Instructions EL16KC1, 508604-01 (6/2025) and the 7/2024 revision","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL16KC1-036-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 16 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · C = AC (condenser) · 1 = single-stage compressor · 3 digits = nominal capacity · 230 = 208/230V-1ph-60Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level (EHB 211054 p1). The EHB decode says 047 = 4.5 T, but its spec table says 4 T. UI 100121 p5 shows an EL22KCV decode by mistake"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 041 / 042 / 047 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B, printed for a 15 ft line set / for a 30 ft line set","value":"018: 4 lb 14 oz / 5 lb 7 oz · 024: 4 lb 14 oz / 5 lb 7 oz · 030: 5 lb 10 oz / 6 lb 3 oz · 036: 6 lb 13 oz / 7 lb 6 oz · 041: 7 lb 7 oz / 8 lb 0 oz · 042: 7 lb 2 oz / 7 lb 11 oz · 047: 7 lb 13 oz / 8 lb 6 oz · 048: 8 lb 14 oz / 9 lb 7 oz · 060: 8 lb 14 oz / 9 lb 7 oz · 059: label only, no spec published - see rating plate (15 ft: EHB 211054 p7-8 and UI 100121 p7; 30 ft: EHB 211054 Sept 2025 p8). The nameplate says which one your unit shipped with","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment - the sources disagree","value":"II 508604-01 7/2024 (p19): 15 ft base, add 3 oz per 5 ft beyond 15 ft. II 508604-01 6/2025: defers to the charging label. Label 581334-02 (UI 100121 p37): 30 ft base, add or subtract 3 oz per 5 ft. Read the nameplate before adjusting","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling against the unit label. Charge liquid only; use saturated liquid temperature","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling target °F ±1 at 65 / 75 / 85 / 95 / 105 / 115 °F outdoor (label 581334-02 Table 3)","value":"018: 9 / 6 / 7 / 6 / 7 / 7 · 024: 9 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 8 / 8 · 030: 10 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 6 · 036: 12 / 10 / 10 / 9 / 8 / 7 · 041: 11 / 9 / 7 / 7 / 7 / 7 · 042: 10 / 7 / 6 / 7 / 7 / 6 · 047: 11 / 10 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 8 · 048: 12 / 10 / 9 / 8 / 8 / 8 · 059: 11 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 9 / 8 · 060: 9 / 7 / 8 / 8 / 8 / 8. The 048 at 85 °F prints '9 (4.4)' - the °C figure matches 8 °F, so one of the two is a label typo","key":true},{"label":"Approach °F at 65 / 75 / 85 / 95 / 105 / 115 °F (label Table 2)","value":"018: 3 / 4 / 4 / 5 / 4 / 3 · 024: 3 / 4 / 4 / 4 / 4 / 4 · 030: 1 / 3 / 4 / 4 / 4 / 4 · 036: 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 / 6 · 041: 1 / 3 / 4 / 4 / 4 / 4 · 042: 2 / 5 / 5 / 5 / 5 / 5 · 047: 2 / 3 / 5 / 6 / 6 / 5 · 048: 3 / 4 / 5 / 6 / 6 / 6 · 059: 1 / 2 / 3 / 3 / 3 / 3 · 060: 2 / 4 / 4 / 4 / 4 / 4"},{"label":"Typical liquid / suction psig, -041 (label Table 1)","value":"75 °F: 246 / 129 · 85 °F: 286 / 134 · 95 °F: 330 / 136 · 105 °F: 378 / 137. Other sizes: read the unit label"},{"label":"Metering (TXV kit)","value":"018-036: 26Z70 · 041 / 042 / 047 / 048: 26Z71 · 060: 26Z72 (EHB 211054 p7-8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (EHB 211054 p7-8; UI 100121 p6-7)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 11.2 / 15 / 8.3 / 45 / 0.74 · 024: 13.6 / 20 / 10.3 / 60.2 / 0.74 · 030: 16.6 / 25 / 12.7 / 75.6 / 0.74 · 036: 21.8 / 30 / 16.7 / 93.5 / 1.0 · 041: 21 / 30 / 14.7 / 109 / 2.6 · 042: MCA 23.2 (EHB) or 23 (UI) / 35 / 17.3 / 123 / fan 1.56 (EHB) or 1.4 (UI) · 047: 25.2 / 40 / 18.1 / 126 / 2.6 · 048: 29.7 / 45 / 22.4 / 126 / 1.7 · 060: MCA 31.2 (EHB) or 31 (UI) / 50 / 23.7 / 157 / fan 1.56 (EHB) or 1.4 (UI)","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"MFD rating not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections (liquid x suction)","value":"018 / 024 / 030: 3/8 x 3/4 · 036 / 041 / 042 / 047 / 048: 3/8 x 7/8 · 060: 3/8 x 1-1/8 (EHB 211054 p7-8)"},{"label":"Length","value":"Rated 15-50 ft. For runs over 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9 (not retrieved - no maximum length or lift confirmed)"}]},{"title":"Controls, switches & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Control board","value":"None - plain contactor, no board codes"},{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens 590 ±10 psig, resets 418 ±5 psig (UI 100121 p27)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Opens 40 ±5 psig, resets 90 ±5 psig (UI 100121 p27)","key":true},{"label":"Crankcase heater thermostat","value":"Closes below 50 °F shell temperature, opens at 70 °F (UI 100121 p27)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Maximum altitude 10,000 ft. Low-ambient limits for this model are not in the documents used here - see the EHB"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required (II 508492-01 p4; UI 100121 p5)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft², sea level)","value":"10 lb = 149.9 · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8. Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.02 at 2,620 ft, 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft. Maximum altitude 10,000 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 CFM · 8 lb = 216 · 10 lb = 271 · 12 lb = 325 (the table runs to 30 lb = 812)"},{"label":"Field joints / tools","value":"Leak-test to 0.2 oz/yr sensitivity. Gauges must be rated 0-800 psig high side; hoses 800 psig with 4000 burst (II 508492-01 p3, p18). Charge liquid only; use saturated liquid temperature for subcooling and saturated vapor temperature for superheat"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"The EHB 211054 footnote and II 508604-01 7/2024 say 15 ft; charging label 581334-02 (UI 100121 p37) says 30 ft with 3 oz per 5 ft, and the 6/2025 II defers to the label. The Sep 2025 EHB lists both a 15 ft and a 30 ft charge per size. Only the nameplate says which charge a given serial shipped with."},{"title":"042 and 060: EHB and UI disagree on MCA and fan FLA","body":"EHB 211054: MCA 23.2 (042) and 31.2 (060), fan FLA 1.56. UI 100121: MCA 23 and 31, fan FLA 1.4. Both are shown above; the rating plate governs."},{"title":"Copy errors in the Lennox documents","body":"UI 100121 p5 shows an EL22KCV model decode. The EHB decode says 047 = 4.5 T while its spec table says 4 T. The -059 appears on the charging label only, with no published spec - see the rating plate."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Capacitor MFD rating, -059 spec data, maximum line length and lift above 50 ft (Corp. 9351-L9 only), and which factory charge (15 or 30 ft) a given serial shipped with."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL18KCV (Elite variable-capacity AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Elite EL18KCV variable-capacity (inverter) split AC condenser, all-aluminum coil, R-454B (A2L) only, SEER2 up to 19.5. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060, 208/230-1. Indoor TXV only; indoor RDS required. Outdoor control with 7-segment E-codes, Charge Mode jumper and unit code. WARNING: UI 100144 p6-7 reprints the EL22KCV spec table word for word, so the EHB (E18) and UI (U18) values conflict on charge, MCA, MOCP, RLA and fan FLA - both are shown below; the rating plate governs.","match":["EL18KCV","EL18KCV-024-230","EL18KCV-036-230","EL18KCV-048-230","EL18KCV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) EL18KCV, Form 211055 (Jan 2025); Lennox Unit Information EL18KCV, Corp. 100144 (Apr 2025), charging label 581344-02 on p85; Lennox Installation Instructions EL18KCV, 508698-01 (6/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL18KCV-048-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 18 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · C = AC (condenser) · V = variable-capacity compressor · 3 digits = nominal capacity · 230 = 208/230V-1ph-60Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level (EHB 211055 p1)"},{"label":"Unit selection code on the outdoor control","value":"80 / 81 / 82 / 83 = 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (UI 100144 p45). A replacement outdoor control needs its unit code set - three bars on the display means it is not configured"},{"label":"Compressor - CONFLICT","value":"EHB 211055 p8 lists 024-048 as variable rotary and 060 as variable SCROLL. UI 100144 p5 says all sizes are rotary"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B for 15 ft - CONFLICT, EHB 211055 p8 [E18] / UI 100144 p7 [U18]","value":"024: 6 lb 3 oz [E18] / 6 lb 10 oz [U18] · 036: 6 lb 7 oz [E18] / 6 lb 11 oz [U18] · 048: 9 lb 8 oz [E18] / 10 lb 3 oz [U18] · 060: 9 lb 10 oz [E18] / 10 lb 7 oz [U18]. The U18 column is the EL22KCV table (probable copy error). Use the rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment - CONFLICT on the base length","value":"0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in. liquid (0.40 for 5/16 in., 1.00 for 1/2 in.). II 508698-01 p8 and UI 100144 p83 Fig 47 say the factory charge covers 15 ft; charging label 581344-02 (UI 100144 p85) says 30 ft base with 3 oz per 5 ft. Read the nameplate","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in, then check subcooling at 100% capacity (Charge Mode jumper), with 70-80 °F return air and outdoor ambient 60 °F or higher (UI 100144 p83 Fig 48). Readings at part speed are not valid. Charge liquid only; saturated liquid temperature for subcooling","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling / approach targets at high capacity, ±1 °F (label 581344-02)","value":"Subcooling 024: 10 · 036: 11.5 · 048: 10.5 · 060: 11 °F. Approach 024: 4 · 036: 4 · 048: 5 · 060: 6.5 °F (UI 100144 p85)","key":true},{"label":"Typical liquid / vapor psig, -048 at high capacity","value":"75 °F: 261 / 125 · 85 °F: 303 / 128 · 95 °F: 348 / 131 · 105 °F: 396 / 133 (UI 100144 p85). Other sizes: read the unit label"},{"label":"Metering (TXV kit)","value":"024 / 036: 26Z70 · 048: 26Z71 · 060: 26Z72"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1 - CONFLICT, EHB 211055 p8 [E18] / UI 100144 p7 [U18]","rows":[{"label":"MCA","value":"024: 15 [both] · 036: 23.4 [E18] / 21.5 [U18] · 048: 28.7 [E18] / 26.4 [U18] · 060: 36.5 [E18] / 30.4 [U18]","key":true},{"label":"MOCP","value":"024: 25 [E18] / 20 [U18] · 036: 35 [both] · 048: 50 [E18] / 40 [U18] · 060: 60 [E18] / 50 [U18]","key":true},{"label":"Compressor RLA","value":"024: 10.8 [E18] / 9.9 [U18] · 036: 15.8 [E18] / 15.1 [U18] · 048: 20.5 [E18] / 19 [U18] · 060: 25.7 [E18] / 22.2 [U18]. LRA not published (inverter)"},{"label":"Fan FLA","value":"024: 0.74 [E18] / 2.6 [U18] · 036: 2.6 [both] · 048: 1.7 [E18] / 2.6 [U18] · 060: 2.6 [both]"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections (liquid x suction)","value":"024: 3/8 x 3/4 · 036 / 048: 3/8 x 7/8 · 060: 3/8 x 1-1/8, up to 50 ft"},{"label":"Long line (51-150 ft)","value":"Max 180 ft equivalent, 150 ft actual, 60 ft vapor riser, 60 ft liquid lift; -048 uses 7/8 horizontal vapor and a 7/8 riser. With 3/8 liquid, maximum elevation is 50 / 41 / 31 / 22 ft at 75 / 100 / 125 / 150 ft of line; a 1/2 in. liquid line allows 60 ft. Over 150 ft is not recommended. Trap the riser when the outdoor unit is 5-60 ft above the indoor unit (II 508698-01 p8-9 Tables 2-4)"}]},{"title":"Controls, pressure protection & operating range (UI 100144 / UI 100104 shared sections)","rows":[{"label":"Charge Mode jumper (CHRG MODE)","value":"Runs the compressor and outdoor fan at 100%, times out after 60 min. On a 24 V thermostat apply Y1 and a blower call first. A 24 V single-stage thermostat needs a Y1-Y2 jumper"},{"label":"Operation Mode jumper (24 V thermostats only)","value":"Efficiency (pins 1-2, factory default, sliding setpoint) · Normal (pins 2-3) = 135 psig suction · Comfort (jumper removed) = 125 psig"},{"label":"Pressure protection","value":"No low-pressure switch: the suction transducer cuts out at 40 psig and back in at 90 (E410); five trips in 1 h locks out (E411). HPS opens at 590, closes at 418 (E412; lockout E413). Anti-short-cycle 300 s","key":true},{"label":"Alert codes","value":"E409 24 V at 18 VAC or less · E181 suction transducer · E183 liquid transducer out of 0.5-4.5 VDC · E416 outdoor coil sensor · E422 compressor top-cap over-temperature · E424 liquid-line sensor (10 kΩ at 77 °F) · E425 low-ambient minimum speed raised (starts at 45 °F, 100% at 17 °F) · E423 inverter circuit problem (4 red flashes) · E430 compressor start failure"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling down to 0 °F (EHB 211055 p5). Maximum altitude 10,000 ft. Wait 7 minutes for the inverter to discharge (the panel label says 7, the text says 5 - wait 7)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required (II 508492-01 p4; UI 100121 p5)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft², sea level)","value":"10 lb = 149.9 · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8. Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.02 at 2,620 ft, 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft. Maximum altitude 10,000 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 CFM · 8 lb = 216 · 10 lb = 271 · 12 lb = 325 (the table runs to 30 lb = 812)"},{"label":"Field joints / tools","value":"Leak-test to 0.2 oz/yr sensitivity. Gauges must be rated 0-800 psig high side; hoses 800 psig with 4000 burst (II 508492-01 p3, p18). Charge liquid only; use saturated liquid temperature for subcooling and saturated vapor temperature for superheat"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"UI 100144 reprints the EL22KCV table","body":"UI 100144 (EL18KCV) p6-7 carries the EL22KCV specs and SEER2 decode word for word: charge 10 lb 3 oz on the 048, MCA 26.4, MOCP 40, RLA 19, fan FLA 2.6. EHB 211055 gives 9 lb 8 oz, 28.7, 50, 20.5 and 1.7 for the same unit. Both columns are shown above as E18 / U18. Use the rating plate."},{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"II 508698-01 p8 and UI 100144 p83 Fig 47 say the factory charge covers 15 ft; charging label 581344-02 (UI 100144 p85) says 30 ft base with 3 oz per 5 ft. Read the nameplate before adding or removing refrigerant."},{"title":"Compressor type: the documents disagree","body":"EHB 211055 p8: 024-048 variable rotary, 060 variable scroll. UI 100144 p5: all rotary."},{"title":"Low suction shows as E410 even though there is no LPS","body":"Check the TXV, airflow and charge before blaming the transducer. Charge only at 100% capacity (Charge Mode)."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Compressor LRA (inverter), capacitor MFD, and which factory charge (15 or 30 ft) a given serial shipped with."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL22KCV (Elite variable-capacity AC, R-454B)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Elite EL22KCV variable-capacity (inverter) split AC condenser, all-aluminum coil, R-454B (A2L) only, SEER2 up to 22.9. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060, 208/230-1. Indoor TXV only; indoor RDS required. Inverter is built into the control on 024/036 and is a separate external inverter on 048/060. Outdoor control with 7-segment E-codes, Charge Mode jumper and unit code. EHB 211056 and UI 100104 agree on the size table.","match":["EL22KCV","EL22KCV-024-230","EL22KCV-036-230","EL22KCV-048-230","EL22KCV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications (EHB) EL22KCV, Form 211056 (Aug 2024); Lennox Unit Information EL22KCV, Corp. 100104 (Apr 2025), charging label 581264-02 on p86; Lennox Installation Instructions EL22KCV, 508484-01 (6/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL22KCV-048-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 22 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · C = AC (condenser) · V = variable-capacity compressor · 3 digits = nominal capacity · 230 = 208/230V-1ph-60Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level"},{"label":"Unit code / inverter","value":"Unit codes 96 / 97 / 98 / 99 = 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (UI 100104 p47). Inverter built into the control on 024 / 036, separate external inverter on 048 / 060 (EHB 211056 p5). A replacement outdoor control needs its unit code set - three bars on the display means it is not configured"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B for 15 ft (EHB 211056 p8; UI 100104 p7 agree)","value":"024: 6 lb 10 oz · 036: 6 lb 11 oz · 048: 10 lb 3 oz · 060: 10 lb 7 oz. The rating plate governs","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment - CONFLICT on the base length","value":"Weigh-in rate 0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in. liquid (II 508484-01 p8). The EHB / UI footnote says the charge covers 15 ft; charging label 581264-02 (UI 100104 p86) says 30 ft base with 3 oz per 5 ft. Read the nameplate","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in, then subcooling at 100% capacity (Charge Mode jumper). On the label's subcooling method, block the coil to hold the liquid line at 325-375 psig (label 581264-02). Charge liquid only; saturated liquid temperature for subcooling","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling / approach targets at maximum capacity, ±1 °F (label 581264-02)","value":"Subcooling 024: 7.5 · 036: 6.5 · 048: 9.5 · 060: 9.5 °F. Approach 024: 4 · 036: 5.5 · 048: 6.5 · 060: 6.5 °F (UI 100104 p86)","key":true},{"label":"Typical liquid / vapor psig, -048 at max speed","value":"75 °F: 267 / 128 · 85 °F: 310 / 134 · 95 °F: 352 / 135 · 105 °F: 406 / 138 (UI 100104 p86). Other sizes: read the unit label"},{"label":"Metering (TXV kit)","value":"024 / 036: 26Z70 · 048: 26Z71 · 060: 26Z72"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / fan FLA (EHB 211056 p8; UI 100104 p7)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 15 / 20 / 9.9 / 2.6 · 036: 21.5 / 35 / 15.1 / 2.6 · 048: 26.4 / 40 / 19 / 2.6 · 060: 30.4 / 50 / 22.2 / 2.6. Fan 1/3 HP ECM. Compressor LRA not published (inverter)","key":true}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections (liquid x suction)","value":"024: 3/8 x 3/4 · 036 / 048: 3/8 x 7/8 · 060: 3/8 x 1-1/8"},{"label":"Long line","value":"Same limits as the EL18KCV: 180 ft equivalent, 150 ft actual, 60 ft vapor riser, 60 ft liquid lift; 7/8 riser on the -048. Over 150 ft not recommended. Trap the riser when the outdoor unit is 5-60 ft above the indoor unit (II 508484-01 p8-9)"}]},{"title":"Controls, pressure protection & operating range (UI 100104 p34-35, p40-47)","rows":[{"label":"Charge Mode jumper (CHRG MODE)","value":"Runs the compressor and outdoor fan at 100%, times out after 60 min. On a 24 V thermostat apply Y1 and a blower call first. A 24 V single-stage thermostat needs a Y1-Y2 jumper"},{"label":"Operation Mode jumper (24 V thermostats only)","value":"Efficiency (pins 1-2, factory default, sliding setpoint) · Normal (pins 2-3) = 135 psig suction · Comfort (jumper removed) = 125 psig"},{"label":"Pressure protection","value":"No low-pressure switch: the suction transducer cuts out at 40 psig and back in at 90 (E410); five trips in 1 h locks out (E411). HPS opens at 590, closes at 418 (E412; lockout E413). Anti-short-cycle 300 s","key":true},{"label":"Alert codes","value":"E409 24 V at 18 VAC or less · E181 suction transducer · E183 liquid transducer out of 0.5-4.5 VDC · E416 outdoor coil sensor (EL22KCV uses a fixed 10 kΩ resistor on pins 5-6) · E422 compressor top-cap over-temperature · E424 liquid-line sensor (10 kΩ at 77 °F) · E425 low-ambient minimum speed raised (starts at 45 °F, 100% at 17 °F) · E423 inverter circuit problem (4 red flashes) · E430 compressor start failure"},{"label":"Inverter discharge wait","value":"The inverter panel label says 'Wait 7 Minutes', the text says 5 minutes. Wait 7 (UI 100104 p6). Maximum altitude 10,000 ft"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required (II 508492-01 p4; UI 100121 p5)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft², sea level)","value":"10 lb = 149.9 · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8. Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.02 at 2,620 ft, 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft. Maximum altitude 10,000 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 CFM · 8 lb = 216 · 10 lb = 271 · 12 lb = 325 (the table runs to 30 lb = 812)"},{"label":"Field joints / tools","value":"Leak-test to 0.2 oz/yr sensitivity. Gauges must be rated 0-800 psig high side; hoses 800 psig with 4000 burst (II 508492-01 p3, p18). Charge liquid only; use saturated liquid temperature for subcooling and saturated vapor temperature for superheat"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"The EHB 211056 / UI 100104 footnote says the factory charge covers 15 ft; charging label 581264-02 (UI 100104 p86) says 30 ft base with 3 oz per 5 ft. Read the nameplate before adding or removing refrigerant."},{"title":"Charge only at 100% capacity","body":"Use the Charge Mode jumper; readings at part speed are not valid. Low suction shows as E410 even though no LPS is fitted - check the TXV, airflow and charge before blaming the transducer."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Compressor LRA (inverter), capacitor MFD, and which factory charge (15 or 30 ft) a given serial shipped with."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SL25KCV (Signature variable-capacity AC, R-454B, communicating only)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Dave Lennox Signature Collection SL25KCV split AC condenser with a variable-capacity inverter scroll, R-454B (A2L), SEER2 up to 26.0. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (2-5 ton), 208/230-1-60 only. COMMUNICATING ONLY: needs an S40 thermostat and a Lennox communicating variable-speed furnace or air handler on 4-wire RSBus (R, I+, I-, C). Indoor TXV; indoor RDS required. Sizes are listed in the order 024 / 036 / 048 / 060.","match":["SL25KCV","SL25KCV-024-230","SL25KCV-036-230","SL25KCV-048-230","SL25KCV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Product Specifications SL25KCV, Form 211060 (Aug 2024); Lennox Installation Instructions SL25KCV, 508447-01 rev B (6/2025); Lennox Unit Information SL25KCV, Corp. 100102 (Jan 20 2025), charging label 581263-02 on p79","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (SL25KCV-036-230A01)","value":"SL = Signature tier · 25 = SEER2 25.0 to 26.0 · K = R-454B · C = air conditioner · V = variable-capacity compressor · 036 = nominal size (024 / 036 / 048 / 060 = 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 tons) · 230 = 208/230V-1ph-60Hz · A = ratings revision level · 01 = revision level (EHB p1)"},{"label":"Power-up unit code","value":"88 / 89 / 90 / 91 = 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (UI p41). E443 = wrong unit size configured. After any part change reconfigure through S40: Dealer Control Center > Equipment > Reset > Reconfigure System (UI p46)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B","value":"11 lb 10 oz / 12 lb 3 oz / 11 lb 12 oz / 12 lb 4 oz (EHB p7)","key":true},{"label":"Line length the charge covers - CONFLICT","value":"EHB p7 fn1 and II p9, p25: 15 ft. The printed charging label (UI p79): 30 ft. Go by the unit label. Added charge: 3/8 in. liquid 0.60 oz/ft (3 oz per 5 ft); 5/16 in. 0.40 oz/ft; 1/2 in. 1.00 oz/ft; subtract at the same rate if shorter than the baseline (II p9, p25)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling at 65 °F outdoor or above; weigh in at 64 °F or below. Approach is the cross-check. Run at 100% capacity. Hold the liquid line at 325 to 375 psig while checking subcooling - block the coil if needed. R-454B is a zeotrope: charge liquid only and use saturated liquid temperature for subcooling (UI p79; II p29)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling / approach target ±1 °F","value":"Subcooling 7 / 8 / 7 / 10 °F (UI p79 Table 1). Approach 4 / 4 / 5 / 5 °F (UI p79 Table 2)","key":true},{"label":"Typical suction / liquid psig at 95 °F outdoor","value":"142 / 320 · 137 / 329 · 135 / 329 · 130 / 344. Tolerance liquid ±10, suction ±5. The full table covers 65 to 115 °F (UI p79 Table 3)"},{"label":"Getting 100% capacity","value":"S40: Menu > Advanced Settings > View Dealer Control Center > Test > Cooling - Maximum Rate Test; or the Dealer Setup App; or the CHRG MODE jumper (II p23-25). Charge mode: 100% compressor and fan, max indoor CFM, 60-min timeout, ignored if the jumper is on at power-up. The display scrolls SP, ST, SH, LP, LT and SC (UI p34, p42-43)"},{"label":"Metering / oil","value":"Indoor TXV 26Z70 / 26Z70 / 26Z71 / 26Z72; EHB p10 has the substitution table for mismatched coils. Oil is PVE (II p8)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1 (024 / 036 / 048 / 060, EHB p7)","rows":[{"label":"MCA / MOCP (HACR)","value":"MCA 14.4 / 21.8 / 29.2 / 28.6 A · MOCP 20 / 35 / 50 / 45 A","key":true},{"label":"Compressor RLA / fan","value":"RLA 9.4 / 15.4 / 21.3 / 20.8 A; LRA not published (inverter) - see rating plate. Fan FLA 2.6 A, 1/3 HP ECM. Voltage range +10% / -5%. Control power 24 VAC, 40 VA minimum (II p17)"},{"label":"Compressor winding resistance at 77 °F (±7%)","value":"0.529 Ω on all legs; 048 U-V is 0.587 Ω (UI p57 Fig 28). There is no run capacitor on this unit"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections","value":"Liquid 3/8 on all sizes. Suction 7/8 / 7/8 / 7/8 / 1-1/8 (EHB p7; II p9) - UI Tables 5 and 6 say 3/4 for the -024 (UI p17-18): CONFLICT, measure the valve"},{"label":"Limits","value":"180 ft equivalent, 150 ft linear, 60 ft liquid lift, 60 ft vapor riser (II p9-10). Over 50 ft the riser size is 5/8 / 3/4 / 7/8 / 7/8; liquid lift depends on length (Table 3) - a -060 on 3/8 in. liquid is not recommended at 150 ft. Suction trap at the riser base when the outdoor unit is 5 to 60 ft above the indoor unit (II p9)"}]},{"title":"Pressure, sensors & protection","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch S4 (liquid line, auto-reset)","value":"Opens 590 ±15 psig, resets 418 ±15 psig (II p25; UI p54)","key":true},{"label":"Low pressure (suction transducer acts as the switch) - CONFLICT","value":"Cut-out 40, cut-in 90 psig (UI p46, p54, p57). Table 10 E410 / E411 says 25 / 40 (UI p36). Figure 23 (35 / 80 psig) is labeled EL21KLV. Backup if the transducer fails: suction temperature sensor at 25 °F (UI p54)"},{"label":"Lockout","value":"5 strikes within 1 h (HPS, LP, top-cap). Cycle 24 VAC to reset (UI p36-40, p46). Anti-short-cycle 300 s default; can be set to 60, 120, 180 or 240 s (UI p46)"},{"label":"Sensors","value":"Transducers: 5 VDC supply, 0.5 to 4.5 VDC signal (UI p34). Ambient, liquid and suction thermistors 10 kΩ at 77 °F (UI p36-37)"},{"label":"Top-cap switch - CONFLICT","value":"Text: opens 230-248 °F, closes 149-185 °F. Figure 36: 221-239 °F and 140-176 °F (UI p63)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater - CONFLICT","value":"Thermostat closes 50 °F, opens 70 °F (UI p46, p61). Wattage: 40 W on all sizes (UI p46) vs 25 W on the 024 (UI p61)"}]},{"title":"Operating range, low ambient & codes","rows":[{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling to 0 °F (EHB p5). E601 lockout at -4 °F (-20 °C) or below; a unit already running continues to -15 °F (UI p40)"},{"label":"Low ambient","value":"Fan modulates below 65 °F to hold the liquid line at 58 to 70 °F; the fan stops below 55 °F liquid (UI p64). Freezestat 93G35 (recommended) opens 29 °F, closes 58 °F (EHB p4)"},{"label":"Codes","value":"Communications E105, E120, E124 · sensors/transducers E180-E183, E424 · low 24 V E409 · low pressure E410 / E411 · high pressure E412 / E413 · top cap E422 / E442 · inverter (with red/green LED flash codes) E423, E426-E441 · wrong unit size E443 · low-ambient lockout E601 (UI p36-40). The control stores 100 alarms and shows the last 10. Push-button modes: E = error recall/clear, F = fan test, A = temperatures"},{"label":"Inverter / compressor service","value":"Wait 5 min for the inverter to discharge (II p17); the UI label graphic says 7 min. Compressor replacement comes out through the top (UI p57). Evacuation: triple evacuation, then 500 microns with no rise in 20 min (II p15-16)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS","value":"RDS sensor and mitigation control are required on the indoor unit. It purges for 5 min at power-up, and the Test button simulates a leak (EHB p4; II p17, p25)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin","value":"10 lb = 149.9 ft² · 15 lb = 224.9 ft² · 20 lb = 299.9 ft². Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft (II p3)"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"11 lb = 298 CFM · 12 lb = 325 CFM · 13 lb = 352 CFM (II p3)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"EHB 211060 p7 fn1 and II 508447-01 p9, p25 say the factory charge covers 15 ft; the printed charging label 581263-02 (UI 100102 p79) says 30 ft. Go by the unit label, and finish with subcooling at 100% capacity."},{"title":"Corp. 100102 page 3 shows another model's tables","body":"It lists EL21KLV, variable rotary, 6 lb 10 oz charge, and page 2 decodes 'EL22KCV'. The size table above comes from EHB 211060 p7."},{"title":"Low-pressure set points conflict","body":"40 / 90 psig (UI p46, p54, p57) vs 25 / 40 psig (Table 10, UI p36). Figure 23 (35 / 80 psig) is labeled EL21KLV. Which set point the firmware uses is not confirmed."},{"title":"Top-cap and crankcase heater values conflict inside the UI","body":"Top-cap: 230-248 / 149-185 °F (text) vs 221-239 / 140-176 °F (Fig 36). Crankcase heater: 40 W all sizes (p46) vs 25 W on the 024 (p61)."},{"title":"Boilerplate to ignore","body":"The E411 and E413 text still says 'HFC410A'. The label's 'call for heat' charging step is heat-pump boilerplate. The unit has no run capacitor, so the 'test capacitor' maintenance step is generic."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"LRA, -024 suction valve size (7/8 or 3/4), per-size SEER2, and which factory charge (15 or 30 ft) a given serial shipped with."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML14KP1 (Merit single-stage heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Merit ML14KP1 split heat pump, single-stage scroll, vertical discharge, R-454B (A2L), SEER2 up to 17.0 / HSPF2 up to 8.2. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (18,000-58,000 Btuh), 208/230-1. Indoor check/expansion valve plus an outdoor expansion valve for heating. The documents disagree on the DEFROST BOARD (EHB: time/temperature; UI and II: A108 demand) and on the charge basis (15 vs 30 ft) - see flags. Read the board fitted in the unit.","match":["ML14KP1","ML14KP1-018-230","ML14KP1-024-230","ML14KP1-030-230","ML14KP1-036-230","ML14KP1-042-230","ML14KP1-048-230","ML14KP1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox ML14KP1 Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211064 (Oct 2024); Lennox ML14KP1 Unit Information, Corp. 100108 (Mar 18 2026); Lennox ML14KP1 Installation Instructions 508733-01 (03/2026; earlier 6/2025 edition, same form number)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML14KP1-024-230A01)","value":"ML = Merit tier · 14 = nominal SEER2 class · K = R-454B · P = heat pump · 1 = single-stage · -024 = cooling capacity in thousands of Btuh (018 = 1.5 ton … 060 = 5 ton) · -230 = 208/230 V, 1 phase, 60 Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = minor revision (E14 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B","value":"018: 4 lb 7 oz · 024: 5 lb 3 oz · 030: 6 lb 7 oz · 036: 7 lb 2 oz · 042: 8 lb 5 oz · 048: 8 lb 6 oz · 060: 9 lb 6 oz (E14 p7-8; U14 p10-11)","key":true},{"label":"Line length the charge covers - CONFLICT","value":"E14 p7 footnote 1: 15 ft. U14 p39: 30 ft, adding 3 oz for every 5 ft over 30 ft on a 3/8 in. liquid line, or subtracting the same when shorter. Always follow the unit charging label","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling to the unit charging label; charge liquid only (I14 p18). Use cooling mode at 60 °F outdoor and above, heating mode below 60 °F (U14 p39)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling targets","value":"See the unit charging label. U14 p39 Table 2 is labeled 'ML14KP1 / EL16KP1' and its total charge minus added charge does not equal the ML14KP1 nameplate charge (024 row: 6 lb 11 oz - 15 oz = 5 lb 12 oz, nameplate 5 lb 3 oz), so its targets are not used here. I14 Table 1 omits the 018-030 rows","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Check/expansion valve at the indoor coil: kit 26Z70 for 018-036, 26Z71 for 042 / 048, 26Z72 for 060. The outdoor unit has its own expansion valve for heating (E14 p3, p7-8)"},{"label":"Evacuation","value":"Pull to 23,000 microns, break with nitrogen, then evacuate until it holds 500 microns for 20 min (I14 p14)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (E14 p7-8)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 9.7 / 15 / 7.2 / 47 / 0.7 · 024: 13.6 / 20 / 10.3 / 60.2 / 0.7 · 030: 16.6 / 25 / 12.5 / 67 / 1.0 · 036: 22.2 / 35 / 16.7 / 93.5 / 1.4 · 042: 22.3 / 35 / 15.8 / 96 / 2.6 · 048: 30.6 / 50 / 22.4 / 126 / 2.6 · 060: 32.2 / 50 / 23.7 / 157 / 2.6","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Rating not published - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections (liquid x vapor)","value":"018-030: 3/8 x 3/4 in. · 036-048: 3/8 x 7/8 in. · 060: 3/8 x 1-1/8 in. Over 50 ft, contact Lennox or use Corp. 9351-L9 (U14 p16; I14 p7)"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches & protection","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch S4 (liquid line)","value":"Opens at 590 ±15 psig (U14 p26), resets at 418 ±15 psig (I14 p19)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch S87","value":"Opens at 25 ±5 psig, closes at 40 ±5 psig (U14 p26). Ignored during defrost and for 90 s after it, for 90 s after compressor start, and for 10 min when it is below 15 °F outdoors (U14 p29). 5 trips on either switch = lockout (U14 p32)","key":true},{"label":"Compressor internal vacuum protector","value":"Unloads below 20 psig (hissing) and resets above 40 psig - do not condemn the compressor (U14 p26)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-installed on 036-060, optional on 018-030 (E14 p4-5). Its thermostat closes at 45 °F and opens at 65 °F (U14 p26)"}]},{"title":"Defrost - the documents disagree on the board","rows":[{"label":"U14 / I14: demand defrost board A108","value":"Termination jumper P1: 50 / 70 / 90 / 100 °F, factory 50 °F; with no jumper the board uses 90 °F. Nominal defrost-time jumper P3: 60 / 100 / 140 / 165 s, factory 140 s. DELAY jumper P5 stops the compressor for 30 s going into and out of defrost; units ship with it installed. Maximum defrost 14 min (U14 p27-31; I14 p19)","key":true},{"label":"A108 frost-accumulation timing","value":"Counted while the coil is below 37 °F. Initial target 90 min, adjusted up or down by 30 min based on the previous defrost. Below 10 °F outdoors the target becomes 360 min; it resets to 90 min above 15 °F. 2 consecutive low-pressure switch trips in heating force a defrost (U14 p30)"},{"label":"E14 p5: time/temperature board","value":"Describes a time/temperature board with 30 / 60 / 90-minute intervals below 42 °F coil temperature, factory 90 min. Read the board fitted in the unit before using either description"},{"label":"LED codes, green DS2 / red DS1 (U14 p32; I14 p20; I16 p20)","value":"Both slow flash together = normal · slow flash alternating = 5-min anti-short-cycle delay · fast flash together = ambient sensor fault · fast flash alternating = coil sensor fault · ON / ON = board failure · OFF / slow = low-pressure fault · OFF / ON = low-pressure lockout · slow / OFF = high-pressure fault · ON / OFF = high-pressure lockout. Discharge-sensor codes point to the 10K resistor that stands in for the sensor"}]},{"title":"Operating range","rows":[{"label":"Cooling / heating limits","value":"Cooling down to 45 °F as shipped, or 30 °F with low ambient kit 54M89. Heating up to 75 °F without mild weather kit 11B97 (E14 p5-6). The optional cut-off 45F08 stops cooling below 35 °F (E14 p5)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation control are required on every system (E14 p4; E15 p3)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft²)","value":"10 / 15 / 20 / 25 / 30 lb → 149.9 / 224.9 / 299.9 / 374.8 / 449.8 ft². Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft (I14 p5; I16 p5)"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb needs 135 cfm, 10 lb 271 cfm, 20 lb 541 cfm, 30 lb 812 cfm (I16 p5)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Defrost board: EHB vs UI / II","body":"E14 (Form 211064) p5 describes a time/temperature board with 30 / 60 / 90-minute intervals below 42 °F coil temperature, factory 90 min. U14 (Corp. 100108) and I14 (508733-01) describe the A108 demand board with P1 / P3 / P5 jumpers. Read the board fitted in the unit."},{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"E14 p7 footnote 1 says the factory charge covers 15 ft; U14 p39 says 30 ft with 3 oz per 5 ft. Always follow the unit charging label."},{"title":"U14 charging table is labeled 'ML14KP1 / EL16KP1' and does not add up","body":"Its total charge minus its added charge does not equal the ML14KP1 nameplate charge (024 row: 6 lb 11 oz - 15 oz = 5 lb 12 oz vs 5 lb 3 oz on the nameplate). Its subcooling targets are unverified - use the unit charging label. U14 also contains copied pages: its model decoder shows an ML13KC1 air conditioner and its dimensions page lists ML14KC1 (U14 p8-9)."},{"title":"Draft text in the II","body":"I14 still carries a draft editing note '[BE1]' next to the defrost-time jumper text."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Capacitor rating, the ML14KP1 charging-label subcooling tables, and the 'Installation and Service Procedures' manual (not found)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML16KP2 (Merit two-stage heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Merit ML16KP2 split heat pump, two-stage scroll (24 V DC solenoid inside the compressor switches stages), vertical discharge, R-454B (A2L), SEER2 up to 17.5 / HSPF2 up to 8.5. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (22,400-58,000 Btuh), 208/230-1. A108 demand defrost board. No Unit Information manual was found - figures are from the EHB and the Installation Instructions.","match":["ML16KP2","ML16KP2-024-230","ML16KP2-036-230","ML16KP2-048-230","ML16KP2-060-230"],"source":"Lennox ML16KP2 Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211270 (June 2026); Lennox ML16KP2 Installation Instructions 508818-01 (03/2026); frost-accumulation timing from the ML14KP1 Unit Information, Corp. 100108 (Mar 18 2026)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML16KP2-048-230A01)","value":"ML = Merit tier · 16 = nominal SEER2 class · K = R-454B · P = heat pump · 2 = two-stage · -048 = cooling capacity in thousands of Btuh · -230 = 208/230 V, 1 phase, 60 Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = minor revision (E16 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B (covers 30 ft of line)","value":"024: 7 lb 7 oz · 036: 8 lb 4 oz · 048: 10 lb 10 oz · 060: 11 lb 1 oz (E16 p7)","key":true},{"label":"Added charge per foot","value":"Not published. See the unit charging label (E16 p7; I16 p18)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling to the unit charging label; charge liquid only (I16 p18). Targets: see the unit charging label (no ML16KP2 label table was found)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor check/expansion valve: 26Z70 for 024 / 036, 26Z71 for 048, 26Z72 for 060 (E16 p7)"},{"label":"Line set (liquid x vapor)","value":"024: 3/8 x 3/4 in. · 036 / 048: 3/8 x 7/8 in. · 060: 3/8 x 1-1/8 in. Over 50 ft, see Corp. 9351-L9 (I16 p7)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (E16 p7)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 15.4 / 25 / 10.3 / 62 / 2.6 · 036: 21.3 / 35 / 14.9 / 90 / 2.6 · 048: 25.5 / 40 / 18.3 / 138 / 2.6 · 060: 34.1 / 50 / 25.2 / 147.3 / 2.6","key":true},{"label":"Staging","value":"A 24 V DC solenoid inside the compressor switches stages (E16 p4). I16 p19 says the product is 'only single stage' - it is two-stage"},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Rating not published - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches & protection","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 590 ±15 psig, resets at 418 ±15 psig (I16 p19)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Closes above 40 ±5 psig (I16 p19). The opening set point is not published - see the switch"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-installed on 036-060 (E16 p4-7)"}]},{"title":"Defrost (A108 demand board, same as ML14KP1)","rows":[{"label":"Jumpers","value":"P1 termination 50 / 70 / 90 / 100 °F, factory 50 °F (90 °F with no jumper). P3 nominal defrost time 60 / 100 / 140 / 165 s, factory 140 s. DELAY jumper installed at the factory (I16 p19; E16 p5)","key":true},{"label":"Frost-accumulation timing","value":"Published only in the ML14KP1 Unit Information: counted while the coil is below 37 °F, initial target 90 min adjusted by 30 min, 360 min below 10 °F, back to 90 min above 15 °F; maximum defrost 14 min (U14 p30)"},{"label":"LED codes, green DS2 / red DS1 (I16 p20)","value":"Both slow flash together = normal · slow flash alternating = 5-min anti-short-cycle delay · fast flash together = ambient sensor fault · fast flash alternating = coil sensor fault · ON / ON = board failure · OFF / slow = low-pressure fault · OFF / ON = low-pressure lockout · slow / OFF = high-pressure fault · ON / OFF = high-pressure lockout"}]},{"title":"Operating range","rows":[{"label":"Cooling / heating limits","value":"Cooling down to 45 °F, or 30 °F with kit 54M89. Heating up to 75 °F without kit 11B97 (E16 p4-7)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation control are required on every system (E14 p4; E15 p3)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (total charge → ft²)","value":"10 / 15 / 20 / 25 / 30 lb → 149.9 / 224.9 / 299.9 / 374.8 / 449.8 ft². Multiply by the altitude factor: 1.12 at 5,250 ft, 1.4 at 10,500 ft (I14 p5; I16 p5)"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb needs 135 cfm, 10 lb 271 cfm, 20 lb 541 cfm, 30 lb 812 cfm (I16 p5)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Factory charge covers 30 ft on this model","body":"E16 (Form 211270) p7 prints the charge for a 30 ft line set. The per-foot adder is not published - see the unit charging label before adding or removing refrigerant."},{"title":"Draft text in the II","body":"I16 (508818-01) still carries a draft editing note '[BE1]' next to the defrost-time jumper text, and says the product is 'only single stage' - the ML16KP2 is two-stage."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Unit Information manual (none found), low-pressure switch opening set point, charging-label subcooling tables, added charge per foot, capacitor rating."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML15KSPV (Merit side-discharge inverter heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Merit ML15KSPV side-discharge split heat pump, variable-capacity (inverter) twin rotary, R-454B (A2L), SEER2 up to 17.7 / HSPF2 up to 9.6. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (17,900-55,000 Btuh), 208/230-1. Electronic expansion valve in the outdoor unit; rated only with an indoor TXV. Flare connections. Charge mode and forced defrost are DIP switches on the service board; the 2-segment display shows live subcooling in cooling. No Unit Information manual was found.","match":["ML15KSPV","ML15KSPV-018-230","ML15KSPV-024-230","ML15KSPV-030-230","ML15KSPV-036-230","ML15KSPV-042-230","ML15KSPV-048-230","ML15KSPV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox ML15KSPV Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211294 (June 2026); Lennox ML15KSPV Installation Instructions 508844-01 (09/2026, supersedes 06/2026)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML15KSPV-048-230A01)","value":"ML = Merit tier · 15 = nominal SEER2 class · K = R-454B · S = side discharge · P = heat pump · V = variable capacity · -048 = cooling capacity in thousands of Btuh · -230 = 208/230 V, 1 phase, 60 Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = minor revision (E15 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B (covers 15 ft)","value":"018: 3 lb 4 oz · 024: 3 lb 12 oz · 030: 4 lb 8 oz · 036: 4 lb 8 oz · 042: 6 lb 11 oz · 048: 7 lb 6 oz · 060: 8 lb 1 oz (E15 p6-7). I15 Table 3 prints decimal ounces: 024 3 lb 11.6 oz · 030 / 036 4 lb 8.3 oz · 042 6 lb 11.4 oz · 048 7 lb 5.5 oz · 060 8 lb 1.1 oz (I15 p18) - the EHB rounds them","key":true},{"label":"Added charge","value":"0.55 oz/ft (E15 p6), or 2.75 oz per 5 ft over 15 ft; subtract the same when the line is under 15 ft (I15 p40)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Put the unit in charge mode with DIP SW1 on the service board (I15 p33, p40). Cooling: the 2-segment display shows live subcooling; compare it after 10 min against Table 10. Heating: measure subcooling with gauges (I15 p32)","key":true},{"label":"Example target","value":"048 with CBK45UHET-048 = 11 °F subcooling in cooling (±1), 5 °F in heating (±3), 0 lb 4 oz added (I15 p35). Other matches: I15 Table 10 / the unit charging label"},{"label":"Metering / oil","value":"Electronic expansion valve in the outdoor unit; rated only with an indoor TXV (E15 p3; I15 p34). POE oil 30.4 oz (018-036) · 29.4 oz (042 / 048) · 47.3 oz (060) (E15 p6-7)"},{"label":"Pressures","value":"Pressure test at 160 psig; maximum allowable pressure 640 psig (I15 p4)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / fan RLA (E15 p6-7)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018 & 024: 18 / 20 / 13.0 / 1.0 · 030 & 036: 20 / 30 / 14.5 / 1.2 · 042 & 048: 26 / 35 / 19.0 / 1.5 · 060: 32 / 40 / 24.0 / 1.5. LRA not published (inverter)","key":true}]},{"title":"Line set (flare connections)","rows":[{"label":"Sizes","value":"Liquid 3/8 in. Suction 3/4 in. on 018-036 and 7/8 in. on 042-060 (I15 p18). 036 CONFLICT: E15 footnote 2 says 5/8 to 7/8 in.; the E15 spec table and I15 Table 3 say 3/4 in."},{"label":"Length","value":"018-036: 150 ft actual / 180 ft equivalent · 042-060: 100 ft actual / 120 ft equivalent. Maximum vapor riser, liquid lift and height difference: 50 ft (I15 p18)"},{"label":"Flare torque","value":"3/8 in. 30.1 ft-lb · 5/8 in. 44.3 ft-lb · 3/4 in. 73.8 ft-lb (I15 p21)"}]},{"title":"Switches, defrost & codes","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 590 ±15 psig, resets at 418 ±15 psig (I15 p41). The low-pressure switch set point is not published","key":true},{"label":"Defrost","value":"Starts automatically on coil frost; the outdoor fan stops during defrost (E15 p3). SW1-4 switched OFF→ON forces a manual defrost (heating mode only). If left ON the unit runs 'strong defrost' - a shorter interval and a longer defrost, meant for humid areas (I15 p33). No intervals or termination temperatures are published. Dual-fuel installs need a Defrost Tempering Kit (I15 p30)","key":true},{"label":"Codes and diagnostics","value":"The alarm list is on the control-panel cover, not in the manual (I15 p31). Diagnostic mode steps through: size, mode (Co / He / oF / ol / dE), Hz, fan step, EEV opening, target and actual refrigerant temperatures, Tao / Tc / Te / Ts / Td, compressor amps, module temperature, software version, fault code (I15 p36)"}]},{"title":"Operating range","rows":[{"label":"Limits","value":"Cooling 40-125 °F; heating 0-75 °F (E15 p6; I15 p10). The unit stops below -22 °F. Keep power on for 12 h after any outage at or below 32 °F (I15 p10). Energize the crankcase heater 24 h before start-up (I15 p39)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation control are required (E15 p3)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin","value":"Own table: 4 lb → 59 ft², up to 11 lb → 164 ft². It assumes supply and return openings more than 2.2 m high (I15 p8)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"036 suction size conflicts","body":"E15 (Form 211294) footnote 2 says 5/8 to 7/8 in.; the E15 spec table and I15 (508844-01) Table 3 say 3/4 in. Measure the flare fitting."},{"title":"EHB and manual differ slightly","body":"E15 rounds the charges that I15 prints to a tenth of an ounce. E15 says codes show 'on the indoor unit', while I15 says the code list is on the outdoor control cover."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Low-pressure switch set point, LRA, capacitor, the fault-code list, defrost intervals and termination temperatures, and the Unit Information manual (none found)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL16KP1 (Elite single-stage heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Elite EL16KP1 split heat pump, fixed-speed scroll, R-454B (A2L), 1.5-5 ton, SEER2 up to 17.0. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060, 208/230-1. Indoor TXV plus outdoor expansion valve for heating. Classic A108 demand-defrost board with DS1 / DS2 LED codes. The EHB lists both a 15 ft and a 30 ft charge - read the nameplate.","match":["EL16KP1","EL16KP1-018-230","EL16KP1-024-230","EL16KP1-030-230","EL16KP1-036-230","EL16KP1-042-230","EL16KP1-048-230","EL16KP1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox EL16KP1 Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211061 (9/2025); Lennox Installation Instructions 508406-01 (6/2025); Lennox Unit Information Corp. 100195 (3/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL16KP1-036-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 16 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · P = heat pump outdoor unit (standard) · 1 = single-stage · 036 = size · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · A = ratings revision letter · 01 = revision number (EHB16 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B, for a 15 ft line set / for a 30 ft line set","value":"018: 4 lb 7 oz / 5 lb 0 oz · 024: 5 lb 3 oz / 5 lb 12 oz · 030: 6 lb 7 oz / 7 lb 0 oz · 036: 7 lb 2 oz / 7 lb 11 oz · 042: 8 lb 5 oz / 8 lb 14 oz · 048: 8 lb 6 oz / 8 lb 15 oz · 060: 9 lb 6 oz / 9 lb 15 oz (EHB16 p8-9). The nameplate says which one your unit shipped with","key":true},{"label":"Charge adjustment - basis unclear","value":"3 oz per 5 ft of 3/8 in. liquid line (UI16 p39). The UI charging label says the nameplate charge is based on 30 ft; the EHB lists both 15 ft and 30 ft charges. Read the nameplate before adjusting","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling, with targets per indoor match on the unit charging label (heat ±5 °F, cool ±1 °F). Use cooling mode at 60 °F outdoor or above, heating mode below 60 °F (II16 p17; UI16 p39 Table 2). Targets: see the unit charging label","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor TXV 26Z70 (018-036), 26Z71 (042-048), 26Z72 (060). Outdoor expansion valve for heating (EHB16 p3, p12)"},{"label":"Line set","value":"3/8 in. liquid on all sizes. Vapor 3/4 in. (018-030), 7/8 in. (036-048), 1-1/8 in. (060). Rated 15-50 ft; over 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9 (II16 Table 1)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (EHB16 p8-9)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 9.7 / 15 / 7.2 / 47 / 0.7 · 024: 13.6 / 20 / 10.3 / 60.2 / 0.7 · 030: 16.6 / 25 / 12.5 / 67 / 1.0 · 036: 22.2 / 35 / 16.7 / 93.5 / 1.4 · 042: 22.3 / 35 / 15.8 / 96 / 2.6 · 048: 30.6 / 50 / 22.4 / 126 / 2.6 · 060: 32.2 / 50 / 23.7 / 157 / 2.6","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Rating not published - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches & protection","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 590 ±15 psig, resets at 418 ±15 psig (II16 p18)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 25 ±5 psig, closes at 40 ±5 psig. Ignored during defrost (UI16 p26)","key":true},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"Factory-installed on 036-060. Its thermostat closes at 45 °F and opens at 65 °F (EHB16 p5; UI16 p26)"}]},{"title":"Defrost (A108 demand defrost)","rows":[{"label":"Jumpers","value":"P1 termination 50 / 70 / 90 / 100 °F, factory 50 °F; with no shunt the default is 90 °F. P3 nominal defrost time 140 s factory (P3-1/2), 100 s (2/3), 60 s (3/4), 165 s (4/5); no shunt = 140 s. P5 DELAY: 30 s compressor-off shift delay, jumper installed at the factory (II16 p18; UI16 p30)","key":true},{"label":"Frost accumulation","value":"Counted while the coil is below 37 °F, starting at 90 min. Adapts in 30-min steps (70% / 130% bands) and resets to 30 min after a 14-min maximum defrost. Below 10 °F outdoor it is set to 360 min, returning to 90 min above 15 °F. Two consecutive LP trips in heat start a defrost. The coil probe sits between the TXV outlet and the distributor (UI16 p30)"},{"label":"LED codes, DS2 green / DS1 red (UI16 p32 Table 4)","value":"Both slow-simultaneous = normal · alternating slow = 5-min anti-short-cycle · simultaneous fast = ambient sensor · alternating fast = coil sensor · both on = board failure · off / slow = LP fault · off / on = LP lockout · slow / off = HP fault · on / off = HP lockout · slow / on = discharge-line temperature fault · fast / on = discharge-line temperature lockout · off / fast = discharge sensor fault · fast / off = discharge sensor lockout. 5 strikes on one code = lockout; the TEST pins clear it"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required. Lennox RDS kits are 27A02 (24 V) and 27A03 (communicating) (II wiring pages)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (sea level, 10 / 20 / 30 lb)","value":"149.9 / 299.9 / 449.8 ft² (II16 p4). Altitude factor 1.12 at 5,250 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm, 30 lb = 812 cfm (II16 p4)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The unit's charging label and rating plate govern: Lennox documents disagree on whether the factory charge covers 15 ft or 30 ft.","body":"EHB 211061 p8-9 lists both a 15 ft and a 30 ft charge per size, but the UI 100195 charging label says the nameplate charge is based on 30 ft. Read the nameplate before adjusting."},{"title":"Copy-paste errors in the EL16KP1 UI","body":"The Corp. 100195 LED table text refers to 'ML14KP1', and p8 contains an EL19KPV spec table. The size table above comes from EHB 211061."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"A minimum heating ambient for the EL16KP1, capacitor rating, and per-match subcooling targets (charging label only)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL19KPV (Elite variable-capacity heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Elite EL19KPV split heat pump, variable-capacity (inverter) rotary compressor, R-454B (A2L), 2-5 ton, SEER2 19.5 / HSPF2 9.0. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060, 208/230-1. Outdoor TXV; 7-segment Lennox communicating control with E-codes, CHRG MODE jumper and unit code. This is a HEAT PUMP - not the ML195 furnace that shares the 'EL19' letters.","match":["EL19KPV","EL19KPV-024-230","EL19KPV-036-230","EL19KPV-048-230","EL19KPV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox EL19KPV Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211062 (9/2025); Lennox Installation Instructions 508605-01 (5/2026); Lennox Unit Information Corp. 100106 (6/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL19KPV-024-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 19 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · P = heat pump outdoor unit (standard) · V = variable capacity · 024 = size · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · A = ratings revision letter · 01 = revision number"},{"label":"Unit codes","value":"76 / 77 / 78 / 79 for 024 / 036 / 048 / 060. E443 = wrong unit code after a board swap - program it from the push-button PU menu (UI19 p42-49)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B, for 15 ft / for 30 ft","value":"024: 8 lb 6 oz / 8 lb 15 oz · 036: 7 lb 15 oz / 8 lb 8 oz · 048: 8 lb 13 oz / 9 lb 6 oz · 060: 9 lb 5 oz / 9 lb 14 oz (EHB19 p9). The nameplate says which one your unit shipped with","key":true},{"label":"Weigh-in adder","value":"0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in. liquid line (0.40 for 5/16 in., 1.00 for 1/2 in.) (II19 p8)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling at 100% capacity, using the CHRG MODE jumper (60-min limit). Targets are per indoor match on the charging sticker - for example, -024 with CBK48MVT-018/024 is heat 31 ±5 °F and cool 14 ±1 °F (UI19 p85-90). Other matches: see the unit charging label","key":true},{"label":"Line set","value":"3/8 in. liquid. Vapor 3/4 / 7/8 / 7/8 / 1-1/8 in. (II19 Table 2). Limits 180 ft equivalent, 150 ft linear, 60 ft liquid lift, 60 ft vapor riser (II19 p8-9)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor input amps / fan FLA (EHB19 p9)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 17.7 / 25 / 12.1 / 2.6 · 036: 23 / 35 / 16.3 / 2.6 · 048: 33.1 / 50 / 24.4 / 2.6 · 060: 39.2 / 60 / 28.5 / 3.6. LRA not published (inverter)","key":true}]},{"title":"Pressures & setpoints","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 590 psig, closes at 418 psig (UI19 p43-44, p62)","key":true},{"label":"Low pressure (emulated by the suction transducer) - CONFLICT","value":"E410 / E411: cut-out 35 psig, cut-in 80 psig (UI19 p43-44). UI19 p62 gives 25 / 40 instead"},{"label":"Non-communicating thermostat setpoints","value":"Cooling suction targets: Normal 135 psig, Comfort 125 psig. Heating Comfort liquid target: 425 psig (UI19 p36)"}]},{"title":"Defrost","rows":[{"label":"Frost accumulation","value":"Counted while the coil is below 35 °F, starting at 90 min, with 80% / 120% bands. Below 10 °F it is set to 360 min. Maximum defrost is 14 min (UI19 p36-37)","key":true},{"label":"Target defrost time","value":"120 / 125 / 130 / 135 s for 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (UI19 p37)"},{"label":"Termination","value":"50 °F default (50 / 70 / 90 / 100). Set it at the S40 thermostat; on 24 V thermostats use the board jumper (UI19 p37). Forced defrost: push-button to '-', then 'd' (UI19 p38)"}]},{"title":"Codes & operating range","rows":[{"label":"E-codes (display) and inverter red/green LED flash codes","value":"E410 / E411 low pressure · E412 / E413 high pressure · E416 coil sensor · E422 / E442 top-cap switch · E424 liquid sensor · E427-E441 inverter faults · E443 wrong unit code · E601 low-temperature lockout (UI19 p42-49)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cooling down to 0 °F. In heating the unit will not start at or below -4 °F; if already running it continues to -15 °F (EHB19 p6)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required. Lennox RDS kits are 27A02 (24 V) and 27A03 (communicating) (II wiring pages)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (sea level, 10 / 20 / 30 lb)","value":"149.9 / 299.9 / 449.8 ft² (II19 p5). Altitude factor 1.12 at 5,250 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm, 30 lb = 812 cfm (II16 p4)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Low-pressure set points conflict","body":"E410 gives 35 / 80 psig (UI19 p43-44) but UI19 p62 gives 25 / 40. Which one the firmware uses is not confirmed."},{"title":"Charge only at 100% capacity","body":"Use the CHRG MODE jumper; readings at part speed are not valid. Per-match subcooling targets are on the charging sticker."},{"title":"Both a 15 ft and a 30 ft charge are printed","body":"EHB 211062 p9 lists both. Read the nameplate before adjusting."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"LRA (inverter) and capacitor."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL21KLV (Elite cold-climate variable-capacity heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Elite EL21KLV cold-climate split heat pump, variable-capacity (inverter) rotary compressor plus outdoor EEV board, R-454B (A2L), 2-5 ton, SEER2 20.5 / HSPF2 10.0, ENERGY STAR Cold Climate. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060, 208/230-1. Same control family as the EL19KPV (7-segment E-codes, CHRG MODE jumper, unit code) plus EEV-board codes E480-E487. L = Cold Climate (Low Ambient).","match":["EL21KLV","EL21KLV-024-230","EL21KLV-036-230","EL21KLV-048-230","EL21KLV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox EL21KLV Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211063 (3/2025); Lennox Installation Instructions 508493-01 (6/2025); Lennox Unit Information 100105 (3/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL21KLV-048-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 21 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · L = Cold Climate (Low Ambient) heat pump · V = variable capacity · 048 = size · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · A = ratings revision letter · 01 = revision number"},{"label":"Unit codes","value":"92 / 93 / 94 / 95 for 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (UI21). E443 = wrong unit code after a board swap - program it from the push-button PU menu"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B, 15 ft","value":"024: 9 lb 10 oz · 036: 9 lb 14 oz · 048: 12 lb 11 oz · 060: 14 lb 2 oz (EHB21 p8). For 30 ft, UI21 p3 lists 10 lb 3 oz for the 024 only. The nameplate says which one your unit shipped with","key":true},{"label":"Adder","value":"0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in. liquid line (II21 p8)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Subcooling at 100% capacity using the CHRG MODE jumper. Per-match targets are on the charging label - see the unit charging label","key":true},{"label":"Line set","value":"180 ft equivalent, 150 ft linear, 60 ft lift (II21 p8). 060 vapor connection CONFLICT: UI21 p3 says 7/8 in., the EHB says 1-1/8 in. - not confirmed, measure the valve"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor input amps / fan FLA (EHB21 p8)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 15.0 / 20 / 9.9 / 2.6 · 036: 20.1 / 30 / 14.0 / 2.6 · 048: 26.9 / 45 / 19.5 / 2.6 · 060: 32.5 / 50 / 24.0 / 2.6. LRA not published (inverter)","key":true}]},{"title":"Pressures, defrost & operating range","rows":[{"label":"Pressure protection","value":"HP 590 / 418 psig. LP (transducer) 35 / 80 psig - consistent across the EL21KLV documents (UI21 p46, p68)","key":true},{"label":"Defrost","value":"Same algorithm as the EL19KPV (frost accumulation below 35 °F from 90 min, 360 min below 10 °F, 14 min maximum). Target defrost time 100 / 133 / 105 / 102 s for 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (UI21 p35, p59)","key":true},{"label":"S40-adjustable defrost","value":"Adder and reducer 5-60 min (default 30), frost accumulation 30-360 min (default 90), nominal defrost time 20-840 s (UI21 p59)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Heating to -15 °F. E601 low-temperature lockout at -4 °F / -15 °F (EHB21 p5; UI21 p50)"}]},{"title":"Codes","rows":[{"label":"Control E-codes","value":"Same E-code set as the EL19KPV (E410 / E411 low pressure, E412 / E413 high pressure, E416, E422 / E442, E424, E427-E441 inverter, E443, E601) plus E444 (reversing-valve position mismatch)"},{"label":"EEV board","value":"E480 no communication · E482 suction sensor (limited to 70 Hz) · E484 / E485 coil current · E486 superheat below 3 °F for 10 min · E487 superheat above 40 °F for 10 min. The EEV coil reads 40-50 Ω from each lead to COM (UI21 p41, p44, p50, p53)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required. Lennox RDS kits are 27A02 (24 V) and 27A03 (communicating) (II wiring pages)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (sea level, 10 / 20 / 30 lb)","value":"150.9 / 301.9 / 452.8 ft² - the EL21KLV table differs from the other models (II21 p3). Altitude factor 1.12 at 5,250 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm, 30 lb = 812 cfm (II16 p4)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"060 vapor connection size not confirmed","body":"UI 100105 p3 says 7/8 in.; EHB 211063 says 1-1/8 in. Measure the valve. The UI also gives two EEV step counts (480 on p44 vs 550 on p41)."},{"title":"Only the 024 has a published 30 ft charge","body":"EHB 211063 p8 prints 15 ft charges; UI 100105 p3 lists a 30 ft charge (10 lb 3 oz) for the 024 only. Read the nameplate before adjusting."},{"title":"Charge only at 100% capacity","body":"Use the CHRG MODE jumper; readings at part speed are not valid."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"LRA (inverter), capacitor, 30 ft charges for 036-060."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SL22KLV (Signature cold-climate variable-capacity heat pump, R-454B, communicating only)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Dave Lennox Signature SL22KLV cold-climate split heat pump, variable-capacity scroll plus outdoor EEV and liquid injection, R-454B (A2L), 2-5 ton, SEER2 21.1 / HSPF2 10.5, ENERGY STAR Cold Climate. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060, 208/230-1. COMMUNICATING ONLY: requires an S40 thermostat and a Lennox communicating variable-speed indoor unit. There is no charge-mode jumper - 100% capacity comes from the S40 'Cooling - Maximum Rate Test'. The documents disagree on the heating limit (see flags).","match":["SL22KLV","SL22KLV-024-230","SL22KLV-036-230","SL22KLV-048-230","SL22KLV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox SL22KLV Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211065 (1/2025); Lennox Installation Instructions 508501-01 (6/2025); Lennox Unit Information Corp. 100131 (6/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (SL22KLV-024-230A01)","value":"SL = Dave Lennox Signature · 22 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · L = Cold Climate (Low Ambient) heat pump · V = variable capacity · 024 = size · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · A = ratings revision letter · 01 = revision number"},{"label":"Unit codes / controls","value":"84 / 85 / 86 / 87 for 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (UI22 p36, p49, p91). Communicating only - S40 plus a Lennox communicating variable-speed indoor unit (EHB22 p2, p6)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B, 15 ft","value":"024: 10 lb 13 oz · 036: 16 lb 13 oz · 048: 16 lb 13 oz · 060: 16 lb 6 oz (EHB22 p8). 30 ft charges not confirmed - read the nameplate","key":true},{"label":"Adder","value":"3 oz per 5 ft of 3/8 in. line, adjusted from 15 ft (II22 p25)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Charge at 100% using the S40 'Cooling - Maximum Rate Test'. There is no charge-mode jumper, only a PUMP DOWN jumper (II22 p18, p25). Per-match subcooling targets: see the unit charging label","key":true},{"label":"Line set","value":"180 ft equivalent, 150 ft linear, 60 ft lift, the same as the EL21KLV. Vapor 7/8 in. (024-048), 1-1/8 in. (060) (II22 p9-10)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / inverter input current (EHB22 p8)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 15.5 / 25 / 10.3 A · 036: 23.5 / 40 / 16.63 A · 048: 31.8 / 50 / 23.4 A · 060: 34.8 / 60 / 25.7 A. LRA not published (inverter)","key":true}]},{"title":"Pressures, defrost & operating range","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"590 / 418 psig (UI22 p63)","key":true},{"label":"Low pressure (transducer) - CONFLICT","value":"E410 gives 35 / 80 psig, but UI22 p63 gives 25 / 90"},{"label":"Heating limit - CONFLICT","value":"The EHB says heating down to -20 °F; UI22 p47 E601 says it locks out at -4 °F and runs only to -15 °F","key":true},{"label":"Defrost","value":"Target defrost time 100 / 120 / 190 / 200 s for 024 / 036 / 048 / 060. Termination is set only at the S40 (default 50 °F) (UI22 p54)"}]},{"title":"Codes","rows":[{"label":"E-codes","value":"As EL21KLV (E410 / E411 low pressure, E412 / E413 high pressure, E416, E422 / E442, E424, E427-E441 inverter, E443 wrong unit code, E444 reversing valve, E480-E487 EEV board, E601 low-temperature lockout) plus E481 (discharge pressure transducer) and E490 (injection EEV coil)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS (refrigerant detection)","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required. Lennox RDS kits are 27A02 (24 V) and 27A03 (communicating) (II wiring pages)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin (sea level, 10 / 20 / 30 lb)","value":"149.9 / 299.9 / 449.8 ft² (II22 p3). Altitude factor 1.12 at 5,250 ft"},{"label":"Minimum mitigation airflow Qmin","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm, 30 lb = 812 cfm (II16 p4)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Heating limit: EHB vs UI","body":"EHB 211065 says heating down to -20 °F; UI 100131 p47 (E601) says the unit locks out at -4 °F and runs only to -15 °F. Do not promise -20 °F operation from the EHB alone."},{"title":"Low-pressure set points conflict","body":"E410 gives 35 / 80 psig but UI 100131 p63 gives 25 / 90. Which one the firmware uses is not confirmed."},{"title":"Charge only at 100% capacity","body":"Use the S40 Cooling - Maximum Rate Test; there is no CHRG MODE jumper on this unit."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"30 ft charges, LRA (inverter), capacitor, per-match subcooling targets (charging label only)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL18KSLV (Elite side-discharge cold-climate inverter heat pump, R-454B)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Elite EL18KSLV side-discharge cold-climate split heat pump, variable-capacity (inverter) rotary, R-454B (A2L). Sizes 024 / 036 / 060 (the 060 can be DIP-set to 4 ton), 208/230-1. A different platform from the top-discharge KPV / KLV line: 2-digit error display, DIP switches, 24 V control only, flare connections, outdoor EEV. The documents disagree on the factory CHARGE and on the CHARGING METHOD (see flags).","match":["EL18KSLV","EL18KSLV-024","EL18KSLV-036","EL18KSLV-060","EL18KSLV-024-230","EL18KSLV-036-230","EL18KSLV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox EL18KSLV Product Specifications (EHB), Form 211074 (3/2025); Lennox Installation Instructions 508700-01 (12/2024); Lennox Unit Information 100203 (5/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL18KSLV-060-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 18 = nominal SEER2 · K = R-454B · S = side-discharge cabinet · L = Cold Climate (Low Ambient) heat pump · V = variable capacity · 060 = size (024 / 036 / 060; the 060 can be DIP-set to 4 ton) · 230 = 208/230-1-60"},{"label":"O/B setting","value":"SW5-7 must match the thermostat: OFF = O (default), ON = B (II18 p23)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-454B, 15 ft - CONFLICT","value":"EHB18 p6: 024: 3 lb 9 oz · 036: 5 lb 9 oz · 060: 7 lb 8 oz. II and UI: 62 / 94 / 125 oz (3 lb 14 oz / 5 lb 14 oz / 7 lb 13 oz). Use the rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Adder - CONFLICT","value":"0.55 oz/ft beyond 15 ft (EHB18 p6 unit table). The generic II figure shows 0.60 oz/ft"},{"label":"Charging method - CONFLICT","value":"UI18 p68 says 'weigh-in is the ONLY way to charge'. II18 p22-25 gives subcooling targets per indoor match (heat ±3 °F, cool ±1 °F) - for example, the 2-ton with CBK48MV-018/024 is heat 6 / cool 5 - with charge mode set on display DIP switch SW1. Weigh in to the nameplate first; other matches: see the unit charging label","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Outdoor EEV holds about 10 °F superheat. Indoor TXV (UI18 p12; II18 Table 4)"},{"label":"Line set (flare)","value":"Suction valve 5/8 / 3/4 / 3/4 in. with 3/4 / 7/8 / 7/8 in. line for 024 / 036 / 060. Maximum length 150 / 150 / 100 ft, maximum height difference 50 ft (EHB18 p6)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MCA / MOCP / compressor RLA / fan A (EHB18 p6)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 21 / 30 / 14.5 / 1.2 · 036: 24 / 35 / 16.5 / 1.5 · 060: 37 / 60 / 26.4 / 2.4","key":true},{"label":"Wiring diagram","value":"II18 p18 shows a PSC/capacitor diagram; use the UI18 wiring diagrams on p50-52 instead"}]},{"title":"Pressures & defrost","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"590 ±15 / 418 ±15 psig (II18 p29)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Trips after 1 min open, and locks out after 3 trips in an hour. Ignored for the first 8 min, during defrost and below 32 °F (UI18 p34)"},{"label":"Defrost start","value":"After 10 min continuous run and 55 min total, when Te ≤ C×Ta - A holds for 5 min. C = 0.8 below 32 °F and 0.6 at or above. A = 8 (moderate, factory) or 6 (severe) (UI18 p31)","key":true},{"label":"Defrost end / forced","value":"Ends at Te above 44 °F for 60 s, or above 54 °F for 30 s, or after 10 min maximum (UI18 p31). DIP SW1-4 forces a defrost; 'strong defrost' shortens the interval (II18 p24)"}]},{"title":"Codes (2-digit display on the outdoor board, UI18 p66)","rows":[{"label":"Code list","value":"1 EEPROM · 2 / 3 / 5 / 24 / 25 overcurrent · 4 drive communication · 6 / 20 high / low voltage · 8 discharge temperature above 115 °C (239 °F) · 9 DC fan · 10-13 and 39 sensors · 16 low charge (Td-Ts ≥ 80 °C, 144 °F) · 17 reversing valve · 18 desynchronization · 23 / 46 module temperature · 42 HP switch · 43 LP switch (3 trips = lockout) · 44 condenser temperature above 65 °C (149 °F) · 45 low pressure (3 trips = lockout) · 51 pressure sensor · LE = 'W' present during cooling (thermostat wiring)"}]},{"title":"Operating range - CONFLICT","rows":[{"label":"EHB vs UI","value":"EHB: cooling 5-115 °F, heating -22 to 86 °F. UI: cooling 5-125 °F, heating -22 to 75 °F"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"RDS","value":"An indoor RDS sensor and mitigation board are required. Lennox RDS kits are 27A02 (24 V) and 27A03 (communicating)","key":true},{"label":"Minimum conditioned area TAmin","value":"4 lb = 59 ft², 11 lb = 164 ft² (II18 p2)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Factory charge: EHB vs II / UI","body":"EHB 211074 gives 3 lb 9 oz / 5 lb 9 oz / 7 lb 8 oz. II 508700-01 and UI 100203 give 62 / 94 / 125 oz (3 lb 14 oz / 5 lb 14 oz / 7 lb 13 oz). The generic II figure shows 0.60 oz/ft, but the unit table shows 0.55. Use the rating plate."},{"title":"Charging method: UI vs II","body":"UI 100203 p68 says 'weigh-in is the ONLY way to charge', while II 508700-01 gives per-match subcooling targets. The liquid-line subcooling source is not confirmed (cool-mode subcooling appears on the display). Weigh in to the nameplate; use the II targets only as a check."},{"title":"Operating range: EHB vs UI","body":"EHB: cooling 5-115 °F, heating -22 to 86 °F. UI: cooling 5-125 °F, heating -22 to 75 °F."},{"title":"Wrong wiring diagram in the II","body":"II 508700-01 p18 shows a PSC/capacitor diagram; use the UI 100203 wiring diagrams on p50-52."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Per-match subcooling targets beyond the example (charging label), capacitor, LRA."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL23XCV (Elite variable-capacity AC, R-410A)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Elite EL23XCV variable-capacity ('Precise Comfort') split AC condenser, R-410A, SEER2 up to 22.4. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (2-5 ton, 20,800-59,000 Btuh), 208/230-1. Rotary compressor on 024-048, scroll on 060. Communicating outdoor control with 7-segment display; works with an S40 plus communicating indoor unit or a conventional 1- or 2-stage stat. Not an A2L refrigerant - no leak-detection or mitigation rules. The compressor oil is PVE, not POE (see flag).","match":["EL23XCV","EL23XCV-024-230","EL23XCV-036-230","EL23XCV-048-230","EL23XCV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox EL23XCV Product Specifications, Bulletin 210987 (Jan 2023); Lennox EL23XCV Unit Information, Corp. 100040 (Feb 14 2023); Lennox EL23XCV Installation Instructions 508273-01 (9/2023)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL23XCV-036-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 23 = nominal efficiency · X = R-410A · C = AC (condenser) · V = variable-capacity compressor · -036 = tons x 12 · -230 = 208/230V-1ph-60Hz · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision level (Bulletin 210987 p1)"},{"label":"Controls","value":"Communicating outdoor control with 7-segment display; stores 100 alarms and shows the last 10; five-strike lockout. Inverter is built into the control on 024 / 036 and is a separate board on 048 / 060 (Bulletin 210987 p5)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (covers 15 ft of line)","value":"024: 7 lb 15 oz · 036: 8 lb 0 oz · 048: 11 lb 14 oz · 060: 11 lb 15 oz (Bulletin 210987 p8; Corp. 100040 p3)","key":true},{"label":"Line adjustment","value":"3/8 in. liquid 0.60 oz/ft (3 oz per 5 ft), added or removed from 15 ft (Corp. 100040 p78 Fig. 48; II p19)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in, then check by subcooling at 100% capacity. The Charge Mode jumper (CHRG MODE) runs 100% and times out after 60 min (Corp. 100040 p76-80). Targets assume 70-80 °F return air and outdoor 60 °F or above (p79). Readings at part speed are not valid","key":true},{"label":"Label subcooling / approach at high capacity, ±1 °F","value":"Subcooling 024: 12 · 036: 6 · 048: 10 · 060: 10 °F. Approach 024: 3 · 036: 7 · 048: 3 · 060: 3 °F (Corp. 100040 p80, Fig. 50)","key":true},{"label":"Label liquid / vapor psig at 95 °F outdoor","value":"024: 361 / 147 · 036: 352 / 141 · 048: 353 / 144 · 060: 358 / 139 (Corp. 100040 p80)"},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor TXV. Field kits: 024 12J18, 036 12J19, 048 / 060 12J20. C35 coils: replace the RFC with the TXV (Bulletin 210987 p11)"},{"label":"Oil / drier","value":"PVE oil, not POE (II 508273-01 p4). The 060 has a liquid-line drier; the other sizes have a suction-line drier (Bulletin 210987 p3)","key":true}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1 (Bulletin 210987 p8)","rows":[{"label":"MCA / MOCP","value":"024: 12.6 / 20 · 036: 19.2 / 30 · 048: 23.6 / 40 · 060: 27.4 / 45","key":true},{"label":"Compressor input amps / fan","value":"024: 8 · 036: 13.3 · 048: 16.8 · 060: 19.8. Inverter-driven, so no RLA / LRA or run capacitor is published. Fan FLA 2.6 (ECM) on all sizes"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections (liquid x suction)","value":"024: 3/8 x 3/4 · 036 and 048: 3/8 x 7/8 · 060: 3/8 x 1-1/8 (Bulletin 210987 p8). Line-set catalog numbers differ between the UI and the II - use the sizes, not the catalog numbers"},{"label":"Maximums","value":"Total equivalent length 180 ft, linear 150 ft, liquid lift 60 ft, vapor riser 60 ft. Over 150 ft not recommended. Trap at the base of the suction riser when the condenser is 5-60 ft above the indoor unit (Corp. 100040 p14-15)"}]},{"title":"Pressure, protection & codes","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens 590 ±15 psig, resets 418 ±15 psig (II p19; Corp. 100040 p36)","key":true},{"label":"Low pressure","value":"No low-pressure switch. A suction transducer emulates one: cut-out 40 psig, cut-in 90 psig (Corp. 100040 p36, p47)"},{"label":"Suction setpoint on a 24 V stat","value":"Normal mode 135 psig, Comfort mode 125 psig. Efficiency mode (factory default) varies with outdoor temperature (Corp. 100040 p30-31)"},{"label":"Codes","value":"E410 low suction (40 / 90) · E411 low-pressure 5-strike lockout · E412 high pressure · E413 high-pressure 5-strike lockout · E422 compressor top-cap hot · E424 liquid sensor fault (10K at 77 °F) · E426-E435 inverter faults · E442 top-cap 5-strike lockout (Corp. 100040 p35-39)"},{"label":"Top-cap switch","value":"Opens at 239-257 °F and closes at 151-187 °F (Corp. 100040 p64)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cools down to 0 °F outdoor with the built-in low-ambient control. Freezestat recommended (Bulletin 210987 p5)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"PVE oil, not POE","body":"II 508273-01 p4: the compressor oil is PVE. The top-off oil type differs from the 13ACXN and 16ACX (POE). Do not top off with POE."},{"title":"Charge only at 100% capacity","body":"Use the Charge Mode jumper or the S40 'Cooling - Maximum Rate' test. Readings taken at part speed are not valid. Wait 5 minutes for the inverter capacitors to discharge before working on the inverter (Corp. 100040 p38)."},{"title":"5-ton scroll hisses at low suction","body":"The 060 scroll has an internal vacuum protector: it unloads below 20 psig (you hear hissing) and resets above 40 psig. Do not replace the compressor for this (II p4)."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Compressor RLA / LRA and run capacitor (inverter-driven)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"13ACXN (Merit single-stage AC, R-410A, North region)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Merit 13ACXN single-stage scroll split AC condenser, R-410A, SEER up to 15.50. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (1.5-5 ton, 17,500-59,000 Btuh), 208/230-1. Model form 13ACXN048-230 (no dash after the family). The 'N' is the NORTH REGION DOE regional-standard flag - it is NOT a dry-charge or replacement flag; the unit ships pre-charged. Ships with an RFCIV orifice for the indoor coil; TXV optional. No board, no codes. Do not confuse with the older 13ACX-xxx-230-xx dash format, whose charges vary by revision.","match":["13ACXN","13ACXN018-230","13ACXN024-230","13ACXN030-230","13ACXN036-230","13ACXN042-230","13ACXN048-230","13ACXN060-230"],"source":"Lennox 13ACXN Product Specifications, Bulletin 210831 (June 2020, distributor copy; values match the Lennox-hosted Bulletin 210739); Lennox 13ACX(N) Product Specifications, Bulletin 210739 (Nov 2017); Lennox 13ACX Installation and Service Procedure, Corp. 0612-L2 (rev. May 2017) for the charging method and switch value","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (13ACXN048-230-17)","value":"13 = nominal SEER · AC = air conditioner · X = R-410A · N = North Region (DOE regional standard) · 048 = capacity · -230 = 208/230V-1ph · -17 = minor revision (Bulletin 210831 p1; Bulletin 210739 p1)","key":true}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (15 ft)","value":"018: 4 lb 1 oz · 024: 3 lb 14 oz · 030: 5 lb 2 oz · 036: 5 lb 4 oz · 042: 6 lb 8 oz · 048: 7 lb 12 oz · 060: 9 lb 0 oz (Bulletin 210831 p7; Bulletin 210739 p6 agrees)","key":true},{"label":"Line adjustment","value":"3 oz per 5 ft of 3/8 in. liquid line from 15 ft (Corp. 0612-L2 p31-33)"},{"label":"Metering (RFCIV orifice shipped with the unit)","value":"018: 0.051 · 024: 0.057 · 030: 0.065 · 036: 0.072 · 042: 0.076 · 048: 0.082 · 060: 0.090. TXV is optional (Chatleff) (Bulletin 210831 p4, p7)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method (13ACX manual, Corp. 0612-L2 p31-33)","value":"TXV at 65 °F and above: approach or subcooling. TXV at 64 °F and below: weigh in. RFC at 40 °F and above: superheat (never below 5 °F). RFC at 39 °F and below: weigh in","key":true},{"label":"Charging targets","value":"See the charging sticker on the unit. Corp. 0612-L2 prints two versions of 13ACX label 580450-01 (dated 1115 and 0517) with the same RFC sizes as the 13ACXN but different TXV approach values (018: 8 °F vs 6 °F; 024: 11 °F vs 15 °F). No 13ACXN-specific label was found"},{"label":"Drier","value":"The liquid-line drier ships loose and must be installed in the field (Bulletin 210831 p3)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MOCP / MCA / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (Bulletin 210831 p7)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 20 / 12.4 / 9.4 / 56.6 / 0.7 · 024: 25 / 14.7 / 11.2 / 60.8 / 0.7 · 030: 25 / 17.1 / 12.8 / 64 / 1.1 · 036: 35 / 22.0 / 16.7 / 70 / 1.1 · 042: 45 / 28.1 / 21.2 / 90 / 1.7 · 048: 50 / 31.9 / 24.2 / 100 / 1.7 · 060: 60 / 34.6 / 26.3 / 125 / 1.7","key":true},{"label":"Compressor / capacitor","value":"PSC compressor. A hard-start kit is optional (Copeland 10J42, LG 88M91). No capacitor rating is printed - see the rating plate (Bulletin 210831 p5, p7)"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections","value":"3/8 in. liquid on all sizes. Suction 5/8 in. (018, 024), 3/4 in. (030-042), 7/8 in. (048, 060) (Bulletin 210831 p7)"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches & operating range","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Auto-reset (Bulletin 210831 p3). The trip value is not printed in the 13ACXN bulletin; Corp. 0612-L2 p24 gives 590 ±15 psig for 13ACX revisions -10 and later","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"None as standard. Loss-of-charge kit 84M23 is optional (Bulletin 210831 p4, p7)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Runs down to 45 °F outdoor without kits. Low-ambient kit 34M72 extends this to 30 °F; add crankcase heater and freezestat with it (Bulletin 210831 p5)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"'N' means North region, not dry charge","body":"The N is the DOE regional-standard flag. The unit ships pre-charged (Bulletin 210831 p3)."},{"title":"Charging sticker versions differ","body":"Corp. 0612-L2 p39-40 prints two versions of 13ACX charging label 580450-01 (dated 1115 and 0517). Both list the same RFC sizes as the 13ACXN, but their TXV approach values differ (018: 8 °F vs 6 °F; 024: 11 °F vs 15 °F). Use the unit's own sticker."},{"title":"Do not confuse with 13ACX-xxx-230-xx","body":"The older dash-format 13ACX has charges that vary by revision (Corp. 0612-L2 p2-3). No 13ACXN-specific installation instructions or service literature were found; the charging method and switch value come from the 13ACX manual."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Sticker targets, capacitor rating, high-pressure switch trip value for the 13ACXN itself. No SEER2 revision was found."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"16ACX (Merit two-stage AC, R-410A)","equip":"Condenser","summary":"Lennox Merit 16ACX two-stage scroll split AC condenser (unloads to about 67%), R-410A, SEER up to 18.00. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (2-5 ton, 23,000-59,000 Btuh), 208/230-1. Y1 = low stage, Y2 = high stage through an internal 24 VDC solenoid. No board, no codes. Charging targets are on the unit sticker only. The 060 suction size conflicts between documents (see flag).","match":["16ACX","16ACX-024-230","16ACX-036-230","16ACX-048-230","16ACX-060-230"],"source":"Lennox 16ACX Product Specifications, Bulletin 210873 (May 2020); Lennox 16ACX Unit Information, Corp. 1916-L9 (Oct 3 2019); Lennox 16ACX Installation Instructions 507875-01 (8/2018)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (16ACX-036-230A01)","value":"16 = nominal SEER · AC = air conditioner · X = R-410A · '-' = all regions · 036 = capacity · 230 = 208/230V-1ph · A = ratings revision · 01 = minor revision (Bulletin 210873 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (15 ft)","value":"024: 7 lb 2 oz · 036: 9 lb 0 oz · 048: 10 lb 6 oz · 060: 13 lb 2 oz (Bulletin 210873 p6; Corp. 1916-L9 p4 agrees)","key":true},{"label":"Charging targets","value":"On the unit charging sticker only. The installation instructions refer to it and print no values (II 507875-01 p13)","key":true},{"label":"Metering","value":"Indoor TXV: 024 12J18, 036 12J19, 048 / 060 12J20 (Bulletin 210873 p8)"},{"label":"Oil","value":"POE (Corp. 1916-L9 p9)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MOCP / MCA / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (Bulletin 210873 p6)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 20 / 15.6 / 10.2 / 55 / 1.0 · 036: 30 / 20.8 / 14.2 / 78 / 1.7 · 048: 40 / 29.2 / 17 / 109 / 1.7 · 060: 50 / 35.7 / 23.5 / 118 / 1.4","key":true},{"label":"Hard-start kit - REQUIRED when supply voltage is below 230 V","value":"63W22 for 024, 10J42 for 036 / 048, 63W24 for 060 (Bulletin 210873 p6). A 208 V supply calls for it - this is required, not optional","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Rating not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Line set","rows":[{"label":"Connections","value":"3/8 in. liquid on all sizes. Suction 3/4 in. (024), 7/8 in. (036 / 048). 060 suction CONFLICT: Bulletin 210873 p6 and II 507875-01 p3 give 1-1/8 in.; Corp. 1916-L9 p9 gives 7/8 in. - a 7/8 to 1-1/8 adapter may be needed"},{"label":"Length","value":"L15 line sets cover 15-50 ft; beyond 50 ft use the piping guide, Corp. 9351-L9 (II 507875-01 p3)"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches, protection & staging","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens 590 ±15 psig, resets 418 ±15 psig (II 507875-01 p14)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Opens 25 ±5 psig, closes 40 ±5 psig. Auto-reset, not adjustable (Corp. 1916-L9 p20)","key":true},{"label":"Top-cap switch (some units)","value":"Opens at 239-257 °F and closes at 151-187 °F (Corp. 1916-L9 p20)"},{"label":"Crankcase heater","value":"From the factory on 048 / 060; optional (93M04) on 024 / 036 (Bulletin 210873 p6)"},{"label":"Staging","value":"Y1 = low stage, Y2 = high stage (internal 24 VDC solenoid). Check both stages with the two-stage checklist (Bulletin 210873 p3; II p13)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Runs down to 45 °F outdoor without kits (Bulletin 210873 p4)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"060 suction size: the documents disagree","body":"Bulletin 210873 p6 and II 507875-01 p3 give 1-1/8 in. Corp. 1916-L9 p9 gives 7/8 in. Measure the valve; a 7/8 to 1-1/8 adapter may be needed."},{"title":"Hard-start kit is required at low voltage","body":"A low compressor voltage (208 V supply) calls for a hard-start kit (63W22 / 10J42 / 63W24 by size). This is required, not optional."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Charging sticker targets (the II prints none), capacitor rating. No SEER2 revision was found."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"16HPX (Merit two-stage heat pump, R-410A)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Merit 16HPX two-stage split heat pump, copper-tube coil, R-410A (HFC-410A), SEER up to 16.50 / HSPF up to 9.50. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 (2-5 ton), 208/230-1. Check/expansion valve (TXV) at the indoor coil plus its own outdoor expansion valve for heating. A108 demand defrost board with DS1 / DS2 LEDs. Charging targets are on the unit sticker only. The factory charge covers a 15 ft line set.","match":["16HPX","16HPX-024-230","16HPX-036-230","16HPX-048-230","16HPX-060-230"],"source":"Lennox 16HPX Product Specifications, Bulletin 210875 (11/2020); Lennox 16HPX Installation Instructions 507876-01 (8/2019); Lennox 16HPX Unit Information, Corp. 1912-L8","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (16HPX-036-230A01)","value":"16 = nominal SEER · HP = heat pump · X = R-410A · '-' = all regions · 036 = tons x 12 · 230 = 208/230V-1ph · A = ratings revision · 01 = revision number (Bulletin 210875 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (15 ft)","value":"024: 7 lb 14 oz · 036: 10 lb 8 oz · 048: 9 lb 9 oz · 060: 11 lb 8 oz (Bulletin 210875 p7)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Use the tables on the unit charging sticker. No subcooling targets are printed in the bulletin, the II or Corp. 1912-L8 (II p13) - use the rating plate or sticker","key":true},{"label":"Charge compensator","value":"Fitted on the 036 only (Bulletin 210875 p3)"},{"label":"Line set","value":"All sizes 3/8 in. liquid. Vapor 3/4 in. (024), 7/8 in. (036, 048), 1-1/8 in. (060) (Bulletin 210875 p7; II p3). 060 CONFLICT: Corp. 1912-L8 Table 2 lists 7/8 in. L15 line sets run 15-50 ft; above 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MOCP / MCA / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (Bulletin 210875 p7)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 25 / 15.3 / 11.7 / 58 / 0.7 · 036: 35 / 22.5 / 16.6 / 83 / 1.7 · 048: 45 / 28.3 / 21.2 / 104 / 1.8 · 060: 60 / 36.7 / 27.1 / 153 / 2.8","key":true},{"label":"Hard-start kit","value":"Required below 230 V. Capacitor rating not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches, staging & operating range","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 590 ±15 psig, resets at 418 ±15 psig (II p15; Corp. 1912-L8 p20)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 25 ±5 psig, closes at 40 ±5 psig. Ignored during defrost. An optional S41 bypass is available for heating below 15 °F (Corp. 1912-L8 p20)","key":true},{"label":"Staging","value":"Part load is about 67% (Bulletin 210875 p4). Y2 lock-in pins (P3) are 40 / 45 / 50 / 55 °F (II p14)"},{"label":"Operating range","value":"Cools down to 45 °F outdoor without a kit, or to 30 °F with the low-ambient kit (Bulletin 210875 p5)"}]},{"title":"Defrost (A108 demand defrost board)","rows":[{"label":"Termination pins P1","value":"50, 70, 90 or 100 °F. Factory setting is 50 °F. If no shunt is fitted, termination defaults to 90 °F (II 507876-01 p14)","key":true},{"label":"Maximum defrost / fallback","value":"14 minutes. If defrost ends on time and the coil did not stay above 35 °F for 4 minutes, the board falls back to a 30-minute time/temperature mode (Corp. 1912-L8 p31)"},{"label":"DELAY pins P5 / TEST pins","value":"Compressor goes off for 30 seconds going into and out of defrost; the jumper is installed at the factory (H2 p14). TEST pins clear the anti-short-cycle delay or a 5-strike lockout, or force a defrost (H2 p15)"},{"label":"LED codes, DS2 green / DS1 red (H2 p16; H3 p24)","value":"Simultaneous slow flash = normal · simultaneous fast flash = 5-minute anti-short-cycle · alternating slow flash = ambient sensor fault · alternating fast flash = coil sensor fault · ON / ON = board failure · OFF / slow flash = low-pressure fault · OFF / ON = low-pressure lockout · slow flash / OFF = high-pressure fault · ON / OFF = high-pressure lockout · slow flash / ON = discharge-line temperature fault (trips above 285 °F, recovers below 225 °F) · fast flash / ON = discharge-line temperature lockout · OFF / fast flash = discharge sensor fault · fast flash / OFF = discharge sensor lockout. Five strikes on any one code causes a lockout"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"060 vapor line: the documents disagree","body":"Corp. 1912-L8 Table 2 lists a 7/8 in. vapor line for the 060 (p9). Bulletin 210875 p7 and II 507876-01 p3 give 1-1/8 in. Measure the valve."},{"title":"Stray 'defrost thermostat' text","body":"Corp. 1912-L8 p20 describes a defrost thermostat that closes at 42 °F and terminates at 70 °F. This unit uses the A108 demand board, so set defrost by the P1 pins."},{"title":"Low suction on scrolls","body":"The scroll unloads (with a hissing sound) below 20 psig suction and resets above 40 psig. This is normal; do not replace the compressor (II p3)."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Subcooling targets (unit sticker only), capacitor rating, maximum line length and lift above 50 ft (Corp. 9351-L9)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SL18XP1 (Signature single-stage heat pump, R-410A)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Dave Lennox Signature SL18XP1 split heat pump, single-stage scroll with SilentComfort variable-speed fan, aluminum coil, R-410A, SEER up to 18.50 / HSPF up to 10.20. Sizes 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (2, 2.5, 3, 3.5, 4 and 5 ton), 208/230-1. A175 outdoor control with a 7-segment display; runs communicating (iComfort, RSBus) or conventional 24 V. The documents disagree on the 024 / 030 charge and on the J1 / J3 defrost settings (see flags). Aluminum coil - use Lennox's special coil-cleaning procedure.","match":["SL18XP1","SL18XP1-024-230","SL18XP1-030-230","SL18XP1-036-230","SL18XP1-042-230","SL18XP1-048-230","SL18XP1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox SL18XP1 Product Specifications, Bulletin 210846 (10/2020); Lennox SL18XP1 Installation Instructions 507468-02 (8/2019); Lennox SL18XP1 Installation and Service Procedure, Corp. 1406-L10 (rev. 8/2018)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (SL18XP1-036-230A01)","value":"SL = Signature · 18 = SEER · X = R-410A · P = heat pump · 1 = single-stage compressor · then tonnage, voltage (230 = 208/230V-1ph), ratings revision and revision level (Bulletin 210846 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (15 ft) - CONFLICT on 024 and 030","value":"024: 8 lb 6 oz (Bulletin 210846 p8) vs 8 lb 11 oz (Corp. 1406-L10 p2) · 030: 8 lb 10 oz (Bulletin) vs 8 lb 11 oz (Corp. 1406-L10) · 036: 9 lb 14 oz · 042: 9 lb 11 oz · 048: 11 lb 0 oz · 060: 10 lb 5 oz (Bulletin 210846 p8). Use the rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Line adjustment","value":"3/8 in. liquid line: add 3 oz per 5 ft over 15 ft, or subtract under 15 ft (Corp. 1406-L10 p54)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in, then verify by subcooling. Charge in cooling mode at 60 °F outdoor and above, in heating mode below 60 °F. Subcooling targets are on the unit sticker (Corp. 1406-L10 p54-55)","key":true},{"label":"Line set","value":"3/8 in. liquid. Vapor 3/4 in. (024, 030), 7/8 in. (036-048), 1-1/8 in. (060, field-fabricated) (Bulletin 210846 p8; II p13). Above 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MOCP / MCA / compressor RLA / LRA (fan FLA 2.8 on every size) (Bulletin 210846 p8; Corp. 1406-L10 p3)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 25 / 20.0 / 10.9 / 59.3 · 030: 30 / 20.0 / 13.5 / 72.5 · 036: 35 / 22.0 / 15.4 / 83.9 · 042: 40 / 25.2 / 17.9 / 112.0 · 048: 45 / 26.8 / 19.2 / 117.0 · 060: 60 / 32.4 / 23.7 / 152.5","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Rating not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Switches & control","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switches","value":"High pressure trips at 590 psig and resets at 418. Low pressure trips at 25 psig and resets at 40. Five-strike lockout (Corp. 1406-L10 p8)","key":true},{"label":"A175 outdoor control","value":"7-segment display; communicating (iComfort, RSBus) or conventional 24 V. Key codes: E410 low pressure · E411 low-pressure lockout · E412 high pressure · E413 high-pressure lockout · E414 discharge temperature over 279 °F · E416 coil sensor · E420 defrost lasting longer than 20 minutes (Corp. 1406-L10 p17-18)"}]},{"title":"Defrost (A175 control) - the documents disagree","rows":[{"label":"J1 termination","value":"Factory setting 50 °F. II 507468-02 p7: options 50 / 70 / 90 / 100 / MAX, and no jumper means MAX. Corp. 1406-L10 p12: 50 / 70 / 90 / MAX only, and no jumper means 90 °F. Check the jumper on the board","key":true},{"label":"Maximum defrost / forced","value":"14 minutes (II p9-10). A defrost is also started after 6 hours of accumulated run time with the coil below 35 °F (Corp. 1406-L10 p31)"},{"label":"J3 Defrost Auto (off by default)","value":"Raises the next termination temperature when heating runs between defrosts are short. Threshold 'less than 50 minutes' (II p7) but 'less than 45 minutes' in Corp. 1406-L10 p12. With J1 at MAX, the control always runs MAX after the compressor has been off more than 30 minutes and ambient is below 35 °F (II p7)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Factory charge: Bulletin vs Corp. 1406-L10","body":"024: 8 lb 6 oz (Bulletin 210846 p8) vs 8 lb 11 oz (Corp. 1406-L10 p2). 030: 8 lb 10 oz vs 8 lb 11 oz. The rating plate governs."},{"title":"J1 no-jumper default and J3 threshold: II vs Corp. 1406-L10","body":"II 507468-02: J1 options 50 / 70 / 90 / 100 / MAX, no jumper = MAX; J3 threshold under 50 minutes. Corp. 1406-L10: J1 options 50 / 70 / 90 / MAX, no jumper = 90 °F; J3 threshold under 45 minutes. Verify the jumper position on the unit."},{"title":"Aluminum coil","body":"Needs Lennox's special coil-cleaning procedure (Corp. 1406-L10 p1)."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Subcooling targets (unit sticker only), capacitor rating, maximum line length and lift above 50 ft (Corp. 9351-L9)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL15XP1 (Elite single-stage heat pump, R-410A)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Elite EL15XP1 split heat pump, single-stage scroll, Quantum aluminum coil, R-410A, SEER up to 16.00 / HSPF up to 9.00. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (1.5-5 ton), 208/230-1. Check/expansion valve (TXV) at the indoor coil plus its own outdoor expansion valve for heating. A108 demand defrost board, 50 °F default termination. Charging targets are on the unit sticker only. The factory charge covers a 15 ft line set. There is no separate EL15XP1 installation instruction - the Unit Information is used.","match":["EL15XP1","EL15XP1-018-230","EL15XP1-024-230","EL15XP1-030-230","EL15XP1-036-230","EL15XP1-042-230","EL15XP1-048-230","EL15XP1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox EL15XP1 Product Specifications, Bulletin 210815 (10/2020); Lennox EL15XP1 Unit Information, Corp. 1704-L8; A108 board detail shared from the 16HPX Installation Instructions 507876-01 (8/2019) and Corp. 1912-L8","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL15XP1-018-230A01)","value":"EL = Elite · 15 = SEER · X = R-410A · P = heat pump · 1 = single-stage compressor · then tonnage, voltage (230 = 208/230V-1ph), ratings revision and revision level (Bulletin 210815 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (15 ft)","value":"018: 7 lb 0 oz · 024: 7 lb 2 oz · 030: 7 lb 3 oz · 036: 8 lb 10 oz · 042: 10 lb 11 oz · 048: 10 lb 11 oz · 060: 12 lb 5 oz (Bulletin 210815 p8-9)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"See the unit sticker. No targets are printed in the bulletin or Corp. 1704-L8","key":true},{"label":"Line set","value":"3/8 in. liquid. Vapor 3/4 in. (018-030), 7/8 in. (036-048), 1-1/8 in. (060, field-fabricated) (Bulletin 210815 p8-9; Corp. 1704-L8 p9). Above 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MOCP / MCA / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (Bulletin 210815 p8-9)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 20 / 12.2 / 9.0 / 48 / 1.0 · 024: 20 / 13.6 / 10.1 / 52 / 1.0 · 030: 25 / 17.0 / 12.8 / 67.8 / 1.0 · 036: 30 / 18.6 / 14.1 / 72.2 / 1.0 · 042: 45 / 25.8 / 19.2 / 123.9 / 1.8 · 048: 45 / 26.2 / 19.6 / 130 / 1.8 · 060: 50 / 29.6 / 22.2 / 127.9 / 1.8","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Rating not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 590 ±15 psig (Corp. 1704-L8 p20)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 25 ±5 psig and closes at 40 ±5 psig. S41 bypass for use below 15 °F (Corp. 1704-L8 p20)","key":true}]},{"title":"Defrost (A108 demand defrost board)","rows":[{"label":"Termination pins P1","value":"50, 70, 90 or 100 °F. Factory setting is 50 °F. If no shunt is fitted, termination defaults to 90 °F (Corp. 1704-L8 p22)","key":true},{"label":"Maximum defrost / fallback","value":"14 minutes. If defrost ends on time and the coil did not stay above 35 °F for 4 minutes, the board falls back to a 30-minute time/temperature mode (Corp. 1704-L8 p29)"},{"label":"DELAY pins P5 / TEST pins","value":"Compressor goes off for 30 seconds going into and out of defrost; the jumper is installed at the factory (H2 p14). TEST pins clear the anti-short-cycle delay or a 5-strike lockout, or force a defrost (H2 p15)"},{"label":"LED codes, DS2 green / DS1 red (H2 p16; H3 p24)","value":"Simultaneous slow flash = normal · simultaneous fast flash = 5-minute anti-short-cycle · alternating slow flash = ambient sensor fault · alternating fast flash = coil sensor fault · ON / ON = board failure · OFF / slow flash = low-pressure fault · OFF / ON = low-pressure lockout · slow flash / OFF = high-pressure fault · ON / OFF = high-pressure lockout · slow flash / ON = discharge-line temperature fault (trips above 285 °F, recovers below 225 °F) · fast flash / ON = discharge-line temperature lockout · OFF / fast flash = discharge sensor fault · fast flash / OFF = discharge sensor lockout. Five strikes on any one code causes a lockout"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Stray 'defrost thermostat' text","body":"Corp. 1704-L8 p20 describes a defrost thermostat that closes at 42 °F and terminates at 70 °F. This unit uses the A108 demand board, so set defrost by the P1 pins."},{"title":"Aluminum coil","body":"Needs Lennox's special coil-cleaning procedure."},{"title":"Low suction on scrolls","body":"The scroll unloads (with a hissing sound) below 20 psig suction and resets above 40 psig. This is normal; do not replace the compressor."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Subcooling targets (unit sticker only), capacitor rating, maximum line length and lift above 50 ft (Corp. 9351-L9). No separate EL15XP1 installation instruction exists."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML16XP1 (Merit single-stage heat pump, R-410A)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Lennox Merit ML16XP1 split heat pump, single-stage scroll, aluminum coil, R-410A, SEER up to 17.00 / HSPF up to 9.80. Sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060 (1.5-5 ton), 208/230-1. Check/expansion valve (TXV) at the indoor coil plus its own outdoor expansion valve for heating. A108 demand defrost board, 50 °F default termination. Charging targets are on the unit sticker only. The factory charge covers a 15 ft line set.","match":["ML16XP1","ML16XP1-018-230","ML16XP1-024-230","ML16XP1-030-230","ML16XP1-036-230","ML16XP1-042-230","ML16XP1-048-230","ML16XP1-060-230"],"source":"Lennox ML16XP1 Product Specifications, Bulletin 210881 (11/2020); Lennox ML16XP1 Installation Instructions 507873-01 (11/2018); Lennox ML16XP1 Unit Information, Corp. 1818-L8; A108 board detail shared from the 16HPX Installation Instructions 507876-01 (8/2019) and Corp. 1912-L8","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML16XP1-036-230A01)","value":"ML = Merit · 16 = SEER · X = R-410A · P = heat pump · 1 = single-stage compressor · then tonnage, voltage (230 = 208/230V-1ph), ratings revision and revision level (Bulletin 210881 p1)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (15 ft)","value":"018: 6 lb 6 oz · 024: 6 lb 11 oz · 030: 7 lb 10 oz · 036: 8 lb 7 oz · 042: 10 lb 12 oz · 048: 10 lb 7 oz · 060: 10 lb 4 oz (Bulletin 210881 p7-8)","key":true},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Use the charging sticker (II 507873-01 p13). No targets are printed in the documents used here","key":true},{"label":"Line set","value":"3/8 in. liquid. Vapor 3/4 in. (018-030), 7/8 in. (036-048), 1-1/8 in. (060, field-fabricated) (Bulletin 210881; Corp. 1818-L8 p10). Above 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230-1: MOCP / MCA / compressor RLA / LRA / fan FLA (Bulletin 210881 p7-8)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"018: 20 / 12.2 / 9 / 48 / 1.0 · 024: 20 / 13.6 / 10.1 / 52 / 1.0 · 030: 25 / 16.4 / 12.3 / 63 / 1.0 · 036: 35 / 20.9 / 14.7 / 75 / 2.6 · 042: 40 / 25 / 15.9 / 112.3 / 2.6 · 048: 40 / 25.8 / 18.5 / 124 / 2.6 · 060: 50 / 30.4 / 22.2 / 127.9 / 2.6","key":true},{"label":"Capacitor","value":"Rating not printed - see the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch","value":"Opens at 590 ±15 psig and resets at 418 ±15 psig (Corp. 1818-L8 p21; II 507873-01 p13)","key":true},{"label":"Low-pressure switch - CONFLICT on whether it is fitted","value":"Opens at 25 ±5 psig and closes at 40 ±5 psig (Corp. 1818-L8 p21; II p13). Bulletin 210881 lists a Loss of Charge Switch Kit (84M23) as an optional accessory, while Corp. 1818-L8 says an S87 low-pressure switch is fitted as standard - check the unit","key":true}]},{"title":"Defrost (A108 demand defrost board)","rows":[{"label":"Termination pins P1","value":"50, 70, 90 or 100 °F. Factory setting is 50 °F. If no shunt is fitted, termination defaults to 90 °F (Corp. 1818-L8 p23)","key":true},{"label":"Maximum defrost / fallback","value":"14 minutes. If defrost ends on time and the coil did not stay above 35 °F for 4 minutes, the board falls back to a 30-minute time/temperature mode (Corp. 1818-L8 p32)"},{"label":"DELAY pins P5 / TEST pins","value":"Compressor goes off for 30 seconds going into and out of defrost; the jumper is installed at the factory (H2 p14). TEST pins clear the anti-short-cycle delay or a 5-strike lockout, or force a defrost (H2 p15)"},{"label":"LED codes, DS2 green / DS1 red (H2 p16; H3 p24)","value":"Simultaneous slow flash = normal · simultaneous fast flash = 5-minute anti-short-cycle · alternating slow flash = ambient sensor fault · alternating fast flash = coil sensor fault · ON / ON = board failure · OFF / slow flash = low-pressure fault · OFF / ON = low-pressure lockout · slow flash / OFF = high-pressure fault · ON / OFF = high-pressure lockout · slow flash / ON = discharge-line temperature fault (trips above 285 °F, recovers below 225 °F) · fast flash / ON = discharge-line temperature lockout · OFF / fast flash = discharge sensor fault · fast flash / OFF = discharge sensor lockout. Five strikes on any one code causes a lockout"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Low-pressure switch: EHB vs Unit Information","body":"Bulletin 210881 lists a Loss of Charge Switch Kit (84M23) as an optional accessory. Corp. 1818-L8 says an S87 low-pressure switch is fitted as standard. Check the unit before diagnosing a low-pressure trip."},{"title":"Aluminum coil","body":"Needs Lennox's special coil-cleaning procedure."},{"title":"Low suction on scrolls","body":"The scroll unloads (with a hissing sound) below 20 psig suction and resets above 40 psig. This is normal; do not replace the compressor."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Subcooling targets (unit sticker only), capacitor rating, maximum line length and lift above 50 ft (Corp. 9351-L9)."}],"checklist":"heatpump"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML193 (Merit 93% single-stage, UH / DF)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Merit ML193 93% AFUE single-stage condensing gas furnace, constant-torque blower, silicon-nitride HSI, low NOx 40 ng/J. UH sizes 030, 045, 070, 090 (36C / 48C), 110 (48C / 60C); DF sizes 045, 070, 090 only. E = LED flash-code board, K = R-454B refrigerant-detection ready (7-segment E-codes). The DOWNFLOW rollout opens at 250 °F, the upflow at 210 °F. Not the ML195 (PSC, inshot) and not the premix EL195UHNE - do not carry that entry's 2.6 µA flame table or 4.5-10.5 supply here.","match":["ML193","ML193UH","ML193DF","ML193UHE","ML193UHEK","ML193DFE","ML193DFEK","ML193UH030","ML193UH045","ML193UH070","ML193UH090XE36C","ML193UH090XE48C","ML193UH110XE48C","ML193UH110XE60C","ML193DF045","ML193DF070","ML193DF090","merit series"],"source":"Lennox ML193UHE(K) Product Specifications, Form 211185 (Sept 2025); ML193DFE Product Specifications, Bulletin 210868 (July 2026); ML193UHEK Unit Information 100163; ML193DFEK Unit Information 100162; ML193UHE Unit Information Corp. 1905-L1 (04/2022); ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 (08/2026) for the K DIP-switch flag","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML193UH030XE36BK)","value":"ML = Merit · 1 or 2 = stages · 93 / 96 / 97 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 030-135 = input · X = low NOx 40 ng/J · E = constant-torque blower, V = variable speed · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling · B 17-1/2, C 21, D 24-1/2 in. cabinet · K = refrigerant-detection (R-454B) ready (product bulletins p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"UH 030, 045, 070, 090 (36C / 48C), 110 (48C / 60C). DF 045, 070, 090 only (Form 211185 p11; Bulletin 210868 p9)"},{"label":"Board","value":"E (no K): IFC 103217-03 or 107163-01, LED flash codes. K: 7-segment E-codes with refrigerant-detection faults (Corp. 1905-L1 p7; UI 100163)"}]},{"title":"Ratings: output / temperature rise","rows":[{"label":"UH","value":"030 29k Btuh, 25-55 °F · 045 42k, 30-60 · 070 63k, 40-70 · 090XE36C 84k, 50-80 · 090XE48C 84k, 45-75 · 110XE48C 104k, 50-80 · 110XE60C 105k, 45-75 (Form 211185 p11)","key":true},{"label":"DF","value":"045 43k Btuh, 30-60 °F · 070 63k, 40-70 · 090 84k, 45-75 (Bulletin 210868 p9)","key":true}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"All sizes, E and K","value":"Normal 1.5 µA · Low 0.5-1.4 µA · Drop out 0.4 µA (UI 100163; UI 100162). NOT the 2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA table of the EL195UHNE","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG / LP","value":"3.5 / 10.0 in. w.c. (single stage, all sizes)","key":true},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 / 11.0-13.0 in. w.c. (every document found; the old entry's 4.5-10.5 appears in none of them)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG","value":"3.3 at 4501-5500 ft · 3.2 at 5501-6500 ft · 3.1 at 6501-7500 ft · back to 3.5 at 7501-10,000 ft with high-altitude orifices (UI 100163 p48; II 508907-02 p58-59)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, LP","value":"9.4 / 9.1 / 8.9 in. w.c. over the same bands, back to 10.0 with orifices. From 4501 ft up the pressure switch must be changed; above 7500 ft the orifices too"},{"label":"High-altitude pressure-switch kits, UH","value":"11U65 for 4501-7500 ft · 11U66 for 7501-10,000 ft (Form 211185 p13)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, NG, 1 cu ft dial","value":"045 = 80 s · 070 = 55 s · 090 = 41 s · 110 = 33 s (UI 100163 p48). 030 is not in the tables used here"}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"CO2, NG / LP","value":"UH 030: 6.5-7.5% / 7.5-8.5%. UH 045-110 and all DF sizes: 7.0-9.0% / 8.0-10.0% (UI 100163 p48; UI 100162 p46)","key":true},{"label":"CO max","value":"100 ppm (UI 100163 p48)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5 in. w.g. (Form 211185 p11; Bulletin 210868 p9)","key":true},{"label":"Airflow","value":"UH 175-2150 cfm · DF 335-1720 cfm"},{"label":"Filter","value":"UH side return 16x25x1; end rack 18x25x1 (B) / 20x25x1 (C). DF: filter cabinet 51W07 / 51W08 with (2) 16x20x1 (Form 211185 p12; Bulletin 210868 p10)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch, all sizes","value":"-0.65 in. w.c. at 0-4500 ft · -0.60 at 4501-7500 ft · -0.55 at 7501-10,000 ft (UI 100163 p20; UI 100162 p18, whose table is labelled 'ML196DFEK' - see flag)","key":true},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), manual reset","value":"UH: open at 210 °F ±12 °F. DF: open at 250 °F ±12 °F (UI 100163 p16; UI 100162 p15)","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride, 39-70 Ω (UI 100163 p16)"},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Primary-limit trip temperature is not published for any of these families - see rating plate"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Downflow rollout is 250 °F, upflow is 210 °F","body":"The ML193DF rollout switches open at 250 °F ±12 °F (UI 100162 p15); the ML193UH at 210 °F ±12 °F (UI 100163 p16). Both are manual reset - the old ML195/ML196E entry called them auto-reset, which is wrong."},{"title":"K units in heat-only or R-410A jobs: the refrigerant-sensor DIP switches ship ENABLED","body":"With no R-454B sensor fitted, disable the refrigerant-detection DIP switches on the K control, or the blower runs continuously (ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 p54). Check this on any K-suffix furnace that heats only or pairs with an R-410A coil."},{"title":"Two control generations under one family name","body":"Older E-suffix units (no K) use IFC 103217-03 or 107163-01 and give LED flash codes (ML196UHE UI Corp. 1911-L7 p8; ML193UHE UI Corp. 1905-L1 p7). K units give 7-segment E-codes with refrigerant-detection faults. Read the board before you read a fault."},{"title":"Document copy error: the ML193DFEK manual labels its pressure-switch table 'ML196DFEK'","body":"UI 100162 (ML193DFEK) prints the switch table under the wrong model name. The values shown here (-0.65 / -0.60 / -0.55) are what that table prints for the ML193DF; the real ML196DF table is different and lives on the ML196 entry."},{"title":"ML193DF K units exist even though the July 2026 bulletin lists only non-K models","body":"Bulletin 210868 (July 2026) shows only ML193DFE, but a K service manual (UI 100162, ML193DFEK) exists. Go by the model on the plate. The K service manuals (1001xx) carry no printed date."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Primary-limit trip temperature."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML196 (Merit 96% single-stage, UH / DF)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Merit ML196 96% AFUE single-stage condensing gas furnace, constant-torque blower, silicon-nitride HSI, low NOx 40 ng/J. UH sizes 030 to 135 (the 135 is a D cabinet, 132k in / 127k out); DF sizes 045, 070, 090, 110. E = LED flash-code board (ML196UHE / ML196DFE), K = R-454B refrigerant-detection ready with 7-segment E-codes (ML196UHEK / ML196DFEK). The downflow has its OWN pressure-switch table. Replaces the ML196 half of the retired ML195/ML196E entry.","match":["ML196","ML196UH","ML196DF","ML196E","ML196UHE","ML196DFE","ML196UHEK","ML196DFEK","ML196UH030","ML196UH045","ML196UH070XE36","ML196UH070XE48","ML196UH090XE36","ML196UH090XE48","ML196UH090XE60","ML196UH110","ML196UH135","ML196DF045","ML196DF070","ML196DF090","ML196DF110","merit series"],"source":"Lennox ML196UHE(K) Product Specifications, Form 211187 (May 2025); ML196DFE(K) Product Specifications, Form 211186 (Apr 2026); ML196UHEK Unit Information 100165; ML196DFEK Unit Information 100164; ML196UHE Unit Information Corp. 1911-L7 (rev. 04/2022); ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 (08/2026) for the K DIP-switch flag","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML196UH135XE60DK)","value":"ML = Merit · 1 or 2 = stages · 93 / 96 / 97 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 030-135 = input · X = low NOx 40 ng/J · E = constant-torque blower, V = variable speed · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling · B 17-1/2, C 21, D 24-1/2 in. cabinet · K = refrigerant-detection (R-454B) ready (product bulletins p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"UH 030 to 135; the 135 is a D cabinet, 132k Btuh in / 127k out. DF 045, 070, 090, 110 (Form 211187 p11; Form 211186 p11)"},{"label":"Board","value":"E (no K): IFC 103217-03 or 107163-01, LED flash codes (Corp. 1911-L7 p8). K: 7-segment E-codes with refrigerant-detection faults (UI 100165)"}]},{"title":"Ratings: temperature rise","rows":[{"label":"UH","value":"030 25-55 °F · 045 35-65 · 070XE36 35-65 · 070XE48 30-60 · 090XE36 45-75 · 090XE48 50-80 · 090XE60 35-65 · 110 45-75 · 135 45-75 (Form 211187 p11)","key":true},{"label":"DF","value":"045 30-60 °F · 070 35-65 · 090 50-80 · 110 40-70 (Form 211186 p11)","key":true}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"All sizes, E and K","value":"Normal 1.5 µA · Low 0.5-1.4 µA · Drop out 0.4 µA (UI 100165 p16; UI 100164 p15)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG / LP","value":"3.5 / 10.0 in. w.c. (single stage, all sizes)","key":true},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 / 11.0-13.0 in. w.c. (every document found; the old entry's 4.5-10.5 appears in none of them)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG","value":"3.3 at 4501-5500 ft · 3.2 at 5501-6500 ft · 3.1 at 6501-7500 ft · back to 3.5 at 7501-10,000 ft with high-altitude orifices (UI 100163 p48; II 508907-02 p58-59)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, LP","value":"9.4 / 9.1 / 8.9 in. w.c. over the same bands, back to 10.0 with orifices. From 4501 ft up the pressure switch must be changed; above 7500 ft the orifices too"},{"label":"Clock the meter, NG, 1 cu ft dial","value":"045 = 80 s · 070 = 55 s · 090 = 41 s · 110 = 33 s · 135 = 27 s (UI 100163 p48; II 508907-02 p58-59). 030 is not in the tables used here"}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"CO2, NG / LP","value":"UH: 7.5-8.5% / 8.2-9.5% (UI 100165 p49). DF: 7.5-8.5% / 8.6-9.6% (UI 100164 p47)","key":true},{"label":"CO max","value":"100 ppm"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5 in. w.g. (Form 211187 p11; Form 211186 p11)","key":true},{"label":"Airflow","value":"UH 175-2400 cfm · DF 505-3115 cfm"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch, UH (0-4500 / 4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"030 and 045: -0.65 / -0.65 / -0.60 · 070: -0.95 / -0.65 / -0.75, as printed in both UI 100165 and Corp. 1911-L7 · 090: -0.90 / -0.80 / -0.65 · 110: -0.90 / -0.85 / -0.65 · 135: -0.90 / -0.80 / -0.65 in. w.c. (UI 100165 p20; Corp. 1911-L7 p16)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch, DF (0-4500 / 4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"045: -0.65 / -0.60 / -0.55 · 070: -0.90 / -0.80 / -0.70 · 090: -0.90 / -0.85 / -0.65 · 110: -1.00 / -0.85 / -0.65 in. w.c. (UI 100164 p19)","key":true},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), manual reset","value":"Open at 210 °F ±12 °F, UH and DF (UI 100165 p16; UI 100164 p15)","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride, 39-70 Ω (UI 100165 p16)"},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Primary-limit trip temperature is not published for any of these families - see rating plate"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The downflow has its own pressure-switch table - the DF 110 is -1.00 in. w.c.","body":"The UH table (030/045 -0.65, 070 -0.95, 090-135 -0.90) is right for the ML196UH only. ML196DF values differ on every size except the 090 (UI 100164 p19)."},{"title":"UH 070 switch prints -0.95 / -0.65 / -0.75 - the middle band is lower than the top band, as printed","body":"Both UI 100165 (K) and Corp. 1911-L7 (2022 E) print the 070 row this way. It is shown as printed, not corrected. Read the set point off the switch body if the reading does not fit."},{"title":"K units in heat-only or R-410A jobs: the refrigerant-sensor DIP switches ship ENABLED","body":"With no R-454B sensor fitted, disable the refrigerant-detection DIP switches on the K control, or the blower runs continuously (ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 p54). Check this on any K-suffix furnace that heats only or pairs with an R-410A coil."},{"title":"Two control generations under one family name","body":"Older E-suffix units (no K) use IFC 103217-03 or 107163-01 and give LED flash codes (ML196UHE UI Corp. 1911-L7 p8; ML193UHE UI Corp. 1905-L1 p7). K units give 7-segment E-codes with refrigerant-detection faults. Read the board before you read a fault."},{"title":"Rollouts are manual reset, 210 °F","body":"The retired ML195/ML196E entry said auto-reset. A tripped switch stays open until reset - find the cause first."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Primary-limit trip temperature. The K service manuals (1001xx) carry no printed date."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML296 (Merit 96% two-stage variable-speed, UH / DF)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Merit ML296 96% AFUE two-stage condensing gas furnace with a variable-speed blower (ML296UHV / ML296DFV; K = R-454B refrigerant-detection ready). UH sizes 045, 070, 090, 110; DF 045, 070, 090. Two manifold pressures (low fire 1.7 NG / 4.5 LP), a dual pressure switch, and a flame table (1.5 / 1.0 / 0.5 µA) that differs from the single-stage ML193/ML196. Cannot be twinned.","match":["ML296","ML296UH","ML296DF","ML296V","ML296UHV","ML296DFV","ML296UHVK","ML296DFVK","ML296UH045","ML296UH070","ML296UH090","ML296UH110","ML296DF045","ML296DF070","ML296DF090","merit series"],"source":"Lennox ML296UHV(K) Product Specifications, Form 211189 (Oct 2025); ML296DFV(K) Product Specifications, Form 211188 (Sept 2025); ML296UHVK(X) Unit Information 100179; ML296DFVK(X) Unit Information 100178; ML296UHV(X) Unit Information Corp. 1903-L1 (rev. 06/2021) for the 7501-10,000 ft table; ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 (08/2026) for the K DIP-switch flag","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML296UH045XV36B)","value":"ML = Merit · 1 or 2 = stages · 93 / 96 / 97 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 030-135 = input · X = low NOx 40 ng/J · E = constant-torque blower, V = variable speed · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling · B 17-1/2, C 21, D 24-1/2 in. cabinet · K = refrigerant-detection (R-454B) ready (product bulletins p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"UH 045, 070, 090, 110. DF 045, 070, 090. The K and non-K spec tables are identical (Form 211189 p12; Form 211188 p11)"},{"label":"Twinning","value":"ML296 cannot be twinned (Form 211189 p2)"}]},{"title":"Ratings","rows":[{"label":"Input, high / low fire","value":"045 44k / 29k · 070 66k / 43k · 090 88k / 57k · 110 (UH only) 110k / 72k Btuh","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, UH (high / low fire)","value":"045 35-65 / 20-50 °F · 070 50-80 / 25-55 · 090 45-75 / 30-60 · 110 45-75 / 35-65 (Form 211189 p12)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, DF (high / low fire)","value":"045 35-65 / 20-50 °F · 070 35-65 / 25-55 · 090 40-70 / 30-60 (Form 211188 p11)","key":true}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"All sizes","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or greater · Low 1.0 µA or less · Drop out 0.5 µA (UI 100179; UI 100178). Different low band and drop-out from the ML193/ML196","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG, low / high fire","value":"1.7 / 3.5 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Manifold LP, low / high fire","value":"4.5 / 10.0 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 / 11.0-13.0 in. w.c."},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG (high fire)","value":"3.3 at 4501-5500 ft · 3.2 at 5501-6500 ft · 3.1 at 6501-7500 ft · back to 3.5 at 7501-10,000 ft with high-altitude orifices (UI 100163 p48; II 508907-02 p58-59)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, LP (high fire)","value":"9.4 / 9.1 / 8.9 in. w.c. over the same bands, back to 10.0 with orifices. From 4501 ft up the pressure switch must be changed; above 7500 ft the orifices too"},{"label":"Clock the meter, NG, 1 cu ft dial (high fire)","value":"045 = 80 s · 070 = 55 s · 090 = 41 s · 110 = 33 s (UI 100163 p48; II 508907-02 p58-59)"}]},{"title":"Combustion: CO2, NG, low / high fire","rows":[{"label":"UH","value":"045 5.4-6.4% / 7.5-8.5% · 070 5.3-6.3 / 7.4-8.4 · 090 5.8-6.8 / 7.6-8.6 · 110 6.1-7.1 / 8.0-9.0 (UI 100179 p51)","key":true},{"label":"DF","value":"045 5.6-6.6% / 7.8-8.8% · 070 5.5-6.5 / 7.3-8.3 · 090 5.9-6.9 / 7.8-8.8 (UI 100178 p51)","key":true},{"label":"CO max","value":"100 ppm"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.8 in. w.g. heating · 1.0 in. w.g. cooling (not the 0.5 of the single-stage ML193/ML196)","key":true},{"label":"Airflow","value":"UH 485-1955 cfm · DF 545-1982 cfm (Form 211189 p12; Form 211188 p11)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch, UH, low / high heat, 0-4500 ft","value":"045 0.40 / 0.70 · 070 0.50 / 0.85 · 090 0.50 / 0.85 · 110 0.50 / 0.90 in. w.c. (UI 100179 p25)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch, UH, low / high heat, 4501-7500 ft","value":"045 0.35 / 0.55 · 070 0.45 / 0.75 · 090 0.50 / 0.85 · 110 0.45 / 0.81 in. w.c. (UI 100179 p25)"},{"label":"Pressure switch, UH, 7501-10,000 ft - CONFLICT / GAP","value":"UI 100179 prints its 4501-7500 ft table twice and has no 7501-10,000 ft table. The older Corp. 1903-L1 (2021, non-K) gives 045 0.35 / 0.50 · 070 0.40 / 0.70 · 090 0.45 / 0.81 · 110 0.41 / 0.74 for 7501-10,000 ft - unconfirmed for K units. See rating plate / switch body"},{"label":"Pressure switch, DF, low / high heat","value":"045 0.35 / 0.60 · 070 0.45 / 0.81 · 090 0.45 / 0.81 in. w.c. The table carries no altitude label (UI 100178 p25)","key":true},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), manual reset","value":"210 °F, no tolerance printed (UI 100179 p22; UI 100178 p22)","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride, 39-70 Ω (UI 100179 p22)"},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Primary-limit trip temperature is not published for any of these families - see rating plate"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The service manual's altitude table is duplicated","body":"UI 100179 (ML296UHVK) prints its 4501-7500 ft pressure-switch table twice and has NO 7501-10,000 ft table. The only 7501-10,000 ft figures found are in the 2021 non-K manual Corp. 1903-L1 (0.35/0.50 · 0.40/0.70 · 0.45/0.81 · 0.41/0.74) and are not confirmed for K units. Above 7500 ft, read the set point off the installed switch."},{"title":"Two stages means two manifold readings and a dual pressure switch","body":"Low fire 1.7 in. w.c. NG / 4.5 LP, high fire 3.5 / 10.0. The pressure switch has a low-heat and a high-heat set point per size - check both."},{"title":"K units in heat-only or R-410A jobs: the refrigerant-sensor DIP switches ship ENABLED","body":"With no R-454B sensor fitted, disable the refrigerant-detection DIP switches on the K control, or the blower runs continuously (ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 p54). Check this on any K-suffix furnace that heats only or pairs with an R-410A coil."},{"title":"Two control generations","body":"Older ML296UHV(X) units (Corp. 1903-L1, 2021) are the non-K generation; K units (UI 100179 / 100178) add refrigerant-detection faults to the E-codes. Read the board before you read a fault."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Primary-limit trip temperature; the ML296 K pressure switch at 7501-10,000 ft. The K service manuals (1001xx) carry no printed date."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML297 (Merit 97% two-stage variable-speed, UH / DF, 2026)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Merit ML297 two-stage condensing gas furnace with a variable-speed blower, R-454B refrigerant-detection ready (ML297UHVK / ML297DFVK), new for 2026. THIN LITERATURE: 97% AFUE is published only on the Lennox product page, and no product bulletin or service manual was found - this entry holds what the installation instructions give, and says 'not published' where they do not. UH sizes 045, 070, 090 (36C / 60C), 110, 135 (D); DF 070, 090, 110. Cannot be twinned.","match":["ML297","ML297UH","ML297DF","ML297V","ML297UHV","ML297DFV","ML297UHVK","ML297DFVK","ML297UH045","ML297UH070","ML297UH090","ML297UH110","ML297UH135","ML297DF070","ML297DF090","ML297DF110","merit series"],"source":"Lennox ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 (08/2026); ML297DFVK Installation Instructions 508909-02 (08/2026); Lennox ML297V product page (lennox.com) for the 97% AFUE claim; ML296UHV(K) Product Specifications Form 211189 (Oct 2025) for the twinning note; ML296 Unit Information 100179 for the shared CO2 figures","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML297UH110XV60CK)","value":"ML = Merit · 1 or 2 = stages · 93 / 96 / 97 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 030-135 = input · X = low NOx 40 ng/J · E = constant-torque blower, V = variable speed · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling · B 17-1/2, C 21, D 24-1/2 in. cabinet · K = refrigerant-detection (R-454B) ready (product bulletins p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"UH 045, 070, 090 (36C / 60C), 110, 135 (D cabinet). DF 070, 090, 110 (II 508907-02 p58; II 508909-02 p54)"},{"label":"AFUE","value":"97% - published only on the Lennox ML297V product page. AFUE per size, input / output and temperature rise: not published in any document found - see rating plate"},{"label":"Board","value":"IFC 107629-01, 7-segment display, E-codes: E200 rollout · E223-E227 pressure switches · E240 low flame · E311 airflow cutback · E390 low-GWP relay (II 508907-02 p44, p47-48)"},{"label":"Twinning","value":"Cannot be twinned (Form 211189 p2)"}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"All sizes","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or greater · Low 1.0 µA or less · Drop out 0.5 µA (II 508907-02 p62; II 508909-02 p60)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas (same as ML296)","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG, low / high fire","value":"1.7 / 3.5 in. w.c. (II 508907-02 p59; II 508909-02 p55)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold LP, low / high fire","value":"4.5 / 10.0 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 / 11.0-13.0 in. w.c."},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG (high fire)","value":"3.3 at 4501-5500 ft · 3.2 at 5501-6500 ft · 3.1 at 6501-7500 ft · back to 3.5 at 7501-10,000 ft with high-altitude orifices (UI 100163 p48; II 508907-02 p58-59)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, LP (high fire)","value":"9.4 / 9.1 / 8.9 in. w.c. over the same bands, back to 10.0 with orifices. From 4501 ft up the pressure switch must be changed; above 7500 ft the orifices too"},{"label":"Clock the meter, NG, 1 cu ft dial (high fire)","value":"045 = 80 s · 070 = 55 s · 090 = 41 s · 110 = 33 s · 135 = 27 s (II 508907-02 p58-59)"}]},{"title":"Combustion: CO2, NG, low / high fire","rows":[{"label":"UH","value":"045 5.4-6.4% / 7.5-8.5% · 070 5.3-6.3 / 7.4-8.4 · 090 5.8-6.8 / 7.6-8.6 · 110 6.1-7.1 / 8.0-9.0 (same as ML296UH) · 135 6.1-7.1 / 7.8-8.8 (II 508907-02 p59)","key":true},{"label":"DF","value":"070 5.5-6.5% / 7.3-8.3% · 090 5.9-6.9 / 7.8-8.8 · 110 6.3-7.3 / 8.2-9.2 (II 508909-02 p55)","key":true},{"label":"CO max","value":"100 ppm (II 508907-02 p58-59)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0-0.8 in. w.g. heating · 0-1.0 in. w.g. cooling (II 508907-02 p68)","key":true},{"label":"Airflow / temperature rise","value":"Not published in the documents found - see rating plate"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure-switch set points","value":"NOT PUBLISHED - see rating plate / the installed switch body","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude pressure-switch kits, UH (4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"045 32C80 / 32C81 · 070 32C78 / 14A54 · 090 14A54 / 32C81 · 110 32L29 / 32L30 · 135 25B94 / 25B95 (II 508907-02 p59)"},{"label":"High-altitude pressure-switch kits, DF (4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"070 32C78 / 14A54 · 090 14A54 / 32C81 · 110 32L29 / 32L30 (II 508909-02 p55)"},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), manual reset","value":"Trip temperature not published - see rating plate (II 508907-02 p62)","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"Silicon nitride, 39-70 Ω (common to the ML193 / ML196 / ML296 / ML297 families)"},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Primary-limit trip temperature is not published for any of these families - see rating plate"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Thin literature - MODERATE confidence","body":"No product bulletin and no service manual were found for the ML297. Figures here come from the two installation instructions (508907-02, 508909-02); AFUE per size, input / output, temperature rise, pressure-switch set points and rollout temperature are NOT published. Use the rating plate for those, and expect Lennox to add documents."},{"title":"Document copy error: the ML297UHVK install manual calls the unit 'ML296UHVK' in its CSA note","body":"II 508907-02 is the ML297UHVK manual; its CSA note names the ML296UHVK. The ML296 and ML297 share gas figures, flame table and CO2 on the 045-110 UH sizes, but the ML297 has its own kits and its own 135 size."},{"title":"K units in heat-only or R-410A jobs: the refrigerant-sensor DIP switches ship ENABLED","body":"With no R-454B sensor fitted, disable the refrigerant-detection DIP switches on the K control, or the blower runs continuously (ML297UHVK Installation Instructions 508907-02 p54). Check this on any K-suffix furnace that heats only or pairs with an R-410A coil."},{"title":"Cannot be twinned","body":"Like the ML296 (Form 211189 p2)."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"AFUE per size, input / output, temperature rise, pressure-switch set points, rollout trip temperature, primary-limit trip temperature."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML195UH (Merit 95% single-stage upflow/horizontal, PSC blower)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Merit ML195UH 95% AFUE single-stage condensing gas furnace, upflow/horizontal, INSHOT burners, silicon-nitride HSI, PSC multi-speed blower (the P in the model), low NOx 40 ng/J. Sizes 045XP24B, 045XP36B, 070XP36B, 090XP36C, 090XP48C, 090XP60C, 110XP48C, 110XP60C, 135XP60D. NOT the premix EL195UHNE - the retired ML195/ML196E entry carried that furnace's flame table (2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA), supply maximum, blower type, rollout and ignitor, all wrong here. The downflow ML195DF has its own entry.","match":["ML195UH","ML195UH045XP24B","ML195UH045XP36B","ML195UH070XP36B","ML195UH090XP36C","ML195UH090XP48C","ML195UH090XP60C","ML195UH110XP48C","ML195UH110XP60C","ML195UH135XP60D","merit series"],"source":"Lennox ML195UH Product Specifications, Bulletin 210591 (Mar 2019); ML195UH Installation Instructions 507268-03 (02/2019); ML195UH Service Literature Corp. 1035-L7 (rev. 03-2014, distributor copy)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML195UH070XP36B)","value":"ML = Merit · 1 = one stage · 95 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal · 070 = input (045 44k, 070 66k, 090 88k, 110 110k, 135 132k Btuh) · X = low NOx 40 ng/J · P = PSC multi-speed blower · 24 / 36 / 48 / 60 = add-on cooling (2 / 3 / 4 / 5 tons) · B 17-1/2, C 21, D 24-1/2 in. cabinet (Bulletin 210591 p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"045XP24B, 045XP36B, 070XP36B, 090XP36C, 090XP48C, 090XP60C, 110XP48C, 110XP60C, 135XP60D (Bulletin 210591 p8). The 2014 SL does not list the 090XP60C"},{"label":"Boards","value":"103085 (later units): one red LED with last-5 code recall - 1 flame with valve off · 2 pressure switch closed with inducer off · 3 pressure switch open with inducer on · 4 primary limit · 5 rollout · 6 pressure-switch cycle lockout · 7 failed to light · 8 lost flame too many times · 9 polarity (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 6 p10; II 507268-03 p39). 100973 (early units): red/green two-LED codes; slow red + fast green = low flame, under 1.5 µA (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 3 p9)"}]},{"title":"Ratings","rows":[{"label":"Output","value":"045XP24B 41,000 · 045XP36B 42,000 · 070 64,000 · 090 85,000 · 110XP48C 105,000 · 110XP60C 106,000 · 135 126,000 Btuh (Bulletin 210591 p8)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, 2019 bulletin","value":"045XP24B 35-65 °F · 045XP36B 25-55 · 070 40-70 · 090XP36C 40-70 · 090XP48C 40-70 · 090XP60C 30-60 · 110 40-70 · 135 45-75 (Bulletin 210591 p8)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise - CONFLICT, 2014 SL","value":"045XP24B 40-70 · 090XP36C 50-80 · 110XP48C 50-80 °F (Corp. 1035-L7 p2). Go by the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Boards 103085 and 100973","value":"Normal 1.5 µA · Low 0.5-1.4 µA · Drop out 0.4 µA (Corp. 1035-L7 p16). The 100973 section adds 'minimum 0.5 µA' (p9). NOT 2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA - that is the EL195UHNE","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG / LP","value":"3.5 / 10.0 in. w.c., all sizes (Bulletin 210591 p8; II 507268-03 Table 11)","key":true},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 / 11.0-13.0 in. w.c. (Bulletin 210591 p10; Corp. 1035-L7 Tables 19/21; II 507268-03 Table 13). CONFLICT: II 507268-03 Table 11 (p42) prints NG 4.5-10.5"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG / LP","value":"4501-5500 ft 3.3 / 9.4 · 5501-6500 ft 3.2 / 9.1 · 6501-7500 ft 3.1 / 8.9 · 7501-10,000 ft back to 3.5 / 10.0 with orifice kits (Bulletin 210591 p10; II 507268-03 Table 13)"},{"label":"Orifices","value":"NG 0.063 · LP 0.0340 (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 7 p14)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, 1 cu ft dial, NG / LP","value":"045 80 / 200 s · 070 55 / 136 · 090 41 / 102 · 110 33 / 82 · 135 27 / 68 (II 507268-03 Table 10; Corp. 1035-L7 Table 18)"},{"label":"Kits (2019 part numbers)","value":"LP conversion 11K49 · NG high-altitude orifices 73W37 · LP high-altitude orifices 11K44 · 36K derate kit (045 only) 10K55 (Bulletin 210591 p9; II 507268-03 Table 14). The 2014 SL lists older kits: LP kit 69W73, LP orifices 68W68"}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"CO2, NG / LP","value":"7.2-8.2% / 8.6-9.6%, all sizes (II 507268-03 Table 12; Corp. 1035-L7 Table 20 p47)","key":true},{"label":"CO max","value":"50 ppm (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 20) - stricter than the 100 ppm on the ML196"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5 in. w.g. (Bulletin 210591 p8)","key":true},{"label":"CFM range","value":"045XP24B 390-1140 · 045XP36B 700-1605 · 070 650-1585 · 090XP36C 655-1630 · 090XP48C 900-2140 · 090XP60C 1290-2445 · 110XP48C 715-2000 · 110XP60C 1235-2485 · 135 1135-2595 (Bulletin 210591 p8)"},{"label":"Blower (PSC, direct drive)","value":"045XP24B 1/5 hp, 3.1 FLA · 36-size units 1/3 hp, 6.1 FLA · 48-size units 1/2 hp, 8.2 FLA · 60-size units 1 hp, 11.5 FLA. MOCP 15 A (Bulletin 210591 p8). CONFLICT: the 2014 SL gives 1/3 hp for the 045XP24B and 12 A MOCP for the smaller units (Corp. 1035-L7 p2). Capacitor: see the motor nameplate"},{"label":"Filter (field supplied)","value":"Side return 16x25x1 on every cabinet, D cabinet takes 2. Bottom return 16x25x1 (B), 20x25x1 (C), 24x25x1 (D) (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 24 p50). End-rack kits 18x25x1 / 20x25x1 / 25x25x1 (Bulletin 210591 p9). 60C / 60D units above 1800 cfm need bottom return, two side returns, or a return-air base (Bulletin 210591 p5)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch (0-4500 / 4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"045: -0.65 / -0.65 / -0.60 · 070: -0.90 / -0.85 / -0.65 · 090: -0.90 / -0.80 / -0.65 · 110: -0.90 / -0.85 / -0.65 · 135: -0.90 / -0.80 / -0.65 in. w.c. (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 10 p18). The 070 is -0.90, not the ML196's -0.95","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude pressure-switch kits (4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"045 no change / 11U65 · 070 11U71 / 11U64 · 090 11U70 / 11U64 · 110 11U71 / 11U64 · 135 11U70 / 11U64 (Bulletin 210591 p9). 2014 SL: 93W87 / 93W93 / 93W92 / 93W86 (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 22)"},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), S47","value":"Manual reset, open at 210 °F ±12 °F (Corp. 1035-L7 p14; Bulletin 210591 p3)","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset, on the vestibule. Trip temperature not published - see rating plate (Corp. 1035-L7 p14)"},{"label":"Ignitor (silicon nitride) - by board","value":"With control 103085: 39-70 Ω, 120 V ±10%. With control 100973: 24-47 Ω, 95 V (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 8 p17)","key":true}]},{"title":"Controls: timings","rows":[{"label":"Sequence","value":"15 s pre-purge · 20 s ignitor warm-up · 4 s trial for ignition · 5 trials, then 60-minute Watchguard"},{"label":"Heat fan delays","value":"Fan on 30 s. Fan off 60 / 90 / 120 / 180 s: factory 120 s on the 103085 (Bulletin 210591 p4; Corp. 1035-L7 p12), 90 s on the 100973 (Corp. 1035-L7 p8)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The retired ML195/ML196E entry was wrong for this furnace on six rows","body":"Flame signal is 1.5 / 0.5-1.4 / 0.4 µA (not 2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1). NG supply maximum is 13.0. The blower is PSC, not constant-torque. Rollouts are manual reset at 210 °F, not auto-reset. Ignitor voltage is 120 V or 95 V by board, not 102-132 V. The 070 pressure switch is -0.90, not -0.95."},{"title":"Two board generations - the ignitor must match the board","body":"The 100973 uses a 24-47 Ω, 95 V ignitor; the 103085 a 39-70 Ω, 120 V ignitor. Do not fit a 120 V ignitor without the matching board (Corp. 1035-L7 Table 8)."},{"title":"Altitude derate depends on the revision","body":"The 2014 SL says -1 through -5 units need no manifold derate; -6 and later units need the derate plus a pressure-switch kit at 4501 ft and up (Corp. 1035-L7 p47)."},{"title":"Conflicts between the 2019 bulletin and the 2014 SL","body":"Temperature rise on three sizes (045XP24B, 090XP36C, 110XP48C), the 045XP24B motor size and the MOCP for the smaller units differ. II 507268-03 Table 11 also prints NG supply 4.5-10.5 where every other table says 4.5-13.0. Go by the rating plate."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Primary-limit trip temperature; blower capacitor (motor nameplate). No post-2014 ML195UH Unit Information was found on a Lennox domain - Corp. 1035-L7 is a distributor copy."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ML195DF (Merit 95% single-stage downflow, PSC blower)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Merit ML195DF 95% AFUE single-stage condensing gas furnace, DOWNFLOW only, inshot burners, silicon-nitride HSI, PSC blower, low NOx 40 ng/J. Sizes 045XP36B, 070XP36B, 090XP60C, 110XP60C (AHRI 4805524 / 4805525 / 4805529 / 4805530). Differs from the ML195UH: rollout 250 °F (UH 210 °F), 045 output 43,000, 070 rise 35-65, its own CFM ranges and pressure-switch rows, top return only, no 135 size.","match":["ML195DF","ML195DF045XP36B","ML195DF070XP36B","ML195DF090XP60C","ML195DF110XP60C","merit series"],"source":"Lennox ML195DF Product Specifications, Bulletin 210622 (March 2019); ML195DF Installation Instructions 507269-03 (02/2019); ML195DF Service Literature Corp. 1130-L7 (rev. 03-2014, distributor copy)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ML195DF070XP36B)","value":"ML = Merit · 1 = one stage · 95 = AFUE · DF = downflow · 070 = input (045 44k, 070 66k, 090 88k, 110 110k Btuh) · X = low NOx · P = PSC multi-speed blower · 36 = 3 t, 60 = 5 t add-on cooling · B 17-1/2 in., C 21 in. cabinet (Bulletin 210622 p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"045XP36B, 070XP36B, 090XP60C, 110XP60C (Bulletin 210622 p7)"},{"label":"Board 103085 (current)","value":"One red LED, push button recalls the last 5 codes (hold more than 5 s to clear). 1 flame with valve off · 2 pressure switch closed with inducer off · 3 pressure switch open with inducer on · 4 primary limit · 5 rollout · 6 pressure-switch cycle lockout · 7 failed to light · 8 flame lost too many times · 9 polarity (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 6 p9; II 507269-03 p38)"},{"label":"Board 100973 (early units), red / green LEDs","value":"Red slow / green on = limit (must reclose within 3 minutes) · red off / green slow = pressure switch · alternating slow = Watchguard · red slow / green off = flame with no gas valve · red on / green slow = rollout · red fast / green slow = polarity · red slow / green fast = low flame (under 1.5 µA) · alternating fast = ground or voltage below 90 V (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 3 p8)"}]},{"title":"Ratings","rows":[{"label":"Output","value":"045 43,000 · 070 64,000 · 090 86,000 · 110 106,000 Btuh (Bulletin 210622 p7; Corp. 1130-L7 p2)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, 2019 bulletin","value":"045 25-55 °F · 070 35-65 · 090 30-60 · 110 40-70 (Bulletin 210622 p7)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise - CONFLICT, 2014 SL","value":"070 40-70 · 090 35-65 °F (Corp. 1130-L7 p2). Go by the rating plate"}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"Boards 103085 and 100973","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or more · Low 0.5-1.4 µA · Drop out 0.4 µA or less. Read after 2 minutes of run time (Corp. 1130-L7 Fig. 14 p15). The 100973 table adds 'minimum 0.5 µA' (p8)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG / LP","value":"3.5 / 10.0 in. w.c., all sizes (Bulletin 210622 p7, p9; II 507269-03 Table 15; Corp. 1130-L7 Table 21)","key":true},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 / 11.0-13.0 in. w.c. (Bulletin 210622 p9; II 507269-03 Table 15 p41; Corp. 1130-L7 Tables 18/21). CONFLICT: II 507269-03 Table 13 (p40) prints NG 4.5-10.5"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG / LP","value":"4501-5500 ft 3.3 / 9.4 · 5501-6500 ft 3.2 / 9.1 · 6501-7500 ft 3.1 / 8.9 · 7501-10,000 ft 3.5 / 10.0 with high-altitude orifices. This is the only permissible derate (Bulletin 210622 p9; II 507269-03 Table 15)"},{"label":"Orifices","value":"NG 0.063 · LP 0.034 (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 7 p13). Inducer (CAI) orifices: 045 0.618 · 070 0.810 · 090 0.973 · 110 1.040 in. (Table 9 p17)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, 1 cu ft dial (2 cu ft is double), NG / LP","value":"045 80 / 200 s · 070 55 / 136 · 090 41 / 102 · 110 33 / 82 (II 507269-03 Table 12 p40; Corp. 1130-L7 Table 19 p43)"},{"label":"Kits (2019 part numbers)","value":"NG to LP 11K49 (includes a manifold spring) · LP to NG 73W81 · high-altitude orifices NG 73W37, LP 11K44 · 36K derate 10K55 (045, NG only; 34,200 output) (Bulletin 210622 p8; II 507269-03 Table 16). Older: LP kit 69W73, LP orifices 68W68 (Corp. 1130-L7)"}]},{"title":"Combustion - CONFLICT between editions","rows":[{"label":"2019 installation instructions","value":"NG 7.2-8.2% · LP 8.6-9.6% · CO max 100 ppm (II 507269-03 Table 14 p41)","key":true},{"label":"2014 SL","value":"NG 7.2-7.9% · LP 8.6-9.3% · CO max 50 ppm (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 20 p43)","key":true},{"label":"Method","value":"All sizes in both. Test after 15 minutes of run time"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.50 in. w.g. heating (Bulletin 210622 p7; II 507269-03 p11). Cooling speed 0.8 in. max (Corp. 1130-L7 p45)","key":true},{"label":"CFM range","value":"045 605-1615 · 070 560-1505 · 090 1270-2305 · 110 1210-2410 (Bulletin 210622 p7; Corp. 1130-L7 p2)"},{"label":"CFM at 0.50 in., high / low tap","value":"045 1300 / 875 · 070 1270 / 835 · 090 1970 / 1500 · 110 2045 / 1500 (Bulletin 210622 blower data)"},{"label":"Blower (PSC, direct drive, 4 taps)","value":"045 and 070: 10x8 wheel, 1/3 hp, 6.1 FLA. 090 and 110: 11-1/2x10 wheel, 1 hp, 11.5 FLA (Bulletin 210622 p7). Capacitor: see the motor nameplate (Corp. 1130-L7 p18)"},{"label":"Electrical","value":"MOCP 15 A all sizes (Bulletin 210622 p7). CONFLICT: the SL gives 12 A for 045 / 070 (Corp. 1130-L7 p2). Transformer 40 VA. Line voltage at the control 97-132 VAC (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 23 p44)"},{"label":"Filter","value":"Return is through the top opening only. One 16x25x1 on B and C cabinets (II 507269-03 Table 3 p11; Corp. 1130-L7 Table 24 p46; II 507269-03 misprints the C cabinet as 21-1/2 in. - it is 21 in.). Downflow filter cabinet 51W07 (B) or 51W08 (C) on top of the furnace, (2) 16x20x1 cleanable filters (Bulletin 210622 p6, p8)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch (0-4500 / 4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft), factory set","value":"045: -0.65 / -0.65 / -0.60 · 070: -0.90 / -0.85 / -0.65 · 090: -0.90 / -0.85 / -0.65 · 110: -0.90 / -0.80 / -0.65 in. w.c. (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 10 p17). Read at the switch after 5 minutes of steady state; the differential must be greater than the set point (p18)","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude pressure-switch kits (4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"045 no change / 11U65 · 070 11U71 / 11U64 · 090 11U70 / 11U64 · 110 11U71 / 11U64 (Bulletin 210622 p8; II 507269-03 Table 16). Older numbers: 80W66 / 80W65 / 80W60 / 80W59 (Corp. 1130-L7 p3) or 93W93 / 93W92 / 93W87 / 93W86 (Table 22)"},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), S47","value":"Manual reset, open at 250 °F ±12 °F (Corp. 1130-L7 p13; Bulletin 210622 p3; II 507269-03 p43). The UH is 210 °F","key":true},{"label":"Primary limit (S10)","value":"Auto reset, on the vestibule panel, not adjustable. Trip temperature not published - see rating plate (Corp. 1130-L7 p13; II 507269-03 p43)"},{"label":"Ignitor (silicon nitride) - by board","value":"Board 103085: 39-70 Ω, 120 V ±10%. Board 100973: 24-47 Ω, 95 V. Check across 4-pin plug terminals 2 and 4 (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 8 p16)","key":true}]},{"title":"Controls: timings","rows":[{"label":"Sequence","value":"15 s pre-purge · 20 s ignitor warm-up · 4 s trial · 5 trials, then 60-minute Watchguard · pressure switch not proven in 2-1/2 minutes: 5-minute wait · 5 s post-purge · inter-purge 30 s (103085) or 35 s (100973)"},{"label":"Fan delays","value":"Heat fan on 30 s. Heat fan off 60 / 90 / 120 / 180 s: 120 s factory on the 103085 (Bulletin 210622 p4; II 507269-03 p43), 90 s on the 100973 (Corp. 1130-L7 p7). Cooling fan on 2 s, off 60 s. TWIN terminal for twinning (Corp. 1130-L7 p11)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Rollout is 250 °F on the downflow - the ML195UH is 210 °F","body":"Both are manual reset (Corp. 1130-L7 p13). Do not carry the upflow figure across."},{"title":"Possible error in the SL's pressure-switch table","body":"The 070 and 110 use the same altitude switch kit (11U71, and 93W93 in the older table) but are printed at different 4501-7500 ft set points (-0.85 vs -0.80). The 090 and 110 rows at 4501-7500 ft are also the reverse of the UH's (DF 090 -0.85 / 110 -0.80; UH 090 -0.80 / 110 -0.85). Read the set point off the installed switch body."},{"title":"Two board generations - the ignitor must match the board","body":"Fitting a 120 V ignitor to a 100973 board (95 V), or the reverse, is a mismatch. Check the board number (Corp. 1130-L7 Table 8)."},{"title":"CO2 and CO limits differ between editions","body":"The 2019 install instructions give 7.2-8.2% NG / 8.6-9.6% LP with 100 ppm CO max; the 2014 SL gives 7.2-7.9% / 8.6-9.3% with 50 ppm. Both are shown; the tighter figures are the older ones."},{"title":"Altitude derate depends on the revision","body":"-1 through -5 units need no derate; -6 and later need the derate and a switch kit at 4501 ft and up (Corp. 1130-L7 p43)."},{"title":"Combustible floor","body":"Heating-only installs on a combustible floor need base 11M60 (B) or 11M61 (C) (Bulletin 210622 p6-8)."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Primary-limit trip temperature; blower capacitor (motor nameplate). No post-2014 ML195DF Unit Information was found - Corp. 1130-L7 is a distributor copy."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL180UHNE (Elite 80% ultra-low-NOx PREMIX, upflow/horizontal, natural gas only)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Elite EL180UHNE 80% AFUE SINGLE-stage non-condensing furnace, upflow/horizontal, ultra-low-NOx (14 ng/J) California unit. Tubular aluminized heat exchanger, single-orifice PREMIX burner, NATURAL GAS ONLY. Sizes 040NE36A / 060NE36A / 080NE48B / 100NE60C, plus a K (refrigerant-detection ready) suffix from 2025. A different platform from the inshot EL180DFE / EL180UHE, which has its own entry. The gas valve is NOT adjustable - never set it to 3.5 in. w.c.; check signal pressure and the air orifice instead. The 2021 and 2025 documents disagree on several rows; both are shown.","match":["EL180UHNE","EL180UHNEK","EL180UH040NE","EL180UH060NE","EL180UH080NE","EL180UH100NE","EL180UH040NE36A","EL180UH060NE36A","EL180UH080NE48B","EL180UH100NE60C"],"source":"Lennox EL180UHNE Product Specifications, Bulletin 210801 (Mar 2025) and (Oct 2021); EL180UHNE(K) Product Specifications, Form 211168 (May 2025); EL180UHNE Service Literature Corp. 1803-L1 (rev. 02/2021); EL180UHNE(K) Installation Instructions 508545-01 (07/2025)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL180UH040NE36AK)","value":"EL = Elite · 1 = single stage · 80 / 95 / 96 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 040-135 = input in kBtuh · N = 14 ng/J ultra-low NOx, X = 40 ng/J low NOx · E = constant-torque blower · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling tons (36 = 1.5-3, 48 = 2.5-4, 60 = 3-5) · A / B / C / D = cabinet width · K = refrigerant-detection ready (Form 211168; Bulletin 210801). The 1 in EL180 means single stage - the two-stage 80% is the EL280"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"040NE36A · 060NE36A · 080NE48B · 100NE60C. Natural gas only - no LP conversion"},{"label":"Controls, non-K","value":"SureLight single red LED: 1 reverse polarity · 2 ground · 3 failed to light · 4 low flame · 5 watchguard · 7 limit · 8 rollout · 9 pressure switch open · 10 pressure-switch watchguard · 11 pressure switch stuck closed · 12 flame without valve · 13 low line voltage (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 4 p8)"},{"label":"Controls, K (2025)","value":"7-segment display with E-codes: E200 rollout · E223 / E224 / E227 pressure switch · E240 low flame · E241 flame out of sequence · E250 limit · E290 ignitor · E150-E164 refrigerant sensor / leak · E390 LGWP relay (II 508545-01 p27-29)"}]},{"title":"Ratings - 2021 vs 2025 documents disagree","rows":[{"label":"Output (040 / 060 / 080 / 100), 2021","value":"32,700 / 49,000 / 70,500 / 81,500 Btuh (Corp. 1803-L1 p2; Bulletin 210801 Oct 2021)","key":true},{"label":"Output (040 / 060 / 080 / 100), 2025","value":"33,000 / 48,000 / 64,000 / 80,000 Btuh (Bulletin 210801 Mar 2025 p9; Form 211168)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"20-50 / 30-60 / 35-65 / 35-65 °F in 2021 (Corp. 1803-L1 p2). The 080 is 30-60 °F in the 2025 bulletin (p9)"}]},{"title":"Gas - the valve is NOT adjustable","rows":[{"label":"Manifold, 2021 SL","value":"Rated 1.8 / 3.4 / 3.4 / '304' (a misprint) in. w.c. Check ranges: 040 = 1.6-2.2, 060-100 = 3.0-3.8 (Corp. 1803-L1 p2)","key":true},{"label":"Signal pressure, 2021 SL","value":"040 0.40-0.50 · 060 0.77-0.85 · 080 0.78-0.86 · 100 0.62-0.70 in. w.c. (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 11 p18)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold, 2025 documents","value":"0.05 (Bulletin 210801 Mar 2025 p9); should read 0.00-0.10 in. w.c. (II 508545-01 p35)","key":true},{"label":"Either way","value":"'Valve is not adjustable'. Do not adjust (Corp. 1803-L1 p18; II 508545-01 p35)"},{"label":"Supply NG - CONFLICT","value":"4.5-13.0 in. w.c. in 2021 (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 10 p18); 4.5-10.5 in 2025 (II 508545-01 Table 16 p35)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, 1 cu ft dial","value":"040 90 s · 060 60 s · 080 45 s · 100 36 s (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 9; II 508545-01 Table 15)"},{"label":"Gas orifice","value":"0.0595 / 0.0595 / 0.0689 / 0.0810 (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 7 p11)"},{"label":"Air orifice","value":"0.969 / 0.969 / 1.094 / 1.250. Resonance and ignition fixes are in Corp. 1803-L1 Table 12 p20"}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"CO2 NG, 2021","value":"6.5-7.5% all sizes, CO max 100 ppm (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 13 p20)","key":true},{"label":"CO2 NG, 2025","value":"040 = 6.3-7.3%, 060-100 = 7.0-8.0% (II 508545-01 Table 17 p35)","key":true}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"All sizes","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or more · Low 0.5-1.4 µA · Drop out 0.4 µA or less (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 5 p10; II 508545-01 Table 18 p36). 1.5 µA is normal here, 'low' only on the EL195UHNE","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Blower (constant torque)","value":"1/2, 1/2, 3/4, 1 hp · airflow 350-1380 / 395-1415 / 750-1785 / 920-2315 cfm · 6.8 / 6.8 / 8.4 / 10.9 FLA (Bulletin 210801 Mar 2025 p9)"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.50 in. w.g. Filter field-supplied","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch, all sizes","value":"Make 0.35 / break 0.20 in. w.c. (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 6 p11)","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"39-70 Ω, 120 V ±10% (Corp. 1803-L1 p11-13)"},{"label":"Thermal switch (intake elbow) - CONFLICT","value":"'Auto-reset' in Corp. 1803-L1 p10 but 'manually reset' in II 508545-01 p35"},{"label":"Primary limit","value":"Auto-reset. Trip temperature: see rating plate (Corp. 1803-L1 p10)"},{"label":"Altitude - CONFLICT","value":"Corp. 1803-L1 p20: 'NOT approved' above 4500 ft. Bulletin 210801 Oct 2021 p8: up to 7500 ft; 040 / 100 need pressure-switch kit 20K91 at 4501-7500 ft. Bulletin Mar 2025 and II 508545-01: up to 7500 ft with no changes"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"The gas valve is NOT adjustable - never set it to 3.5 in. w.c.","body":"This is a premix burner with a non-adjustable valve. Manifold reads about 0.05 (0.00-0.10) in. w.c. in the 2025 documents or 1.6-3.8 in the 2021 SL, never 3.5. Check the signal pressure (Corp. 1803-L1 Table 11) and the air orifice instead. Natural gas only."},{"title":"2021 and 2025 documents disagree","body":"Manifold, NG supply maximum, CO2, output and altitude all differ between Corp. 1803-L1 / the Oct 2021 bulletin and the Mar 2025 bulletin / II 508545-01. Which set applies to a non-K unit built after 2024 is not confirmed. Trust the rating plate and the manual shipped with the unit."},{"title":"'EL180' covers two unrelated furnaces","body":"EL180UH…NE… is this premix, NG-only unit. EL180DF…E… and EL180UH…(X)E… are the inshot 'E' platform with a 3.5 / 10.0 manifold and their own entry. Read the letters after the size."},{"title":"It is 80% and non-condensing, single stage","body":"No condensate, Category I venting. The 1 in EL180 = single stage; the two-stage 80% is the EL280."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Primary-limit trip temperature."}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL180DFE / EL180UHE (Elite 80% single-stage inshot, constant torque)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Elite EL180E 80% AFUE single-stage non-condensing furnace, constant-torque blower, INSHOT burners, natural gas or LP. Downflow EL180DF045E36A / 070E36B / 090E48B / 110E60C; upflow EL180UH045-135(X)E. Figures below are the EL180DFE tables; the EL180UHE differs where noted (own pressure-switch table, own CO2, derate from 2001 ft). NOT the premix EL180UHNE (040 / 060 / 080 / 100 NE sizes), which has its own entry and a non-adjustable valve.","match":["EL180DF","EL180DFE","EL180UHE","EL180DF045E36A","EL180DF070E36B","EL180DF090E48B","EL180DF110E60C","EL180UH045E","EL180UH045XE","EL180UH070E","EL180UH070XE","EL180UH090E","EL180UH090XE","EL180UH110E","EL180UH110XE","EL180UH135E","EL180UH135XE"],"source":"Lennox EL180DFE Product Specifications, Bulletin 210661 (Apr 2019); EL180DFE Service Literature Corp. 1301-L1 (rev. 09/2017); EL180UHE Product Specifications, Bulletin 210660 (Apr 2019); EL180UHE(X) Service Literature Corp. 1302-L1 (rev. 09/2017)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL180DF045E36A)","value":"EL = Elite · 1 = single stage · 80 / 95 / 96 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 040-135 = input in kBtuh · N = 14 ng/J ultra-low NOx, X = 40 ng/J low NOx · E = constant-torque blower · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling tons (36 = 1.5-3, 48 = 2.5-4, 60 = 3-5) · A / B / C / D = cabinet width · K = refrigerant-detection ready (Bulletin 210661; Bulletin 210660)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"DF: 045E36A, 070E36B, 090E48B, 110E60C (Bulletin 210661). UH: 045, 070, 090, 110, 135 (X)E (Bulletin 210660)"},{"label":"Controls","value":"SureLight single red LED: 1 reverse polarity · 2 ground · 3 failed to light · 4 low flame · 5 watchguard · 7 limit · 8 rollout · 9 pressure switch open · 10 pressure-switch watchguard · 11 pressure switch stuck closed · 12 flame without valve · 13 low line voltage (Corp. 1301-L1 p8)"}]},{"title":"Ratings (DFE)","rows":[{"label":"Input / output","value":"045 44 / 36 · 070 66 / 54 · 090 88 / 72 · 110 110 / 90 kBtuh, 80% AFUE (Bulletin 210661 p6)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"045 15-45 °F · 070 30-60 · 090 30-60 · 110 30-60 (Bulletin 210661 p6)","key":true}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"All sizes","value":"Normal 1.5 µA · Low 0.5-1.4 µA · Drop out 0.4 µA (Corp. 1301-L1 Table 6 p11)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG / LP","value":"3.5 / 10.0 in. w.c. (Bulletin 210661 p6)","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, DFE","value":"At 4501-7500 ft NG drops to 3.3 (the 045 stays 3.5); LP 10.0 throughout. At 7501-10,000 ft: NG orifice kit 73W37, back to 3.5 (Bulletin 210661 p7; Corp. 1301-L1 Table 12 p19)"},{"label":"High-altitude, UHE","value":"Derate starts at 2001 ft (Bulletin 210660 p9; Corp. 1302-L1 Table 12 p22)"},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"4.5-13.0 / 11-13 in. w.c. (Bulletin 210661 p7; Corp. 1301-L1)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, 1 cu ft dial, NG / LP","value":"045 80 / 200 s · 070 55 / 136 · 090 41 / 102 · 110 33 / 82 (Corp. 1301-L1 Table 10 p18)"}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"CO2, DFE","value":"NG 6.8-7.4% · LP 7.5-9.0% · CO max 100 ppm (Corp. 1301-L1 Table 11 p18)","key":true},{"label":"CO2, UHE","value":"NG 7.2-7.8% · LP 7.5-9.0% (Corp. 1302-L1 Table 11 p21)","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Blower, DFE (constant torque)","value":"355-1430 / 430-1475 / 680-1750 / 990-2410 cfm · 6.8 / 6.8 / 8.4 / 10.9 FLA (Bulletin 210661 p6)"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.50 in. w.g.","key":true},{"label":"Filter, DFE","value":"Optional downflow cabinet 51W06 with (1) 20x20x1; 51W07 / 51W08 with (2) 20x16x1 (Bulletin 210661 p6)"}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch, DFE (make / break, ±0.05)","value":"045E36A -0.75 / -0.60 · 070E36B -0.80 / -0.65 · 090E48B -0.75 / -0.60 · 110E60C -0.80 / -0.65 in. w.c. (Corp. 1301-L1 Table 8 p13)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch, UHE","value":"Its own table: -0.75 to -0.85 make, by model and revision (Corp. 1302-L1 Table 8 p15) - see that table or the switch body for your size"},{"label":"Pressure-switch altitude kits, DFE","value":"80W52 on 070 / 110 at 4501-7500 ft; 80W51 on all sizes at 7501-10,000 ft (Bulletin 210661 p6; Corp. 1301-L1 Table 13)"},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"39-70 Ω, 120 V ±10% (Corp. 1301-L1 p12)"},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), S47","value":"Manual reset, 210 °F (Corp. 1301-L1 p10)","key":true},{"label":"Limits","value":"Primary and secondary, auto-reset. Trip temperature: see rating plate"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"'EL180' covers two unrelated furnaces - this is the inshot E platform","body":"EL180DF…E… / EL180UH…(X)E… (this entry) has a 3.5 / 10.0 manifold and NG or LP. EL180UH…NE… is the premix, NG-only unit with a non-adjustable valve - do not set a NE unit to 3.5 in. w.c."},{"title":"Rollouts are manual reset at 210 °F","body":"Find the cause (blocked heat exchanger or vent, low inducer draft) before resetting."},{"title":"UHE differs from DFE on three rows","body":"Own pressure-switch table (-0.75 to -0.85 make by model and revision), CO2 7.2-7.8% NG, and derate from 2001 ft. Everything else here is the DFE table."},{"title":"It is 80% and non-condensing, single stage","body":"No condensate, Category I venting. The two-stage 80% is the EL280."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Primary and secondary limit trip temperatures."}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL196 (Elite 96% single-stage, UH / DF)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Elite EL196UHE / EL196DFE 96% AFUE single-stage condensing gas furnace, constant-torque blower, DuralokPlus heat exchanger with stainless secondary, direct or non-direct vent, X = 40 ng/J low NOx. UH sizes 030XE36B, 045XE36B, 070XE36B, 090XE48C, 110XE60C; DF 045XE36B, 070XE48B, 090XE48C (no DF 110 found). Closest to the ML196UHE, but with manual-reset rollouts and published altitude steps, rise, CO2 and clocking. Not the ML195 entry.","match":["EL196","EL196UH","EL196DF","EL196UHE","EL196DFE","EL196UH030XE36B","EL196UH045XE36B","EL196UH070XE36B","EL196UH090XE48C","EL196UH110XE60C","EL196DF045XE36B","EL196DF070XE48B","EL196DF090XE48C"],"source":"Lennox EL196UHE Product Specifications, Bulletin 210855 (Apr 2021); EL196DFE Product Specifications, Bulletin 210856 (Nov 2021); EL196UHE Service Literature Corp. 1805-L1 (rev. 04/2022); EL196UHE Installation Instructions 507764-06 (04/2024); EL196DFE Installation Instructions 507766-03 (06/2019)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL196UH110XE60C)","value":"EL = Elite · 1 = single stage · 80 / 95 / 96 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 040-135 = input in kBtuh · N = 14 ng/J ultra-low NOx, X = 40 ng/J low NOx · E = constant-torque blower · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling tons (36 = 1.5-3, 48 = 2.5-4, 60 = 3-5) · A / B / C / D = cabinet width · K = refrigerant-detection ready"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"UH 030XE36B, 045XE36B, 070XE36B, 090XE48C, 110XE60C (Bulletin 210855 p9). DF 045XE36B, 070XE48B, 090XE48C - no DF 110 was found (Bulletin 210856 p8)"},{"label":"Controls","value":"IFC 103217-03 or 107163-01, red LED. Codes 1-13 are the same on both: 3 failed to light · 4 low flame · 7 limit · 8 rollout · 9-11 pressure switch. The 107163-01 fan-off delay is set by DIP switch (60 / 90 / 120 / 180 s, factory 90) (Corp. 1805-L1 Tables 4-5 p8-10)"}]},{"title":"Ratings","rows":[{"label":"Output, UH (030 / 045 / 070 / 090 / 110)","value":"29,000 / 42,800 / 63,900 / 85,600 / 107,200 Btuh (Bulletin 210855 p9)","key":true},{"label":"Output, DF (045 / 070 / 090)","value":"42,000 / 64,000 / 85,000 Btuh (Bulletin 210856 p8)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, UH","value":"25-55 / 35-65 / 35-65 / 50-80 / 45-75 °F (Bulletin 210855 p9)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise, DF","value":"30-60 / 35-65 / 50-80 °F (Bulletin 210856 p8)"}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"UH (DF: not confirmed, no DF service manual found)","value":"Normal 1.5 µA or more · Low 0.5-1.4 µA · Drop out 0.4 µA or less (Corp. 1805-L1 p13)","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG / LP","value":"3.5 / 10.0 in. w.c.","key":true},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, NG","value":"3.3 at 4501-5500 ft · 3.2 at 5501-6500 ft · 3.1 at 6501-7500 ft · back to 3.5 at 7501-10,000 ft with orifice kit 73W37 (Bulletin 210855 p11; Bulletin 210856 p10; Corp. 1805-L1 Table 20 p45)"},{"label":"High-altitude manifold, LP","value":"9.4 / 9.1 / 8.9 over the same ranges, back to 10.0 with orifice kit 11K44"},{"label":"Supply NG - CONFLICT","value":"4.5-13.0 in. w.c. in Bulletins 210855 / 210856, Corp. 1805-L1 Table 19 and II 507766-03 Table 17. 4.5-10.5 in II 507764-06 Table 12 p45 and II 507766-03 Table 15 p40. Keep to 10.5 if unsure","key":true},{"label":"Supply LP","value":"11.0-13.0 in. w.c. (all documents)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, 1 cu ft dial, NG / LP","value":"030 = 120 / 300 s · 045 = 80 / 200 · 070 = 55 / 136 · 090 = 41 / 102 · 110 = 33 / 82 (Corp. 1805-L1 Table 17; II 507764-06 Table 11)"}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"CO2, UH","value":"NG 7.5-8.5% · LP 8.2-9.5% (Corp. 1805-L1 Table 18; II 507764-06 Table 13)","key":true},{"label":"CO2, DF","value":"NG 7.2-8.2% · LP 8.6-9.6% (II 507766-03 Table 16 p41)","key":true},{"label":"CO max","value":"100 ppm"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Blower, UH 110","value":"1 hp, 1055-2220 cfm, 10.9 FLA (Bulletin 210855 p9)"},{"label":"Blower, 090","value":"3/4 hp, 760-1740 cfm (UH) or 860-1760 cfm (DF), 8.4 FLA"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5 in. w.g. Filter field-supplied","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch, UH (0-4500 / 4501-7500 / 7501-10,000 ft)","value":"030 and 045: -0.65 / -0.65 / -0.60 · 070: -0.95 / -0.85 / -0.75 · 090: -0.90 / -0.80 / -0.65 · 110: -0.90 / -0.85 / -0.65 in. w.c. (Corp. 1805-L1 Table 7 p15)","key":true},{"label":"Pressure switch, DF","value":"Set points not published in the DF documents found - see rating plate"},{"label":"Inducer orifice, UH","value":"0.525 / 0.618 / 0.775 / 0.905 / 1.040 in. (Corp. 1805-L1 Table 6)"},{"label":"Pressure-switch altitude kits","value":"UH: 070 and 110 = 11U71, 090 = 11U70 at 4501-7500 ft; 11U65 / 11U67 / 11U64 at 7501-10,000 ft (Corp. 1805-L1 Table 21). DF: 070 = 17V95 (not 11U71), 090 = 11U70 (II 507766-03 Table 18)"},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"39-70 Ω, 102-132 VAC (Corp. 1805-L1 p12)"},{"label":"Rollout switches (2), S47","value":"Manual reset, open at 210 °F ±12 °F (Corp. 1805-L1 p11; both bulletins)","key":true},{"label":"Limits","value":"Primary and secondary, auto-reset. Trip temperature: see rating plate (Corp. 1805-L1)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"NG supply maximum: 13.0 in the SL and bulletins, 10.5 in the current install manuals","body":"Bulletins 210855 / 210856 and Corp. 1805-L1 say 4.5-13.0; II 507764-06 (2024) and II 507766-03 Table 15 say 4.5-10.5. Keep to 10.5 if unsure."},{"title":"Rollouts are manual reset at 210 °F ±12 °F","body":"The retired ML195/ML196E entry said auto-reset. A tripped S47 stays open until reset - find the cause first."},{"title":"The downflow has its own CO2 and its own 070 altitude kit","body":"DF CO2 is 7.2-8.2% / 8.6-9.6% (not the UH's 7.5-8.5 / 8.2-9.5) and the DF 070 uses kit 17V95, not 11U71. DF pressure-switch set points and flame table were not found in any DF document - use the rating plate."},{"title":"Flame signal: 1.5 µA is normal","body":"Do not apply the EL195UHNE table (2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA) - it would call a healthy reading low."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Limit trip temperatures; DF pressure-switch set points; whether an EL196DF110 exists."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"EL195UH (EL195UHNE, Elite 95% ultra-low-NOx premix)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Elite EL195UHNE 95% AFUE single-stage condensing furnace, upflow/horizontal, ultra-low NOx (14 ng/J). PREMIX burner with air and gas orifices and a signal-pressure check. Sizes EL195UH040NE36B, 060NE36B, 080NE48C, 100NE60C; LP on 060 and 080 only. This is the furnace the retired ML195/ML196E entry was actually written from (Corp. 1801-L1): flame 2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA, NG supply 4.5-10.5, pressure switch 0.50 on all sizes. Those figures belong HERE, not on the ML195UH or ML196.","match":["EL195UH","EL195UHNE","EL195UH040NE36B","EL195UH060NE36B","EL195UH080NE48C","EL195UH100NE60C"],"source":"Lennox EL195UHNE Product Specifications, Bulletin 210812 (Apr 2021); EL195UHNE Unit Information Corp. 1801-L1 (rev. 04/2024); EL195UHNE Installation Instructions 507758-05 (04/2024)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (EL195UH040NE36B)","value":"EL = Elite · 1 = single stage · 80 / 95 / 96 = AFUE · UH = upflow/horizontal, DF = downflow · 040-135 = input in kBtuh · N = 14 ng/J ultra-low NOx, X = 40 ng/J low NOx · E = constant-torque blower · 36 / 48 / 60 = cooling tons (36 = 1.5-3, 48 = 2.5-4, 60 = 3-5) · A / B / C / D = cabinet width · K = refrigerant-detection ready"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"040NE36B, 060NE36B, 080NE48C, 100NE60C. LP: 060 and 080 only (Bulletin 210812 p8; Corp. 1801-L1)"},{"label":"Controls","value":"IFC 103217-03 or 107163-01. SureLight single red LED: 1 reverse polarity · 2 ground · 3 failed to light · 4 low flame · 5 watchguard · 7 limit · 8 rollout · 9 pressure switch open · 10 pressure-switch watchguard · 11 pressure switch stuck closed · 12 flame without valve · 13 low line voltage (Corp. 1801-L1 p8)"}]},{"title":"Ratings","rows":[{"label":"Output (040 / 060 / 080 / 100)","value":"39,000 / 58,000 / 78,000 / 97,000 Btuh (Bulletin 210812 p8)","key":true},{"label":"Temperature rise","value":"30-60 / 35-65 / 40-70 / 45-75 °F (Bulletin 210812 p8)","key":true}]},{"title":"Flame signal","rows":[{"label":"All sizes","value":"Normal 2.6 µA or more · Low 2.5 µA or less · Drop out 1.1 µA (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 7 p12). A 1.5 µA reading is LOW on this furnace, normal on the EL196 / EL180 / ML195","key":true}]},{"title":"Gas - premix, check signal pressure","rows":[{"label":"Manifold NG","value":"3.5 in. w.c. (Bulletin 210812; II 507758-05 Table 12). SL check range 3.2-3.8 (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 19 p41)","key":true},{"label":"Manifold LP (060 / 080 only) - CONFLICT","value":"4.0 in. w.c. in Bulletin 210812 p8; 3.6 in Corp. 1801-L1 Table 19 and II 507758-05 Table 12. Not 10.0","key":true},{"label":"Manifold at 4501-7500 ft","value":"NG 3.2 / 2.3 / 2.4 / 2.3 (040 / 060 / 080 / 100); LP 2.5 / 2.8 (060 / 080) (Corp. 1801-L1; II 507758-05)"},{"label":"Signal pressure, 0-4500 ft","value":"040 0.80-0.93 · 060 0.69-0.93 · 080 0.73-0.93 · 100 0.75-0.82 in. w.c. (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 19)","key":true},{"label":"Supply NG / LP","value":"NG 4.5-10.5; LP 11.0-13.0 with kits 19K05 / 19K06 (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 18 p40; II 507758-05)"},{"label":"Clock the meter, 1 cu ft dial, NG / LP","value":"040 90 s · 060 60 / 150 · 080 45 / 112 · 100 36 s (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 17)"},{"label":"Gas orifice","value":"0.0472 / 0.0595 / 0.0689 / 0.0810 (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 6)"},{"label":"Air orifices","value":"See Corp. 1801-L1 Table 20 p43 (sizes are not reproduced here)"}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"CO2 NG (040 / 060 / 080 / 100)","value":"6.3-7.8 / 6.5-8.2 / 7.2-8.4 / 7.3-8.5% (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 21 p45; II 507758-05)","key":true},{"label":"CO2 LP","value":"060 = 8.4-9.9% · 080 = 9.0-10.4%. CO max 100 ppm (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 21)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Blower (constant torque)","value":"260-990 / 550-1380 / 760-1740 / 1260-2405 cfm (Bulletin 210812 p8)"},{"label":"Max external static","value":"0.5 in. w.g.","key":true}]},{"title":"Safeties","rows":[{"label":"Pressure switch","value":"0.50 in. w.c. on all sizes (Corp. 1801-L1 Table 8 p14) - not the ML196UHE per-size table","key":true},{"label":"Ignitor","value":"39-70 Ω, 102-132 VAC (Corp. 1801-L1 p12)"},{"label":"Thermal switch","value":"Auto-reset (Corp. 1801-L1 p11; Bulletin 210812)"},{"label":"Rollout (S47)","value":"Reset type and set point not published - see rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Altitude - CONFLICT","value":"Bulletin 210812 p10: up to 4500 ft with no changes. Corp. 1801-L1 p40 and II 507758-05 p46: up to 7500 ft using the derate table"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"This is a premix burner - 2.6 µA is normal, 1.5 µA is low","body":"The flame table (2.6 / 2.5 / 1.1 µA), the 4.5-10.5 NG supply and the 0.50 pressure switch are unique to this platform. The retired ML195/ML196E entry applied them to the ML195UH by mistake."},{"title":"LP manifold is 3.6 (or 4.0), not 10.0, and only on the 060 and 080","body":"Bulletin 210812 says 4.0 in. w.c.; Corp. 1801-L1 and II 507758-05 say 3.6. The 040 and 100 have no LP conversion."},{"title":"Altitude conflict","body":"The 2021 bulletin allows 4500 ft with no changes; the 2024 SL and install instructions allow 7500 ft using the manifold derate table. Go by the manual shipped with the unit."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Rollout reset type and set point; limit trip temperatures."}],"checklist":"furnace90"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBK45UHPT / CBK45UHET / CBK45UHVT (Merit upflow/horizontal air handler, R-454B)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Lennox Merit CBK45UH air handlers for R-454B: UHPT = PSC motor, 1.5-3.5 tons; UHET = constant torque, 2-5 tons in the -71 edition; UHVT = variable speed, 1.5-5 tons. The revision digits matter: -01 ships with an R-410A TXV (R-454B field-convertible at initial install only), -71 ships with an R-454B TXV and factory RDS. Electric-heat rows read MCA / MOCP at 230 V single-phase; a bracketed pair is the separate circuits of a 2-circuit CB kit.","match":["CBK45","CBK45UH","CBK45UHPT","CBK45UHET","CBK45UHVT","CBK45UHPT-71","CBK45UHET-71","CBK45UHVT-71","CBK45UHPT-01","CBK45UHET-01","CBK45UHVT-01"],"source":"Lennox EHB 211147 (CBK45UHPT-71), 211146 (CBK45UHET-71), 211148 (CBK45UHVT-71), 211067 (CBK45UHPT-01); IOM 508438-01 (CBK45UHET, R-454B), 508470-01 (CBK45UHET, R-410A), 508469-01 (CBK45UHPT), 508471-01 (CBK45UHVT); Unit Information 100112 (A2L figures); 27A02 RDS board setup guide 508426-01; Model ID bulletin 210965","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (CBK45UHET-036-230-71)","value":"CB = air handler · K = Quantum aluminum coil / R-454B · 43 or 45 = Merit, 47 = Elite, 48 = Dave Lennox Signature · UH = upflow/horizontal, M = multi-position · P = PSC, E = Power Saver constant torque, V = variable speed · T = factory check/expansion valve (non-bleed) · 018-060 = 1.5-5 tons · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · -01 = R-410A TXV installed (R-454B available), -71 = R-454B TXV installed. Bulletin 210965 shows a major-revision letter after the voltage (for example '230A')"},{"label":"-01 vs -71","value":"-01 = R-410A TXV installed, R-454B available by conversion at the initial install only (EHB 211067 p3). -71 = R-454B TXV installed with factory RDS","key":true},{"label":"Common figures","value":"Coil 3 rows · liquid line 3/8 · suction 3/4 on 018-030 (UHET: 024-030), 7/8 on 036 and up · condensate (2) 3/4 FPT · unit MOCP 15 A · TXV 26Z70 (018-036), 26Z71 (042-048), 26Z72 (060) · filter 15x20x1 on 018-030, 18x20x1 on 036 and up (EHB 211147 p8, 211146 p8, 211148 p9)"}]},{"title":"CBK45UHPT (PSC)","rows":[{"label":"Blower","value":"3-speed PSC. Hi = black, Med = blue, Lo = red. FACTORY SETTING IS MEDIUM. To change speed, move the lead at blower relay pin 2 (IOM 508469-01 p5). Tables published 0.10-0.50 in. w.g. (EHB 211147 p9)","key":true},{"label":"Unit electrical","value":"MCA 5.0. FLA 1.1 / 1.6 / 2.2 / 2.0 / 2.5 (018 to 042). Blower delay relay 1 s on, 45 s off"},{"label":"With electric heat","value":"Approved 'at 0.5 in. minimum at maximum and medium blower speed' (as printed). Downflow with heat runs on high speed (IOM 508469-01 p16)"},{"label":"ECB45 heat, MCA/MOCP (018 / 024 / 030 / 036 / 042)","value":"4 kW 21/25 · 22/25 · 23/25 · 22/25 · 23/25. 5 kW 25/25 · 26/30 · 27/30 · 26/30 · 27/30. 7.5 kW 39/40 · 39/40 · 40/40 · 40/40 · 41/45. 10 kW 49/50 · 50/50 · 51/60 · 50/50 · 51/60. 12.5CB (030 / 036 / 042 only) 65/70 (44/45 + 21/25) · 65/70 (44/45 + 21/25) · 66/70 (45/45 + 21/25). 15CB (030 / 036 / 042 only) 75/80 (51/60 + 24/25) · 74/80 (50/50 + 24/25) · 75/80 (51/60 + 24/25) (EHB 211147 pp10-13)","key":true}]},{"title":"CBK45UHET (constant torque)","rows":[{"label":"Blower taps (R-454B edition)","value":"Tap 1 continuous fan / low · tap 2 half a ton below nominal at 0.5 in. · tap 3 cooling, 400 cfm/ton at 0.5 in. · tap 4 electric heat (minimum setting for heat) · tap 5 half a ton above nominal (IOM 508438-01 p4). Fan-off delay 45 s; 120 s on tap 4. Tables to 0.80 in. (024-042) and 0.90 in. (048 / 060) (EHB 211146 pp9-10)","key":true},{"label":"Unit electrical","value":"MCA 5.1 / 8 / 9.5. FLA 4.1 (024-036), 6.0 (042), 7.6 (048 / 060)"},{"label":"Heat, MCA/MOCP (024-036 / 042 / 048-060)","value":"4 kW 25/25 · 27/30 · 29/30. 5 kW 29/30 · 31/35 · 33/35. 7.5 kW 43/45 · 45/45 · 47/50. 10 kW 53/60 · 55/60 · 57/60. 12.5CB 68/70 (030 and 036 only) · 70/70 · 72/80. 15CB 77/80 (030 and 036 only) · 79/80 · 81/90. 20CB n/a · n/a · 105/110 (57/60 + 48/50) (EHB 211146 pp11-15)","key":true}]},{"title":"CBK45UHVT (variable speed)","rows":[{"label":"Blower control","value":"BDC3 with COOL and HEAT jumpers (pins 1-4) and an ADJUST jumper (+ / NORM / -, about ±10%). DELAY jumper selects one of 4 profiles (EHB 211148 p4). Constant airflow holds cfm up to 0.8 in. total ESP. Factory pins: 018 on COOL #2 / HEAT #2; all other sizes #3 / #3 (IOM 508471-01 p5)","key":true},{"label":"NORM cfm at the factory pin","value":"018 650 · 024 820 · 030 1020 · 036 1260 · 042 1440 · 048 1655 · 060 1855 (EHB 211148 pp11-17)","key":true},{"label":"Staging / LED / test","value":"First stage is 70% of COOL; continuous fan about 50%. CFM LED: 1 flash = 100 cfm. TEST pin runs the motor at about 70%"},{"label":"Unit electrical","value":"MCA 4.9 / FLA 3.9 (018-036); MCA 9.3 / FLA 7.4 (042-060)"},{"label":"Heat, MCA/MOCP (018-024 / 030-036 / 042 / 048-060)","value":"4 kW 25/25 · 25/25 · 29/30 · 29/30. 5 kW 29/30 · 29/30 · 33/35 · 33/35. 7.5 kW 42/45 · 42/45 · 47/50 · 47/50. 10 kW 53/60 · 53/60 · 57/60 · 57/60. 12.5CB n/a · 67/70 · 72/80 · 72/80. 15CB n/a · 77/80 · 81/90 · 81/90. 20CB n/a · n/a · n/a · 105/110 (EHB 211148 pp18-21)","key":true}]},{"title":"RDS Non-Communicating board (-71 units; also field kit 27A02)","rows":[{"label":"Start-up","value":"5-minute purge with demands disabled"},{"label":"Leak response","value":"The board removes R (24 VAC) from the thermostat, runs the blower on high, then keeps it running 7 min after the refrigerant level drops below threshold","key":true},{"label":"LED states","value":"Initializing = flashing green · Monitoring = solid green (a blue blip means a prior mitigation happened) · Mitigating = flashing blue · Fault = solid blue plus a red flash code"},{"label":"Red flash codes (air-handler IOM)","value":"1 = sensor fault · 2 = float switch active · 3 = incompatible sensor · 4 = sensor communications · 5 = R-input not available (IOM 508438-01 p26). See the flag: the 27A02 guide reads 2 and 5 differently","key":true},{"label":"Test button / alarm relay","value":"Short press in Monitoring runs a mitigation test and clears the purge counter; long press resets. Alarm relay: dry contact rated 3 A at 30 VAC/DC"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"Minimum conditioned area (TAmin) by total charge","value":"10 lb = 149.9 ft² · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8 ft² (identical in every R-454B IOM checked)","key":true},{"label":"Altitude factor","value":"1.12 at 5,250 ft · 1.40 at 10,500 ft. The table prints 1.05 at 3,280 ft and 1.04 at 3,940 ft (as printed). Maximum altitude 3,200 m"},{"label":"Mitigation airflow (Qmin) by charge","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm · 10 lb = 271 · 15 lb = 406 · 20 lb = 541 · 25 lb = 676 · 30 lb = 812 cfm (UI 100112 p5). Mitigation minimum airflow is factory set at 350 CFM/ton","key":true},{"label":"RDS load / sensor","value":"The RDS adds 3 VA to the transformer load (UI 100112 p4). Check the sensor every 6 months. Replacement sensor 26Z69"}]},{"title":"Condensate (all three)","rows":[{"label":"Draw-through coil - every drain needs a trap","value":"Trap depth about 2 in. Vent 2 in. above the drain pan. Slope 1 in. per 10 ft. Always run an overflow line, or fit a float switch (IOM 508438-01 p16)","key":true}]}],"flags":[{"title":"-01 vs -71: read the revision before you touch the refrigerant circuit","body":"-01 ships with an R-410A TXV; it can be made R-454B only at the initial install (EHB 211067 p3), with sensor kit 27J27, RDS board 27A02 (non-communicating) or 27A03 (universal), and R-454B TXV 26Z70 / 26Z71 / 26Z72. -71 is factory R-454B with the RDS fitted. On the CBK43UHET the -01 means something else entirely (first revision, factory R-454B)."},{"title":"27A02 field-kit DIP switches expect TWO sensors","body":"The default (DIP1 off, DIP2 off) expects two sensors. With one sensor, set DIP2 ON or the board faults (27A02 setup guide 508426-01 p12)."},{"title":"Red flash-code conflict between documents","body":"The 27A02 setup guide 508426-01 pp14-15 lists red 2 as 'spare/unused' and red 5 as 'indoor unit wired to the Black TSTAT strip'. The air handler IOMs (508438-01 p26) list red 2 as the float switch and red 5 as R-input missing. Check which board and which document you are holding."},{"title":"CBK45UHET tap definitions differ between editions","body":"In the R-410A edition 508470-01 p4, tap 5 = 400 cfm/ton at 0.8 in. In the R-454B edition 508438-01 p4, tap 5 = half a ton above nominal at 0.5 in. Match the IOM to the unit."},{"title":"CBK45UHPT-71 heat range: the cover says 4-20 kW, the tables stop at 15 kW","body":"EHB 211147 p1 vs pp10-13. Only kits with a published row are listed here."},{"title":"RDS sensor: reposition, remove for coil cleaning, keep the unit powered","body":"The sensor must be repositioned for horizontal and downflow installs (EHB p4). Remove the RDS sensor before cleaning the coil. A leak-detection system is installed, so keep power on except during service. The RDS cuts R to the thermostat - thermostats that lose memory can lose setpoints (508438-01 p27)."},{"title":"Not confirmed","body":"R-454B IOMs for the CBK45UHPT-71 and CBK45UHVT-71 were not found; their taps, jumpers and RDS codes are taken from the R-410A editions and the -71 EHBs."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBK43UHET (Merit dual-voltage air handler, R-454B)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Lennox Merit CBK43UHET R-454B air handler, 1.5-5 tons, runs on 115 V or 208/230 V (DV in the model). Factory R-454B - on this model '-01' means first revision, NOT an R-410A TXV. 9-speed constant-torque blower set by DIP switches on the RDS board, which is a different board with a 7-SEGMENT display and E-codes. NO electric heat on 115 V.","match":["CBK43","CBK43UH","CBK43UHET","CBK43UHET-DV","CBK43UHET-DV-01"],"source":"Lennox EHB 211278 (CBK43UHET); IOM 508799-01 (CBK43UHET); Unit Information 100112 (A2L figures); 27A02 RDS board setup guide 508426-01; Model ID bulletin 210965","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (CBK43UHET-036-DV-01)","value":"CB = air handler · K = Quantum aluminum coil / R-454B · 43 or 45 = Merit, 47 = Elite, 48 = Dave Lennox Signature · UH = upflow/horizontal, M = multi-position · P = PSC, E = Power Saver constant torque, V = variable speed · T = factory check/expansion valve (non-bleed) · 018-060 = 1.5-5 tons · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · -01 = R-410A TXV installed (R-454B available), -71 = R-454B TXV installed. Bulletin 210965 shows a major-revision letter after the voltage (for example '230A'). On THIS model DV = 115 V or 208/230 V and '01' = first revision; it is factory R-454B, unlike the -01 on CBK45 models (EHB 211278 pp1, 8)","key":true},{"label":"Common figures","value":"Coil 4 rows · TXV 26Z70 / 26Z71 / 26Z72 · filter 15x20x1 (018-036), 18x20x1 (042-060) · drains (2) 3/4"}]},{"title":"Blower (9-speed constant torque, DIP switches on the RDS board)","rows":[{"label":"Defaults","value":"G: tap 1 · Y1: tap 1 · Y2: tap 6 · W: tap 6; set to 9 for high static (IOM 508799-01 p5). Tables run to 1.00 in. w.g. (EHB 211278 pp9-11)","key":true}]},{"title":"Electrical","rows":[{"label":"208/230 V","value":"MCA 5 / 7.5 / 9.5"},{"label":"115 V","value":"MCA 8 / 11.5 / 14.5; MOCP 15 / 20 / 25. NO ELECTRIC HEAT ON 115 V (IOM 508799-01 p22)","key":true},{"label":"Heat at 230 V, MCA/MOCP (018-024 / 030-036 / 042 / 048-060)","value":"4 kW 25/25 · 25/25 · 27/30 · 29/30. 5 kW 29/30 · 29/30 · 31/35 · 33/35. 7.5 kW 42/45 · 42/45 · 45/45 · 46/50. 10 kW 53/60 · 53/60 · 55/60 · 57/60. 12.5CB n/a · 67/70 · 70/70 · 71/80. 15CB n/a · 77/80 · 79/80 · 81/90. 20CB n/a · n/a · n/a · 105/110 (EHB 211278 pp12-15)","key":true},{"label":"Blower FLA - CONFLICT","value":"Spec table 6.0 A (042) and 7.4 A (048 / 060); the heat tables use 5.8 A and 7.2 A"}]},{"title":"RDS board: 7-segment display (IOM 508799-01 pp27-29)","rows":[{"label":"E-codes","value":"E150 leak detected · E167 prior leak (press button to clear) · E151 sensor fault · E154 sensor communications · E160 incompatible sensor · E163 R power quality (needs 24 VAC ±3 Hz) · E371 float switch open · E372 airflow DIPs misconfigured (Y2 must be at or above Y1)","key":true},{"label":"Display codes","value":"Airflow A1-A9 = active tap. Demand: C1 / C2 cooling stages · H1 / H2 electric heat stages · h1 / h2 heat pump stages · df defrost · d dehumidification"},{"label":"Post-purge after a leak clears","value":"5 min (7 min on the CBK45 / CBK47 board)"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"Minimum conditioned area (TAmin) by total charge","value":"10 lb = 149.9 ft² · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8 ft² (identical in every R-454B IOM checked)","key":true},{"label":"Altitude factor","value":"1.12 at 5,250 ft · 1.40 at 10,500 ft. The table prints 1.05 at 3,280 ft and 1.04 at 3,940 ft (as printed). Maximum altitude 3,200 m"},{"label":"Mitigation airflow (Qmin) by charge","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm · 10 lb = 271 · 15 lb = 406 · 20 lb = 541 · 25 lb = 676 · 30 lb = 812 cfm (UI 100112 p5). Mitigation minimum airflow is factory set at 350 CFM/ton","key":true},{"label":"RDS load / sensor","value":"The RDS adds 3 VA to the transformer load (UI 100112 p4). Check the sensor every 6 months. Replacement sensor 26Z69"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"No electric heat on 115 V","body":"IOM 508799-01 p22. Heat kits are listed for 230 V only."},{"title":"On this model '-01' does NOT mean R-410A","body":"CBK43UHET-036-DV-01 is a first-revision, factory R-454B unit. The -01 / -71 TXV convention belongs to the CBK45 family."},{"title":"E372 = airflow DIPs misconfigured","body":"Y2 must be set at or above Y1 (IOM 508799-01 pp27-29)."},{"title":"27A02 field-kit DIP switches expect TWO sensors","body":"The default (DIP1 off, DIP2 off) expects two sensors. With one sensor, set DIP2 ON or the board faults (27A02 setup guide 508426-01 p12)."},{"title":"Red flash-code conflict between documents","body":"The 27A02 setup guide 508426-01 pp14-15 lists red 2 as 'spare/unused' and red 5 as 'indoor unit wired to the Black TSTAT strip'. The air handler IOMs (508438-01 p26) list red 2 as the float switch and red 5 as R-input missing. Check which board and which document you are holding."},{"title":"RDS sensor: reposition, remove for coil cleaning, keep the unit powered","body":"The sensor must be repositioned for horizontal and downflow installs (EHB p4). Remove the RDS sensor before cleaning the coil. A leak-detection system is installed, so keep power on except during service. The RDS cuts R to the thermostat - thermostats that lose memory can lose setpoints (508438-01 p27)."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBK47UHET (Elite upflow/horizontal air handler, R-454B)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Lennox Elite CBK47UHET-71 R-454B air handler, 1.5-5 tons, 5-tap constant-torque blower, communicating over RSBus or non-communicating. Coil 3 rows, TXV 26Z70 / 26Z71 / 26Z72. Electric-heat rows read MCA / MOCP at 230 V single-phase (ECB47 kits); three-phase kits are also listed in the EHB.","match":["CBK47","CBK47UH","CBK47UHET","CBK47UHET-71"],"source":"Lennox EHB 211149 (CBK47UHET-71); IOM 508443-01 (CBK47UHET, R-454B); Unit Information 100112 (CBK47UHET); 27A02 RDS board setup guide 508426-01; Model ID bulletin 210965","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (CBK47UHET-042-230-71)","value":"CB = air handler · K = Quantum aluminum coil / R-454B · 43 or 45 = Merit, 47 = Elite, 48 = Dave Lennox Signature · UH = upflow/horizontal, M = multi-position · P = PSC, E = Power Saver constant torque, V = variable speed · T = factory check/expansion valve (non-bleed) · 018-060 = 1.5-5 tons · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · -01 = R-410A TXV installed (R-454B available), -71 = R-454B TXV installed. Bulletin 210965 shows a major-revision letter after the voltage (for example '230A')"},{"label":"Common figures","value":"Communicating over RSBus, or non-communicating (UI 100112 p1) · coil 3 rows · TXV 26Z70 / 26Z71 / 26Z72 (UI 100112 p9) · filter 20x20x1 (018-036), 20x24x1 (042-060) · drains (2) 3/4 (EHB 211149 p7)"},{"label":"Unit electrical","value":"MCA 5.1 / FLA 4.1 (018-036); MCA 10 / FLA 7.6 (042-060) (EHB 211149 p7)"}]},{"title":"Blower (5-tap constant torque)","rows":[{"label":"Taps","value":"Same tap meanings as the CBK45UHET -71: tap 1 continuous fan / low · tap 2 half a ton below nominal · tap 3 cooling, 400 cfm/ton · tap 4 = heat pump with electric heat · tap 5 half a ton above nominal (IOM 508443-01 p5). Tables run to 0.90-1.00 in. (EHB 211149 pp9-11)","key":true}]},{"title":"Electric heat, ECB47 kits, MCA/MOCP (018-024 / 030 / 036 / 042-060)","rows":[{"label":"4 / 5 / 6 kW","value":"4 kW 26/30 · 26/30 · 26/30 · 30/30. 5 kW 31/35 · 31/35 · 31/35 · 36/40. 6 kW 36/40 · 36/40 · 36/40 · 41/45 (EHB 211149 pp12-15)","key":true},{"label":"8 / 9 kW","value":"8 kW 47/50 · 47/50 · 47/50 · 51/60. 9 kW 52/60 · 52/60 · 52/60 · 56/60","key":true},{"label":"12.5 / 15 / 20 / 25 CB","value":"12.5CB n/a · 70/70 (27/30 + 43/45) · 70/70 (27/30 + 43/45) · 75/80. 15CB n/a · 83/90 · 83/90 · 88/90. 20CB n/a · n/a · 109/125 · 114/125. 25CB n/a · n/a · n/a · 140/150 (53/60 + 43/45 + 43/45)","key":true},{"label":"25 kW clearance","value":"1 in. to the plenum and to the duct within 3 ft (EHB 211149 p8)"}]},{"title":"RDS Non-Communicating board (post-purge 7 min, IOM 508443-01 p27)","rows":[{"label":"Start-up","value":"5-minute purge with demands disabled"},{"label":"Leak response","value":"The board removes R (24 VAC) from the thermostat, runs the blower on high, then keeps it running 7 min after the refrigerant level drops below threshold","key":true},{"label":"LED states","value":"Initializing = flashing green · Monitoring = solid green (a blue blip means a prior mitigation happened) · Mitigating = flashing blue · Fault = solid blue plus a red flash code"},{"label":"Red flash codes (air-handler IOM)","value":"1 = sensor fault · 2 = float switch active · 3 = incompatible sensor · 4 = sensor communications · 5 = R-input not available (IOM 508438-01 p26). See the flag: the 27A02 guide reads 2 and 5 differently","key":true},{"label":"Test button / alarm relay","value":"Short press in Monitoring runs a mitigation test and clears the purge counter; long press resets. Alarm relay: dry contact rated 3 A at 30 VAC/DC"}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"Minimum conditioned area (TAmin) by total charge","value":"10 lb = 149.9 ft² · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8 ft² (identical in every R-454B IOM checked)","key":true},{"label":"Altitude factor","value":"1.12 at 5,250 ft · 1.40 at 10,500 ft. The table prints 1.05 at 3,280 ft and 1.04 at 3,940 ft (as printed). Maximum altitude 3,200 m"},{"label":"Mitigation airflow (Qmin) by charge","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm · 10 lb = 271 · 15 lb = 406 · 20 lb = 541 · 25 lb = 676 · 30 lb = 812 cfm (UI 100112 p5). Mitigation minimum airflow is factory set at 350 CFM/ton","key":true},{"label":"RDS load / sensor","value":"The RDS adds 3 VA to the transformer load (UI 100112 p4). Check the sensor every 6 months. Replacement sensor 26Z69"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"27A02 field-kit DIP switches expect TWO sensors","body":"The default (DIP1 off, DIP2 off) expects two sensors. With one sensor, set DIP2 ON or the board faults (27A02 setup guide 508426-01 p12)."},{"title":"Red flash-code conflict between documents","body":"The 27A02 setup guide 508426-01 pp14-15 lists red 2 as 'spare/unused' and red 5 as 'indoor unit wired to the Black TSTAT strip'. The air handler IOMs (508438-01 p26) list red 2 as the float switch and red 5 as R-input missing. Check which board and which document you are holding."},{"title":"RDS sensor: reposition, remove for coil cleaning, keep the unit powered","body":"The sensor must be repositioned for horizontal and downflow installs (EHB p4). Remove the RDS sensor before cleaning the coil. A leak-detection system is installed, so keep power on except during service. The RDS cuts R to the thermostat - thermostats that lose memory can lose setpoints (508438-01 p27)."},{"title":"Not confirmed","body":"Factory default tap and jumper positions for the CBK47UHET were not found in the documents used."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBK48MVT (Dave Lennox Signature multi-position variable-speed air handler, R-454B)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Lennox Dave Lennox Signature CBK48MVT R-454B multi-position variable-speed air handler, 1.5-5 tons. The Lennox Communicating Control (AHC) has an INTEGRATED RDS; the COOL / HEAT / ADJUST jumpers apply only in non-communicating mode. The model string may omit the voltage (for example CBK48MVT-030-71). Electric-heat rows read MCA / MOCP at 230 V single-phase (ECB48 kits).","match":["CBK48","CBK48M","CBK48MVT","CBK48MVT-71"],"source":"Lennox EHB 211150 (CBK48MVT); IOM 508444-01 (CBK48MVT); Unit Information 100113 (CBK48MVT); Unit Information 100112 (A2L figures); 27A02 RDS board setup guide 508426-01; Model ID bulletin 210965","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (CBK48MVT-030-71)","value":"CB = air handler · K = Quantum aluminum coil / R-454B · 43 or 45 = Merit, 47 = Elite, 48 = Dave Lennox Signature · UH = upflow/horizontal, M = multi-position · P = PSC, E = Power Saver constant torque, V = variable speed · T = factory check/expansion valve (non-bleed) · 018-060 = 1.5-5 tons · 230 = 208/230-1-60 · -01 = R-410A TXV installed (R-454B available), -71 = R-454B TXV installed. Bulletin 210965 shows a major-revision letter after the voltage (for example '230A'). The CBK48 uses 018 / 024 as one size group; the voltage may be left off the string"},{"label":"Common figures","value":"TXV 26Z70 / 26Z71 / 26Z72 · filter 20x20x1 (018/024-036), 20x24x1 (042-060) · drains (2) 3/4 · unit MCA 5 / 5 / 8 / 10 (EHB 211150 p8)"}]},{"title":"Blower and controls (AHC with integrated RDS)","rows":[{"label":"Jumpers","value":"COOL / HEAT / ADJUST apply only in non-communicating mode. A missing jumper sets CODE 130 and the control falls back to factory defaults (IOM 508444-01 p10). Constant airflow from 0 to 0.8 in.","key":true},{"label":"NORM cfm for COOL pins 1 / 2 / 3 / 4","value":"018/024: 400 / 575 / 795 / 940 · 030: 545 / 785 / 995 / 1195 · 036: 815 / 1165 / 1315 / 1435 · 042: 1000 / 1200 / 1400 / 1600 · 048: 1460 / 1670 / 1870 / 2100 · 060: 1525 / 1680 / 1850 / 2075 (EHB 211150 pp10-15)","key":true},{"label":"Continuous fan / minimum airflow","value":"28 / 38 (default) / 70 / 100%. Minimum airflow 450 cfm on 048 / 060 (IOM 508444-01 p18). The AHC configures ECB48 heat automatically (IOM 508444-01 p2)"}]},{"title":"Electric heat, ECB48 kits, MCA/MOCP (018/024 and 030 / 036 / 042-060)","rows":[{"label":"4 / 5 / 6 / 8 kW","value":"4 kW 25/25 · 27/30 · 29/30. 5 kW 30/30 · 32/35 · 34/35. 6 kW 35/35 · 37/40 · 39/40. 8 kW 45/45 · 47/50 · 49/50 (EHB 211150 pp16-19)","key":true},{"label":"9 / 12.5 / 15 / 20 / 25 CB","value":"9CB 50/50 · 52/60 · 54/60. 12.5CB 67/70 (030 only) · 70/70 · 72/80. 15CB 80/80 (030 only) · 82/90 · 84/90. 20CB n/a · 107/110 · 109/110. 25CB n/a · n/a · 134/150 (048 / 060 only)","key":true}]},{"title":"RDS codes (IOM 508444-01 p13)","rows":[{"label":"E-codes","value":"E150 leak · E151 sensor fault · E154 sensor communications lost (latches at least 5 min) · E160 wrong sensor type · E163 RDS controller failed · E371 float switch open","key":true}]},{"title":"A2L (R-454B) requirements","rows":[{"label":"Minimum conditioned area (TAmin) by total charge","value":"10 lb = 149.9 ft² · 15 lb = 224.9 · 20 lb = 299.9 · 25 lb = 374.8 · 30 lb = 449.8 ft² (identical in every R-454B IOM checked)","key":true},{"label":"Altitude factor","value":"1.12 at 5,250 ft · 1.40 at 10,500 ft. The table prints 1.05 at 3,280 ft and 1.04 at 3,940 ft (as printed). Maximum altitude 3,200 m"},{"label":"Mitigation airflow (Qmin) by charge","value":"5 lb = 135 cfm · 10 lb = 271 · 15 lb = 406 · 20 lb = 541 · 25 lb = 676 · 30 lb = 812 cfm (UI 100112 p5). Mitigation minimum airflow is factory set at 350 CFM/ton","key":true},{"label":"RDS load / sensor","value":"The RDS adds 3 VA to the transformer load (UI 100112 p4). Check the sensor every 6 months. Replacement sensor 26Z69"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Code 130 = a jumper is missing","body":"In non-communicating mode a missing COOL / HEAT / ADJUST jumper sets code 130 and the control runs on factory defaults (IOM 508444-01 p10). In communicating mode the jumpers are ignored."},{"title":"27A02 field-kit DIP switches expect TWO sensors","body":"The default (DIP1 off, DIP2 off) expects two sensors. With one sensor, set DIP2 ON or the board faults (27A02 setup guide 508426-01 p12)."},{"title":"Red flash-code conflict between documents","body":"The 27A02 setup guide 508426-01 pp14-15 lists red 2 as 'spare/unused' and red 5 as 'indoor unit wired to the Black TSTAT strip'. The air handler IOMs (508438-01 p26) list red 2 as the float switch and red 5 as R-input missing. Check which board and which document you are holding."},{"title":"RDS sensor: reposition, remove for coil cleaning, keep the unit powered","body":"The sensor must be repositioned for horizontal and downflow installs (EHB p4). Remove the RDS sensor before cleaning the coil. A leak-detection system is installed, so keep power on except during service. The RDS cuts R to the thermostat - thermostats that lose memory can lose setpoints (508438-01 p27)."},{"title":"Not confirmed","body":"Factory default jumper positions for the CBK48MVT were not found in the documents used."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"CBA27UHE (Elite upflow/horizontal air handler, R-410A)","equip":"Air Handler","summary":"Lennox Elite CBA27UHE air handler, 1.5-5 tons, 5-tap constant-torque blower. R-410A: the EHB titles it 'R-410A', the A in the model decodes as aluminum coil / R-410A, and it has NO refrigerant-detection (RDS) board - it is not the CBK family. 230 or 460 V (on 460 V the blower is 460 V single-phase and the heat is 460 V three-phase). Electric-heat rows read MCA / MOCP at 230 V single-phase (ECB29 kits, which match the ECB47 values on the CBK47).","match":["CBA27","CBA27UH","CBA27UHE","CBA27UHE-230","CBA27UHE-460"],"source":"Lennox EHB 210675 (CBA27UHE); IOM 507674-01 (CBA27UHE, 2017)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (CBA27UHE-036-230-6-01)","value":"CB = air handler · A = aluminum coil / R-410A · 27 = Elite · UH = upflow/horizontal · E = constant torque · 036 = size · 230 or 460 = voltage · metering digit: 2 = fixed orifice, 3 = TXV bleed, 4 = TXV non-bleed, 5 = TXV non-bleed (outdoor unit), 6 = R-410A TXV non-bleed (indoor unit) · 01 = revision (Bulletin 210675 p1)","key":true},{"label":"Refrigerant","value":"R-410A only. No RDS, no A2L requirements. Do not apply the CBK rules (TAmin, Qmin, sensor) here","key":true},{"label":"Common figures","value":"Sizes 1.5-5 tons · filter 20x20x1 (018-036), 20x24x1 (042-060) · drains (2) 3/4"},{"label":"Unit electrical","value":"MCA 5 / FLA 4.1 (018-036); MCA 10 / FLA 7.6 (042-060) (Bulletin 210675 p8)"}]},{"title":"Blower (5-tap constant torque)","rows":[{"label":"Factory taps","value":"Tap 3 for cooling, tap 4 for heat (minimum) (IOM 507674-01 p9). Tables run to 0.80 in. (Bulletin 210675 pp9-10)","key":true}]},{"title":"Electric heat, ECB29 kits, MCA/MOCP (018-024 / 030 / 036 / 042-060)","rows":[{"label":"2.5 / 4 / 5 / 6 kW","value":"2.5 kW 18/20 (018 only). 4 kW 26/30 · 26/30 · 26/30 · 30/30. 5 kW 31/35 · 31/35 · 31/35 · 36/40. 6 kW 36/40 · 36/40 · 36/40 · 41/45 (Bulletin 210675 pp11-20)","key":true},{"label":"8 / 9 / 10 kW","value":"8 kW 47/50 · 47/50 · 47/50 · 51/60. 9CB 52/60 · 52/60 · 52/60 · 56/60. 10 kW 57/60 · 57/60 · 57/60 · n/a","key":true},{"label":"12.5 / 15 / 20 / 25 CB","value":"12.5CB n/a · 70/70 · 70/70 · 75/80. 15CB n/a · 83/90 · 83/90 · 88/90. 20CB n/a · n/a · 109/125 · 114/125. 25CB n/a · n/a · n/a · 140/150","key":true}]}],"flags":[{"title":"R-410A, not R-454B","body":"The Tag Scanner note that groups this model with the R-454B CBK48MVT manual is about where the manual lives, not the refrigerant. Bulletin 210675 titles the CBA27UHE 'R-410A' and it carries no RDS content. Match it with R-410A outdoor units."},{"title":"Not confirmed - see the rating plate","body":"The TXV part number, and whether a newer IOM than 507674-01 (2017) exists."}],"checklist":"airhandler"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"ELO183 (Elite oil furnace, UF / BF / BR / DH, PSC blower)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Elite ELO183 OIL furnace (filed under Gas Furnace by house convention). No. 1 or No. 2 oil, 'up to 84%' AFUE, Beckett AFG flame-retention burner, Beckett GeniSys 7505B primary, 4-speed PSC direct-drive blower. UF = upflow, BF = lo-boy front flue, BR = lo-boy rear flue, DH = downflow/horizontal. The number pair is input with the low-fire / high-fire nozzle (ELO183UF68/86P36). No Unit Information or service manual exists - figures are from the EHBs and installation instructions.","match":["ELO183","ELO183UF","ELO183BF","ELO183BR","ELO183DH","ELO183B","ELO183UF68/86P36","ELO183UF101/114P48","ELO183UF135/150P60","ELO183BF101/114P48","ELO183BR101/114P48","ELO183BF135/150P60","ELO183BR135/150P60","ELO183DH101/114P36","ELO183DH135/150P60","oil furnace","oil"],"source":"Lennox ELO183UF Product Specifications, Bulletin 210628 (May 2020); ELO183B Bulletin 210629 (Feb 2019); ELO183DH Bulletin 210630 (Feb 2019); ELO183UF Installation Instructions 506901-02 (02/2020); ELO183B 506902-02 (02/2020); ELO183DH 506903-02 (02/2020)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (ELO183UF135/150P60)","value":"EL = Elite · O = oil · 1 = one stage · 83 = nominal AFUE · UF = upflow, BF = lo-boy front flue, BR = lo-boy rear flue, DH = downflow/horizontal · 135/150 = input with the low-fire nozzle / with the high-fire nozzle · P = PSC blower · 36 / 48 / 60 = add-on cooling tons (Bulletin 210628 p1; 210629 p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"UF68/86P36, UF101/114P48, UF135/150P60 · BF/BR101/114P48, BF/BR135/150P60 · DH101/114P36, DH135/150P60"}]},{"title":"Firing: input / output, nozzle (low / high fire), pump","rows":[{"label":"UF68/86","value":"67,500 / 85,500 Btuh in · 57,000 / 72,000 out · 84% AFUE · nozzle .50 gph 80° hollow (low) / .65 gph 80° solid (high) · pump 100 psig (Bulletin 210628 p5)","key":true},{"label":"UF101/114","value":"101,000 / 113,500 in · 84,000 / 95,000 out · 83% · nozzle .65 / .75 gph, 80° solid · pump 140 psig","key":true},{"label":"UF135/150","value":"135,000 / 151,000 in · 113,000 / 126,000 out · 83% · nozzle .85 / 1.00 gph, 80° solid · pump 140 psig","key":true},{"label":"B 101/114 and B 135/150","value":"101,000 / 113,500 in, 85,000 / 95,000 out, .65 / .75 80° solid, 140 psig · 134,000 / 151,000 in, 113,000 / 127,000 out, .85 / 1.00 80° solid, 140 psig (Bulletin 210629 p5)","key":true},{"label":"DH101/114 and DH135/150","value":"101,000 / 113,500 in, 85,000 / 95,000 out, .65 / .75, 140 psig · 135,000 / 150,000 in, 113,000 / 126,000 out, .85 / 1.00, 140 psig (Bulletin 210630 p5)","key":true},{"label":"Nozzle brand","value":"All Delavan. Pattern letter A for the UF68 low-fire nozzle, B for the rest (II 506901-02 Table 8 p15)"}]},{"title":"Burner (Beckett AFG)","rows":[{"label":"UF68/86","value":"Burner 100195-08, spec ARM1812, air tube AF46XZTHS, head F0, insertion 4.75 in., static plate 2.75 in. (II 506901-02 Table 8 p15)"},{"label":"UF / B 101/114","value":"Burner 100195-09, spec ARM1813, AF46XNHS, head F3, insertion 4.75, static plate 2.75 (II 506901-02 p15; II 506902-02 p15)"},{"label":"UF / B 135/150","value":"Burner 100195-07, spec ARM1811, AF46WPHS, head F4, insertion 4.75, static plate 3.38"},{"label":"DH101/114 and DH135/150","value":"100196-06, spec ARM1910, AF46XNHS, head F3 · 100196-07, spec ARM1911, AF46WPHS, head F4, static plate 3.38 (II 506903-02 Table 9 p16)"},{"label":"Electrode gap","value":"5/32 in., set with the Beckett T-501 gauge (II 506901-02 p21). Nozzle depth and alignment: T-501 or Z-2000 gauge (p7)","key":true}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"Draft","value":"At least 0.03 in. with the burner off. 0.04 to 0.05 in. at the breech with the burner firing. Overfire draft 0.02 less than the breech reading and never positive (II 506901-02 p15)","key":true},{"label":"Smoke / CO2","value":"Set to a trace (0 to #1). Then add air until CO2 drops 2% below the trace-smoke reading (example: 12% becomes 10%). The smoke should then read 0 (II 506901-02 p15-16). No CO2 % target is published","key":true},{"label":"Stack temperature","value":"Take a net stack temperature for the efficiency chart. No target value is published (II 506901-02 p16)"}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise - CONFLICT","value":"EHB: UF68/86 and UF101/114 50-80 °F · UF135/150 55-85 · B and DH 45-75 (Bulletins p5). Installation instructions: 68/86 55-80 · 101, 135 65-75 · 114, 150 70-80 °F (II 506901-02 Table 7 p14; II 506902-02 p15; II 506903-02 p16)","key":true},{"label":"Blower, UF","value":"1/2 hp (68/86, 101/114), 3/4 hp (135/150). CFM at 0.20-0.90 in. w.g.: 605-1410, 690-1755, 1110-2090 (Bulletin 210628 p6)"},{"label":"Blower, B and DH","value":"B: 101/114 1/2 hp; 135/150 3/4 hp, up to 2360 cfm at 0.20 in. (Bulletin 210629 p6). DH: 1/2 hp / 3/4 hp, up to 1410 / 2205 cfm (Bulletin 210630 p6)"},{"label":"Fan delays (DIP switches)","value":"ON 30 / 60 / 90 / 120 s, OFF 1 / 2 / 4 / 6 min. Standard is 60 s on, 2 min off (II 506901-02 Table 9 p15)"},{"label":"Filter","value":"UF: not furnished (Bulletin 210628 p4). B: one cleanable filter, 18x19x1 (101/114) or 19x21x1 (135/150). DH: kit 35K05, (2) 10-1/4x20-1/2x1, or kit 35K06, (2) 11-3/4x23-1/2x1"},{"label":"Oil filter / accessories","value":"10 micron with bracket 53P92 · restriction gauge 53P90 · two-stage pump with solenoid 71M18 (Bulletin 210628 p5)"}]},{"title":"Safeties and electrical","rows":[{"label":"Limit","value":"Fixed. 'Do not adjust from factory setting.' No temperature is published - see rating plate (II 506901-02 p15)","key":true},{"label":"Electrical","value":"120 V, 1-phase. Max overcurrent protection 15 A. 40 VA transformer (Bulletin 210628 p4-5)"}]},{"title":"Controls: Beckett GeniSys 7505B (II 506901-02 p17-18)","rows":[{"label":"Sequence","value":"15 s prepurge · ignition · ignition held 10 s after flame · 15 s trial-for-ignition lockout"},{"label":"Lockouts","value":"First failure = soft lockout, clear with a click of under 1 s. Second failure = restricted (hard) lockout, clear by holding reset 15 s or more. Do not press the reset more than once","key":true},{"label":"Reset button","value":"Hold more than 1 s while running = burner disabled. Hold 15 s or more, then click during ignition = pump prime mode (4 minutes)"},{"label":"LEDs","value":"Red solid = restricted (hard) lockout, red flashing = soft lockout · green solid = flame sensed (in standby, could be stray light), green flashing = recycle · yellow solid = pump prime, or reset held 15 s or more"},{"label":"Cad cell","value":"Ohm values are not published"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Pump pressure: the UF68/86 runs at 100 psig, but every ELO183 start-up checklist says 'recommended minimum 140 psi'","body":"Bulletin 210628 p5 and II 506901-02 Table 8 give 100 psig for the 68/86; the checklist on II 506901-02 p2 says 140 minimum. Set the size you are on to its own table value."},{"title":"Document errors in the installation instructions","body":"II 506901-02 Table 8, UF101 low-fire row, prints '0.80° B' - the spec sheet gives .65 gph 80° solid. II 506902-02 Table 8 (ELO183B) lists 114,000 on both 101/114 rows and 135,000 with 0.85 on the 135/150 high-fire row - use Bulletin 210629: 101,000 / 113,500 and 134,000 / 151,000 with 1.00 gph for high fire."},{"title":"High-fire nozzle: furnished or not?","body":"The spec footnotes say the nozzle 'must be field provided'. II 506901-02 says a larger nozzle is in the bag, and Bulletin 210629 p1 says it 'is provided'. Check the bag before ordering one."},{"title":"Fan-on delay conflict","body":"Bulletin 210628 says 60-90 s. II 506901-02 p18 says '1 to 30 seconds - non-adjustable'. The DIP table (30-120 s) is adjustable."},{"title":"Filter conflict on the UF","body":"Bulletin 210628 says no filter is furnished. II 506901-02 p16 mentions 'permanent filters supplied'."},{"title":"Two-pipe systems and pump lift","body":"Install the bypass plug; the return line must end 3-4 in. above the supply inlet (II 506901-02 p12). Single-stage pump lifts up to 10 ft (10 in. Hg); use the two-stage pump beyond that (p11-12)."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Limit and fan-limit temperatures, CO2 % target (only the '2% below trace smoke' method), stack-temperature target, cad-cell resistance. No Unit Information or service manual exists for this family."}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SLO185 (Dave Lennox Signature oil furnace, UF / BF / BR, variable-speed blower)","equip":"Gas Furnace","summary":"Lennox Dave Lennox Signature SLO185 OIL furnace (filed under Gas Furnace by house convention). 'Up to 87%' AFUE, ENERGY STAR, Beckett NX burner with a GeniSys 7505B primary, variable-speed blower with the A54 blower control and the ST9103A (A15) control. UF = upflow, BF = lo-boy front flue, BR = lo-boy rear flue, in 79/105V42 and 124/141V60. NOT for zoning (Harmony). No Unit Information or service manual exists.","match":["SLO185","SLO185UF","SLO185BF","SLO185BR","SLO185UFV","SLO185BV","SLO185UF79/105V42","SLO185UF124/141V60","SLO185BF79/105V42","SLO185BF124/141V60","SLO185BR79/105V42","SLO185BR124/141V60","oil furnace","oil"],"source":"Lennox SLO185UFV Product Specifications, Bulletin 210676 (Feb 2019); SLO185BV Bulletin 210677 (Feb 2019); SLO185UFV Installation Instructions 507263-01 (08/2018); SLO185BV Installation Instructions 507262-01 (08/2018)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (SLO185UF124/141V60)","value":"SL = Signature · O = oil · 1 = one stage · 85 = nominal AFUE · UF = upflow, BF = lo-boy front flue, BR = lo-boy rear flue · 124/141 = input at low / high fire · V = variable speed · 42 / 60 = add-on cooling tons (Bulletin 210676 p1; 210677 p1)"},{"label":"Sizes","value":"UF, BF and BR in 79/105V42 and 124/141V60"},{"label":"Zoning","value":"Does not work with Harmony zoning (Bulletin 210676 p3; II 507263-01 p16)","key":true}]},{"title":"Firing: input / output, nozzle (low / high fire), pump","rows":[{"label":"79/105","value":"79,000 / 105,000 Btuh in · 67,000 / 87,000 out · nozzle .50 / .65 gph, 60° A hollow · pump 150 psig (Bulletin 210676 p6; II 507263-01 Table 9 p20)","key":true},{"label":"124/141","value":"124,000 / 141,000 Btuh in · 104,000 / 118,000 out · nozzle .75 / .85 gph, 60° A hollow · pump 145 psig (Bulletin 210676 p6; II 507263-01 p20)","key":true},{"label":"Nozzle brand","value":"Delavan (II 507263-01 p20)"},{"label":"AFUE (low / high fire)","value":"UF: 86 / 85% (79/105), 87 / 85% (124/141) (Bulletin 210676 p6). BF: 86 / 85 and 85 / 85. BR: 87 / 85 and 85 / 85 (Bulletin 210677 p5)"}]},{"title":"Burner (Beckett NX)","rows":[{"label":"79/105","value":"Burner 103880-01, spec ARM2201, air tube NX70LHHS. 6-slot head, 5 in. insertion, static plate 3.00 in. (II 507263-01 p20; II 507262-01 p22)"},{"label":"124/141","value":"Burner 103880-02, spec ARM2202, air tube NX70LCHS. 6-slot head, 5 in. insertion, static plate 3.25 in."},{"label":"Electrode gap","value":"5/32 in. (T-501 gauge) (II 507263-01 p7)","key":true}]},{"title":"Combustion","rows":[{"label":"Draft","value":"At least 0.04 in. w.c. while firing (II 507263-01 p8). The manual prints the overfire target as '-0,1\" to -.02\"' and the breech as '-0.2 to -.04\"' - these look like typos for -0.01 to -0.02 and -0.02 to -0.04, but Lennox has not confirmed that (II 507263-01 p20; II 507262-01 p21)","key":true},{"label":"Smoke / CO2","value":"#1 or less, then adjust to the 'desired CO2' - no % is published. Use a 5/16 in. test hole at least 2 flue diameters above the breech (II 507263-01 p19-20)","key":true}]},{"title":"Air","rows":[{"label":"Temperature rise - CONFLICT","value":"EHB: 79/105 50-80 °F · UF124/141 60-85 · BF124/141 45-70 · BR124/141 50-80 (Bulletin 210676 p6; 210677 p5). Installation instructions: 79/105 45-55 · 124/141 55-65 °F (II 507263-01 Table 8 p19; II 507262-01 p21)","key":true},{"label":"Blower, UF","value":"79/105: 1/2 hp, heat 1500 cfm high fire / 1200 low fire, cool 650-1500. 124/141: 3/4 hp, heat 1850 / 1550, cool 1050-2000 (Bulletin 210676 p7)"},{"label":"Blower, BF / BR","value":"79/105: 1/2 hp, heat 1450 / 1200 (BF), 1550 / 1200 (BR), cool 650-1500. 124/141: 1 hp, heat 1730 / 1550 (BF), 1730 / 1450 (BR), cool 950-2100 (Bulletin 210677 p5, p7)"},{"label":"Static / continuous fan","value":"Tables cover 0-0.50 in. w.g. Continuous fan runs at 50% of the COOL cfm (Bulletin 210676 p7)"},{"label":"A54 blower control","value":"ADJUST jumper ±15%, cooling only; the HEAT jumper must stay at the table setting (II 507263-01 p17). Cooling ramp 82% for 7.5 min; two-stage cooling 57% then 70% (p16). Heat-off ramp 82% for 3.5 min. Dehumidification: cut JW1 and the blower drops 18%. CFM LED: 1 flash per 100 cfm (p17)"},{"label":"Filter","value":"UF: not furnished (Bulletin 210676 p4). BF / BR: one cleanable filter, 18x19x1 (79/105) or 19x21x1 (124/141) (Bulletin 210677 p5)"},{"label":"Oil filter / accessories","value":"53P92 / 53P90 · two-stage pump 71M18 · air intake kit 11F44 (Bulletin 210676 p6)"}]},{"title":"Safeties and electrical","rows":[{"label":"Limit","value":"Fixed, do not adjust. No temperature is published - see rating plate (II 507263-01 p19)","key":true},{"label":"Electrical","value":"120 V, 1-phase, 15 A max (Bulletin 210676 p6)"}]},{"title":"Controls: Beckett GeniSys 7505B (II 507263-01 p21-22)","rows":[{"label":"Sequence","value":"15 s prepurge · ignition · ignition held 10 s after flame · 15 s trial-for-ignition lockout"},{"label":"Lockouts","value":"First failure = soft lockout, clear with a click of under 1 s. Second failure = restricted (hard) lockout, clear by holding reset 15 s or more. Do not press the reset more than once","key":true},{"label":"Reset button","value":"Hold more than 1 s while running = burner disabled. Hold 15 s or more, then click during ignition = pump prime mode (4 minutes)"},{"label":"LEDs","value":"Red solid = restricted (hard) lockout, red flashing = soft lockout · green solid = flame sensed (in standby, could be stray light), green flashing = recycle · yellow solid = pump prime, or reset held 15 s or more"},{"label":"Cad cell","value":"Ohm values are not published"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Not for zoning","body":"The SLO185 does not work with Harmony zoning (Bulletin 210676 p3; II 507263-01 p16)."},{"title":"Nozzle conflict","body":"Bulletins 210676 / 210677 say the high-fire nozzle is furnished. The table footnotes in II 507263-01 / 507262-01 say it 'must be field-installed'. Check the bag."},{"title":"Temperature rise: the manual ranges are much narrower than the spec-sheet ranges","body":"Both are shown. The factory heat speed is the mid-rise setting; changing the nozzle changes the heat cfm column."},{"title":"Limit-trip conflict inside the install manual","body":"II 507263-01 p22 says the blower runs at 'cool speed' when the limit opens; the table on p23 says 'heat speed'."},{"title":"Draft targets are misprinted","body":"The overfire and breech draft figures in II 507263-01 p20 / II 507262-01 p21 look like typos (see the Draft row). Only the 0.04 in. minimum while firing is printed cleanly."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"Limit and fan-limit temperatures, CO2 % target, stack-temperature target, cad-cell resistance. No Unit Information or service manual exists, and no newer revision of 507263 or 507262 was found."}],"checklist":"furnace80"},
  {"brand":"Lennox","model":"SL25XPV (Signature variable-capacity heat pump, R-410A, communicating only)","equip":"Heat Pump","summary":"Dave Lennox Signature SL25XPV split heat pump, variable-capacity R-scroll (inverter) compressor, HFC-410A (R-410A) with PVE oil, 2-5 ton. Sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060, 208/230V-1ph. Indoor check/expansion valve plus an outdoor EEV for heating. COMMUNICATING ONLY: needs an S30 thermostat and a Lennox communicating variable-speed air handler or furnace. Demand defrost set from the S30. The Lennox documents disagree on the defrost termination choices and on the coil-sensor wiring - see flags.","match":["SL25XPV","SL25XPV-024-230","SL25XPV-036-230","SL25XPV-048-230","SL25XPV-060-230"],"source":"Lennox Unit Information 'SL25XPV (HFC-410A) Series Outdoor Units', Corp. 100026, Service Literature (June 1, 2022) (UI); Lennox SL25XPV Installation Instructions 508104-01 (4/2021) (II)","groups":[{"title":"Identify it right first","rows":[{"label":"Model decode (SL25XPV-036-230A01)","value":"SL = Dave Lennox Signature Collection · 25 = series · X = R-410A · P = heat pump outdoor unit · V = variable capacity compressor · 024 / 036 / 048 / 060 = 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 tons · 230 = 208/230V-1ph-60Hz · A = ratings revision level · 01 = minor revision number (UI p2)"},{"label":"Unit codes","value":"45 / 47 / 49 / 50 for 024 / 036 / 048 / 060. Three horizontal bars at power-up = unit code not programmed - set it from the push-button P U menu (UI p44, p46, p49). E443 = incorrect appliance unit size code (UI p43)"},{"label":"Required controls (communicating only)","value":"S30 Smart Wi-Fi thermostat (19V30) plus a Lennox communicating variable-speed air handler or furnace, wired R, I+, I-, C (UI p3, p30, p72, p74; II p1, p17-18). Neither document mentions the S40 smart thermostat - the 'S40' in the UI is the crankcase heater thermostat (UI p50, p68)"},{"label":"Refrigerant & metering","value":"HFC-410A with PVE oil (UI p2, p14; II p1, p4). Indoor: check/expansion valve, ordered separately - approved kits are in the EHB (UI p2; II p10). Outdoor: EEV and check valve for heating, controlling to 8 °F superheat (UI p33)"}]},{"title":"Refrigerant & charging (sizes 024 / 036 / 048 / 060)","rows":[{"label":"Factory charge R-410A (covers a 15 ft line set)","value":"024: 13 lbs. 3 oz. · 036: 12 lbs. 10 oz. · 048: 16 lbs. 0 oz. · 060: 15 lbs. 14 oz. (UI p3). Sufficient for 15 ft of line (UI p3 note 1, p87; II p20). The nameplate governs","key":true},{"label":"Line-length adder","value":"3/8 in. liquid line: 3 oz per 5 ft longer than 15 ft; subtract the same when shorter (II p20; UI p87). Weigh-in chart ('64 °F (17.7 °C) and Below'): 0.60 oz/ft for 3/8 in., 0.40 for 5/16 in., 1.00 for 1/2 in. (UI p15, p85; II p5)"},{"label":"Charging method","value":"Weigh in, then verify by subcooling with the unit at 100% capacity: S30 Menu > Advanced Settings > View Dealer Control Center > Test > Cooling - Maximum Rate Test (or Heating - Maximum Rate Test), or the Lennox Dealer Setup App (UI p83; II p19-20). Cooling mode at 60 °F outdoor and above, heating mode below 60 °F (UI p85, p87)","key":true},{"label":"Subcooling targets and extra charge per indoor match","value":"From the unit charging label, UI p87 Table 2, which also lists charge to add on top of the nameplate. CBA38MV examples (heat ±5 / cool ±1 °F, add): 024 + CBA38MV-036: 19 / 10, add 0 lb 12 oz · 036 + CBA38MV-036: 22 / 9, add 2 lb 0 oz · 048 + CBA38MV-048: 15 / 13, add 0 lb 8 oz · 060 + CBA38MV-060: 11 / 14, add 0 lb 11 oz. Cooling targets assume 70-80 °F return air, heating 65-75 °F (UI p87). Other matches: see the charging label"},{"label":"Line set","value":"3/8 in. liquid; vapor 7/8 in. (024-048), 1-1/8 in. (060) (UI p3, p15; II p6). Limits 180 ft total equivalent, 150 ft linear, 60 ft liquid lift, 60 ft vapor riser; over 50 ft see Corp. 9351-L9 (UI p14; II p4-5)"}]},{"title":"Electrical 208/230V-1ph: MCA / MOCP / inverter input current / fan FLA (UI p3)","rows":[{"label":"By size","value":"024: 20.3 / 25 / 14 / 2.6 · 036: 25.6 / 30 / 18.2 / 2.6 · 048: 32.8 / 35 / 24 / 2.6 · 060: 32.8 / 35 / 24 / 2.6. MOCP is an HACR breaker or fuse. The II prints no electrical figures - it points to the nameplate (II p13). LRA not published (inverter) - see the rating plate","key":true},{"label":"Low voltage","value":"24 VAC from the indoor unit transformer, 40 VA minimum (II p13). E409 = outdoor control secondary voltage is 18VAC or less (UI p40)"}]},{"title":"Pressure switches & low-temperature limit","rows":[{"label":"High-pressure switch S4","value":"Opens at 590 psig, closes at 418 psig (UI p40, p59, p64); II p21 prints 590 ± 15 / 418 ± 15 psig. 5 opens within one hour = E413 lockout (UI p40)"},{"label":"Low-pressure switch S87","value":"Cut-out 25 psig, cut-in 40 psig (UI p40, p59, p64). Ignored for 90 s after the contactor energizes and in cold weather (flowchart: 15 °F or below; note: below 15 °F) (UI p56, p62). 5 trips within one hour = E411 lockout (UI p40)"},{"label":"Low-temperature protection E601","value":"Will not start at or below -4 °F (-20 °C); if already running it continues until the thermostat is satisfied or the outdoor temperature drops to -15 °F (-26 °C) (UI p44, p73)"}]},{"title":"Defrost - how it works","rows":[{"label":"Demand defrost algorithm","value":"The control counts heat-pump heating run time while the outdoor coil is below 35 °F (frost accumulation time) and starts a defrost when it reaches the target - initially 90 min. Defrost ends when the coil reaches the termination temperature, or is cut off at the 14-minute maximum. After each defrost the defrost cycle time (timed until the coil reaches 50 °F, whatever the termination setting) is compared with the size's target: 80% or less = accumulation time +30 min; 120% or more = -30 min; between 80% and 120% = no change; 200% or more, or ended at the 14-minute maximum = set to 30 min. Two consecutive low-pressure-switch trips in heating also start a defrost (e.g. freezing rain) (UI p50-51, p58)"},{"label":"Target defrost cycle time","value":"024: 60 s · 036: 85 s · 048: 100 s · 060: 110 s (UI p51, p58)"},{"label":"Termination temperature - CONFLICT","value":"Factory default 50 °F (10 °C). Choices: UI p30 and p75 say 50, 70, 80, 90 and 100 °F; UI p51 says 50, 70, 90 and 100 °F; the S30 screen on UI p52 reads 'range: 50 - 100 F, default: 50 F, inc: 10 F'. Change it at the S30 Dealer Control Center > Heat Pump > Defrost Termination Temp, or remotely on the LennoxPros Service Dashboard (UI p51-52). Colder climates may need a higher setting (UI p30, p51)","key":true},{"label":"Coil sensor location","value":"UI p51: at the outlet of the outdoor expansion valve (Figure 26 shows it below the EEV valve assembly). UI p30, p75: spring clip on the outdoor TXV distributor. II p19: spring clip on the outside coil tubing. Both say location matters for proper defrost. Component photos: UI p6-8"},{"label":"S30 adjustable defrost parameters (Dealer Control Center > heat pump)","value":"Defrost Time Adder 5-60 min, default 30 · Defrost Time Reducer 5-60 min, default 30 · Default Frost Accumulation Time 30-360 min, default 90 · Defrost Time Increase Value 0%-100%, default 80% · Defrost Time Decrease Value 100%-200%, default 120% · Defrost Time Reset Limit 150%-400%, default 200% · Nominal Defrost Time 20-840 s, default 024: 60 s, 036: 85 s, 048: 100 s, 060: 110 s. Lennox: in most cases these should not need adjusting (UI p51)"}]},{"title":"Defrost - forced test & checks","rows":[{"label":"dF on the 7-segment display","value":"dF = system is in defrost mode, shown only while a defrost is active (UI p45-46). To enter defrost the unit must be running in the heating mode, outdoor ambient must be below 65 °F and the outdoor coil must be below the defrost termination temperature (UI p46)","key":true},{"label":"Forced defrost - Table 8 'Solid d'","value":"Table 8 lists 'Solid d - Starts forced defrost test' in the push-button field-test menu (UI p48). Lennox prints the full button sequence only for the F (fan) and A options; d is in the same menu, so it is written here as that same sequence: push and hold until a solid '-' appears, release (display flashes); within 10 s push and hold until d displays, release; within 10 s push and hold until the display stops flashing, release (UI p46, p71). If the button is not pushed within 10 s the control exits test mode - repeat (UI p46). No exit step is printed for d (the three-horizontal-bars exit is printed only for the fan test and error-code recall, UI p46-47). Idle vs heating: see flags","key":true},{"label":"Readings to check","value":"Push-button A option shows error codes and ambient (A), outdoor coil (c) and liquid (L) temperatures in °F (UI p46). The S30 shows Target Frost Accumulation, Frost Accumulation Time and Coil Temp (UI p50)"},{"label":"Defrost-related codes (UI Table 6)","value":"E416 'The outdoor coil sensor has malfunctioned.' - 'SL25XPV has a fixed 10K ohm resistor installed on the harness connector between pins 5 & 6. Check connections on pins 5 & 6 and check for resistance of 10K ohms. Error code will occur on open or shorted circuit' (p40) · E345 'Heat Pump or Air Conditioner Alert Code - The \"O\" relay on the outdoor board has failed.' (p40) · E410 'The outdoor unit cycled off due to low suction pressure.' - two consecutive low-pressure trips in heating start a defrost (p40, p51) · E431 (inverter, PFC over-current) cause (2): 'System testing was set up and code was generated when the reversing valve is de-energized coming out of defrost' (p41)"}]}],"flags":[{"title":"Communicating only - S30 thermostat","body":"UI p30, p72, p74 and II p1 require a fully communicating system: S30 thermostat plus a communicating variable-speed air handler or furnace. The UI still carries conventional-thermostat text (Y1 / O terminals in Table 5, p31; 'staged mode' notes on E181 / E183, p40) - do not take that as permission to run it on a 24 V thermostat. Neither document mentions the S40 smart thermostat; the 'S40' in the UI is the crankcase heater thermostat."},{"title":"Defrost termination choices disagree","body":"UI p30 and p75: 50, 70, 80, 90 and 100 °F. UI p51: 50, 70, 90 and 100 °F. S30 screen on UI p52: range 50 - 100 F, inc 10 F. All three agree the factory default is 50 °F. Pick from what the S30 actually offers."},{"title":"Coil sensor wiring - the UI contradicts itself","body":"E416 (p40), Table 5 (p32) and p75 say pins 5 & 6 of the 6-pin harness carry a fixed 10K ohm resistor, not a sensor. p75 (RT21) then says the sensor at the outlet of the outdoor TXV is on pins 5 and 6, and Figure 51 (p76) lists COIL on pins 6 and 5 (brown sleeve). On E416, check pins 5 & 6 for 10K ohms as E416 says, and look at what is actually on the harness before replacing parts."},{"title":"Forced defrost 'd': steps and mode not fully printed","body":"Table 8 (UI p48) lists 'Solid d - Starts forced defrost test', but step-by-step text is printed only for F and A (UI p46, p71). Figure 23 (p46) says the push-button menu needs the control in IDLE (no heating or cooling), yet dF needs the unit running in heating with ambient below 65 °F and the coil below the termination temperature (p46). Lennox does not say which applies to d, and prints no exit step for it."},{"title":"No 'Charge Mode' jumper on this control","body":"UI p83 and p85 say to use a 'Charge Mode' jumper (p85: 'see Charge Mode Jumper section on page 80'), but the A175 control shows only a PUMP DOWN jumper (UI p30, p32; II p14) and page 80 has no such section. Use the S30 Cooling - Maximum Rate Test / Heating - Maximum Rate Test or the Dealer Setup App (UI p83; II p19-20)."},{"title":"Defrost length: 14 min max vs '5 to 15 minutes'","body":"UI p50-51 caps a defrost at 14 minutes. The homeowner section of II p21 says a defrost lasts 5 to 15 minutes. The UI figure is the control limit."},{"title":"Copied text in the documents","body":"UI p2 and II p1 call the SL25XPV an 'air conditioner' - it is a heat pump. II p19 points to the 'XP25 Installation and Service Procedures Corp. 1252-L11'. UI p3 lists the 88K38 discharge air sensor under Required Components, but its footnote says it is for optional service diagnostics."},{"title":"Not published - see the rating plate","body":"LRA and compressor RLA (inverter unit), capacitor rating, and subcooling targets for indoor matches not on the charging label."}],"checklist":"heatpump"}
];

